window.TWG_I18N=window.TWG_I18N||{};TWG_I18N["zh-hant"]=Object.assign(TWG_I18N["zh-hant"]||{},{"I'll build you a tailor-made path to pass your Level 2 exam. It takes 5 quick questions.":"我會為你量身打造一條通過 Level 2 考試的學習路徑，只需回答 5 個簡單問題。","The vine and the grape":"葡萄樹與葡萄","Climate, weather and site":"氣候、天氣與園地","Choices in the vineyard":"葡萄園裡的選擇","Reading the label: origin and rules":"讀懂酒標：產地與法規","Winery choices and ageing":"酒廠的選擇與熟成","Pinot Grigio / Pinot Gris":"灰皮諾（Pinot Grigio / Pinot Gris）","Syrah / Shiraz":"希哈／希拉茲（Syrah / Shiraz）","Label terms: Burgundy, Bordeaux, Alsace, Germany":"酒標術語：布根地、波爾多、阿爾薩斯、德國","Reds of France and Spain":"法國與西班牙的紅酒","Reds of Italy":"義大利的紅酒","New World reds":"新世界的紅酒","Regional whites":"地區性白酒","Sherry":"Sherry","Serving wine":"侍酒","Tasting with a method":"有方法地品飲","From vineyard to winery":"從葡萄園到酒廠","The principal grapes":"主要葡萄品種","Regional grapes":"地區性葡萄品種","r3":"r3","Sparkling and fortified":"氣泡酒與加烈酒","s3":"s3","Service, storage and food":"侍酒、儲存與餐酒搭配","Which part of the grape gives a red wine its colour?":"葡萄的哪個部位讓紅酒有顏色？","The seeds":"葡萄籽","The stems":"果梗","Colour is held in the skins of black grapes; the pulp is almost always pale.":"顏色存在於黑葡萄的果皮中；果肉幾乎都是淺色的。","With very few exceptions, the pulp of white and black grapes is the same pale colour. The skin holds colour and tannin, both much more plentiful in black grapes. So a red wine only gains its colour if the juice stays in contact with the skins; seeds and stems mainly bring tannin, not colour.":"除了極少數例外，白葡萄和黑葡萄的果肉都是同樣的淺色。果皮含有顏色和單寧，而黑葡萄的果皮含量多得多。所以紅酒只有在葡萄汁與果皮保持接觸時才會染上顏色；葡萄籽和果梗主要帶來單寧，而不是顏色。","What is grape pulp mainly made of?":"葡萄果肉主要由什麼組成？","Water and sugar":"水和糖","Colour and flavour":"顏色和風味","Tannin and acids":"單寧和酸","Pulp is mostly water and sugar, with some acids and flavours.":"果肉主要是水和糖，還有一些酸和風味物質。","The pulp is the juicy part of the grape: water and sugar are its main components, along with acids and flavours. Colour and tannin are concentrated in the skin, while seeds and stems are rich in tannin. Knowing what each part contains helps explain how white, rosé and red wines are made.":"果肉是葡萄多汁的部分：主要成分是水和糖，另外還有酸和風味物質。顏色和單寧集中在果皮，而葡萄籽和果梗富含單寧。了解每個部位含有什麼，有助於理解白酒、粉紅酒和紅酒的釀造方式。","Why must seeds and stems be handled gently in the winery?":"為什麼在酒廠裡必須輕柔處理葡萄籽和果梗？","They are high in tannins that can make wine bitter":"它們含有大量單寧，可能讓酒變苦","They contain almost all of the grape's sugar":"它們含有葡萄幾乎所有的糖分","They are the main source of the wine's colour":"它們是葡萄酒顏色的主要來源","They release acids that make the wine too sour":"它們會釋放讓酒過酸的酸","Seeds and stems hold a lot of tannin, which turns bitter if they are handled roughly.":"葡萄籽和果梗含有大量單寧，處理過於粗暴就會變苦。","Seeds and stems contain plenty of tannin, and if they are crushed or worked roughly this passes into the wine and makes it very bitter. Sugar is found in the pulp and colour in the skins of black grapes, so the other answers give seeds and stems a role they do not play.":"葡萄籽和果梗含有大量單寧，如果被壓碎或粗暴處理，單寧就會進入酒中，讓酒非常苦澀。糖存在於果肉，顏色存在於黑葡萄的果皮，所以其他選項賦予了葡萄籽和果梗它們並不具備的作用。","Which process allows the vine to produce sugars?":"哪個過程讓葡萄樹能夠產生糖分？","Photosynthesis":"光合作用","Pollination":"授粉","In photosynthesis, sunlight lets the vine combine CO2 and water into sugars.":"光合作用中，陽光讓葡萄樹把 CO2 和水結合成糖。","The leaves take in carbon dioxide from the air and the roots take up water from the soil. Using sunlight, the vine combines these to make sugars: this is photosynthesis. The sugars fuel the plant's growth and the ripening of the grapes. Véraison, pollination and fruit set are stages in the development of the grape itself.":"葉片從空氣中吸收二氧化碳，根部從土壤中吸收水分。葡萄樹利用陽光把兩者結合成糖：這就是光合作用。這些糖為植株的生長和葡萄的成熟提供能量。轉色期、授粉和著果則是葡萄本身發育的不同階段。","Why does the vine go dormant in winter?":"為什麼葡萄樹在冬天會進入休眠？","There is not enough heat for it to grow":"熱量不足，無法生長","The soil no longer contains nutrients":"土壤中已經沒有養分","The roots stop absorbing CO2":"根部停止吸收 CO2","The plant has just been pruned":"植株剛被修剪過","Without enough heat a vine cannot grow, so in winter it stops.":"沒有足夠的熱量，葡萄樹就無法生長，所以冬天會停止生長。","Heat, supplied by the sun, is one of the vine's five needs. When it is too cold the plant cannot grow and becomes dormant, having dropped its leaves in autumn. CO2 is taken in by the leaves, not the roots, and winter pruning happens precisely because the vine is already dormant.":"由太陽提供的熱量是葡萄樹的五大需求之一。天氣太冷時，植株無法生長而進入休眠，葉子在秋天就已掉落。CO2 是由葉片而不是根部吸收的，而冬季修剪正是因為葡萄樹已經在休眠才進行的。","What does the vine take in through its leaves?":"葡萄樹透過葉片吸收什麼？","Nutrients":"養分","Leaves take in CO2 from the air; water and nutrients come through the roots.":"葉片從空氣中吸收 CO2；水和養分則由根部吸收。","A vine takes what it needs either from the soil through its roots or from the air through its leaves. Carbon dioxide enters through the leaves; water and small amounts of nutrients come in through the roots. Sugars are not absorbed at all: the plant makes them itself by photosynthesis, using light, CO2 and water.":"葡萄樹所需的東西，不是透過根部從土壤中取得，就是透過葉片從空氣中取得。二氧化碳從葉片進入；水和少量養分從根部進入。糖完全不是吸收來的：植株利用光、CO2 和水，透過光合作用自己製造糖。","How are vine flowers pollinated?":"葡萄樹的花是怎麼授粉的？","They pollinate themselves":"自花授粉","By bees":"靠蜜蜂","By birds":"靠鳥類","By hand, by the grower":"由種植者人工授粉","Vines are self-pollinating, so they do not need showy flowers to attract insects.":"葡萄樹會自花授粉，所以不需要鮮豔的花朵來吸引昆蟲。","Many plants have colourful flowers to attract pollinating insects. Vines do not: their flowers pollinate themselves. Each pollinated flower can then grow seeds and swell, becoming a grape at fruit set. That is why vine flowers are small and inconspicuous.":"許多植物有色彩鮮豔的花朵來吸引授粉昆蟲。葡萄樹不需要：它的花會自花授粉。每朵授粉的花接著就能長出種子並膨大，在著果時成為一顆葡萄。這就是為什麼葡萄樹的花又小又不顯眼。","What is the stage called when the pollinated flower swells into a grape?":"授粉後的花膨大成葡萄的階段叫什麼？","Extra-ripening":"過熟","At fruit set the flower grows seeds, swells and becomes a small green grape.":"著果時，花朵長出種子、膨大，變成一顆綠色小葡萄。","The order is: flowering in spring, fruit set when the pollinated flower starts to grow seeds and swell, then summer growth, véraison in mid-summer and finally ripening. Newly set grapes are small, hard, green and unpleasant; they still need to grow and ripen to become wine grapes.":"順序是：春天開花，授粉的花開始長出種子並膨大時為著果，接著是夏季生長、盛夏的轉色期，最後是成熟。剛著果的葡萄又小又硬、呈綠色且難吃；它們還需要長大、成熟，才能成為釀酒葡萄。","What happens at véraison?":"轉色期會發生什麼？","Grapes lose their green colour and ripening begins":"葡萄褪去綠色，開始成熟","Flowers are pollinated and start forming seeds":"花朵授粉並開始形成種子","The vine drops its leaves and goes dormant":"葡萄樹落葉並進入休眠","Grapes shrivel and turn into raisins":"葡萄乾縮變成葡萄乾","Véraison marks the start of ripening, when grapes change colour.":"轉色期標誌著成熟的開始，葡萄在這時改變顏色。","By mid-summer the grapes are big enough for the vine to start ripening them. Véraison is when they lose their green colour: white grapes turn golden, black grapes go red and then purple. Pollination happens much earlier, leaf fall comes in autumn, and shrivelling only occurs if picking is delayed a long time.":"到了盛夏，葡萄已經長得夠大，葡萄樹開始讓它們成熟。轉色期就是葡萄褪去綠色的時候：白葡萄轉為金黃色，黑葡萄先變紅再變紫。授粉發生得早得多，落葉在秋天，而乾縮只有在採收大幅延後時才會出現。","What colour do black grapes turn during véraison?":"黑葡萄在轉色期會變成什麼顏色？","Red, then purple":"先紅後紫","Golden, then red":"先金黃後紅","Purple, then red":"先紫後紅","Yellow, then brown":"先黃後褐","At véraison black grapes go from green to red and then purple.":"轉色期時，黑葡萄從綠色變成紅色，再變成紫色。","Véraison is the colour change that opens the ripening period. White grapes go from green to golden, while black grapes first turn red and then purple. The colour sits in the skin, which is exactly where a red wine gets its hue during winemaking.":"轉色期是開啟成熟期的顏色變化。白葡萄從綠色轉為金黃色，黑葡萄則先轉紅再轉紫。顏色存在於果皮中，而紅酒在釀造過程中正是從果皮獲得色澤。","How do acidity and sugar change during ripening?":"成熟過程中，酸度和糖分如何變化？","Acidity falls and sugar rises":"酸度下降，糖分上升","Acidity rises and sugar falls":"酸度上升，糖分下降","Both rise":"兩者都上升","Both fall":"兩者都下降","As grapes ripen they lose acidity and build up sugar.":"葡萄成熟時會失去酸度並累積糖分。","Unripe grapes are very acidic with hardly any sugar. As they ripen, they swell with water, acidity drops and sugar rises, while herbaceous notes give way to the variety's signature flavours. Only with extra-ripeness and shrivelling do acids and sugars become concentrated together, because water evaporates.":"未成熟的葡萄非常酸，幾乎沒有糖分。隨著成熟，葡萄吸水膨大，酸度下降、糖分上升，草本氣息也逐漸讓位給品種的招牌風味。只有在過熟和乾縮時，由於水分蒸發，酸和糖才會一起濃縮。","A black grape is picked with unripe tannins. Which fault is most likely in the wine?":"一批黑葡萄在單寧尚未成熟時採收。酒中最可能出現哪種缺點？","Bitterness":"苦味","Excessive sweetness":"過甜","Dried-fruit aromas":"乾果香氣","Overly deep colour":"顏色過深","Unripe tannins can make a red wine taste bitter.":"未成熟的單寧可能讓紅酒嚐起來有苦味。","During ripening, along with sugar and flavours, the tannins in black grape skins also ripen. Tannins shape the mouthfeel of red wines, but unripe tannins taste bitter. So the grower must time the harvest by checking not just the sugar level but also how ripe the tannins are.":"成熟過程中，除了糖分和風味，黑葡萄果皮中的單寧也會成熟。單寧塑造紅酒的口感，但未成熟的單寧嚐起來是苦的。所以種植者決定採收時機時，不只要檢查糖分，也要檢查單寧的成熟度。","In some white grapes, how do aromas develop as ripeness increases?":"對某些白葡萄來說，隨著成熟度提高，香氣如何發展？","From green fruit to stone fruit to tropical fruit":"從綠色水果到核果再到熱帶水果","From tropical fruit to stone fruit to green fruit":"從熱帶水果到核果再到綠色水果","From fresh fruit to cooked fruit":"從新鮮水果到煮熟的水果","From dried fruit to fresh fruit":"從乾果到新鮮水果","The riper a white grape gets, the more its aromas move from green to stone to tropical fruit.":"白葡萄越成熟，香氣就越從綠色水果轉向核果，再轉向熱帶水果。","As grapes ripen, herbaceous notes fade and varietal flavours appear. For some white grapes the typical path is green fruit, then stone fruit, then tropical fruit. The shift from fresh to cooked fruit describes black grapes instead, while dried-fruit aromas only come with extra-ripeness.":"葡萄成熟時，草本氣息減弱，品種風味出現。對某些白葡萄來說，典型的路徑是綠色水果、核果，然後是熱帶水果。從新鮮水果到煮熟水果描述的是黑葡萄，而乾果香氣只在過熟時才會出現。","Why is dry weather needed to leave grapes on the vine beyond the normal harvest?":"為什麼要把葡萄留在樹上超過正常採收期，必須有乾燥的天氣？","Rain can lead to fungal diseases":"下雨可能引發真菌病害","Rain makes acidity rise too much":"下雨會讓酸度上升太多","Rain makes the skins darker":"下雨會讓果皮顏色變深","Rain stops photosynthesis":"下雨會中止光合作用","Rain brings moisture that encourages fungi which can spoil the grapes.":"下雨帶來濕氣，助長可能破壞葡萄的真菌。","For extra-ripening the weather must stay dry, because rain encourages fungal diseases, and warm enough for ripening to carry on. Under these conditions aromas become riper, sugar rises and, over time, the grapes shrivel, concentrating sugars and acids: ideal fruit for sweet wines.":"要讓葡萄過熟，天氣必須保持乾燥，因為下雨會助長真菌病害；也必須夠溫暖，讓成熟得以持續。在這樣的條件下，香氣變得更成熟、糖分上升，久而久之葡萄乾縮，糖和酸隨之濃縮：這是釀造甜酒的理想果實。","A grape left on the vine for a long time shrivels. Which aromas does it tend to develop?":"一顆葡萄在樹上留了很久而乾縮。它傾向於發展出哪種香氣？","Dried fruit":"乾果","Herbaceous":"草本","Green fruit":"綠色水果","Fresh floral":"清新花香","As the grapes shrivel, water evaporates and dried-fruit aromas appear.":"葡萄乾縮時水分蒸發，乾果香氣隨之出現。","In the early stages of extra-ripeness, aromas become very ripe and sugar rises. If the grapes stay on the vine longer, water evaporates and they turn almost into raisins: acids and sugars concentrate and dried-fruit aromas develop. Herbaceous and green-fruit notes, by contrast, are typical of unripe grapes.":"在過熟的初期，香氣變得非常成熟，糖分上升。如果葡萄在樹上留得更久，水分蒸發，它們幾乎變成葡萄乾：酸和糖濃縮，發展出乾果香氣。相反地，草本和綠色水果的氣息是未成熟葡萄的典型特徵。","Which of these is NOT one of the five things a vine needs?":"下列哪一項不是葡萄樹的五大需求之一？","Insects to pollinate its flowers":"為花朵授粉的昆蟲","Warmth":"溫暖","Carbon dioxide taken from the air by the leaves":"葉片從空氣中吸收的二氧化碳","Vines pollinate themselves: they need warmth, sunlight, carbon dioxide, water and nutrients, not insects.":"葡萄樹會自花授粉：它需要溫暖、陽光、二氧化碳、水和養分，而不需要昆蟲。","A vine's five needs are warmth, sunlight, carbon dioxide, water and nutrients, so warmth, CO2 and nutrients are all essential. Unlike many plants with bright flowers, the vine does not need to attract insects, because its flowers pollinate themselves.":"葡萄樹的五大需求是溫暖、陽光、二氧化碳、水和養分，所以溫暖、CO2 和養分都不可或缺。不同於許多花朵鮮豔的植物，葡萄樹不需要吸引昆蟲，因為它的花會自花授粉。","Through which part does the vine take up water and nutrients?":"葡萄樹透過哪個部位吸收水和養分？","The roots":"根部","The leaves":"葉片","The flowers, during spring":"春天時的花朵","The skins of the ripening grapes":"成熟中的葡萄果皮","Water and nutrients come from the soil and are taken up by the roots.":"水和養分來自土壤，由根部吸收。","Because it is rooted to the ground, the vine takes what it needs either from the soil, through its roots, or from the air, through its leaves. The leaves take in carbon dioxide, not water. Flowers and grape skins play no part in this.":"由於扎根於地面，葡萄樹所需的東西不是透過根部從土壤中取得，就是透過葉片從空氣中取得。葉片吸收的是二氧化碳，不是水。花朵和葡萄果皮在這方面都不起作用。","What does the vine use the sugars made by photosynthesis for?":"葡萄樹用光合作用產生的糖來做什麼？","To power its growth and ripen its grapes":"為生長提供能量，並讓葡萄成熟","To protect itself from frost during winter dormancy":"在冬季休眠期保護自己免受霜害","To attract insects to its flowers":"吸引昆蟲到花朵上","To make tannins in the seeds":"在葡萄籽中製造單寧","Sugars from photosynthesis fuel the plant's growth and the ripening of its grapes.":"光合作用產生的糖為植株生長和葡萄成熟提供能量。","Sunlight lets the vine combine CO2 and water into sugars, which are its source of energy. In winter the vine is dormant because there is not enough heat, not because it uses sugar against frost. It has no need to attract insects, since it pollinates itself.":"陽光讓葡萄樹把 CO2 和水結合成糖，這是它的能量來源。葡萄樹冬天休眠是因為熱量不足，而不是因為用糖來抵抗霜凍。它也不需要吸引昆蟲，因為它會自花授粉。","How long can a vine live?":"葡萄樹可以活多久？","60 years or more":"60 年或更久","A single growing season":"只有一個生長季","About 5 years, then it must be replaced":"大約 5 年，之後就必須更換","No more than 15–20 years in most vineyards":"在多數葡萄園裡不超過 15–20 年","The vine is a long-lived plant that can live for 60 years or more, repeating the same cycle every year.":"葡萄樹是長壽的植物，可以活 60 年或更久，每年重複同樣的週期。","The vine is not an annual plant: each spring it starts again from the same trunk. This long life is what makes 'old vines' possible, prized for the quality of their grapes. The other lifespans offered are far too short.":"葡萄樹不是一年生植物：每年春天都從同一根主幹重新開始。正是這種長壽造就了備受珍視、葡萄品質出眾的「老藤」。其他選項的壽命都太短了。","Which description of the vine's yearly cycle is correct?":"下列哪一項對葡萄樹年度週期的描述是正確的？","Shoots and flowers in spring, ripe grapes by late summer, leaves dropping in autumn":"春天長出新梢和花朵，夏末葡萄成熟，秋天落葉","Flowers in winter, fruit in spring, dormancy in summer":"冬天開花，春天結果，夏天休眠","Leaves dropping in spring, flowers in summer and grapes ripe only in the middle of winter":"春天落葉，夏天開花，直到隆冬葡萄才成熟","Continuous growth all year, with no real pause":"全年持續生長，沒有真正的停頓","The growing season runs from spring to autumn; in winter the vine rests.":"生長季從春天持續到秋天；冬天葡萄樹休息。","In spring the vine grows shoots, leaves and flowers; by late summer the flowers have become ripe grapes. Leaf fall in autumn ends the season, and in winter the plant is dormant because it is too cold to grow. Year-round growth is therefore impossible.":"春天葡萄樹長出新梢、葉子和花朵；到了夏末，花朵已經變成成熟的葡萄。秋天落葉結束這一季，冬天植株因為太冷無法生長而休眠。所以全年生長是不可能的。","Riesling and Cabernet Sauvignon differ greatly in colour and flavour. What are they, botanically?":"麗絲玲和卡本內蘇維濃在顏色和風味上差異很大。從植物學上看，它們是什麼？","Two varieties of the same European species":"同一個歐洲物種的兩個品種","Two different species, one European and one American":"兩個不同物種，一個是歐洲種，一個是美洲種","Two wild species gathered in nature":"在野外採集的兩個野生物種","Two recent crosses between North American and Asian species":"北美與亞洲物種的兩個近期雜交種","Almost all wine comes from one European species, which exists in many different varieties.":"幾乎所有葡萄酒都來自同一個歐洲物種，它有許多不同的品種。","There are several vine species native to Eurasia or North America, but wine is almost always made from the European one. Its varieties differ in the look of the grapes, their taste and their flavours. Wine grapes are not gathered from the wild either: they are grown in carefully managed vineyards.":"原生於歐亞大陸或北美洲的葡萄屬物種有好幾種，但葡萄酒幾乎都是用歐洲種釀造的。它的各個品種在葡萄外觀、味道和風味上各不相同。釀酒葡萄也不是從野外採集的：它們種植在精心管理的葡萄園裡。","What does each cluster of vine flowers become?":"葡萄樹的每一串花會變成什麼？","A bunch of grapes":"一串葡萄","A new shoot for the following year":"來年的一根新梢","One single, very large grape":"一顆非常大的葡萄","A leaf, while the single flowers become grapes":"一片葉子，而單朵花才會變成葡萄","Each flower cluster becomes a bunch of grapes; each pollinated flower becomes one grape.":"每一串花會變成一串葡萄；每一朵授粉的花會變成一顆葡萄。","In spring the vine produces clusters of flowers. Each individual flower, once pollinated, grows seeds and swells into a grape, and together they form the bunch. That is why poor flowering directly reduces the crop.":"春天葡萄樹長出一串串花。每一朵花授粉後長出種子並膨大成一顆葡萄，合起來就成了一串葡萄。這就是為什麼開花不良會直接減少收成。","What is the correct order of the stages of grape formation?":"葡萄形成各階段的正確順序是什麼？","Flowering, fruit set, véraison, ripening":"開花、著果、轉色期、成熟","Fruit set, flowering, ripening, véraison":"著果、開花、成熟、轉色期","Flowering, véraison, fruit set, ripening":"開花、轉色期、著果、成熟","Véraison, flowering, ripening and finally fruit set":"轉色期、開花、成熟，最後著果","First the flower, then the green grape (fruit set), then the colour change (véraison) that starts ripening.":"先是花，然後是綠色的葡萄（著果），接著是開啟成熟的顏色變化（轉色期）。","The vine flowers in spring, and the pollinated flower becomes a small, hard, green grape. In mid-summer véraison marks the start of ripening, which continues until harvest. Véraison cannot come before fruit set: without a grape there is nothing to change colour.":"葡萄樹在春天開花，授粉的花變成一顆又小又硬的綠色葡萄。盛夏時，轉色期標誌著成熟的開始，成熟一直持續到採收。轉色期不可能在著果之前：沒有葡萄，就沒有東西可以變色。","What colour do white grapes turn at véraison?":"白葡萄在轉色期會變成什麼顏色？","Golden":"金黃色","Dark green":"深綠色","Brown, like a raisin":"像葡萄乾一樣的褐色","At véraison grapes lose their green: white grapes turn golden, black grapes red and then purple.":"轉色期時葡萄褪去綠色：白葡萄轉為金黃色，黑葡萄先變紅再變紫。","Véraison happens in mid-summer and marks the start of ripening. The red-then-purple change applies to black grapes, not white ones. A brown, shrivelled look only appears much later, if grapes stay on the vine until they turn into raisins.":"轉色期發生在盛夏，標誌著成熟的開始。先紅後紫的變化是黑葡萄的，不是白葡萄的。褐色、乾縮的外觀要晚得多才會出現，只有當葡萄留在樹上直到變成葡萄乾時才會這樣。","At the start of ripening, what is a grape like?":"成熟剛開始時，葡萄是什麼樣子？","Very acidic, with hardly any sugar and a herbaceous taste":"非常酸，幾乎沒有糖分，帶有草本味道","Sweet, low in acid, with tropical fruit aromas":"甜、低酸，帶有熱帶水果香氣","Soft and juicy, already showing its signature aromas":"柔軟多汁，已經展現出招牌香氣","High in sugar, but with tannins still unripe in the pulp":"糖分高，但果肉中的單寧仍未成熟","Before ripening, the grape is very acidic, low in sugar and has an unattractive herbaceous taste.":"成熟之前，葡萄非常酸、糖分低，還帶有不討喜的草本味道。","During ripening the grape swells with water and softens, acidity falls, sugar rises and herbaceous notes give way to the variety's signature aromas. Sweetness and tropical fruit therefore belong to a ripe grape, not the start of ripening. Tannins, meanwhile, are in the skin, not the pulp.":"成熟過程中，葡萄吸水膨大並變軟，酸度下降，糖分上升，草本氣息讓位給品種的招牌香氣。所以甜味和熱帶水果屬於成熟的葡萄，而不是成熟剛開始時。至於單寧，它存在於果皮，而不是果肉。","As a black grape ripens, how do its aromas change?":"黑葡萄成熟時，香氣如何變化？","From tropical fruit to green fruit":"從熱帶水果到綠色水果","From cooked fruit to fresh fruit":"從煮熟的水果到新鮮水果","From vanilla and coconut to crunchy red fruit":"從香草和椰子到爽脆的紅色水果","In black grapes, rising ripeness moves the flavours from fresh fruit towards cooked fruit.":"對黑葡萄來說，成熟度提高會讓風味從新鮮水果轉向煮熟的水果。","The green-to-stone-to-tropical sequence applies to some white grapes, and runs in that direction, not the reverse. Vanilla and coconut come from new oak, not from the grape. For black grapes, the marker is the move from fresh to cooked fruit.":"綠色水果到核果再到熱帶水果的順序適用於某些白葡萄，而且是這個方向，不是相反。香草和椰子來自新橡木桶，不是來自葡萄。對黑葡萄來說，指標是從新鮮水果轉向煮熟的水果。","What do tannins contribute to a red wine?":"單寧為紅酒帶來什麼？","To its mouthfeel":"口感","To its red colour, which comes entirely from the tannins in the seeds":"紅色，完全來自葡萄籽中的單寧","To its sweetness":"甜味","To its alcohol level":"酒精濃度","Tannins from black grape skins give red wines their mouthfeel.":"來自黑葡萄果皮的單寧賦予紅酒口感。","Tannins are compounds in the skins of black grapes (and also in seeds and stems), and they ripen during the ripening period. Colour comes from skin pigments, not seeds. Sweetness and alcohol depend on sugar, not on tannin.":"單寧是存在於黑葡萄果皮（以及葡萄籽和果梗）中的化合物，會在成熟期間逐漸成熟。顏色來自果皮的色素，不是葡萄籽。甜味和酒精取決於糖分，與單寧無關。","Why does a grape left on the vine until it shrivels have more concentrated sugars and acids?":"為什麼留在樹上直到乾縮的葡萄，糖和酸會更濃縮？","Because the water in the grape evaporates":"因為葡萄中的水分蒸發了","Because a fungus pierces the skin":"因為真菌刺穿了果皮","Because the water freezes inside the grape":"因為葡萄裡的水結冰了","Because the vine keeps pumping sugar and acid into the grapes even after its leaves have fallen":"因為即使葉子掉光，葡萄樹仍持續把糖和酸送進葡萄","With a long hang time the water evaporates and the grape becomes a raisin, concentrating sugars and acids.":"長時間掛在樹上，水分蒸發，葡萄變成葡萄乾，糖和酸隨之濃縮。","This is raisining on the vine, which also brings dried-fruit aromas. The fungus that pierces the skin is Botrytis (noble rot) and freezing the water is how icewine is made: two other ways of concentrating sugar. A vine with no leaves can no longer make sugar by photosynthesis.":"這就是在樹上風乾成葡萄乾，同時也會帶來乾果香氣。刺穿果皮的真菌是貴腐菌（Botrytis），而讓水結冰是冰酒的釀造方式：這是另外兩種濃縮糖分的方法。沒有葉子的葡萄樹已經無法透過光合作用製造糖。","In the early stages of extra-ripeness, what happens to the grapes?":"在過熟的初期，葡萄會發生什麼？","They develop exaggerated ripe aromas and build up more sugar":"發展出誇張的成熟香氣，累積更多糖分","They lose sugar and regain herbaceous notes":"失去糖分，重新出現草本氣息","They shrivel at once and taste of dried fruit":"立刻乾縮，嚐起來有乾果味","They turn green and hard again, as just after fruit set":"重新變綠變硬，就像剛著果時一樣","Early extra-ripeness exaggerates ripe aromas and increases sugar; shrivelling only comes later.":"過熟初期會放大成熟香氣並提高糖分；乾縮要晚一點才會出現。","If grapes stay on the vine past the normal harvest, in dry and warm enough weather, they keep developing. Only after a longer period does water evaporate, the grapes shrivel and dried-fruit notes appear. Herbaceous notes belong to unripe grapes.":"如果葡萄在正常採收期之後仍留在樹上，而天氣夠乾燥、夠溫暖，它們會繼續發展。要再過較長一段時間，水分才會蒸發，葡萄乾縮，出現乾果氣息。草本氣息則屬於未成熟的葡萄。","Where in the grape are flavours most concentrated?":"葡萄的風味最集中在哪裡？","In the skin and just beneath it":"果皮及其正下方","In the seeds":"葡萄籽","In the stem holding the bunch":"支撐果串的果梗","At the centre of the pulp, far from the skin, where there is most water":"果肉中心，遠離果皮、水分最多的地方","The skin and the area immediately below it hold high levels of flavour.":"果皮及其正下方的區域含有大量風味物質。","The pulp also contains acids and flavours, but it is mostly water and sugar. Seeds and stems are known for tannins, which can turn bitter if handled roughly. This is why contact with the skins matters so much to a wine's flavour.":"果肉也含有酸和風味物質，但主要是水和糖。葡萄籽和果梗以單寧著稱，處理粗暴時可能變苦。這就是為什麼與果皮的接觸對葡萄酒的風味如此重要。","Which parts of the grape and bunch contain tannins?":"葡萄和果串的哪些部位含有單寧？","Skins, seeds and stems":"果皮、葡萄籽和果梗","Only the pulp":"只有果肉","Pulp and juice, but never the skin or seeds":"果肉和果汁，但絕不在果皮或葡萄籽中","Only the stems":"只有果梗","Tannins are in the skins, especially of black grapes, and at high levels in seeds and stems.":"單寧存在於果皮中（尤其是黑葡萄），在葡萄籽和果梗中的含量也很高。","The pulp is mainly water, sugar, acids and flavours, not tannin. Tannins from black skins give red wines their structure, while those from seeds and stems can make wine bitter if crushed roughly. That is why winemakers handle them gently.":"果肉主要是水、糖、酸和風味物質，不是單寧。黑葡萄果皮的單寧賦予紅酒結構，而葡萄籽和果梗的單寧若被粗暴壓碎，可能讓酒變苦。所以釀酒師會輕柔地處理它們。","Climate is the long-term average, weather is what happens day to day":"氣候是長期平均，天氣是每天發生的狀況","Climate changes every year, weather stays stable for decades":"氣候每年都在變，天氣則數十年保持穩定","Climate covers only rainfall, weather only temperature":"氣候只涵蓋降雨，天氣只涵蓋溫度","Climate refers to one vineyard, weather to a whole country":"氣候指的是一座葡萄園，天氣指的是整個國家","Climate is the long-term average pattern; weather is what actually happens each day.":"氣候是長期的平均模式；天氣是每天實際發生的狀況。","Climate describes the average levels of temperature, sunlight and rainfall a region can expect; it does not change from year to year, though it can shift over decades. Weather is what actually happens day to day: cool or hot vintages, frost, hail and sudden downpours are all matters of weather.":"氣候描述的是一個產區可預期的平均溫度、日照和降雨水準；它不會年年改變，但可能在數十年間轉變。天氣則是每天實際發生的事：涼爽或炎熱的年份、霜凍、冰雹和突如其來的大雨，都屬於天氣。","A region has an average growing season temperature of 15.5°C. How is its climate classified?":"某產區生長季的平均溫度為 15.5°C。它的氣候屬於哪一類？","An average growing season temperature of 16.5°C or below counts as cool.":"生長季平均溫度在 16.5°C 以下屬於涼爽氣候。","The three bands used are: cool, 16.5°C (62°F) or below; moderate, 16.5 to 18.5°C (62 to 65°F); warm, 18.5 to 21°C (65 to 70°F). At 15.5°C the region is below the 16.5°C threshold, so its climate is cool. Such a climate tends to give grapes with higher acidity and less-ripe flavours.":"使用的三個區間是：涼爽，16.5°C（62°F）以下；溫和，16.5 至 18.5°C（62 至 65°F）；溫暖，18.5 至 21°C（65 至 70°F）。15.5°C 低於 16.5°C 的門檻，所以這個產區屬於涼爽氣候。這樣的氣候往往讓葡萄酸度較高、風味較不成熟。","When does the growing season run in the southern hemisphere?":"南半球的生長季在什麼時候？","January to June":"1 月到 6 月","July to December":"7 月到 12 月","In the southern hemisphere the season runs October to April, the reverse of the north.":"南半球的生長季是 10 月到 4 月，與北半球相反。","Seasons are reversed between the two hemispheres. In the northern hemisphere the growing season runs from April to October; in the southern hemisphere from October to April. That is why the Australian harvest happens early in the calendar year, while California's comes towards the end.":"南北半球的季節相反。北半球的生長季從 4 月到 10 月；南半球則從 10 月到 4 月。這就是為什麼澳洲在年初採收，而加州的採收接近年底。","Which grape is given as an example of a variety that only ripens well in warm climates?":"哪個品種被舉例為只有在溫暖氣候才能好好成熟的品種？","Grenache can only grow and ripen successfully in warm climates.":"格那希只能在溫暖氣候中順利生長和成熟。","Temperature decides which varieties can grow in a region. Grenache is the example of a grape that needs a warm climate to ripen. Chardonnay is the opposite example: it grows well in a range of climates but develops different flavours depending on the heat available.":"溫度決定了一個產區能種哪些品種。格那希是需要溫暖氣候才能成熟的例子。夏多內則是相反的例子：它在各種氣候中都長得很好，但會依可得的熱量發展出不同的風味。","What is the most important factor influencing a wine region's climate?":"影響葡萄酒產區氣候最重要的因素是什麼？","Soil type":"土壤類型","Nearness to a river":"鄰近河流","Slope aspect":"坡向","Latitude is the main factor: the closer to the equator, the hotter.":"緯度是主要因素：越接近赤道越熱。","The closer a region is to the equator, the hotter it tends to be. That is why most vineyards lie between 30° and 50° north or south: outside this band it is usually too hot or too cold. Soil, rivers and aspect can then modify the climate of an area or a single vineyard.":"產區越接近赤道，往往越熱。這就是為什麼大多數葡萄園位於南北緯 30° 到 50° 之間：在這個範圍之外通常太熱或太冷。土壤、河流和坡向則可以調節一個地區或單一葡萄園的氣候。","Between which latitudes are most vineyards found?":"大多數葡萄園位於哪兩個緯度之間？","Between 30° and 50° north or south":"南北緯 30° 到 50° 之間","Between 10° and 30° north or south":"南北緯 10° 到 30° 之間","Between 40° and 60° north or south":"南北緯 40° 到 60° 之間","Between 0° and 20° north or south":"南北緯 0° 到 20° 之間","Nearly all vineyards lie between 30° and 50° latitude in both hemispheres.":"幾乎所有葡萄園都位於南北半球緯度 30° 到 50° 之間。","The band between 30° and 50° latitude, north and south of the equator, offers temperatures suited to vines. Closer to the equator it is usually too hot, and further away too cold, for vines to survive. Within the band, altitude, seas, mountains and aspect fine-tune the local climate.":"赤道南北緯度 30° 到 50° 之間的地帶，提供了適合葡萄樹的溫度。越接近赤道通常太熱，越遠離則太冷，葡萄樹難以存活。在這個地帶內，海拔、海洋、山脈和坡向會微調當地氣候。","Two vineyards are at the same latitude, but one is much higher. What should you expect of the higher vineyard?":"兩座葡萄園位於同一緯度，但其中一座海拔高得多。你可以預期海拔較高的葡萄園會怎樣？","A cooler climate":"氣候較涼爽","A warmer climate":"氣候較溫暖","The same climate":"氣候相同","More summer rain":"夏季雨量較多","Temperature drops with altitude, so the higher vineyard is cooler.":"溫度隨海拔升高而下降，所以海拔較高的葡萄園較涼爽。","At the same latitude, a higher vineyard always has a cooler climate. This slows ripening: grapes tend to keep more acidity and build up sugar more slowly. Altitude is therefore a way to make fresher wines even in regions that would be warm because of their latitude.":"在同一緯度上，海拔較高的葡萄園氣候一定較涼爽。這會減緩成熟：葡萄往往保留較多酸度，糖分累積也較慢。因此，即使在因緯度而偏溫暖的產區，海拔也是釀出較清爽葡萄酒的一種方式。","Why does a vineyard on a slope facing the equator produce riper grapes?":"為什麼面向赤道的坡地葡萄園能產出較成熟的葡萄？","It receives more heat and light":"它接收到更多熱量和光照","It receives more rain":"它接收到更多雨水","It has more nutrient-rich soils":"它的土壤養分更豐富","It is more exposed to fog":"它更容易受霧氣影響","A slope facing the equator gets more heat and light, so grapes ripen more.":"面向赤道的坡地接收到更多熱量和光照，所以葡萄更成熟。","Far from the equator, light and heat are scarce and ripening grapes is hard. Planting on a slope facing the equator increases the heat and light reaching the vines. The result is riper grapes than those from a vineyard on flat land or on a slope facing the other way.":"在遠離赤道的地方，光照和熱量都很稀少，葡萄很難成熟。種在面向赤道的坡地上，可以增加葡萄樹接收到的熱量和光照。結果是葡萄比平地或背向坡地的葡萄園更成熟。","What effect do cold ocean currents have on the vineyards of the Cape in South Africa?":"寒冷洋流對南非 Cape 產區的葡萄園有什麼影響？","They cool a warm climate":"為溫暖的氣候降溫","They warm a cool climate":"讓涼爽的氣候變暖","They increase summer rainfall":"增加夏季降雨","They encourage noble rot":"促進貴腐菌生長","Cold currents moderate the Cape's warm climate by cooling it.":"寒冷洋流讓 Cape 溫暖的氣候變得涼爽而溫和。","Warm regions close to the sea can benefit from a moderating influence. In the Cape's grape-growing areas, the climate is cooled by cold ocean currents. The opposite happens in northern Europe, where warm currents warm the vineyards. Breezes blowing in from cold seas also cool coastal areas.":"靠近海洋的溫暖產區可以受益於海洋的調節作用。在 Cape 的葡萄種植區，氣候受到寒冷洋流的冷卻。北歐則相反，溫暖的洋流讓葡萄園變暖。從寒冷海面吹來的微風也會讓沿海地區降溫。","In a cool region, how does a river near the vineyard help?":"在涼爽產區，葡萄園附近的河流有什麼幫助？","It gives warmth, protects from frost and extends ripening":"提供溫暖、防止霜害並延長成熟期","It cools the vineyard and lowers sugar levels":"讓葡萄園降溫並降低糖分","It blocks light and slows photosynthesis":"遮擋光線並減緩光合作用","It shelters the vineyard from cloud and rain":"為葡萄園遮擋雲層和雨水","Rivers hold warmth in autumn, protect against frost and extend the ripening period.":"河流在秋天保有溫暖，防止霜害並延長成熟期。","Rivers warm up and cool down more slowly than land, so in autumn they are warmer than the ground around them. In cool regions they provide warmth, help prevent frost and extend the period warm enough to ripen grapes. They also reflect sunlight. Sheltering vineyards from cloud and rain is the role of mountains, not rivers.":"河流升溫和降溫都比陸地慢，所以秋天時比周圍的土地溫暖。在涼爽產區，河流提供溫暖，有助於防止霜害，並延長足以讓葡萄成熟的溫暖期。河流也會反射陽光。為葡萄園遮擋雲層和雨水是山脈的作用，不是河流。","In which areas is fog an important cooling influence?":"霧氣在哪些地區是重要的降溫因素？","Coastal California and Chile":"加州和智利的沿海地區","Warm regions of Australia":"澳洲的溫暖產區","The Cape regions of South Africa":"南非的 Cape 產區","Northern European vineyards":"北歐的葡萄園","Fog forms at ground level and cools coastal California and Chile.":"霧氣在地面形成，讓加州和智利的沿海地區降溫。","Fog is water vapour that forms at ground level and cools the vineyard; it is a very important moderating influence in coastal California and Chile. In some warmer Australian regions, cloud cover matters instead by reducing sunlight, while at the Cape the key factor is cold ocean currents.":"霧是在地面形成的水氣，會讓葡萄園降溫；它在加州和智利沿海地區是非常重要的調節因素。在澳洲某些較溫暖的產區，重要的反而是減少日照的雲層，而在 Cape，關鍵因素是寒冷洋流。","How can stones on the soil surface help ripening?":"土壤表面的石頭如何幫助成熟？","They absorb heat and warm the vineyard":"吸收熱量，讓葡萄園變暖","They hold more water for the vine":"為葡萄樹保存更多水分","They add nutrients to the soil":"為土壤增添養分","They shelter the vines from wind":"為葡萄樹擋風","Stones absorb heat and make the vineyard warmer, which helps ripening.":"石頭吸收熱量讓葡萄園變暖，有助於成熟。","Soil supplies water and nutrients, but it can also affect vineyard temperature. When the surface is covered in stones, they absorb heat and make the vineyard warmer. That extra heat can help grapes ripen, which is especially useful where the climate struggles to deliver full ripeness.":"土壤提供水和養分，但也可能影響葡萄園的溫度。當地表覆蓋著石頭時，石頭會吸收熱量，讓葡萄園變暖。這些額外的熱量有助於葡萄成熟，在氣候難以讓葡萄完全成熟的地方特別有用。","What typically happens to grapes in a cooler-than-normal vintage?":"在比平常涼爽的年份，葡萄通常會怎樣？","Acidity too high and sugar too low":"酸度太高，糖分太低","Acidity too low and sugar too high":"酸度太低，糖分太高","Dried-fruit aromas and sunburn":"乾果香氣和日灼","Swollen grapes with diluted flavours":"葡萄膨脹，風味被稀釋","With little heat and light, grapes struggle to ripen and stay acidic and low in sugar.":"熱量和光照不足時，葡萄難以成熟，維持高酸低糖。","In a cool vintage temperatures are lower and sunlight less bright than usual, so the vine struggles to ripen its grapes. Acidity stays too high, sugar too low and the variety's signature aromas may not develop. Dried-fruit aromas and sunburn point instead to a very hot vintage.":"在涼爽的年份，溫度比平常低、陽光也不如平常強，葡萄樹難以讓葡萄成熟。酸度維持太高，糖分太低，品種的招牌香氣也可能發展不出來。乾果香氣和日灼則指向非常炎熱的年份。","Why can heavy rain just before harvest reduce grape quality?":"為什麼採收前的大雨會降低葡萄品質？","Grapes swell with water and flavours are diluted":"葡萄吸水膨脹，風味被稀釋","Grapes dry out and turn into raisins":"葡萄乾掉變成葡萄乾","The skins become too dark":"果皮變得太深色","The vine immediately goes dormant":"葡萄樹立刻進入休眠","Excess water in the soil makes the grapes swell, diluting their flavours.":"土壤中過多的水分讓葡萄膨脹，稀釋了風味。","Heavy rain causes two problems. The moisture helps fungal diseases spread, which can reduce both the quantity and quality of grapes. And if heavy rain falls close to harvest, the excess water in the soil makes the grapes swell and dilutes their flavours, so the wine may be less concentrated.":"大雨會造成兩個問題。濕氣助長真菌病害蔓延，可能同時降低葡萄的產量和品質。而如果大雨落在採收前不久，土壤中過多的水分會讓葡萄膨脹、稀釋風味，酒就可能比較不濃郁。","Why are spring frosts particularly dangerous for vines?":"為什麼春霜對葡萄樹特別危險？","They damage new growth and reduce the crop":"它會損害新生枝葉，減少收成","They shrivel grapes that are already ripe":"它會讓已經成熟的葡萄乾縮","They dilute the flavours of the grapes":"它會稀釋葡萄的風味","They cause sunburn on the skins":"它會讓果皮日灼","In spring, frost kills new shoots, so there will be fewer bunches.":"春天的霜凍會凍死新梢，所以果串會變少。","In spring the vine is producing shoots, leaves and flowers. A frost at this point can damage or kill the new growth, reducing the number of bunches the plant can carry that year. The result is a smaller crop. Hail also cuts yields, but by striking vines and grapes at any point in the season.":"春天葡萄樹正在長出新梢、葉子和花朵。這時的霜凍可能損害甚至凍死新生枝葉，減少植株當年能承載的果串數量。結果就是收成變少。冰雹也會降低產量，但它是在生長季的任何時候打傷葡萄樹和葡萄。","Which months does the growing season cover in the northern hemisphere?":"北半球的生長季涵蓋哪幾個月？","All year round, without a break":"全年無休","In the northern hemisphere the season runs April to October; in the southern, October to April.":"北半球的生長季是 4 月到 10 月；南半球是 10 月到 4 月。","The seasons are reversed between the hemispheres, and so is the growing season. October to April is the southern calendar, for example in Australia or Chile. The vine is dormant in winter, so it does not grow all year.":"南北半球的季節相反，生長季也是如此。10 月到 4 月是南半球的時間表，例如澳洲或智利。葡萄樹冬天休眠，所以不會全年生長。","A region has an average growing season temperature of 17.5°C. How is its climate classified?":"某產區生長季的平均溫度為 17.5°C。它的氣候屬於哪一類？","Too cold to ripen any grape variety":"太冷，任何葡萄品種都無法成熟","An average between 16.5°C and 18.5°C means a moderate climate.":"平均溫度介於 16.5°C 與 18.5°C 之間屬於溫和氣候。","Cool means 16.5°C or below, warm 18.5°C to 21°C. At 17.5°C the region sits in between. A moderate climate ripens many varieties, so the last option is wrong.":"涼爽是指 16.5°C 以下，溫暖是 18.5°C 至 21°C。17.5°C 的產區介於兩者之間。溫和氣候能讓許多品種成熟，所以最後一個選項是錯的。","Why is Chardonnay given as an example when discussing climate?":"討論氣候時，為什麼會以夏多內為例？","It grows well in different climates, but its flavours change with climate":"它在不同氣候中都長得好，但風味會隨氣候改變","It only ripens in warm climates":"它只在溫暖氣候中成熟","It tastes the same wherever it is grown":"無論種在哪裡，嚐起來都一樣","It can only be grown in cool climates, near rivers or the sea":"它只能種在涼爽氣候、靠近河流或海洋的地方","Chardonnay adapts to many climates, but develops different flavours depending on temperature.":"夏多內能適應多種氣候，但會依溫度發展出不同的風味。","Temperature decides both which varieties can grow and which flavours they develop. Grenache is the example of a variety that only ripens in warm climates. Chardonnay, by contrast, grows in cool, moderate and warm climates with different flavour profiles.":"溫度既決定哪些品種能種植，也決定它們發展出什麼風味。格那希是只在溫暖氣候中成熟的品種的例子。相反地，夏多內在涼爽、溫和和溫暖氣候中都能生長，風味特徵各不相同。","What effect do warm ocean currents have on the vineyards of northern Europe?":"溫暖洋流對北歐的葡萄園有什麼影響？","They warm them":"讓它們變暖","They cool them":"讓它們降溫","They bring fogs that encourage noble rot every vintage":"每個年份都帶來助長貴腐菌的霧氣","They have no effect":"沒有影響","In northern Europe, warm ocean currents have a warming influence on the climate.":"在北歐，溫暖洋流對氣候有增溫作用。","The sea moderates climate both ways. In South Africa's Cape, cold currents cool a warm climate; in northern Europe, warm currents help a cold one. The morning mists linked to noble rot come mainly from rivers in autumn.":"海洋對氣候的調節是雙向的。在南非的 Cape，寒冷洋流讓溫暖的氣候降溫；在北歐，溫暖洋流則幫助寒冷的氣候。與貴腐菌相關的晨霧主要來自秋天的河流。","How can mountains cool a warm vineyard lower down at night?":"山脈如何在夜間讓低處溫暖的葡萄園降溫？","Cold air flows down from the mountains to lower altitudes":"冷空氣從山上流向較低的海拔","They block warm ocean currents":"它們阻擋溫暖洋流","They shade the vineyard all night":"它們整晚為葡萄園遮蔭","They hold clouds over the vineyard and stop heat escaping":"它們把雲留在葡萄園上方，阻止熱量散失","At night cold mountain air moves downhill and cools vineyards where heat built up during the day.":"夜間，山上的冷空氣往下坡移動，讓白天累積熱量的葡萄園降溫。","Cool air, whether from the sea or mountains, moderates the climate. Shade means nothing at night, as the sun has already set. If anything, mountains shelter vineyards from cloud, rain and cold winds; they do not trap clouds over them.":"無論來自海洋還是山脈，涼爽的空氣都能調節氣候。遮蔭在夜間沒有意義，因為太陽已經下山了。山脈頂多是為葡萄園遮擋雲層、雨水和冷風，而不是把雲困在葡萄園上方。","A vineyard is sheltered by a mountain range. Which conditions is it most likely to enjoy?":"一座葡萄園受到山脈的屏障。它最可能享有哪些條件？","Sunny summers, dry autumns and a longer growing season":"陽光充足的夏天、乾燥的秋天和較長的生長季","More rain and more cloud":"更多雨水和雲層","Thick fog every summer morning":"每個夏日清晨都有濃霧","Constant cold winds that shorten ripening in autumn":"持續的冷風，縮短秋天的成熟期","Mountains act as a barrier to cloud, rain and cold winds, extending the season.":"山脈是阻擋雲、雨和冷風的屏障，能延長生長季。","Because they block cloud and rain, mountains bring sunny summers and dry autumns. Shelter from cold winds lets grapes ripen for longer, not shorter. Thick fogs are typical of some coastal areas, such as California and Chile.":"由於阻擋了雲和雨，山脈帶來陽光充足的夏天和乾燥的秋天。擋住冷風能讓葡萄成熟得更久，而不是更短。濃霧則是某些沿海地區的典型現象，例如加州和智利。","How can cloud slow down ripening in some warm Australian regions?":"在澳洲某些溫暖產區，雲層如何減緩成熟？","They block sunlight and slow photosynthesis":"它們遮擋陽光，減緩光合作用","They form at ground level and chill the roots":"它們在地面形成，讓根部受寒","They always bring hail, which reduces the crop":"它們總是帶來冰雹，減少收成","They raise humidity and encourage noble rot on the grapes every year":"它們提高濕度，每年都讓葡萄長出貴腐菌","Clouds form above ground and block the sun: less photosynthesis, slower ripening.":"雲在地面上方形成並遮住太陽：光合作用減少，成熟變慢。","This is an important moderating factor in some warm Australian regions. What forms at ground level is fog, not cloud. Noble rot needs morning mists followed by warm, dry afternoons instead.":"這是澳洲某些溫暖產區重要的調節因素。在地面形成的是霧，不是雲。貴腐菌需要的則是晨霧，加上溫暖乾燥的午後。","Which form of water vapour is essential for noble rot to develop?":"哪種形式的水氣對貴腐菌的發展不可或缺？","Autumn morning mists near rivers":"秋天清晨河流附近的薄霧","Low summer clouds that hide the sun for weeks":"連續數週遮住太陽的夏季低雲","Coastal Californian fog":"加州沿海的霧","Spring rain":"春雨","Mists rising from rivers on autumn mornings let the fungus develop.":"秋天早晨從河流升起的薄霧讓這種真菌得以發展。","Mist is a less dense form of fog. It must reach grapes that are already ripe, so in autumn, not spring. Coastal Californian fog mainly cools vineyards, while clouds block light and slow ripening.":"薄霧是比霧稀薄的形式。它必須接觸到已經成熟的葡萄，所以是在秋天，而不是春天。加州沿海的霧主要讓葡萄園降溫，而雲層則遮擋光線、減緩成熟。","Besides giving warmth in autumn, how else can a river help ripening far from the equator?":"在遠離赤道的地方，河流除了在秋天提供溫暖，還能以什麼方式幫助成熟？","It reflects sunlight onto the vines":"把陽光反射到葡萄樹上","It supplies nutrients to the leaves":"為葉片提供養分","It cools summers that are too hot":"讓過熱的夏天降溫","It prevents any mist from forming, so avoiding fungal disease":"阻止任何薄霧形成，從而避免真菌病害","The water's surface reflects light, which helps where sun and heat are scarce.":"水面反射光線，在陽光和熱量稀少的地方很有幫助。","Rivers warm up and cool down more slowly than land: in autumn they stay warmer, protect against frost and extend ripening. They do not feed the leaves, which take CO2 from the air. And river mists are exactly what encourages noble rot.":"河流升溫和降溫都比陸地慢：秋天時保持較溫暖，防止霜害並延長成熟期。它們不會餵養葉片，葉片是從空氣中吸收 CO2 的。而河流的薄霧正是助長貴腐菌的因素。","What is the soil's main role for the vine?":"土壤對葡萄樹的主要作用是什麼？","To supply water and nutrients":"提供水和養分","To supply carbon dioxide for photosynthesis":"為光合作用提供二氧化碳","To pollinate the flowers in spring":"在春天為花朵授粉","To protect the bunches from hail and birds during summer":"在夏天保護果串免受冰雹和鳥害","The soil must store enough water and nutrients to keep the vine healthy.":"土壤必須儲存足夠的水和養分，讓葡萄樹保持健康。","CO2 comes from the air through the leaves, not from the soil. Soil can also affect temperature: stones on the surface absorb heat and warm the vineyard. Against hail and birds, growers use nets, not soil.":"CO2 是透過葉片從空氣中取得的，不是來自土壤。土壤也可能影響溫度：地表的石頭吸收熱量，讓葡萄園變暖。對付冰雹和鳥類，種植者用的是網子，不是土壤。","A very hot, bright vintage: what risk do the grapes face?":"一個非常炎熱、陽光充足的年份：葡萄面臨什麼風險？","Untypical dried-fruit aromas and sunburn":"不典型的乾果香氣和日灼","Swollen grapes and diluted flavours":"葡萄膨脹，風味被稀釋","Strong herbaceous notes, as in grapes picked too early":"強烈的草本氣息，就像太早採收的葡萄","Excess heat and light can give untypical dried-fruit aromas and sunburn the grapes.":"過多的熱量和光照可能帶來不典型的乾果香氣，並讓葡萄日灼。","High acidity, little sugar and herbaceous notes are cool-vintage problems. Swollen grapes and diluted flavours come from heavy rain close to harvest. In extreme heat and drought, the vine may even shut down and fail to ripen its grapes.":"高酸、低糖和草本氣息是涼爽年份的問題。葡萄膨脹、風味稀釋則是採收前大雨造成的。在極端炎熱和乾旱下，葡萄樹甚至可能停止運作，無法讓葡萄成熟。","Why may grapes fail to ripen in a very hot summer with no rain?":"為什麼在非常炎熱又不下雨的夏天，葡萄可能無法成熟？","Short of water, the vine shuts down to protect itself":"缺水時，葡萄樹會停止運作以保護自己","The heat kills the yeasts on the skins and stops photosynthesis":"高溫殺死果皮上的酵母並中止光合作用","The grapes take up too much water from the roots":"葡萄從根部吸收了太多水","The leaves fall straight after flowering":"葉子在開花後立刻掉落","Heat increases the vine's need for water; without it, the vine shuts down and the grapes stop developing.":"高溫增加葡萄樹對水的需求；缺水時，葡萄樹停止運作，葡萄也停止發育。","High temperatures usually come with little rain, and in the worst cases the vine can die. Irrigation helps, but in these conditions there is often no water to use. Yeasts belong to fermentation in the winery, not ripening in the vineyard.":"高溫通常伴隨著少雨，最嚴重時葡萄樹可能死亡。灌溉有幫助，但在這種情況下往往無水可用。酵母屬於酒廠裡的發酵，不屬於葡萄園裡的成熟。","What causes drought?":"乾旱是什麼造成的？","Long periods of below-average rainfall, often made worse by heat":"長期降雨低於平均，常因高溫而更加嚴重","A single spring frost":"一次春霜","Too much irrigation":"過度灌溉","Coastal fog":"沿海的霧","Drought comes from prolonged low rainfall and worsens with above-average temperatures.":"乾旱來自長期的低降雨量，在溫度高於平均時會更嚴重。","In drought the vine cannot ripen its grapes and at worst it dies. Irrigation can help, but water is not always available. Frost damages new shoots and fog cools: neither causes drought.":"乾旱時葡萄樹無法讓葡萄成熟，最嚴重時會死亡。灌溉有幫助，但不一定有水可用。霜凍損害新梢，霧氣則帶來涼爽：兩者都不會造成乾旱。","What is the worst damage a heavy hailstorm can cause?":"一場猛烈的冰雹最嚴重會造成什麼損害？","Destroying the whole year's crop":"摧毀整年的收成","Slightly diluting the grapes' flavours":"輕微稀釋葡萄的風味","Starting noble rot on the ripe grapes":"讓成熟的葡萄開始長出貴腐菌","Delaying véraison by a few days with no effect on quality":"讓轉色期延後幾天，對品質沒有影響","Hail can badly damage vines and grapes, even wiping out the entire annual crop.":"冰雹可能嚴重損害葡萄樹和葡萄，甚至讓整年的收成化為烏有。","That is why, in some areas such as Argentina, growers stretch hail nets over the rows. Diluted flavours come from rain close to harvest. Noble rot needs morning mists and dry afternoons, not hail.":"所以在某些地區，例如阿根廷，種植者會在葡萄樹行上方架設防雹網。風味稀釋來自採收前的降雨。貴腐菌需要的是晨霧和乾燥的午後，而不是冰雹。","Why does a very wet season worry a grower even well before harvest?":"為什麼非常潮濕的季節，即使離採收還很久，也讓種植者擔心？","Moisture helps fungal diseases spread":"濕氣助長真菌病害蔓延","Rain stops photosynthesis for the whole summer":"下雨讓光合作用整個夏天都停止","Rain always increases the grapes' sugar":"下雨總是會提高葡萄的糖分","Rainwater stops the roots taking up any nutrients from the soil":"雨水讓根部無法從土壤吸收任何養分","High moisture helps fungi spread on leaves and grapes.":"高濕度助長真菌在葉片和葡萄上蔓延。","Fungal diseases reduce both the quality and the quantity of grapes. Close to harvest, rain also swells the grapes and dilutes flavours. Rain does not raise sugar; if anything, it dilutes it.":"真菌病害會同時降低葡萄的品質和產量。接近採收時，下雨還會讓葡萄膨脹、稀釋風味。下雨不會提高糖分；如果有影響，也是稀釋糖分。","Which statement about climate change and grape growing is correct?":"關於氣候變遷與葡萄種植，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","Average temperatures are rising and extreme events are more frequent":"平均溫度正在上升，極端事件也更加頻繁","Climate changes completely from one year to the next":"氣候每年都會徹底改變","It only affects air temperatures, not ocean temperatures":"它只影響氣溫，不影響海洋溫度","No producers or industry bodies are yet taking action to adapt":"還沒有任何生產者或產業組織採取調適行動","Records show a sustained rise in air and ocean temperatures, with more droughts and floods.":"紀錄顯示氣溫和海洋溫度持續上升，乾旱和洪水也變多了。","Climate does not change from year to year, but it can shift over decades; it is weather that varies each year. A growing number of producers and industry bodies are already acting to adapt and mitigate. The rise affects both air and oceans.":"氣候不會年年改變，但可能在數十年間轉變；每年變化的是天氣。越來越多生產者和產業組織已經採取行動，進行調適和減緩。溫度上升同時影響空氣和海洋。","When are vines usually pruned?":"葡萄樹通常在什麼時候修剪？","In winter, while the vine is dormant":"冬天，葡萄樹休眠時","In spring, during flowering":"春天，開花期間","In summer, at véraison":"夏天，轉色期時","In autumn, just before harvest":"秋天，就在採收前","Pruning is done in winter, when the vine is dormant, to keep its shape.":"修剪在冬天葡萄樹休眠時進行，以維持樹形。","Training and pruning ensure a healthy, commercially viable crop each year. Pruning is generally done in winter, when the vine is dormant and not growing, and it keeps each vine in its required shape. In spring and summer the plant is busy growing and then ripening its grapes.":"整枝和修剪能確保每年都有健康、具商業價值的收成。修剪一般在冬天進行，這時葡萄樹休眠、不生長，修剪能讓每株葡萄樹維持所需的樹形。春天和夏天，植株正忙著生長和讓葡萄成熟。","What are most vines trained on?":"大多數葡萄樹以什麼來整枝？","Trellises":"棚架","Trees":"樹木","Stone walls":"石牆","Hail nets":"防雹網","Most vines are trained on trellises of posts and wires.":"大多數葡萄樹以立柱和鐵絲組成的棚架來整枝。","Training gives the vine its shape and, together with pruning, helps produce a regular, healthy crop. In the vast majority of cases vines are supported by trellises of posts and wires. Nets serve other purposes, such as protecting against hail or keeping birds away.":"整枝賦予葡萄樹樹形，並與修剪一起幫助產出穩定、健康的收成。絕大多數情況下，葡萄樹由立柱和鐵絲組成的棚架支撐。網子則有其他用途，例如防冰雹或驅趕鳥類。","Why do most growers now use irrigation sparingly?":"為什麼現在大多數種植者都節制地使用灌溉？","Water is increasingly limited and expensive":"水越來越有限，也越來越貴","Irrigation is banned in all regions":"所有產區都禁止灌溉","Water makes sugar levels rise too much":"水會讓糖分上升太多","Irrigation causes spring frosts":"灌溉會引發春霜","Water is an increasingly limited and expensive resource.":"水是越來越有限、越來越昂貴的資源。","In regions with little rain, irrigation is usually allowed, with methods ranging from flooding the field to watering individual vines. However, water has become an increasingly limited and expensive resource, so it is used sparingly. In a severe drought, there is often no water available for irrigation anyway.":"在雨量少的產區，灌溉通常是允許的，方法從漫灌整片田地到為單株葡萄樹澆水都有。不過，水已經成為越來越有限、越來越昂貴的資源，所以要節制使用。而在嚴重乾旱時，往往根本無水可供灌溉。","Which product is used to kill fungi in the vineyard?":"葡萄園裡用哪種產品殺死真菌？","Fungicide":"殺菌劑","Insecticide":"殺蟲劑","Herbicide":"除草劑","Fertiliser":"肥料","Fungicides kill fungi; insecticides and herbicides target insects and weeds.":"殺菌劑殺死真菌；殺蟲劑和除草劑分別針對昆蟲和雜草。","Fungi and insects are hard to control, and one solution is chemical sprays. Fungicides act against fungi, insecticides against insects and herbicides against weeds. Because some of these products can cause longer-term problems, many growers try to use them as little as possible.":"真菌和昆蟲很難控制，其中一個解決方法是噴灑化學藥劑。殺菌劑對付真菌，殺蟲劑對付昆蟲，除草劑對付雜草。由於有些產品可能造成長期問題，許多種植者盡量少用。","What does it mean if a vineyard is certified organic?":"葡萄園獲得有機認證代表什麼？","Grapes are grown without most chemicals":"種植葡萄時不使用大部分化學藥劑","No sprays of any kind are ever used":"完全不使用任何噴灑藥劑","Grapes are always picked by hand":"葡萄一律人工採收","The maximum yield is set by law":"最高產量由法律規定","Organic growing avoids most chemicals, though some sprays are still permitted.":"有機種植避免使用大部分化學藥劑，但仍允許部分噴灑藥劑。","A certified organic vineyard does without most chemicals. It is not a total ban, though: some sprays are still allowed to keep the worst fungal diseases under control. Organic status says nothing about harvesting method or yields, which depend on other choices or rules.":"獲得有機認證的葡萄園不使用大部分化學藥劑。但這並非全面禁止：仍允許部分噴灑藥劑，以控制最嚴重的真菌病害。有機身分與採收方式或產量無關，那取決於其他選擇或法規。","What effect can an excessively high yield have on the grapes?":"產量過高會對葡萄造成什麼影響？","Diluted flavours and less sugar":"風味被稀釋，糖分較少","More concentrated flavours and more sugar":"風味更濃縮，糖分更多","Dried-fruit and raisin aromas":"乾果和葡萄乾的香氣","With yields too high, grapes can have diluted flavours and lower sugar.":"產量太高時，葡萄可能風味稀釋、糖分較低。","Yield measures how much fruit is produced per unit of area, and in some regions it is capped by law. If a vine carries too many bunches, the grapes can be lower in sugar with diluted flavours. On the other hand, with too few bunches the crop becomes too small to be commercially viable.":"產量衡量的是每單位面積生產多少果實，在某些產區有法定上限。如果一株葡萄樹掛了太多果串，葡萄可能糖分較低、風味稀釋。反過來說，果串太少，收成就太小，不具商業價值。","A producer wants a fresh white with crisp acidity. Which harvest choice helps most?":"一位生產者想釀出酸度爽脆的清爽白酒。哪種採收選擇最有幫助？","Picking earlier in the ripening process":"在成熟過程中較早採收","Picking very late":"非常晚才採收","Waiting for the grapes to shrivel":"等葡萄乾縮","Waiting for noble rot":"等貴腐菌出現","Grapes picked early have more acidity, less sugar and less-ripe flavours.":"較早採收的葡萄酸度較高、糖分較少、風味較不成熟。","Harvest timing changes the balance of the grapes. Picked early, they have higher acidity, less sugar and less-ripe flavours, ideal for a fresh style. Picking late, waiting for shrivelling or for noble rot instead brings more sugar and riper or more concentrated flavours, typical of richer or sweet wines.":"採收時機會改變葡萄的平衡。較早採收的葡萄酸度較高、糖分較少、風味較不成熟，非常適合清爽的風格。相反地，晚採、等待乾縮或等待貴腐菌，則帶來更多糖分和更成熟或更濃縮的風味，是較豐潤或甜型葡萄酒的典型特徵。","Which statement about hand and machine harvesting is correct?":"關於人工採收和機器採收，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","Machines cannot be used on steep slopes":"機器無法在陡坡上使用","Hand-picking always gives better wines":"人工採收總是釀出更好的酒","Machine picking always gives better wines":"機器採收總是釀出更好的酒","Machines are compulsory in organic vineyards":"有機葡萄園規定必須使用機器","Neither method is inherently better, but machines cannot work steep slopes.":"兩種方法本身沒有優劣之分，但機器無法在陡坡上作業。","Grapes can be picked by hand or by machine, and neither method is inherently better for wine quality. The choice usually depends on the style being made. There is one practical constraint, however: machine harvesters cannot work on steep slopes, where hand-picking is needed.":"葡萄可以用人工或機器採收，兩種方法本身對葡萄酒品質沒有優劣之分。選擇通常取決於要釀造的風格。不過有一個實際的限制：採收機無法在陡坡上作業，那裡需要人工採收。","How does the Botrytis fungus concentrate the sugar in a grape?":"貴腐菌如何濃縮葡萄中的糖分？","It makes tiny holes in the skin so water evaporates":"在果皮上造成微小的孔洞，讓水分蒸發","It turns the water in the grape into ice":"把葡萄裡的水變成冰","It adds sugar from its own growth":"藉由自身生長添加糖分","It blocks photosynthesis in the leaves":"阻斷葉片的光合作用","Botrytis pierces the skin, water evaporates, and sugars, acids and flavours concentrate.":"貴腐菌刺穿果皮，水分蒸發，糖、酸和風味隨之濃縮。","Noble rot is caused by the Botrytis fungus, which creates tiny holes in the skin. Water evaporates through these holes, concentrating acids, sugars and flavours. Turning water into ice is instead the mechanism behind the frozen grapes used for icewine. Grapes affected by noble rot nearly always go into sweet wines.":"貴腐是由貴腐菌（Botrytis）引起的，它會在果皮上造成微小的孔洞。水分從這些孔洞蒸發，使酸、糖和風味濃縮。把水變成冰則是用來釀造冰酒的冰凍葡萄的原理。受貴腐菌感染的葡萄幾乎都用來釀造甜酒。","Which weather conditions are ideal for beneficial noble rot?":"哪種天氣條件最適合有益的貴腐菌？","Damp misty mornings, then warm dry afternoons":"潮濕多霧的早晨，接著是溫暖乾燥的午後","Constant rain throughout autumn":"整個秋天持續下雨","Hot, dry days with no moisture at all":"炎熱乾燥、完全沒有濕氣的日子","Night frosts followed by cold days":"夜間霜凍，接著是寒冷的白天","Morning damp lets the fungus grow; warm, dry afternoons stop it destroying the grapes.":"早晨的濕氣讓真菌生長；溫暖乾燥的午後則阻止它毀掉葡萄。","Botrytis can easily destroy grapes, so it must act in a controlled way. First, the grapes must be ripe. Then damp, misty mornings, often from mists near rivers, allow the fungus to grow and spread, followed by warm, dry afternoons that limit its growth before it ruins the crop.":"貴腐菌很容易毀掉葡萄，所以它必須在受控的情況下作用。首先，葡萄必須已經成熟。接著，潮濕多霧的早晨（霧氣常來自河流附近）讓真菌生長蔓延，隨後溫暖乾燥的午後限制它的生長，以免毀掉收成。","Why are grapes for icewine pressed while still frozen?":"為什麼冰酒用的葡萄要在結冰狀態下壓榨？","The ice stays behind, leaving more concentrated juice":"冰留在壓榨機裡，留下更濃縮的果汁","The cold adds colour to the juice":"寒冷為果汁增添顏色","Freezing kills the noble rot on the grapes":"冰凍會殺死葡萄上的貴腐菌","Frozen grapes have more tannin":"結冰的葡萄單寧較多","Pressing frozen grapes leaves ice and skins behind, so the little juice is very concentrated.":"壓榨結冰的葡萄時，冰和果皮留在壓榨機裡，所以少量的果汁非常濃縮。","In frozen grapes much of the water has turned to ice. By pressing before they thaw, the ice crystals stay behind with the skins and only a small amount of unfrozen liquid runs off, very rich in acids, sugars and flavours. This is the basis of icewines: sweet, concentrated and with pure varietal character.":"在結冰的葡萄中，大部分的水已經變成冰。在解凍前壓榨，冰晶會和果皮一起留下，只有少量未結冰的液體流出，富含酸、糖和風味。這就是冰酒的基礎：甜美、濃縮，帶有純粹的品種特色。","What do extra-ripeness, noble rot and frozen grapes have in common?":"過熟、貴腐和冰凍葡萄有什麼共同點？","They concentrate sugar and are often used for sweet wines":"它們都會濃縮糖分，常用來釀造甜酒","They lower sugar and give dry, light wines":"它們會降低糖分，釀出不甜、輕盈的酒","They all need a warm climate with no fog":"它們都需要沒有霧氣的溫暖氣候","They mainly increase colour and tannin":"它們主要增加顏色和單寧","All three methods concentrate grape sugar, ideal for sweet wines.":"三種方法都會濃縮葡萄的糖分，非常適合釀造甜酒。","These are three different ways of getting very sweet grapes. With extra-ripeness, water slowly evaporates and the grapes shrivel; with noble rot, the fungus pierces the skin and water evaporates; with freezing, the water stays locked in ice during pressing. In every case sugars and acids are concentrated and the grapes suit sweet wines.":"這是取得非常甜的葡萄的三種不同方法。過熟時，水分緩慢蒸發，葡萄乾縮；貴腐時，真菌刺穿果皮，水分蒸發；冰凍時，水在壓榨過程中被鎖在冰裡。在每一種情況下，糖和酸都會濃縮，葡萄都適合釀造甜酒。","What is the main purpose of training and pruning vines?":"整枝和修剪葡萄樹的主要目的是什麼？","To get a healthy, commercially viable crop every year":"每年都獲得健康、具商業價值的收成","To make vineyards suitable only for hand harvesting":"讓葡萄園只適合人工採收","To push each vine's yield as high as possible, whatever the ripeness":"不管成熟度如何，盡可能提高每株葡萄樹的產量","To prevent winter dormancy":"防止冬季休眠","Training and pruning ensure a healthy, viable crop can be harvested successfully every year.":"整枝和修剪確保每年都能順利採收健康、具商業價值的收成。","Winter pruning keeps each vine in its required shape, and most vines are trained on trellises. An excessive yield dilutes flavour and sugar, so that is not the goal. Winter dormancy is natural and cannot be avoided.":"冬季修剪讓每株葡萄樹維持所需的樹形，而大多數葡萄樹以棚架整枝。過高的產量會稀釋風味和糖分，所以那不是目標。冬季休眠是自然現象，無法避免。","Which irrigation system can water each individual vine?":"哪一種灌溉系統可以為每一株葡萄樹單獨澆水？","Drip irrigation":"滴灌","Flooding the field":"漫灌整片田地","Digging a channel next to the vineyard to raise the river level":"在葡萄園旁挖渠道以抬高河水水位","A drip system delivers water directly to each vine.":"滴灌系統把水直接送到每一株葡萄樹。","Methods range from flooding the whole field to systems that measure water vine by vine. The latter are valuable because water is increasingly scarce and expensive. Fog cools a vineyard but is not an irrigation system.":"灌溉方法從漫灌整片田地，到逐株計量用水的系統都有。後者非常有價值，因為水越來越稀少、越來越昂貴。霧氣能讓葡萄園降溫，但它不是灌溉系統。","In which regions are growers normally allowed to irrigate?":"種植者通常在哪些產區被允許灌溉？","Where there is a lack of rainfall":"缺乏降雨的地方","Only in cool-climate regions":"只在涼爽氣候產區","Anywhere, without limit, even in very rainy areas":"任何地方都行，毫無限制，連多雨地區也一樣","Only in organic vineyards":"只在有機葡萄園","Irrigation is normally permitted in regions that lack rainfall.":"在缺乏降雨的產區，灌溉通常是允許的。","Irrigation makes up for a natural lack of water, typical of warm, dry areas rather than cool ones. Even where it is allowed, growers now use it sparingly because water is a limited resource. Organic rules are about chemicals, not water.":"灌溉是為了彌補天然的缺水，這是溫暖乾燥地區而非涼爽地區的典型問題。即使在允許灌溉的地方，種植者現在也節制使用，因為水是有限的資源。有機規範涉及的是化學藥劑，不是水。","A grower wants to control weeds with a chemical spray. What do they use?":"一位種植者想用化學噴劑控制雜草。他會用什麼？","A herbicide":"除草劑","A fungicide":"殺菌劑","An insecticide":"殺蟲劑","A fine mesh net stretched over the rows":"架在葡萄樹行上方的細網","Herbicides are used to control weeds.":"除草劑用來控制雜草。","Fungicides kill fungi and insecticides kill insects. Nets protect against birds, larger animals or hail, not weeds. Many growers try to limit these chemicals anyway, as they can cause longer-term problems.":"殺菌劑殺死真菌，殺蟲劑殺死昆蟲。網子防的是鳥類、較大的動物或冰雹，不是雜草。無論如何，許多種植者都盡量限制這些化學藥劑，因為它們可能造成長期問題。","How are grapes most easily protected from birds and larger animals?":"保護葡萄免受鳥類和較大動物侵害，最簡單的方法是什麼？","With nets and fences":"用網子和圍欄","With fungicides sprayed on the leaves":"在葉片上噴灑殺菌劑","With shorter pruning in summer":"夏天修剪得更短","By harvesting just after fruit set, before the grapes turn sweet":"在著果後、葡萄變甜之前就採收","Birds and animals are kept away with physical barriers such as nets and fences.":"用網子和圍欄等實體屏障讓鳥類和動物遠離。","Large pests are fairly easy to keep out; fungi and insects are much harder to control. Fungicides act on fungi, not birds. Harvesting right after fruit set would give hard, green, inedible grapes.":"大型害物相對容易阻擋；真菌和昆蟲則難控制得多。殺菌劑作用於真菌，不是鳥類。著果後立刻採收，得到的會是又硬又綠、無法食用的葡萄。","In some areas, such as Argentina, nets are stretched over the vines. What are they mainly for?":"在某些地區，例如阿根廷，葡萄樹上方會架設網子。它們主要用來做什麼？","Against hail":"防冰雹","Against spring frost":"防春霜","To hold fog over the vineyard":"把霧氣留在葡萄園上方","To stop the roots taking up too much water after summer storms":"防止根部在夏季暴雨後吸收太多水","Hail nets shield vines and bunches from hailstones.":"防雹網保護葡萄樹和果串免受冰雹打擊。","A violent hailstorm can destroy a whole crop, and a net is an effective physical barrier. A net does little against frost, as the cold gets through anyway. Nets have no effect on fog or roots.":"一場猛烈的冰雹可能摧毀整年的收成，而網子是有效的實體屏障。網子對霜凍幫助不大，因為寒冷照樣會穿透。網子對霧氣或根部都沒有影響。","Why do many growers try to limit their use of chemical sprays?":"為什麼許多種植者盡量限制使用化學噴劑？","They can cause longer-term problems in vineyards":"它們可能在葡萄園造成長期問題","They are banned in every wine region except outside the EU":"除了歐盟以外，所有葡萄酒產區都禁止使用","They make wine sweeter":"它們讓葡萄酒更甜","They have no effect on fungi or insects":"它們對真菌或昆蟲沒有作用","Some of these chemicals can cause longer-term problems in vineyards.":"其中一些化學藥劑可能在葡萄園造成長期問題。","Fungicides, insecticides and herbicides do work, which is why they are used. They are not banned everywhere; organic growing uses very few, but some sprays against the worst fungal diseases are still allowed. A wine's sweetness has nothing to do with them.":"殺菌劑、殺蟲劑和除草劑確實有效，所以才會被使用。它們並非到處都被禁止；有機種植用得很少，但仍允許部分對付最嚴重真菌病害的噴劑。葡萄酒的甜度與它們無關。","Which statement about a certified organic vineyard is correct?":"關於獲得有機認證的葡萄園，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","Some sprays against the worst fungal diseases are still allowed":"仍允許部分對付最嚴重真菌病害的噴劑","No sprays of any kind are allowed":"不允許任何噴劑","Harvesting must be done by machine":"必須用機器採收","Irrigation is banned and vines must live on rainwater alone":"禁止灌溉，葡萄樹只能靠雨水生存","Organic growing avoids most chemicals, but some anti-fungal sprays remain permitted.":"有機種植避免使用大部分化學藥劑，但仍允許部分抗真菌噴劑。","'Organic' on a label means grapes grown without most chemicals, not with no treatment at all. The rules do not impose a harvesting method. Irrigation depends on lack of rainfall, not on organic status.":"酒標上的「有機」代表種植葡萄時不使用大部分化學藥劑，而不是完全不做任何處理。法規並未規定採收方式。灌溉與否取決於是否缺乏降雨，與有機身分無關。","Where do the fungi that attack vines grow, and what harm do they do?":"侵襲葡萄樹的真菌長在哪裡？會造成什麼危害？","On grapes and leaves; they reduce grape quality and quantity":"長在葡萄和葉片上；會降低葡萄的品質和產量","Only on the roots; they lower the wine's alcohol":"只長在根部；會降低葡萄酒的酒精濃度","Only on the trunk; they never touch the grapes":"只長在主幹上；從不接觸葡萄","In winery barrels; they add vanilla and coconut notes to the wine":"長在酒廠的橡木桶裡；為酒增添香草和椰子氣息","Fungi grow on grapes and leaves and can greatly reduce crop quality and quantity.":"真菌長在葡萄和葉片上，可能大幅降低收成的品質和產量。","Vines are vulnerable to many fungal diseases, sometimes with very serious damage. That is why fungicides are used, partly even in organic vineyards. Vanilla and coconut come from new oak, not a fungus.":"葡萄樹容易感染許多真菌病害，有時損害非常嚴重。這就是為什麼要使用殺菌劑，甚至有機葡萄園也部分使用。香草和椰子來自新橡木桶，不是真菌。","What is the problem if a vine produces too few grapes?":"如果一株葡萄樹結的葡萄太少，會有什麼問題？","The crop is too small to be commercially viable":"收成太小，不具商業價值","The flavours become diluted":"風味變得稀釋","The grapes always have less sugar":"葡萄的糖分總是比較少","The wine automatically becomes a late harvest wine":"酒會自動變成晚收酒","With too low a yield, there is not enough fruit for the vineyard to pay its way.":"產量太低時，果實不夠多，葡萄園無法回本。","Growers look for a balance: too many grapes give diluted flavours and less sugar, too few do not pay. Dilution and low sugar are therefore the risks of excessive yields, not low ones. 'Late harvest' depends on picking date, not yield.":"種植者追求的是平衡：葡萄太多會稀釋風味、降低糖分，太少則不划算。所以稀釋和低糖是產量過高的風險，而不是產量過低。「晚收」取決於採收日期，與產量無關。","Which statement about yield is correct?":"關於產量，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","In some regions the maximum yield is set by law":"在某些產區，最高產量由法律規定","Yield measures the finished wine's alcohol":"產量衡量的是成品酒的酒精濃度","The higher the yield, the more concentrated the flavours":"產量越高，風味越濃縮","Yield depends only on climate and the grower cannot influence it in any way":"產量只取決於氣候，種植者完全無法影響","Yield is fruit produced per unit of area, and in some regions the law sets a maximum.":"產量是每單位面積生產的果實量，在某些產區法律訂有上限。","Excessive yields dilute flavours and lower sugar rather than concentrating them. Yield measures the amount of fruit, not alcohol. Pruning and vineyard management exist precisely to regulate the crop.":"過高的產量會稀釋風味、降低糖分，而不是讓它們濃縮。產量衡量的是果實的數量，不是酒精。修剪和葡萄園管理正是為了調節收成而存在。","A producer harvests later than usual. What kind of grapes should they expect?":"一位生產者比平常晚採收。他應該預期得到什麼樣的葡萄？","More sugar, less acidity and riper flavours":"糖分較多、酸度較低、風味較成熟","Less sugar, more acidity and greener flavours":"糖分較少、酸度較高、風味較青澀","The same sugar and acidity, but paler skins":"糖分和酸度相同，但果皮顏色較淺","More acidity and more unripe tannins":"酸度較高，未成熟的單寧較多","Picking later means higher sugar, lower acidity and riper flavours.":"較晚採收代表糖分較高、酸度較低、風味較成熟。","Harvest timing is a key style decision. More acidity, less sugar and less ripe flavours come from picking early. If grapes stay on the vine even longer, they shrivel and take on raisin notes.":"採收時機是關鍵的風格決定。酸度較高、糖分較少、風味較不成熟來自較早採收。如果葡萄在樹上留得更久，就會乾縮並帶有葡萄乾的氣息。","Between hand and machine harvesting, which gives better-quality wine?":"人工採收和機器採收，哪一種能釀出品質更好的酒？","Neither is fundamentally better":"兩者本質上沒有優劣之分","Always hand harvesting":"永遠是人工採收","Always machine harvesting":"永遠是機器採收","Machine on steep slopes, hand only on flat land":"陡坡用機器，平地才用人工","Neither method is fundamentally better: the choice mainly depends on the wine style.":"兩種方法本質上沒有優劣之分：選擇主要取決於葡萄酒的風格。","The practical limit is that machines cannot work on steep slopes, where hand picking is needed; the last option gets this backwards. Always linking hand picking with quality is a cliché, not a rule.":"實際的限制是機器無法在陡坡上作業，那裡需要人工採收；最後一個選項正好說反了。總是把人工採收和品質畫上等號只是刻板印象，不是規則。","Which condition is essential for Botrytis to be 'noble' rather than destructive?":"貴腐菌要成為「貴腐」而非破壞性的，哪個條件不可或缺？","It must grow on grapes that are already ripe":"它必須長在已經成熟的葡萄上","It must attack grapes just after fruit set":"它必須在著果後立刻侵襲葡萄","It must rain heavily every afternoon":"每天下午都必須下大雨","The grapes must freeze on the vine before the fungus appears":"葡萄必須在真菌出現之前就在樹上結冰","The fungus is only beneficial on ripe grapes, with the right weather.":"這種真菌只有在成熟的葡萄上、配合合適的天氣，才是有益的。","Botrytis can easily destroy grapes. It needs ripe grapes, then damp, misty mornings to grow and warm, dry afternoons to hold it back. Afternoon rain would let it run out of control; freezing relates to icewine instead.":"貴腐菌很容易毀掉葡萄。它需要成熟的葡萄，接著需要潮濕多霧的早晨讓它生長，以及溫暖乾燥的午後抑制它。午後下雨會讓它失控；結冰則與冰酒有關。","In the development of noble rot, what is the role of warm, dry afternoons?":"在貴腐菌的發展過程中，溫暖乾燥的午後扮演什麼角色？","To limit the fungus so it does not destroy the grapes":"抑制真菌，以免它毀掉葡萄","To start the fungus growing on the grapes":"讓真菌開始在葡萄上生長","To freeze the water in the grapes":"讓葡萄裡的水結冰","To add water to the grapes to dilute acidity before harvest":"在採收前為葡萄補水以稀釋酸度","Warm, dry afternoons slow the fungus and stop it ruining the grapes.":"溫暖乾燥的午後減緩真菌生長，阻止它毀掉葡萄。","Damp, misty mornings are what allow the fungus to grow and spread. Alternating the two creates noble rot, which evaporates water and concentrates sugars, acids and flavours. Freezing grapes is the icewine technique.":"讓真菌生長蔓延的是潮濕多霧的早晨。兩者交替就形成貴腐，使水分蒸發，糖、酸和風味濃縮。冰凍葡萄則是冰酒的技術。","What style of wine is usually made from grapes frozen on the vine (icewine)?":"用在樹上結冰的葡萄（冰酒）通常釀成什麼風格的酒？","Sweet, concentrated and with pure varietal character":"甜美、濃縮，帶有純粹的品種特色","Dry and light, with flavours diluted by the ice water":"不甜、輕盈，風味被冰水稀釋","A tannic red for long ageing":"適合長期陳年的高單寧紅酒","Sweet, with strong noble-rot and raisin notes":"甜，帶有強烈的貴腐和葡萄乾氣息","Pressing healthy frozen grapes gives a little juice rich in sugar, acid and pure flavours: sweet, concentrated wines.":"壓榨健康的結冰葡萄，能得到少量富含糖、酸和純粹風味的果汁：釀出甜美濃縮的酒。","For icewine, healthy grapes stay on the vine through autumn into winter, are picked frozen and pressed before they thaw. Ice and skins stay in the press, so there is no dilution. Noble-rot and raisin notes belong to other concentration methods.":"釀造冰酒時，健康的葡萄從秋天一直留在樹上到冬天，在結冰狀態下採收，並在解凍前壓榨。冰和果皮留在壓榨機裡，所以不會被稀釋。貴腐和葡萄乾氣息屬於其他的濃縮方法。","A legally defined vineyard area":"法律界定的葡萄園區域","A grape variety permitted in a region":"某產區允許使用的葡萄品種","A brand registered by a producer":"生產者註冊的品牌","A quality ranking of vintages":"年份的品質排名","A GI is a legally defined vineyard area, large or small.":"GI 是法律界定的葡萄園區域，可大可小。","A GI legally defines a vineyard area. It can be very large, up to a whole region or country, or very small, such as a single vineyard. GIs appear on labels worldwide because the place where grapes grow can influence wine style. Not every wine comes from a GI, but some statement of origin must always be given.":"GI（地理標示）在法律上界定一個葡萄園區域。它可以非常大，大到整個產區或國家，也可以非常小，例如單一葡萄園。世界各地的酒標上都有 GI，因為葡萄生長的地方會影響葡萄酒的風格。並非每一款酒都來自某個 GI，但一定要標示某種產地說明。","Why is an EU GI a more reliable guide to style than a GI outside the EU?":"為什麼歐盟的 GI 比歐盟以外的 GI 更能可靠地反映風格？","It has rules on permitted grapes and winemaking":"它對允許的品種和釀造方式有規定","It always covers larger areas":"它涵蓋的區域總是比較大","It always names the grape on the label":"它總是在酒標上標示品種","It bans the use of irrigation":"它禁止灌溉","In the EU each GI sets which grapes may be grown and how the wine is made.":"在歐盟，每個 GI 都規定可以種植哪些品種，以及酒要如何釀造。","Outside the EU, a GI mainly shows where the grapes were grown: growers plant what they like and rules are minimal, so styles vary widely. In the EU, each GI adds rules on permitted varieties and winemaking methods. That is why an EU GI tells you much more about the expected style, even without the grape name.":"在歐盟以外，GI 主要表示葡萄種植的地點：種植者想種什麼就種什麼，規定極少，所以風格差異很大。在歐盟，每個 GI 還加上允許品種和釀造方式的規定。這就是為什麼即使沒有標示品種，歐盟的 GI 也能告訴你更多關於預期風格的資訊。","Which description best fits a PDO compared with a PGI?":"與 PGI 相比，哪一項描述最符合 PDO？","Smaller area and stricter rules":"區域較小，規定較嚴格","Wider area and more flexible rules":"區域較廣，規定較彈性","No rules on which grapes to use":"對使用的品種沒有規定","Only inexpensive high-volume wines":"只有平價的大量生產酒款","PDOs usually cover small areas with tight rules; PGIs are wider and more flexible.":"PDO 通常涵蓋小區域、規定嚴格；PGI 則區域較廣、較有彈性。","PDOs generally cover relatively small areas with tight regulations and include many of Europe's most prestigious wines. PGIs cover much wider areas with less strict rules, giving more freedom over grapes and techniques. PGI wines range from inexpensive high-volume wines to outstanding, premium-priced ones, so they are not only simple wines.":"PDO（受保護原產地名稱）一般涵蓋相對較小的區域，規定嚴格，包括歐洲許多最負盛名的葡萄酒。PGI（受保護地理標示）涵蓋廣得多的區域，規定較寬鬆，在品種和技術上給予更多自由。PGI 葡萄酒從平價的大量生產酒款到價格高昂的傑出酒款都有，所以不只是簡單的酒。","Which French term indicates a PGI?":"哪一個法文術語代表 PGI？","In France PGI is Indication géographique protégée; AOC and AOP indicate PDO.":"在法國，PGI 是 Indication géographique protégée；AOC 和 AOP 代表 PDO。","France uses two terms for PDO: Appellation d'origine protégée (AOP) and the traditional Appellation d'origine contrôlée (AOC). For PGI it uses Indication géographique protégée (IGP). Vieilles vignes, on the other hand, means old vines and is not even a legally defined term.":"法國的 PDO 有兩個術語：Appellation d'origine protégée（AOP）和傳統的 Appellation d'origine contrôlée（AOC）。PGI 則使用 Indication géographique protégée（IGP）。另一方面，Vieilles vignes 的意思是老藤，甚至不是法律定義的術語。","Which Italian term corresponds to PGI?":"哪一個義大利文術語對應 PGI？","In Italy PGI is Indicazione Geografica Tipica (IGT); DOC and DOCG are PDO.":"在義大利，PGI 是 Indicazione Geografica Tipica（IGT）；DOC 和 DOCG 是 PDO。","Italy has two traditional terms for PDO: Denominazione di Origine Controllata (DOC) and Denominazione di Origine Controllata e Garantita (DOCG). For PGI it uses Indicazione Geografica Tipica (IGT). DOCa is a Spanish term, Denominación de Origen Calificada, which belongs to the PDO category.":"義大利的 PDO 有兩個傳統術語：Denominazione di Origine Controllata（DOC）和 Denominazione di Origine Controllata e Garantita（DOCG）。PGI 則使用 Indicazione Geografica Tipica（IGT）。DOCa 是西班牙術語 Denominación de Origen Calificada，屬於 PDO 類別。","Which Spanish term indicates a PGI?":"哪一個西班牙文術語代表 PGI？","In Spain PGI is Vino de la Tierra; DO and DOCa are PDO.":"在西班牙，PGI 是 Vino de la Tierra；DO 和 DOCa 是 PDO。","In Spain, PDO is expressed by Denominación de Origen (DO) and Denominación de Origen Calificada (DOCa), while PGI is called Vino de la Tierra. Landwein is also a PGI term, but it is German, not Spanish, so it is the trap to avoid here.":"在西班牙，PDO 以 Denominación de Origen（DO）和 Denominación de Origen Calificada（DOCa）表示，而 PGI 稱為 Vino de la Tierra。Landwein 也是 PGI 術語，但它是德文，不是西班牙文，所以這是要避開的陷阱。","In Germany, which term corresponds to PGI?":"在德國，哪一個術語對應 PGI？","Germany's PGI term is Landwein; Qualitätswein and Prädikatswein are PDO.":"德國的 PGI 術語是 Landwein；Qualitätswein 和 Prädikatswein 是 PDO。","In Germany there are two traditional terms for PDO, Qualitätswein and Prädikatswein, while PGI corresponds to Landwein. Eiswein is not an origin category at all: it is a grape-growing term meaning the grapes were left to freeze on the vine before harvest.":"德國的 PDO 有兩個傳統術語：Qualitätswein 和 Prädikatswein，而 PGI 對應 Landwein。Eiswein 根本不是產地類別：它是葡萄種植術語，意思是葡萄在採收前留在樹上結冰。","A label reads Appellation Chablis Contrôlée but names no grape. Which grape is the wine made from?":"一張酒標上寫著 Appellation Chablis Contrôlée，但沒有標示品種。這款酒是用哪個品種釀的？","Chablis rules require Chardonnay, even though it is not shown on the label.":"Chablis 的法規規定使用夏多內，即使酒標上沒有標示。","Chablis is a French GI, and Appellation Contrôlée is the traditional French term for PDO. The rules of this appellation require the wines to be made from Chardonnay. For European PDO wines the grape does not have to appear on the label, so knowing the rules of the area tells you what is in the bottle.":"Chablis 是法國的 GI，而 Appellation Contrôlée 是法國 PDO 的傳統術語。這個法定產區的法規要求以夏多內釀造。歐洲的 PDO 葡萄酒不必在酒標上標示品種，所以了解產區法規就能知道瓶中是什麼。","Why are wines from old vines often highly prized?":"為什麼老藤釀的酒常常備受珍視？","Fewer grapes, with more concentrated, complex aromas":"葡萄較少，香氣更濃縮、更複雜","Higher yields with fresher aromas":"產量較高，香氣更清新","The term legally guarantees a minimum age":"這個術語在法律上保證最低樹齡","They are always sweet wines from shrivelled grapes":"它們總是用乾縮葡萄釀的甜酒","Old vines produce smaller crops, often with more concentrated, complex fruit.":"老藤的收成較小，果實常常更濃縮、更複雜。","As vines age, they tend to produce fewer bunches. A smaller crop can give grapes with more concentrated and complex aromas, and so higher-quality wines. That is why such wines are often labelled Old Vine or vieilles vignes. However, the term is not legally defined, so it guarantees no minimum age and its use can be disputed.":"隨著樹齡增長，葡萄樹結的果串往往變少。較小的收成可能帶來香氣更濃縮、更複雜的葡萄，因而釀出品質更高的酒。這就是為什麼這類酒常標示 Old Vine 或 vieilles vignes。不過，這個術語沒有法律定義，所以不保證任何最低樹齡，其使用也可能引起爭議。","An Australian and a Californian wine are both labelled 2022. Which statement is correct?":"一款澳洲酒和一款加州酒都標示 2022。下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","The Australian wine is about six months older":"澳洲酒大約老六個月","The Californian wine is about six months older":"加州酒大約老六個月","They are exactly the same age":"兩者年齡完全相同","The Australian wine is about a year older":"澳洲酒大約老一年","The southern hemisphere harvest comes about six months before the northern one.":"南半球的採收比北半球早大約六個月。","The vintage is the year of harvest. In the southern hemisphere the growing season runs from October to April, so grapes are picked early in the year; in the northern hemisphere it runs from April to October, with harvest towards the end of the year. An Australian 2022 is therefore about half a year older than a Californian 2022.":"年份是採收的年份。南半球的生長季從 10 月到 4 月，所以葡萄在年初採收；北半球則從 4 月到 10 月，在接近年底時採收。因此，2022 年的澳洲酒比 2022 年的加州酒大約老半年。","What does the term Late Harvest on a label indicate?":"酒標上的 Late Harvest 代表什麼？","Grapes picked well after the normal time":"葡萄在正常時間之後很久才採收","Grapes affected by noble rot":"葡萄受到貴腐菌感染","Grapes frozen on the vine":"葡萄在樹上結冰","Grapes from vines at least 60 years old":"葡萄來自至少 60 年樹齡的葡萄樹","Late Harvest means grapes left on the vine and picked much later than usual.":"Late Harvest 是指葡萄留在樹上，比平常晚很多才採收。","Late Harvest wines are made from grapes left on the vine beyond the normal picking time. The grapes have riper flavours and more sugar, and the wines are fuller-bodied and more concentrated than those from grapes picked at the usual time. Noble rot and frozen grapes have their own terms: Botrytis/Noble Rot and icewine/Eiswein.":"Late Harvest（晚收）葡萄酒是用留在樹上超過正常採收時間的葡萄釀造的。這些葡萄風味更成熟、糖分更多，釀出的酒比正常時間採收的葡萄酒體更飽滿、更濃縮。貴腐和冰凍葡萄則有各自的術語：Botrytis/Noble Rot 以及 icewine/Eiswein。","Which statement about a wine labelled Late Harvest is correct?":"關於標示 Late Harvest 的酒，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It can be dry, off-dry, medium or sweet":"它可以是不甜、微甜、半甜或甜","It is always a sweet wine":"它一定是甜酒","It is always lighter than a normal wine":"它一定比一般的酒輕盈","It is always made from frozen grapes":"它一定是用冰凍葡萄釀的","Late Harvest wines are fuller and more concentrated, but their sweetness varies.":"Late Harvest 葡萄酒更飽滿、更濃縮，但甜度不一。","Late-picked grapes have more sugar and riper flavours, giving fuller-bodied, more concentrated wines. That does not mean the wine must be sweet: a Late Harvest wine can be dry, off-dry, medium or sweet. By contrast, grapes with noble rot nearly always go into sweet wines, and icewine uses frozen grapes, not just late-picked ones.":"晚採的葡萄糖分更多、風味更成熟，釀出酒體更飽滿、更濃縮的酒。但這不代表酒一定是甜的：Late Harvest 葡萄酒可以是不甜、微甜、半甜或甜。相對地，受貴腐菌感染的葡萄幾乎都用來釀甜酒，而冰酒用的是冰凍的葡萄，不只是晚採的葡萄。","Which statement about the size of a geographical indication (GI) is correct?":"關於地理標示（GI）的大小，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It can range from a single vineyard to a whole country":"它可以從單一葡萄園到整個國家","It must always match one village":"它必須總是對應一個村莊","It can never exceed 100 hectares":"它絕不能超過 100 公頃","It always covers a whole administrative region, never a smaller area":"它總是涵蓋整個行政區，絕不會是較小的區域","A GI is a legally defined vineyard area, as large as a country or as small as one vineyard.":"GI 是法律界定的葡萄園區域，可以大如一個國家，也可以小如一座葡萄園。","GIs appear on labels because where grapes are grown influences the wine's style. There is no fixed size and no required link to administrative borders. For example, 'South Eastern Australia' is a very large GI, while others are tiny.":"酒標上出現 GI，是因為葡萄種植的地點會影響酒的風格。GI 沒有固定大小，也不必與行政邊界對應。例如「South Eastern Australia」是非常大的 GI，而其他有些則非常小。","A wine does not come from any GI. Which statement of origin must still appear on the label, where applicable?":"一款酒不來自任何 GI。酒標上仍必須標示哪一種產地說明（如適用）？","The country of origin":"原產國","The vineyard name":"葡萄園名稱","The age of the vines":"葡萄樹的樹齡","The exact harvest date and the names of the pickers":"確切的採收日期和採收者的姓名","Not every wine has a GI, but some statement of origin is required, such as the country.":"並非每一款酒都有 GI，但必須標示某種產地說明，例如國家。","A vineyard name is used only when the wine truly comes from it, and is often a GI itself. Vine age ('old vines') is optional and not legally defined. Exact dates and pickers' names do not appear on labels.":"葡萄園名稱只有在酒確實來自該葡萄園時才會使用，而且它本身常常就是一個 GI。樹齡（「老藤」）是選擇性的，沒有法律定義。確切日期和採收者姓名不會出現在酒標上。","A customer is looking at a wine from a non-EU GI and wants to predict its style. What is most useful to check on the label?":"一位顧客在看一款來自歐盟以外 GI 的酒，想預測它的風格。酒標上最值得查看的是什麼？","The grape variety":"葡萄品種","The GI name alone":"只看 GI 名稱","The colour of the capsule":"瓶封的顏色","The bottle size, which varies with the style of wine":"酒瓶容量，它會隨葡萄酒風格而不同","Outside the EU a GI only shows where the grapes grew, so the grape variety is the best clue.":"在歐盟以外，GI 只表示葡萄生長的地點，所以葡萄品種是最好的線索。","Outside the EU growers can plant whatever varieties they like, with few restrictions, so one place name can cover very different styles. That is why these wines are often varietally labelled. Capsule colour and bottle size tell you nothing reliable about style.":"在歐盟以外，種植者可以種任何想種的品種，限制很少，所以同一個地名可能涵蓋非常不同的風格。這就是為什麼這些酒常以品種標示。瓶封顏色和酒瓶容量都無法可靠地反映風格。","Which pair of Italian terms both indicate a PDO?":"下列哪一組義大利術語都代表 PDO？","IGT and DOC":"IGT 和 DOC","IGT and DOCG":"IGT 和 DOCG","IGT and table wine showing a region":"IGT 和標示產區的餐酒","In Italy DOC and DOCG are the traditional terms for PDO; IGT corresponds to PGI.":"在義大利，DOC 和 DOCG 是 PDO 的傳統術語；IGT 對應 PGI。","Each EU country uses its own traditional terms for the two categories. Any pair containing IGT mixes a PDO with a PGI. PDOs usually cover smaller areas with stricter rules.":"每個歐盟國家都用自己的傳統術語表示這兩個類別。任何包含 IGT 的組合都把 PDO 和 PGI 混在一起了。PDO 通常涵蓋較小的區域，規定較嚴格。","A Spanish label shows 'DOCa'. What does this tell you?":"一張西班牙酒標上寫著「DOCa」。這告訴你什麼？","That the wine is a PDO":"這款酒是 PDO","That the wine is a PGI":"這款酒是 PGI","That the wine is made from frozen grapes":"這款酒是用冰凍葡萄釀的","That the wine has no GI and comes from several countries":"這款酒沒有 GI，來自多個國家","In Spain, DO and DOCa are traditional terms for PDO.":"在西班牙，DO 和 DOCa 是 PDO 的傳統術語。","Spain's PGI term is Vino de la Tierra. DOCa (Denominación de Origen Calificada) belongs to the tier with smaller areas and tighter rules. It has nothing to do with frozen grapes, which is how icewine is made.":"西班牙的 PGI 術語是 Vino de la Tierra。DOCa（Denominación de Origen Calificada）屬於區域較小、規定較嚴格的等級。它與冰凍葡萄無關，冰凍葡萄是冰酒的釀法。","A German label says 'Prädikatswein'. Which EU category does the wine belong to?":"一張德國酒標上寫著「Prädikatswein」。這款酒屬於哪個歐盟類別？","Wine with no geographical indication":"沒有地理標示的葡萄酒","A category reserved for certified organic wines":"專屬於有機認證葡萄酒的類別","In Germany, Qualitätswein and Prädikatswein correspond to PDO; Landwein to PGI.":"在德國，Qualitätswein 和 Prädikatswein 對應 PDO；Landwein 對應 PGI。","Landwein is Germany's PGI term, with looser rules. Prädikatswein, like Qualitätswein, belongs to the higher tier. Organic is a separate certification, unrelated to the origin category.":"Landwein 是德國的 PGI 術語，規定較寬鬆。Prädikatswein 和 Qualitätswein 一樣屬於較高的等級。有機是另一種認證，與產地類別無關。","In France, what is the difference between AOC and AOP on a label?":"在法國，酒標上的 AOC 和 AOP 有什麼不同？","None: both are terms for the same PDO category":"沒有不同：兩者都是同一個 PDO 類別的術語","AOC is a PDO, AOP is a PGI":"AOC 是 PDO，AOP 是 PGI","AOP is used only for sweet wines":"AOP 只用於甜酒","AOC means organic, while AOP means a wine from old vines":"AOC 代表有機，而 AOP 代表老藤釀的酒","Appellation d'origine contrôlée and appellation d'origine protégée both indicate PDO.":"Appellation d'origine contrôlée 和 appellation d'origine protégée 都代表 PDO。","France's PGI term is Indication géographique protégée (IGP). AOC is the traditional term and is still widely seen, as in 'Appellation Chablis Contrôlée'. Neither term has anything to do with organic status, sweetness or vine age.":"法國的 PGI 術語是 Indication géographique protégée（IGP）。AOC 是傳統術語，至今仍很常見，例如「Appellation Chablis Contrôlée」。這兩個術語都與有機身分、甜度或樹齡無關。","Which of these terms does NOT indicate a PDO?":"下列哪一個術語不代表 PDO？","IGT is Italy's PGI term; the other three all indicate a PDO.":"IGT 是義大利的 PGI 術語；其他三個都代表 PDO。","DOCa (Spain), Qualitätswein (Germany) and AOC (France) all belong to the PDO tier. PGIs cover wider areas, with more freedom over grapes and techniques. That is why one producer's IGT wines can differ widely.":"DOCa（西班牙）、Qualitätswein（德國）和 AOC（法國）都屬於 PDO 等級。PGI 涵蓋較廣的區域，在品種和技術上有更多自由。這就是為什麼同一家生產者的 IGT 葡萄酒可能差異很大。","Which of these terms does NOT indicate a PGI?":"下列哪一個術語不代表 PGI？","DOC is an Italian PDO term; Landwein, Vino de la Tierra and IGP all indicate PGI.":"DOC 是義大利的 PDO 術語；Landwein、Vino de la Tierra 和 IGP 都代表 PGI。","Watch out for similar acronyms: Italy's DOC is a PDO, as is Spain's DO. The PGI terms are Landwein in Germany, Vino de la Tierra in Spain, IGP in France and IGT in Italy. Learning the table country by country avoids mix-ups.":"小心相似的縮寫：義大利的 DOC 是 PDO，西班牙的 DO 也是。PGI 術語在德國是 Landwein，在西班牙是 Vino de la Tierra，在法國是 IGP，在義大利是 IGT。逐國記住這張表就不會混淆。","Which statement about PGI wines is correct?":"關於 PGI 葡萄酒，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","They range from cheap, high-volume wines to outstanding low-volume wines":"從便宜的大量生產酒款，到產量稀少的傑出酒款都有","They are always lower in quality than any PDO":"品質一定比任何 PDO 都低","They must be made from one grape only":"必須只用單一品種釀造","They have stricter rules than PDOs on grapes and winemaking":"在品種和釀造方面的規定比 PDO 更嚴格","PGIs' more flexible rules allow a very wide range of styles and quality levels.":"PGI 較彈性的規定容許非常廣泛的風格和品質等級。","PGIs cover wide areas with looser rules than PDOs, giving producers more freedom. Some use that freedom to make outstanding wines sold at a premium. Nothing requires a single grape variety.":"PGI 涵蓋廣大區域，規定比 PDO 寬鬆，給予生產者更多自由。有些生產者利用這份自由釀出以高價出售的傑出酒款。沒有任何規定要求使用單一品種。","Which statement about the term 'Old Vine' / vieilles vignes is correct?":"關於「Old Vine」／vieilles vignes 這個術語，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It is not legally defined, so its use can be disputed":"它沒有法律定義，所以其使用可能引起爭議","It means vines at least 50 years old under EU law":"根據歐盟法律，它代表至少 50 年樹齡的葡萄樹","It may be used only on PDO wines":"它只能用在 PDO 葡萄酒上","It guarantees a sweet wine, because old vines give sweeter grapes":"它保證是甜酒，因為老藤結的葡萄比較甜","'Old vines' has no legal definition, so there can be disagreement over its use.":"「老藤」沒有法律定義，所以其使用可能有爭議。","Old vines give fewer grapes with more concentrated, complex flavours, hence their prestige. But no law sets a minimum age or limits the term to certain categories. It is about yield and concentration, not sweetness.":"老藤結的葡萄較少，風味更濃縮、更複雜，因此享有聲望。但沒有法律規定最低樹齡，也沒有把這個術語限制在特定類別。它關乎的是產量和濃縮度，而不是甜度。","What does the vintage on a label refer to?":"酒標上的年份指的是什麼？","The year the grapes were harvested":"葡萄採收的年份","The year the wine was bottled":"葡萄酒裝瓶的年份","The year the wine went on sale":"葡萄酒上市的年份","The year the vines that made the wine were planted":"釀酒的葡萄樹種植的年份","The vintage is the year of harvest.":"年份就是採收的年份。","Bottling and release can happen months or years after harvest. The vines' planting year is never shown as the vintage. Knowing the vintage helps you judge the wine's age and whether it is at its best.":"裝瓶和上市可能在採收後數月或數年才進行。葡萄樹的種植年份從不會標示為年份。了解年份有助於判斷酒的年齡，以及它是否處於最佳狀態。","Why is the vintage especially useful for expensive wines from prestigious regions with variable weather?":"對於來自天氣多變的知名產區的昂貴葡萄酒，為什麼年份特別有用？","Each year's weather can greatly affect grape quality":"每年的天氣可能大幅影響葡萄品質","It shows which grape was used":"它顯示使用了哪個品種","It reveals whether the wine is organic":"它透露這款酒是否有機","It proves the wine always has the same style, whatever the year's weather":"它證明無論當年天氣如何，酒的風格總是一樣","Where weather varies a lot year to year, the vintage helps predict style and quality.":"在天氣年年差異很大的地方，年份有助於預測風格和品質。","A cool or rainy year can produce a wine different from what you expect. Knowing it helps you decide if the price is justified and when to drink the wine. The last option says the opposite: variability is exactly why the vintage matters.":"涼爽或多雨的年份釀出的酒可能和你預期的不同。了解這一點有助於判斷價格是否合理，以及何時飲用。最後一個選項說的正好相反：正是因為多變，年份才重要。","A customer wants a dry white and points to an Australian bottle labelled 'Botrytis Semillon'. What should you tell them?":"一位顧客想要不甜的白酒，指著一瓶標示「Botrytis Semillon」的澳洲酒。你應該怎麼告訴他？","That it is almost certainly a sweet wine":"這幾乎可以肯定是一款甜酒","That it is a light, dry white":"這是一款輕盈、不甜的白酒","That it is a red, because Semillon is a black grape":"這是紅酒，因為榭密雍是黑葡萄","That it was ruined by a vineyard disease and should be avoided completely":"它被葡萄園的病害毀了，應該完全避開","Noble-rot grapes are highly concentrated in sugar and nearly always make sweet wines.":"貴腐葡萄的糖分高度濃縮，幾乎都用來釀甜酒。","Semillon is a white grape; outside the EU, varietal labelling is common. Here the Botrytis is beneficial: it is noble rot, which concentrates sugars and acids. For a dry white, suggest a different bottle.":"榭密雍是白葡萄；在歐盟以外，以品種標示很常見。這裡的貴腐菌是有益的：它就是貴腐，會濃縮糖和酸。想要不甜的白酒，就建議另一瓶吧。","What does 'Icewine' or 'Eiswein' on a label tell you about the harvest?":"酒標上的「Icewine」或「Eiswein」告訴你什麼採收資訊？","The grapes were left to freeze on the vine before picking":"葡萄在採收前留在樹上結冰","The grapes were frozen in the winery after harvest":"葡萄在採收後於酒廠冷凍","The wine is meant to be served over ice":"這款酒應該加冰塊飲用","The grapes were affected by noble rot in a very cold region":"葡萄在非常寒冷的產區受到貴腐菌感染","Icewine/Eiswein means grapes frozen naturally on the vine and pressed while still frozen.":"Icewine/Eiswein 是指葡萄在樹上自然結冰，並在結冰狀態下壓榨。","The ice stays in the press and the juice is rich in sugar and acid, usually for sweet wines. Freezing must happen in the vineyard, not the winery. Noble rot is a different concentration method, labelled as Botrytis or Noble Rot.":"冰留在壓榨機裡，果汁富含糖和酸，通常用來釀甜酒。結冰必須發生在葡萄園，而不是酒廠。貴腐是另一種濃縮方法，標示為 Botrytis 或 Noble Rot。","Compared with a wine from a normal harvest, what can you expect from a 'Late Harvest' wine of the same grape?":"與正常採收的酒相比，同一品種的「Late Harvest」葡萄酒可以預期有什麼不同？","More body and more concentration":"酒體更飽滿、更濃縮","Less alcohol and more acidity":"酒精較低、酸度較高","Greener, more herbaceous flavours":"風味更青澀、更有草本氣息","Exactly the same style, since only the bottling date matters":"風格完全相同，因為只有裝瓶日期才重要","Later-picked grapes are riper and sweeter, giving fuller-bodied, more concentrated wines.":"較晚採收的葡萄更成熟、更甜，釀出酒體更飽滿、更濃縮的酒。","Late harvest brings riper flavours and more sugar, not green notes. The wine can still be dry, off-dry, medium or sweet. Lower alcohol and higher acidity are typical of grapes picked early.":"晚收帶來更成熟的風味和更多糖分，而不是青澀的氣息。這款酒仍然可以是不甜、微甜、半甜或甜。酒精較低、酸度較高是早採葡萄的典型特徵。","Which microorganisms carry out alcoholic fermentation?":"哪一種微生物進行酒精發酵？","Bacteria":"細菌","Moulds":"黴菌","Yeast feed on the sugars in the juice and turn them into alcohol.":"酵母以果汁中的糖為食，把糖轉化為酒精。","Alcoholic fermentation is the one process common to all wines, and it is carried out by yeast. Bacteria, on the other hand, are responsible for malolactic conversion, which happens afterwards and lowers acidity. Moulds and enzymes are not what produce the alcohol: mixing them up with yeast is a common exam mistake.":"酒精發酵是所有葡萄酒共有的唯一過程，由酵母進行。相對地，細菌負責乳酸轉化，它發生在之後並降低酸度。製造酒精的不是黴菌或酵素：把它們和酵母搞混是考試中常見的錯誤。","Apart from alcohol, what do yeast produce during fermentation?":"除了酒精，酵母在發酵過程中還產生什麼？","Carbon dioxide and heat":"二氧化碳和熱","Oxygen and acidity":"氧氣和酸","Sugar and water":"糖和水","Fermentation turns sugar into alcohol, CO2 and heat.":"發酵把糖轉化為酒精、CO2 和熱。","As they consume sugar, yeast release alcohol, carbon dioxide and heat. For still wines the CO2 usually escapes into the air, while the heat must be controlled because temperature affects style. Colour and tannin are not made by yeast: they are extracted from the skins of black grapes, and the heat of fermentation helps that extraction.":"酵母消耗糖時，會釋放酒精、二氧化碳和熱。釀造靜態酒時，CO2 通常散逸到空氣中，而熱必須加以控制，因為溫度會影響風格。顏色和單寧不是酵母製造的：它們是從黑葡萄的果皮萃取出來的，發酵的熱有助於萃取。","What mainly determines the alcohol level of a dry wine?":"主要是什麼決定了不甜葡萄酒的酒精濃度？","The amount of sugar in the grapes":"葡萄中的糖量","The type of vessel used":"使用的容器類型","The length of storage":"儲存的時間長短","The amount of tannin in the skins":"果皮中的單寧量","The more sugar in the grapes, the more alcohol the yeast can make.":"葡萄中的糖越多，酵母能產生的酒精就越多。","In a dry wine the yeast use up all the available sugar, so the final alcohol depends on how much sugar there was at the start, in other words on grape ripeness. That is why warm-climate wines tend to be higher in alcohol. Vessels, storage time and tannins affect other aspects of style, but not how much alcohol is produced.":"在不甜的葡萄酒中，酵母會把所有可用的糖消耗殆盡，所以最終的酒精濃度取決於一開始有多少糖，也就是葡萄的成熟度。這就是為什麼溫暖氣候的葡萄酒酒精濃度往往較高。容器、儲存時間和單寧會影響風格的其他方面，但不影響產生多少酒精。","What is the typical alcohol range of most dry wines?":"大多數不甜葡萄酒的典型酒精濃度範圍是多少？","About 11.5–16% abv":"約 11.5–16% abv","About 5–9% abv":"約 5–9% abv","About 15–20% abv":"約 15–20% abv","About 18–22% abv":"約 18–22% abv","Most dry wines sit between about 11.5% and 16% abv.":"大多數不甜葡萄酒的酒精濃度約在 11.5% 到 16% abv 之間。","The alcohol level of dry wines depends on grape sugar and usually falls between 11.5% and 16% abv. The 15–20% abv range belongs to fortified wines, where alcohol is added to stop fermentation. Very low levels, under 10%, are not typical of dry wines, because they suggest that not all the sugar has been converted.":"不甜葡萄酒的酒精濃度取決於葡萄的糖分，通常介於 11.5% 到 16% abv 之間。15–20% abv 的範圍屬於加烈酒，它們是添加酒精來中止發酵的。低於 10% 的極低酒精濃度不是不甜葡萄酒的典型特徵，因為這表示並非所有的糖都被轉化了。","In white winemaking, when does pressing usually take place?":"釀造白酒時，壓榨通常在什麼時候進行？","Before alcoholic fermentation":"酒精發酵之前","After alcoholic fermentation":"酒精發酵之後","During oak maturation":"橡木桶熟成期間","Just before bottling":"就在裝瓶前","For whites, grapes are crushed and pressed before fermenting, without skins.":"釀造白酒時，葡萄在發酵前破皮和壓榨，不帶果皮發酵。","The typical order for a white is crushing, pressing, fermentation, storage or maturation, packaging. The juice ferments apart from the skins, which are usually discarded, because colour and tannin are not wanted. For reds it is the opposite: pressing comes after fermentation, because the skins must stay in contact with the fermenting juice.":"白酒的典型順序是破皮、壓榨、發酵、儲存或熟成、包裝。果汁與果皮分開發酵，果皮通常被丟棄，因為不需要顏色和單寧。紅酒則相反：壓榨在發酵之後，因為果皮必須與發酵中的果汁保持接觸。","What is the typical order for a dry red wine?":"不甜紅酒的典型順序是什麼？","Draining, crushing, fermentation, pressing":"排汁、破皮、發酵、壓榨","In reds the skins ferment with the juice; draining and pressing come afterwards.":"釀造紅酒時，果皮與果汁一起發酵；排汁和壓榨在之後進行。","A red must be made from black grapes, and the skins must stay in the juice during fermentation to give colour and tannin. Only when fermentation is finished is the wine drained off the skins, and the wine left in them is recovered by pressing. Storage or maturation and finally packaging follow.":"紅酒必須用黑葡萄釀造，而且發酵期間果皮必須留在果汁中，以帶來顏色和單寧。只有在發酵結束後，才把酒從果皮中排出，留在果皮中的酒則透過壓榨回收。接著是儲存或熟成，最後是包裝。","Why can white wine be made from black grapes?":"為什麼可以用黑葡萄釀造白酒？","The colour is found only in the skin":"顏色只存在於果皮中","The colour disappears during fermentation":"顏色在發酵過程中消失","The colour is found only in the seeds":"顏色只存在於葡萄籽中","The colour is removed by oak":"顏色被橡木桶去除","Black grape pulp is clear, so gentle pressing keeps the juice colourless.":"黑葡萄的果肉是透明的，所以輕柔壓榨能讓果汁保持無色。","In black grapes the coloured pigments are found only in the skin, not the pulp. If the grapes are pressed very gently, the juice comes out almost colourless and, fermented away from the skins, makes a white wine. For a red, by contrast, the skins must take part in fermentation precisely to release their colour.":"黑葡萄的色素只存在於果皮，不在果肉。如果非常輕柔地壓榨葡萄，流出的果汁幾乎無色，與果皮分開發酵後就成了白酒。相反地，釀造紅酒時，果皮必須參與發酵，正是為了釋放顏色。","In the short maceration method for rosé, when are the skins removed?":"以短時間浸皮法釀造粉紅酒時，果皮在什麼時候移除？","After several weeks of fermentation":"發酵數週之後","Only at bottling":"直到裝瓶時","The skins stay in contact for just a few hours, enough for a light colour.":"果皮只接觸幾個小時，足以帶來淡淡的顏色。","With short maceration, black grapes are used and the process starts like a red, but the fermenting juice is drained off the skins after a few hours. The brief contact gives a pink colour and little tannin. Fermentation then continues without the skins, at the cooler temperatures used for whites, and rosés rarely see oak.":"短時間浸皮法使用黑葡萄，一開始像釀紅酒一樣，但幾個小時後就把發酵中的果汁從果皮中排出。短暫的接觸帶來粉紅色和少量單寧。之後發酵在沒有果皮的情況下繼續進行，溫度與白酒一樣較低，而粉紅酒很少經過橡木桶。","Which rosé method is not permitted in many parts of Europe?":"哪一種粉紅酒釀法在歐洲許多地方不被允許？","Blending red wine with white wine":"把紅酒和白酒混合","Short maceration of black grapes":"黑葡萄短時間浸皮","Fermenting at low temperature":"低溫發酵","Using stainless steel tanks":"使用不鏽鋼槽","Rosé made by blending red and white is banned in many European regions.":"把紅酒和白酒混合釀成的粉紅酒，在歐洲許多產區是禁止的。","The two most common rosé methods are short maceration and blending. In blending, a red wine is mixed with a white wine to achieve the pink colour. It is a simple technique, but it is not permitted in many parts of Europe. Short maceration, by contrast, is allowed and widely used.":"最常見的兩種粉紅酒釀法是短時間浸皮法和混合法。混合法是把紅酒和白酒混合，得到粉紅色。這是一種簡單的技術，但在歐洲許多地方不被允許。相反地，短時間浸皮法是允許的，而且廣泛使用。","Why are red wines fermented at higher temperatures than whites?":"為什麼紅酒的發酵溫度比白酒高？","To extract colour and tannin from the skins":"為了從果皮萃取顏色和單寧","To preserve delicate fruity aromas":"為了保留細緻的果香","To increase the wine's acidity":"為了提高酒的酸度","To stop the yeast early":"為了提早讓酵母停止作用","Heat helps extract colour and tannin from the skins.":"熱有助於從果皮萃取顏色和單寧。","Reds ferment at roughly 20–32°C, whites at 12–22°C. The higher temperatures allow reds to extract colour and tannin from the skins, which are essential to their style. Whites, which ferment without skins, benefit instead from cooler temperatures, which bring out fruity aromas.":"紅酒的發酵溫度約為 20–32°C，白酒則為 12–22°C。較高的溫度讓紅酒能從果皮萃取顏色和單寧，這對紅酒的風格不可或缺。不帶果皮發酵的白酒，則受益於較低的溫度，能帶出果香。","Which temperature range is typical for fermenting white wines?":"白酒典型的發酵溫度範圍是多少？","12–22°C (54–72°F)":"12–22°C（54–72°F）","20–32°C (68–90°F)":"20–32°C（68–90°F）","2–8°C (36–46°F)":"2–8°C（36–46°F）","30–40°C (86–104°F)":"30–40°C（86–104°F）","Whites ferment at 12–22°C, cooler than reds.":"白酒在 12–22°C 發酵，比紅酒低。","Whites ferment at roughly 12–22°C. At the cooler end of that range, fermentation can produce pronounced fruity aromas, prized in many fresh whites. The 20–32°C range belongs to reds, which need heat to extract colour and tannin. Short-maceration rosés, once drained, ferment at temperatures similar to whites.":"白酒的發酵溫度約為 12–22°C。在這個範圍的低溫端發酵，可以產生濃郁的果香，這在許多清爽的白酒中備受珍視。20–32°C 的範圍屬於紅酒，紅酒需要熱來萃取顏色和單寧。短時間浸皮的粉紅酒在排汁後，以類似白酒的溫度發酵。","A white wine fermented at a very cool temperature is most likely to show...":"一款在非常低溫下發酵的白酒，最可能表現出……","Pronounced fruity aromas":"濃郁的果香","High tannin":"高單寧","Nut and caramel aromas":"堅果和焦糖香氣","A deep amber colour":"深琥珀色","Cool white fermentations can produce pronounced fruity aromas.":"低溫發酵的白酒可以產生濃郁的果香。","At the cool end of the white range, around 12°C, fermentation can bring out pronounced fruity aromas. Nut and caramel come from contact with oxygen during barrel maturation, while an amber colour is a sign of age. High tannin does not apply to whites, which ferment without their skins.":"在白酒溫度範圍的低溫端，約 12°C 左右，發酵可以帶出濃郁的果香。堅果和焦糖來自橡木桶熟成期間與氧氣的接觸，而琥珀色則是陳年的跡象。高單寧不適用於白酒，因為白酒不帶果皮發酵。","What is the \"cap\" in red winemaking?":"紅酒釀造中的「酒帽」是什麼？","The layer of skins that floats to the top":"浮到頂部的果皮層","The layer of dead yeast at the bottom":"底部的死酵母層","The lid used to close the vessel":"用來封住容器的蓋子","The CO2 foam on top of the wine":"酒液表面的 CO2 泡沫","The skins float and form a thick layer called the cap.":"果皮浮起，形成一層稱為酒帽的厚層。","During red fermentation the skins rise and form the cap. Left undisturbed it gives up little colour and tannin, so it must be mixed often with the liquid by punching down or pumping over. The layer of dead yeast at the bottom, on the other hand, is called the lees and mostly matters in white winemaking.":"紅酒發酵期間，果皮上浮形成酒帽。如果不加處理，酒帽釋放的顏色和單寧很少，所以必須經常透過壓帽或淋汁讓它與液體混合。另一方面，底部的死酵母層稱為酒渣，主要在白酒釀造中發揮作用。","In which technique is liquid from the bottom of the vessel sprayed over the cap?":"哪一種技術是把容器底部的液體噴淋到酒帽上？","In pumping over, liquid is pumped through a hose and sprayed over the cap.":"淋汁是用管子抽取液體，噴淋到酒帽上。","Pumping over and punching down both mix skins and liquid to extract colour and tannin. In pumping over, liquid is drawn from the bottom of the vessel and sprayed over the cap; in punching down, a plunger pushes the cap down into the liquid. Draining and pressing take place once fermentation has finished.":"淋汁和壓帽都是讓果皮與液體混合，以萃取顏色和單寧。淋汁是從容器底部抽取液體，噴淋到酒帽上；壓帽則是用壓棒把酒帽壓入液體中。排汁和壓榨在發酵結束後進行。","In a cool vintage, why might a winemaker increase the sugar in the juice?":"在涼爽的年份，釀酒師為什麼可能提高果汁中的糖分？","To avoid a wine low in alcohol and body":"避免酒的酒精和酒體不足","To make the wine sweet":"讓酒變甜","To lower the acidity":"降低酸度","To extract more tannin":"萃取更多單寧","More sugar to ferment means more alcohol and more body.":"可發酵的糖越多，酒精和酒體就越多。","In cool climates or vintages the grapes may not ripen fully and may lack sugar, giving a wine low in alcohol and lacking body. Raising the sugar in the juice gives the yeast more to convert, so the finished wine has more alcohol. The added sugar is fermented, so the wine stays dry.":"在涼爽的氣候或年份，葡萄可能無法完全成熟、糖分不足，釀出的酒酒精低、酒體單薄。提高果汁中的糖分，讓酵母有更多可轉化的糖，成品酒的酒精就更高。添加的糖會被發酵掉，所以酒仍然是不甜的。","In a warm climate, which adjustment is most likely?":"在溫暖氣候中，最可能進行哪一種調整？","Adding acid":"加酸","Neutralising acid":"中和酸","Adding sugar":"加糖","Adding tannin":"添加單寧","In warm climates acidity drops sharply, leaving the wine unbalanced.":"在溫暖氣候中，酸度會大幅下降，讓酒失去平衡。","During ripening in a warm climate, grape acidity can fall very low. A wine with too little acidity would be unbalanced, so the winemaker may add acid in the winery. Neutralising acid and raising sugar are, by contrast, typical adjustments for cool climates, where grapes ripen with more acid and less sugar.":"在溫暖氣候中成熟時，葡萄的酸度可能降得非常低。酸度太低的酒會失去平衡，所以釀酒師可能在酒廠中加酸。相反地，中和酸和提高糖分是涼爽氣候的典型調整，因為那裡的葡萄成熟時酸較多、糖較少。","How does Tokaji Aszú get its sweetness?":"Tokaji Aszú 的甜味是怎麼來的？","From grapes with concentrated sugars":"來自糖分濃縮的葡萄","By adding alcohol":"添加酒精","By filtering out the yeast":"把酵母過濾掉","By adding juice to a dry wine":"在不甜的酒中加入果汁","The sugar is so concentrated that the yeast cannot consume it all.":"糖分濃縮到酵母無法全部消耗。","Tokaji Aszú from Hungary is made from grapes with highly concentrated sugars. When the juice is that sugary, the yeast cannot ferment it all, and fermentation stops with residual sugar left over. Adding alcohol is typical of Port, and filtering out yeast of White Zinfandel.":"匈牙利的 Tokaji Aszú 是用糖分高度濃縮的葡萄釀造的。當果汁這麼甜時，酵母無法把糖全部發酵完，發酵停止時就留下殘糖。添加酒精是 Port 的典型做法，過濾酵母則是 White Zinfandel 的做法。","Which sweet wine is made by removing the yeast with very fine filters?":"哪一種甜酒是用非常細的過濾器去除酵母釀成的？","Californian White Zinfandel uses filters that catch the yeast.":"加州的 White Zinfandel 使用能攔住酵母的過濾器。","Removing yeast from fermenting juice requires extremely sophisticated filters with holes small enough to catch them. Without yeast, fermentation stops and residual sugar remains: this is how White Zinfandel from California is made. Port is made by adding alcohol, while Tokaji Aszú and icewine start from grapes with concentrated sugars.":"要從發酵中的果汁去除酵母，需要極為精密、孔洞小到能攔住酵母的過濾器。沒有了酵母，發酵就停止，留下殘糖：加州的 White Zinfandel 就是這樣釀成的。Port 是添加酒精釀成的，而 Tokaji Aszú 和冰酒則是從糖分濃縮的葡萄開始。","Why is a fortified wine such as Port in no danger of fermenting again?":"為什麼像 Port 這樣的加烈酒沒有再次發酵的風險？","Alcohol at 15–20% abv kills the yeast":"15–20% abv 的酒精會殺死酵母","All the sugar has been used up":"所有的糖都已經用完了","The wine is filtered several times":"酒經過多次過濾","The wine is kept at a low temperature":"酒保存在低溫下","The added alcohol takes the wine to a level that kills yeast.":"添加的酒精讓酒達到足以殺死酵母的濃度。","Fortification adds alcohol to the fermenting juice, raising it to 15–20% abv. At this level the yeast die before they have used all the sugar, which stays in the wine as sweetness. The high alcohol also stops fermentation from restarting later, which is why Port is stable even though it is sweet.":"加烈是在發酵中的果汁裡添加酒精，把濃度提高到 15–20% abv。在這個濃度下，酵母在用完所有糖之前就死亡了，剩下的糖以甜味的形式留在酒中。高酒精也能防止日後重新發酵，這就是為什麼 Port 雖然是甜的，卻很穩定。","What is the main advantage of adding sweetness to a dry wine?":"在不甜的酒中添加甜味，主要的好處是什麼？","Precise control of the sweetness level":"精準控制甜度","A much higher alcohol level":"酒精濃度大幅提高","Softer tannins":"單寧更柔和","More intense oak flavours":"橡木桶風味更濃郁","Adding sweetness after fermentation lets the final sugar be set exactly.":"在發酵後添加甜味，可以準確設定最終的糖分。","This technique is widely used for red, white and rosé wines precisely because the winemaker can control sweetness accurately. The added sugar always comes from grapes: unfermented juice, very sweet concentrated juice, or a sweet wine blended with the dry one. It does not affect tannins or oak flavours.":"這項技術廣泛用於紅酒、白酒和粉紅酒，正是因為釀酒師可以精準控制甜度。添加的糖一定來自葡萄：未發酵的葡萄汁、非常甜的濃縮葡萄汁，或與不甜的酒混合的甜酒。它不會影響單寧或橡木桶風味。","What does crushing involve?":"破皮是指什麼？","Splitting the skins to release some of the juice":"把果皮弄破，釋放出一部分果汁","Squeezing the grapes to extract as much liquid as possible":"擠壓葡萄，盡可能取出最多液體","Separating the wine from the lees after fermentation":"發酵後把酒和酒渣分開","Pushing the cap of skins into the liquid with a plunger during red fermentation":"紅酒發酵期間用壓棒把果皮形成的酒帽壓入液體","Crushing means splitting the grape skins so some juice comes out.":"破皮是把葡萄果皮弄破，讓一部分果汁流出。","Squeezing hard is pressing, done in a press. Pushing the cap into the liquid is punching down, used for reds. Crushing is the first step for both white and red wines.":"用力擠壓是壓榨，在壓榨機中進行。把酒帽壓入液體是壓帽，用於紅酒。破皮是白酒和紅酒共同的第一步。","Which statement about pressing is correct?":"關於壓榨，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It can take place before or after fermentation":"它可以在發酵之前或之後進行","It always happens after fermentation":"它總是在發酵之後進行","It always happens before crushing":"它總是在破皮之前進行","It is only used for sweet wines from frozen or noble-rot grapes":"它只用於以冰凍或貴腐葡萄釀造的甜酒","White wines are pressed before fermentation, red wines after it.":"白酒在發酵前壓榨，紅酒在發酵後壓榨。","Pressing squeezes crushed grapes to get out as much liquid as possible. For whites it separates juice from skins before fermentation; for reds it recovers the wine left in the skins after draining. It always follows crushing, never precedes it.":"壓榨是擠壓破皮後的葡萄，盡可能取出最多液體。對白酒來說，它在發酵前把果汁與果皮分開；對紅酒來說，它在排汁後回收留在果皮中的酒。壓榨總是在破皮之後，從不在之前。","When making a still wine, what happens to the carbon dioxide produced by the yeast?":"釀造靜態酒時，酵母產生的二氧化碳會怎樣？","It escapes into the atmosphere":"散逸到大氣中","It stays dissolved and makes the wine fizzy":"保持溶解，讓酒有氣泡","It turns into alcohol":"轉化為酒精","It is reabsorbed by the skins and deepens a red wine's colour":"被果皮重新吸收，加深紅酒的顏色","For still wines, fermentation CO2 is allowed to escape into the air.":"釀造靜態酒時，發酵產生的 CO2 會散逸到空氣中。","Yeast turn sugar into alcohol, CO2 and heat; CO2 is a product, it does not become alcohol. If it were trapped the wine would be fizzy. Red colour comes from the skins, helped by fermentation heat, not from CO2.":"酵母把糖轉化為酒精、CO2 和熱；CO2 是產物，不會變成酒精。如果把它封住，酒就會有氣泡。紅酒的顏色來自果皮，並藉助發酵的熱，而不是來自 CO2。","When does alcoholic fermentation usually stop naturally?":"酒精發酵通常在什麼時候自然停止？","When the yeast have eaten all the sugar":"當酵母把糖全部吃完時","After exactly one week":"剛好一週之後","When the wine reaches 5% abv":"當酒達到 5% abv 時","When the winemaker adds concentrated grape sugar to block the yeast":"當釀酒師加入濃縮葡萄糖來阻止酵母時","Fermentation typically ends on its own once no sugar is left, giving a dry wine.":"發酵通常在沒有糖剩下時自行結束，得到不甜的酒。","The final strength depends on the starting sugar: most dry wines are 11.5–16% abv. There is no fixed duration. Sweet wines use other techniques, such as highly concentrated grapes, filtration or adding alcohol.":"最終的酒精濃度取決於起始糖分：大多數不甜葡萄酒為 11.5–16% abv。發酵沒有固定的時間長度。甜酒則使用其他技術，例如高度濃縮的葡萄、過濾或添加酒精。","For most wines, how long is the storage period before bottling, and with what effect?":"對大多數葡萄酒來說，裝瓶前的儲存期有多長？效果如何？","Less than a year, with flavours changing little if at all":"不到一年，風味幾乎沒有變化","Several years in oak, with strong tertiary development":"在橡木桶中數年，發展出強烈的三級香氣","A few days, during which the wine gets sweeter":"幾天，期間酒會變甜","At least ten years in bottle, because every wine improves with time":"至少在瓶中十年，因為每一款酒都會隨時間變好","Most wine is stored for under a year, sometimes only months, and changes very little.":"大多數葡萄酒儲存不到一年，有時只有幾個月，變化非常小。","Only some wines are kept for long; this is called maturation, with flavours moving from primary to tertiary. Most wines do not improve in bottle and are best drunk young. Storage adds no sugar.":"只有部分葡萄酒會長期存放；這稱為熟成，風味從一級香氣轉向三級香氣。大多數葡萄酒不會在瓶中變好，最好趁年輕飲用。儲存不會增加糖分。","What happens to a wine during extended maturation?":"長時間熟成期間，葡萄酒會發生什麼？","Flavours move from primary to tertiary and tannins become more integrated":"風味從一級轉向三級，單寧變得更融合","The wine regains the flavours of fresh grape juice":"酒重新獲得新鮮葡萄汁的風味","The alcohol rises by a few degrees":"酒精上升幾度","Tannins get harsher and red wines keep getting deeper in colour":"單寧變得更粗糙，紅酒的顏色越來越深","Maturation brings tertiary flavours and makes structure, such as tannin, more integrated.":"熟成帶來三級風味，並讓單寧等結構更融合。","Maturation usually takes place in oak, which can also add secondary flavours. Fruit loses freshness and never returns to fresh juice character. Tannins soften and red colour tends to fade; alcohol does not rise.":"熟成通常在橡木桶中進行，橡木桶也可能增添二級風味。果味失去新鮮感，再也不會回到新鮮果汁的特徵。單寧變柔和，紅酒的顏色傾向變淡；酒精不會上升。","What is still the most popular form of wine packaging?":"至今最受歡迎的葡萄酒包裝形式是什麼？","The glass bottle":"玻璃瓶","Bag-in-box":"盒中袋","The plastic bottle":"塑膠瓶","The carton brick, now used more than any other container":"紙盒包裝，現在比任何其他容器都更常用","Glass bottles remain the most widely used wine packaging.":"玻璃瓶仍然是使用最廣泛的葡萄酒包裝。","Bag-in-box, plastic bottles and cartons are real alternatives, but less common than glass. Packaging is the last step, after storage or maturation.":"盒中袋、塑膠瓶和紙盒都是實際可行的替代方案，但不如玻璃瓶普遍。包裝是最後一步，在儲存或熟成之後。","Which two conditions are needed to make a red wine?":"釀造紅酒需要哪兩個條件？","Black grapes, with the skins in the fermentation":"黑葡萄，且果皮參與發酵","Black grapes, pressed before fermentation":"黑葡萄，且在發酵前壓榨","Any grapes, and ageing in new oak":"任何葡萄，並在新橡木桶中陳年","White and black grapes mixed and fermented very cool":"白葡萄和黑葡萄混合，在非常低溫下發酵","Red wine comes from black grapes fermented with their skins, which give colour and tannin.":"紅酒來自與果皮一起發酵的黑葡萄，果皮帶來顏色和單寧。","Pressing black grapes before fermentation gives a white or nearly white wine, because the colour stays in the skins. Oak does not make wine red. Reds ferment warmer, 20–32°C, precisely to extract more.":"在發酵前壓榨黑葡萄，會得到白酒或近乎白色的酒，因為顏色留在果皮中。橡木桶不會讓酒變紅。紅酒在較高的溫度（20–32°C）下發酵，正是為了萃取更多。","In punching down, how are the skins mixed with the liquid?":"壓帽時，果皮是怎麼與液體混合的？","A plunger pushes the cap down into the liquid":"用壓棒把酒帽壓入液體","Liquid from the bottom is pumped up and sprayed over the cap":"把底部的液體抽上來噴淋到酒帽上","The skins are filtered out":"把果皮過濾掉","Alcohol is added to make the skins sink to the bottom of the tank":"加入酒精讓果皮沉到槽底","Punching down uses a plunger to push the cap of skins into the liquid.":"壓帽是用壓棒把果皮形成的酒帽壓入液體中。","Pumping liquid from the bottom over the cap is pumping over, the other common technique. Both extract colour and tannin from the skins. Adding alcohol is fortification, which stops fermentation.":"把底部的液體抽上來淋在酒帽上是淋汁，另一種常見的技術。兩者都是從果皮萃取顏色和單寧。添加酒精是加烈，會中止發酵。","Why must the cap of skins be mixed often during red fermentation?":"為什麼紅酒發酵期間必須經常混合果皮形成的酒帽？","Left undisturbed on top, it gives up little colour and tannin":"如果放著不動浮在上面，它釋放的顏色和單寧很少","To cool the must down to 12°C":"為了把葡萄汁冷卻到 12°C","To remove all tannin from the wine":"為了去除酒中所有的單寧","To release the alcohol faster, which would otherwise stay trapped in the skins":"為了更快釋放原本會困在果皮中的酒精","Skins float to form the cap; without mixing, extraction stays poor.":"果皮浮起形成酒帽；不加混合，萃取效果就很差。","Fermentation heat helps extraction, but is not enough on its own. That is why winemakers punch down or pump over frequently and thoroughly. Low temperatures such as 12°C suit whites, not reds.":"發酵的熱有助於萃取，但光靠它還不夠。這就是為什麼釀酒師會頻繁而徹底地壓帽或淋汁。12°C 這樣的低溫適合白酒，不適合紅酒。","In red winemaking, why are the skins pressed after draining?":"釀造紅酒時，為什麼要在排汁後壓榨果皮？","To recover the wine left in the skins":"為了回收留在果皮中的酒","To start the alcoholic fermentation":"為了開始酒精發酵","To make a rosé":"為了釀造粉紅酒","To add the sugar left in the skins and make the wine sweeter":"為了加入果皮中殘留的糖，讓酒更甜","After fermentation the wine is drained off, then the press extracts what remains in the skins.":"發酵後先把酒排出，再用壓榨機取出留在果皮中的部分。","The red order is crushing, fermentation, draining, pressing, storage, packaging. By then fermentation is over and the sugar has been used up. Rosé is made by separating the juice from the skins after only a few hours.":"紅酒的順序是破皮、發酵、排汁、壓榨、儲存、包裝。到這時發酵已經結束，糖也已經用完了。粉紅酒則是在短短幾小時後就把果汁與果皮分開。","In a short-maceration rosé, at what temperature does fermentation continue once the skins are removed?":"以短時間浸皮法釀造粉紅酒時，移除果皮後，發酵在什麼溫度下繼續？","At temperatures similar to white wines":"與白酒類似的溫度","At red-wine temperatures, up to 32°C":"紅酒的溫度，最高 32°C","Below freezing, as for icewine":"冰點以下，就像冰酒","It doesn't: fermentation always stops when the skins come out":"不會繼續：果皮一取出，發酵就停止","Once drained, rosé ferments like a white, at cooler temperatures.":"排汁後，粉紅酒像白酒一樣在較低溫度下發酵。","Fermentation starts as for a red, but the liquid is drained off the skins after a few hours and carries on without them. There is no more need to extract colour and tannin, so cooler temperatures are used. Rosés are rarely matured in oak.":"發酵一開始像紅酒，但幾小時後把液體從果皮中排出，接著在沒有果皮的情況下繼續發酵。這時已經不需要萃取顏色和單寧，所以使用較低的溫度。粉紅酒很少在橡木桶中熟成。","Which statement about maturing rosé wines is correct?":"關於粉紅酒的熟成，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","They are rarely stored or matured in oak":"它們很少在橡木桶中儲存或熟成","They are always matured in new barriques":"它們總是在新的小型橡木桶中熟成","They must age for at least five years":"它們必須陳年至少五年","They stay on the skins for months during maturation to deepen the colour":"熟成期間它們與果皮接觸數月，以加深顏色","Rosés usually skip oak, which keeps their flavours fresh and fruity.":"粉紅酒通常不經橡木桶，這能讓風味保持清新果香。","The rosé style relies on fresh fruit, which oak flavours would mask. Skin contact lasts only a few hours; months of maceration would make a red. There is no minimum ageing requirement for rosé.":"粉紅酒的風格仰賴新鮮果味，橡木桶的風味會掩蓋它。果皮接觸只持續幾個小時；浸皮數月就會變成紅酒了。粉紅酒沒有最低陳年要求。","In white winemaking, what usually happens to the grape skins?":"釀造白酒時，葡萄果皮通常會怎樣？","They are removed at pressing, before fermentation":"在發酵前的壓榨階段被移除","They ferment with the juice for several days":"與果汁一起發酵數天","They are added back after fermentation for tannin":"在發酵後重新加入以增添單寧","They are kept throughout maturation, forming a cap on top of the wine":"在整個熟成期間保留，在酒液表面形成酒帽","For whites, grapes are crushed and pressed before fermentation and the skins are usually discarded.":"釀造白酒時，葡萄在發酵前破皮和壓榨，果皮通常被丟棄。","The white order is crushing, pressing, fermentation, storage, packaging. A cap of skins and long extraction belong to red winemaking. That is why white wines have very little tannin.":"白酒的順序是破皮、壓榨、發酵、儲存、包裝。果皮形成的酒帽和長時間萃取屬於紅酒釀造。這就是為什麼白酒的單寧非常少。","What is residual sugar?":"什麼是殘糖？","Sugar added to the juice before fermentation":"發酵前加入果汁中的糖","Sugar that settles at the bottom of the bottle":"沉澱在酒瓶底部的糖","Sugar left in the stems and seeds after pressing":"壓榨後殘留在果梗和葡萄籽中的糖","It is the sugar not converted into alcohol that remains in the finished wine.":"殘糖是沒有被轉化為酒精、留在成品酒中的糖。","Off-dry wines have a little, sweet wines can have a great deal. Sugar added before fermentation raises alcohol and is normally fermented away. Bottle deposit is typical of aged reds, not sugar.":"微甜的酒有一點殘糖，甜酒則可能有非常多。發酵前加入的糖會提高酒精，通常會被發酵掉。瓶中沉澱物是陳年紅酒的典型特徵，不是糖。","Why does juice from raisined, botrytised or frozen grapes often give a sweet wine without intervention?":"為什麼用風乾、貴腐或冰凍葡萄的果汁，常常不需干預就能釀出甜酒？","There is so much sugar that the yeast cannot eat it all":"糖多到酵母無法全部吃完","These juices contain no yeast":"這些果汁不含酵母","Alcohol is always added to stop fermentation":"總是會添加酒精來中止發酵","Very high acidity turns the alcohol already made back into sugar":"非常高的酸度把已經產生的酒精變回糖","With such concentrated sugar, fermentation stops by itself, leaving residual sugar.":"糖分如此濃縮，發酵會自行停止，留下殘糖。","Hungary's Tokaji Aszú is an example of this method. Adding alcohol is a different technique, fortification, used for example in Port. Yeast are present; they simply stop before finishing the sugar.":"匈牙利的 Tokaji Aszú 就是這種方法的例子。添加酒精是另一種技術，稱為加烈，例如用於 Port。酵母是存在的；它們只是在吃完糖之前就停止了。","Which of these is NOT one of the ways of adding sweetness to a dry wine?":"下列哪一項不是為不甜的酒添加甜味的方法之一？","Adding cane sugar syrup":"加入蔗糖糖漿","Adding unfermented grape juice":"加入未發酵的葡萄汁","Adding concentrated grape juice":"加入濃縮葡萄汁","Blending the dry wine with a sweet wine":"把不甜的酒與甜酒混合","The added sweetness comes from grapes: juice, concentrated juice or a sweet wine.":"添加的甜味來自葡萄：葡萄汁、濃縮葡萄汁或甜酒。","This technique is widely used because it allows precise control of sweetness, for reds, whites and rosés. The three valid options all use grape sugars. Cane sugar is not among the methods described.":"這項技術使用廣泛，因為它能精準控制紅酒、白酒和粉紅酒的甜度。三個有效的選項都使用葡萄的糖。蔗糖不在所述的方法之中。","In a cool vintage the grapes are too acidic. What can the winemaker do?":"在涼爽的年份，葡萄太酸。釀酒師可以怎麼做？","Neutralise some of the acid":"中和一部分的酸","Add more acid":"加入更多酸","Ferment at 32°C":"在 32°C 下發酵","Add fresh grape juice after bottling to dilute the acidity":"在裝瓶後加入新鮮葡萄汁來稀釋酸度","In cool conditions some acid can be neutralised so the wine is not unbalanced by acidity.":"在涼爽的條件下，可以中和一部分的酸，以免酸度讓酒失去平衡。","Adding acid is the typical correction in warm climates, where acidity falls too low. In cool conditions the winemaker may also raise the sugar in the juice for more alcohol and body. Adjustments are made during winemaking, not after bottling.":"加酸是溫暖氣候的典型調整，那裡的酸度會降得太低。在涼爽的條件下，釀酒師也可能提高果汁中的糖分，以獲得更多酒精和酒體。調整是在釀造過程中進行的，不是在裝瓶後。","Why must the winemaker monitor fermentation temperature?":"為什麼釀酒師必須監控發酵溫度？","Fermentation creates heat, and the temperature must suit the style":"發酵會產生熱，而溫度必須符合想要的風格","Otherwise the wine turns sparkling":"否則酒會變成氣泡酒","To decide which vintage goes on the label":"為了決定酒標上要標示哪個年份","Because the law requires the same temperature for all wines, white or red":"因為法律規定所有葡萄酒，無論白酒或紅酒，都要用相同的溫度","Fermentation warms the juice, so it must be kept within the right range for the intended wine.":"發酵會讓果汁升溫，所以必須把溫度保持在適合目標酒款的範圍內。","Wineries today have technology to chill or warm a fermentation. Reds and whites have different ranges, 20–32°C versus 12–22°C, so there is no single temperature. The vintage depends only on the harvest year.":"現今的酒廠擁有可以為發酵降溫或加溫的技術。紅酒和白酒的溫度範圍不同，分別是 20–32°C 和 12–22°C，所以沒有單一的溫度。年份只取決於採收年。","A tank of red wine is fermenting at 28°C. What would a winemaker think?":"一槽紅酒正在 28°C 下發酵。釀酒師會怎麼想？","It is a normal temperature for a red":"這是紅酒的正常溫度","Too hot: reds ferment between 12 and 22°C":"太熱了：紅酒應在 12 到 22°C 之間發酵","Too cold to extract any colour":"太冷了，無法萃取任何顏色","It is the typical temperature for a rosé already drained off its skins":"這是已經排汁的粉紅酒的典型溫度","Reds usually ferment at 20–32°C, so 28°C is well within range.":"紅酒通常在 20–32°C 發酵，所以 28°C 完全在範圍內。","Higher temperatures help extract colour and tannin from the skins. The 12–22°C range is for whites, and for rosé after draining. At 28°C extraction is helped, not prevented.":"較高的溫度有助於從果皮萃取顏色和單寧。12–22°C 的範圍適用於白酒，以及排汁後的粉紅酒。在 28°C 下，萃取是受到幫助，而不是被阻礙。","What is today the most common way of killing the yeast to leave sugar in the wine?":"現今殺死酵母、把糖留在酒中最常見的方法是什麼？","Adding alcohol to the fermenting juice":"在發酵中的果汁裡添加酒精","Chilling the wine to 12°C":"把酒冷卻到 12°C","Mixing the cap of skins often during fermentation":"在發酵期間經常混合果皮形成的酒帽","Fortification raises alcohol to 15–20% abv, which kills the yeast.":"加烈把酒精提高到 15–20% abv，從而殺死酵母。","There are several ways to kill yeast, but adding alcohol is the most widely used today. 12°C is a normal white fermentation temperature and does not stop yeast. Acid adjusts balance, and mixing the cap is for extraction.":"殺死酵母的方法有好幾種，但添加酒精是現今使用最廣泛的。12°C 是白酒的正常發酵溫度，不會讓酵母停止。酸用來調整平衡，混合酒帽則是為了萃取。","Why would a winemaker choose stainless steel for a fresh, fruity white?":"為什麼釀酒師會為清爽果香的白酒選擇不鏽鋼槽？","It is inert and can be airtight":"它是惰性的，而且可以密封","It adds vanilla flavours":"它會增添香草風味","It lets oxygen in":"它會讓氧氣進入","It softens tannins":"它會讓單寧變柔和","Steel adds no flavour and can keep oxygen out, preserving the fruit.":"不鏽鋼不會增添風味，還能隔絕氧氣，保留果味。","Stainless steel and concrete are inert materials: they give no flavour to the wine. They can also be made airtight, stopping oxygen from changing the flavours. For a white where the aim is fresh, primary fruit, they are the ideal choice. Vanilla, oxygen contact and softer tannins are, by contrast, typical effects of oak barrels.":"不鏽鋼和混凝土是惰性材質：它們不會為酒增添任何風味。它們也可以做成密封的，防止氧氣改變風味。對於追求新鮮一級果味的白酒來說，它們是理想的選擇。相反地，香草、與氧氣接觸和更柔和的單寧，是橡木桶的典型效果。","Which pair of vessel materials is considered inert?":"下列哪一組容器材質被視為惰性的？","Stainless steel and concrete":"不鏽鋼和混凝土","New oak and old oak":"新橡木桶和舊橡木桶","Oak and concrete":"橡木和混凝土","Stainless steel and oak":"不鏽鋼和橡木","Stainless steel and concrete add no flavour to the wine.":"不鏽鋼和混凝土不會為酒增添風味。","Winery vessels divide into inert and oak. Stainless steel and concrete are inert: they can be used for fermentation and storage without changing the flavours. Oak, new or old, is not inert: even an old barrel, which gives little flavour, still lets oxygen in and makes the wine evolve during maturation.":"酒廠的容器分為惰性容器和橡木容器。不鏽鋼和混凝土是惰性的：可以用來發酵和儲存而不改變風味。橡木無論新舊都不是惰性的：即使是幾乎不帶風味的舊桶，仍然會讓氧氣進入，使酒在熟成期間演變。","What are the two ways an oak barrel influences wine style?":"橡木桶影響葡萄酒風格的兩種方式是什麼？","Adding flavour and allowing oxygen contact":"增添風味，以及讓酒與氧氣接觸","Raising alcohol and acidity":"提高酒精和酸度","Adding sugar and tannin":"增添糖分和單寧","Filtering the wine and clarifying it":"過濾並澄清酒液","Oak gives its own flavours and, not being airtight, lets oxygen in.":"橡木桶會帶來自身的風味，而且因為不密封，會讓氧氣進入。","Barrels are watertight but not airtight. They therefore work in two ways: they add flavours such as vanilla, coconut or spice directly, especially when new, and they let a little oxygen interact with the wine, developing caramel and nut notes and softening red wine tannins. They do not raise alcohol, acidity or sugar.":"橡木桶不漏水，但並不密封。因此它以兩種方式發揮作用：直接增添香草、椰子或香料等風味，尤其是新桶；以及讓少量氧氣與酒相互作用，發展出焦糖和堅果氣息，並讓紅酒的單寧變柔和。它們不會提高酒精、酸度或糖分。","Which flavours are typical of a new oak barrel?":"哪些風味是新橡木桶的典型特徵？","Vanilla, coconut, charred wood, spice":"香草、椰子、炭烤木頭、香料","Biscuit, bread, toast crust":"餅乾、麵包、烤麵包皮","Butter, cream, yoghurt":"奶油、鮮奶油、優格","Fig, prune, wet leaves":"無花果、黑李乾、濕葉子","New oak gives lots of flavour: vanilla, coconut, charred wood and spice.":"新橡木桶帶來大量風味：香草、椰子、炭烤木頭和香料。","A barrel that has never been used still has all its flavour potential and can give a lot: vanilla, coconut, charred wood and spice. Biscuit and bread notes come instead from lees contact, buttery notes from malolactic conversion, while fig, prune and wet leaves are tertiary flavours of reds aged in bottle.":"從未使用過的橡木桶仍保有全部的風味潛力，能帶來很多風味：香草、椰子、炭烤木頭和香料。餅乾和麵包的氣息則來自與酒渣接觸，奶油氣息來自乳酸轉化，而無花果、黑李乾和濕葉子是瓶中陳年紅酒的三級風味。","After how many uses does a barrel have very little flavour left to give?":"橡木桶使用幾次之後，就幾乎沒有風味可以給了？","After two or three uses":"使用兩到三次之後","After a single use":"只使用一次之後","Never, oak always gives flavour":"永遠不會，橡木總是會帶來風味","After two or three uses a barrel is old oak, with little flavour left.":"使用兩到三次之後，橡木桶就成了舊桶，幾乎沒有風味可以給了。","Every time a barrel is filled it gives up some of its flavour. From the second use it already gives less than a new barrel, and after two or three uses it has very little left: this is called old oak. Such barrels are still useful when the aim is the effect of oxygen without strong oak character.":"每次裝酒，橡木桶都會釋出一部分風味。從第二次使用起，它給的風味就已經比新桶少，使用兩到三次之後就幾乎所剩無幾：這稱為舊桶。當目標是氧氣的效果、而不要強烈的橡木特徵時，這樣的桶仍然很有用。","What determines a barrel's toast level?":"什麼決定了橡木桶的烘烤程度？","How long and how hot the staves are heated":"桶板加熱的時間長短和溫度高低","The age of the oak trees":"橡樹的樹齡","How many times the barrel has been used":"橡木桶使用過的次數","The temperature of the cellar":"酒窖的溫度","Staves are heated over flame: time and heat set the toast level.":"桶板在火上加熱：時間和熱度決定烘烤程度。","To make a barrel, the oak staves are heated over an open flame and bent into shape. The longer and hotter the heating, the higher the toast level. Toasting changes the flavours the wood gives to the wine and can produce sweet-spice and charred-wood notes.":"製作橡木桶時，橡木桶板在明火上加熱並彎曲成形。加熱時間越長、溫度越高，烘烤程度就越高。烘烤會改變木頭為酒帶來的風味，可能產生甜香料和炭烤木頭的氣息。","Why do oxygen-related changes happen faster in small barrels?":"為什麼在小型橡木桶中，與氧氣相關的變化發生得比較快？","More of the wine is in contact with the wood":"有更多的酒與木頭接觸","Small barrels are always made of newer oak":"小型橡木桶總是用較新的橡木製成","Small barrels are airtight":"小型橡木桶是密封的","Small barrels are more heavily toasted":"小型橡木桶烘烤得比較重","In small barrels a greater share of the wine touches the wood.":"在小型橡木桶中，有較大比例的酒接觸到木頭。","In a small barrel the ratio of wood surface to wine volume is higher, so more of the wine is in contact with the barrel. Interactions with oxygen, such as the development of caramel and nut flavours and the softening of tannins, therefore happen faster. Large oak vessels are rarely used to give oak flavour.":"在小型橡木桶中，木頭表面積與酒液體積的比例較高，所以有更多的酒與桶接觸。因此，與氧氣的相互作用，例如焦糖和堅果風味的發展以及單寧的柔化，發生得更快。大型橡木容器很少用來增添橡木風味。","Which flavours can develop from oxygen during barrel maturation?":"橡木桶熟成期間，氧氣會發展出哪些風味？","Caramel, dried fruit, hazelnut":"焦糖、果乾、榛果","Citrus, green apple, flowers":"柑橘、青蘋果、花香","Butter and cream":"奶油和鮮奶油","Bread and biscuit":"麵包和餅乾","Oxygen entering the barrel develops caramel, dried fruit and nut notes.":"進入橡木桶的氧氣會發展出焦糖、果乾和堅果氣息。","Barrels are not airtight: during maturation a little oxygen gets in and interacts with the wine, encouraging caramel, dried fruit and nut flavours such as hazelnut, almond and walnut. Citrus and green apple are primary grape flavours; butter comes from malolactic conversion; bread and biscuit from lees contact.":"橡木桶並不密封：熟成期間少量氧氣進入並與酒相互作用，促進焦糖、果乾以及榛果、杏仁和核桃等堅果風味。柑橘和青蘋果是葡萄的一級風味；奶油來自乳酸轉化；麵包和餅乾來自與酒渣接觸。","How can oak flavour be given to an inexpensive wine?":"如何為平價的葡萄酒增添橡木風味？","With staves or chips in an inert vessel":"在惰性容器中加入橡木條或橡木片","With long lees contact":"長時間與酒渣接觸","Through malolactic conversion":"透過乳酸轉化","With large old oak vessels":"使用大型舊橡木容器","Staves and chips cost far less than barrels and still give oak flavour.":"橡木條和橡木片比橡木桶便宜得多，仍然能帶來橡木風味。","Oak barrels are expensive. For cheaper wines, oak staves or chips can be added to wine stored in an inert vessel, giving oak flavour at a lower cost. Large old oak vessels rarely add oak flavour, while lees and malolactic conversion give bread and buttery notes respectively, not oak.":"橡木桶很昂貴。對於較便宜的葡萄酒，可以在儲存於惰性容器中的酒裡加入橡木條或橡木片，以較低的成本帶來橡木風味。大型舊橡木容器很少增添橡木風味，而酒渣和乳酸轉化分別帶來麵包和奶油氣息，不是橡木風味。","Which microorganism carries out malolactic conversion?":"哪一種微生物進行乳酸轉化？","Moulds from the oak":"來自橡木的黴菌","Malolactic conversion is carried out by bacteria, not yeast.":"乳酸轉化是由細菌進行的，不是酵母。","Malolactic conversion takes place after alcoholic fermentation and is the work of bacteria. Yeast are responsible for alcoholic fermentation, while botrytis is a fungus that acts in the vineyard, concentrating grape sugars. The bacteria's activity lowers the wine's acidity and can add buttery flavours.":"乳酸轉化發生在酒精發酵之後，是細菌的作用。酵母負責酒精發酵，而貴腐菌是在葡萄園中作用、濃縮葡萄糖分的真菌。細菌的活動會降低酒的酸度，並可能增添奶油風味。","What are the effects of malolactic conversion?":"乳酸轉化有什麼效果？","Lower acidity and possible buttery flavours":"降低酸度，可能帶來奶油風味","Higher acidity and citrus flavours":"提高酸度，帶來柑橘風味","More alcohol and more body":"更多酒精和更飽滿的酒體","More tannin and deeper colour":"更多單寧和更深的顏色","The bacteria lower acidity and can give buttery flavours.":"細菌會降低酸度，並可能帶來奶油風味。","The bacteria's activity during malolactic conversion lowers the wine's acidity and can add buttery flavours, giving a softer style. It does not produce alcohol, which comes only from yeast in alcoholic fermentation, nor does it add tannin or colour, which come from the skins. That is why it is avoided when a lively, fresh white is wanted.":"乳酸轉化期間細菌的活動會降低酒的酸度，並可能增添奶油風味，讓風格更柔和。它不會產生酒精，酒精只來自酒精發酵中的酵母；也不會增添單寧或顏色，那些來自果皮。這就是為什麼想要活潑清爽的白酒時會避免它。","For which grape is malolactic conversion usually prevented?":"對哪一個品種通常會阻止乳酸轉化？","For aromatic grapes like Riesling, acidity and fruit are kept intact.":"對於麗絲玲這類芳香品種，會完整保留酸度和果味。","In whites, malolactic conversion is a choice. For aromatic varieties like Riesling it is usually prevented, because it would lower acidity and add buttery notes that would mask the fruit. Certain styles of Chardonnay, on the other hand, benefit from it. In reds such as Cabernet Sauvignon and Pinot Noir it nearly always takes place.":"對白酒來說，乳酸轉化是一種選擇。對於麗絲玲這類芳香品種，通常會阻止它，因為它會降低酸度，並增添掩蓋果味的奶油氣息。另一方面，某些風格的夏多內則受益於它。在卡本內蘇維濃和黑皮諾等紅酒中，它幾乎總是會發生。","What are lees?":"什麼是酒渣？","Dead yeast cells that settle at the bottom":"沉到底部的死酵母細胞","Skins floating on the surface":"浮在表面的果皮","Oak chips added to the wine":"加入酒中的橡木片","The deposit in aged red wines":"陳年紅酒中的沉澱物","After fermentation the yeast die and form a layer at the bottom.":"發酵結束後，酵母死亡並在底部形成一層。","When alcoholic fermentation ends, the yeast die and fall to the bottom of the vessel, forming a layer of dead cells: the lees. Floating skins form the cap in red winemaking instead, and the deposit that appears in reds aged in bottle is a different phenomenon, linked to maturation.":"酒精發酵結束時，酵母死亡並落到容器底部，形成一層死細胞：這就是酒渣。浮起的果皮則是在紅酒釀造中形成酒帽，而瓶中陳年紅酒出現的沉澱物是另一種與熟成相關的現象。","What effect does stirring the lees have on a white wine?":"攪動酒渣對白酒有什麼效果？","More body and bread and biscuit flavours":"更飽滿的酒體，以及麵包和餅乾風味","More acidity and citrus flavours":"更高的酸度和柑橘風味","More tannin and colour":"更多單寧和顏色","Less alcohol and less body":"酒精更低，酒體更輕","Lees contact adds body and bread and biscuit notes.":"與酒渣接觸會增添酒體以及麵包和餅乾氣息。","If the winemaker keeps a white in contact with its lees, they can be stirred through the wine during maturation. This increases the wine's body and adds flavours such as biscuit and bread. It does not raise acidity or tannin, nor lower alcohol. It is a typical choice for rich whites, often combined with malolactic conversion or oak.":"如果釀酒師讓白酒與酒渣保持接觸，就可以在熟成期間把酒渣攪入酒中。這會增加酒體，並增添餅乾和麵包等風味。它不會提高酸度或單寧，也不會降低酒精。這是豐潤型白酒的典型選擇，常與乳酸轉化或橡木桶結合。","Why are different wines blended each year for a branded wine?":"為什麼品牌酒每年都要混調不同的酒？","To keep the style consistent":"為了保持風格一致","To avoid malolactic conversion":"為了避免乳酸轉化","To make the wine clearer":"為了讓酒更清澈","Consumers expect a branded wine to taste the same every year.":"消費者期待品牌酒每年喝起來都一樣。","Each vintage gives different wines because of climate and weather. For a branded wine, though, consumers expect the same taste year after year. The winemaker therefore blends different wines to rebuild the same profile. Blending also serves to create complexity, but its purpose is not to raise alcohol or clarify the wine.":"由於氣候和天氣，每個年份的酒都不同。但對於品牌酒，消費者期待年年都是同樣的味道。因此釀酒師會混調不同的酒，重建相同的風味特徵。混調也用來創造複雜度，但它的目的不是提高酒精或澄清酒液。","Which kind of blending aims mainly at complexity?":"哪一種混調主要是為了複雜度？","Combining wines from different grapes, sites or techniques":"結合來自不同品種、園地或技術的酒","Combining dry wine and grape juice":"結合不甜的酒和葡萄汁","Combining red and white wine":"結合紅酒和白酒","Combining wine and spirit":"結合葡萄酒和烈酒","Different components make the wine more complex than its parts.":"不同的組成讓酒比各部分更複雜。","By blending wines from different grape varieties, vineyard locations or techniques, the winemaker creates a wine more complex than its individual components. Combining dry wine with juice is used for sweetening, combining red and white is a rosé method, and adding spirit is fortification.":"透過混調來自不同葡萄品種、葡萄園位置或技術的酒，釀酒師能創造出比各個組成更複雜的酒。結合不甜的酒和葡萄汁是為了增甜，結合紅酒和白酒是粉紅酒的釀法，加入烈酒則是加烈。","Why do some winemakers choose not to filter their wine?":"為什麼有些釀酒師選擇不過濾他們的酒？","They feel it can strip the wine's character":"他們認為過濾可能剝奪酒的個性","It makes the wine more alcoholic":"過濾會讓酒的酒精更高","It adds oak flavours":"過濾會增添橡木風味","It increases the wine's acidity":"過濾會提高酒的酸度","Some believe filtration can take something away from the wine's character.":"有些人認為過濾可能奪走酒的部分個性。","Most consumers want a perfectly clear wine, and filtration helps achieve that. Some winemakers, however, feel these techniques can take something away from the wine's character and prefer not to use them. Their wine may therefore look less than perfectly clear in the glass. Filtration does not affect alcohol, oak or acidity.":"大多數消費者想要完全清澈的酒，而過濾有助於達到這一點。不過，有些釀酒師認為這些技術可能奪走酒的部分個性，因此寧可不用。他們的酒在杯中可能看起來不那麼完全清澈。過濾不會影響酒精、橡木或酸度。","How does a white wine's colour change with age?":"白酒的顏色如何隨年齡變化？","Lemon → gold → amber, deeper":"檸檬色 → 金黃色 → 琥珀色，越來越深","Gold → lemon → green, paler":"金黃色 → 檸檬色 → 綠色，越來越淺","Amber → gold → lemon, paler":"琥珀色 → 金黃色 → 檸檬色，越來越淺","Lemon → pink → garnet":"檸檬色 → 粉紅色 → 石榴紅","Whites go from lemon to gold to amber and deepen in colour.":"白酒從檸檬色變成金黃色再到琥珀色，顏色加深。","Over time, the colour of whites moves from lemon to gold and finally amber, also becoming deeper. This is the opposite of reds, which tend to get paler with age, moving from ruby to garnet, tawny and brown. Alongside the colour change, tertiary flavours such as dried apricot, honey, nut and spice appear.":"隨著時間推移，白酒的顏色從檸檬色轉為金黃色，最後成為琥珀色，同時也變得更深。這與紅酒相反，紅酒隨著陳年往往變淡，從寶石紅轉為石榴紅、茶褐色和褐色。伴隨顏色變化，還會出現杏桃乾、蜂蜜、堅果和香料等三級風味。","Which set of flavours signals a red wine that has aged in bottle?":"哪一組風味表示紅酒經過瓶中陳年？","Fig, prune, meat, wet leaves":"無花果、黑李乾、肉、濕葉子","Strawberry, raspberry, fresh cherry":"草莓、覆盆子、新鮮櫻桃","Butter, bread, biscuit":"奶油、麵包、餅乾","Fig, prune, meat and wet leaves are tertiary flavours of reds.":"無花果、黑李乾、肉和濕葉子是紅酒的三級風味。","With bottle age, the fresh fruit of reds gives way to dried fruit and complex notes: fig, prune, meat and wet leaves, as well as mushroom and leather. Strawberry and fresh cherry are primary flavours of a young wine; vanilla and coconut come from new oak; butter, bread and biscuit from malolactic conversion and lees.":"經過瓶中陳年，紅酒的新鮮果味讓位給果乾和複雜的氣息：無花果、黑李乾、肉和濕葉子，還有蘑菇和皮革。草莓和新鮮櫻桃是年輕酒款的一級風味；香草和椰子來自新橡木桶；奶油、麵包和餅乾則來自乳酸轉化和酒渣。","Which feature matters most for a wine to improve in bottle?":"一款酒要在瓶中變好，哪個特徵最重要？","Enough concentration of flavour":"足夠的風味濃縮度","A low alcohol level":"低酒精濃度","Low acidity":"低酸度","A plastic closure":"塑膠瓶塞","Above all, the wine needs enough flavour concentration to evolve well.":"最重要的是，酒需要足夠的風味濃縮度才能好好演變。","Most wines do not improve in bottle: their fruit fades and vegetal notes appear. Wines for ageing often have high acidity, plenty of sugar if sweet and plenty of tannin if red, components that preserve them. Above all, though, they need enough concentration of flavour to evolve positively and gain complexity.":"大多數葡萄酒不會在瓶中變好：果味會消退，出現植物性氣息。適合陳年的酒往往酸度高，若是甜酒則糖分多，若是紅酒則單寧多，這些成分能保存酒。但最重要的是，它們需要足夠的風味濃縮度，才能正向演變並增添複雜度。","Which statement about oak barrels is correct?":"關於橡木桶，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","They are watertight but not airtight":"不漏水但不密封","They are airtight like steel tanks":"像不鏽鋼槽一樣密封","They let both air and wine through":"空氣和酒都會透過","They are inert and give no flavour to the wine, like concrete":"像混凝土一樣是惰性的，不會為酒增添風味","Wood holds the wine in but lets some oxygen in during maturation.":"木頭能留住酒液，但熟成期間會讓一些氧氣進入。","This oxygen contact is exactly what develops caramel, dried fruit and nut notes and softens tannins. Steel and concrete, by contrast, are inert and can be made airtight. Oak is not inert: especially when new, it adds flavour.":"正是這種與氧氣的接觸發展出焦糖、果乾和堅果氣息，並讓單寧變柔和。相反地，不鏽鋼和混凝土是惰性的，而且可以做成密封的。橡木不是惰性的：尤其是新桶，會增添風味。","A winemaker wants a wine to mature with some oxygen contact but without picking up oak flavour. Which vessel fits best?":"一位釀酒師希望酒在熟成時與一些氧氣接觸，但不沾染橡木風味。哪一種容器最合適？","A large, old oak vessel":"大型舊橡木容器","A small, new, heavily toasted barrel":"重度烘烤的小型新橡木桶","A sealed stainless steel tank":"密封的不鏽鋼槽","A sealed concrete tank with new oak chips added":"加入新橡木片的密封混凝土槽","Large old oak vessels allow oxygen exchange but give very little oak flavour.":"大型舊橡木容器允許氧氣交換，但帶來的橡木風味非常少。","Large vessels are rarely used to add oak flavour, and after two or three uses the wood has little left to give. A small new barrel would add lots of oak. A sealed steel tank keeps oxygen out, and chips are used precisely to add oak flavour.":"大型容器很少用來增添橡木風味，而木頭使用兩到三次之後也所剩無幾。小型新橡木桶會增添大量橡木風味。密封的不鏽鋼槽會隔絕氧氣，而橡木片正是用來增添橡木風味的。","What effect does oxygen entering the barrel have on a red wine's tannins?":"進入橡木桶的氧氣對紅酒的單寧有什麼影響？","It softens them":"讓單寧變柔和","It makes them harsher and bitter":"讓單寧變粗糙苦澀","It removes them completely":"把單寧完全去除","None, because oxygen only affects white wines":"沒有影響，因為氧氣只影響白酒","Slow oxygen contact helps soften red wine tannins.":"緩慢的氧氣接觸有助於柔化紅酒的單寧。","These changes are faster in small barrels, where more of the wine touches the wood. Tannins soften but do not disappear. Oxygen affects whites and reds alike, developing notes such as caramel and dried fruit.":"在小型橡木桶中，這些變化更快，因為有更多的酒接觸到木頭。單寧會變柔和，但不會消失。氧氣對白酒和紅酒都有影響，會發展出焦糖和果乾等氣息。","Which aromas are linked in particular to the toast level of a barrel?":"哪些香氣特別與橡木桶的烘烤程度有關？","Sweet spice and charred wood":"甜香料和炭烤木頭","Fresh citrus and crisp green apple":"清新的柑橘和爽脆的青蘋果","Heating the staves over a flame gives sweet-spice and charred-wood notes.":"在火上加熱桶板會帶來甜香料和炭烤木頭的氣息。","Butter and cream come from malolactic conversion, bread and biscuit from lees contact. Citrus and green apple are primary grape aromas. The length and heat of toasting decide how strong it is.":"奶油和鮮奶油來自乳酸轉化，麵包和餅乾來自與酒渣接觸。柑橘和青蘋果是葡萄的一級香氣。烘烤的時間長短和溫度高低決定了烘烤的強度。","Which statement about concrete vessels is correct?":"關於混凝土容器，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","They are inert and can be used for fermentation and storage":"它們是惰性的，可用於發酵和儲存","They give vanilla and coconut flavours":"它們帶來香草和椰子風味","They are used only for storage, never for fermentation":"它們只用於儲存，從不用於發酵","They always let in lots of oxygen, more than a small oak barrel":"它們總是讓大量氧氣進入，比小型橡木桶還多","Like steel, concrete is inert, adds no flavour and is used for both fermentation and storage.":"和不鏽鋼一樣，混凝土是惰性的，不會增添風味，可同時用於發酵和儲存。","Concrete vessels can also be made airtight, stopping oxygen from changing the flavours. Vanilla and coconut are typical of new oak. It is oak, not concrete, that lets some oxygen in.":"混凝土容器也可以做成密封的，防止氧氣改變風味。香草和椰子是新橡木桶的典型特徵。讓一些氧氣進入的是橡木，不是混凝土。","When does malolactic conversion take place?":"乳酸轉化在什麼時候發生？","After the alcoholic fermentation":"酒精發酵之後","In the vineyard, during véraison":"在葡萄園中，轉色期間","At the same time as alcoholic fermentation, by the same yeast":"與酒精發酵同時，由同樣的酵母進行","Malolactic conversion follows alcoholic fermentation and is carried out by bacteria, not yeast.":"乳酸轉化在酒精發酵之後，由細菌而不是酵母進行。","It is a winery step that lowers acidity and may add buttery notes. It has nothing to do with the vineyard. The last option mixes up the two microorganisms: yeast for alcohol, bacteria for malolactic.":"這是在酒廠中進行的步驟，會降低酸度，並可能增添奶油氣息。它與葡萄園無關。最後一個選項把兩種微生物搞混了：酵母負責酒精，細菌負責乳酸轉化。","Which statement about malolactic conversion in red wines is correct?":"關於紅酒中的乳酸轉化，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It nearly always happens and buttery notes are barely noticeable":"它幾乎總是會發生，奶油氣息幾乎察覺不到","It is nearly always prevented":"它幾乎總是被阻止","It makes reds more acidic":"它讓紅酒更酸","It always gives reds a strong buttery aroma, far more than in whites":"它總是讓紅酒帶有強烈的奶油香氣，比白酒明顯得多","In reds, malolactic conversion is almost routine and buttery notes are not really noticeable.":"在紅酒中，乳酸轉化幾乎是例行步驟，奶油氣息並不明顯。","The real choice is for whites: winemakers can block it to keep acidity, as for Riesling, or seek it for some Chardonnay styles. It always lowers acidity, never raises it. Buttery notes are more obvious in some whites.":"真正需要選擇的是白酒：釀酒師可以阻止它以保留酸度，例如麗絲玲；也可以為某些夏多內風格刻意進行。它總是降低酸度，從不提高。奶油氣息在某些白酒中更明顯。","For which white grape can malolactic conversion benefit certain styles?":"乳酸轉化對哪一個白葡萄品種的某些風格有益？","None: in whites, malolactic is always a fault":"沒有：在白酒中，乳酸轉化總是缺陷","Any aromatic grape, because butter lifts floral aromas":"任何芳香品種，因為奶油會提升花香","Some Chardonnay styles benefit from malolactic conversion and its buttery notes.":"某些夏多內風格受益於乳酸轉化及其奶油氣息。","For aromatic grapes such as Riesling it is usually prevented, to keep acidity and aromatic purity. It is not a fault but a style choice. Buttery notes would mask floral aromas, not lift them.":"對於麗絲玲這類芳香品種，通常會阻止乳酸轉化，以保留酸度和純淨的香氣。它不是缺陷，而是一種風格選擇。奶油氣息會掩蓋花香，而不是提升花香。","A white wine smells of butter and cream. Which winemaking step best explains this?":"一款白酒聞起來有奶油和鮮奶油的氣味。哪一個釀造步驟最能解釋這一點？","A very cool fermentation":"非常低溫的發酵","Maturation in sealed steel":"在密封的不鏽鋼槽中熟成","A very early harvest to keep all the grapes' natural acidity":"非常早採收，以保留葡萄所有的天然酸度","Butter and cream are secondary aromas typical of malolactic conversion.":"奶油和鮮奶油是乳酸轉化典型的二級香氣。","Cheese can also be a malolactic aroma. A cool fermentation mainly gives fruity notes, and sealed steel adds nothing. An early harvest brings acidity and less ripe flavours, not dairy notes.":"乳酪也可能是乳酸轉化的香氣。低溫發酵主要帶來果香，密封的不鏽鋼槽則什麼也不增添。早採帶來酸度和較不成熟的風味，而不是乳製品氣息。","A white wine has more body than usual and bread and biscuit notes, but no oak. Which winery choice is most likely?":"一款白酒的酒體比平常飽滿，帶有麵包和餅乾氣息，但沒有橡木味。最可能是哪一種酒廠選擇？","Maturation on stirred lees":"在攪動的酒渣上熟成","Blocked malolactic conversion":"阻止乳酸轉化","Fermentation at red-wine temperature":"以紅酒的溫度發酵","Adding toasted oak chips to a steel tank":"在不鏽鋼槽中加入烘烤過的橡木片","Stirring the lees adds body and bread and biscuit flavours.":"攪動酒渣會增添酒體以及麵包和餅乾風味。","Lees are dead yeast cells that settle after fermentation; keeping wine on them is a typical white-wine choice. Oak chips would give oak flavours, which are absent here. Blocking malolactic keeps acidity but adds neither body nor bready notes.":"酒渣是發酵後沉澱的死酵母細胞；讓酒留在酒渣上是白酒的典型選擇。橡木片會帶來橡木風味，而這裡並沒有。阻止乳酸轉化能保留酸度，但不會增添酒體或麵包氣息。","At what point in winemaking can blending take place?":"混調可以在釀造過程的哪個時間點進行？","At many different stages of the process":"在過程中的許多不同階段","Only in the vineyard, before harvest":"只在葡萄園中，採收之前","Only after bottling":"只在裝瓶之後","Only on the day of crushing, never after fermentation starts":"只在破皮當天，發酵開始後就不行","Blending can happen at many stages of winemaking.":"混調可以在釀造的許多階段進行。","Blending defines and maintains a wine's style, for consistency or complexity. Wines from different grapes, sites or techniques can be combined. Once bottled, a wine is no longer blended.":"混調界定並維持酒的風格，以求一致或增添複雜度。可以結合來自不同品種、園地或技術的酒。酒一旦裝瓶，就不再混調。","A customer notices their wine is slightly hazy. The producer states it is unfiltered. What is the best reply?":"一位顧客發現他的酒有點混濁。生產者聲明這款酒未經過濾。最好的回答是什麼？","It is the producer's choice, to avoid stripping the wine's character":"這是生產者的選擇，為了避免剝奪酒的個性","The wine has definitely gone off":"這瓶酒肯定已經壞了","It shows a failed malolactic conversion":"這表示乳酸轉化失敗","The wine has clearly been aged in over-toasted new barrels":"這瓶酒顯然是在烘烤過度的新橡木桶中陳年的","Skipping filtration means accepting a less than perfectly clear wine to keep its character.":"不過濾，就是為了保留酒的個性而接受酒不那麼完全清澈。","Most customers expect perfectly clear wine, and filtration helps achieve this. Some producers, however, feel it takes something away from the wine. A slight haze in an unfiltered wine is not a fault in itself.":"大多數顧客期待完全清澈的酒，而過濾有助於做到這一點。不過，有些生產者認為過濾會奪走酒的某些東西。未過濾的酒略顯混濁，本身並不是缺陷。","What happens to most wines if they are kept in bottle for a long time?":"大多數葡萄酒如果在瓶中存放很久，會發生什麼？","Fruit fades and vegetal notes appear":"果味消退，出現植物性氣息","They always improve and gain complexity":"它們總是會變好，增添複雜度","They become sweeter":"它們會變甜","They stay exactly the same for decades as long as the bottle stays closed":"只要瓶子不開，它們數十年都會保持原樣","Most wines do not improve in bottle: fruit fades and is replaced by vegetal notes.":"大多數葡萄酒不會在瓶中變好：果味消退，被植物性氣息取代。","Only some wines, with the right features, develop positively over years or decades. For the rest, the vintage helps you tell whether they are still at their best. In bottle, wine neither gets sweeter nor stays unchanged.":"只有部分具備合適特徵的酒，會在數年或數十年間正向發展。至於其他的酒，年份能幫你判斷它們是否仍處於最佳狀態。在瓶中，酒既不會變甜，也不會保持不變。","Which feature does NOT help a wine keep and improve in bottle?":"下列哪一個特徵無助於酒在瓶中保存並變好？","Very low acidity":"非常低的酸度","High tannin, in a red":"高單寧（紅酒）","High residual sugar, in a sweet wine":"高殘糖（甜酒）","Enough concentration of flavour to develop positively":"足以正向發展的風味濃縮度","High acidity, sugar or tannin preserve a wine; low acidity does not help.":"高酸度、糖分或單寧能保存酒；低酸度則沒有幫助。","Wines for ageing often have high acidity and, depending on style, high residual sugar or tannin. Above all, they need enough flavour concentration to evolve into complexity. A low-acid wine tends to fade early instead.":"適合陳年的酒往往酸度高，並依風格有高殘糖或高單寧。最重要的是，它們需要足夠的風味濃縮度，才能演變出複雜度。低酸的酒反而往往很早就衰退。","In a wine that matures well in bottle, how do fresh fruit flavours evolve?":"在一款能在瓶中好好熟成的酒裡，新鮮果味會如何演變？","They turn to dried fruit, with notes such as mushroom and leather":"轉變為果乾，帶有蘑菇和皮革等氣息","They become fresher tropical fruit":"變成更新鮮的熱帶水果","They stay exactly the same":"保持完全不變","They turn into vanilla and coconut thanks to the cork":"多虧軟木塞而變成香草和椰子","With age, fresh fruit becomes dried fruit and complex notes such as mushroom and leather develop.":"隨著陳年，新鮮果味變成果乾，並發展出蘑菇和皮革等複雜氣息。","These are tertiary aromas, linked to ageing. Vanilla and coconut are secondary aromas from new oak, not the cork. Fruit loses freshness over time, so it does not become fresher.":"這些是與陳年相關的三級香氣。香草和椰子是來自新橡木桶的二級香氣，不是來自軟木塞。果味會隨時間失去新鮮感，所以不會變得更新鮮。","Which tertiary aromas can a white wine develop with bottle age?":"白酒經過瓶中陳年會發展出哪些三級香氣？","Dried apricot, honey, nuts and spice":"杏桃乾、蜂蜜、堅果和香料","Fresh strawberry and raspberry":"新鮮草莓和覆盆子","Cut grass and green apple":"青草和青蘋果","Green pepper, tomato leaf and asparagus, ever more intense":"青椒、番茄葉和蘆筍，越來越濃","With age a white can develop dried apricot, honey, nut and spice.":"隨著陳年，白酒可能發展出杏桃乾、蜂蜜、堅果和香料。","Grass, green apple and herbaceous notes are primary aromas, typical of young wines or less ripe grapes. Fresh red fruit is primary and mostly linked to reds. With age, white wine colour also moves from lemon to gold to amber.":"青草、青蘋果和草本氣息是一級香氣，是年輕酒款或較不成熟葡萄的典型特徵。新鮮紅色水果是一級香氣，主要與紅酒有關。隨著陳年，白酒的顏色也會從檸檬色轉為金黃色再到琥珀色。","With bottle age, how does colour intensity change in white and red wines?":"經過瓶中陳年，白酒和紅酒的顏色深淺如何變化？","Whites get deeper, reds get paler":"白酒變深，紅酒變淡","Both get paler":"兩者都變淡","Whites get paler, reds get deeper":"白酒變淡，紅酒變深","Neither changes in intensity; only the hue changes":"兩者的深淺都不變；只有色調改變","Whites deepen (lemon to gold to amber), while reds tend to lose intensity.":"白酒顏色加深（檸檬色到金黃色到琥珀色），而紅酒往往失去深度。","In reds, the hue moves from ruby to garnet to tawny and finally brown, with ever less intensity. In whites, by contrast, the colour deepens. So both hue and intensity change.":"紅酒的色調從寶石紅轉為石榴紅、茶褐色，最後是褐色，深度越來越淺。相反地，白酒的顏色會加深。所以色調和深淺都會改變。","What is the correct order of colours as a red wine ages?":"紅酒陳年時，顏色的正確順序是什麼？","Ruby, garnet, tawny, brown":"寶石紅、石榴紅、茶褐色、褐色","Purple, ruby, lemon, gold":"紫色、寶石紅、檸檬色、金黃色","Brown, tawny, garnet, ruby":"褐色、茶褐色、石榴紅、寶石紅","Garnet, ruby, purple and finally deep black after many years":"石榴紅、寶石紅、紫色，多年後最終變成深黑色","A red moves from ruby to garnet, then tawny and finally brown.":"紅酒從寶石紅轉為石榴紅，接著是茶褐色，最後是褐色。","The second option mixes red and white colours: lemon and gold are white-wine hues. The third gives the reverse order. With age, red colour gets paler, not darker.":"第二個選項把紅酒和白酒的顏色混在一起了：檸檬色和金黃色是白酒的色調。第三個選項的順序正好相反。隨著陳年，紅酒的顏色會變淡，而不是變深。","An old bottle of red has thrown a lot of deposit. What is usually done before serving it?":"一瓶老紅酒產生了大量沉澱物。侍酒前通常會怎麼做？","It is decanted":"換瓶","The bottle is shaken well":"用力搖晃酒瓶","Water is added to dilute the deposit":"加水稀釋沉澱物","It is sent back to the producer, since deposit always means a fault":"退回給生產者，因為沉澱物一定代表有缺陷","If there is a lot of deposit, the wine is normally decanted off it.":"如果沉澱物很多，通常會換瓶，把酒與沉澱物分開。","Deposit often forms in reds that mature in bottle; it is normal, not a fault. Shaking would stir it back into the wine. Decanting lets you pour the clear wine and leave the sediment in the bottle.":"在瓶中熟成的紅酒常會形成沉澱物；這是正常的，不是缺陷。搖晃會把沉澱物重新攪入酒中。換瓶可以倒出清澈的酒，把沉澱物留在瓶中。","A wine has spent a long time maturing in barrel with oxygen contact. Which tertiary aromas are most likely?":"一款酒在橡木桶中與氧氣接觸、熟成了很長時間。最可能出現哪些三級香氣？","Coffee and caramel":"咖啡和焦糖","Fresh flowers and citrus":"新鮮花香和柑橘","Green apple and gooseberry, typical of a very young wine":"青蘋果和醋栗，非常年輕酒款的典型特徵","Oxidative ageing, for example in barrel, brings notes such as coffee and caramel.":"氧化陳年，例如在橡木桶中，會帶來咖啡和焦糖等氣息。","Petrol, honey and mushroom are typical of ageing protected from oxygen, such as in bottle. Flowers, citrus, green apple and gooseberry are primary aromas of young wines. In both kinds of ageing, fruit loses freshness.":"汽油、蜂蜜和蘑菇是隔絕氧氣陳年（例如在瓶中）的典型特徵。花香、柑橘、青蘋果和醋栗是年輕酒款的一級香氣。在兩種陳年方式中，果味都會失去新鮮感。","A winemaker wants only a light touch of oak in a white. Which barrel suits best?":"一位釀酒師只想讓白酒帶一點輕微的橡木味。哪一種橡木桶最合適？","A barrel that has already been used several times":"已經使用過多次的橡木桶","A new barrique":"新的小型橡木桶","A heavily toasted new barrique":"重度烘烤的新小型橡木桶","A small new barrel with toasted oak chips added too":"小型新橡木桶，另外再加入烘烤過的橡木片","A used barrel gives less flavour than a new one; after two or three uses it gives very little.":"用過的橡木桶給的風味比新桶少；使用兩到三次之後就非常少了。","New barrels give lots of vanilla, coconut, charred wood and spice, even more when heavily toasted. Adding chips would increase the effect, not reduce it. For a light touch, old oak is the logical choice.":"新橡木桶會帶來大量香草、椰子、炭烤木頭和香料，重度烘烤時更多。加入橡木片會增強效果，而不是減弱。要輕微的橡木味，舊桶是合理的選擇。","Which profile is typical of a cool-climate Chardonnay?":"哪一種風味特徵是涼爽氣候夏多內的典型特徵？","High acidity, apple, lemon, wet stones":"高酸度、蘋果、檸檬、濕石頭","Medium acidity, pineapple, banana, full body":"中等酸度、鳳梨、香蕉、酒體飽滿","Low acidity, peach, melon, full body":"低酸度、桃子、哈密瓜、酒體飽滿","Medium acidity, mango, honey, ginger":"中等酸度、芒果、蜂蜜、薑","Cool weather slows ripening, so grapes keep acidity and show green fruit and citrus.":"涼爽的天氣減緩成熟，所以葡萄保留酸度，展現綠色水果和柑橘。","In a cool climate Chardonnay ripens slowly and does not build much sugar. The result is a wine with high acidity, light to medium body and aromas of green fruit (apple, pear), lemon and wet stones. Pineapple and banana instead point to a warm climate, where acidity drops to medium and the body becomes full.":"在涼爽氣候中，夏多內成熟緩慢，累積的糖分不多。結果是一款酸度高、酒體輕盈至中等、帶有綠色水果（蘋果、梨）、檸檬和濕石頭香氣的酒。鳳梨和香蕉則指向溫暖氣候，那裡的酸度降到中等，酒體變得飽滿。","Which flavours typify a warm-climate Chardonnay?":"哪些風味是溫暖氣候夏多內的典型特徵？","Apple, pear and wet stones":"蘋果、梨和濕石頭","Grass, green pepper and asparagus":"青草、青椒和蘆筍","Rose, lychee and apricot":"玫瑰、荔枝和杏桃","Heat ripens the grapes fully, so stone fruit and tropical fruit dominate.":"熱量讓葡萄完全成熟，所以核果和熱帶水果佔主導。","In warm climates Chardonnay gains more sugar and loses acid. The wine is full-bodied with medium acidity and ripe aromas of peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple and banana. Apple and wet stones belong to cool climates; grass and asparagus suggest Sauvignon Blanc; rose and lychee suggest Gewurztraminer.":"在溫暖氣候中，夏多內累積更多糖分、失去酸度。酒的酒體飽滿、酸度中等，帶有桃子和鳳梨、香蕉等熱帶水果的成熟香氣。蘋果和濕石頭屬於涼爽氣候；青草和蘆筍讓人想到白蘇維濃；玫瑰和荔枝則讓人想到格烏茲塔明那。","Why are many warm-climate Chardonnays acidified?":"為什麼許多溫暖氣候的夏多內要加酸？","To balance their high alcohol and body":"為了平衡它們的高酒精和飽滿酒體","To add butter and cream flavours":"為了增添奶油和鮮奶油風味","To protect the wine against frost":"為了保護酒免受霜害","To reduce the amount of alcohol":"為了降低酒精含量","Warm-climate grapes lack acid; adding it balances full-bodied, alcoholic wines.":"溫暖氣候的葡萄缺酸；加酸能平衡酒體飽滿、酒精高的酒。","In heat the grapes ripen fully, build sugar (hence alcohol) and lose acid. The wine could taste heavy and flat. Acidification, adding acid in the winery, is therefore common to restore freshness and balance. It does not add dairy notes, which come from malolactic conversion, and it does not lower alcohol.":"在高溫下，葡萄完全成熟，累積糖分（因此酒精也高）並失去酸度。酒可能嚐起來沉重而平淡。因此常會在酒廠中加酸，以恢復清新感和平衡。加酸不會增添乳製品氣息，那來自乳酸轉化；也不會降低酒精。","Which technique adds butter and cream flavours to Chardonnay?":"哪一種技術為夏多內增添奶油和鮮奶油風味？","Lees contact":"與酒渣接觸","Stainless steel fermentation":"不鏽鋼槽發酵","Malolactic conversion softens acidity and brings dairy notes of butter and cream.":"乳酸轉化讓酸度變柔和，帶來奶油和鮮奶油的乳製品氣息。","Malolactic conversion turns harsh acids into softer ones and leaves dairy aromas of butter and cream. Lees contact instead gives body and bread or biscuit notes, while stainless steel is an inert vessel that adds no flavour. Acidification raises acidity and brings no dairy character.":"乳酸轉化把尖銳的酸轉化為較柔和的酸，並留下奶油和鮮奶油的乳製品香氣。與酒渣接觸則帶來酒體以及麵包或餅乾氣息，而不鏽鋼槽是不增添任何風味的惰性容器。加酸會提高酸度，不會帶來乳製品特徵。","What does lees contact during maturation add to Chardonnay?":"熟成期間與酒渣接觸會為夏多內增添什麼？","Body and bread and biscuit notes":"酒體以及麵包和餅乾氣息","Higher acidity and lemon notes":"更高的酸度和檸檬氣息","Hazelnut and mushroom notes":"榛果和蘑菇氣息","Lees enrich the wine with more body and bread and biscuit aromas.":"酒渣讓酒更豐富，帶來更飽滿的酒體以及麵包和餅乾香氣。","Keeping the wine on its lees during maturation increases the feeling of body and adds secondary aromas of bread and biscuit. Vanilla and coconut come from oak; hazelnut and mushroom are tertiary aromas that appear as the best wines age in bottle. Lees do not raise acidity.":"熟成期間讓酒留在酒渣上，會增加酒體感，並增添麵包和餅乾的二級香氣。香草和椰子來自橡木桶；榛果和蘑菇是最好的酒在瓶中陳年時出現的三級香氣。酒渣不會提高酸度。","Why do inexpensive Chardonnay brands often use oak chips or staves?":"為什麼平價的夏多內品牌常使用橡木片或橡木條？","They cost less than new barrels":"它們比新橡木桶便宜","They give the wine more acidity":"它們讓酒的酸度更高","They allow long bottle ageing":"它們讓酒能長期瓶中陳年","They prevent malolactic conversion":"它們能阻止乳酸轉化","Chips and staves give oak flavours far more cheaply than new barrels.":"橡木片和橡木條帶來橡木風味，成本比新橡木桶低得多。","New oak barrels are expensive. To give high-volume wines vanilla, smoke or coconut flavours at a low price, many producers soak chips or staves in the wine. It is a cost choice, common for example in Pays d'Oc IGP and California Central Valley brands; it does nothing for acidity or longevity.":"新橡木桶很昂貴。為了以低價讓大量生產的酒帶有香草、煙燻或椰子風味，許多生產者會把橡木片或橡木條浸泡在酒中。這是成本上的選擇，例如在 Pays d'Oc IGP 和 California Central Valley 的品牌中很常見；它對酸度或陳年潛力毫無幫助。","What does the term unoaked on a Chardonnay label tell you?":"夏多內酒標上的 unoaked 告訴你什麼？","The wine has had no oak treatment":"這款酒沒有經過任何橡木處理","The wine was made from late-picked grapes":"這款酒用晚採的葡萄釀造","The wine is blended with Semillon":"這款酒混調了榭密雍","The wine has been acidified":"這款酒經過加酸","Unoaked or unwooded tells consumers no oak was used.":"Unoaked 或 unwooded 告訴消費者沒有使用橡木。","Some producers want a pure-fruited Chardonnay: they use inert vessels and sometimes avoid malolactic conversion and lees. To tell buyers, they may print unoaked or unwooded on the label. The term says nothing about harvest timing, blending or acidification. It is a simple way to guide people looking for a fresh, fruit-led style.":"有些生產者想要果味純淨的夏多內：他們使用惰性容器，有時也避免乳酸轉化和酒渣接觸。為了告知買家，他們可能在酒標上印上 unoaked 或 unwooded。這個術語與採收時機、混調或加酸無關。這是為尋找清爽、以果味為主風格的人提供指引的簡單方式。","Which tertiary flavours do fine Chardonnays develop with bottle age?":"優質夏多內經過瓶中陳年會發展出哪些三級風味？","Hazelnut and mushroom":"榛果和蘑菇","Smoke and vanilla":"煙燻和香草","With years in bottle, tertiary notes of hazelnut and mushroom appear.":"在瓶中多年後，會出現榛果和蘑菇的三級氣息。","Very good or outstanding Chardonnays can evolve for years, and the best Burgundies for decades, developing tertiary aromas of hazelnut and mushroom. Butter and cream (malolactic), smoke and vanilla (oak) and bread and biscuit (lees) are secondary aromas linked to winery choices.":"非常好或傑出的夏多內可以演變多年，最好的布根地白酒甚至可達數十年，發展出榛果和蘑菇的三級香氣。奶油和鮮奶油（乳酸轉化）、煙燻和香草（橡木桶）以及麵包和餅乾（酒渣）都是與酒廠選擇相關的二級香氣。","Which Burgundy appellation gives cool-climate, light to medium-bodied wines that almost never show oak?":"哪一個布根地法定產區出產涼爽氣候、酒體輕盈至中等、幾乎從不帶橡木味的酒？","Chablis producers ferment in inert vessels to keep the delicate cool-climate fruit.":"Chablis 的生產者使用惰性容器發酵，以保留涼爽氣候細緻的果味。","Chablis is the coolest part of Burgundy: dry wines, high acidity, apple, lemon and wet stones. With very few exceptions no oak is detectable, as producers prefer inert vessels. Meursault, Puligny-Montrachet and Pouilly-Fuissé, by contrast, often use barrels to add body and complexity.":"Chablis 是布根地最涼爽的地區：不甜的酒、高酸度、蘋果、檸檬和濕石頭。除了極少數例外，喝不出橡木味，因為生產者偏好惰性容器。相反地，Meursault、Puligny-Montrachet 和 Pouilly-Fuissé 則常使用橡木桶來增添酒體和複雜度。","Which weather hazard is a key concern that can limit Chablis production?":"哪一種天氣災害是可能限制 Chablis 產量的主要隱憂？","Frost":"霜凍","Drought":"乾旱","Excessive heat":"過熱","Morning fog":"晨霧","In this cool region, frost can cut the crop from year to year.":"在這個涼爽產區，霜凍可能年年削減收成。","Chablis lies at the northern tip of Burgundy and has a cool climate. That is why frost is a constant worry: it can damage the vines and limit how much wine is made each year. Drought and excessive heat are problems of warmer areas; fog is a cooling factor elsewhere, for example in Los Carneros.":"Chablis 位於布根地的最北端，屬於涼爽氣候。這就是為什麼霜凍是持續的隱憂：它可能損害葡萄樹，限制每年的產量。乾旱和過熱是較溫暖地區的問題；霧則是其他地方的降溫因素，例如 Los Carneros。","Why do Chablis Premier Cru and Grand Cru vineyards give more complex wines?":"為什麼 Chablis Premier Cru 和 Grand Cru 的葡萄園能釀出更複雜的酒？","South/south-west slopes: more sun, riper grapes":"朝南／西南的坡地：日照更多，葡萄更成熟","They are always made in new barrels":"它們總是在新橡木桶中釀造","They lie on flat land, safe from frost":"它們位於平地，不受霜害","They are irrigated to raise yields":"它們經過灌溉以提高產量","Slope aspect increases sunshine, hence ripeness, flavour and complexity.":"坡向增加了日照，因而提升成熟度、風味和複雜度。","In a cool climate like Chablis every bit of sun matters. The best vineyards, labelled Premier Cru or Grand Cru, usually sit on hillsides facing south or south-west. This aspect increases sun exposure, so grapes ripen better and wines are more flavourful and complex. New oak, by contrast, is an exception in Chablis.":"在像 Chablis 這樣的涼爽氣候中，每一點陽光都很重要。最好的葡萄園，標示為 Premier Cru 或 Grand Cru，通常位於朝南或西南的山坡上。這樣的坡向增加了日照，所以葡萄成熟得更好，酒的風味更豐富、更複雜。相反地，新橡木桶在 Chablis 是例外。","What style is a Chardonnay labelled Bourgogne AOC usually?":"標示 Bourgogne AOC 的夏多內通常是什麼風格？","Simple, high acidity, apple and lemon":"簡單、高酸度、蘋果和檸檬","Full, tropical, lots of new oak":"飽滿、熱帶水果、大量新橡木桶","Sweet, from late-harvested grapes":"甜，用晚收葡萄釀造","Complex, hazelnut and mushroom":"複雜、榛果和蘑菇","It is the regional appellation: grapes from anywhere in Burgundy, simple fresh wines.":"這是地區級法定產區：葡萄可來自布根地任何地方，酒款簡單清爽。","Bourgogne AOC is the regional level: grapes can come from anywhere in Burgundy. These wines are generally simple, with high acidity and apple and lemon aromas. The more complex styles with hazelnut and mushroom come from the premier cru and grand cru sites of villages such as Meursault or Puligny-Montrachet.":"Bourgogne AOC 是地區級：葡萄可以來自布根地任何地方。這些酒一般很簡單，酸度高，帶有蘋果和檸檬香氣。帶有榛果和蘑菇的較複雜風格，來自 Meursault 或 Puligny-Montrachet 等村莊的 premier cru 和 grand cru 園地。","In which part of the Côte d'Or is Chardonnay production focused?":"Côte d'Or 的夏多內生產集中在哪個部分？","Côte de Beaune, south of Beaune":"Côte de Beaune，Beaune 以南","The Mâconnais, in the far south":"最南端的 Mâconnais","Chablis, in the north":"北部的 Chablis","The plains along the Rhône":"隆河沿岸的平原","Côte d'Or Chardonnay is focused south of Beaune, in the Côte de Beaune.":"Côte d'Or 的夏多內集中在 Beaune 以南的 Côte de Beaune。","The Côte d'Or has a moderate climate and gives fuller, riper Chardonnay than Chablis. White wine production is focused south of the town of Beaune, in the Côte de Beaune, home to famous villages such as Meursault and Puligny-Montrachet. Chablis and the Mâconnais are part of Burgundy but not of the Côte d'Or.":"Côte d'Or 屬於溫和氣候，釀出的夏多內比 Chablis 更飽滿、更成熟。白酒生產集中在 Beaune 鎮以南的 Côte de Beaune，這裡有 Meursault 和 Puligny-Montrachet 等著名村莊。Chablis 和 Mâconnais 屬於布根地，但不屬於 Côte d'Or。","Which two Côte de Beaune villages are famous for outstanding Chardonnay?":"Côte de Beaune 的哪兩個村莊以傑出的夏多內聞名？","Mâcon and Pouilly-Fuissé":"Mâcon 和 Pouilly-Fuissé","Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé":"Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé","Meursault and Puligny-Montrachet are the great Chardonnay villages of the Côte de Beaune.":"Meursault 和 Puligny-Montrachet 是 Côte de Beaune 偉大的夏多內村莊。","Meursault AOC and Puligny-Montrachet AOC produce very good to outstanding Chardonnay, barrel fermented and/or matured and aged on lees. Mâcon and Pouilly-Fuissé are in the Mâconnais; Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé are Loire Sauvignon Blanc appellations; Graves and Pessac-Léognan are in Bordeaux.":"Meursault AOC 和 Puligny-Montrachet AOC 出產非常好到傑出的夏多內，在橡木桶中發酵和／或熟成，並在酒渣上陳年。Mâcon 和 Pouilly-Fuissé 位於 Mâconnais；Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé 是羅亞爾河的白蘇維濃法定產區；Graves 和 Pessac-Léognan 則位於波爾多。","A simple, fruity, mostly unoaked wine with lemon, peach and melon most likely comes from which appellation?":"一款簡單、果香豐富、大多未經橡木桶、帶有檸檬、桃子和哈密瓜的酒，最可能來自哪個法定產區？","The Mâconnais makes fruity, mostly unoaked Chardonnay labelled Mâcon AOC.":"Mâconnais 出產果香豐富、大多未經橡木桶的夏多內，標示為 Mâcon AOC。","In the Mâconnais, the southernmost part of Burgundy, Chardonnay gives fruity wines with simple lemon, peach and melon flavours, rarely oaked. Meursault relies on barrels and lees; Chablis Grand Cru is crisper and stonier; Pessac-Léognan is a Bordeaux white from Sauvignon Blanc and Semillon.":"在布根地最南端的 Mâconnais，夏多內釀出果香豐富的酒，帶有簡單的檸檬、桃子和哈密瓜風味，很少經過橡木桶。Meursault 仰賴橡木桶和酒渣；Chablis Grand Cru 更爽脆、礦石感更強；Pessac-Léognan 則是以白蘇維濃和榭密雍釀造的波爾多白酒。","What makes Pouilly-Fuissé wines higher in quality than Mâcon AOC?":"是什麼讓 Pouilly-Fuissé 的酒品質高於 Mâcon AOC？","Steep east/south-east slopes and more concentrated fruit":"朝東／東南的陡坡，以及更濃縮的果實","A cooler climate, the same as Chablis":"更涼爽的氣候，與 Chablis 相同","The exclusive use of inert vessels":"只使用惰性容器","Higher yields thanks to irrigation":"灌溉帶來更高的產量","Steep, well-exposed slopes give concentrated grapes, often enhanced by barrel use.":"日照良好的陡坡帶來濃縮的葡萄，常再藉由橡木桶加以提升。","Around the village of Pouilly-Fuissé, vineyards lie on steep slopes facing east and south-east. They give wines with concentrated stone and tropical fruit, often barrel fermented and/or matured for extra body and complexity. Simpler Mâcon AOC is largely unoaked. Both are found in the Mâconnais, in southern Burgundy.":"在 Pouilly-Fuissé 村周圍，葡萄園位於朝東和東南的陡坡上。這裡的酒帶有濃縮的核果和熱帶水果風味，常在橡木桶中發酵和／或熟成，以增添酒體和複雜度。較簡單的 Mâcon AOC 大多未經橡木桶。兩者都位於布根地南部的 Mâconnais。","Under which label is most Chardonnay from Languedoc-Roussillon sold?":"Languedoc-Roussillon 的夏多內大多以什麼標示出售？","The region is home to Pays d'Oc IGP, used for most of its Chardonnay.":"這個地區有 Pays d'Oc IGP，大部分的夏多內都用這個標示。","Languedoc-Roussillon, on the Mediterranean coast, makes several AOC wines, but most of its Chardonnay is labelled Pays d'Oc IGP. The warm climate gives large volumes of ripe, fruity wine with peach, pineapple and banana. Bourgogne, Touraine and Alsace are appellations of other French regions.":"位於地中海沿岸的 Languedoc-Roussillon 出產數種 AOC 葡萄酒，但大部分的夏多內都標示為 Pays d'Oc IGP。溫暖的氣候帶來大量成熟、果香豐富的酒，帶有桃子、鳳梨和香蕉。Bourgogne、Touraine 和 Alsace 則是法國其他地區的法定產區。","Why does California's Central Valley produce high-volume Chardonnay with medium acidity?":"為什麼加州的 Central Valley 出產酸度中等的大量生產夏多內？","It is very hot, dry, irrigated and cut off from the sea":"它非常炎熱、乾燥、經過灌溉，並與海洋隔絕","It is cooled by fog from San Pablo Bay":"它受到 San Pablo Bay 的霧氣降溫","It has high-altitude vineyards with long seasons":"它有生長季很長的高海拔葡萄園","It is exposed to cool Pacific breezes":"它受到涼爽的太平洋微風吹拂","Mountains block sea influence; heat and irrigation give high yields and moderate acidity.":"山脈阻擋了海洋的影響；高溫和灌溉帶來高產量和中等酸度。","The Central Valley is cut off from the ocean by mountains, so it is very hot and dry. Irrigation allows high yields, ideal for high-volume brands labelled California. Grapes ripen fully: peach and pineapple, medium acidity and body, any oak from chips or staves. Fog and breezes instead cool coastal areas such as Los Carneros and Sonoma.":"Central Valley 被山脈與海洋隔開，所以非常炎熱乾燥。灌溉讓產量很高，非常適合標示 California 的大量生產品牌。葡萄完全成熟：桃子和鳳梨、中等酸度和酒體，若有橡木味則來自橡木片或橡木條。霧氣和微風則讓 Los Carneros 和 Sonoma 等沿海地區降溫。","Which Californian area is cooled by morning fogs from San Pablo Bay?":"加州哪個地區受到 San Pablo Bay 晨霧的降溫？","Northern Napa Valley":"Napa Valley 北部","Bay fogs cool Los Carneros, helping the grapes keep their acidity.":"海灣的霧氣讓 Los Carneros 降溫，幫助葡萄保留酸度。","In northern California, Los Carneros receives morning fogs from San Pablo Bay. This cooling slows ripening, so the grapes keep acidity while building complex flavours. Napa Valley warms up further north, the Central Valley is hot and cut off from the sea, and Santa Barbara County is cooled by breezes funnelled through valleys.":"在北加州，Los Carneros 受到來自 San Pablo Bay 的晨霧影響。這種降溫減緩成熟，讓葡萄在發展複雜風味的同時保留酸度。Napa Valley 越往北越溫暖，Central Valley 炎熱且與海洋隔絕，而 Santa Barbara County 則受到經由山谷導入的微風降溫。","Which Californian region is known for full-bodied, tropical Chardonnay with vanilla and spice from new oak?":"加州哪個產區以酒體飽滿、帶熱帶水果和新橡木桶香草與香料的夏多內聞名？","Napa Valley grows warmer and sunnier to the north: ripe, oaky wines.":"Napa Valley 越往北越溫暖、陽光越充足：成熟、帶橡木味的酒。","Moving north up Napa Valley the climate becomes warmer and sunnier. Grapes ripen fully and give full-bodied Chardonnay with pronounced tropical fruit plus vanilla and spice from new oak. Los Carneros and Sonoma are cooler thanks to fog and breezes; moderate Oregon is known for high acidity.":"沿著 Napa Valley 往北，氣候變得更溫暖、陽光更充足。葡萄完全成熟，釀出酒體飽滿的夏多內，帶有濃郁的熱帶水果，以及新橡木桶的香草和香料。Los Carneros 和 Sonoma 因為霧氣和微風而較涼爽；氣候溫和的奧勒岡則以高酸度著稱。","What cools the vineyards of Santa Barbara County?":"是什麼讓 Santa Barbara County 的葡萄園降溫？","Sea breezes funnelled inland by lateral valleys":"由橫向山谷導入內陸的海風","The altitude of inland hills":"內陸丘陵的海拔","Ocean currents from the south":"來自南方的洋流","Fogs from San Pablo Bay":"來自 San Pablo Bay 的霧氣","Valleys open to the sea channel cool breezes inland.":"向海洋開口的山谷把涼爽的微風導入內陸。","Santa Barbara County, on California's Central Coast, gets cool sea breezes funnelled inland by lateral valleys. Styles range from wines like the Côte de Beaune to more tropical versions with higher alcohol and more new oak. San Pablo Bay fogs relate to Los Carneros; altitude cools Adelaide Hills, for example.":"位於加州中部海岸的 Santa Barbara County，受到由橫向山谷導入內陸的涼爽海風吹拂。風格從類似 Côte de Beaune 的酒，到酒精更高、新橡木桶更多的熱帶水果風格都有。San Pablo Bay 的霧氣與 Los Carneros 有關；海拔則讓例如 Adelaide Hills 降溫。","What can a Chardonnay labelled South Eastern Australia indicate?":"標示 South Eastern Australia 的夏多內可能代表什麼？","A high-volume wine from a very broad area":"來自非常廣大區域的大量生產酒款","A single-vineyard wine from high altitude":"來自高海拔的單一葡萄園酒款","A wine from one cool coastal zone":"來自單一涼爽沿海地帶的酒","A sweet wine from late-picked grapes":"用晚採葡萄釀的甜酒","The label covers a huge area, often using warm, irrigated inland fruit.":"這個標示涵蓋廣大的區域，常使用溫暖、經灌溉的內陸果實。","South Eastern Australia allows grapes from a vast area, often warm, irrigated inland vineyards. These high-volume Chardonnays are sometimes blended with other varieties such as Semillon, or with wines from cooler sites; blending helps achieve better balance. Cooler regions such as Adelaide Hills or Yarra Valley give finer wines instead.":"South Eastern Australia 允許使用來自廣大區域的葡萄，常是溫暖、經灌溉的內陸葡萄園。這些大量生產的夏多內有時會與榭密雍等其他品種混調，或與較涼爽園地的酒混調；混調有助於取得更好的平衡。Adelaide Hills 或 Yarra Valley 等較涼爽的產區則出產較精緻的酒。","What cools the Australian region of Adelaide Hills?":"是什麼讓澳洲的 Adelaide Hills 產區降溫？","Morning fogs":"晨霧","Heavy irrigation":"大量灌溉","Adelaide Hills is cooled by altitude; Yarra Valley by ocean currents.":"Adelaide Hills 因海拔而涼爽；Yarra Valley 則因洋流而涼爽。","Adelaide Hills in South Australia owes its coolness to altitude, while Yarra Valley in Victoria is cooled by ocean currents from the south. Both enjoy long seasons, giving Chardonnay with ripe peach, sometimes tropical fruit, medium to high acidity and well-balanced oak.":"南澳的 Adelaide Hills 因海拔而涼爽，而維多利亞的 Yarra Valley 則受到來自南方的洋流降溫。兩者都享有很長的生長季，釀出帶有成熟桃子、有時帶熱帶水果、酸度中等至高、橡木味平衡良好的夏多內。","Which moderate New Zealand region gives full-bodied Chardonnay balanced by high acidity?":"紐西蘭哪個氣候溫和的產區出產以高酸度平衡飽滿酒體的夏多內？","In Hawke's Bay Chardonnay is the most planted white: full, crisp, stone-fruited wines.":"在 Hawke's Bay，夏多內是種植最多的白葡萄：飽滿、爽脆、帶核果風味的酒。","Hawke's Bay, on the east coast of the North Island, has a moderate climate and Chardonnay is its most planted white grape. It gives full-bodied wines balanced by high acidity, with pronounced stone fruit. Marlborough is cooler, with subtle oak; Margaret River is Australian and Walker Bay South African.":"位於北島東岸的 Hawke's Bay 屬於溫和氣候，夏多內是當地種植最多的白葡萄品種。它釀出酒體飽滿、以高酸度平衡、帶有濃郁核果風味的酒。Marlborough 較涼爽，橡木味細緻；Margaret River 在澳洲，Walker Bay 則在南非。","Why does Casablanca Valley make refreshing Chardonnay despite Chile's warmth?":"儘管智利很溫暖，為什麼 Casablanca Valley 能釀出清爽的夏多內？","Pacific breezes and fogs slow ripening":"太平洋的微風和霧氣減緩成熟","The vineyards are heavily irrigated":"葡萄園大量灌溉","The grapes are picked very late":"葡萄非常晚才採收","Mountains block the sea's influence":"山脈阻擋了海洋的影響","The ocean cools the valley: slow ripening, preserved acidity, lemon and peach.":"海洋讓山谷降溫：成熟緩慢、保留酸度、檸檬和桃子。","Casablanca Valley is a coastal region exposed to Pacific sea breezes and morning fogs. This cooling slows ripening and gives refreshing Chardonnay with lemon and peach and varying levels of oak. The larger, warmer Central Valley covers every level, from cheap brands to altitude-moderated wines.":"Casablanca Valley 是受到太平洋海風和晨霧影響的沿海產區。這種降溫減緩成熟，釀出帶有檸檬和桃子、橡木程度不一的清爽夏多內。較大、較溫暖的 Central Valley 則涵蓋各個等級，從便宜的品牌到受海拔調節的酒款都有。","Which South African region, among the country's coolest, is known for very good Chardonnay?":"南非哪個產區是全國最涼爽的地區之一，以非常好的夏多內聞名？","Inland Western Cape":"西開普內陸","Walker Bay is cooled by strong southerly sea breezes: high acidity and ripe fruit.":"Walker Bay 受到強勁的南方海風降溫：高酸度和成熟果味。","Coastal Walker Bay is among South Africa's coolest areas thanks to strong sea breezes from the south. It makes very good Chardonnay with high acidity, peach, pineapple and oak. The hot inland Western Cape vineyards mostly supply high-volume brands, sometimes blended with Chenin Blanc.":"沿海的 Walker Bay 因為來自南方的強勁海風，成為南非最涼爽的地區之一。這裡出產非常好的夏多內，帶有高酸度、桃子、鳳梨和橡木味。炎熱的西開普內陸葡萄園則主要供應大量生產的品牌，有時與白梢楠混調。","Why is Chardonnay considered such a versatile grape?":"為什麼夏多內被視為如此多才多藝的品種？","It makes outstanding wines in cool, moderate and warm climates":"它在涼爽、溫和和溫暖氣候中都能釀出傑出的酒","It withstands winter cold better than any other white grape variety":"它比任何其他白葡萄品種都更耐冬季寒冷","It is used mainly for sweet botrytised wines":"它主要用來釀造貴腐甜酒","Its aromas are so neutral that they never change with climate":"它的香氣非常中性，從不隨氣候改變","Chardonnay reaches outstanding quality in all three climate types, in different styles.":"夏多內在三種氣候類型中都能達到傑出品質，風格各不相同。","From light, crisp cool-climate wines to full, tropical warm-climate ones, Chardonnay covers a huge range, from high-volume brands to wines that evolve for years. It is not known for cold-hardiness (that is Riesling) or for botrytised sweet wines. Its primary aromas actually change a great deal with climate.":"從涼爽氣候輕盈爽脆的酒，到溫暖氣候飽滿帶熱帶水果的酒，夏多內涵蓋非常廣的範圍，從大量生產的品牌到可以演變多年的酒款都有。它不以耐寒著稱（那是麗絲玲），也不以貴腐甜酒著稱。它的一級香氣其實會隨氣候大幅改變。","Which profile fits a moderate-climate Chardonnay?":"哪一種風味特徵符合溫和氣候的夏多內？","Medium to high acidity, medium to full body, lemon, peach, melon":"酸度中等至高、酒體中等至飽滿、檸檬、桃子、哈密瓜","High acidity, light body, green apple, pear and wet stones":"高酸度、酒體輕盈、青蘋果、梨和濕石頭","Medium acidity, full body, very ripe pineapple and banana":"中等酸度、酒體飽滿、非常成熟的鳳梨和香蕉","Low acidity, light body, floral and cut-grass notes":"低酸度、酒體輕盈、花香和青草氣息","In a moderate climate Chardonnay sits in the middle: lemon and peach, sometimes melon, with medium to high acidity.":"在溫和氣候中，夏多內居於中間：檸檬和桃子，有時帶哈密瓜，酸度中等至高。","A moderate climate gives riper fruit than a cool one but keeps more freshness than a warm one. Apple, pear and wet stones with a light body point to a cool climate; pineapple and banana with medium acidity point to a warm one. Grassy notes with low acidity do not describe Chardonnay.":"溫和氣候帶來比涼爽氣候更成熟的果味，但比溫暖氣候保留更多清新感。蘋果、梨和濕石頭配上輕盈酒體指向涼爽氣候；鳳梨和香蕉配上中等酸度則指向溫暖氣候。低酸帶青草氣息並不是在描述夏多內。","Besides butter aromas, what else does malolactic conversion do to a Chardonnay?":"除了奶油香氣，乳酸轉化對夏多內還有什麼作用？","It softens harsh acids":"讓尖銳的酸變柔和","It raises the alcohol level and the wine's warming sensation":"提高酒精濃度和酒的溫熱感","It adds vanilla and coconut notes":"增添香草和椰子氣息","It makes the wine sweeter":"讓酒更甜","Malolactic conversion turns sharp acids into softer ones.":"乳酸轉化把尖銳的酸轉化為較柔和的酸。","Malolactic conversion has two effects: dairy notes (butter, cream) and softer acidity. It produces no alcohol and adds no sugar. Vanilla and coconut come from oak, not from malolactic conversion.":"乳酸轉化有兩種效果：乳製品氣息（奶油、鮮奶油）和更柔和的酸度。它不會產生酒精，也不會增加糖分。香草和椰子來自橡木桶，不是乳酸轉化。","Which flavours suggest that a Chardonnay was fermented or matured in oak?":"哪些風味表示夏多內曾在橡木桶中發酵或熟成？","Smoke, vanilla, coconut":"煙燻、香草、椰子","Butter, cream and a softer texture":"奶油、鮮奶油和更柔和的質地","Apple, lemon and wet stones":"蘋果、檸檬和濕石頭","Oak brings body and flavours of smoke, vanilla and coconut.":"橡木桶帶來酒體以及煙燻、香草和椰子風味。","Each technique leaves its own signature: oak = smoke, vanilla, coconut; malolactic = butter and cream; lees = bread and biscuit. Apple, lemon and wet stones are primary grape aromas from a cool climate, not from wood.":"每種技術都留下自己的特徵：橡木桶 = 煙燻、香草、椰子；乳酸轉化 = 奶油和鮮奶油；酒渣 = 麵包和餅乾。蘋果、檸檬和濕石頭是涼爽氣候葡萄的一級香氣，不是來自木頭。","Why do not all Chardonnays benefit from malolactic, lees and oak?":"為什麼不是所有的夏多內都受益於乳酸轉化、酒渣和橡木桶？","Strong secondary flavours can swamp a delicately flavoured wine":"強烈的二級風味可能淹沒風味細緻的酒","European law forbids them for wines with a protected origin":"歐洲法律禁止受保護產地的酒使用它們","They make the wine unstable and cause it to referment in bottle":"它們讓酒不穩定，導致在瓶中再次發酵","They always lower quality":"它們總是會降低品質","Only wines with enough fruit intensity can carry these secondary flavours.":"只有果味強度足夠的酒，才承載得了這些二級風味。","These techniques are all optional: on a light wine they can hide the fruit, while in an intense wine they add complexity. They are not banned by law (Meursault uses oak and lees) and do not automatically lower quality. They do not cause refermentation in bottle.":"這些技術都是選擇性的：用在輕盈的酒上可能掩蓋果味，用在濃郁的酒上則能增添複雜度。法律並未禁止它們（Meursault 就使用橡木桶和酒渣），它們也不會自動降低品質。它們不會導致瓶中再次發酵。","A producer wants a pure-fruited Chardonnay with no secondary flavours. What will they most likely do?":"一位生產者想要果味純淨、沒有二級風味的夏多內。他最可能怎麼做？","Use inert vessels and avoid malolactic and lees contact":"使用惰性容器，避免乳酸轉化和酒渣接觸","Ferment in new barrels and leave the wine on its lees for a long time":"在新橡木桶中發酵，並讓酒長時間留在酒渣上","Add oak chips":"加入橡木片","Encourage full malolactic conversion to highlight freshness":"促進完全的乳酸轉化以突顯清新感","Inert vessels with no malolactic or lees contact keep only primary fruit aromas.":"使用惰性容器、不做乳酸轉化也不接觸酒渣，就只保留一級果香。","Steel or concrete give no flavour; avoiding malolactic and lees keeps out butter, cream, bread and biscuit. New barrels and chips add oak flavours instead. Malolactic does not highlight freshness: it softens acidity and adds dairy notes.":"不鏽鋼或混凝土不會帶來風味；避免乳酸轉化和酒渣，就不會有奶油、鮮奶油、麵包和餅乾。新橡木桶和橡木片則會增添橡木風味。乳酸轉化不會突顯清新感：它會讓酸度變柔和並增添乳製品氣息。","What is the order of Burgundy's areas, from north to south?":"布根地各地區由北到南的順序是什麼？","Chablis is in the cool north, the Côte d'Or in the moderate middle, the Mâconnais in the south.":"Chablis 位於涼爽的北部，Côte d'Or 位於溫和的中部，Mâconnais 位於南部。","Going south the climate warms: this is why Chablis is the coolest and crispest, the Côte d'Or gives fuller wines and the Mâconnais fruity, simple ones, with Pouilly-Fuissé as the exception. The other orders put Chablis or the Mâconnais in the wrong place.":"越往南氣候越溫暖：這就是為什麼 Chablis 最涼爽、最爽脆，Côte d'Or 的酒更飽滿，而 Mâconnais 的酒果香豐富、簡單，Pouilly-Fuissé 則是例外。其他順序都把 Chablis 或 Mâconnais 放錯了位置。","Compared with a Chablis, what does a Côte d'Or Chardonnay usually show?":"與 Chablis 相比，Côte d'Or 的夏多內通常表現出什麼？","More body and riper fruit, such as peach and melon":"更飽滿的酒體和更成熟的果味，例如桃子和哈密瓜","More acidity and stronger wet-stone notes":"更高的酸度和更強烈的濕石頭氣息","Less alcohol and more noticeable residual sugar":"酒精更低，殘糖更明顯","Grass and asparagus aromas":"青草和蘆筍香氣","The Côte d'Or's moderate climate ripens grapes further than cool Chablis.":"Côte d'Or 的溫和氣候讓葡萄比涼爽的 Chablis 更成熟。","Chablis is cool: light to medium body, apple, lemon and wet stones with high acidity. In the Côte d'Or the moderate climate gives more body and fruit such as peach and melon. Both are dry; grass and asparagus belong to Sauvignon Blanc.":"Chablis 很涼爽：酒體輕盈至中等，蘋果、檸檬和濕石頭，酸度高。在 Côte d'Or，溫和的氣候帶來更飽滿的酒體和桃子、哈密瓜等果味。兩者都是不甜的；青草和蘆筍屬於白蘇維濃。","How do producers in Meursault and Puligny-Montrachet add complexity and body?":"Meursault 和 Puligny-Montrachet 的生產者如何增添複雜度和酒體？","By fermenting or maturing in oak barrels and ageing on the lees":"在橡木桶中發酵或熟成，並在酒渣上陳年","By late-harvesting grapes affected by noble rot":"晚採受貴腐菌感染的葡萄","By adding unfermented grape juice before bottling":"在裝瓶前加入未發酵的葡萄汁","With oak chips":"用橡木片","In the Côte de Beaune, barrels and lees give body and complexity to the great Chardonnays.":"在 Côte de Beaune，橡木桶和酒渣為偉大的夏多內帶來酒體和複雜度。","These villages make top-level dry whites worked in oak barrels and on their lees. They are not sweet wines, so neither noble rot nor added juice is used. Chips are a cheap shortcut typical of high-volume wines, not of Côte de Beaune crus.":"這些村莊出產頂級的不甜白酒，在橡木桶中並在酒渣上釀製。它們不是甜酒，所以既不用貴腐菌，也不加葡萄汁。橡木片是大量生產酒款典型的便宜捷徑，不是 Côte de Beaune 特級酒款的做法。","A label reads 'Bourgogne' and 'Chardonnay'. Where can the grapes come from?":"一張酒標上寫著「Bourgogne」和「Chardonnay」。葡萄可以來自哪裡？","From anywhere in Burgundy":"布根地的任何地方","Only from Côte de Beaune premier cru vineyards":"只能來自 Côte de Beaune 的 premier cru 葡萄園","Only from the village of Chablis":"只能來自 Chablis 村","From any region of France, because it is a protected geographical indication":"法國任何地區，因為它是受保護地理標示","Bourgogne AOC is the regional appellation covering the whole of Burgundy.":"Bourgogne AOC 是涵蓋整個布根地的地區級法定產區。","As the broadest appellation, Bourgogne AOC allows grapes from the whole region to be combined: that is why the wine is usually simple, with apple, lemon and high acidity. Premier cru and Chablis have their own, narrower appellations. It is not a nationwide PGI: it stays within Burgundy.":"作為範圍最廣的法定產區，Bourgogne AOC 允許結合來自整個地區的葡萄：這就是為什麼這種酒通常很簡單，帶有蘋果、檸檬和高酸度。Premier cru 和 Chablis 有各自範圍更小的法定產區。它不是全國性的 PGI：範圍仍在布根地之內。","A customer asks for a Pouilly-Fuissé. What wine are they asking for?":"一位顧客要一瓶 Pouilly-Fuissé。他要的是什麼酒？","A Mâconnais Chardonnay, often oak-matured":"Mâconnais 的夏多內，常經橡木桶熟成","A Loire Sauvignon Blanc, dry and herbaceous":"羅亞爾河的白蘇維濃，不甜且帶草本氣息","A Pinot Noir from the Côte de Nuits":"Côte de Nuits 的黑皮諾","A sweet Chenin Blanc made from grapes affected by noble rot":"以受貴腐菌感染的葡萄釀造的甜型白梢楠","Pouilly-Fuissé is a Chardonnay white from the Mâconnais in southern Burgundy.":"Pouilly-Fuissé 是來自布根地南部 Mâconnais 的夏多內白酒。","The name is easily confused with Pouilly-Fumé, which is a Loire Sauvignon Blanc. Pouilly-Fuissé comes from steep east- and south-east-facing slopes, with concentrated fruit and often barrel treatment. It is neither a red nor a sweet wine.":"這個名字很容易和 Pouilly-Fumé 混淆，後者是羅亞爾河的白蘇維濃。Pouilly-Fuissé 來自朝東和東南的陡坡，果味濃縮，常經過橡木桶處理。它既不是紅酒，也不是甜酒。","An inexpensive Central Valley Chardonnay says only 'California' and tastes slightly of vanilla. What can you infer?":"一款平價的 Central Valley 夏多內只標示「California」，嚐起來略帶香草味。你可以推斷什麼？","High-volume grapes; the vanilla probably comes from oak chips or staves":"大量生產的葡萄；香草味可能來自橡木片或橡木條","Grapes from a coastal Sonoma vineyard, matured in new barrels":"來自 Sonoma 沿海葡萄園的葡萄，在新橡木桶中熟成","A Los Carneros wine":"一款 Los Carneros 的酒","A wine fermented in barrel on its lees":"一款在橡木桶中帶酒渣發酵的酒","Without a more specific GI, Central Valley grapes are sold as 'California'; any oak usually comes from chips or staves.":"沒有更具體的 GI 時，Central Valley 的葡萄以「California」出售；若有橡木味，通常來自橡木片或橡木條。","The Central Valley is hot, dry and irrigated, with high yields destined for high-volume brands. In an inexpensive wine, oak flavours almost always come from chips or staves, which cost less than barrels. Sonoma or Los Carneros would appear on the label as more specific GIs.":"Central Valley 炎熱、乾燥、經過灌溉，產量很高，用於大量生產的品牌。在平價的酒中，橡木風味幾乎總是來自比橡木桶便宜的橡木片或橡木條。Sonoma 或 Los Carneros 會作為更具體的 GI 出現在酒標上。","What changes in Napa Valley as you go further north?":"在 Napa Valley 越往北走，會有什麼變化？","It becomes warmer and sunnier":"變得更溫暖、陽光更充足","It becomes cooler thanks to the bay fogs":"因為海灣的霧氣而變得更涼爽","It becomes rainier and suits only sparkling base wines":"變得更多雨，只適合氣泡酒的基酒","It becomes higher and windier":"變得更高、風更大","Further north, Napa Valley gets further from the bay and becomes warmer and sunnier.":"越往北，Napa Valley 離海灣越遠，變得更溫暖、陽光更充足。","The rising warmth explains the typical style: full-bodied Chardonnays with pronounced tropical fruit and vanilla and spice from new oak. San Pablo Bay fogs cool the south, towards Los Carneros, not the north. Altitude and rain are not the factors involved.":"溫度上升解釋了典型的風格：酒體飽滿的夏多內，帶有濃郁的熱帶水果，以及新橡木桶的香草和香料。San Pablo Bay 的霧氣讓南部（往 Los Carneros 方向）降溫，而不是北部。海拔和雨水都不是相關因素。","What effect do Pacific breezes have on Chardonnay from Sonoma's coastal vineyards?":"太平洋微風對 Sonoma 沿海葡萄園的夏多內有什麼影響？","Grapes keep their acidity while developing complex flavours":"葡萄在發展複雜風味的同時保留酸度","Grapes ripen faster and build more sugar and alcohol":"葡萄成熟得更快，累積更多糖分和酒精","Grapes are more often affected by noble rot":"葡萄更常受到貴腐菌感染","The wine becomes more tannic":"酒變得更有單寧感","Cooling slows ripening: acidity is kept and flavours become more complex.":"降溫減緩成熟：保留酸度，風味變得更複雜。","Coastal influences temper California's heat and allow slow, balanced ripening. Faster ripening would be the effect of a warmer climate, not a cooler one. Noble rot is not part of these dry wines, and a white does not become tannic.":"沿海的影響緩和了加州的高溫，讓葡萄緩慢而均衡地成熟。成熟加快是較溫暖氣候的效果，而不是較涼爽氣候的。貴腐菌與這些不甜的酒無關，白酒也不會變得有單寧感。","What range of styles does Santa Barbara County Chardonnay offer?":"Santa Barbara County 的夏多內提供哪些風格範圍？","From Côte de Beaune-like wines to tropical styles with more new oak":"從類似 Côte de Beaune 的酒，到新橡木桶更多的熱帶水果風格","Only light, unoaked wines similar to Chablis":"只有類似 Chablis、輕盈且未經橡木桶的酒","Mainly sweet late-harvest wines":"主要是甜型晚收酒","Only high-volume wines sold under the simple California label":"只有以簡單的 California 標示出售的大量生產酒款","In Santa Barbara, styles run from Burgundian-style Chardonnay to more tropical, higher-alcohol, oakier wines.":"在 Santa Barbara，風格從布根地式的夏多內，到熱帶水果更多、酒精更高、橡木味更重的酒都有。","Sea breezes funnelled by lateral valleys allow elegant wines close to the Côte de Beaune, while other producers aim for tropical fruit, higher alcohol and pronounced new oak. The area is known for quality, not for bulk or sweet wines.":"由橫向山谷導入的海風讓這裡能釀出接近 Côte de Beaune 的優雅酒款，而其他生產者則追求熱帶水果、更高的酒精和濃郁的新橡木桶風味。這個地區以品質著稱，而不是大量生產酒或甜酒。","Which description fits Oregon Chardonnay?":"哪一項描述符合奧勒岡的夏多內？","High acidity, lemon to melon; small production compared with California":"高酸度、從檸檬到哈密瓜；與加州相比產量很小","Low acidity, very ripe banana and pineapple":"低酸度、非常成熟的香蕉和鳳梨","Sweet style, with noble rot":"甜型風格，帶有貴腐","Large volumes from hot, irrigated inland vineyards, sold as brands":"來自炎熱、經灌溉的內陸葡萄園的大量酒款，以品牌出售","Oregon's moderate climate gives fresh Chardonnays with lemon and melon notes.":"奧勒岡的溫和氣候帶來帶有檸檬和哈密瓜氣息的清爽夏多內。","Oregon has a generally moderate climate: its Chardonnay has refreshing high acidity and flavours from citrus to light tropical notes. Production is small compared with California. Bulk wines from hot inland vineyards describe California's Central Valley, not Oregon.":"奧勒岡整體屬於溫和氣候：它的夏多內有令人清爽的高酸度，風味從柑橘到淡淡的熱帶水果氣息。與加州相比，產量很小。來自炎熱內陸葡萄園的大量生產酒款描述的是加州的 Central Valley，不是奧勒岡。","Why are some 'South Eastern Australia' Chardonnays blended with Semillon or with wine from cooler vineyards?":"為什麼有些「South Eastern Australia」夏多內會與榭密雍或較涼爽葡萄園的酒混調？","To achieve better balance":"為了取得更好的平衡","Because Australian law requires at least two grapes in every branded wine":"因為澳洲法律規定每款品牌酒至少要用兩個品種","To make them fit for long ageing":"為了讓它們適合長期陳年","Grapes from warm, irrigated inland vineyards benefit from blending that rebalances the wine.":"來自溫暖、經灌溉的內陸葡萄園的葡萄，受益於能重新平衡酒款的混調。","The South Eastern Australia GI covers a vast area; much of the fruit comes from warm inland zones. Adding Semillon or cooler-site wine helps balance, for example between acidity and body. There is no blending requirement, these wines are not made for long ageing, and Semillon brings no oak notes.":"South Eastern Australia 這個 GI 涵蓋廣大的區域；大部分的果實來自溫暖的內陸地帶。加入榭密雍或較涼爽園地的酒，有助於取得平衡，例如在酸度和酒體之間。並沒有混調的規定，這些酒也不是為長期陳年而釀的，而榭密雍不會帶來橡木氣息。","Which Australian region owes its cooler climate to ocean currents from the south rather than to altitude?":"澳洲哪個產區的涼爽氣候來自南方的洋流，而不是海拔？","Yarra Valley, in Victoria, is cooled by ocean currents from the south.":"維多利亞的 Yarra Valley 受到來自南方的洋流降溫。","Adelaide Hills, Clare Valley and Eden Valley are all in South Australia and owe their coolness mainly to altitude. Yarra Valley is moderated by the ocean instead. Both influences lengthen the season and give Chardonnays with peach and medium to high acidity.":"Adelaide Hills、Clare Valley 和 Eden Valley 都位於南澳，主要因海拔而涼爽。Yarra Valley 則受到海洋的調節。兩種影響都能延長生長季，釀出帶有桃子、酸度中等至高的夏多內。","Which statement about Margaret River is correct?":"關於 Margaret River，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","Warm climate moderated by sea breezes; small volumes, consistent quality":"受海風調節的溫暖氣候；產量小，品質穩定","It is the main source of irrigated South Eastern Australia brands":"它是經灌溉的 South Eastern Australia 品牌的主要來源","It lies in the state of Victoria":"它位於維多利亞州","It has a cold climate, cooled by altitude":"它屬於寒冷氣候，因海拔而涼爽","Margaret River, in Western Australia, is warm but sea-cooled, with limited production and high quality.":"西澳的 Margaret River 很溫暖但受海洋降溫，產量有限、品質很高。","Sea breezes slow ripening and give medium- to full-bodied Chardonnays with peach and pineapple. The region is in Western Australia, not Victoria, and is not about altitude or bulk wine: it produces far less than South Eastern Australia.":"海風減緩成熟，釀出酒體中等至飽滿、帶有桃子和鳳梨的夏多內。這個產區位於西澳，不是維多利亞，與海拔或大量生產酒款無關：它的產量遠少於 South Eastern Australia。","Which profile fits a Marlborough Chardonnay?":"哪一種風味特徵符合 Marlborough 的夏多內？","Ripe lemon, peach, melon, high acidity, subtle oak":"成熟的檸檬、桃子、哈密瓜，高酸度，細緻的橡木味","Banana and pineapple, medium acidity, strong new-oak vanilla and a very full body":"香蕉和鳳梨，中等酸度，強烈的新橡木桶香草味，酒體非常飽滿","Sweet, with honey and dried apricot":"甜，帶有蜂蜜和杏桃乾","Marlborough is cool but sunny: ripe fruit with high natural acidity.":"Marlborough 涼爽但陽光充足：成熟的果味配上高天然酸度。","In the north-east of the South Island, Marlborough has sea breezes and plentiful rain: its Chardonnay is very good, fresh, with light oak. Strong vanilla and medium acidity describe warm styles; grass and asparagus are typical of its Sauvignon Blanc, not its Chardonnay.":"位於南島東北部的 Marlborough 有海風和充沛的雨水：它的夏多內非常好、清爽，橡木味輕盈。強烈的香草味和中等酸度描述的是溫暖風格；青草和蘆筍是它的白蘇維濃的典型特徵，不是夏多內。","In Chile, where do the outstanding Chardonnays of the Central Valley come from?":"在智利，Central Valley 傑出的夏多內來自哪裡？","From vineyards moderated by altitude":"來自受海拔調節的葡萄園","From the hottest, flattest irrigated valley-floor vineyards":"來自最炎熱、最平坦、經灌溉的谷底葡萄園","From grapes affected by noble rot":"來自受貴腐菌感染的葡萄","From vineyards on the Argentine border":"來自阿根廷邊境的葡萄園","In the warm Central Valley, the best Chardonnays come from vineyards cooled by altitude.":"在溫暖的 Central Valley，最好的夏多內來自因海拔而涼爽的葡萄園。","The Central Valley is larger and warmer than Casablanca Valley and produces everything from cheap brands to outstanding wines. Altitude tempers the heat and allows quality wines. The hot, irrigated valley floor mainly gives volume; noble rot and the Argentine border are irrelevant.":"Central Valley 比 Casablanca Valley 更大、更溫暖，出產從便宜品牌到傑出酒款的各種酒。海拔緩和了高溫，讓優質酒款成為可能。炎熱、經灌溉的谷底主要帶來產量；貴腐菌和阿根廷邊境都無關。","In the hot inland vineyards of the Western Cape, which grape is Chardonnay sometimes blended with?":"在西開普炎熱的內陸葡萄園，夏多內有時會與哪個品種混調？","Pinotage, the country's signature black grape":"皮諾塔吉，這個國家的招牌黑葡萄","For high-volume brands, Western Cape Chardonnay is sometimes blended with Chenin Blanc.":"用於大量生產的品牌時，西開普的夏多內有時會與白梢楠混調。","The hot inland vineyards of the Western Cape mainly supply branded wines, and Chenin Blanc is South Africa's most planted white grape. Pinot Noir and Pinotage are black grapes, not used in such a white; Riesling is not the partner mentioned.":"西開普炎熱的內陸葡萄園主要供應品牌酒，而白梢楠是南非種植最多的白葡萄品種。黑皮諾和皮諾塔吉是黑葡萄，不會用在這樣的白酒中；麗絲玲也不是所提到的搭檔。","Why has Chardonnay suffered from a poor image in many markets?":"為什麼夏多內在許多市場的形象不佳？","Because of its link with the heavy oak of the 1980s and 1990s":"因為它與 1980 和 1990 年代的濃重橡木味有關","Because it was linked to low-quality sweet wines such as Liebfraumilch":"因為它與 Liebfraumilch 等低品質甜酒有關","Because its herbaceous aromas are tiring":"因為它的草本香氣令人厭倦","Because it never ages":"因為它從不陳年","The very oaky style of those decades shaped the grape's image.":"那幾十年橡木味極重的風格塑造了這個品種的形象。","Today the aim is not to hide the fruit under wood, but Chardonnay is still more likely to show oak than Pinot Grigio or Sauvignon Blanc. Liebfraumilch harmed Riesling; worries about herbaceous aromas concern Sauvignon Blanc. Great Chardonnays can age for decades.":"現在的目標不是用木頭掩蓋果味，但夏多內仍比灰皮諾或白蘇維濃更可能帶有橡木味。Liebfraumilch 傷害的是麗絲玲；對草本香氣的顧慮涉及的是白蘇維濃。偉大的夏多內可以陳年數十年。","Which two factors have helped Chablis stay steadily popular?":"哪兩個因素幫助 Chablis 保持穩定的人氣？","Unoaked style and labelling by region, not by grape":"未經橡木桶的風格，以及以產區而非品種標示","Low prices and large volumes from irrigated vineyards":"低價格和來自灌溉葡萄園的大量產量","Strong new oak and very ripe tropical fruit":"強烈的新橡木桶味和非常成熟的熱帶水果","Noticeable residual sugar and low alcohol, designed for broad appeal":"明顯的殘糖和低酒精，為了廣泛的吸引力而設計","Chablis is unoaked and labelled by region, which separates it from Chardonnay's 'oaky' image.":"Chablis 未經橡木桶且以產區標示，讓它與夏多內「橡木味重」的形象區隔開來。","Many consumers link Chardonnay with heavy oak; Chablis avoids both problems, being fresh and unoaked and often not naming the grape at all. It is not a bulk wine from irrigated vineyards, nor tropical or sweet.":"許多消費者把夏多內與濃重的橡木味聯想在一起；Chablis 避開了這兩個問題，它清爽、未經橡木桶，而且常常根本不標示品種。它不是來自灌溉葡萄園的大量生產酒款，也不是熱帶水果風格或甜酒。","Which of these is NOT a secondary flavour in Chardonnay?":"下列哪一項不是夏多內的二級風味？","Hazelnut":"榛果","Butter":"奶油","Biscuit":"餅乾","Hazelnut is a tertiary flavour that develops with bottle age.":"榛果是隨瓶中陳年發展出的三級風味。","Secondary flavours come from the winery: butter from malolactic, biscuit from lees, vanilla from oak. Hazelnut and mushroom instead appear in quality Chardonnays after years in bottle, so they are tertiary.":"二級風味來自酒廠：奶油來自乳酸轉化，餅乾來自酒渣，香草來自橡木桶。榛果和蘑菇則是優質夏多內在瓶中多年後才出現的，所以是三級風味。","Which aromas are the hallmark of Sauvignon Blanc?":"哪些香氣是白蘇維濃的招牌特徵？","Grass, green bell pepper, asparagus":"青草、青椒、蘆筍","Rose, lychee, apricot":"玫瑰、荔枝、杏桃","Butter, cream, vanilla":"奶油、鮮奶油、香草","Pear, ginger, honey":"梨、薑、蜂蜜","Sauvignon Blanc is known for pronounced herbaceous aromas.":"白蘇維濃以濃郁的草本香氣著稱。","Sauvignon Blanc is an aromatic grape whose wines are recognised by herbaceous notes: grass, green bell pepper and asparagus. Rose and lychee point to Gewurztraminer; butter, cream and vanilla are winemaking aromas typical of many Chardonnays; pear, ginger and honey suggest Pinot Gris, especially with age.":"白蘇維濃是芳香型品種，它的酒以草本氣息辨識：青草、青椒和蘆筍。玫瑰和荔枝指向格烏茲塔明那；奶油、鮮奶油和香草是許多夏多內典型的釀造香氣；梨、薑和蜂蜜則讓人想到灰皮諾，尤其是陳年後。","In which climates does Sauvignon Blanc perform best?":"白蘇維濃在哪些氣候中表現最好？","Cool and moderate":"涼爽和溫和","Hot and dry":"炎熱乾燥","Only warm and irrigated":"只在溫暖且經灌溉的地方","Hot and humid":"炎熱潮濕","Coolness preserves the grape's high acidity and herbaceous aromas.":"涼爽能保留這個品種的高酸度和草本香氣。","Sauvignon Blanc grows best in cool and moderate climates, where it keeps the high acidity and herbaceous aromas that make it recognisable. In areas that are too warm it loses freshness, which is why in Languedoc the best wines come from high sites and in California growers seek cooler areas or pick early.":"白蘇維濃在涼爽和溫和氣候中生長得最好，在那裡能保留讓它容易辨識的高酸度和草本香氣。在太溫暖的地區，它會失去清新感，這就是為什麼在 Languedoc 最好的酒來自高海拔園地，而在加州種植者會尋找較涼爽的地區或提早採收。","Riper Sauvignon Blanc grapes give which flavours?":"較成熟的白蘇維濃葡萄會帶來哪些風味？","Peach and passion fruit":"桃子和百香果","Green apple and gooseberry":"青蘋果和醋栗","Grapefruit and wet stones":"葡萄柚和濕石頭","With more ripeness the fruit moves from green and citrus to peach and tropical.":"成熟度越高，果味就從綠色水果和柑橘轉向桃子和熱帶水果。","Sauvignon Blanc's fruit depends on ripeness. Less ripe grapes give apple, gooseberry, grapefruit and wet stones; riper grapes bring stone fruit such as peach and tropical fruit such as passion fruit. Hazelnut and mushroom are tertiary aromas typical of aged Chardonnay.":"白蘇維濃的果味取決於成熟度。較不成熟的葡萄帶來蘋果、醋栗、葡萄柚和濕石頭；較成熟的葡萄則帶來桃子等核果和百香果等熱帶水果。榛果和蘑菇是陳年夏多內典型的三級香氣。","Why is single-varietal Sauvignon Blanc usually made in inert vessels?":"為什麼單一品種的白蘇維濃通常在惰性容器中釀造？","New oak would mask its herbaceous aromas":"新橡木桶會掩蓋它的草本香氣","To increase body and alcohol":"為了增加酒體和酒精","To encourage long ageing":"為了促進長期陳年","Because the law bans oak":"因為法律禁止使用橡木桶","Its distinctive herbaceous aromas are easily overwhelmed by new oak.":"它獨特的草本香氣很容易被新橡木桶壓過。","Sauvignon Blanc's appeal lies in its herbaceous and fruity aromas. New oak flavours would easily mask them, so single-varietal wines are mostly made in stainless steel or other inert vessels. Oak is not banned: when used, labels often show terms such as barrel aged.":"白蘇維濃的魅力在於它的草本和果香。新橡木桶的風味很容易掩蓋這些香氣，所以單一品種的酒大多在不鏽鋼槽或其他惰性容器中釀造。橡木桶並沒有被禁止：使用時，酒標上常會出現 barrel aged 等術語。","What happens to many Sauvignon Blancs after a couple of years in bottle?":"許多白蘇維濃在瓶中放了一兩年後會怎樣？","They lose freshness and turn vegetal":"失去清新感，變得有植物味","They develop hazelnut and mushroom":"發展出榛果和蘑菇","They become sweeter and more tropical":"變得更甜、更有熱帶水果味","They gain butter and cream notes":"增添奶油和鮮奶油氣息","It is best young; with time the fresh aromas fade.":"它最好趁年輕喝；隨著時間，清新的香氣會消退。","Most Sauvignon Blanc is meant to be drunk young. Even outstanding wines can lose their fresh aromas within a couple of years of the vintage and develop unattractive vegetal notes. Exceptions include some Semillon blends, such as the best Graves and Pessac-Léognan, which age to develop honey and nutty notes.":"大多數白蘇維濃都是要趁年輕喝的。即使是傑出的酒款，也可能在年份後一兩年內失去清新的香氣，發展出不討喜的植物性氣息。例外包括一些與榭密雍混調的酒，例如最好的 Graves 和 Pessac-Léognan，它們陳年後會發展出蜂蜜和堅果氣息。","Which grape is Sauvignon Blanc often blended with?":"白蘇維濃常與哪個品種混調？","Semillon":"榭密雍","Semillon is the classic partner, adding body and ageing ability.":"榭密雍是經典的搭檔，增添酒體和陳年能力。","Sauvignon Blanc is mainly a single-varietal wine, but when blended its typical partner is Semillon: in Bordeaux (Bordeaux AOC, Graves, Pessac-Léognan) and in Australia (Margaret River, Adelaide Hills). Semillon adds body and helps the wine age. Sauvignon, for its part, brings acidity and herbaceous aromas to the blend.":"白蘇維濃主要以單一品種釀造，但混調時典型的搭檔是榭密雍：在波爾多（Bordeaux AOC、Graves、Pessac-Léognan）和澳洲（Margaret River、Adelaide Hills）都是如此。榭密雍增添酒體並幫助酒陳年。白蘇維濃則為混調帶來酸度和草本香氣。","In which two Loire appellations is Sauvignon Blanc the only permitted white grape?":"在哪兩個羅亞爾河法定產區，白蘇維濃是唯一允許的白葡萄品種？","Touraine and Vouvray":"Touraine 和 Vouvray","Chablis and Pouilly-Fuissé":"Chablis 和 Pouilly-Fuissé","Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé, facing across the Loire, allow only Sauvignon Blanc for whites.":"隔著羅亞爾河相望的 Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé，白酒只允許使用白蘇維濃。","Sancerre AOC and Pouilly-Fumé AOC face each other across the Loire in a cool climate. For whites only Sauvignon Blanc is allowed: dry wines with high acidity, green apple, grass, asparagus and sometimes wet stones. Graves and Pessac-Léognan are in Bordeaux; Chablis and Pouilly-Fuissé are Burgundy Chardonnay appellations.":"Sancerre AOC 和 Pouilly-Fumé AOC 在涼爽氣候中隔著羅亞爾河相望。白酒只允許使用白蘇維濃：不甜、高酸度，帶有青蘋果、青草、蘆筍，有時還有濕石頭。Graves 和 Pessac-Léognan 位於波爾多；Chablis 和 Pouilly-Fuissé 是布根地的夏多內法定產區。","Which profile best describes a white Sancerre?":"哪一種風味特徵最能描述 Sancerre 白酒？","Dry, high acidity, green apple, grass, asparagus":"不甜、高酸度、青蘋果、青草、蘆筍","Full, low acidity, rose and lychee":"飽滿、低酸度、玫瑰和荔枝","Full, new oak, pineapple and vanilla":"飽滿、新橡木桶、鳳梨和香草","Off-dry, peach, mango and ginger":"微甜、桃子、芒果和薑","The cool Loire climate gives dry, crisp wines with green fruit and herbaceous notes.":"羅亞爾河的涼爽氣候帶來不甜、爽脆、帶有綠色水果和草本氣息的酒。","Sancerre is a cool Loire appellation dedicated, for whites, to Sauvignon Blanc. The cool climate preserves high acidity and leaves green fruit such as apple, herbaceous grass and asparagus notes and sometimes wet stones. Rose and lychee indicate Gewurztraminer; mango and ginger an Alsace Pinot Gris.":"Sancerre 是羅亞爾河的涼爽法定產區，白酒專門使用白蘇維濃。涼爽的氣候保留了高酸度，留下蘋果等綠色水果、青草和蘆筍等草本氣息，有時還有濕石頭。玫瑰和荔枝表示格烏茲塔明那；芒果和薑則表示阿爾薩斯的灰皮諾。","What style does Touraine AOC Sauvignon Blanc usually offer?":"Touraine AOC 的白蘇維濃通常是什麼風格？","Fruity and inexpensive":"果香豐富且價格平實","Concentrated, oaked, built to age":"濃縮、經橡木桶、適合陳年","Sweet, from very ripe grapes":"甜，用非常成熟的葡萄釀造","Full, blended with Semillon":"飽滿，與榭密雍混調","Touraine covers a wide area west of Sancerre: fruity, affordable wines.":"Touraine 涵蓋 Sancerre 以西的廣大區域：果香豐富、價格親民的酒。","Touraine AOC grapes come from the wide Touraine sub-region, west of Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé. The wines are typically fruity and inexpensive. The concentrated, oak-matured, age-worthy style belongs instead to the best Graves and Pessac-Léognan, where Sauvignon is blended with Semillon.":"Touraine AOC 的葡萄來自廣大的 Touraine 子產區，位於 Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé 以西。這些酒通常果香豐富、價格平實。濃縮、經橡木桶熟成、適合陳年的風格，則屬於最好的 Graves 和 Pessac-Léognan，那裡的白蘇維濃會與榭密雍混調。","What role does Semillon play in Graves and Pessac-Léognan whites?":"榭密雍在 Graves 和 Pessac-Léognan 白酒中扮演什麼角色？","It adds body and helps the wine age":"增添酒體並幫助酒陳年","It adds acidity and herbaceous notes":"增添酸度和草本氣息","It adds floral rose aromas":"增添玫瑰花香","It lowers alcohol and body":"降低酒精和酒體","Semillon fills out Sauvignon: more body and longer life.":"榭密雍讓白蘇維濃更豐滿：酒體更飽滿，壽命更長。","Graves AOC and Pessac-Léognan AOC make whites more concentrated and complex than simple Bordeaux AOC, usually blending Sauvignon Blanc and Semillon. Sauvignon brings acidity and herbaceous aromas; Semillon adds body and helps the wine age. The best are oak-matured and develop honey and nutty notes in bottle.":"Graves AOC 和 Pessac-Léognan AOC 出產比簡單的 Bordeaux AOC 更濃縮、更複雜的白酒，通常混調白蘇維濃和榭密雍。白蘇維濃帶來酸度和草本香氣；榭密雍增添酒體並幫助酒陳年。最好的酒款經橡木桶熟成，在瓶中會發展出蜂蜜和堅果氣息。","Which flavours do the best Pessac-Léognan whites develop in bottle?":"最好的 Pessac-Léognan 白酒在瓶中會發展出哪些風味？","Honey and nuts":"蜂蜜和堅果","Grass and asparagus":"青草和蘆筍","Lychee and rose":"荔枝和玫瑰","Banana and pineapple":"香蕉和鳳梨","Oak-matured blends evolve towards complex honey and nutty notes.":"經橡木桶熟成的混調酒會朝複雜的蜂蜜和堅果氣息演變。","Very good or outstanding Graves and Pessac-Léognan whites, Sauvignon Blanc and Semillon blends often matured in oak, can age in bottle. Over time they develop complex aromas of honey and nuts. Grass and asparagus are primary aromas of young Sauvignon; lychee and rose belong to Gewurztraminer.":"非常好或傑出的 Graves 和 Pessac-Léognan 白酒，是常經橡木桶熟成的白蘇維濃與榭密雍混調，可以在瓶中陳年。隨著時間，它們會發展出蜂蜜和堅果的複雜香氣。青草和蘆筍是年輕白蘇維濃的一級香氣；荔枝和玫瑰則屬於格烏茲塔明那。","Where do Languedoc-Roussillon's best Sauvignon Blancs come from?":"Languedoc-Roussillon 最好的白蘇維濃來自哪裡？","From areas cooled by altitude":"來自因海拔而涼爽的地區","From the hottest coastal plains":"來自最炎熱的沿海平原","From irrigated, high-yield vineyards":"來自經灌溉的高產量葡萄園","From very late-harvested grapes":"來自非常晚採收的葡萄","Much of the region is too warm; altitude provides the coolness needed.":"這個地區大部分都太溫暖；海拔提供了所需的涼爽。","Languedoc-Roussillon is mostly too warm for a cool-loving grape like Sauvignon Blanc. The best wines therefore come from areas cooled by altitude: dry, high in acidity, with passion fruit and herbaceous grass notes, usually labelled Pays d'Oc IGP. The tropical fruit reflects the region's generally warm climate.":"對白蘇維濃這種喜愛涼爽的品種來說，Languedoc-Roussillon 大部分地方都太溫暖了。因此最好的酒來自因海拔而涼爽的地區：不甜、酸度高，帶有百香果和青草等草本氣息，通常標示為 Pays d'Oc IGP。熱帶水果反映了這個地區整體溫暖的氣候。","Why do Marlborough Sauvignon Blancs show such a broad range of fruit flavours?":"為什麼 Marlborough 的白蘇維濃展現如此廣泛的果味？","Blending across sites and ripeness levels":"混調來自不同園地和成熟度的葡萄","Long ageing in new barrels":"在新橡木桶中長時間陳年","Systematic blending with Chardonnay":"有系統地與夏多內混調","Late harvest of raisined grapes":"晚收風乾的葡萄","Combining sites and ripeness brings grapefruit, peach and passion fruit together.":"結合不同園地和成熟度，讓葡萄柚、桃子和百香果匯聚一堂。","In Marlborough many Sauvignon Blancs are made by blending grapes from different sites or picked at different ripeness levels. Grapefruit (less ripe) then sits alongside peach and passion fruit (riper), with intense green pepper and asparagus. The result is a more pronounced style than the Loire's.":"在 Marlborough，許多白蘇維濃是混調來自不同園地或在不同成熟度採收的葡萄釀成的。葡萄柚（較不成熟）與桃子和百香果（較成熟）並存，再加上濃烈的青椒和蘆筍。結果是比羅亞爾河更鮮明的風格。","A Sauvignon Blanc with grapefruit, passion fruit and intense green pepper most likely comes from?":"一款帶有葡萄柚、百香果和濃烈青椒味的白蘇維濃，最可能來自哪裡？","Marlborough gives the most pronounced style: tropical fruit and intense herbaceous notes.":"Marlborough 的風格最鮮明：熱帶水果加上濃烈的草本氣息。","Marlborough's classic style combines a broad range of fruit, from grapefruit to passion fruit, with very pronounced green pepper and asparagus. Pessac-Léognan is more complex and often oaked; Touraine is fruity but simple; Elgin, South Africa's coolest region, leans to green apple and wet stones.":"Marlborough 的經典風格結合了從葡萄柚到百香果的廣泛果味，以及非常鮮明的青椒和蘆筍。Pessac-Léognan 更複雜，常經橡木桶；Touraine 果香豐富但簡單；南非最涼爽的產區 Elgin 則偏向青蘋果和濕石頭。","How are some Marlborough producers experimenting beyond the classic style?":"有些 Marlborough 的生產者如何在經典風格之外進行嘗試？","Cooler sites, or a little oak and lees":"使用較涼爽的園地，或加入少許橡木桶和酒渣","Fermenting on skins like a red":"像紅酒一樣帶皮發酵","Stopping fermentation for a sweet wine":"中止發酵以釀造甜酒","Blending with Gewurztraminer":"與格烏茲塔明那混調","Some seek a Loire-like style from cool sites; others add complexity with oak or lees.":"有些人從涼爽園地追求類似羅亞爾河的風格；其他人則用橡木桶或酒渣增添複雜度。","Experimentation is increasingly common in Marlborough. Some producers choose grapes from cooler sites for wines similar to the Loire; others use small amounts of oak or lees contact to add complexity and body. The aim is to offer variety to drinkers who might tire of intense herbaceous aromas.":"在 Marlborough，各種嘗試越來越普遍。有些生產者選用較涼爽園地的葡萄，釀出類似羅亞爾河的酒；其他人則使用少量橡木桶或酒渣接觸，增添複雜度和酒體。目的是為可能對濃烈草本香氣感到厭倦的飲酒者提供多樣選擇。","In which Australian region is Sauvignon Blanc the most widely planted grape?":"在澳洲哪個產區，白蘇維濃是種植最廣泛的品種？","Altitude-cooled Adelaide Hills has Sauvignon Blanc as its leading grape.":"因海拔而涼爽的 Adelaide Hills，以白蘇維濃為主要品種。","In Adelaide Hills, South Australia, altitude cools the vineyards and Sauvignon Blanc is the most planted variety. Wines are generally fresh and fruity, from citrus to tropical fruit; some are blended with Semillon for more body and ageing potential. Margaret River is known mainly for Sauvignon-Semillon blends.":"在南澳的 Adelaide Hills，海拔讓葡萄園保持涼爽，白蘇維濃是種植最多的品種。酒款一般清爽、果香豐富，從柑橘到熱帶水果都有；有些會與榭密雍混調，以增添酒體和陳年潛力。Margaret River 則主要以白蘇維濃與榭密雍的混調著稱。","What Sauvignon Blanc style is Margaret River known for?":"Margaret River 以哪一種白蘇維濃風格聞名？","Semillon blends, concentrated and herbaceous":"與榭密雍混調，濃縮且帶草本氣息","Sweet late-harvest wines":"甜型晚收酒","Light, cheap single-varietals":"輕盈、便宜的單一品種酒","Chardonnay blends in new oak":"在新橡木桶中與夏多內混調","In Margaret River Sauvignon is often blended with Semillon, with concentrated herbaceous aromas.":"在 Margaret River，白蘇維濃常與榭密雍混調，帶有濃縮的草本香氣。","Margaret River in Western Australia has built a reputation for Sauvignon Blanc, most often blended with Semillon. These wines show concentrated herbaceous aromas such as grass, and some are made in contact with oak. They are neither sweet wines nor simple cheap ones.":"西澳的 Margaret River 以白蘇維濃建立了名聲，大多與榭密雍混調。這些酒展現青草等濃縮的草本香氣，有些會與橡木接觸釀造。它們既不是甜酒，也不是簡單的便宜酒。","Why is Casablanca Valley known for very good Sauvignon Blanc?":"為什麼 Casablanca Valley 以非常好的白蘇維濃聞名？","It is cooled by sea breezes and morning fog":"它受到海風和晨霧降溫","It is cooled by Andean altitude":"它受到安地斯山脈的海拔降溫","It is Chile's warmest area":"它是智利最溫暖的地區","It always uses new oak":"它總是使用新橡木桶","Pacific breezes and fog keep freshness and acidity.":"太平洋的微風和霧氣保留了清新感和酸度。","Casablanca Valley is a coastal Chilean region cooled both by sea breezes and by Pacific morning fogs. These conditions suit Sauvignon Blanc's fresh, herbaceous style. The larger Central Valley produces wines at every level, from cheap brands to very good examples.":"Casablanca Valley 是智利的沿海產區，同時受到海風和太平洋晨霧的降溫。這樣的條件適合白蘇維濃清爽、帶草本氣息的風格。較大的 Central Valley 則出產各個等級的酒，從便宜品牌到非常好的酒款都有。","Why is South African Sauvignon Blanc concentrated in coastal regions?":"為什麼南非的白蘇維濃集中在沿海產區？","Inland vineyards are generally too warm":"內陸葡萄園一般太溫暖","Inland is too cold and frosty":"內陸太冷、容易結霜","The law bans the grape inland":"法律禁止在內陸種植這個品種","Only the coast has suitable soils":"只有沿海有合適的土壤","Sauvignon likes coolness; the coast offers breezes the hot interior lacks.":"白蘇維濃喜歡涼爽；沿海有炎熱內陸所缺乏的微風。","In South Africa inland vineyards are generally too warm for Sauvignon Blanc, which needs coolness to keep its acidity and herbaceous aromas. Plantings are therefore concentrated on the coast: Constantia is cooled by Southern Ocean breezes, while Elgin owes its coolness to altitude.":"在南非，內陸葡萄園對白蘇維濃來說一般太溫暖，而這個品種需要涼爽才能保留酸度和草本香氣。因此種植集中在沿海：Constantia 受到南冰洋微風的降溫，而 Elgin 則因海拔而涼爽。","Which South African region, south of Cape Town, is cooled by Southern Ocean breezes?":"南非哪個位於開普敦以南的產區受到南冰洋微風的降溫？","Constantia, south of Cape Town, gives fresh, tropical and herbaceous Sauvignon.":"開普敦以南的 Constantia 出產清爽、帶熱帶水果和草本氣息的白蘇維濃。","Constantia lies south of Cape Town and is cooled by Southern Ocean breezes. It produces refreshing Sauvignon Blanc with ripe tropical fruit and herbaceous aromas. Elgin is cooled by altitude instead; Walker Bay is mainly noted here for Chardonnay. As elsewhere in the country, the coast is preferred to the hot interior.":"Constantia 位於開普敦以南，受到南冰洋微風的降溫。這裡出產令人清爽的白蘇維濃，帶有成熟的熱帶水果和草本香氣。Elgin 則是因海拔而涼爽；Walker Bay 在這裡主要以夏多內著稱。和這個國家其他地方一樣，人們偏好沿海而非炎熱的內陸。","Which region is often cited as South Africa's coolest wine region?":"哪個產區常被稱為南非最涼爽的葡萄酒產區？","Small, altitude-cooled Elgin gives Sauvignon with green apple and wet stones.":"小巧、因海拔而涼爽的 Elgin，出產帶有青蘋果和濕石頭的白蘇維濃。","Elgin is a small region cooled by altitude and often cited as South Africa's coolest wine area. Its Sauvignon Blancs typically show green fruit such as apple and sometimes wet stones, signs of a cool climate. Casablanca Valley is Chilean; the inland Western Cape is hot.":"Elgin 是因海拔而涼爽的小產區，常被稱為南非最涼爽的葡萄酒產區。它的白蘇維濃通常展現蘋果等綠色水果，有時還有濕石頭，這是涼爽氣候的跡象。Casablanca Valley 在智利；西開普內陸則很炎熱。","How is a fresh, herbaceous Sauvignon Blanc achieved in California?":"在加州，如何釀出清爽、帶草本氣息的白蘇維濃？","Cooler sites and early picking":"較涼爽的園地和提早採收","Late picking for more ripeness":"晚採以提高成熟度","Irrigation and very high yields":"灌溉和非常高的產量","Long maturation in new oak":"在新橡木桶中長時間熟成","Heat must be offset: cool sites and early harvest keep acidity and aromas.":"必須抵消高溫：涼爽園地和提早採收能保留酸度和香氣。","California is mostly too warm for the fresh, herbaceous style typical of France and New Zealand. The finest grapes therefore come from cooler areas and may be picked early to retain acidity and herbaceous aromas. Very good examples come from cooler parts of Napa Valley, sometimes oaked for body and smoky notes.":"對於法國和紐西蘭典型的清爽草本風格來說，加州大部分地方都太溫暖了。因此最好的葡萄來自較涼爽的地區，並可能提早採收以保留酸度和草本香氣。非常好的酒款來自 Napa Valley 較涼爽的地方，有時會經橡木桶以增添酒體和煙燻氣息。","What does oak add to some Napa Valley Sauvignon Blancs?":"橡木桶為某些 Napa Valley 的白蘇維濃增添什麼？","Body and smoky flavour":"酒體和煙燻風味","Acidity and herbaceous notes":"酸度和草本氣息","Floral rose aromas":"玫瑰花香","Residual sweetness":"殘留的甜味","Oak contact adds body and a smoky touch.":"與橡木接觸會增添酒體和一絲煙燻味。","Cooler parts of Napa Valley make very good Sauvignon Blanc, sometimes in contact with oak. The wood adds body and flavours such as smoke. Acidity and herbaceous notes come from the cool climate and early picking, not from oak; residual sugar plays no part.":"Napa Valley 較涼爽的地方出產非常好的白蘇維濃，有時會與橡木接觸。木頭增添酒體和煙燻等風味。酸度和草本氣息來自涼爽氣候和提早採收，不是來自橡木桶；殘糖則毫無作用。","Which label term often signals a Sauvignon Blanc that has seen oak?":"哪一個酒標術語常表示白蘇維濃經過橡木桶？","Since it is usually unoaked, oak use is flagged by terms such as barrel aged.":"由於它通常不經橡木桶，使用橡木桶時會以 barrel aged 等術語標示。","Most Sauvignon Blanc is made without oak so as not to mask its herbaceous aromas. When oak has been used, producers often say so with terms like barrel aged. Unwooded means the opposite; Vendanges tardives means late harvest in Alsace; Grand Cru is a vineyard term.":"大多數白蘇維濃不使用橡木桶，以免掩蓋它的草本香氣。使用橡木桶時，生產者常以 barrel aged 等術語說明。Unwooded 的意思正好相反；Vendanges tardives 在阿爾薩斯是晚收的意思；Grand Cru 則是葡萄園術語。","What style is a simple white Bordeaux AOC based on Sauvignon Blanc usually?":"以白蘇維濃為主的簡單 Bordeaux AOC 白酒通常是什麼風格？","Fresh, grass and green apple":"清爽、青草和青蘋果","Full, honey and nuts":"飽滿、蜂蜜和堅果","Sweet, from extra-ripe grapes":"甜，用過熟的葡萄釀造","Full, rose and lychee":"飽滿、玫瑰和荔枝","Simple Bordeaux AOC offers fresh grass and green apple aromas.":"簡單的 Bordeaux AOC 帶有清新的青草和青蘋果香氣。","In Bordeaux, Sauvignon Blanc covers many styles. Simple Bordeaux AOC has fresh grass and green apple aromas and may be single-varietal or blended with Semillon. Honey and nutty notes belong instead to the best aged Graves and Pessac-Léognan, which are more concentrated and often oak-matured.":"在波爾多，白蘇維濃涵蓋許多風格。簡單的 Bordeaux AOC 帶有清新的青草和青蘋果香氣，可能是單一品種，也可能與榭密雍混調。蜂蜜和堅果氣息則屬於最好的陳年 Graves 和 Pessac-Léognan，它們更濃縮，常經橡木桶熟成。","Which flavours do less ripe grapes give to Sauvignon Blanc?":"較不成熟的葡萄為白蘇維濃帶來哪些風味？","Apple, gooseberry, grapefruit, wet stones":"蘋果、醋栗、葡萄柚、濕石頭","Peach, passion fruit and other very ripe tropical fruit":"桃子、百香果和其他非常成熟的熱帶水果","Strawberry, raspberry and red cherry":"草莓、覆盆子和紅櫻桃","Honey and dried fruit":"蜂蜜和果乾","Less ripe grapes give green fruit, citrus and wet stones.":"較不成熟的葡萄帶來綠色水果、柑橘和濕石頭。","Sauvignon Blanc runs from green fruit (apple, gooseberry), grapefruit and wet stones to peach and passion fruit when the grapes are riper. Red fruits belong to Pinot Noir; honey and dried fruit are tertiary or sweet-wine notes.":"白蘇維濃的風味範圍從綠色水果（蘋果、醋栗）、葡萄柚和濕石頭，到葡萄較成熟時的桃子和百香果。紅色水果屬於黑皮諾；蜂蜜和果乾則是三級香氣或甜酒的氣息。","Which structure is typical of a Sauvignon Blanc?":"哪一種結構是白蘇維濃的典型特徵？","Dry, light to medium body, high acidity":"不甜、酒體輕盈至中等、高酸度","Off-dry, full body, low acidity and high alcohol":"微甜、酒體飽滿、低酸度和高酒精","Dry, full body, medium acidity":"不甜、酒體飽滿、中等酸度","Sweet, full body, high acidity":"甜、酒體飽滿、高酸度","Sauvignon Blanc is usually dry, light to medium-bodied and very fresh.":"白蘇維濃通常不甜、酒體輕盈至中等，非常清爽。","Refreshing high acidity is its hallmark, together with herbaceous aromas. Full body and medium acidity describe a warm-climate Chardonnay instead. Sweet wines exist in blends with Semillon, but the typical Sauvignon Blanc style is dry.":"令人清爽的高酸度是它的招牌特徵，再加上草本香氣。酒體飽滿和中等酸度描述的則是溫暖氣候的夏多內。與榭密雍混調的甜酒是存在的，但白蘇維濃的典型風格是不甜的。","How can complexity be added to a Sauvignon Blanc without using oak?":"如何在不使用橡木桶的情況下為白蘇維濃增添複雜度？","By blending grapes from different sites at different ripeness levels":"混調來自不同園地、不同成熟度的葡萄","By leaving the grapes on the vine until they freeze":"把葡萄留在樹上直到結冰","By macerating the juice for a long time with black grape skins":"讓果汁與黑葡萄果皮長時間浸泡","Combining riper and less ripe grapes layers green, citrus and tropical flavours.":"結合較成熟和較不成熟的葡萄，能疊加綠色水果、柑橘和熱帶水果風味。","Sauvignon Blanc changes a lot with ripeness: blending different sites adds layers of flavour. Leaving grapes to freeze is for sweet wines, maceration with black skins would make a rosé or red, and chips are still oak.":"白蘇維濃的風味隨成熟度變化很大：混調不同園地能增添風味層次。讓葡萄結冰是釀甜酒的方法，與黑葡萄果皮浸泡會釀成粉紅酒或紅酒，而橡木片仍然是橡木。","Where are Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé in relation to each other?":"Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé 彼此的相對位置如何？","Facing each other across the Loire River":"隔著羅亞爾河相望","One in the Loire and the other in Bordeaux":"一個在羅亞爾河，另一個在波爾多","Both in the Mâconnais, in southern Burgundy":"兩者都在布根地南部的 Mâconnais","Both near the Loire estuary, close to the Atlantic":"兩者都在靠近大西洋的羅亞爾河河口附近","Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé face each other across the Loire.":"Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé 隔著羅亞爾河相望。","These neighbouring appellations share a cool climate and the same grape, Sauvignon Blanc, for dry, crisp wines. Pouilly-Fuissé, with its similar name, is in the Mâconnais. Touraine lies to the west, but neither appellation is near the Atlantic.":"這兩個相鄰的法定產區有相同的涼爽氣候和同一個品種——白蘇維濃，釀出不甜、爽脆的酒。名字相似的 Pouilly-Fuissé 則位於 Mâconnais。Touraine 位於西邊，但這兩個法定產區都不靠近大西洋。","A label reads 'Pouilly-Fumé'. Which grape is the wine made from?":"一張酒標上寫著「Pouilly-Fumé」。這款酒是用哪個品種釀的？","Mâconnais Chardonnay":"Mâconnais 的夏多內","A barrel-aged Sauvignon Blanc and Semillon blend":"經橡木桶陳年的白蘇維濃與榭密雍混調","In Pouilly-Fumé, Sauvignon Blanc is the only white grape allowed.":"在 Pouilly-Fumé，白蘇維濃是唯一允許的白葡萄品種。","Many European appellations do not name the grape, so you need to know the rules. Pouilly-Fumé is a Loire white made only from Sauvignon Blanc. Chardonnay is Pouilly-Fuissé; the Semillon blend is typical of Graves and Pessac-Léognan.":"許多歐洲法定產區不標示品種，所以你需要了解法規。Pouilly-Fumé 是只用白蘇維濃釀造的羅亞爾河白酒。夏多內是 Pouilly-Fuissé；與榭密雍的混調則是 Graves 和 Pessac-Léognan 的典型特徵。","Where do the grapes for a Touraine AOC Sauvignon Blanc come from?":"Touraine AOC 白蘇維濃的葡萄來自哪裡？","From the wider Touraine area, west of Sancerre":"來自 Sancerre 以西更廣大的 Touraine 地區","Only from the steepest slopes of Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé":"只來自 Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé 最陡的坡地","From high-altitude Languedoc-Roussillon vineyards":"來自 Languedoc-Roussillon 的高海拔葡萄園","From the Graves area":"來自 Graves 地區","Touraine AOC covers a broad Loire sub-region west of Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé.":"Touraine AOC 涵蓋 Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé 以西廣大的羅亞爾河子產區。","As a broader area, Touraine gives fruity, inexpensive Sauvignons, less sought after than Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé. High southern vineyards give Pays d'Oc IGP, and Graves is in Bordeaux.":"作為較廣大的區域，Touraine 出產果香豐富、價格平實的白蘇維濃，不如 Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé 搶手。南部的高海拔葡萄園出產 Pays d'Oc IGP，而 Graves 位於波爾多。","What can a simple white labelled Bordeaux AOC contain?":"標示 Bordeaux AOC 的簡單白酒可以包含什麼？","Sauvignon Blanc alone, or Sauvignon Blanc with Semillon":"只有白蘇維濃，或白蘇維濃加榭密雍","Only Chardonnay":"只有夏多內","A blend that must contain at least half Riesling":"必須含有至少一半麗絲玲的混調","Only botrytised Semillon, always sweet":"只有貴腐榭密雍，一定是甜的","White Bordeaux AOC can be a pure Sauvignon or a blend with Semillon.":"Bordeaux AOC 白酒可以是純白蘇維濃，也可以與榭密雍混調。","Simple white Bordeaux AOC is fresh, with grass and green apple, from Sauvignon alone or with Semillon. Chardonnay and Riesling are not Bordeaux grapes. Botrytised Semillon is typical of Sauternes, a different appellation.":"簡單的 Bordeaux AOC 白酒很清爽，帶有青草和青蘋果，以白蘇維濃單獨或與榭密雍一起釀造。夏多內和麗絲玲不是波爾多的品種。貴腐榭密雍是 Sauternes 的典型特徵，那是另一個法定產區。","Compared with a simple white Bordeaux AOC, what are Graves and Pessac-Léognan whites like?":"與簡單的 Bordeaux AOC 白酒相比，Graves 和 Pessac-Léognan 白酒是什麼樣子？","More concentrated and complex":"更濃縮、更複雜","Lighter and meant to be drunk within months of the harvest":"更輕盈，要在採收後幾個月內喝掉","Always sweet":"一定是甜的","Made only in steel, with no Semillon and no oak at all":"只在不鏽鋼槽中釀造，完全沒有榭密雍也沒有橡木桶","Graves and Pessac-Léognan give more concentrated, complex whites, often oak-matured.":"Graves 和 Pessac-Léognan 出產更濃縮、更複雜的白酒，常經橡木桶熟成。","They are usually Sauvignon Blanc and Semillon blends; the best see oak and develop honey and nuts in bottle. They are not wines for immediate drinking, not sweet by definition, and Semillon is often part of them.":"它們通常是白蘇維濃與榭密雍的混調；最好的酒款經過橡木桶，在瓶中會發展出蜂蜜和堅果。它們不是要立刻喝的酒，按定義也不是甜酒，而且常常含有榭密雍。","Which profile does a typical Pays d'Oc IGP Sauvignon Blanc have?":"典型的 Pays d'Oc IGP 白蘇維濃有什麼風味特徵？","Dry, high acidity, passion fruit and grass":"不甜、高酸度、百香果和青草","Sweet, with honey and apricot":"甜，帶有蜂蜜和杏桃","Full body and low acidity, with strong vanilla and coconut":"酒體飽滿、低酸度，帶有強烈的香草和椰子","Light red":"淡紅酒","The higher, cooler parts of southern France give a dry, fresh, tropical and grassy Sauvignon.":"法國南部較高、較涼爽的地方出產不甜、清爽、帶熱帶水果和青草的白蘇維濃。","Much of Languedoc-Roussillon is too warm for this grape, but altitude keeps the acidity. The result combines passion fruit with grassy notes. It is neither a sweet wine nor a fat, oaky white.":"Languedoc-Roussillon 大部分地方對這個品種來說太溫暖，但海拔能保留酸度。結果結合了百香果和青草氣息。它既不是甜酒，也不是肥厚、橡木味重的白酒。","Where is the Marlborough region?":"Marlborough 產區在哪裡？","In the north-east of New Zealand's South Island":"在紐西蘭南島的東北部","On the east coast of New Zealand's North Island":"在紐西蘭北島的東岸","In Western Australia":"在西澳","In the south of the South Island, ringed by mountains":"在南島南部，四周群山環繞","Marlborough lies in the north-eastern part of the South Island.":"Marlborough 位於南島的東北部。","It is a cool region now closely linked with Sauvignon Blanc. The North Island's east coast is Hawke's Bay; the mountainous south of the South Island is Central Otago; Margaret River is in Western Australia.":"這是一個涼爽產區，現在與白蘇維濃密不可分。北島東岸是 Hawke's Bay；南島多山的南部是 Central Otago；Margaret River 則在西澳。","What generally distinguishes a Marlborough Sauvignon Blanc from a Loire one?":"一般來說，Marlborough 的白蘇維濃與羅亞爾河的有什麼不同？","More pronounced characteristics":"特徵更鮮明","Much lower acidity and a heavier body":"酸度低得多，酒體更厚重","Compulsory maturation in new oak for at least a year":"規定必須在新橡木桶中熟成至少一年","Strong wet-stone notes":"強烈的濕石頭氣息","Marlborough Sauvignon is usually more intense and aromatic than Loire Sauvignon.":"Marlborough 的白蘇維濃通常比羅亞爾河的更濃烈、更芳香。","Marlborough shows grapefruit, peach, passion fruit and very marked green pepper. Both styles have high acidity. Wet stones are more typical of Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé, and there is no oak requirement.":"Marlborough 展現葡萄柚、桃子、百香果和非常明顯的青椒。兩種風格都有高酸度。濕石頭更是 Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé 的典型特徵，也沒有橡木桶的規定。","A Marlborough producer wants a Sauvignon closer in style to Sancerre. What will they do?":"一位 Marlborough 的生產者想要風格更接近 Sancerre 的白蘇維濃。他會怎麼做？","Use grapes from cooler vineyard sites":"使用較涼爽葡萄園的葡萄","Pick riper grapes to boost tropical fruit":"採收更成熟的葡萄以增強熱帶水果","Ferment in new barrels":"在新橡木桶中發酵","Add unfermented juice to leave some sweetness":"加入未發酵的葡萄汁以保留一些甜味","Cooler sites give less tropical fruit, closer to the Loire style.":"較涼爽的園地帶來較少的熱帶水果，更接近羅亞爾河的風格。","Sancerre is dry, with green apple, grass and sometimes wet stones. Riper grapes would go the opposite way, new oak would hide the herbaceous aromas, and residual sugar does not match the dry Loire style.":"Sancerre 不甜，帶有青蘋果、青草，有時還有濕石頭。較成熟的葡萄會往相反方向走，新橡木桶會掩蓋草本香氣，而殘糖也不符合羅亞爾河不甜的風格。","Which statement about Adelaide Hills Sauvignon Blanc is correct?":"關於 Adelaide Hills 的白蘇維濃，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","Most are fresh and fruity, from citrus to tropical fruit":"大多清爽、果香豐富，從柑橘到熱帶水果都有","Almost all are sweet, from late-harvested grapes":"幾乎都是用晚收葡萄釀的甜酒","They come from hot, irrigated inland plains":"它們來自炎熱、經灌溉的內陸平原","They are never blended with Semillon":"它們從不與榭密雍混調","Cooled by altitude, Adelaide Hills gives fresh Sauvignons with fruit from citrus to tropical.":"因海拔而涼爽的 Adelaide Hills，出產果味從柑橘到熱帶水果的清爽白蘇維濃。","Sauvignon Blanc is the area's most planted grape. Some wines are blended with Semillon for more body and ageing potential, so 'never' is wrong. They are not sweet and do not come from hot plains.":"白蘇維濃是這個地區種植最多的品種。有些酒會與榭密雍混調以增添酒體和陳年潛力，所以「從不」是錯的。它們不是甜酒，也不是來自炎熱的平原。","Why do some Adelaide Hills producers add Semillon to Sauvignon Blanc?":"為什麼有些 Adelaide Hills 的生產者會在白蘇維濃中加入榭密雍？","For more body and greater ageing potential":"為了更飽滿的酒體和更強的陳年潛力","To boost green-pepper aromas":"為了增強青椒香氣","To lower the alcohol level":"為了降低酒精濃度","To give the wine a pink tint that looks better on the shelf":"為了讓酒帶點粉紅色調，在貨架上更好看","Semillon adds body and helps the wine age.":"榭密雍增添酒體並幫助酒陳年。","Semillon plays the same role as in Bordeaux: it makes the wine fuller and longer-lived. It does not strengthen the herbaceous aromas, which come from Sauvignon, and it does not lower alcohol. It is a white grape, so it gives no pink colour.":"榭密雍扮演的角色和在波爾多一樣：讓酒更飽滿、壽命更長。它不會增強來自白蘇維濃的草本香氣，也不會降低酒精。它是白葡萄，所以不會帶來粉紅色。","A Margaret River Sauvignon Blanc–Semillon blend: what should you expect?":"一款 Margaret River 的白蘇維濃與榭密雍混調：你應該預期什麼？","Concentrated grassy aromas; sometimes oak contact":"濃縮的青草香氣；有時與橡木接觸","A sweet botrytised wine with honey, apricot and caramel":"帶有蜂蜜、杏桃和焦糖的貴腐甜酒","A neutral, light wine from very early-picked grapes":"用非常早採的葡萄釀造的中性輕盈酒款","Red fruit and soft tannins":"紅色水果和柔和的單寧","Margaret River is known for Sauvignon–Semillon blends with concentrated grassy notes, sometimes with oak contact.":"Margaret River 以帶有濃縮青草氣息的白蘇維濃與榭密雍混調著稱，有時與橡木接觸。","These dry blends show intense grassiness and, in some cases, a touch of oak. Sweet botrytised wine is typical of Sauternes; neutral early-picked Semillon describes Hunter Valley. Red fruit and tannins point to a red.":"這些不甜的混調展現濃烈的青草味，有些還帶一絲橡木味。貴腐甜酒是 Sauternes 的典型特徵；中性的早採榭密雍描述的是 Hunter Valley。紅色水果和單寧則指向紅酒。","What range of quality does Chile's Central Valley Sauvignon Blanc offer?":"智利 Central Valley 的白蘇維濃提供什麼樣的品質範圍？","From inexpensive high-volume brands to very good examples":"從平價的大量生產品牌到非常好的酒款","Only very expensive wines from tiny plots":"只有來自極小地塊、非常昂貴的酒","Only sweet wines":"只有甜酒","None: the area is too cold to ripen Sauvignon Blanc":"沒有：這個地區太冷，白蘇維濃無法成熟","The large Central Valley makes Sauvignon at every level, from brands to very good wines.":"廣大的 Central Valley 出產各個等級的白蘇維濃，從品牌酒到非常好的酒款都有。","The Central Valley is larger and warmer than coastal Casablanca Valley, known for very good quality. Its size is exactly what explains the range of levels. It is not too cold (it is warm) and does not specialise in sweet wines.":"Central Valley 比以非常好的品質著稱的沿海 Casablanca Valley 更大、更溫暖。正是它的面積解釋了等級的多樣。它並不太冷（它很溫暖），也不專門生產甜酒。","What style of Sauvignon Blanc does Constantia produce?":"Constantia 出產什麼風格的白蘇維濃？","Refreshing, with ripe tropical fruit and herbaceous notes":"令人清爽，帶有成熟的熱帶水果和草本氣息","Neutral, with apple and wet stones":"中性，帶有蘋果和濕石頭","Sweet and botrytised, made for long cellaring":"甜型貴腐酒，適合長期窖藏","Heavily oaked, with vanilla":"橡木味很重，帶有香草","Southern Ocean breezes cool Constantia: fresh, tropical and herbaceous Sauvignon.":"南冰洋的微風讓 Constantia 降溫：清爽、帶熱帶水果和草本氣息的白蘇維濃。","Constantia, south of Cape Town, combines ripe tropical fruit and herbaceous notes in refreshing wines. Apple and wet stones are more typical of cooler Elgin. It is neither a sweet nor a heavily oaked style.":"開普敦以南的 Constantia，在令人清爽的酒中結合了成熟的熱帶水果和草本氣息。蘋果和濕石頭更是較涼爽的 Elgin 的典型特徵。它既不是甜型風格，也不是橡木味很重的風格。","A South African Sauvignon Blanc tastes of green apple and wet stones. Which area does it most likely come from?":"一款南非白蘇維濃嚐起來有青蘋果和濕石頭。它最可能來自哪個地區？","The hot inland vineyards of the Western Cape":"西開普炎熱的內陸葡萄園","Elgin, cooled by altitude, gives Sauvignons with green apple and sometimes wet stones.":"因海拔而涼爽的 Elgin，出產帶有青蘋果、有時帶濕石頭的白蘇維濃。","Elgin is often cited as South Africa's coolest region, hence the green fruit. Constantia gives a more tropical style; inland vineyards are generally too warm for Sauvignon. Stellenbosch is known mainly for reds.":"Elgin 常被稱為南非最涼爽的產區，因此有綠色水果。Constantia 的風格更具熱帶水果味；內陸葡萄園對白蘇維濃來說一般太溫暖。Stellenbosch 則主要以紅酒著稱。","What cools Elgin, compared with Constantia?":"與 Constantia 相比，是什麼讓 Elgin 涼爽？","Altitude; Constantia is cooled by sea breezes":"海拔；Constantia 則因海風而涼爽","Morning fog from a bay; Constantia by altitude":"來自海灣的晨霧；Constantia 則因海拔而涼爽","A mountain range that blocks rain; Constantia by a cold current":"阻擋雨水的山脈；Constantia 則因寒冷洋流而涼爽","Nothing: both are warm":"沒有：兩者都很溫暖","Elgin is cool because of altitude, Constantia because of Southern Ocean breezes.":"Elgin 因海拔而涼爽，Constantia 則因南冰洋的微風而涼爽。","Two nearby areas, two different influences: altitude makes Elgin the coolest and gives green fruit; the sea cools Constantia, which keeps more tropical fruit. Both are coastal and cool, not warm like the interior.":"兩個相鄰的地區，兩種不同的影響：海拔讓 Elgin 成為最涼爽的地區，帶來綠色水果；海洋讓 Constantia 降溫，保留較多熱帶水果。兩者都是涼爽的沿海地區，不像內陸那樣溫暖。","Why does much of California struggle to make the classic fresh, herbaceous Sauvignon?":"為什麼加州大部分地區難以釀出經典的清爽草本風格白蘇維濃？","The climate is mostly too warm":"氣候大多太溫暖","The climate is too cold and wet":"氣候太冷太濕","The law forbids single-varietal Sauvignon Blanc":"法律禁止單一品種的白蘇維濃","Chalky soils stop the grapes from developing herbaceous aromas":"白堊土讓葡萄無法發展出草本香氣","Heat strips acidity and herbaceous aromas, so cooler areas and early picking are needed.":"高溫會奪走酸度和草本香氣，所以需要較涼爽的地區和提早採收。","Sauvignon Blanc prefers cool and moderate climates. In California the best come from the cooler areas, such as parts of Napa Valley, with early picking. Cold, legal bans or soils are not the causes.":"白蘇維濃偏好涼爽和溫和的氣候。在加州，最好的酒來自較涼爽的地區，例如 Napa Valley 的部分地方，並提早採收。寒冷、法律禁令或土壤都不是原因。","Why are some Sauvignon Blanc producers experimenting beyond the classic style?":"為什麼有些白蘇維濃生產者會在經典風格之外進行嘗試？","They fear consumers may tire of intense herbaceous aromas":"他們擔心消費者可能對濃烈的草本香氣感到厭倦","The grape has become unpopular and sales are collapsing everywhere":"這個品種已經不受歡迎，各地銷量都在崩跌","New laws require oak":"新法律規定必須使用橡木桶","The climate has become too cold":"氣候變得太冷","The style is so recognisable that some producers look for points of difference to keep it interesting.":"這種風格太容易辨識，有些生產者尋找差異點來保持新鮮感。","Sauvignon Blanc is very popular today, almost like a trusted brand: that is exactly why some fear fatigue. Sales are not collapsing and oak is not compulsory; using wood or lees is a choice.":"白蘇維濃現在非常受歡迎，幾乎像一個值得信賴的品牌：正是因此有人擔心消費者會厭倦。銷量並沒有崩跌，橡木桶也不是強制的；使用木桶或酒渣是一種選擇。","A customer opens a simple, unoaked Sauvignon Blanc from four years ago. What will they most likely find?":"一位顧客打開一瓶四年前的簡單、未經橡木桶的白蘇維濃。他最可能發現什麼？","Faded fresh aromas and unattractive vegetal notes":"清新香氣已經消退，出現不討喜的植物性氣息","Complex honey, hazelnut and dried-fruit notes, like a great aged white":"複雜的蜂蜜、榛果和果乾氣息，就像偉大的陳年白酒","More fresh tropical fruit":"更多新鮮的熱帶水果","Forest-floor and mushroom aromas":"森林地表和蘑菇香氣","Sauvignon Blanc is for drinking young: after a couple of years it loses freshness and turns vegetal.":"白蘇維濃要趁年輕喝：一兩年後就會失去清新感，變得有植物味。","Only some oaked Semillon blends from Graves or Pessac-Léognan develop honey and nuts. A simple, unoaked Sauvignon instead loses its fresh aromas. Fruit does not increase with time, and forest floor and mushroom are typical of reds such as aged Pinot Noir.":"只有一些來自 Graves 或 Pessac-Léognan、經橡木桶的榭密雍混調會發展出蜂蜜和堅果。簡單、未經橡木桶的白蘇維濃反而會失去清新的香氣。果味不會隨時間增加，而森林地表和蘑菇是陳年黑皮諾等紅酒的典型特徵。","Which of these regions is NOT known for South African Sauvignon Blanc?":"下列哪一個產區不以南非白蘇維濃著稱？","The coastal areas near Cape Town":"開普敦附近的沿海地區","Casablanca Valley is in Chile, not South Africa.":"Casablanca Valley 在智利，不在南非。","Casablanca Valley is also known for very good Sauvignon Blanc, but it is a Chilean coastal area cooled by Pacific breezes and fog. In South Africa, Sauvignon is concentrated on the coast: Constantia, south of Cape Town, and Elgin.":"Casablanca Valley 也以非常好的白蘇維濃著稱，但它是智利的沿海地區，受到太平洋微風和霧氣的降溫。在南非，白蘇維濃集中在沿海：開普敦以南的 Constantia 以及 Elgin。","Two Sauvignon Blancs: one with green apple, grass and wet stones, the other with grapefruit, passion fruit and intense green pepper. Which origins are most likely?":"兩款白蘇維濃：一款帶有青蘋果、青草和濕石頭，另一款帶有葡萄柚、百香果和濃烈的青椒。最可能的產地是什麼？","The first Sancerre, the second Marlborough":"第一款是 Sancerre，第二款是 Marlborough","The first Marlborough, the second Sancerre":"第一款是 Marlborough，第二款是 Sancerre","Both Pessac-Léognan, but from different vintages and oak regimes":"兩款都是 Pessac-Léognan，但年份和橡木桶處理不同","The first Constantia, the second Touraine":"第一款是 Constantia，第二款是 Touraine","The restrained wet-stone style is Loire; the explosive tropical, green-pepper style is Marlborough.":"內斂、帶濕石頭的風格是羅亞爾河；熱帶水果和青椒奔放的風格是 Marlborough。","Sancerre is cool: green apple, grass, asparagus and sometimes wet stones. Marlborough blends grapes from different sites and ripeness levels, with grapefruit, peach, passion fruit and pronounced green pepper. Constantia is tropical and Touraine fruity and simple, so the last pairing does not fit.":"Sancerre 很涼爽：青蘋果、青草、蘆筍，有時還有濕石頭。Marlborough 混調來自不同園地和成熟度的葡萄，帶有葡萄柚、桃子、百香果和鮮明的青椒。Constantia 帶熱帶水果味，Touraine 果香豐富但簡單，所以最後一個組合不符合。","A label reads 'Pessac-Léognan blanc'. Which grapes does it most likely contain?":"一張酒標上寫著「Pessac-Léognan blanc」。它最可能含有哪些品種？","Chardonnay and Pinot Gris":"夏多內和灰皮諾","Only Sauvignon Blanc, by law, as in Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé":"依法只能用白蘇維濃，就像 Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé","Riesling and Chenin Blanc":"麗絲玲和白梢楠","Pessac-Léognan whites are usually Sauvignon Blanc and Semillon blends.":"Pessac-Léognan 白酒通常是白蘇維濃與榭密雍的混調。","As in Graves, Semillon adds body and longevity to Sauvignon and the best wines see oak. The Sauvignon-only rule applies to Sancerre and Pouilly-Fumé, not Bordeaux. Chardonnay, Pinot Gris, Riesling and Chenin are not grapes of this area.":"和 Graves 一樣，榭密雍為白蘇維濃增添酒體和陳年潛力，最好的酒款會經過橡木桶。只能用白蘇維濃的規定適用於 Sancerre 和 Pouilly-Fumé，不適用於波爾多。夏多內、灰皮諾、麗絲玲和白梢楠都不是這個地區的品種。","Which statement about Sauvignon Blanc is FALSE?":"關於白蘇維濃，下列哪一項敘述是錯誤的？","It performs best in warm climates":"它在溫暖氣候中表現最好","It is considered a French variety":"它被視為法國品種","It is usually made without oak":"它通常不使用橡木桶","It is usually best young, while still fresh and highly aromatic":"它通常最好趁年輕喝，那時仍清爽且香氣濃郁","Sauvignon Blanc performs best in cool and moderate climates, not warm ones.":"白蘇維濃在涼爽和溫和氣候中表現最好，而不是溫暖氣候。","Heat strips Sauvignon of acidity and herbaceous aromas: in warm areas it needs altitude, breezes or early picking. The other statements are true: it is considered French, is now grown worldwide, is mostly unoaked and is best drunk young.":"高溫會奪走白蘇維濃的酸度和草本香氣：在溫暖地區，它需要海拔、微風或提早採收。其他敘述都是正確的：它被視為法國品種，現在種植於世界各地，大多不經橡木桶，最好趁年輕喝。","Which climate does Riesling prefer?":"麗絲玲偏好哪種氣候？","Cool to moderate":"涼爽至溫和","Moderate to hot":"溫和至炎熱","Riesling is a cold-hardy grape that prefers cool to moderate climates.":"麗絲玲是耐寒的品種，偏好涼爽至溫和的氣候。","Riesling copes well with cold and prefers cool to moderate climates, where the grapes ripen slowly and keep their high natural acidity. It does best in cool, dry, sunny regions such as the Mosel, Rheingau, Alsace or Australia's higher-altitude Clare and Eden Valleys. A hot climate would cost it freshness and aromatic finesse.":"麗絲玲很能耐寒，偏好涼爽至溫和的氣候，在那裡葡萄成熟緩慢，保留高天然酸度。它在涼爽、乾燥、陽光充足的產區表現最好，例如 Mosel、Rheingau、阿爾薩斯，或澳洲海拔較高的 Clare Valley 和 Eden Valley。炎熱的氣候會讓它失去清新感和細緻的香氣。","Why can Riesling make outstanding wines at every sweetness level?":"為什麼麗絲玲在每一種甜度都能釀出傑出的酒？","High natural acidity and susceptibility to botrytis":"高天然酸度，以及容易感染貴腐菌","Thick skins and high tannins":"厚果皮和高單寧","Low acidity and high alcohol":"低酸度和高酒精","Fast ripening and high yields":"成熟快速和高產量","Acidity balances sweetness, and botrytis concentrates grapes for sweet styles.":"酸度平衡甜度，而貴腐菌為甜型風格濃縮葡萄。","Riesling has high natural acidity that persists even when the grapes are very ripe. That acidity keeps dry wines fresh and balances the sugar in sweet wines perfectly. The grape is also susceptible to botrytis, which concentrates sugars, acidity and flavours and allows great sweet wines such as Beerenauslese and Trockenbeerenauslese.":"麗絲玲有高天然酸度，即使葡萄非常成熟時依然存在。這種酸度讓不甜的酒保持清爽，也完美平衡甜酒中的糖分。這個品種也容易感染貴腐菌，貴腐菌會濃縮糖分、酸度和風味，造就 Beerenauslese 和 Trockenbeerenauslese 等偉大的甜酒。","Which aromas do just-ripe Riesling grapes usually give?":"剛成熟的麗絲玲葡萄通常帶來哪些香氣？","Green apple, lemon, lime, blossom":"青蘋果、檸檬、萊姆、花香","Mango, pineapple, dried apricot":"芒果、鳳梨、杏桃乾","Honey, petrol, dried fruit":"蜂蜜、汽油、果乾","Just-ripe grapes give green fruit, citrus and blossom.":"剛成熟的葡萄帶來綠色水果、柑橘和花香。","Riesling's aromas follow ripeness. With just-ripe grapes, green fruit such as apple and pear, citrus such as lemon and lime, and floral notes dominate. With extra-ripe grapes, peach, apricot, mango, pineapple and sometimes dried fruit appear. Honey and petrol, by contrast, are tertiary aromas that come with bottle age.":"麗絲玲的香氣隨成熟度變化。葡萄剛成熟時，以蘋果和梨等綠色水果、檸檬和萊姆等柑橘以及花香為主。葡萄過熟時，會出現桃子、杏桃、芒果、鳳梨，有時還有果乾。相反地，蜂蜜和汽油是瓶中陳年後才出現的三級香氣。","Which aromas point to a Riesling made from extra-ripe grapes?":"哪些香氣表示麗絲玲是用過熟的葡萄釀造的？","Peach, apricot, mango, pineapple":"桃子、杏桃、芒果、鳳梨","Green apple, pear, lemon":"青蘋果、梨、檸檬","Grass, green pepper, gooseberry":"青草、青椒、醋栗","Forest floor, mushroom, earth":"森林地表、蘑菇、泥土","Extra-ripe grapes bring stone and tropical fruit, sometimes dried fruit.":"過熟的葡萄帶來核果和熱帶水果，有時還有果乾。","When Riesling is picked extra-ripe, its aromas shift from green fruit and citrus to stone fruit (peach, apricot) and tropical fruit (mango, pineapple). In the most extreme cases, dried-fruit notes such as dried apricot appear too. These aromas are typical of Spätlese, Auslese and concentrated sweet styles.":"麗絲玲在過熟時採收，香氣會從綠色水果和柑橘轉向核果（桃子、杏桃）和熱帶水果（芒果、鳳梨）。在最極端的情況下，也會出現杏桃乾等果乾氣息。這些香氣是 Spätlese、Auslese 和濃縮甜型風格的典型特徵。","Why is Riesling suited to late harvesting?":"為什麼麗絲玲適合晚收？","It keeps its acidity and builds sugar slowly":"它能保留酸度，糖分累積緩慢","Its thick skins resist autumn rain":"它的厚果皮能抵抗秋雨","It loses acidity quickly late in the season":"它在季末會迅速失去酸度","It ripens very early in summer":"它在夏天很早就成熟","Riesling stays acidic while sugar and flavour build slowly, given a dry, sunny autumn.":"麗絲玲保持酸度，糖分和風味緩慢累積，前提是秋天乾燥晴朗。","Riesling builds sugar and flavour slowly without losing its acidity. In regions with dry, sunny autumns, the grapes can therefore hang on the vine for a long time and concentrate. The result is richer, often sweet wines that stay fresh thanks to their acidity. A grape that lost acidity quickly would give heavy, unbalanced sweet wines instead.":"麗絲玲緩慢累積糖分和風味，卻不會失去酸度。因此在秋天乾燥晴朗的產區，葡萄可以在樹上掛很久並濃縮。結果是更豐潤、常常是甜的酒，因為酸度而保持清爽。迅速失去酸度的品種，則會釀出沉重、失衡的甜酒。","Unfermented grape juice added to the wine":"加入酒中的未發酵葡萄汁","Yeast added to restart fermentation":"加入酵母以重新啟動發酵","Wine aged in wooden barrels":"在木桶中陳年的酒","Süssreserve is unfermented juice used to sweeten off-dry or medium Riesling.":"Süssreserve 是用來為微甜或半甜麗絲玲增甜的未發酵葡萄汁。","Off-dry and medium Riesling styles can be made in two ways. The first is to stop fermentation by removing the yeasts, which leaves sugar and lower alcohol. The second is to add a small amount of unfermented grape juice, called Süssreserve, to a dry wine, bringing sweetness and fresh grape flavour.":"微甜和半甜的麗絲玲風格可以用兩種方式釀造。第一種是去除酵母以中止發酵，留下糖分，酒精也較低。第二種是在不甜的酒中加入少量未發酵的葡萄汁，稱為 Süssreserve，帶來甜味和新鮮的葡萄風味。","What happens when a Riesling fermentation is stopped by removing the yeasts?":"以去除酵母的方式中止麗絲玲的發酵，會發生什麼？","Residual sugar remains and alcohol is lower":"留下殘糖，酒精較低","The wine becomes dry and higher in alcohol":"酒變得不甜，酒精較高","Acidity falls and the colour darkens":"酸度下降，顏色變深","The wine develops honey and petrol notes":"酒發展出蜂蜜和汽油氣息","Without yeasts, some sugar is never turned into alcohol: sweeter, lower-alcohol wine.":"沒有酵母，部分糖分永遠不會轉化為酒精：酒更甜、酒精更低。","During fermentation, yeasts turn the sugar in the juice into alcohol. If they are removed before they finish, some sugar stays in the wine as residual sugar and the alcohol level remains lower. This is one of the methods used to make off-dry and medium Rieslings, alongside adding Süssreserve.":"發酵期間，酵母把果汁中的糖轉化為酒精。如果在它們完成之前就被去除，部分糖分會以殘糖的形式留在酒中，酒精濃度也較低。這是釀造微甜和半甜麗絲玲的方法之一，另一種是加入 Süssreserve。","Why does fermentation stop naturally in the sweetest Riesling styles?":"為什麼在最甜的麗絲玲風格中，發酵會自然停止？","The juice is too sugary for the yeasts":"果汁對酵母來說太甜了","Alcohol is added during fermentation":"發酵期間加入了酒精","It is fermented in new oak barrels":"在新橡木桶中發酵","Süssreserve is added to the juice":"在果汁中加入 Süssreserve","With extra-ripe grapes, sugar is so high that yeasts cannot ferment it all.":"用過熟的葡萄時，糖分高到酵母無法全部發酵。","The sweetest Riesling styles come from extra-ripe grapes, often concentrated by late harvesting, botrytis or freezing. The juice contains so much sugar that yeasts cannot convert it all into alcohol, and fermentation stops on its own. The wines therefore stay sweet and low in alcohol, balanced by high acidity.":"最甜的麗絲玲風格來自過熟的葡萄，常經由晚收、貴腐或冰凍而濃縮。果汁含有大量的糖，酵母無法把它全部轉化為酒精，發酵就自行停止。因此這些酒保持甜美、酒精低，並以高酸度平衡。","Why is Riesling usually fermented in stainless steel?":"為什麼麗絲玲通常在不鏽鋼槽中發酵？","To preserve its floral aromas":"為了保留它的花香","To add vanilla and smoke notes":"為了增添香草和煙燻氣息","To soften the tannins":"為了讓單寧變柔和","To encourage oxidation":"為了促進氧化","Inert vessels add no flavour and protect Riesling's aromatic character.":"惰性容器不會增添風味，能保護麗絲玲的芳香特色。","Riesling is an aromatic grape whose appeal lies in its fruit and floral aromas. That is why inert vessels such as stainless steel are used: they add no oak flavours and protect the fruit. Vanilla and smoke notes would come from oak, and as a white wine, Riesling has no significant tannins to soften.":"麗絲玲是芳香型品種，魅力在於果香和花香。這就是為什麼使用不鏽鋼槽等惰性容器：它們不會增添橡木風味，能保護果味。香草和煙燻氣息會來自橡木桶，而麗絲玲作為白酒，沒有明顯的單寧需要柔化。","Which tertiary aromas does a fine aged Riesling develop?":"優質的陳年麗絲玲會發展出哪些三級香氣？","Honey and petrol":"蜂蜜和汽油","Earth and meat":"泥土和肉","Vanilla and coffee":"香草和咖啡","With age, Riesling develops honey and petrol while acidity keeps it fresh.":"隨著陳年，麗絲玲發展出蜂蜜和汽油，而酸度讓它保持清爽。","The finest Rieslings can age for years or decades. Over time they develop complex tertiary aromas of honey and petrol, while high acidity keeps them fresh. Forest floor and mushroom are typical of aged Pinot Noir, earth and meat of old-vine Zinfandel, and vanilla and coffee come from oak.":"最優質的麗絲玲可以陳年數年甚至數十年。隨著時間，它們會發展出蜂蜜和汽油的複雜三級香氣，而高酸度讓它們保持清爽。森林地表和蘑菇是陳年黑皮諾的典型特徵，泥土和肉是老藤金芬黛的典型特徵，香草和咖啡則來自橡木桶。","Which style is typical of a Mosel Riesling?":"哪一種風格是 Mosel 麗絲玲的典型特徵？","Light body, medium sweetness, very high acidity":"酒體輕盈、半甜、酸度非常高","Full body, dry, low acidity":"酒體飽滿、不甜、低酸度","Medium body, dry, new-oak notes":"酒體中等、不甜、帶新橡木桶氣息","Full body, sweet, low acidity":"酒體飽滿、甜、低酸度","Its northerly latitude makes Mosel Riesling light, with sweetness balancing very high acidity.":"偏北的緯度讓 Mosel 麗絲玲輕盈，以甜度平衡非常高的酸度。","The Mosel is one of Germany's most northerly wine regions. The cool climate gives grapes with very high acidity and wines lighter in body than those from further south. To balance that acidity, many Mosel Rieslings have medium sweetness. The Rheingau and Pfalz, warmer and sunnier, give drier, fuller-bodied wines instead.":"Mosel 是德國最北的葡萄酒產區之一。涼爽的氣候讓葡萄酸度非常高，酒體也比更南方的酒輕盈。為了平衡這樣的酸度，許多 Mosel 麗絲玲是半甜的。更溫暖、陽光更充足的 Rheingau 和 Pfalz 則出產更不甜、酒體更飽滿的酒。","What helps grapes ripen in the best Mosel vineyards?":"在 Mosel 最好的葡萄園中，是什麼幫助葡萄成熟？","Steep south-facing slopes, stony soils and light reflected off the river":"朝南的陡坡、多石的土壤和河面反射的光線","Flat valley floors and deep clay soils":"平坦的谷底和深厚的黏土","Morning fogs and ocean breezes":"晨霧和海風","High altitude and warm nights":"高海拔和溫暖的夜晚","Southerly aspect, heat-holding stones and river-reflected light all aid ripening.":"朝南的坡向、能保溫的石頭和河面反射的光線都有助於成熟。","In the cool Mosel, every source of warmth counts. The best vineyards are planted on very steep south- or south-west-facing slopes along the river. The aspect increases the sunlight received, the stony soils aid ripening, and the river reflects sunlight back onto the vines. This lets the grapes ripen despite the northerly latitude.":"在涼爽的 Mosel，每一點熱源都很重要。最好的葡萄園種在沿河、朝南或西南的非常陡峭的坡地上。坡向增加了接收的日照，多石的土壤有助於成熟，而河流把陽光反射回葡萄樹上。這讓葡萄儘管緯度偏北也能成熟。","How do Rheingau Rieslings differ from Mosel Rieslings?":"Rheingau 的麗絲玲與 Mosel 的麗絲玲有什麼不同？","They are drier and fuller-bodied":"更不甜，酒體更飽滿","They are sweeter and lighter":"更甜、更輕盈","They are more tannic and new-oaked":"單寧更多，經新橡木桶","They are always made from frozen grapes":"總是用冰凍的葡萄釀造","South-facing slopes on the Rhine's north bank give drier, fuller Rieslings than the Mosel.":"萊茵河北岸的朝南坡地，釀出比 Mosel 更不甜、更飽滿的麗絲玲。","In the Rheingau, vineyards lie on steep south-facing slopes on the north bank of the Rhine to make the most of sun and warmth. The grapes ripen more fully, and the wines are generally drier and fuller-bodied than in the Mosel, where the more northerly climate gives light Rieslings, often with medium sweetness.":"在 Rheingau，葡萄園位於萊茵河北岸朝南的陡坡上，以充分利用陽光和熱量。葡萄成熟得更充分，酒一般比 Mosel 更不甜、酒體更飽滿；Mosel 較偏北的氣候則帶來輕盈、常常是半甜的麗絲玲。","Which German region, sheltered by mountains to the west, is seen as a climatic extension of Alsace?":"德國哪個產區西邊受山脈屏障，被視為阿爾薩斯氣候的延伸？","The Pfalz, near the French border, is dry and sunny like Alsace and makes dry Rieslings.":"靠近法國邊境的 Pfalz 像阿爾薩斯一樣乾燥晴朗，出產不甜的麗絲玲。","The Pfalz lies towards the French border and is sheltered by mountains to the west, giving it a dry, sunny climate. It is therefore seen almost as a climatic extension of Alsace, and its wines are similar in style: a typical Pfalz Riesling is dry and medium-bodied. The Mosel and Rheingau are other German regions, while Clare Valley is in Australia.":"Pfalz 位於靠近法國邊境的地方，西邊受山脈屏障，氣候乾燥晴朗。因此它幾乎被視為阿爾薩斯氣候的延伸，酒的風格也相似：典型的 Pfalz 麗絲玲不甜、酒體中等。Mosel 和 Rheingau 是德國的其他產區，而 Clare Valley 在澳洲。","Why is Alsace one of the driest and sunniest wine regions in France?":"為什麼阿爾薩斯是法國最乾燥、陽光最充足的葡萄酒產區之一？","The Vosges shelter it from rainy westerly winds":"孚日山脈為它擋住多雨的西風","Rhine fogs trap the heat":"萊茵河的霧氣留住了熱量","It lies at a very southerly latitude":"它位於非常偏南的緯度","It receives warm Mediterranean breezes":"它受到溫暖的地中海微風吹拂","Alsace lies east of the Vosges, which block rain-bearing westerly winds.":"阿爾薩斯位於孚日山脈以東，山脈阻擋了帶雨的西風。","Alsace AOC lies east of the Vosges Mountains. These mountains stop the moist winds coming from the west, so the region gets little rain and plenty of sun. The best vineyards are on east- or south-east-facing slopes for the morning sun, and dry autumns extend ripening, giving dry, intense Rieslings.":"Alsace AOC 位於孚日山脈以東。這些山脈擋住了從西方吹來的潮濕氣流，所以這個地區雨量少、陽光充足。最好的葡萄園位於朝東或東南的坡地上，以接收早晨的陽光，而乾燥的秋天延長了成熟期，釀出不甜、濃郁的麗絲玲。","Which description fits a typical Alsace Riesling?":"哪一項描述符合典型的阿爾薩斯麗絲玲？","Dry, pronounced, medium body, high acidity":"不甜、香氣濃郁、酒體中等、高酸度","Light, medium sweetness, low alcohol":"輕盈、半甜、低酒精","Sweet, amber, with caramel notes":"甜、琥珀色、帶焦糖氣息","Dry, neutral, low acidity":"不甜、中性、低酸度","Alsace Riesling is dry, with ripe citrus and stone fruit, medium body and high acidity.":"阿爾薩斯麗絲玲不甜，帶有成熟的柑橘和核果，酒體中等，酸度高。","Alsace's dry, sunny climate brings the grapes to good ripeness. A typical Alsace Riesling is therefore dry, with pronounced aromas and flavours of ripe citrus and stone fruit, medium body and high acidity. The best come from grand cru vineyards. The light, medium-sweet style is more typical of the Mosel.":"阿爾薩斯乾燥晴朗的氣候讓葡萄達到良好的成熟度。因此典型的阿爾薩斯麗絲玲不甜，帶有成熟柑橘和核果的濃郁香氣和風味，酒體中等，酸度高。最好的酒來自 grand cru 葡萄園。輕盈半甜的風格則更是 Mosel 的典型特徵。","What does Vendanges Tardives on an Alsace Riesling label indicate?":"阿爾薩斯麗絲玲酒標上的 Vendanges Tardives 代表什麼？","A sweeter style from late-harvested grapes":"用晚收葡萄釀的較甜風格","A wine from a grand cru vineyard":"來自 grand cru 葡萄園的酒","A dry wine aged in new oak":"在新橡木桶中陳年的不甜酒","A wine from grapes frozen on the vine":"用在樹上結冰的葡萄釀的酒","Vendanges Tardives means late harvest: riper grapes and a sweeter wine.":"Vendanges Tardives 是晚收的意思：葡萄更成熟，酒更甜。","Alongside dry Rieslings, Alsace also makes sweeter styles. These come from leaving the grapes on the vine for longer, taking advantage of dry autumns so sugars and flavours concentrate. Such wines are labelled Vendanges Tardives. Wines from grapes frozen on the vine are German Eiswein instead.":"除了不甜的麗絲玲，阿爾薩斯也出產較甜的風格。這些酒來自讓葡萄在樹上留得更久，利用乾燥的秋天讓糖分和風味濃縮。這樣的酒標示為 Vendanges Tardives。用在樹上結冰的葡萄釀的酒，則是德國的 Eiswein。","Why do Eden Valley and Clare Valley have moderate climates, unlike nearby Barossa Valley?":"為什麼 Eden Valley 和 Clare Valley 屬於溫和氣候，而不像鄰近的 Barossa Valley？","Because of their higher altitude":"因為它們海拔較高","Because of Pacific fogs":"因為太平洋的霧氣","Because of a ring of mountains":"因為一圈環繞的山脈","Because of light reflected off rivers":"因為河面反射的光線","Altitude cools Eden and Clare Valleys, suiting dry, fresh Riesling.":"海拔讓 Eden Valley 和 Clare Valley 保持涼爽，適合不甜、清爽的麗絲玲。","Australia's premium Riesling is centred on South Australia's Eden Valley and Clare Valley. These valleys sit higher than the nearby warm Barossa Valley, and the altitude lowers temperatures, creating a moderate climate. They produce refreshing dry Rieslings with pronounced aromas of lime, lemon and sometimes petrol.":"澳洲的頂級麗絲玲集中在南澳的 Eden Valley 和 Clare Valley。這些山谷比鄰近溫暖的 Barossa Valley 海拔更高，海拔降低了溫度，形成溫和氣候。它們出產令人清爽的不甜麗絲玲，帶有萊姆、檸檬，有時還有汽油的濃郁香氣。","A dry, refreshing Riesling with pronounced lime, lemon and a hint of petrol most likely comes from:":"一款不甜、清爽、帶有濃郁萊姆、檸檬和一絲汽油味的麗絲玲，最可能來自：","Mosel, medium-sweet style":"Mosel，半甜風格","Alsace, Vendanges Tardives":"阿爾薩斯，Vendanges Tardives","Germany, Eiswein":"德國，Eiswein","Lime, lemon and petrol in a dry Riesling are typical of Clare and Eden Valleys.":"不甜麗絲玲中的萊姆、檸檬和汽油，是 Clare Valley 和 Eden Valley 的典型特徵。","Australia's Clare and Eden Valleys, kept moderate by altitude, produce dry, refreshing Rieslings with pronounced lime and lemon and sometimes petrol. The other options are sweeter styles: the Mosel often gives medium-sweet wines, Alsace Vendanges Tardives is sweeter, and Eiswein is a sweet wine from frozen grapes.":"澳洲的 Clare Valley 和 Eden Valley 因海拔而保持溫和，出產不甜、清爽、帶有濃郁萊姆和檸檬、有時還有汽油的麗絲玲。其他選項都是較甜的風格：Mosel 常出產半甜的酒，阿爾薩斯的 Vendanges Tardives 更甜，而 Eiswein 是用冰凍葡萄釀的甜酒。","Why is Riesling often misunderstood by consumers?":"為什麼麗絲玲常被消費者誤解？","It is linked with Liebfraumilch, a low-quality sweet wine":"它與低品質的甜酒 Liebfraumilch 有關","It is confused with a black grape":"它被誤認為黑葡萄","People think it cannot age":"人們以為它無法陳年","People believe it is always oaked":"人們以為它總是經過橡木桶","Its German roots tie it to Liebfraumilch, a simple sweetened style now out of fashion.":"它的德國淵源讓它與 Liebfraumilch 連在一起，那是一種現已過時的簡單加甜風格。","Many consumers wrongly link Riesling with Liebfraumilch, a low-quality sweetened German wine that has fallen out of fashion. In fact Riesling makes high-quality wines from dry to sweet, and enthusiasts value it for its versatility, flavour intensity and ability to age. It is these premium wines that keep driving Riesling sales worldwide.":"許多消費者誤把麗絲玲與 Liebfraumilch 聯想在一起，那是一種已經過時的低品質加甜德國酒。事實上，麗絲玲能釀出從不甜到甜的高品質酒款，愛好者珍視它的多才多藝、風味強度和陳年能力。正是這些頂級酒款持續推動麗絲玲在全球的銷售。","What does it mean that Riesling is a 'cold-hardy' grape?":"麗絲玲是「耐寒」品種，這是什麼意思？","It copes well with cold, so it thrives in cool climates":"它很能耐寒，所以在涼爽氣候中生長茁壯","It must be fermented at very low temperatures":"它必須在非常低的溫度下發酵","It can only be grown where grapes freeze on the vine every year":"它只能種在葡萄每年都會在樹上結冰的地方","It must be served ice-cold":"它必須冰鎮後飲用","Cold-hardiness lets Riesling thrive in cool climates such as Germany.":"耐寒讓麗絲玲能在德國等涼爽氣候中生長茁壯。","The term is about the vine, not the winery or service. Riesling prefers cool to moderate climates; grapes freezing on the vine matter only for Eiswein, which is not made every year.":"這個術語說的是葡萄樹，不是酒廠或侍酒。麗絲玲偏好涼爽至溫和的氣候；葡萄在樹上結冰只與 Eiswein 有關，而 Eiswein 並不是每年都能釀。","Which of these does NOT concentrate sugars and flavours in Riesling grapes?":"下列哪一項不會濃縮麗絲玲葡萄的糖分和風味？","Adding Süssreserve":"加入 Süssreserve","Late harvesting":"晚收","Noble rot (botrytis)":"貴腐（貴腐菌）","Grapes freezing naturally on the vine, as for Eiswein":"葡萄在樹上自然結冰，如 Eiswein","Süssreserve is juice added to the wine: it sweetens but does not concentrate the grapes.":"Süssreserve 是加入酒中的果汁：它能增甜，但不會濃縮葡萄。","Late harvest, botrytis and freezing act on the grapes in the vineyard, concentrating sugar, acidity and flavour. Süssreserve is added after fermentation and is a way to make off-dry or medium wines, not a form of concentration.":"晚收、貴腐和冰凍都是在葡萄園中作用於葡萄，濃縮糖分、酸度和風味。Süssreserve 是在發酵後加入的，是釀造微甜或半甜酒的方法，不是一種濃縮方式。","Which autumn conditions does Riesling need for a successful late harvest?":"麗絲玲需要什麼樣的秋天條件才能成功晚收？","Dry, sunny autumns":"乾燥晴朗的秋天","Wet, warm autumns":"潮濕溫暖的秋天","Early September frosts that stop ripening early":"九月初的霜凍，讓成熟提早結束","Frequent hail":"頻繁的冰雹","A dry, sunny autumn keeps grapes healthy on the vine and lets them keep ripening slowly.":"乾燥晴朗的秋天讓葡萄在樹上保持健康，並繼續緩慢成熟。","Riesling builds sugar and flavour slowly while keeping its acidity: it is ideal for late harvesting, but only if the weather stays dry and sunny. Rain encourages unwanted rot, hail damages the grapes, and an early frost cuts ripening short.":"麗絲玲緩慢累積糖分和風味，同時保留酸度：它非常適合晚收，但前提是天氣保持乾燥晴朗。下雨會助長不受歡迎的腐爛，冰雹會損傷葡萄，而早來的霜凍會讓成熟提早中斷。","Its high natural acidity balances the sweetness":"它的高天然酸度平衡了甜度","The grape's tannins offset the sugar":"葡萄的單寧抵消了糖分","Its very high alcohol masks the sugar and warms the finish":"它非常高的酒精掩蓋了糖分，讓餘韻溫熱","New-oak ageing dries it out":"新橡木桶陳年讓它變乾","Riesling's high acidity is perfect for balancing high sugar levels.":"麗絲玲的高酸度非常適合平衡高糖分。","Acidity brings freshness and keeps sweet wines lively even after years. Riesling is a white without notable tannin; the sweetest examples often have low alcohol, and it is usually made in steel, not new oak.":"酸度帶來清新感，讓甜酒即使過了多年依然活潑。麗絲玲是沒有明顯單寧的白酒；最甜的酒款常常酒精很低，而且它通常在不鏽鋼槽而不是新橡木桶中釀造。","What keeps a fine Riesling tasting fresh after decades in bottle?":"是什麼讓優質麗絲玲在瓶中數十年後依然嚐起來清爽？","Its high natural acidity":"它的高天然酸度","Time in new barrels":"在新橡木桶中的時間","Carbon dioxide added at bottling":"裝瓶時加入的二氧化碳","High alcohol, acting as a natural preservative for many years":"高酒精，多年來作為天然防腐劑","High acidity keeps the wine lively while it develops honey and petrol.":"高酸度讓酒在發展出蜂蜜和汽油的同時保持活潑。","In Riesling, acidity is the key to longevity: the wine stays fresh as tertiary notes appear. It is usually made in inert vessels without new oak; alcohol is not the factor involved, and carbon dioxide has nothing to do with ageing.":"在麗絲玲中，酸度是長壽的關鍵：酒在三級氣息出現的同時保持清爽。它通常在惰性容器中釀造，不使用新橡木桶；酒精不是相關因素，二氧化碳也與陳年無關。","Why are Mosel Rieslings usually light-bodied?":"為什麼 Mosel 麗絲玲通常酒體輕盈？","Because of the very northerly latitude":"因為緯度非常偏北","Because they are always cut with water or juice, as German law requires":"因為德國法律規定一定要摻水或果汁","Because yields are very high":"因為產量非常高","Because of very fertile soils":"因為土壤非常肥沃","Mosel is among Germany's most northerly regions: grapes ripen less and wines are lighter.":"Mosel 是德國最北的產區之一：葡萄成熟度較低，酒也較輕盈。","Further north means less warmth and therefore less sugar and alcohol: that is why Mosel Riesling is lighter than wines from more southerly regions. There is no required blending, and the best vineyards are on steep, stony slopes, not fertile soils.":"越往北熱量越少，因此糖分和酒精也越少：這就是為什麼 Mosel 麗絲玲比更南方產區的酒輕盈。沒有規定要摻混，而最好的葡萄園位於多石的陡坡上，不是肥沃的土壤。","Why do many Mosel Rieslings have medium sweetness?":"為什麼許多 Mosel 麗絲玲是半甜的？","To balance very high acidity":"為了平衡非常高的酸度","To hide very harsh tannins":"為了掩蓋非常粗糙的單寧","Because the law bans dry Riesling in this region":"因為法律禁止這個產區釀造不甜的麗絲玲","To raise the alcohol and give more body and warmth":"為了提高酒精，帶來更多酒體和溫熱感","In the cool Mosel, residual sugar balances very high acidity.":"在涼爽的 Mosel，殘糖平衡了非常高的酸度。","The cool climate gives very acidic wines; a little sugar brings harmony. Riesling is not tannic, no law bans the dry style, and residual sugar does not raise alcohol: on the contrary, unfermented sugar means less alcohol.":"涼爽的氣候帶來非常酸的酒；一點糖分能帶來和諧。麗絲玲沒有單寧感，沒有法律禁止不甜風格，而殘糖也不會提高酒精：相反地，未發酵的糖代表酒精更少。","Why are the Rheingau's vineyards on the north bank of the Rhine?":"為什麼 Rheingau 的葡萄園位於萊茵河北岸？","So the slopes face south and get more sun and warmth":"讓坡地朝南，獲得更多陽光和熱量","To shield the vines from strong sun":"為葡萄樹遮擋強烈的陽光","Because the south bank is legally reserved for black grapes":"因為南岸依法保留給黑葡萄","To encourage fog and rot":"為了促進霧氣和腐爛","On the river's north bank, steep slopes face south and maximise light and warmth.":"在河的北岸，陡坡朝南，能最大化光照和熱量。","In a cool climate like Germany's, aspect is decisive: a south-facing slope ripens grapes better. This is why Rheingau Rieslings are drier and fuller than Mosel ones. The other options make no sense where the problem is a lack of warmth.":"在德國這樣的涼爽氣候中，坡向具有決定性：朝南的坡地讓葡萄成熟得更好。這就是為什麼 Rheingau 的麗絲玲比 Mosel 的更不甜、更飽滿。在問題是熱量不足的地方，其他選項都說不通。","A dry, medium-bodied Riesling from a German region near the French border most likely comes from:":"一款來自德國靠近法國邊境產區、不甜且酒體中等的麗絲玲，最可能來自：","Pfalz, towards the French border, gives dry, medium-bodied Rieslings.":"靠近法國邊境的 Pfalz 出產不甜、酒體中等的麗絲玲。","Pfalz is sheltered by mountains to the west, dry and sunny, and its wines resemble those of Alsace. Mosel gives lighter wines, often with medium sweetness; the Rheingau is not near France. Clare Valley is in Australia.":"Pfalz 西邊受山脈屏障，乾燥晴朗，它的酒與阿爾薩斯的相似。Mosel 的酒較輕盈，常常是半甜的；Rheingau 並不靠近法國。Clare Valley 則在澳洲。","Why are many German label terms based on grape ripeness?":"為什麼許多德國酒標術語是以葡萄成熟度為基礎？","The cool climate makes the desired ripeness hard to reach":"涼爽的氣候讓葡萄難以達到想要的成熟度","Because naming the grape on the label is banned in Germany":"因為德國禁止在酒標上標示品種","Because grapes always ripen too fast":"因為葡萄總是成熟得太快","Because all German wines are sweet":"因為所有德國酒都是甜的","In a cool climate ripeness is precious, so the categories measure sugar in the grapes at harvest.":"在涼爽氣候中成熟度很珍貴，所以這些類別衡量的是採收時葡萄的糖分。","German growers often struggle to reach their desired ripeness, so the system rewards higher sugar levels. The grape can appear on the label (e.g. Riesling Kabinett), grapes do not ripen too fast, and many German wines are dry.":"德國種植者常常難以達到想要的成熟度，所以這個體系獎勵更高的糖分。品種可以出現在酒標上（例如 Riesling Kabinett），葡萄不會成熟得太快，而且許多德國酒是不甜的。","Which style is typical of a German Landwein?":"哪一種風格是德國 Landwein 的典型特徵？","Light-bodied, dry to off-dry":"酒體輕盈，不甜至微甜","Very sweet, from botrytised grapes":"非常甜，用貴腐葡萄釀造","Full-bodied, high in alcohol and long aged in new barrels":"酒體飽滿、酒精高，在新橡木桶中長期陳年","Landwein, Germany's PGI, is usually light and dry to off-dry.":"Landwein 是德國的 PGI，通常輕盈，不甜至微甜。","Landwein requires less ripeness than Qualitätswein, so it gives lighter wines. Very sweet botrytised wines belong to the top Prädikat levels such as BA and TBA. Full body and new oak do not describe this category.":"Landwein 要求的成熟度比 Qualitätswein 低，所以釀出的酒較輕盈。非常甜的貴腐酒屬於 BA 和 TBA 等最高的 Prädikat 等級。飽滿的酒體和新橡木桶並不符合這個類別。","What does a Qualitätswein require compared with a Landwein?":"與 Landwein 相比，Qualitätswein 有什麼要求？","One of 13 winegrowing areas and riper grapes":"來自 13 個葡萄酒產區之一，且葡萄更成熟","Botrytis-affected grapes":"受貴腐菌感染的葡萄","Grapes frozen on the vine, picked at night below zero":"在樹上結冰、於零度以下夜間採收的葡萄","A single grand cru vineyard":"單一 grand cru 葡萄園","Qualitätswein comes from one of the 13 areas, such as Mosel or Rheingau, with a higher minimum ripeness than Landwein.":"Qualitätswein 來自 13 個產區之一，例如 Mosel 或 Rheingau，最低成熟度要求比 Landwein 高。","The result is usually more intense, fuller wines than Landwein. Botrytis and frozen grapes concern Prädikat levels such as BA, TBA and Eiswein; grand cru is a Burgundy and Alsace concept, not part of this German category.":"結果通常是比 Landwein 更濃郁、更飽滿的酒。貴腐和冰凍葡萄涉及的是 BA、TBA 和 Eiswein 等 Prädikat 等級；grand cru 是布根地和阿爾薩斯的概念，不屬於這個德國類別。","Two Mosel Rieslings from the same producer: a Kabinett and a Spätlese. What should you expect from the Spätlese?":"同一家生產者的兩款 Mosel 麗絲玲：一款 Kabinett 和一款 Spätlese。你應該對 Spätlese 有什麼預期？","More concentrated flavours and more body, with ripe citrus and peach":"風味更濃縮、酒體更飽滿，帶有成熟的柑橘和桃子","A lighter, more delicate wine with green apple and blossom":"更輕盈、更細緻的酒，帶有青蘋果和花香","Dried apricot, mango and honey from botrytis":"來自貴腐菌的杏桃乾、芒果和蜂蜜","Fine bubbles":"細緻的氣泡","Spätlese ('late harvest') comes from riper grapes than Kabinett: more concentration and body.":"Spätlese（「晚收」）來自比 Kabinett 更成熟的葡萄：更濃縮、酒體更飽滿。","Kabinett is the lightest Prädikat, with green apple, lime and blossom. Spätlese adds ripe citrus and a touch of peach. Botrytis, mango and dried fruit describe higher levels such as Beerenauslese; bubbles are irrelevant.":"Kabinett 是最輕盈的 Prädikat，帶有青蘋果、萊姆和花香。Spätlese 增添了成熟的柑橘和一絲桃子。貴腐菌、芒果和果乾描述的是 Beerenauslese 等更高的等級；氣泡則無關。","Which statement about Riesling Eiswein is correct?":"關於麗絲玲 Eiswein，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It cannot be made every year":"它無法每年都釀造","Botrytis is essential to make it":"釀造它必須有貴腐菌","It has high yields and low prices, because picking is quick and mechanised":"它產量高、價格低，因為採收快速且機械化","It is a dry, high-alcohol wine":"它是不甜、高酒精的酒","The weather for Eiswein, grapes frozen on the vine, does not occur every year.":"讓葡萄在樹上結冰以釀造 Eiswein 的天氣，並不是每年都會出現。","Eiswein has vibrant peach, apricot, mango and pineapple aromas, and botrytis plays no part. It is labour-intensive with tiny yields, hence expensive. It is sweet and naturally low in alcohol, because yeast cannot ferment so much sugar.":"Eiswein 帶有鮮明的桃子、杏桃、芒果和鳳梨香氣，貴腐菌不參與其中。它耗費大量人力、產量極少，因此價格昂貴。它是甜的，天然酒精低，因為酵母無法發酵這麼多的糖。","Which pair of Prädikat levels requires the same minimum sugar at harvest?":"哪一組 Prädikat 等級要求相同的採收最低糖分？","Beerenauslese and Eiswein":"Beerenauslese 和 Eiswein","Kabinett and Spätlese":"Kabinett 和 Spätlese","Auslese and Trockenbeerenauslese":"Auslese 和 Trockenbeerenauslese","Spätlese and Beerenauslese":"Spätlese 和 Beerenauslese","Beerenauslese and Eiswein are the one exception to the rising order: they share the same minimum sugar.":"Beerenauslese 和 Eiswein 是遞增順序中唯一的例外：它們的最低糖分相同。","The six Prädikat levels rise by minimum sugar: Kabinett, Spätlese, Auslese, then Beerenauslese and Eiswein at the same level, and finally Trockenbeerenauslese. The other pairs have different levels.":"六個 Prädikat 等級依最低糖分遞增：Kabinett、Spätlese、Auslese，接著是同一等級的 Beerenauslese 和 Eiswein，最後是 Trockenbeerenauslese。其他組合的等級都不同。","Which statement about Australian Riesling is correct?":"關於澳洲麗絲玲，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It has been grown since the early 19th century; the best come from Eden and Clare Valley":"從 19 世紀初就開始種植；最好的來自 Eden Valley 和 Clare Valley","It was only introduced in the 2000s":"直到 2000 年代才引進","It is made mostly in a sweet style in the warm Barossa Valley":"主要在溫暖的 Barossa Valley 釀成甜型風格","It is almost always aged in new oak":"幾乎總是在新橡木桶中陳年","Australia has grown Riesling since the early 1800s; premium Riesling centres on Eden Valley and Clare Valley.":"澳洲從 1800 年代初就種植麗絲玲；頂級麗絲玲集中在 Eden Valley 和 Clare Valley。","These two South Australian valleys are moderated by altitude and give dry Rieslings with lime and lemon. Nearby Barossa Valley is warm and not the centre of Riesling, and the typical style is dry. As almost everywhere, Riesling is made without new oak.":"這兩個南澳的山谷受海拔調節，出產帶有萊姆和檸檬的不甜麗絲玲。鄰近的 Barossa Valley 很溫暖，不是麗絲玲的中心，而典型的風格是不甜的。和幾乎所有地方一樣，麗絲玲不使用新橡木桶釀造。","In Alsace, where are the best Riesling vineyards usually located?":"在阿爾薩斯，最好的麗絲玲葡萄園通常位於哪裡？","On Vosges foothills facing east or south-east":"孚日山脈山麓朝東或東南的坡地","On the fertile, deep alluvial plain of the Rhine":"萊茵河肥沃深厚的沖積平原","On the western side of the Vosges":"孚日山脈的西側","On the banks of the Mosel":"Mosel 河畔","The best vineyards are in the Vosges foothills, facing east or south-east for morning sun.":"最好的葡萄園位於孚日山脈山麓，朝東或東南以接收早晨的陽光。","Alsace lies east of the Vosges, which shelter it from rain; east-facing slopes catch the morning sun, and dry autumns extend ripening. The western side is rainy and outside Alsace; the plain gives less rich wines; the Mosel is in Germany.":"阿爾薩斯位於孚日山脈以東，山脈為它擋住雨水；朝東的坡地接收早晨的陽光，乾燥的秋天延長了成熟期。西側多雨，而且不屬於阿爾薩斯；平原出產的酒不那麼豐富；Mosel 則在德國。","Compared with a typical Mosel Riesling, an Alsace Riesling is usually:":"與典型的 Mosel 麗絲玲相比，阿爾薩斯麗絲玲通常：","Drier and fuller-bodied":"更不甜，酒體更飽滿","Sweeter and lighter":"更甜、更輕盈","More tannic, deeper in colour and marked by new oak":"單寧更多、顏色更深，帶有明顯的新橡木桶味","Lightly sparkling":"微帶氣泡","Dry, sunny Alsace gives dry, medium-bodied Rieslings; Mosel gives light wines, often medium-sweet.":"乾燥晴朗的阿爾薩斯出產不甜、酒體中等的麗絲玲；Mosel 出產輕盈、常常半甜的酒。","Shelter from the Vosges makes Alsace one of France's driest, sunniest areas: riper grapes, dry wines with ripe citrus and stone fruit. The Mosel, further north, is cooler. Both Rieslings are usually made without new oak.":"孚日山脈的屏障讓阿爾薩斯成為法國最乾燥、陽光最充足的地區之一：葡萄更成熟，酒不甜，帶有成熟的柑橘和核果。更北的 Mosel 則較涼爽。兩地的麗絲玲通常都不使用新橡木桶。","Where do the finest Alsace Rieslings come from, in appellation terms?":"就法定產區而言，最優質的阿爾薩斯麗絲玲來自哪裡？","From individual grand cru vineyards":"來自個別的 grand cru 葡萄園","From region-wide blends sold as Alsace AOC":"來自以 Alsace AOC 出售的全區混調","From irrigated plain vineyards":"來自經灌溉的平原葡萄園","From vineyards classified as Prädikatswein, as in Germany":"來自像德國一樣分級為 Prädikatswein 的葡萄園","In Alsace, the best Rieslings come from grand cru vineyards.":"在阿爾薩斯，最好的麗絲玲來自 grand cru 葡萄園。","Alsace grands crus are specific sites on the Vosges foothills, and Riesling is among the permitted grapes. Alsace AOC is the regional appellation; Prädikatswein is a German term, not an Alsace one.":"阿爾薩斯的 grand cru 是孚日山脈山麓上的特定園地，麗絲玲是允許的品種之一。Alsace AOC 是地區級法定產區；Prädikatswein 是德國術語，不是阿爾薩斯的。","Where does Riesling find ideal conditions to reach its potential?":"麗絲玲在哪裡能找到發揮潛力的理想條件？","In cool, dry areas sunny enough for slow ripening":"在涼爽、乾燥、陽光足以讓葡萄緩慢成熟的地區","In hot, humid areas where it ripens fast":"在炎熱潮濕、讓它快速成熟的地區","In very rainy areas where grey rot strikes every year":"在每年都會發生灰黴病的非常多雨地區","Only on irrigated plains":"只在經灌溉的平原","Riesling likes cool, dry, sunny areas where sugars and flavours develop slowly.":"麗絲玲喜歡涼爽、乾燥、晴朗的地區，在那裡糖分和風味緩慢發展。","Slow ripening keeps acidity and builds intense flavours, which is why regions like the Mosel, Alsace and Clare Valley give great Rieslings. Humid heat speeds things up and encourages disease, constant rain brings unwanted rot, and irrigated plains suit volume wines.":"緩慢成熟能保留酸度並累積濃郁的風味，這就是為什麼 Mosel、阿爾薩斯和 Clare Valley 等產區能釀出偉大的麗絲玲。濕熱會加快成熟並助長病害，持續下雨帶來不受歡迎的腐爛，而經灌溉的平原適合大量生產的酒。","What drives Riesling sales around the world today?":"今天是什麼推動了麗絲玲在全球的銷售？","Premium-quality wines":"頂級品質的酒款","Cheap sweet Liebfraumilch-style wines":"便宜的 Liebfraumilch 式甜酒","New-oak Rieslings with vanilla and coconut":"帶有香草和椰子的新橡木桶麗絲玲","High-volume sparkling Rieslings":"大量生產的氣泡麗絲玲","Enthusiasts value Riesling's versatility, intensity and ageing ability: premium wines drive its sales.":"愛好者珍視麗絲玲的多才多藝、濃郁度和陳年能力：頂級酒款推動了它的銷售。","Liebfraumilch harmed Riesling's image and has gone out of fashion. Today quality is what supports the grape. New oak is not typical of Riesling, and sparkling wine is not the style named as the sales driver.":"Liebfraumilch 傷害了麗絲玲的形象，而且已經過時。今天支撐這個品種的是品質。新橡木桶不是麗絲玲的典型特徵，氣泡酒也不是被點名推動銷售的風格。","What is the relationship between Pinot Grigio and Pinot Gris?":"Pinot Grigio 和 Pinot Gris 是什麼關係？","They are the same grape with two names":"它們是同一個品種的兩個名字","They are two different related grapes":"它們是兩個不同但相關的品種","Pinot Gris is a red-skinned version":"Pinot Gris 是紅皮的版本","Pinot Grigio is a cross of Pinot Gris":"Pinot Grigio 是 Pinot Gris 的雜交種","Grigio is the Italian and Gris the French name for one white grape.":"Grigio 是義大利文名稱，Gris 是法文名稱，指的是同一個白葡萄品種。","Pinot Grigio and Pinot Gris are the same white variety: the first is the Italian name, the second the French. Any difference in the glass comes not from the name but from vineyard choices, above all yield and harvest timing. Outside Europe the two names are used to hint at style.":"Pinot Grigio 和 Pinot Gris 是同一個白葡萄品種（灰皮諾）：前者是義大利文名稱，後者是法文名稱。杯中的任何差異並非來自名稱，而是來自葡萄園的選擇，尤其是產量和採收時機。在歐洲以外，這兩個名稱被用來暗示風格。","Which vineyard choices produce the light Pinot Grigio style?":"哪些葡萄園選擇會造就輕盈的 Pinot Grigio 風格？","High yields and early harvest":"高產量和提早採收","Low yields and late harvest":"低產量和晚採","Low yields and dried grapes":"低產量和風乾葡萄","High yields and late harvest":"高產量和晚採","Large crops picked early keep acidity and make a light, simple wine.":"早採的大量收成保留酸度，釀出輕盈簡單的酒。","The most common style comes from high yields and early picking, which preserves acidity. The wine is dry and light with medium to high acidity and simple pear and lemon flavours. Controlled yields and later picking give the opposite style: full-bodied, with more sugar and complexity and medium acidity.":"最常見的風格來自高產量和提早採收，這能保留酸度。酒不甜、輕盈，酸度中等至高，帶有簡單的梨和檸檬風味。控制產量並較晚採收則帶來相反的風格：酒體飽滿，糖分和複雜度更高，酸度中等。","Which flavours characterise a light Pinot Grigio?":"哪些風味是輕盈的 Pinot Grigio 的特徵？","Simple pear and lemon":"簡單的梨和檸檬","Mango, banana and ginger":"芒果、香蕉和薑","Green pepper and asparagus":"青椒和蘆筍","The light style shows simple pear and lemon flavours.":"輕盈的風格展現簡單的梨和檸檬風味。","Light Pinot Grigio, from high yields and early picking, is dry and fresh with simple pear and lemon flavours. Mango, banana and ginger point to the rich, ripe style, as in Alsace. Green pepper and asparagus are typical of Sauvignon Blanc; rose and lychee of Gewurztraminer.":"來自高產量和提早採收的輕盈 Pinot Grigio，不甜、清爽，帶有簡單的梨和檸檬風味。芒果、香蕉和薑指向豐潤成熟的風格，例如阿爾薩斯。青椒和蘆筍是白蘇維濃的典型特徵；玫瑰和荔枝則是格烏茲塔明那的。","Why do late-picked Pinot Gris grapes give a fuller wine?":"為什麼晚採的灰皮諾葡萄能釀出更飽滿的酒？","They have more sugar and more complex flavours":"它們糖分更多、風味更複雜","They have more acid and less sugar":"它們酸更多、糖更少","They always ferment in new oak":"它們總是在新橡木桶中發酵","They come from higher yields":"它們來自更高的產量","More ripeness means more sugar (alcohol, body), less acid and richer flavours.":"成熟度越高，糖分越多（酒精、酒體）、酸越少、風味越豐富。","With controlled yields and delayed harvest the grapes ripen further: they gain sugar, lose acid and build complex flavours. The result is a powerful, full-bodied wine with medium acidity and pronounced lemon, peach, mango and banana. Pinot Gris is usually made in inert vessels, not new oak.":"控制產量並延後採收，葡萄會更成熟：糖分增加、酸度下降，並累積複雜的風味。結果是一款強勁、酒體飽滿、酸度中等的酒，帶有濃郁的檸檬、桃子、芒果和香蕉。灰皮諾通常在惰性容器而不是新橡木桶中釀造。","Why is Pinot Grigio/Gris usually fermented in inert vessels?":"為什麼灰皮諾通常在惰性容器中發酵？","To preserve its fruity flavours":"為了保留它的果味","To raise acidity":"為了提高酸度","To make a sweet wine":"為了釀造甜酒","Inert vessels add no flavour and protect the grape's fruit.":"惰性容器不會增添風味，能保護這個品種的果味。","Pinot Grigio/Gris is usually fermented in inert vessels such as stainless steel, which add no flavour and keep the fruit intact. Oak would add vanilla, which is not the aim. Any sweetness comes from stopping fermentation, not from the type of vessel.":"灰皮諾通常在不鏽鋼槽等惰性容器中發酵，這些容器不會增添風味，能完整保留果味。橡木桶會增添香草味，那不是目標。任何甜味都來自中止發酵，與容器類型無關。","How do some producers make off-dry or medium Pinot Gris?":"有些生產者如何釀造微甜或半甜的灰皮諾？","They stop fermentation by removing the yeast":"去除酵母以中止發酵","They add acid during winemaking":"在釀造過程中加酸","They use oak chips":"使用橡木片","They pick very early":"非常早就採收","Removing the yeast leaves some sugar in the wine as sweetness.":"去除酵母會在酒中留下部分糖分作為甜味。","The light Italian style is almost always fermented dry. Producers of the riper, fuller style sometimes stop fermentation by removing the yeast: sugar not yet turned into alcohol stays in the wine, making it off-dry or medium. Acidification and oak do not create sweetness.":"輕盈的義大利風格幾乎都發酵至不甜。較成熟、較飽滿風格的生產者有時會去除酵母以中止發酵：尚未轉化為酒精的糖留在酒中，讓酒成為微甜或半甜。加酸和橡木桶都不會帶來甜味。","Which notes can concentrated, full-bodied Pinot Gris develop in bottle?":"濃縮、酒體飽滿的灰皮諾在瓶中會發展出哪些氣息？","Ginger and honey":"薑和蜂蜜","Smoke and coconut":"煙燻和椰子","With age, rich Pinot Gris evolves towards ginger and honey.":"隨著陳年，豐潤的灰皮諾會朝薑和蜂蜜演變。","Light Pinot Grigio styles should be drunk young, as their simple flavours fade fast. More concentrated, full-bodied examples, such as those from Alsace, can instead evolve in bottle and develop ginger and honey. Butter and cream come from malolactic conversion; smoke and coconut from oak.":"輕盈的 Pinot Grigio 風格要趁年輕喝，因為它們簡單的風味很快就會消退。相反地，更濃縮、酒體飽滿的酒款，例如阿爾薩斯的，可以在瓶中演變，發展出薑和蜂蜜。奶油和鮮奶油來自乳酸轉化；煙燻和椰子來自橡木桶。","Under which labels is much Veneto Pinot Grigio sold?":"許多威尼托的 Pinot Grigio 以什麼標示出售？","delle Venezie DOC or Veneto IGT":"delle Venezie DOC 或 Veneto IGT","Veneto Pinot Grigio is sold as delle Venezie DOC or Veneto IGT.":"威尼托的 Pinot Grigio 以 delle Venezie DOC 或 Veneto IGT 出售。","Much Italian Pinot Grigio comes from the Veneto in the north-east and is labelled delle Venezie DOC or Veneto IGT. These are simple, light, unoaked wines, inexpensive because they are made in high volumes. Alsace Grand Cru and Pays d'Oc IGP are French; Friuli-Venezia Giulia is noted for a more complex style.":"許多義大利 Pinot Grigio 來自東北部的威尼托，標示為 delle Venezie DOC 或 Veneto IGT。這些是簡單、輕盈、未經橡木桶的酒，因為大量生產而價格平實。Alsace Grand Cru 和 Pays d'Oc IGP 是法國的；Friuli-Venezia Giulia 則以較複雜的風格著稱。","What is the typical quality of high-volume Veneto Pinot Grigio?":"大量生產的威尼托 Pinot Grigio 典型品質如何？","Acceptable to good, short finish":"可接受至良好，餘韻短","Outstanding, very long finish":"傑出，餘韻非常長","Very good, built for long ageing":"非常好，適合長期陳年","Poor, always faulty":"欠佳，總是有缺陷","High volume and low price: simple wines, short finish, acceptable or good quality.":"產量大、價格低：簡單的酒，餘韻短，品質可接受或良好。","High-volume Veneto Pinot Grigio is inexpensive, simple and light. It usually has a short finish and acceptable to good quality. It is not made for ageing, as its simple flavours fade quickly. A more complex style is found in Friuli-Venezia Giulia.":"大量生產的威尼托 Pinot Grigio 價格平實、簡單而輕盈。它通常餘韻短，品質可接受至良好。它不是為陳年而釀的，因為簡單的風味很快就會消退。較複雜的風格可以在 Friuli-Venezia Giulia 找到。","Which Italian region is known for a more complex, fuller-bodied Pinot Grigio?":"義大利哪個地區以較複雜、酒體較飽滿的 Pinot Grigio 聞名？","In Italy's north-eastern corner, Friuli gives a fuller, more complex Pinot Grigio.":"在義大利東北角，Friuli 出產更飽滿、更複雜的 Pinot Grigio。","Most Italian Pinot Grigio is simple and light, often from the Veneto. A more complex, fuller-bodied style is found in Friuli-Venezia Giulia, in northern Italy's eastern corner. It shows how the same grape can deliver more intensity through different choices.":"大多數義大利 Pinot Grigio 簡單而輕盈，常來自威尼托。較複雜、酒體較飽滿的風格則可以在北義東角的 Friuli-Venezia Giulia 找到。這顯示同一個品種如何透過不同的選擇展現更多濃郁度。","How is Pinot Gris usually harvested in Alsace?":"在阿爾薩斯，灰皮諾通常如何採收？","Late, when grapes are extra-ripe":"晚採，在葡萄過熟時","Early, to keep high acidity":"早採，以保留高酸度","With very high yields and irrigation":"以非常高的產量並灌溉","After the grapes have frozen":"在葡萄結冰之後","Alsace picks late: more sugar, medium acidity and complex flavours.":"阿爾薩斯晚採：糖分更多、酸度中等、風味複雜。","In Alsace AOC, Pinot Gris is usually picked later in the season when the grapes are extra-ripe. By then acidity is medium and the grapes have more sugar and flavour complexity. The wines, dry to medium, have medium to full body with pronounced peach and mango.":"在 Alsace AOC，灰皮諾通常在季末葡萄過熟時才採收。這時酸度中等，葡萄的糖分和風味複雜度都更高。這些酒從不甜到半甜，酒體中等至飽滿，帶有濃郁的桃子和芒果。","A full-bodied white with medium acidity, pronounced peach and mango and slight sweetness is most likely?":"一款酒體飽滿、酸度中等、帶有濃郁桃子和芒果、略帶甜味的白酒，最可能是什麼？","An Alsace Pinot Gris":"阿爾薩斯的灰皮諾","A delle Venezie Pinot Grigio":"delle Venezie 的 Pinot Grigio","A Sancerre":"Sancerre","Extra-ripe grapes and sometimes stopped fermentation: the Alsace style.":"過熟的葡萄，有時還中止發酵：這是阿爾薩斯的風格。","Alsace Pinot Gris comes from extra-ripe grapes: medium to full body, medium acidity, pronounced peach and mango and sweetness from dry to medium. Delle Venezie Pinot Grigio is light and dry with pear and lemon; Sancerre and Chablis are crisp whites with high acidity.":"阿爾薩斯的灰皮諾來自過熟的葡萄：酒體中等至飽滿、酸度中等、濃郁的桃子和芒果，甜度從不甜到半甜。delle Venezie 的 Pinot Grigio 輕盈不甜，帶有梨和檸檬；Sancerre 和 Chablis 則是高酸度的爽脆白酒。","Where are Alsace's best Pinot Gris vineyards?":"阿爾薩斯最好的灰皮諾葡萄園在哪裡？","In grand cru sites on the Vosges slopes":"在孚日山脈坡地上的 grand cru 園地","On the plains along the Rhine":"在萊茵河沿岸的平原","In cool north-facing valleys":"在涼爽、朝北的山谷","On sea-cooled coasts":"在受海洋降溫的海岸","Grand cru sites on steep east/south-east slopes get more sun.":"位於朝東／東南陡坡的 grand cru 園地能獲得更多陽光。","The best Alsace Pinot Gris comes from grand cru vineyards, mostly on the steep foothills of the Vosges facing east and south-east. These sites get more sunlight and give riper-tasting, fuller wines than vineyards on the flatter plains. These wines can also develop honey and ginger in bottle.":"最好的阿爾薩斯灰皮諾來自 grand cru 葡萄園，大多位於孚日山脈朝東和東南的陡峭山麓。這些園地接收更多日照，釀出的酒比較平坦的平原葡萄園嚐起來更成熟、更飽滿。這些酒在瓶中也能發展出蜂蜜和薑。","What does Vendanges tardives (VT) mean on an Alsace label?":"阿爾薩斯酒標上的 Vendanges tardives（VT）是什麼意思？","A medium to sweet wine from extra-ripe grapes":"用過熟葡萄釀的半甜至甜型酒","A dry wine from early-picked grapes":"用早採葡萄釀的不甜酒","A wine aged long in oak":"在橡木桶中長時間陳年的酒","A wine from a single grand cru":"來自單一 grand cru 的酒","It means late harvest: extra-ripe grapes for medium to sweet wines.":"它是晚收的意思：用過熟的葡萄釀造半甜至甜型的酒。","Vendanges tardives means late harvest. In Alsace it usually denotes a medium to sweet wine made from extra-ripe grapes. Pinot Gris, Riesling and Gewurztraminer can carry it, in both Alsace and Alsace Grand Cru. It says nothing about oak or a single vineyard.":"Vendanges tardives 是晚收的意思。在阿爾薩斯，它通常代表用過熟葡萄釀造的半甜至甜型酒。灰皮諾、麗絲玲和格烏茲塔明那都可以使用這個標示，在 Alsace 和 Alsace Grand Cru 皆然。它與橡木桶或單一葡萄園無關。","Outside Italy and France, what does the name Pinot Gris suggest compared with Pinot Grigio?":"在義大利和法國以外，與 Pinot Grigio 相比，Pinot Gris 這個名稱暗示什麼？","More body and complexity":"更多酒體和複雜度","More acidity and lightness":"更多酸度、更輕盈","An always sweet wine":"一定是甜酒","Pinot Grigio suggests light and crisp; Pinot Gris fuller and more complex.":"Pinot Grigio 暗示輕盈爽脆；Pinot Gris 則暗示更飽滿、更複雜。","In many regions outside Europe, producers use the name as a style hint. Pinot Grigio recalls the Italian style, crisper and lighter; Pinot Gris recalls Alsace, with more body and complexity. The name implies neither bubbles nor guaranteed sweetness. It is a useful clue when choosing a bottle.":"在歐洲以外的許多產區，生產者把名稱當作風格提示。Pinot Grigio 讓人想到較爽脆、較輕盈的義大利風格；Pinot Gris 讓人想到阿爾薩斯，酒體更飽滿、更複雜。名稱既不暗示氣泡，也不保證甜度。挑選酒款時，這是很有用的線索。","A wine is labelled 'Pinot Gris'. Which language does this grape name come from?":"一款酒標示為「Pinot Gris」。這個品種名稱來自哪一種語言？","Italian":"義大利文","German":"德文","Pinot Gris is the French name; Pinot Grigio is the Italian name of the same grape.":"Pinot Gris 是法文名稱；Pinot Grigio 是同一個品種的義大利文名稱。","The two names refer to a single grape. In Alsace it is Pinot Gris; in Veneto and Friuli, Pinot Grigio. Outside Europe, the chosen name often hints at the style.":"這兩個名稱指的是同一個品種。在阿爾薩斯稱為 Pinot Gris；在威尼托和 Friuli 稱為 Pinot Grigio。在歐洲以外，選用的名稱常暗示風格。","In which climates is Pinot Grigio/Pinot Gris mainly grown?":"灰皮諾主要種植在哪些氣候中？","Cool or moderate":"涼爽或溫和","Only warm":"只在溫暖氣候","Very hot and dry, with constant irrigation all season":"非常炎熱乾燥，整季持續灌溉","Tropical":"熱帶","Pinot Grigio/Gris grows mainly in cool or moderate climates.":"灰皮諾主要種植在涼爽或溫和的氣候中。","Its classic areas, north-east Italy and Alsace, are cool or moderate. There, vineyard choices (yields and picking date) decide whether the wine is light and fresh or rich and ripe. Warm or tropical climates are not its typical home.":"它的經典產區——義大利東北部和阿爾薩斯——都屬於涼爽或溫和氣候。在那裡，葡萄園的選擇（產量和採收日期）決定了酒是輕盈清爽，還是豐潤成熟。溫暖或熱帶氣候並不是它典型的家。","What mainly determines the two very different styles of Pinot Grigio/Gris?":"主要是什麼決定了灰皮諾兩種截然不同的風格？","Grape-growing and harvesting choices":"葡萄種植和採收的選擇","Whether or not new barrels are used":"是否使用新橡木桶","The length of skin maceration, which also adds colour and tannin":"浸皮時間長短，它也會增添顏色和單寧","Yields and picking date decide whether the wine will be light or rich.":"產量和採收日期決定了酒會輕盈還是豐潤。","High yields and early picking give the light style; controlled yields and delayed picking give the full style. In the winery it is usually made in inert vessels, so oak is not the key factor; maceration and Süssreserve are not the choices involved.":"高產量和提早採收帶來輕盈的風格；控制產量和延後採收帶來飽滿的風格。在酒廠中，它通常在惰性容器中釀造，所以橡木桶不是關鍵因素；浸皮和 Süssreserve 也不是相關的選擇。","What happens to acidity when Pinot Gris picking is delayed?":"灰皮諾延後採收時，酸度會怎樣？","It falls while sugar rises":"酸度下降，糖分上升","It rises along with sugar, making the wine sharper and lighter":"隨糖分一起上升，讓酒更尖酸、更輕盈","It stays the same":"保持不變","It disappears completely":"完全消失","Riper grapes have more sugar and less acidity: hence the medium acidity of the rich style.":"較成熟的葡萄糖分更多、酸度更低：所以豐潤風格的酸度是中等的。","As grapes ripen, acidity falls and sugar and flavour build. The light, early-picked style has medium to high acidity; the rich, late-picked style has medium acidity. Acidity does not vanish and does not rise with ripeness.":"隨著葡萄成熟，酸度下降，糖分和風味累積。輕盈、早採的風格酸度中等至高；豐潤、晚採的風格酸度中等。酸度不會消失，也不會隨成熟度上升。","Which of these is NOT typical of the full, ripe style of young Pinot Gris?":"下列哪一項不是年輕灰皮諾飽滿成熟風格的典型特徵？","Peach":"桃子","Mango and banana":"芒果和香蕉","Grass and green pepper belong to Sauvignon Blanc, not ripe Pinot Gris.":"青草和青椒屬於白蘇維濃，不是成熟的灰皮諾。","The full style has pronounced lemon, stone fruit (peach) and tropical fruit (mango, banana). Herbaceous notes are Sauvignon Blanc's signature. Ginger and honey only come with bottle age.":"飽滿的風格帶有濃郁的檸檬、核果（桃子）和熱帶水果（芒果、香蕉）。草本氣息是白蘇維濃的招牌特徵。薑和蜂蜜只有在瓶中陳年後才會出現。","How is light Italian Pinot Grigio usually fermented?":"輕盈的義大利 Pinot Grigio 通常如何發酵？","Almost always to dryness":"幾乎總是發酵至不甜","Stopped early to leave medium sweetness":"提早中止以保留半甜","In new barrels with long lees ageing and full malolactic":"在新橡木桶中，長時間酒渣陳年並完全乳酸轉化","With sweet juice added after fermentation":"在發酵後加入甜的葡萄汁","The light Italian style is almost always dry.":"輕盈的義大利風格幾乎總是不甜的。","Light Pinot Grigio is fermented dry in inert vessels to keep its simple pear and lemon fruit. Stopping fermentation to keep sweetness is a choice some producers of the rich style make. New oak and added juice are not part of this style.":"輕盈的 Pinot Grigio 在惰性容器中發酵至不甜，以保留簡單的梨和檸檬果味。中止發酵以保留甜味，是部分豐潤風格生產者的選擇。新橡木桶和添加葡萄汁都不屬於這種風格。","A customer wants to keep a light, inexpensive Pinot Grigio for five years. What should you advise?":"一位顧客想把一瓶輕盈、平價的 Pinot Grigio 存放五年。你應該怎麼建議？","Drink it young: its simple flavours fade quickly":"趁年輕喝：它簡單的風味很快就會消退","Wait, as it will develop ginger and honey":"等一等，它會發展出薑和蜂蜜","Store it upright near a heat source to speed up its development":"直立存放在熱源附近，以加速它的發展","Wait at least ten years":"至少等十年","Light Pinot Grigio is best drunk fresh and young.":"輕盈的 Pinot Grigio 最好趁新鮮年輕時喝。","Ginger and honey only appear in full, concentrated versions such as the best Alsace Pinot Gris. A light style quickly loses its pear and lemon flavours. Heat damages any wine.":"薑和蜂蜜只出現在飽滿濃縮的版本中，例如最好的阿爾薩斯灰皮諾。輕盈的風格很快就會失去梨和檸檬風味。高溫會損害任何葡萄酒。","Why is most Veneto Pinot Grigio inexpensive?":"為什麼大多數威尼托 Pinot Grigio 價格平實？","Because it is made in high volumes":"因為它是大量生產的","Because the grapes are picked late":"因為葡萄是晚採的","Because it is aged for a long time in used barrels from other regions":"因為它在來自其他產區的舊橡木桶中長時間陳年","Because it comes from grand cru vineyards":"因為它來自 grand cru 葡萄園","The Veneto's large volumes keep prices low.":"威尼托的大量生產讓價格保持低廉。","The Veneto, in north-east Italy, makes huge quantities of simple, unoaked, light Pinot Grigio sold as delle Venezie DOC or Veneto IGT. Late harvesting and grands crus belong to the richer Alsace style, not to these wines.":"義大利東北部的威尼托生產大量簡單、未經橡木桶、輕盈的 Pinot Grigio，以 delle Venezie DOC 或 Veneto IGT 出售。晚採和 grand cru 屬於較豐潤的阿爾薩斯風格，不屬於這些酒。","Where is Friuli-Venezia Giulia?":"Friuli-Venezia Giulia 在哪裡？","In Italy's north-eastern corner":"在義大利東北角","In southern France, along the Mediterranean coast":"在法國南部的地中海沿岸","In southern Italy":"在義大利南部","In north-west Italy":"在義大利西北部","Friuli-Venezia Giulia lies in Italy's far north-east, next to the Veneto.":"Friuli-Venezia Giulia 位於義大利的最東北部，緊鄰威尼托。","Here you find a more complex, fuller-bodied Pinot Grigio than the Italian average. Southern and north-west Italy are not the areas named for this grape, and Mediterranean France is Languedoc-Roussillon.":"在這裡可以找到比義大利平均水準更複雜、酒體更飽滿的 Pinot Grigio。義大利南部和西北部不是以這個品種著稱的地區，而地中海沿岸的法國是 Languedoc-Roussillon。","An Alsace Pinot Gris can be dry or medium-sweet. What does this depend on?":"阿爾薩斯的灰皮諾可以是不甜或半甜。這取決於什麼？","On the winemaker's preference":"取決於釀酒師的偏好","On a rule requiring sweet wines in grands crus":"取決於 grand cru 必須是甜酒的規定","On the age of the vines":"取決於葡萄樹的樹齡","On the bottle type, as the Alsace flute is legally reserved for sweet wines":"取決於酒瓶類型，因為阿爾薩斯長笛瓶依法保留給甜酒","In Alsace, Pinot Gris ranges from dry to medium depending on the winemaker's preference.":"在阿爾薩斯，灰皮諾依釀酒師的偏好，從不甜到半甜都有。","Alsace grapes are picked very ripe: the producer decides whether to ferment to dryness or keep some sugar. This is why a sweetness indication on the label is useful. No rule requires sweetness in grands crus and the bottle shape does not show it.":"阿爾薩斯的葡萄在非常成熟時採收：生產者決定要發酵至不甜還是保留一些糖分。這就是為什麼酒標上的甜度標示很有用。沒有規定要求 grand cru 必須是甜的，瓶型也不會顯示甜度。","From the 2021 vintage, what must an Alsace AOC label show?":"從 2021 年份起，Alsace AOC 的酒標必須標示什麼？","The sweetness level, on a standard scale":"依標準刻度標示的甜度","The name of the single vineyard":"單一葡萄園的名稱","The percentage of new oak used":"使用新橡木桶的比例","The Prädikat level reached by the grapes at harvest":"葡萄採收時達到的 Prädikat 等級","Since 2021, Alsace wines must show their sweetness on a standardised scale.":"從 2021 年起，阿爾薩斯葡萄酒必須以標準化刻度標示甜度。","Because the same grape can be dry or medium, the indication helps consumers. Alsace wines usually also name the grape. A vineyard name appears on grands crus but is not required for all; Prädikat is a German system.":"由於同一個品種可能是不甜或半甜，這個標示有助於消費者。阿爾薩斯葡萄酒通常也會標示品種。葡萄園名稱會出現在 grand cru 上，但並非所有酒都必須標示；Prädikat 是德國的體系。","Which of these is NOT a typical grand cru grape in Alsace?":"下列哪一個不是阿爾薩斯典型的 grand cru 品種？","Pinot Gris, Riesling and Gewurztraminer are typical Alsace grand cru grapes; Chardonnay is not.":"灰皮諾、麗絲玲和格烏茲塔明那是阿爾薩斯典型的 grand cru 品種；夏多內不是。","Alsace grands crus are on steep east/south-east-facing Vosges slopes and give riper, fuller wines. The same three grapes can also be labelled Vendanges tardives. Chardonnay is Burgundy's great white, not Alsace's.":"阿爾薩斯的 grand cru 位於孚日山脈朝東／東南的陡坡上，出產更成熟、更飽滿的酒。這三個品種也可以標示 Vendanges tardives。夏多內是布根地的偉大白葡萄，不是阿爾薩斯的。","What trend does the recent success of light Pinot Grigio show?":"輕盈的 Pinot Grigio 近年的成功顯示了什麼趨勢？","A move away from heavy, oaky whites":"遠離厚重、橡木味重的白酒","A return to sweet whites":"回歸甜白酒","Growing interest in whites for long bottle ageing":"對適合長期瓶中陳年的白酒越來越感興趣","A preference for red wines":"偏好紅酒","The boom in simple Pinot Grigio shows consumers moving away from heavy, oaky styles.":"簡單 Pinot Grigio 的熱潮顯示消費者正遠離厚重、橡木味重的風格。","Light, dry, unoaked Pinot Grigio is exported in huge quantities from the Veneto. It is neither sweet nor for long ageing, so the other trends do not explain its success.":"輕盈、不甜、未經橡木桶的 Pinot Grigio 從威尼托大量出口。它既不甜，也不適合長期陳年，所以其他趨勢都無法解釋它的成功。","What kind of food do the riper styles of Pinot Gris pair well with?":"較成熟風格的灰皮諾適合搭配什麼樣的食物？","Strongly flavoured food":"風味濃郁的食物","Only very delicate dishes":"只適合非常清淡的菜餚","Only chocolate desserts":"只適合巧克力甜點","With no food: they are sipping wines, too rich for the table":"不適合搭餐：它們是單喝的酒，太豐潤不適合上桌","Riper Pinot Gris styles have the intensity and complexity to stand up to strongly flavoured food.":"較成熟風格的灰皮諾有足夠的濃郁度和複雜度，能撐得住風味濃郁的食物。","Full body and pronounced flavours make these wines good partners for bold flavours, where a light wine would be overwhelmed. They are not limited to delicate dishes, are not aimed at chocolate, and work well at the table.":"飽滿的酒體和濃郁的風味讓這些酒成為重口味的好搭檔，而輕盈的酒會被壓過。它們不只限於清淡的菜餚，不是針對巧克力，搭餐表現也很好。","Outside Italy and France, a producer calls their wine 'Pinot Grigio'. Which style does this suggest?":"在義大利和法國以外，一位生產者把他的酒稱為「Pinot Grigio」。這暗示什麼風格？","Lighter-bodied with higher acidity":"酒體較輕盈，酸度較高","Fuller, more complex and sometimes medium-sweet, on the Alsace model":"更飽滿、更複雜，有時半甜，以阿爾薩斯為範本","Aged in new barrels":"在新橡木桶中陳年","A light red wine":"淡紅酒","The name Pinot Grigio points to the Italian style: light and fresh.":"Pinot Grigio 這個名稱指向義大利風格：輕盈清爽。","Elsewhere, the name is a signal: Pinot Grigio for a higher-acid, lighter style, Pinot Gris for a fuller, more complex wine. Neither name indicates new oak, and it is always a white wine.":"在其他地方，名稱是一種訊號：Pinot Grigio 代表酸度較高、較輕盈的風格，Pinot Gris 代表更飽滿、更複雜的酒。兩個名稱都不表示新橡木桶，而且它永遠是白酒。","What does Pinot Grigio/Gris clearly demonstrate, according to wine experts?":"根據葡萄酒專家的說法，灰皮諾清楚地展示了什麼？","How yields and ripeness shape style, quality and price":"產量和成熟度如何塑造風格、品質和價格","That new oak always improves white wines":"新橡木桶總是能提升白酒","That soil is the only factor that matters":"土壤是唯一重要的因素","That picking date has no effect at all on the final wine style":"採收日期對最終的酒款風格完全沒有影響","The same grape gives light, cheap wines or rich, complex ones depending on yields and ripeness.":"同一個品種依產量和成熟度，能釀出輕盈便宜的酒，也能釀出豐潤複雜的酒。","High yields and early picking give the Veneto's volume Pinot Grigio; controlled yields and late picking give Alsace Pinot Gris, richer and pricier. Oak is not central for this grape, and picking date is precisely the deciding factor.":"高產量和提早採收帶來威尼托大量生產的 Pinot Grigio；控制產量和晚採帶來更豐潤、價格更高的阿爾薩斯 Pinot Gris。橡木桶對這個品種並非核心，而採收日期正是決定性的因素。","What climate does Pinot Noir need to produce good-quality grapes?":"黑皮諾需要什麼氣候才能產出優質的葡萄？","Pinot Noir needs a cool to moderate climate to keep its fresh fruit.":"黑皮諾需要涼爽至溫和的氣候，才能保留新鮮的果味。","Pinot Noir is a delicate, thin-skinned grape. In a cool to moderate climate it ripens slowly and keeps fresh red fruit and high acidity. If the climate is too warm, the fruit tastes cooked and the wines can become overly alcoholic. That is why the best regions, from Burgundy to Central Otago, are cool or have influences that temper the heat.":"黑皮諾是嬌貴、果皮薄的品種。在涼爽至溫和的氣候中，它成熟緩慢，保留新鮮的紅色水果和高酸度。如果氣候太溫暖，果味會嚐起來像煮過，酒也可能酒精過高。這就是為什麼最好的產區，從布根地到 Central Otago，都很涼爽，或有緩和高溫的影響因素。","What happens to Pinot Noir grown in a climate that is too warm?":"種在過於溫暖氣候中的黑皮諾會怎樣？","It loses fresh fruit and tastes cooked":"失去新鮮果味，嚐起來像煮過","It becomes more tannic and darker":"變得更有單寧感、顏色更深","It develops grassy, green notes":"發展出青草、青澀的氣息","It gains acidity and freshness":"增加酸度和清新感","Too much heat strips Pinot Noir of its fresh aromas and gives cooked flavours.":"過多的熱量會奪走黑皮諾的新鮮香氣，帶來煮過的風味。","Pinot Noir performs best in cool or moderate climates. When it is too warm, its delicate strawberry, raspberry and cherry aromas turn cooked and unattractive. Planting in over-warm sites has also brought overly alcoholic wines to market that lack the typical fruit needed for balance. It is a clear example of why matching grape and climate matters.":"黑皮諾在涼爽或溫和氣候中表現最好。太溫暖時，它細緻的草莓、覆盆子和櫻桃香氣會變得像煮過一樣，不討喜。種在過於溫暖的園地，也讓市場上出現酒精過高、缺乏平衡所需典型果味的酒。這清楚說明了為什麼品種與氣候的搭配很重要。","Which structure is typical of Pinot Noir?":"哪一種結構是黑皮諾的典型特徵？","High acidity, low to medium tannins":"高酸度，單寧低至中等","Low acidity, high tannins":"低酸度，高單寧","Medium acidity, high tannins":"中等酸度，高單寧","Low acidity, low tannins":"低酸度，低單寧","Pinot Noir pairs high acidity with gentle, low to medium tannins.":"黑皮諾結合了高酸度和柔和、低至中等的單寧。","Pinot Noir has thin skins and gives wines that are pale to medium in colour. On the palate acidity is high while tannins stay low to medium. This combination makes it fresh and easy-drinking, enjoyable even without food. Reds with lots of tannin and little acidity have a very different profile and are not typical of this grape.":"黑皮諾果皮薄，釀出的酒顏色淺至中等。口中酸度高，而單寧保持低至中等。這樣的組合讓它清爽易飲，即使不搭餐也很好喝。單寧多而酸度少的紅酒風味特徵截然不同，不是這個品種的典型特徵。","Blackcurrant, blackberry, black plum":"黑醋栗、黑莓、黑李","Green apple, lemon, pear":"青蘋果、檸檬、梨","Prune, raisin, fig":"黑李乾、葡萄乾、無花果","Pinot Noir is a red-fruit grape: strawberry, raspberry and red cherry.":"黑皮諾是紅色水果品種：草莓、覆盆子和紅櫻桃。","Pinot Noir's main aromas are red fruits: strawberry, raspberry and red cherry. Depending on ripeness, the fruit can be crisp and fresh or riper and cooked. Black fruits such as blackcurrant and blackberry belong to other grapes, while dried fruits like prune and raisin point to over-ripe grapes, a trait linked more with Zinfandel.":"黑皮諾的主要香氣是紅色水果：草莓、覆盆子和紅櫻桃。依成熟度不同，果味可以爽脆新鮮，也可以更成熟、像煮過。黑醋栗和黑莓等黑色水果屬於其他品種，而黑李乾和葡萄乾等果乾則指向過熟的葡萄，這個特徵更常與金芬黛連結。","Why are older or larger barrels often used for Pinot Noir?":"為什麼黑皮諾常使用較舊或較大的橡木桶？","They give less flavour and do not swamp the delicate fruit":"它們給的風味較少，不會淹沒細緻的果味","They add more tannin to a wine that is too light":"它們為太輕盈的酒增添更多單寧","They make the colour darker and deeper":"它們讓顏色更深更濃","They give strong vanilla and coconut aromas":"它們帶來強烈的香草和椰子香氣","Small new oak barrels can overwhelm Pinot Noir's delicate fruit.":"小型新橡木桶可能壓過黑皮諾細緻的果味。","Pinot Noir has delicate red-fruit aromas. Small new barrels give a lot of flavour and can mask them. Older or larger barrels give less flavour, so the oak stays in the background. In the best wines you notice only subtle smoke, clove and vanilla notes sitting in balance with the fruit.":"黑皮諾有細緻的紅色水果香氣。小型新橡木桶帶來大量風味，可能掩蓋這些香氣。較舊或較大的橡木桶給的風味較少，讓橡木退居幕後。在最好的酒中，你只會察覺到與果味平衡的細微煙燻、丁香和香草氣息。","Which tertiary aromas does a fine aged Pinot Noir develop?":"優質的陳年黑皮諾會發展出哪些三級香氣？","With age, Pinot Noir develops tertiary notes of forest floor and mushroom.":"隨著陳年，黑皮諾會發展出森林地表和蘑菇的三級氣息。","Most Pinot Noir is drunk young, but very good and outstanding examples evolve in bottle. Over the years the fresh fruit gives way to tertiary aromas of forest floor and mushroom. Honey and petrol, by contrast, are typical of aged Riesling, while fresh strawberry and raspberry are primary aromas of a young wine.":"大多數黑皮諾都是趁年輕喝，但非常好和傑出的酒款會在瓶中演變。多年後，新鮮的果味讓位給森林地表和蘑菇的三級香氣。相反地，蜂蜜和汽油是陳年麗絲玲的典型特徵，而新鮮的草莓和覆盆子是年輕酒款的一級香氣。","In which type of wine is Pinot Noir most notably blended?":"黑皮諾最常在哪一種酒中被混調？","In sparkling wines such as Champagne":"在 Champagne 等氣泡酒中","In red Bourgogne AOC":"在 Bourgogne AOC 紅酒中","In Côte de Nuits Grand Cru wines":"在 Côte de Nuits Grand Cru 酒款中","In Central Otago reds":"在 Central Otago 紅酒中","Pinot Noir is usually a single-varietal wine; the main exception is sparkling wine like Champagne.":"黑皮諾通常以單一品種釀造；主要的例外是 Champagne 這樣的氣泡酒。","Most still wines made from Pinot Noir are single-varietal, in Burgundy and elsewhere. The best-known exception is sparkling wine, such as Champagne, where Pinot Noir is blended with other grapes. Bourgogne AOC, Grand Cru wines and Central Otago reds are all still Pinot Noir wines, generally made from the grape alone.":"以黑皮諾釀造的靜態酒，無論在布根地或其他地方，大多是單一品種。最知名的例外是氣泡酒，例如 Champagne，其中黑皮諾會與其他品種混調。Bourgogne AOC、Grand Cru 酒款和 Central Otago 紅酒都是黑皮諾靜態酒，一般只用這個品種釀造。","Which statement about Pinot Noir in the vineyard is correct?":"關於葡萄園中的黑皮諾，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It is prone to rot and disease":"它容易腐爛和感染病害","It has thick, tough skins":"它的果皮厚而堅韌","It performs best in hot climates":"它在炎熱氣候中表現最好","It is very easy to grow":"它非常容易種植","Pinot Noir is prone to rot and disease, so poor vintages yield little good fruit.":"黑皮諾容易腐爛和感染病害，所以在不佳的年份很少有好的果實。","Pinot Noir is seen as a difficult grape. It has thin skins, needs a cool to moderate climate and is prone to rot and disease. In poor vintages it can be hard to produce even small amounts of quality fruit. This fragility, together with strong demand, helps explain the high prices of its best wines.":"黑皮諾被視為難種的品種。它果皮薄，需要涼爽至溫和的氣候，而且容易腐爛和感染病害。在不佳的年份，連生產少量優質果實都可能很困難。這種脆弱性加上強勁的需求，有助於解釋它最好的酒款為何價格高昂。","In Burgundy, where are the best Pinot Noir vineyards usually located?":"在布根地，最好的黑皮諾葡萄園通常位於哪裡？","On south- and south-east-facing slopes":"朝南和東南的坡地","On north-facing slopes":"朝北的坡地","On flat valley floors":"平坦的谷底","On west-facing slopes":"朝西的坡地","South- and south-east-facing slopes get extra sun and give concentrated wines.":"朝南和東南的坡地獲得額外的陽光，釀出濃縮的酒。","Burgundy's climate runs from cool to moderate, so every bit of sunshine counts. Slopes facing south and south-east receive more light and warmth, helping the grapes ripen. These sites give the most concentrated, complex and age-worthy wines, including the premiers crus and grands crus. Valley floors and north-facing slopes are less favourable.":"布根地的氣候從涼爽到溫和，所以每一點陽光都很重要。朝南和東南的坡地接收更多光照和熱量，幫助葡萄成熟。這些園地出產最濃縮、最複雜、最適合陳年的酒，包括 premier cru 和 grand cru。谷底和朝北的坡地則較不理想。","What is the northern half of the Côte d'Or called?":"Côte d'Or 的北半部叫什麼？","The Côte d'Or splits into the Côte de Nuits in the north and Côte de Beaune in the south.":"Côte d'Or 分為北部的 Côte de Nuits 和南部的 Côte de Beaune。","Burgundy's most celebrated vineyards lie in the Côte d'Or, which is split into two halves. The northern half is the Côte de Nuits, home to villages such as Gevrey-Chambertin and Nuits-Saint-Georges. The southern half is the Côte de Beaune, with villages such as Beaune and Pommard. The Mâconnais and Chablis are other parts of Burgundy, outside the Côte d'Or.":"布根地最著名的葡萄園位於 Côte d'Or，它分為兩半。北半部是 Côte de Nuits，有 Gevrey-Chambertin 和 Nuits-Saint-Georges 等村莊。南半部是 Côte de Beaune，有 Beaune 和 Pommard 等村莊。Mâconnais 和 Chablis 是布根地的其他地區，位於 Côte d'Or 之外。","Which of these Pinot Noir village appellations is in the Côte de Beaune?":"下列哪一個黑皮諾村莊級法定產區位於 Côte de Beaune？","Pommard, like Beaune, is a village in the Côte de Beaune.":"Pommard 和 Beaune 一樣，是 Côte de Beaune 的村莊。","The most famous Pinot Noir villages are in the Côte d'Or. In its southern half, the Côte de Beaune, Beaune and Pommard stand out. Gevrey-Chambertin and Nuits-Saint-Georges, by contrast, are in the Côte de Nuits to the north. Pouilly-Fuissé is a Mâconnais appellation known for white wine, not Pinot Noir.":"最著名的黑皮諾村莊位於 Côte d'Or。在它的南半部 Côte de Beaune，Beaune 和 Pommard 尤為突出。相反地，Gevrey-Chambertin 和 Nuits-Saint-Georges 位於北邊的 Côte de Nuits。Pouilly-Fuissé 是以白酒而非黑皮諾著稱的 Mâconnais 法定產區。","Which of these Pinot Noir village appellations is in the Côte de Nuits?":"下列哪一個黑皮諾村莊級法定產區位於 Côte de Nuits？","Gevrey-Chambertin, like Nuits-Saint-Georges, is in the Côte de Nuits.":"Gevrey-Chambertin 和 Nuits-Saint-Georges 一樣，位於 Côte de Nuits。","The Côte de Nuits is the northern half of the Côte d'Or and is home to celebrated Pinot Noir villages such as Gevrey-Chambertin and Nuits-Saint-Georges. Beaune and Pommard belong to the Côte de Beaune further south. Meursault is also in the Côte de Beaune and is best known for Chardonnay.":"Côte de Nuits 是 Côte d'Or 的北半部，有 Gevrey-Chambertin 和 Nuits-Saint-Georges 等著名的黑皮諾村莊。Beaune 和 Pommard 屬於更南邊的 Côte de Beaune。Meursault 也位於 Côte de Beaune，最著名的是夏多內。","Which description fits a typical red Bourgogne AOC?":"哪一項描述符合典型的 Bourgogne AOC 紅酒？","Light, low tannin, fresh red fruit, for drinking young":"輕盈、低單寧、新鮮紅色水果，適合趁年輕喝","Full-bodied, very tannic, for long ageing":"酒體飽滿、單寧非常多，適合長期陳年","Sweet, low alcohol, simple red fruit":"甜、低酒精、簡單的紅色水果","Ripe black fruit, marked new oak":"成熟的黑色水果，明顯的新橡木桶味","Red Bourgogne AOC is light, fresh and fruity, made to be drunk young.":"Bourgogne AOC 紅酒輕盈、清爽、果香豐富，是要趁年輕喝的。","Bourgogne AOC is the broadest regional appellation, covering the whole of Burgundy. Its reds are light to medium-bodied, with low tannins, high acidity and fresh red fruit. They lack the intensity to age, so they are meant to be drunk young. Although it is the base of the pyramid, strong demand for red Burgundy can still make it expensive.":"Bourgogne AOC 是範圍最廣的地區級法定產區，涵蓋整個布根地。它的紅酒酒體輕盈至中等，單寧低，酸度高，帶有新鮮的紅色水果。它們缺乏陳年所需的濃郁度，所以是要趁年輕喝的。雖然它位於金字塔的底層，但由於布根地紅酒需求強勁，價格仍可能很昂貴。","What is the top level of Burgundy's appellation hierarchy?":"布根地法定產區分級的最高等級是什麼？","Village appellation":"村莊級法定產區","Grands crus are the best single vineyards and sit at the top of the pyramid.":"Grand cru 是最好的單一葡萄園，位於金字塔的頂端。","Burgundy's hierarchy climbs from Bourgogne AOC, the regional appellation, to the village appellations, then Premier Cru vineyards and finally Grand Cru. The grands crus are a handful of small, well-placed vineyards that regularly give outstanding grapes. They have their own appellations and make the most concentrated, complex and long-lived wines, at very high prices.":"布根地的分級從地區級法定產區 Bourgogne AOC 開始，往上是村莊級法定產區，接著是 Premier Cru 葡萄園，最後是 Grand Cru。Grand cru 是少數幾座位置絕佳的小型葡萄園，經常產出傑出的葡萄。它們擁有各自的法定產區，釀出最濃縮、最複雜、最長壽的酒，價格非常高昂。","How is a Burgundy Premier Cru shown on the label?":"布根地的 Premier Cru 如何在酒標上標示？","Village name with Premier Cru, sometimes the vineyard":"村莊名稱加上 Premier Cru，有時還有葡萄園名稱","Only the vineyard name with Grand Cru":"只有葡萄園名稱加上 Grand Cru","Bourgogne followed by the grape name":"Bourgogne 後面接品種名稱","Name of the Côte followed by Supérieur":"Côte 的名稱後面接 Supérieur","A Premier Cru shows the village plus Premier Cru, and may name the vineyard.":"Premier Cru 標示村莊名稱加上 Premier Cru，也可能標示葡萄園名稱。","Some high-quality vineyards within village appellations are classified as premier cru. Wines made only from these vineyards may put Premier Cru next to the village name, for example Gevrey-Chambertin Premier Cru. If the wine comes from a single premier cru vineyard, it can name that vineyard too. Grands crus, by contrast, show the vineyard name with Grand Cru.":"村莊級法定產區內有些高品質的葡萄園被列為 premier cru。只用這些葡萄園的葡萄釀造的酒，可以在村莊名稱旁加上 Premier Cru，例如 Gevrey-Chambertin Premier Cru。如果酒來自單一 premier cru 葡萄園，也可以標示該葡萄園的名稱。相反地，grand cru 則標示葡萄園名稱加上 Grand Cru。","Why do Burgundy village wines usually show more intensity than Bourgogne AOC?":"為什麼布根地村莊級酒款通常比 Bourgogne AOC 更濃郁？","Better-sited vineyards on slopes with good drainage":"位置更好、排水良好的坡地葡萄園","Higher yields and younger vines":"更高的產量和更年輕的葡萄樹","Blending with other grape varieties":"與其他品種混調","Compulsory use of new small barrels":"規定必須使用小型新橡木桶","Village vineyards are often on well-exposed, well-drained slopes that give more concentrated grapes.":"村莊級葡萄園常位於日照良好、排水良好的坡地上，能產出更濃縮的葡萄。","Village appellations are generally better situated than basic Bourgogne AOC vineyards. Many lie on slopes with favourable aspect and free-draining soils, where grapes ripen better. The result is wine with more intensity, complexity and length, and the best can age. The grape is the same; it is the place that makes the difference.":"村莊級法定產區的位置一般比基本的 Bourgogne AOC 葡萄園更好。許多位於坡向有利、土壤排水良好的坡地上，葡萄成熟得更好。結果是更濃郁、更複雜、餘韻更長的酒，最好的還能陳年。品種是一樣的；造成差異的是地方。","What cools the vineyards of Los Carneros?":"是什麼讓 Los Carneros 的葡萄園降溫？","Morning fog from San Pablo Bay":"來自 San Pablo Bay 的晨霧","Breezes from the Southern Ocean":"來自南冰洋的微風","A ring of mountains":"一圈環繞的山脈","Los Carneros is cooled by morning fog from San Pablo Bay.":"Los Carneros 受到來自 San Pablo Bay 的晨霧降溫。","Most of California is too warm for Pinot Noir, but some coastal areas are exceptions. In the north of the state, Los Carneros gets morning fog from San Pablo Bay, which lowers temperatures and preserves the fruit. Southern Ocean breezes, by contrast, cool Yarra Valley and Mornington Peninsula, while a ring of mountains protects Central Otago.":"加州大部分地方對黑皮諾來說太溫暖，但有些沿海地區是例外。在加州北部，Los Carneros 受到來自 San Pablo Bay 的晨霧影響，降低了溫度並保留了果味。相反地，南冰洋的微風讓 Yarra Valley 和 Mornington Peninsula 降溫，而一圈山脈則保護著 Central Otago。","Why is Oregon generally cooler than California?":"為什麼奧勒岡一般比加州涼爽？","More northerly latitude and Pacific exposure":"緯度更偏北，並受到太平洋的影響","Very high vineyard altitude":"葡萄園海拔非常高","Fog from San Pablo Bay":"來自 San Pablo Bay 的霧氣","Southern Ocean breezes":"南冰洋的微風","Its northerly position and Pacific influence give Oregon a mostly moderate climate.":"偏北的位置和太平洋的影響讓奧勒岡大致屬於溫和氣候。","Oregon lies further north than California and is exposed to the Pacific Ocean. Together these make it generally cooler, with a mostly moderate climate that suits Pinot Noir ideally. The best wines have complex, fresh red fruit, subtle oak and, with age, earthy and mushroom notes. San Pablo Bay fog, by contrast, cools Los Carneros.":"奧勒岡比加州更偏北，並受到太平洋的影響。兩者結合讓它一般較涼爽，大致屬於溫和氣候，非常適合黑皮諾。最好的酒帶有複雜、新鮮的紅色水果，細緻的橡木味，陳年後還有泥土和蘑菇氣息。相反地，San Pablo Bay 的霧氣讓 Los Carneros 降溫。","In which country is Casablanca Valley, known for good-value Pinot Noir?":"以物超所值的黑皮諾聞名的 Casablanca Valley 位於哪個國家？","Casablanca Valley is a coastal area of Chile, north of Santiago.":"Casablanca Valley 是智利的沿海地區，位於聖地牙哥以北。","Casablanca Valley is a coastal sub-region of Chile, north of Santiago. Sea breezes and morning fog from the Pacific keep it cool, which suits Pinot Noir. The wines show red fruit such as strawberry, sometimes with herbal notes. Pinot Noir is rarely cheap, but Chile's examples often offer excellent value for money.":"Casablanca Valley 是智利的沿海子產區，位於聖地牙哥以北。來自太平洋的海風和晨霧讓它保持涼爽，適合黑皮諾。這裡的酒展現草莓等紅色水果，有時帶有草本氣息。黑皮諾很少便宜，但智利的酒款常常非常物超所值。","Which South African region, cooled by strong southerly breezes, is known for Pinot Noir?":"南非哪個受強勁南風降溫的產區以黑皮諾聞名？","Walker Bay in South Africa is cooled by strong southerly sea breezes.":"南非的 Walker Bay 受到強勁的南方海風降溫。","In South Africa, Pinot Noir is focused on the coolest coastal regions. In Walker Bay, strong southerly sea breezes keep the grapes cool and encourage vibrant red fruit; a number of very good and outstanding wines are made here. Casablanca Valley is in Chile, Yarra Valley in Australia and Martinborough in New Zealand.":"在南非，黑皮諾集中在最涼爽的沿海產區。在 Walker Bay，強勁的南方海風讓葡萄保持涼爽，造就鮮明的紅色水果；這裡出產許多非常好和傑出的酒款。Casablanca Valley 在智利，Yarra Valley 在澳洲，Martinborough 則在紐西蘭。","What makes Yarra Valley and Mornington Peninsula cool enough for Pinot Noir?":"是什麼讓 Yarra Valley 和 Mornington Peninsula 涼爽到足以種植黑皮諾？","A protective ring of mountains":"一圈具保護作用的山脈","A latitude above 50°":"高於 50° 的緯度","Southern Ocean breezes cool these two Victorian regions.":"南冰洋的微風讓維多利亞的這兩個產區降溫。","Australia's wine regions are generally warm. In Victoria, however, Yarra Valley and Mornington Peninsula receive cool breezes from the Southern Ocean and are among the few areas suited to Pinot Noir. Styles range from light and fragrant to riper wines with cooked red fruit such as red plum and strawberry, and medium tannins.":"澳洲的葡萄酒產區一般都很溫暖。不過在維多利亞，Yarra Valley 和 Mornington Peninsula 受到來自南冰洋的涼爽微風吹拂，是少數適合黑皮諾的地區。風格從輕盈芬芳，到帶有紅李和草莓等煮過的紅色水果、單寧中等的較成熟酒款都有。","Which region makes New Zealand's ripest and most powerful Pinot Noir?":"哪個產區出產紐西蘭最成熟、最強勁的黑皮諾？","Central Otago, mountain-sheltered and very sunny, gives the country's most powerful Pinot Noir.":"受山脈屏障且陽光非常充足的 Central Otago，出產這個國家最強勁的黑皮諾。","Despite its far-southern latitude, Central Otago makes New Zealand's ripest and most powerful Pinot Noir. The wines show pronounced strawberry and red cherry, medium to full body and medium tannins, often with time in oak. Martinborough and Marlborough have cooler climates, while Mornington Peninsula is in Australia.":"儘管緯度極南，Central Otago 出產紐西蘭最成熟、最強勁的黑皮諾。這些酒展現濃郁的草莓和紅櫻桃，酒體中等至飽滿，單寧中等，常經過橡木桶。Martinborough 和 Marlborough 的氣候較涼爽，而 Mornington Peninsula 在澳洲。","Why can Central Otago ripen Pinot Noir so well despite its southerly latitude?":"儘管緯度偏南，為什麼 Central Otago 能讓黑皮諾成熟得這麼好？","Sheltering mountains and intensely sunny days":"具屏障作用的山脈和陽光強烈的白天","Morning fogs that warm the vineyards":"讓葡萄園變暖的晨霧","Strong southerly sea breezes":"強勁的南方海風","Warm nights and frequent rain":"溫暖的夜晚和頻繁的降雨","A ring of mountains blocks breezes and rain; days are sunny and nights cool.":"一圈山脈擋住了微風和雨水；白天晴朗，夜晚涼爽。","Central Otago is ringed by mountains that shield it from sea breezes and rain. The vines enjoy intensely sunny days followed by cool nights: the strong sun drives ripening, while the cool nights help preserve the fruit. The result is ripe, powerful Pinot Noir with pronounced fruit, medium to full body and medium tannins.":"Central Otago 四周群山環繞，為它擋住海風和雨水。葡萄樹享有陽光強烈的白天，接著是涼爽的夜晚：強烈的陽光推動成熟，涼爽的夜晚則幫助保留果味。結果是成熟、強勁的黑皮諾，果味濃郁，酒體中等至飽滿，單寧中等。","What problem has resulted from planting Pinot Noir in regions that are too warm?":"把黑皮諾種在太溫暖的產區造成了什麼問題？","Overly alcoholic wines lacking typical Pinot fruit":"酒精過高、缺乏黑皮諾典型果味的酒","Wines that are too acidic and thin":"太酸、太單薄的酒","Wines that are too tannic and harsh":"單寧太多、太粗糙的酒","Wines with too much fresh red fruit":"新鮮紅色水果過多的酒","In over-warm sites Pinot Noir gives alcoholic wines lacking the fruit needed for balance.":"在過於溫暖的園地，黑皮諾釀出酒精高、缺乏平衡所需果味的酒。","Pinot Noir's popularity and limited supply have led to planting in regions that are too warm. There the grapes build up lots of sugar but lose their typical fresh fruit, so the wines end up overly alcoholic and unbalanced. Comparing them with wines from cool or moderate sites shows how important it is to match the grape to the right climate.":"黑皮諾的人氣和有限的供應，導致它被種在太溫暖的產區。在那裡，葡萄累積大量糖分，卻失去了典型的新鮮果味，所以酒最後酒精過高、失去平衡。把它們與涼爽或溫和園地的酒比較，就能看出讓品種與合適氣候搭配有多重要。","Which New Zealand regions are noted for cool climates suited to Pinot Noir?":"紐西蘭哪些產區以適合黑皮諾的涼爽氣候著稱？","Martinborough and Marlborough":"Martinborough 和 Marlborough","Yarra Valley and Mornington Peninsula":"Yarra Valley 和 Mornington Peninsula","Sonoma and Los Carneros":"Sonoma 和 Los Carneros","Walker Bay and Casablanca Valley":"Walker Bay 和 Casablanca Valley","Martinborough and Marlborough have cool climates and make very good to outstanding Pinot Noir.":"Martinborough 和 Marlborough 屬於涼爽氣候，出產非常好到傑出的黑皮諾。","In New Zealand, Pinot Noir is the leading black grape. Martinborough and Marlborough, with their cool climates, both make very good and outstanding examples. Central Otago, more sheltered and sunny, gives the ripest and most powerful style instead. The other pairs of regions are in Australia, California, South Africa and Chile.":"在紐西蘭，黑皮諾是首要的黑葡萄。氣候涼爽的 Martinborough 和 Marlborough 都出產非常好和傑出的酒款。更受屏障、陽光更充足的 Central Otago 則出產最成熟、最強勁的風格。其他組合的產區分別位於澳洲、加州、南非和智利。","Pinot Noir has thin skins. What is the effect on the wine?":"黑皮諾果皮薄。這對酒有什麼影響？","A colour that is usually pale to medium":"顏色通常淺至中等","Very deep colour and very high tannins that need years to soften":"顏色非常深、單寧非常高，需要多年才能柔化","Black-fruit flavours":"黑色水果風味","Thin skins give little colour and low to medium tannin: Pinot Noir is usually pale.":"薄果皮帶來的顏色很少，單寧低至中等：黑皮諾通常顏色淺。","Colour and tannin are extracted from the skins; thin skins mean a pale, soft wine. Pinot Noir's acidity is high, not low, and its fruit is red (strawberry, raspberry, cherry), not black. Thin skins also make it prone to rot.":"顏色和單寧是從果皮萃取的；果皮薄就代表酒顏色淺、口感柔和。黑皮諾的酸度高而不是低，它的果味是紅色水果（草莓、覆盆子、櫻桃），而不是黑色水果。薄果皮也讓它容易腐爛。","What often happens to Pinot Noir in poor vintages?":"在不佳的年份，黑皮諾常會怎樣？","It can be a struggle to make even small amounts of good wine":"連釀出少量好酒都可能很困難","Yields rise sharply":"產量大幅上升","It turns darker and more tannic, with intense black-fruit flavours":"顏色變深、單寧變多，帶有濃郁的黑色水果風味","Pinot Noir is prone to rot and disease: in poor years, good quality is scarce.":"黑皮諾容易腐爛和感染病害：在不佳的年份，好品質很稀少。","Thin skins and susceptibility to disease make Pinot Noir a difficult grape for growers. A cold, wet year does not raise yields of good fruit or make the wine darker or more tannic.":"薄果皮和易感病害讓黑皮諾成為種植者眼中難種的品種。寒冷多雨的年份不會提高好果實的產量，也不會讓酒顏色更深或單寧更多。","Which statement about ageing Pinot Noir is correct?":"關於黑皮諾的陳年，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","Most are for drinking young; the finest improve for years":"大多數要趁年輕喝；最優質的能逐年變好","All Pinot Noirs need at least ten years in bottle to be enjoyable":"所有黑皮諾都需要在瓶中至少十年才好喝","No Pinot Noir can age":"沒有任何黑皮諾能陳年","It ages only when blended":"它只有在混調時才能陳年","Many Pinot Noirs are fruity and ready young; only the finest gain complexity over years.":"許多黑皮諾果香豐富、年輕時就適飲；只有最優質的會隨著歲月增添複雜度。","Pinot Noir is refreshing and rarely needs a long wait; the best examples, however, develop forest floor and mushroom and may take years to show their best. It is usually single-varietal, so blending is not needed for ageing.":"黑皮諾令人清爽，很少需要久等；不過最好的酒款會發展出森林地表和蘑菇，可能需要多年才能展現最佳狀態。它通常是單一品種，所以陳年不需要混調。","What decides whether Pinot Noir's red fruit tastes fresh or cooked?":"是什麼決定了黑皮諾的紅色水果嚐起來是新鮮還是像煮過？","The ripeness of the grapes":"葡萄的成熟度","The serving temperature":"侍酒溫度","The amount of yeast added to the juice during fermentation":"發酵期間加入果汁的酵母量","Just-ripe grapes give fresh fruit; overripe grapes from warm areas give cooked fruit.":"剛成熟的葡萄帶來新鮮果味；溫暖地區的過熟葡萄帶來煮過的果味。","This is why climate matters so much: in climates that are too warm, Pinot Noir loses its fresh fruit. In Yarra Valley and Mornington Peninsula, for example, styles range from light and fragrant to riper with cooked red fruit. Bottle, temperature and yeast do not change the fruit's character.":"這就是為什麼氣候如此重要：在太溫暖的氣候中，黑皮諾會失去新鮮果味。例如在 Yarra Valley 和 Mornington Peninsula，風格從輕盈芬芳到帶有煮過紅色水果的較成熟酒款都有。酒瓶、溫度和酵母都不會改變果味的特徵。","Which oak aromas are found, well balanced, in the best Pinot Noirs?":"在最好的黑皮諾中，可以找到哪些平衡良好的橡木香氣？","Smoke, cloves, vanilla":"煙燻、丁香、香草","Honey, petrol and dried apricot":"蜂蜜、汽油和杏桃乾","Oak gives Pinot Noir subtle notes of smoke, cloves and vanilla, balanced by the fruit.":"橡木為黑皮諾帶來細微的煙燻、丁香和香草氣息，與果味平衡。","In great Pinot Noirs the wood stays discreet so as not to hide the delicate fruit. Butter and cream come from malolactic in whites such as Chardonnay; grass and asparagus belong to Sauvignon Blanc; honey and petrol to aged Riesling.":"在偉大的黑皮諾中，木頭保持低調，以免掩蓋細緻的果味。奶油和鮮奶油來自夏多內等白酒的乳酸轉化；青草和蘆筍屬於白蘇維濃；蜂蜜和汽油屬於陳年麗絲玲。","A producer matures a delicate Pinot Noir in small new barrels. What is the risk?":"一位生產者把細緻的黑皮諾放在小型新橡木桶中熟成。有什麼風險？","The oak may overwhelm the delicate fruit":"橡木可能壓過細緻的果味","The wine may turn paler and more acidic":"酒可能變得更淡、更酸","The wine may referment and turn fizzy":"酒可能再次發酵而產生氣泡","It may lose all its tannin and turn white within months":"它可能在幾個月內失去所有單寧而變成白色","Small new barrels give a lot of flavour and can overwhelm a delicate Pinot Noir.":"小型新橡木桶帶來大量風味，可能壓過細緻的黑皮諾。","This is why many producers prefer older or larger barrels, which give less flavour. Oak does not make the wine paler or more acidic, does not cause refermentation and does not remove tannin.":"這就是為什麼許多生產者偏好給風味較少的較舊或較大的橡木桶。橡木不會讓酒更淡或更酸，不會導致再次發酵，也不會去除單寧。","In Burgundy, where does Pinot Noir perform best?":"在布根地，黑皮諾在哪裡表現最好？","In the moderate areas, where it fully ripens":"在溫和的地區，那裡它能完全成熟","In the coldest northern areas, where grapes keep more acidity":"在最冷的北部地區，那裡葡萄保留更多酸度","On the most fertile plains":"在最肥沃的平原","Burgundy ranges from cool in the north to moderate further south; Pinot Noir prefers the moderate parts.":"布根地從北部的涼爽到更南的溫和；黑皮諾偏好溫和的地方。","In moderate areas such as the Côte d'Or, Pinot Noir ripens fully. In the north it is too cool to guarantee this. In Burgundy small site differences matter a lot, so it is not 'the same everywhere', and the best vineyards are on slopes, not fertile plains.":"在 Côte d'Or 等溫和地區，黑皮諾能完全成熟。在北部，天氣太涼爽，無法保證這一點。在布根地，園地之間的細微差異非常重要，所以並非「到處都一樣」，而最好的葡萄園位於坡地，不是肥沃的平原。","Why can even a basic red Bourgogne AOC be expensive?":"為什麼即使是基本的 Bourgogne AOC 紅酒也可能很昂貴？","Because of strong demand for red Burgundy":"因為布根地紅酒的需求強勁","Because it always comes from grand cru vineyards":"因為它總是來自 grand cru 葡萄園","Because it must age at least ten years before release":"因為它上市前必須陳年至少十年","Because it is a sweet wine":"因為它是甜酒","Demand for red Burgundy is so high that even the entry level is costly.":"布根地紅酒的需求如此之高，連入門等級都很昂貴。","Bourgogne AOC is the bottom step of the hierarchy: light, fresh, for drinking young. Its price reflects supply and demand, not site quality. It does not come from grands crus, has no long-ageing rule and is not sweet.":"Bourgogne AOC 是分級的最底層：輕盈、清爽、要趁年輕喝。它的價格反映的是供需，而不是園地品質。它不是來自 grand cru，沒有長期陳年的規定，也不是甜酒。","A label says only 'Gevrey-Chambertin – Appellation Gevrey-Chambertin Contrôlée'. What type of wine is it?":"一張酒標上只寫著「Gevrey-Chambertin – Appellation Gevrey-Chambertin Contrôlée」。這是什麼類型的酒？","A village appellation wine":"村莊級法定產區酒款","A grand cru":"Grand cru","A regional Bourgogne AOC":"地區級的 Bourgogne AOC","A single-vineyard premier cru whose name is not shown":"未標示名稱的單一葡萄園 premier cru","The village name alone indicates a village appellation.":"只有村莊名稱表示是村莊級法定產區。","A premier cru adds 'Premier Cru' to the village name, sometimes with the vineyard. A grand cru carries the vineyard name with 'Grand Cru'. Bourgogne AOC uses the region's name. Village wines offer more intensity and complexity than Bourgogne AOC.":"Premier cru 會在村莊名稱後加上「Premier Cru」，有時還有葡萄園名稱。Grand cru 標示葡萄園名稱加上「Grand Cru」。Bourgogne AOC 使用地區的名稱。村莊級酒款比 Bourgogne AOC 更濃郁、更複雜。","A label reads 'Gevrey-Chambertin – Clos Saint-Jacques – Premier Cru'. What does 'Clos Saint-Jacques' indicate?":"一張酒標上寫著「Gevrey-Chambertin – Clos Saint-Jacques – Premier Cru」。「Clos Saint-Jacques」代表什麼？","The single premier cru vineyard the wine comes from":"這款酒來自的單一 premier cru 葡萄園","The producer's name":"生產者的名稱","A grand cru vineyard with its own appellation, separate from the village":"擁有獨立法定產區、與村莊分開的 grand cru 葡萄園","A neighbouring village":"鄰近的村莊","A wine from one premier cru vineyard may show its name next to the village and the words Premier Cru.":"來自單一 premier cru 葡萄園的酒，可以在村莊名稱和 Premier Cru 字樣旁標示該葡萄園的名稱。","Premier crus are high-quality vineyards within a village appellation: the label gives the village plus 'Premier Cru' and, if the wine comes from one vineyard, its name. Grands crus have their own appellations and need no village name.":"Premier cru 是村莊級法定產區內的高品質葡萄園：酒標標示村莊名稱加上「Premier Cru」，如果酒來自單一葡萄園，還會標示它的名稱。Grand cru 擁有各自的法定產區，不需要村莊名稱。","A label reads 'Le Chambertin – Grand Cru'. Why is no village name used as the appellation?":"一張酒標上寫著「Le Chambertin – Grand Cru」。為什麼沒有使用村莊名稱作為法定產區？","Each grand cru has its own appellation":"每個 grand cru 都有自己的法定產區","Because it is a basic regional wine":"因為它是基本的地區級酒款","Because the producer forgot it":"因為生產者忘了標示","Because the wine blends grapes from several Côte de Nuits villages":"因為這款酒混調了 Côte de Nuits 數個村莊的葡萄","Grands crus have their own appellations: the label shows the vineyard name and 'Grand Cru'.":"Grand cru 擁有各自的法定產區：酒標標示葡萄園名稱和「Grand Cru」。","Grands crus are a handful of small, well-sited vineyards, Burgundy's best, giving the rarest and most age-worthy wines. That is the opposite of a basic regional wine or a multi-village blend.":"Grand cru 是少數幾座位置絕佳的小型葡萄園，是布根地最好的，出產最稀有、最適合陳年的酒。這與基本的地區級酒款或多村莊混調正好相反。","What is the correct order of Burgundy's hierarchy, from bottom to top?":"布根地分級由下而上的正確順序是什麼？","Village, regional, grand cru, premier cru":"村莊級、地區級、grand cru、premier cru","Regional, premier cru, village, grand cru":"地區級、premier cru、村莊級、grand cru","Grand cru, premier cru, village, regional":"Grand cru、premier cru、村莊級、地區級","It starts with regional Bourgogne AOC, then village, premier cru and, at the top, grand cru.":"從地區級的 Bourgogne AOC 開始，接著是村莊級、premier cru，最頂端是 grand cru。","Each step means a smaller area and generally more concentrated wines. Premier crus sit within villages and below grands crus. The last option lists the same hierarchy, but from top to bottom.":"每往上一級，代表區域越小，酒一般也越濃縮。Premier cru 位於村莊之內，低於 grand cru。最後一個選項列出的是同樣的分級，但是由上而下。","Which profile best describes a mature Burgundy premier or grand cru Pinot Noir?":"哪一種風味特徵最能描述成熟的布根地 premier cru 或 grand cru 黑皮諾？","Concentrated fruit, subtle oak, pronounced forest floor and mushroom":"濃縮的果味、細緻的橡木味、濃郁的森林地表和蘑菇","Light, fresh fruit with no tertiary notes":"輕盈、新鮮的果味，沒有三級氣息","Very ripe black fruit, very high tannin and dominant new-oak vanilla":"非常成熟的黑色水果、非常高的單寧和主導的新橡木桶香草味","Sweet, with honey":"甜，帶有蜂蜜","The best vineyards give concentrated strawberry and cherry, subtle oak and pronounced tertiary notes.":"最好的葡萄園帶來濃縮的草莓和櫻桃、細緻的橡木味和濃郁的三級氣息。","Facing south or south-east, premier and grand crus get more sun and warmth and make the most complex wines, which evolve for a long time in bottle. Light fruit with no tertiary notes describes Bourgogne AOC; black fruit and very high tannin are not typical of Pinot Noir; it is not a sweet wine.":"朝南或東南的 premier cru 和 grand cru 獲得更多陽光和熱量，釀出最複雜的酒，能在瓶中長時間演變。輕盈、沒有三級氣息的果味描述的是 Bourgogne AOC；黑色水果和非常高的單寧不是黑皮諾的典型特徵；它也不是甜酒。","Why is most of California unsuited to Pinot Noir?":"為什麼加州大部分地方不適合黑皮諾？","It is too warm":"太溫暖了","It is too cold and wet":"太冷太濕了","The law bans French grapes outside designated coastal zones":"法律禁止在指定沿海區域以外種植法國品種","The soils are too poor":"土壤太貧瘠","Most of California is too warm: quality Pinot Noir comes from a few areas near the coast.":"加州大部分地方太溫暖：優質黑皮諾來自少數靠近海岸的地區。","Coastal fog and breezes cool areas such as Los Carneros, western Sonoma and Santa Barbara County, avoiding over-cooked flavours. The problem is heat, not cold; there is no legal ban of this kind and soils are not the factor.":"沿海的霧氣和微風讓 Los Carneros、Sonoma 西部和 Santa Barbara County 等地區降溫，避免風味過熟。問題是高溫，不是寒冷；沒有這類法律禁令，土壤也不是相關因素。","What cools the western parts of Sonoma, suited to Pinot Noir?":"是什麼讓適合黑皮諾的 Sonoma 西部降溫？","Pacific Ocean breezes":"太平洋的微風","The altitude of nearby mountains":"鄰近山脈的海拔","Cold Southern Ocean currents":"寒冷的南冰洋洋流","A ring of mountains that blocks afternoon sun and keeps out rain":"一圈擋住午後陽光、阻隔雨水的山脈","Western Sonoma is cooled by Pacific breezes.":"Sonoma 西部受到太平洋微風的降溫。","In California much depends on closeness to the coast: Los Carneros has San Pablo Bay fogs, western Sonoma ocean breezes. The Southern Ocean concerns Australia and South Africa; the ring of mountains describes Central Otago, which actually has very sunny days.":"在加州，很多事取決於與海岸的距離：Los Carneros 有 San Pablo Bay 的霧氣，Sonoma 西部有海風。南冰洋與澳洲和南非有關；一圈山脈描述的是 Central Otago，那裡其實白天陽光非常充足。","Where is Santa Barbara County and what cools it?":"Santa Barbara County 在哪裡？是什麼讓它降溫？","On the Central Coast; sea breezes from the west and south":"在中部海岸；來自西方和南方的海風","In Northern California; San Pablo Bay fogs":"在北加州；San Pablo Bay 的霧氣","Inland in the Central Valley; the altitude of surrounding hills":"在內陸的 Central Valley；周圍丘陵的海拔","In Oregon; latitude":"在奧勒岡；緯度","Santa Barbara County, on the Central Coast, is cooled by sea breezes from the west and south.":"位於中部海岸的 Santa Barbara County，受到來自西方和南方的海風降溫。","These influences stop Pinot Noir from developing over-cooked flavours. San Pablo fogs concern Los Carneros, in the north; the Central Valley is hot and far from the sea; Oregon is a different state further north.":"這些影響讓黑皮諾不會發展出過熟的風味。San Pablo 的霧氣與北部的 Los Carneros 有關；Central Valley 炎熱且遠離海洋；奧勒岡則是更北邊的另一個州。","A Pinot Noir with ripe strawberry and red cherry and noticeable smoke, cloves and vanilla is most likely:":"一款帶有成熟草莓和紅櫻桃、以及明顯煙燻、丁香和香草的黑皮諾，最可能是：","Californian":"加州的","A basic Bourgogne AOC":"基本的 Bourgogne AOC","A light, fragrant very-cool-climate Pinot Noir made in steel":"在不鏽鋼槽中釀造、輕盈芬芳的極涼爽氣候黑皮諾","A herbal Casablanca Valley wine":"帶有草本氣息的 Casablanca Valley 酒款","Californian Pinot Noirs usually show ripe red fruit and noticeable oak.":"加州黑皮諾通常展現成熟的紅色水果和明顯的橡木味。","The Californian style combines ripe fruit and noticeable oak; the best develop forest floor and mushroom. Bourgogne AOC is light and fresh, without obvious oak; a steel-made wine would show no oak; Casablanca is known for strawberry and herbal notes.":"加州風格結合了成熟的果味和明顯的橡木味；最好的酒款會發展出森林地表和蘑菇。Bourgogne AOC 輕盈清爽，沒有明顯的橡木味；在不鏽鋼槽中釀造的酒不會有橡木味；Casablanca 則以草莓和草本氣息著稱。","Which tertiary notes can a good Oregon Pinot Noir develop?":"優質的奧勒岡黑皮諾可以發展出哪些三級氣息？","Earth and mushroom":"泥土和蘑菇","Cut grass, green pepper and asparagus":"青草、青椒和蘆筍","With age the best Oregon Pinot Noirs develop earthy and mushroom notes.":"隨著陳年，最好的奧勒岡黑皮諾會發展出泥土和蘑菇氣息。","Oregon's mostly moderate climate gives fresh, complex red fruit, subtle oak and, in bottle, earth and mushroom. Petrol and honey belong to Riesling, butter and cream to malolactic in whites, grass and asparagus to Sauvignon Blanc.":"奧勒岡大致溫和的氣候帶來新鮮、複雜的紅色水果、細緻的橡木味，在瓶中則有泥土和蘑菇。汽油和蜂蜜屬於麗絲玲，奶油和鮮奶油屬於白酒的乳酸轉化，青草和蘆筍屬於白蘇維濃。","Which description fits Casablanca Valley Pinot Noir?":"哪一項描述符合 Casablanca Valley 的黑皮諾？","Strawberry, sometimes herbal notes; often excellent value":"草莓，有時帶草本氣息；常常非常物超所值","Black fruit, high tannin and a big body":"黑色水果、高單寧和厚實的酒體","South America's most powerful, expensive Pinot Noir, made in tiny amounts":"南美洲最強勁、最昂貴、產量極少的黑皮諾","A sweet wine":"甜酒","Cooled by Pacific breezes and fog, Casablanca gives strawberry-fruited, sometimes herbal Pinot Noir at good value.":"受到太平洋微風和霧氣降溫的 Casablanca，以實惠的價格出產帶草莓果味、有時帶草本氣息的黑皮諾。","Casablanca Valley, north of Santiago, makes very good Pinot Noir. Although Pinot Noir is rarely cheap, Chile's can offer excellent value. Black fruit and high tannin are not typical of the grape, and the wine is not sweet.":"聖地牙哥以北的 Casablanca Valley 出產非常好的黑皮諾。雖然黑皮諾很少便宜，智利的酒款卻可能非常物超所值。黑色水果和高單寧不是這個品種的典型特徵，這款酒也不是甜的。","Where is Casablanca Valley in relation to Santiago, Chile?":"Casablanca Valley 相對於智利聖地牙哥的位置在哪裡？","North of Santiago, near the coast":"聖地牙哥以北，靠近海岸","South of Santiago, in the hot interior":"聖地牙哥以南，在炎熱的內陸","In the Andes above 2,000 metres, near the Argentine border":"在安地斯山脈海拔 2,000 公尺以上，靠近阿根廷邊境","In the Atacama Desert":"在阿他加馬沙漠","Casablanca Valley is a coastal sub-region north of Santiago.":"Casablanca Valley 是聖地牙哥以北的沿海子產區。","Closeness to the ocean is the key: Pacific sea breezes and morning fog cool the vineyards and allow fresh Pinot Noir, Chardonnay and Sauvignon Blanc. The hot interior is the Central Valley; the Andes and the desert are not where it lies.":"靠近海洋是關鍵：太平洋的海風和晨霧讓葡萄園降溫，造就清新的黑皮諾、夏多內和白蘇維濃。炎熱的內陸是 Central Valley；安地斯山脈和沙漠都不是它所在的位置。","Which Pinot Noir style is found in Yarra Valley and Mornington Peninsula?":"Yarra Valley 和 Mornington Peninsula 出產哪一種黑皮諾風格？","From light and fragrant to riper, with red plum and medium tannin":"從輕盈芬芳到較成熟、帶紅李和中等單寧","Only very tannic, dark wines":"只有單寧非常多、顏色很深的酒","Only sparkling wines":"只有氣泡酒","Sweet wines made from grapes left to freeze on the vine":"用在樹上結冰的葡萄釀的甜酒","In these Victorian areas, the style runs from light and fragrant to riper, with cooked red fruit.":"在維多利亞的這些地區，風格從輕盈芬芳到較成熟、帶煮過的紅色水果都有。","Australia is warm overall, but Southern Ocean breezes make these two regions cool enough for Pinot Noir. The riper style shows red plum and strawberry with medium tannin. They are not known for dark, tannic wines or for sweet wines.":"澳洲整體很溫暖，但南冰洋的微風讓這兩個產區涼爽到足以種植黑皮諾。較成熟的風格帶有紅李和草莓，單寧中等。它們不以深色、單寧多的酒或甜酒著稱。","What role does Pinot Noir play in New Zealand?":"黑皮諾在紐西蘭扮演什麼角色？","It is the country's premier black grape":"它是這個國家首要的黑葡萄","It is used only for rosé":"它只用來釀粉紅酒","It is almost absent":"它幾乎不存在","It is grown only on the North Island, as the South Island is too cold":"它只種在北島，因為南島太冷","Pinot Noir is New Zealand's most important black grape.":"黑皮諾是紐西蘭最重要的黑葡萄。","The country makes very good and outstanding Pinot Noir in Martinborough, Marlborough and Central Otago. Marlborough and Central Otago are on the South Island, so the last option is wrong.":"這個國家在 Martinborough、Marlborough 和 Central Otago 出產非常好和傑出的黑皮諾。Marlborough 和 Central Otago 位於南島，所以最後一個選項是錯的。","Which profile is typical of a Central Otago Pinot Noir?":"哪一種風味特徵是 Central Otago 黑皮諾的典型特徵？","Pronounced fruit, medium to full body, medium tannin, often oak":"濃郁的果味、酒體中等至飽滿、單寧中等、常經橡木桶","Very pale, very light-bodied and delicate, for drinking within months":"顏色非常淺、酒體非常輕盈細緻，要在幾個月內喝掉","Very high tannin and black fruit":"非常高的單寧和黑色水果","Sweet and lightly sparkling":"甜而微帶氣泡","Central Otago gives ripe, powerful Pinot Noir with strawberry and cherry and medium tannin.":"Central Otago 出產成熟、強勁的黑皮諾，帶有草莓和櫻桃，單寧中等。","Very sunny days and cool nights give intense wines, often oak-matured, that may need a few years in bottle. The very light style does not match the country's ripest region; black fruit and very high tannin are not typical of Pinot Noir.":"陽光非常充足的白天和涼爽的夜晚帶來濃郁的酒，常經橡木桶熟成，可能需要在瓶中放幾年。非常輕盈的風格不符合這個國家最成熟的產區；黑色水果和非常高的單寧不是黑皮諾的典型特徵。","What is Pinot Noir famous for among Burgundy enthusiasts?":"黑皮諾在布根地愛好者之間以什麼著稱？","Expressing small differences between nearby vineyards":"能表現相鄰葡萄園之間的細微差異","Tasting the same wherever it is grown":"無論種在哪裡嚐起來都一樣","Its very high tannins":"它非常高的單寧","Always being a cheap wine, easy to find in any supermarket":"總是便宜的酒，任何超市都買得到","Pinot Noir reflects the vineyard it comes from with great precision.":"黑皮諾非常精準地反映它所來自的葡萄園。","The most experienced enthusiasts claim to detect differences between plots just metres apart. This is why the Burgundy system gives so much weight to individual vineyards. Pinot Noir has low to medium tannin and is rarely cheap.":"最資深的愛好者宣稱能察覺相距僅數公尺的地塊之間的差異。這就是為什麼布根地的體系如此重視個別葡萄園。黑皮諾的單寧低至中等，而且很少便宜。","A customer wants a refreshing red, enjoyable with or without food and ready to drink. Which grape suits well?":"一位顧客想要一款令人清爽、搭不搭餐都好喝、已經適飲的紅酒。哪個品種很適合？","Young, very tannic Cabernet Sauvignon that needs years in bottle":"年輕、單寧非常多、需要在瓶中多年的卡本內蘇維濃","A Riesling Trockenbeerenauslese":"麗絲玲 Trockenbeerenauslese","Pinot Noir is a fresh red, good with or without food, and rarely needs long ageing.":"黑皮諾是清爽的紅酒，搭不搭餐都好，很少需要長期陳年。","High acidity, low to medium tannin and red fruit make Pinot Noir enjoyable young. A young Cabernet can be too tannic; Sauternes and TBA are sweet whites, not reds.":"高酸度、低至中等的單寧和紅色水果，讓黑皮諾年輕時就好喝。年輕的卡本內可能單寧太多；Sauternes 和 TBA 是甜白酒，不是紅酒。","How can regions closer to the equator than Burgundy make excellent Pinot Noir?":"比布根地更接近赤道的產區，如何能釀出優秀的黑皮諾？","Thanks to moderating influences such as sea, fog or altitude":"靠著海洋、霧氣或海拔等調節因素","By always picking very late":"總是非常晚才採收","By adding deeper-coloured black grapes":"加入顏色更深的黑葡萄","By heavy irrigation to cool the vines and lengthen the season":"大量灌溉以讓葡萄樹降溫並延長生長季","Ocean, fog and altitude create cool enough climates even at warmer latitudes.":"即使在較溫暖的緯度，海洋、霧氣和海拔也能創造夠涼爽的氣候。","Los Carneros (fog), Casablanca (breezes and fog), Walker Bay (southerly winds) and Yarra Valley (Southern Ocean) are examples. Picking late in warm areas would give cooked fruit; blending or irrigating does not create a cool climate.":"Los Carneros（霧氣）、Casablanca（微風和霧氣）、Walker Bay（南風）和 Yarra Valley（南冰洋）都是例子。在溫暖地區晚採會帶來煮過的果味；混調或灌溉都無法創造涼爽的氣候。","Which description fits a typical single-varietal Cabernet Sauvignon?":"哪一項描述符合典型的單一品種卡本內蘇維濃？","Deep colour, high acidity, high tannins":"顏色深、高酸度、高單寧","Pale colour, high acidity, low tannins":"顏色淺、高酸度、低單寧","Medium colour, medium acidity, medium tannins":"顏色中等、酸度中等、單寧中等","Deep colour, low acidity, low tannins":"顏色深、低酸度、低單寧","Thick skins give lots of colour and tannin, and the grape keeps high acidity.":"厚果皮帶來大量顏色和單寧，而這個品種保有高酸度。","Cabernet's grapes have thick skins rich in colour, flavour and tannin. The wine is therefore deeply coloured, dry, with high acidity, high tannins and a medium to full body. Medium acidity and tannins describe Merlot instead, while a pale colour and low tannin do not fit a grape with such thick skins.":"卡本內的葡萄果皮厚，富含顏色、風味和單寧。因此酒的顏色深、不甜，酸度高、單寧高，酒體中等至飽滿。中等的酸度和單寧描述的則是梅洛，而顏色淺、單寧低不符合果皮這麼厚的品種。","Which group of flavours is typical of young Cabernet Sauvignon?":"哪一組風味是年輕卡本內蘇維濃的典型特徵？","Blackcurrant, black cherry, mint, green bell pepper":"黑醋栗、黑櫻桃、薄荷、青椒","Strawberry, raspberry, violet, white pepper":"草莓、覆盆子、紫羅蘭、白胡椒","Cooked blackberry, liquorice, leather, meat":"煮過的黑莓、甘草、皮革、肉","Red plum, dried fruit, tobacco, earth":"紅李、果乾、菸草、泥土","Cabernet combines intense black fruit with herbal or herbaceous notes.":"卡本內結合了濃郁的黑色水果和草本或植物性氣息。","Cabernet's primary flavours are black fruits such as blackcurrant and black cherry, usually with mint or green bell pepper. Leather, meat, tobacco, earth and dried fruit come with age or belong to other grapes, while liquorice and cooked fruit are typical of warm-climate Shiraz.":"卡本內的一級風味是黑醋栗和黑櫻桃等黑色水果，通常帶有薄荷或青椒。皮革、肉、菸草、泥土和果乾隨陳年出現，或屬於其他品種，而甘草和煮過的果味是溫暖氣候希拉茲的典型特徵。","What does Cabernet Sauvignon need to ripen fully?":"卡本內蘇維濃需要什麼才能完全成熟？","A long, warm growing season":"漫長而溫暖的生長季","A short, cool growing season":"短而涼爽的生長季","Very high yields and irrigation":"非常高的產量和灌溉","Its thick-skinned grapes need plenty of time and warmth to ripen.":"它果皮厚的葡萄需要充足的時間和熱量才能成熟。","Cabernet grows in moderate and warm climates, but in a moderate climate it ripens with difficulty except on the warmest sites. That is why heat-holding gravel matters so much in Bordeaux, and why New Zealand needs its warmest sites. In Napa Valley, by contrast, the warmth and long season are ideal.":"卡本內生長在溫和和溫暖的氣候中，但在溫和氣候中，除了最溫暖的園地外，它很難成熟。這就是為什麼能保溫的礫石在波爾多如此重要，也是紐西蘭需要最溫暖園地的原因。相反地，在 Napa Valley，溫暖和漫長的生長季非常理想。","Why can the best Cabernet Sauvignons age for many years?":"為什麼最好的卡本內蘇維濃能陳年多年？","High tannin and acidity act as preservatives":"高單寧和高酸度起到防腐作用","High residual sugar protects the wine":"高殘糖保護了酒","Low alcohol slows oxidation":"低酒精減緩氧化","Thin skins release few unstable compounds":"薄果皮釋放的不穩定化合物很少","High tannin and acidity are natural preservatives that support long ageing.":"高單寧和高酸度是支撐長期陳年的天然防腐劑。","Cabernet has thick skins and high acidity, so its wine is rich in tannin and freshness. These two elements protect the wine and let it mature for a long time in bottle. Over time the tannins soften and tertiary notes appear, such as dried fruit, earth and forest floor. Typical red Cabernet is dry and thick-skinned.":"卡本內果皮厚、酸度高，所以它的酒富含單寧和清新感。這兩個元素保護酒，讓它能在瓶中長時間熟成。隨著時間，單寧變柔和，並出現果乾、泥土和森林地表等三級氣息。典型的卡本內紅酒是不甜的，果皮也很厚。","Why is Cabernet Sauvignon often matured in oak barrels before bottling?":"為什麼卡本內蘇維濃常在裝瓶前於橡木桶中熟成？","Slow oxygen contact softens the tannins":"緩慢的氧氣接觸讓單寧變柔和","Oak raises the wine's acidity":"橡木提高酒的酸度","Oak removes colour from an overly dark wine":"橡木去除顏色過深的酒的顏色","Oak adds strawberry and red plum notes":"橡木增添草莓和紅李氣息","Fresh from fermentation it is very tannic; oxygen through the wood softens the tannins.":"剛發酵完時單寧非常多；透過木頭進入的氧氣讓單寧變柔和。","A newly fermented Cabernet can taste unpleasantly tannic. In barrel, small amounts of oxygen reach the wine over months or years and soften its tannins. If the barrel is new, it also adds secondary flavours such as smoke, vanilla, cloves and cedar. Strawberry and red plum are primary grape flavours instead.":"剛發酵完的卡本內嚐起來可能單寧多得令人不悅。在橡木桶中，少量氧氣在數月或數年間接觸到酒，讓單寧變柔和。如果是新桶，還會增添煙燻、香草、丁香和雪松等二級風味。草莓和紅李則是葡萄的一級風味。","Which secondary flavours does a new oak barrel add to Cabernet?":"新橡木桶為卡本內增添哪些二級風味？","Smoke, vanilla, cloves, cedar":"煙燻、香草、丁香、雪松","Dried fruit, earth, forest floor":"果乾、泥土、森林地表","Leather, meat, black pepper":"皮革、肉、黑胡椒","Smoke, vanilla, cloves and cedar come from new oak, not from the grape.":"煙燻、香草、丁香和雪松來自新橡木桶，而不是葡萄。","Secondary flavours come from the winery. In Cabernet, new oak brings smoke, vanilla, cloves and cedar, on top of the grape's black fruit. Dried fruit, earth and forest floor are tertiary notes from bottle age, while blackcurrant, black cherry and mint are primary grape flavours.":"二級風味來自酒廠。在卡本內中，新橡木桶在葡萄的黑色水果之上，再帶來煙燻、香草、丁香和雪松。果乾、泥土和森林地表是瓶中陳年的三級氣息，而黑醋栗、黑櫻桃和薄荷是葡萄的一級風味。","Which tertiary flavours does a fine Cabernet Sauvignon develop with age?":"優質的卡本內蘇維濃隨陳年會發展出哪些三級風味？","Dried fruit, earth and forest floor":"果乾、泥土和森林地表","Vanilla, coconut and smoke":"香草、椰子和煙燻","Strawberry, red plum and bell pepper":"草莓、紅李和甜椒","Flowers, black pepper and cherry":"花香、黑胡椒和櫻桃","With bottle age, tannins soften and dried fruit, earth and forest floor appear.":"經過瓶中陳年，單寧變柔和，出現果乾、泥土和森林地表。","Tertiary flavours come from slow ageing. In very good or outstanding Cabernets, time in bottle turns fresh fruit into dried fruit and brings earth and forest floor notes, while the tannins soften. Vanilla, coconut and smoke come from oak, and strawberry and bell pepper are primary flavours.":"三級風味來自緩慢的陳年。在非常好或傑出的卡本內中，瓶中的時間把新鮮果味變成果乾，帶來泥土和森林地表氣息，同時單寧變柔和。香草、椰子和煙燻來自橡木桶，而草莓和甜椒是一級風味。","Why do the Left Bank's gravel soils help Cabernet Sauvignon?":"為什麼左岸的礫石土壤對卡本內蘇維濃有幫助？","They drain fast and hold heat into the evening":"排水快，並能把熱量保持到傍晚","They hold water through dry summers":"在乾燥的夏天保存水分","They are very fertile and raise yields":"非常肥沃，能提高產量","They reflect light and cool the vineyards":"反射光線，讓葡萄園降溫","Gravel sheds water after rain and releases the day's heat, aiding ripening.":"礫石在雨後迅速排水，並釋放白天的熱量，幫助成熟。","Bordeaux has a rainy maritime climate, and Cabernet struggles to ripen on the coolest sites. Left Bank gravel lets water drain away quickly after heavy rain and, by soaking up heat during the day, keeps the vineyard warm into the evening. Cabernet therefore ripens better and gives the great blends of the Haut-Médoc and Graves.":"波爾多屬於多雨的海洋性氣候，卡本內在最涼爽的園地很難成熟。左岸的礫石讓大雨後的水迅速排走，並在白天吸收熱量，讓葡萄園一直溫暖到傍晚。因此卡本內成熟得更好，造就 Haut-Médoc 和 Graves 偉大的混調酒。","Why does the share of Merlot in Bordeaux blends rise in some years?":"為什麼某些年份波爾多混調中梅洛的比例會上升？","Cabernet Sauvignon has not ripened well":"卡本內蘇維濃沒有好好成熟","Merlot has suffered from excess heat":"梅洛受到過熱的影響","The rules require more Merlot in hot years":"法規要求炎熱年份使用更多梅洛","Cabernet has become too soft":"卡本內變得太柔軟","When Cabernet ripens poorly, more Merlot softens the blend's tannin and acidity.":"卡本內成熟不佳時，更多的梅洛能柔化混調的單寧和酸度。","Bordeaux weather varies a lot from year to year, and in some years Cabernet fails to ripen well even on gravel. Under-ripe Cabernet has even harder tannin and acidity and marked herbaceous notes. By raising the share of Merlot, which has medium tannins and ripens more easily, the producer gets a better-balanced blend.":"波爾多的天氣年年差異很大，有些年份即使在礫石上，卡本內也無法好好成熟。未完全成熟的卡本內單寧和酸度更硬，草本氣息也很明顯。提高單寧中等、較容易成熟的梅洛的比例，生產者就能得到更平衡的混調。","Which of these appellations lies within the Haut-Médoc?":"下列哪一個法定產區位於 Haut-Médoc 之內？","Pauillac, like Margaux, is a smaller appellation within the Haut-Médoc.":"Pauillac 和 Margaux 一樣，是 Haut-Médoc 之內較小的法定產區。","Haut-Médoc AOC lies north of the city of Bordeaux, on the Left Bank, and includes appellations such as Margaux and Pauillac, famous for Cabernet-led blends. Pessac-Léognan is part of Graves, south of the city. Pomerol and Saint-Émilion are on the Right Bank, where Merlot dominates.":"Haut-Médoc AOC 位於波爾多市以北的左岸，包括 Margaux 和 Pauillac 等以卡本內為主的混調著稱的法定產區。Pessac-Léognan 屬於波爾多市以南的 Graves。Pomerol 和 Saint-Émilion 位於右岸，那裡以梅洛為主。","Pessac-Léognan AOC lies within which area?":"Pessac-Léognan AOC 位於哪個地區之內？","Pessac-Léognan is the high-quality appellation within Graves, south of Bordeaux.":"Pessac-Léognan 是波爾多以南 Graves 之內的高品質法定產區。","Graves AOC lies south of the city of Bordeaux, on the Left Bank, and includes Pessac-Léognan AOC. As in the Haut-Médoc, Cabernet Sauvignon is usually the leading grape in the blend, supported by Merlot. Saint-Émilion and Pomerol are on the Right Bank instead.":"Graves AOC 位於波爾多市以南的左岸，包括 Pessac-Léognan AOC。和 Haut-Médoc 一樣，卡本內蘇維濃通常是混調中的主要品種，由梅洛輔助。Saint-Émilion 和 Pomerol 則位於右岸。","Why does Cabernet Sauvignon ripen reliably in Languedoc-Roussillon?":"為什麼卡本內蘇維濃在 Languedoc-Roussillon 能穩定成熟？","Warm climate and steadier weather than Bordeaux":"溫暖的氣候，天氣比波爾多穩定","Gravel soils and heavy Atlantic rain":"礫石土壤和大西洋的大量降雨","Cloud and cool breezes that lengthen the season":"延長生長季的雲層和涼爽微風","High altitude and south-facing slopes":"高海拔和朝南的坡地","The steady warmth of southern France lets Cabernet ripen every year.":"法國南部穩定的溫暖讓卡本內每年都能成熟。","In Languedoc-Roussillon the climate is warm and the weather varies less than in Bordeaux. Cabernet, which needs warmth to ripen, manages it reliably here. You find varietal wines and blends with Merlot and other black grapes, usually labelled Pays d'Oc IGP. Gravel and Atlantic rain describe Bordeaux instead.":"Languedoc-Roussillon 氣候溫暖，天氣變化比波爾多小。需要熱量才能成熟的卡本內在這裡能穩定成熟。這裡有單一品種酒，也有與梅洛和其他黑葡萄的混調，通常標示為 Pays d'Oc IGP。礫石和大西洋的降雨描述的則是波爾多。","Which Napa Valley sub-regions are known for full Cabernets with high, ripe tannins?":"Napa Valley 的哪些子產區以單寧高而成熟的飽滿卡本內著稱？","Oakville and Rutherford":"Oakville 和 Rutherford","Maipo and Colchagua":"Maipo 和 Colchagua","Margaux and Pauillac":"Margaux 和 Pauillac","Coonawarra and Margaret River":"Coonawarra 和 Margaret River","Oakville and Rutherford, in Napa Valley, give full Cabernets with ripe black fruit.":"Napa Valley 的 Oakville 和 Rutherford 出產帶有成熟黑色水果的飽滿卡本內。","Napa Valley has a warm, sunny climate and a long season, ideal for Cabernet. The sub-regions of Oakville and Rutherford give full-bodied wines with intense ripe black fruit and high but ripe tannins. Maipo and Colchagua are in Chile, Margaux and Pauillac in Bordeaux, Coonawarra and Margaret River in Australia.":"Napa Valley 氣候溫暖晴朗，生長季漫長，非常適合卡本內。Oakville 和 Rutherford 這兩個子產區出產酒體飽滿、帶有濃郁成熟黑色水果、單寧高而成熟的酒。Maipo 和 Colchagua 在智利，Margaux 和 Pauillac 在波爾多，Coonawarra 和 Margaret River 在澳洲。","What sets Calistoga apart within Napa Valley?":"Calistoga 在 Napa Valley 中有什麼不同之處？","It is warmer and gives some of the ripest wines":"它更溫暖，出產最成熟的酒款之一","It is cooler and gives light, herbaceous wines":"它更涼爽，出產輕盈、帶草本氣息的酒","It has gravel soils like the Left Bank":"它有和左岸一樣的礫石土壤","It mainly makes wines labelled California":"它主要出產標示 California 的酒","Calistoga, at the valley's far north, is warmer still and gives very ripe, full wines.":"位於山谷最北端的 Calistoga 更加溫暖，出產非常成熟、飽滿的酒。","Napa Valley is already warm, but in the far north, at Calistoga, it is warmer still. Here you find some of the ripest, fullest-bodied Cabernets in the valley. More heat means more ripeness, so richer black fruit and fuller body, not light, herbaceous wines.":"Napa Valley 已經很溫暖，但在最北端的 Calistoga 更加溫暖。這裡有山谷中最成熟、酒體最飽滿的卡本內。熱量越多代表越成熟，因此有更豐富的黑色水果和更飽滿的酒體，而不是輕盈、帶草本氣息的酒。","What should you expect from a Cabernet Sauvignon labelled simply California?":"只標示 California 的卡本內蘇維濃，你應該預期什麼？","Grapes from across the state, a wine to drink young":"來自全州各地的葡萄，適合趁年輕喝的酒","Grapes only from Oakville, a wine for long ageing":"只來自 Oakville 的葡萄，適合長期陳年的酒","Grapes from cool slopes, a light herbaceous wine":"來自涼爽坡地的葡萄，輕盈帶草本氣息的酒","Sonoma grapes, aged only in new barrels":"Sonoma 的葡萄，只在新橡木桶中陳年","The California label allows grapes from the whole state, often the hot Central Valley, for early drinking.":"California 標示允許使用全州的葡萄，常來自炎熱的 Central Valley，適合早飲。","Wines labelled California can blend grapes grown anywhere in the state. Much of the fruit comes from the hot, irrigated vineyards of the Central Valley, and the wines are made for immediate drinking. Any oak flavour often comes from alternatives such as chips or staves, which are cheaper than barrels.":"標示 California 的酒可以混調在全州任何地方種植的葡萄。大部分的果實來自 Central Valley 炎熱、經灌溉的葡萄園，這些酒是為立即飲用而釀的。若有橡木風味，常來自比橡木桶便宜的橡木片或橡木條等替代品。","Which grape is the most widely planted in Chile?":"智利種植最廣泛的品種是哪一個？","Cabernet Sauvignon is Chile's most widely planted grape.":"卡本內蘇維濃是智利種植最廣泛的品種。","Cabernet Sauvignon is Chile's most planted grape, with key sub-regions such as Maipo Valley and Colchagua Valley in the Central Valley. Carmenère is the local speciality, often blended with Cabernet and Merlot, but it is not the most planted. Merlot matters mainly for soft, high-volume wines.":"卡本內蘇維濃是智利種植最多的品種，Central Valley 的 Maipo Valley 和 Colchagua Valley 是重要的子產區。卡門內爾是當地特色品種，常與卡本內和梅洛混調，但不是種植最多的。梅洛主要用於柔和的大量生產酒款。","Maipo Valley and Colchagua Valley are sub-regions of which region?":"Maipo Valley 和 Colchagua Valley 是哪個產區的子產區？","Central Valley (Chile)":"Central Valley（智利）","Central Valley (California)":"Central Valley（加州）","Maipo and Colchagua are key Cabernet sub-regions within Chile's Central Valley.":"Maipo 和 Colchagua 是智利 Central Valley 之內重要的卡本內子產區。","Watch the name: California also has a hot, irrigated Central Valley, the source of wines labelled California. Maipo and Colchagua, however, are Chilean valleys running from the Andes foothills to the Coastal Ranges, with flatter, more fertile valley floors. This range of sites gives producers plenty of choice.":"注意名稱：加州也有一個炎熱、經灌溉的 Central Valley，是標示 California 的酒的來源。不過 Maipo 和 Colchagua 是智利的山谷，從安地斯山脈山麓延伸到海岸山脈，谷底較平坦、較肥沃。這樣多樣的園地給了生產者充分的選擇。","Which notes do Chilean Cabernets from the mountain foothills often show?":"來自山麓的智利卡本內常展現哪些氣息？","Mint and green bell pepper with black fruit":"薄荷和青椒，加上黑色水果","Flowers and black pepper with red fruit":"花香和黑胡椒，加上紅色水果","Coconut and vanilla with no fruit":"椰子和香草，沒有果味","Leather and meat with dried fruit":"皮革和肉，加上果乾","Andean foothill wines pair mint and green bell pepper with black fruit and oak.":"安地斯山麓的酒把薄荷和青椒與黑色水果和橡木結合在一起。","In Chile producers can choose between slopes and valley floors. Cabernets from the Andes foothills often show herbal mint and herbaceous green bell pepper notes alongside black fruit and oak. Flowers and black pepper point to Syrah, while leather and meat are notes of age.":"在智利，生產者可以在坡地和谷底之間選擇。來自安地斯山麓的卡本內常在黑色水果和橡木之外，展現草本的薄荷和植物性的青椒氣息。花香和黑胡椒指向希哈，而皮革和肉是陳年的氣息。","What is a Cape Blend?":"什麼是 Cape Blend？","A South African blend including Pinotage":"含有皮諾塔吉的南非混調","A Chilean blend including Carmenère":"含有卡門內爾的智利混調","An Australian blend including Shiraz":"含有希拉茲的澳洲混調","A French blend including Grenache":"含有格那希的法國混調","In South Africa, Cabernet and Merlot are sometimes blended with Pinotage: the Cape Blend.":"在南非，卡本內和梅洛有時會與皮諾塔吉混調：這就是 Cape Blend。","Pinotage is South Africa's local speciality. When it is blended with Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot, the wine is often called a Cape Blend. Carmenère is Chile's speciality, blended with Cabernet in Chilean wines, while Shiraz and Grenache belong to other countries and traditions.":"皮諾塔吉是南非的在地特色品種。當它與卡本內蘇維濃和梅洛混調時，這款酒常被稱為 Cape Blend。卡門內爾是智利的特色品種，在智利酒中與卡本內混調，而希拉茲和格那希則屬於其他國家和傳統。","Why do Stellenbosch Cabernets range from fresh and herbal to full and alcoholic?":"為什麼 Stellenbosch 的卡本內從清爽帶草本到飽滿高酒精都有？","The climate changes with vineyard altitude":"氣候隨葡萄園海拔而變化","The rules impose different styles per zone":"法規對各區規定不同的風格","Yields vary with irrigation":"產量隨灌溉而變化","Gravel soils vary from site to site":"礫石土壤因園地而異","A mountainous region: high vineyards are cooler, low ones warmer.":"多山的產區：高處的葡萄園較涼爽，低處較溫暖。","Stellenbosch is mountainous and its climate ranges from moderate to warm with altitude. On cooler sites Cabernet ripens more slowly and keeps fresh, herbal notes; on warmer sites it ripens further and gives full wines with cooked fruit and high alcohol. A clear case of climate shaping style.":"Stellenbosch 多山，氣候隨海拔從溫和到溫暖。在較涼爽的園地，卡本內成熟得較慢，保留清新的草本氣息；在較溫暖的園地，它成熟得更充分，釀出帶有煮過果味、酒精高的飽滿酒款。這是氣候塑造風格的清楚例子。","What tempers Margaret River's warm climate?":"是什麼緩和了 Margaret River 的溫暖氣候？","Coastal breezes and plentiful winter rain":"海岸微風和充沛的冬季降雨","Cloud cover and cold southerly winds":"雲層和寒冷的南風","The altitude of Andean foothills":"安地斯山麓的海拔","Gravel soils that drain water":"能排水的礫石土壤","Margaret River is warm but cooled by sea breezes and abundant winter rain.":"Margaret River 很溫暖，但受到海風和充沛冬雨的降溫。","Margaret River in Western Australia is known for quality Cabernet, sometimes blended with Merlot. Its heat is tempered by coastal breezes and plentiful winter rain, and the wines show ripe black fruit and subtle oak. Cloud cover and southerly winds are the cooling factors of Coonawarra instead.":"西澳的 Margaret River 以優質的卡本內著稱，有時與梅洛混調。它的高溫受到海岸微風和充沛冬雨的緩和，酒款展現成熟的黑色水果和細緻的橡木味。雲層和南風則是 Coonawarra 的降溫因素。","An Australian Cabernet with marked mint, intense blackcurrant, smoke and cedar, built to age. Where is it most likely from?":"一款帶有明顯薄荷、濃郁黑醋栗、煙燻和雪松、適合陳年的澳洲卡本內。它最可能來自哪裡？","Mint, intense blackcurrant, and smoke and cedar from oak are Coonawarra Cabernet's signature.":"薄荷、濃郁的黑醋栗以及來自橡木的煙燻和雪松，是 Coonawarra 卡本內的招牌特徵。","Coonawarra, a small South Australian region, is cooled by cloud cover and southerly breezes. Its Cabernets show mint, intense blackcurrant, and smoke and cedar from oak, and can develop for many years. Barossa and Hunter Valley are famous for Shiraz, while South Eastern Australia means inexpensive, high-volume wine.":"南澳的小產區 Coonawarra 受到雲層和南方微風的降溫。它的卡本內展現薄荷、濃郁的黑醋栗以及來自橡木的煙燻和雪松，能發展多年。Barossa 和 Hunter Valley 以希拉茲聞名，而 South Eastern Australia 代表平價的大量生產酒款。","Why is Cabernet Sauvignon often blended with Merlot in Hawke's Bay?":"為什麼在 Hawke's Bay，卡本內蘇維濃常與梅洛混調？","In a moderate climate Cabernet ripens only on the warmest sites":"在溫和氣候中，卡本內只在最溫暖的園地成熟","Extreme heat makes Cabernet too alcoholic":"極端高溫讓卡本內酒精太高","The rules forbid varietal Cabernet":"法規禁止單一品種的卡本內","Merlot adds missing tannin and colour":"梅洛補足所缺的單寧和顏色","Hawke's Bay is moderate: Cabernet ripens with difficulty and the more common Merlot completes the blend.":"Hawke's Bay 屬於溫和氣候：卡本內很難成熟，由種植較普遍的梅洛補足混調。","In Hawke's Bay's moderate climate, Cabernet needs the warmest sites to ripen fully. It is therefore often combined with Merlot, which is more widely grown there, giving wines with fresh red and black fruit and herbaceous green bell pepper notes, a sign of a not-too-warm climate. Merlot has medium tannins, so it does not add tannin.":"在 Hawke's Bay 的溫和氣候中，卡本內需要最溫暖的園地才能完全成熟。因此它常與當地種植更廣的梅洛結合，釀出帶有新鮮紅色和黑色水果以及植物性青椒氣息的酒，這是氣候不太溫暖的跡象。梅洛的單寧中等，所以不會增添單寧。","Which recent trend lets Cabernet Sauvignon be enjoyed younger?":"近年的哪一個趨勢讓卡本內蘇維濃可以更年輕時就享用？","Gentler methods that extract less tannin":"較溫和、萃取較少單寧的方法","Longer ageing in new barrels":"在新橡木桶中陳年更久","Later harvests for riper grapes":"更晚採收以獲得更成熟的葡萄","Blending in more Syrah for colour":"混入更多希哈以增添顏色","Extracting less tannin gives fresh, fruity Cabernet for early drinking; Chile succeeds with this style.":"萃取較少的單寧能帶來適合早飲的清新果香卡本內；智利在這種風格上很成功。","Cabernet remains popular with big brands and premium producers, and food helps soften its tannin and acidity. Some producers use gentler winemaking that extracts less tannin, so the wine can be enjoyed young while it is fresh and fruity. Chilean producers are having particular success with this style.":"卡本內在大品牌和頂級生產者中仍很受歡迎，而食物有助於柔化它的單寧和酸度。有些生產者使用較溫和、萃取較少單寧的釀造方式，讓酒可以在年輕、清新、果香豐富時享用。智利生產者在這種風格上尤其成功。","Which statement about Napa Valley and Sonoma wines labelled Cabernet Sauvignon is correct?":"關於標示 Cabernet Sauvignon 的 Napa Valley 和 Sonoma 酒款，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","They may contain small amounts of other grapes":"它們可能含有少量其他品種","They must all come from the Central Valley":"它們必須全部來自 Central Valley","They are always light and for drinking young":"它們總是輕盈、要趁年輕喝","They may not be aged in oak":"它們不得在橡木桶中陳年","Even labelled Cabernet Sauvignon, these wines may include a little of other varieties.":"即使標示 Cabernet Sauvignon，這些酒也可能含有少量其他品種。","Napa Valley and Sonoma make many very good to outstanding Cabernets: full, ripe and powerful, especially in Sonoma's warmer inland areas and in Napa sub-regions such as Oakville, Rutherford and Calistoga. Even when the label says only Cabernet Sauvignon, the wine may contain small amounts of other grapes. It is wines labelled California that often come from the Central Valley.":"Napa Valley 和 Sonoma 出產許多非常好到傑出的卡本內：飽滿、成熟、強勁，尤其是在 Sonoma 較溫暖的內陸地區，以及 Oakville、Rutherford 和 Calistoga 等 Napa 子產區。即使酒標只寫 Cabernet Sauvignon，酒中也可能含有少量其他品種。常來自 Central Valley 的是標示 California 的酒。","Where does Cabernet Sauvignon originally come from?":"卡本內蘇維濃原本來自哪裡？","South-west France":"法國西南部","The Northern Rhône, on its steep hillsides":"北隆河的陡峭山坡","Chile's Central Valley":"智利的 Central Valley","Cabernet Sauvignon is a black grape from south-west France.":"卡本內蘇維濃（Cabernet Sauvignon）是來自法國西南部的黑葡萄。","It is the grape behind many of the most famous Left Bank Bordeaux wines and is now grown worldwide. The Northern Rhône is Syrah's home and Burgundy is Pinot Noir's; Chile plants it more than any other grape, but that is not where it began.":"它是左岸許多最著名波爾多酒背後的品種，現在種植於世界各地。北隆河是希哈的故鄉，布根地是黑皮諾的故鄉；智利種植它比任何其他品種都多，但那不是它的發源地。","A grower in a moderate climate wants to plant Cabernet Sauvignon. Which sites suit it best?":"一位溫和氣候的種植者想種卡本內蘇維濃。哪些園地最適合它？","Only the warmest ones":"只有最溫暖的園地","The coolest, windiest ones, to keep acidity":"最涼爽、風最大的園地，以保留酸度","Fertile, damp valley-floor sites":"肥沃潮濕的谷底園地","North-facing sites, sheltered from the sun":"朝北、避開陽光的園地","In a moderate climate Cabernet struggles to ripen except on the warmest sites.":"在溫和氣候中，卡本內除了最溫暖的園地外都很難成熟。","Its thick skins and late ripening need a long, warm season. Cool, windy or north-facing sites would slow ripening further and give green, harsh wines; fertile valley floors give high yields but less ripe grapes.":"它的厚果皮和晚熟特性需要漫長而溫暖的生長季。涼爽、多風或朝北的園地會讓成熟更慢，釀出青澀粗糙的酒；肥沃的谷底產量高，但葡萄較不成熟。","What do Cabernet Sauvignon's thick skins contain in large amounts?":"卡本內蘇維濃的厚果皮含有大量的什麼？","Colour, flavour and tannin":"顏色、風味和單寧","Sugar, water and wild yeast":"糖、水和野生酵母","Floral aromas and black pepper notes":"花香和黑胡椒氣息","Noble rot and honey aromas":"貴腐菌和蜂蜜香氣","The thick skins are rich in colour, flavour and tannin.":"厚果皮富含顏色、風味和單寧。","This is why a single-varietal Cabernet is deeply coloured and very tannic. Black pepper belongs to Syrah, flowers to aromatic grapes, and noble rot to certain sweet wines, not to Cabernet.":"這就是為什麼單一品種的卡本內顏色深、單寧非常多。黑胡椒屬於希哈，花香屬於芳香型品種，貴腐菌則屬於某些甜酒，都不屬於卡本內。","Which of these is NOT a typical primary aroma of Cabernet Sauvignon?":"下列哪一項不是卡本內蘇維濃典型的一級香氣？","Mint":"薄荷","Vanilla comes from new oak barrels: it is a secondary aroma.":"香草來自新橡木桶：它是二級香氣。","Blackcurrant and black cherry are Cabernet's fruit, often with mint or green bell pepper. Smoke, vanilla, cloves and cedar come from new oak during maturation instead.":"黑醋栗和黑櫻桃是卡本內的果味，常帶有薄荷或青椒。煙燻、香草、丁香和雪松則來自熟成期間的新橡木桶。","How does Cabernet Sauvignon's fruit change in a warm climate?":"在溫暖氣候中，卡本內蘇維濃的果味如何變化？","It can take on a cooked character":"可能帶有煮過的特徵","It turns more vegetal, with lots of green bell pepper":"變得更有植物味，帶大量青椒","It shifts to fresh red fruit":"轉向新鮮的紅色水果","It develops citrus and white-flower notes":"發展出柑橘和白花氣息","With heat, Cabernet's black fruit can become cooked.":"在高溫下，卡本內的黑色水果可能變得像煮過。","Green bell pepper notes are linked to less ripe grapes, so to cooler climates or years. Cabernet remains a black-fruit grape: fresh red fruit, citrus and white flowers are not its profile.":"青椒氣息與較不成熟的葡萄有關，也就是較涼爽的氣候或年份。卡本內始終是黑色水果品種：新鮮的紅色水果、柑橘和白花都不是它的風味特徵。","Why is blending especially useful for Cabernet in cool vintages in moderate climates?":"在溫和氣候的涼爽年份，為什麼混調對卡本內特別有用？","It softens very high tannin and acidity":"柔化非常高的單寧和酸度","It adds colour and tannin to a wine that is too light and pale":"為太輕盈、太淡的酒增添顏色和單寧","It allows an earlier harvest than planned":"讓採收能比計畫中更早","It removes the need for barrel maturation":"不再需要橡木桶熟成","A blend, for instance with Merlot, tones down the tannin and acidity of under-ripe Cabernet.":"混調（例如與梅洛）能緩和未完全成熟的卡本內的單寧和酸度。","In cool years Cabernet ripens poorly and tastes even harsher. It lacks neither colour nor tannin; if anything it has too much. Blending does not change the harvest date or replace oak maturation.":"在涼爽的年份，卡本內成熟不佳，嚐起來更加粗糙。它既不缺顏色也不缺單寧；如果有什麼問題，是太多了。混調不會改變採收日期，也無法取代橡木桶熟成。","How long is Cabernet Sauvignon often matured in oak before bottling?":"卡本內蘇維濃裝瓶前常在橡木桶中熟成多久？","Several months or even years":"數個月甚至數年","A few days, just long enough to settle":"幾天，剛好足以沉澱","Never: it is always bottled straight after fermentation":"從不：總是在發酵後立刻裝瓶","At least twenty years by law":"依法至少二十年","Freshly fermented Cabernet is very tannic, so it often spends months or years in barrel.":"剛發酵完的卡本內單寧非常多，所以常在橡木桶中待上數月或數年。","A newly fermented Cabernet can taste unpleasantly tannic; slow oxygen contact in barrel softens it. A few days would not be enough; younger styles exist, but it is not always bottled at once, and no rule demands twenty years.":"剛發酵完的卡本內嚐起來可能單寧多得令人不悅；在橡木桶中緩慢的氧氣接觸能讓它變柔和。幾天是不夠的；較年輕的風格是存在的，但它並非總是立刻裝瓶，也沒有規定要求二十年。","A Cabernet Sauvignon shows dried fruit, earth, forest floor and soft tannins. What does this suggest?":"一款卡本內蘇維濃展現果乾、泥土、森林地表和柔和的單寧。這表示什麼？","A high-quality wine aged many years in bottle":"一款在瓶中陳年多年的高品質酒款","A young wine just out of a new barrel":"一款剛從新橡木桶出來的年輕酒款","Grapes picked too early in a cool year":"涼爽年份中太早採收的葡萄","A simple wine made with oak chips":"用橡木片釀的簡單酒款","Dried fruit, earth and forest floor are tertiary notes of aged Cabernet.":"果乾、泥土和森林地表是陳年卡本內的三級氣息。","High tannin and acidity act as natural preservatives: over time tannins soften and tertiary notes appear. A young wine from new oak shows smoke, vanilla and cedar; unripe grapes give vegetal notes; oak chips flavour wines meant to be drunk young.":"高單寧和高酸度是天然的防腐劑：隨著時間，單寧變柔和，並出現三級氣息。來自新橡木桶的年輕酒款展現煙燻、香草和雪松；未成熟的葡萄帶來植物性氣息；橡木片則用來為要趁年輕喝的酒增添風味。","In which Bordeaux vineyards can Cabernet Sauvignon fail to ripen reliably?":"在波爾多哪些葡萄園，卡本內蘇維濃可能無法穩定成熟？","The coolest sites":"最涼爽的園地","The free-draining gravel soils of the Left Bank":"左岸排水良好的礫石土壤","The warmest, sunniest vineyards":"最溫暖、陽光最充足的葡萄園","Irrigated inland vineyards":"經灌溉的內陸葡萄園","In Bordeaux's moderate climate, the coolest sites are not enough for Cabernet.":"在波爾多的溫和氣候中，最涼爽的園地對卡本內來說不夠。","This is exactly why Cabernet dominates on the Left Bank gravels, which drain water and hold heat. Bordeaux is not a region of irrigated vineyards, and warm, sunny sites are where it ripens best.":"這正是卡本內在左岸礫石上佔主導的原因，礫石能排水並保留熱量。波爾多不是灌溉葡萄園的產區，而溫暖晴朗的園地正是它成熟得最好的地方。","Which grape usually leads the wines of Margaux and Pauillac?":"Margaux 和 Pauillac 的酒通常以哪個品種為主？","Margaux and Pauillac lie in the Haut-Médoc on the Left Bank: Cabernet-led blends.":"Margaux 和 Pauillac 位於左岸的 Haut-Médoc：以卡本內為主的混調。","On the Left Bank Merlot is usually in the blend but does not lead; it leads in Saint-Émilion and Pomerol. Syrah and Pinot Noir are not Bordeaux grapes.":"在左岸，梅洛通常也在混調中，但不佔主導；它在 Saint-Émilion 和 Pomerol 才佔主導。希哈和黑皮諾不是波爾多的品種。","A customer wants a red to cellar for many years. Which choice suits best?":"一位顧客想要一款能窖藏多年的紅酒。哪個選擇最合適？","A top Pauillac AOC":"頂級的 Pauillac AOC","A high-volume Cabernet labelled simply California":"只標示 California 的大量生產卡本內","A big-brand Chilean Merlot for drinking now":"適合現在喝的大品牌智利梅洛","A simple, fruity Bordeaux AOC":"簡單、果香豐富的 Bordeaux AOC","The best Left Bank wines, such as Pauillac, have very long ageing potential.":"最好的左岸酒款，例如 Pauillac，有非常長的陳年潛力。","Haut-Médoc Cabernet-led blends combine tannin, acidity and concentration. Wines labelled California, big-brand Chilean Merlot and simple Bordeaux AOC are made to be drunk young.":"Haut-Médoc 以卡本內為主的混調結合了單寧、酸度和濃縮度。標示 California 的酒、大品牌智利梅洛和簡單的 Bordeaux AOC 都是要趁年輕喝的。","Where are the Haut-Médoc and Graves in relation to the city of Bordeaux?":"Haut-Médoc 和 Graves 相對於波爾多市的位置在哪裡？","Haut-Médoc to the north, Graves to the south":"Haut-Médoc 在北，Graves 在南","Haut-Médoc to the south, Graves to the north":"Haut-Médoc 在南，Graves 在北","Both east of the Dordogne, on the Right Bank":"兩者都在多爾多涅河以東的右岸","Both on the Atlantic coast":"兩者都在大西洋沿岸","The Haut-Médoc is north of the city and Graves south of it, both on the Left Bank.":"Haut-Médoc 在波爾多市以北，Graves 在以南，兩者都位於左岸。","The Haut-Médoc, in the Médoc district, includes Margaux and Pauillac; Graves includes Pessac-Léognan. The Right Bank, north and east of the Gironde and Dordogne, is Merlot country with Saint-Émilion and Pomerol.":"位於 Médoc 地區的 Haut-Médoc 包括 Margaux 和 Pauillac；Graves 包括 Pessac-Léognan。吉倫特河和多爾多涅河以北和以東的右岸是梅洛的天下，有 Saint-Émilion 和 Pomerol。","A single-varietal Cabernet Sauvignon from France's warm south: how is it most likely labelled?":"一款來自法國溫暖南部的單一品種卡本內蘇維濃：它最可能如何標示？","In Languedoc-Roussillon, Cabernet, alone or blended, is usually labelled Pays d'Oc IGP.":"在 Languedoc-Roussillon，卡本內無論單獨或混調，通常都標示為 Pays d'Oc IGP。","Languedoc-Roussillon's warm, steady climate ripens Cabernet every year. Haut-Médoc and Bordeaux Supérieur are Bordeaux appellations; Crozes-Hermitage is a Northern Rhône Syrah appellation.":"Languedoc-Roussillon 溫暖穩定的氣候讓卡本內每年都能成熟。Haut-Médoc 和 Bordeaux Supérieur 是波爾多的法定產區；Crozes-Hermitage 是北隆河的希哈法定產區。","Which climate makes Napa Valley ideal for Cabernet Sauvignon?":"哪一種氣候讓 Napa Valley 非常適合卡本內蘇維濃？","Warm and sunny, with a long growing season":"溫暖晴朗，生長季漫長","Cool and cloudy, with southerly breezes":"涼爽多雲，有南方微風","Very rainy, with gravel soils":"非常多雨，有礫石土壤","Cold, with frequent spring frosts":"寒冷，經常有春霜","Napa's sun and long season bring Cabernet to full ripeness.":"Napa 的陽光和漫長的生長季讓卡本內完全成熟。","This is why Oakville, Rutherford and Calistoga wines are full and ripe. Cloud and southerly breezes describe Coonawarra, rain and gravel describe Bordeaux; a cold, frosty climate would not ripen Cabernet.":"這就是為什麼 Oakville、Rutherford 和 Calistoga 的酒飽滿而成熟。雲層和南方微風描述的是 Coonawarra，雨水和礫石描述的是波爾多；寒冷多霜的氣候無法讓卡本內成熟。","In which part of Sonoma can Cabernets as powerful as Napa Valley's be made?":"在 Sonoma 的哪個地方能釀出和 Napa Valley 一樣強勁的卡本內？","The warmer inland areas":"較溫暖的內陸地區","The coolest coast, swept by Pacific fogs":"受太平洋霧氣籠罩的最涼爽海岸","Very cool high-altitude vineyards":"非常涼爽的高海拔葡萄園","Nowhere: Sonoma makes only white wines":"哪裡都不行：Sonoma 只出產白酒","Sonoma's warmer inland areas give similarly powerful Cabernets.":"Sonoma 較溫暖的內陸地區出產同樣強勁的卡本內。","Cabernet needs warmth: the cool coast and cool heights give less ripe grapes. Sonoma, Napa Valley's neighbour, makes many quality reds, not only whites.":"卡本內需要熱量：涼爽的海岸和涼爽的高處帶來的葡萄較不成熟。Napa Valley 的鄰居 Sonoma 出產許多優質紅酒，不只有白酒。","Where does much of the fruit for Cabernets labelled simply California come from?":"只標示 California 的卡本內，大部分的果實來自哪裡？","The hot, irrigated vineyards of the Central Valley":"Central Valley 炎熱、經灌溉的葡萄園","The best plots of Oakville and Rutherford":"Oakville 和 Rutherford 最好的地塊","Cool, hand-picked coastal hillsides":"涼爽、人工採收的沿海山坡","Old, low-yielding vines in Calistoga":"Calistoga 低產量的老藤","These state-wide wines use a lot of fruit from the hot, irrigated Central Valley.":"這些全州性的酒使用大量來自炎熱、經灌溉的 Central Valley 的果實。","These are wines to drink young, with any oak flavour often coming from chips or staves. Oakville, Rutherford and Calistoga are Napa Valley sub-regions for more ambitious wines that carry their own names on the label.":"這些是要趁年輕喝的酒，若有橡木風味常來自橡木片或橡木條。Oakville、Rutherford 和 Calistoga 是 Napa Valley 的子產區，出產更有企圖心、在酒標上標示自己名稱的酒。","How do the Maipo and Colchagua valleys extend?":"Maipo 和 Colchagua 山谷如何延伸？","From the Andes in the east to the Coastal Ranges in the west":"從東邊的安地斯山脈到西邊的海岸山脈","North to south along the Pacific, always on flat land":"沿著太平洋南北延伸，始終在平地上","Over a single steep, south-facing hill":"在單一朝南的陡峭山丘上","On both banks of a large Atlantic estuary":"在一個大型大西洋河口的兩岸","These Central Valley sub-regions run from the Andean foothills to the Coastal Ranges.":"這些 Central Valley 子產區從安地斯山麓延伸到海岸山脈。","Between the two ranges lie slopes and a flatter, more fertile valley floor, giving producers a broad choice of sites. The single hill describes Hermitage, the estuary describes Bordeaux.":"在兩座山脈之間有坡地，也有較平坦、較肥沃的谷底，給了生產者廣泛的園地選擇。單一山丘描述的是 Hermitage，河口描述的是波爾多。","With which local speciality is Cabernet Sauvignon sometimes blended in Chile?":"在智利，卡本內蘇維濃有時會與哪個在地特色品種混調？","In Chile Cabernet appears alone or with Merlot and Carmenère, the local speciality.":"在智利，卡本內可以單獨出現，或與梅洛和在地特色品種卡門內爾一起。","Pinotage is South Africa's speciality used in Cape Blends. Grenache mainly partners Syrah; Viognier is a white grape sometimes co-fermented with Syrah in Côte-Rôtie.":"皮諾塔吉是用於 Cape Blend 的南非特色品種。格那希主要是希哈的搭檔；維歐尼耶是白葡萄，在 Côte-Rôtie 有時與希哈共同發酵。","A Stellenbosch Cabernet comes from a low, warm vineyard. Which style is most likely?":"一款 Stellenbosch 卡本內來自低海拔、溫暖的葡萄園。最可能是什麼風格？","Full body, cooked fruit, high alcohol":"酒體飽滿、煮過的果味、高酒精","Fresh and herbal, with light body and modest alcohol":"清爽帶草本氣息，酒體輕盈，酒精適中","Delicate red fruit and low tannin":"細緻的紅色水果和低單寧","Sweet, made from nobly rotten grapes":"甜，用貴腐葡萄釀造","At low altitude Stellenbosch is warm: full, alcoholic wines with cooked fruit.":"在低海拔，Stellenbosch 很溫暖：帶有煮過果味的飽滿高酒精酒款。","In this mountainous region the climate runs from moderate to warm depending on altitude. The fresh, herbal style comes from higher vineyards. Cabernet stays tannic with black fruit, and it is not used here for sweet botrytis wines.":"在這個多山的產區，氣候依海拔從溫和到溫暖。清爽帶草本氣息的風格來自較高的葡萄園。卡本內依然單寧多、帶黑色水果，而這裡也不用它來釀貴腐甜酒。","Which profile describes a typical Margaret River Cabernet?":"哪一種風味特徵描述典型的 Margaret River 卡本內？","Ripe black fruit and subtle oak notes":"成熟的黑色水果和細緻的橡木氣息","Fresh red fruit, black pepper and floral Viognier notes":"新鮮的紅色水果、黑胡椒和維歐尼耶的花香","Cooked fruit, liquorice and very high alcohol":"煮過的果味、甘草和非常高的酒精","Citrus, honey and residual sweetness":"柑橘、蜂蜜和殘留的甜味","Margaret River gives Cabernet with ripe black fruit and subtle oak.":"Margaret River 出產帶有成熟黑色水果和細緻橡木味的卡本內。","The region is warm but tempered by coastal breezes and plentiful winter rain; Cabernet is sometimes blended with Merlot. Black pepper and Viognier point to Syrah, liquorice and very high alcohol to hotter styles.":"這個產區很溫暖，但受到海岸微風和充沛冬雨的緩和；卡本內有時會與梅洛混調。黑胡椒和維歐尼耶指向希哈，甘草和非常高的酒精則指向更炎熱的風格。","What moderates the climate of Coonawarra?":"是什麼調節了 Coonawarra 的氣候？","Cloud cover and cooling southerly breezes":"雲層和帶來涼意的南方微風","Andean altitude":"安地斯山脈的海拔","Morning fogs from a nearby bay":"來自鄰近海灣的晨霧","A large estuary nearby":"附近的大型河口","Small Coonawarra, in South Australia, is cooled by cloud and southerly breezes.":"南澳的小產區 Coonawarra 受到雲層和南方微風的降溫。","The result is Cabernet with mint, intense blackcurrant and often smoke and cedar from oak, able to age. Andean altitude belongs to Chile, bay fogs to Los Carneros in California, the estuary to Bordeaux.":"結果是帶有薄荷、濃郁黑醋栗、常有來自橡木的煙燻和雪松、能陳年的卡本內。安地斯山脈的海拔屬於智利，海灣的霧氣屬於加州的 Los Carneros，河口屬於波爾多。","What style does a Hawke's Bay Cabernet-Merlot blend usually have?":"Hawke's Bay 的卡本內與梅洛混調通常是什麼風格？","Fresh red and black fruit with green bell pepper":"新鮮的紅色和黑色水果，帶青椒","Cooked black fruit and liquorice":"煮過的黑色水果和甘草","Strawberry and raspberry with no tannin at all":"草莓和覆盆子，完全沒有單寧","Apricot and honey from noble rot":"來自貴腐菌的杏桃和蜂蜜","The moderate climate gives blends with fresh red and black fruit and herbaceous notes.":"溫和的氣候帶來有新鮮紅色和黑色水果以及草本氣息的混調。","In Hawke's Bay Cabernet needs the warmest sites and is joined with the more widely grown Merlot. Cooked fruit and liquorice belong to warm climates; the tannin does not disappear, and noble rot concerns sweet wines.":"在 Hawke's Bay，卡本內需要最溫暖的園地，並與種植較廣的梅洛結合。煮過的果味和甘草屬於溫暖氣候；單寧不會消失，而貴腐菌與甜酒有關。","Why is Cabernet Sauvignon a popular choice with food?":"為什麼卡本內蘇維濃是受歡迎的佐餐選擇？","Food can help soften its tannin and acidity":"食物有助於柔化它的單寧和酸度","Its residual sugar balances salty dishes":"它的殘糖能平衡鹹的菜餚","Its tannins are low enough to suit any dish":"它的單寧低到適合任何菜餚","Its floral aromas enhance desserts":"它的花香能提升甜點","At the table, food helps tone down Cabernet's high tannin and acidity.":"在餐桌上，食物有助於緩和卡本內的高單寧和高酸度。","Cabernet is dry with high tannin and acidity: it is not sweet, low in tannin or floral. It is also very familiar to consumers and popular with both big brands and premium producers.":"卡本內不甜，單寧和酸度都高：它不甜、不低單寧，也沒有花香。消費者對它也非常熟悉，大品牌和頂級生產者都很喜愛它。","In which country are gently extracted Cabernets, made to drink young and fruity, proving successful?":"在哪個國家，以溫和萃取、要趁年輕果香豐富時喝的卡本內獲得成功？","France, on Bordeaux's Left Bank":"法國，波爾多左岸","Chilean producers are succeeding with this lower-tannin, younger style.":"智利生產者在這種單寧較低、較年輕的風格上獲得成功。","Extracting less tannin lets the wine be enjoyed fresh and fruity without long ageing. The Left Bank is known for long-lived Cabernet; New Zealand grows little of it and Germany is not Cabernet country.":"萃取較少的單寧，讓酒不需長期陳年就能在清新果香時享用。左岸以長壽的卡本內著稱；紐西蘭種得很少，而德國也不是卡本內的產地。","Which of these regions is NOT a key region for Cabernet Sauvignon?":"下列哪一個產區不是卡本內蘇維濃的重要產區？","Hunter Valley is known for Shiraz, not Cabernet.":"Hunter Valley 以希拉茲而不是卡本內著稱。","Coonawarra and Margaret River are Australia's key Cabernet regions, Stellenbosch is South Africa's. Hunter Valley, in New South Wales, is famous for medium-bodied Shiraz.":"Coonawarra 和 Margaret River 是澳洲重要的卡本內產區，Stellenbosch 是南非的。新南威爾斯的 Hunter Valley 以酒體中等的希拉茲聞名。","A label reads Oakville, Napa Valley, Cabernet Sauvignon. What wine can you expect?":"一張酒標上寫著 Oakville, Napa Valley, Cabernet Sauvignon。你可以預期什麼樣的酒？","Full body, ripe black fruit, high ripe tannins":"酒體飽滿、成熟的黑色水果、高而成熟的單寧","Light and herbal, from grapes grown across the state":"輕盈帶草本氣息，用全州各地種植的葡萄釀造","A Pinotage blend typical of the coast":"典型的沿海皮諾塔吉混調","A sweet late-harvest wine":"甜型晚收酒","Oakville is a Napa Valley sub-region for full, ripe Cabernet.":"Oakville 是 Napa Valley 出產飽滿成熟卡本內的子產區。","The warm, sunny climate gives full wines with high but ripe tannins; they may contain small amounts of other grapes. Wines from across the state are labelled California; Pinotage is South African.":"溫暖晴朗的氣候帶來單寧高而成熟的飽滿酒款；它們可能含有少量其他品種。來自全州的酒標示為 California；皮諾塔吉是南非的。","Which structure is typical of a single-varietal Merlot?":"哪一種結構是單一品種梅洛的典型特徵？","Medium acidity and medium tannins":"中等酸度和中等單寧","High acidity and high tannins":"高酸度和高單寧","Low acidity and low tannins":"低酸度和低單寧","High acidity and low tannins":"高酸度和低單寧","Merlot usually gives dry wines with both acidity and tannins at a medium level.":"梅洛通常釀出酸度和單寧都在中等水準的不甜酒。","This medium structure explains Merlot's softness and its versatility. It is why the grape is used to soften more tannic varieties such as Cabernet Sauvignon, which has high acidity and tannins. A light style can be drunk young and unoaked, while a richer style handles barrel ageing well.":"這種中等的結構解釋了梅洛的柔和與多才多藝。這就是為什麼它被用來柔化卡本內蘇維濃等單寧更多的品種，卡本內的酸度和單寧都很高。輕盈的風格可以趁年輕喝且不經橡木桶，較豐潤的風格則很能承受橡木桶陳年。","Which flavours are typical of Merlot made from just-ripe grapes?":"哪些風味是用剛成熟葡萄釀造的梅洛的典型特徵？","Strawberry, red plum and green bell pepper":"草莓、紅李和青椒","Cooked blackberry, black plum and liquorice":"煮過的黑莓、黑李和甘草","Black cherry, black pepper and leather":"黑櫻桃、黑胡椒和皮革","Just-ripe grapes give fresh red fruit and a herbaceous green bell pepper note.":"剛成熟的葡萄帶來新鮮的紅色水果和植物性的青椒氣息。","Merlot's profile depends on ripeness. Just-ripe grapes give light to medium-bodied wines with strawberry, red plum and green bell pepper. Riper grapes bring medium to full body and cooked black fruit such as blackberry and black plum. Blackcurrant and mint point instead to Cabernet Sauvignon, black pepper to Syrah.":"梅洛的風味特徵取決於成熟度。剛成熟的葡萄釀出酒體輕盈至中等、帶有草莓、紅李和青椒的酒。較成熟的葡萄則帶來中等至飽滿的酒體，以及黑莓和黑李等煮過的黑色水果。黑醋栗和薄荷則指向卡本內蘇維濃，黑胡椒指向希哈。","How can a grower in a moderate climate make a riper, fuller Merlot?":"溫和氣候的種植者如何釀出更成熟、更飽滿的梅洛？","By harvesting later":"更晚採收","By increasing yields":"提高產量","By using oak chips":"使用橡木片","By co-fermenting with Viognier":"與維歐尼耶共同發酵","Picking later lets the grapes ripen further, giving fuller body and cooked black fruit.":"較晚採收讓葡萄更成熟，帶來更飽滿的酒體和煮過的黑色水果。","Merlot's rich style, with medium to full body and cooked black fruit, comes from very ripe grapes. A warm climate delivers this easily, but in a moderate climate it can be reached by leaving the grapes on the vine longer. Oak adds flavour but does not make grapes riper, and higher yields would tend to work the other way.":"梅洛的豐潤風格，酒體中等至飽滿、帶有煮過的黑色水果，來自非常成熟的葡萄。溫暖的氣候很容易做到這一點，但在溫和氣候中，可以藉由讓葡萄在樹上留得更久來達成。橡木桶會增添風味，但不會讓葡萄更成熟，而提高產量往往會產生反效果。","Why is Merlot often blended with Cabernet Sauvignon?":"為什麼梅洛常與卡本內蘇維濃混調？","To lower tannins and make the wine ready sooner":"降低單寧，讓酒更早適飲","To raise acidity and lengthen the wine's life":"提高酸度，延長酒的壽命","To add black pepper and liquorice aromas":"增添黑胡椒和甘草香氣","To increase the blend's tannin and colour":"增加混調的單寧和顏色","With medium tannins, Merlot softens Cabernet and adds red fruit.":"單寧中等的梅洛能柔化卡本內，並增添紅色水果。","Cabernet Sauvignon has high tannin and acidity and can taste hard when young. Adding Merlot, with its medium tannins, lowers the overall tannin level and brings red fruit and softness, so the blend can be drunk earlier. In Bordeaux the share of Merlot also rises in years when Cabernet struggles to ripen.":"卡本內蘇維濃的單寧和酸度都很高，年輕時嚐起來可能很硬。加入單寧中等的梅洛，能降低整體的單寧水準，帶來紅色水果和柔和感，讓混調可以更早飲用。在波爾多，卡本內難以成熟的年份，梅洛的比例也會上升。","Which notes do the best Merlot-based wines develop with age?":"最好的梅洛酒款隨陳年會發展出哪些氣息？","Dried fruit and tobacco":"果乾和菸草","Strawberry and green bell pepper":"草莓和青椒","Black pepper and flowers":"黑胡椒和花香","With bottle age, top Merlot evolves towards dried fruit and tobacco.":"經過瓶中陳年，頂級梅洛會朝果乾和菸草演變。","Strawberry and green bell pepper are primary flavours from less ripe grapes, while vanilla and coconut come from new oak. Notes that appear over time are tertiary: in long-lived Merlot, such as the best Saint-Émilion and Pomerol, dried fruit and tobacco develop. Black pepper and floral notes point more to Côte-Rôtie Syrah.":"草莓和青椒是較不成熟葡萄的一級風味，而香草和椰子來自新橡木桶。隨時間出現的氣息是三級的：在長壽的梅洛中，例如最好的 Saint-Émilion 和 Pomerol，會發展出果乾和菸草。黑胡椒和花香則更指向 Côte-Rôtie 的希哈。","Which two appellations make Bordeaux's most famous Merlot-based wines?":"哪兩個法定產區出產波爾多最著名的梅洛酒款？","Haut-Médoc and Sauternes":"Haut-Médoc 和 Sauternes","Saint-Émilion and Pomerol lie on the Right Bank, where Merlot dominates.":"Saint-Émilion 和 Pomerol 位於以梅洛為主的右岸。","The other options are Left Bank appellations: Pauillac and Margaux lie within the Haut-Médoc and Pessac-Léognan within Graves, where Cabernet Sauvignon usually leads the blend. Saint-Émilion and Pomerol, on the Right Bank, give the most famous Merlot: full-bodied wines with intense black fruit and oak that can age for many years.":"其他選項都是左岸的法定產區：Pauillac 和 Margaux 位於 Haut-Médoc 之內，Pessac-Léognan 位於 Graves 之內，那裡通常以卡本內蘇維濃為混調的主導品種。右岸的 Saint-Émilion 和 Pomerol 出產最著名的梅洛：酒體飽滿、帶有濃郁黑色水果和橡木味、能陳年多年的酒。","Which estuary splits the Bordeaux region into Left Bank and Right Bank?":"哪一個河口把波爾多產區分為左岸和右岸？","Gironde":"吉倫特河口","The Gironde Estuary is formed where the Garonne and Dordogne meet.":"吉倫特河口由加隆河與多爾多涅河匯流而成。","The Gironde divides Bordeaux in two. West and south of the Gironde and Garonne is the Left Bank (Médoc, Graves, Sauternes), where Cabernet Sauvignon often dominates. North and east of the Gironde and Dordogne is the Right Bank (Saint-Émilion, Pomerol), Merlot country. The Rhône, Loire and Mosel flow through other regions.":"吉倫特河把波爾多一分為二。吉倫特河和加隆河以西和以南是左岸（Médoc、Graves、Sauternes），那裡常以卡本內蘇維濃為主。吉倫特河和多爾多涅河以北和以東是右岸（Saint-Émilion、Pomerol），是梅洛的天下。隆河、羅亞爾河和 Mosel 則流經其他產區。","What kind of climate does Bordeaux have?":"波爾多屬於什麼樣的氣候？","Moderate, with high rainfall from the Atlantic":"溫和，大西洋帶來大量降雨","Warm and dry, with steady Mediterranean summers":"溫暖乾燥，夏季是穩定的地中海型","Hot, with irrigated vineyards and very high yields":"炎熱，葡萄園經灌溉，產量非常高","Cool and cloudy, with southerly breezes slowing ripening":"涼爽多雲，南方微風減緩成熟","Closeness to the Atlantic gives Bordeaux a moderate, rainy climate.":"靠近大西洋讓波爾多屬於溫和多雨的氣候。","Bordeaux's moderate, damp climate changes a lot from one year to the next. That is why blending matters so much: the proportions of Merlot and Cabernet Sauvignon are adjusted to the style, the soils and each year's weather. The Languedoc, by contrast, is warm and more consistent, while California's Central Valley is hot and irrigated.":"波爾多溫和潮濕的氣候年年變化很大。這就是為什麼混調如此重要：梅洛和卡本內蘇維濃的比例會依風格、土壤和每年的天氣調整。相反地，Languedoc 溫暖而較穩定，加州的 Central Valley 則炎熱且經灌溉。","Which grape is the most widely planted in Bordeaux?":"波爾多種植最廣泛的品種是哪一個？","In Bordeaux, Merlot covers more vineyard area than even Cabernet Sauvignon.":"在波爾多，梅洛的種植面積甚至超過卡本內蘇維濃。","Cabernet Sauvignon is famous for the great Left Bank wines, but Merlot is the most widely grown grape across the whole region. It is the backbone of most Bordeaux AOC and Bordeaux Supérieur AOC wines and dominates on the Right Bank, in Saint-Émilion and Pomerol. Syrah and Grenache are linked instead to the Rhône and the south of France.":"卡本內蘇維濃以偉大的左岸酒款聞名，但梅洛才是整個產區種植最廣泛的品種。它是大多數 Bordeaux AOC 和 Bordeaux Supérieur AOC 酒款的骨幹，並在右岸的 Saint-Émilion 和 Pomerol 佔主導。希哈和格那希則與隆河和法國南部有關。","What is a red Bordeaux AOC or Bordeaux Supérieur AOC usually like?":"Bordeaux AOC 或 Bordeaux Supérieur AOC 紅酒通常是什麼樣子？","A Merlot-led blend from grapes grown anywhere in the region":"以梅洛為主、葡萄可來自產區任何地方的混調","A Cabernet-led blend from the Left Bank only":"只來自左岸、以卡本內為主的混調","A pure Merlot from Saint-Émilion and Pomerol only":"只來自 Saint-Émilion 和 Pomerol 的純梅洛","A Syrah-Grenache blend from riverside vineyards":"來自河畔葡萄園的希哈與格那希混調","These are regional appellations: grapes may come from all over Bordeaux, and Merlot leads.":"這些是地區級法定產區：葡萄可以來自波爾多各地，以梅洛為主。","Bordeaux AOC and Bordeaux Supérieur AOC cover the entire region, so they are not tied to one bank or village. Since Merlot is Bordeaux's most planted grape, these wines are usually blends led by it. Bordeaux Supérieur follows slightly stricter rules on yields, ageing and minimum alcohol.":"Bordeaux AOC 和 Bordeaux Supérieur AOC 涵蓋整個產區，所以不限於某一岸或某個村莊。由於梅洛是波爾多種植最多的品種，這些酒通常是以它為主的混調。Bordeaux Supérieur 在產量、陳年和最低酒精方面的規定稍嚴格一些。","How is Languedoc-Roussillon Merlot usually labelled?":"Languedoc-Roussillon 的梅洛通常如何標示？","Southern French Merlot, varietal or blended, is usually sold as Pays d'Oc IGP.":"法國南部的梅洛，無論單一品種或混調，通常以 Pays d'Oc IGP 出售。","Languedoc-Roussillon is warm and Merlot is widely planted there. You find varietal wines at every quality level and blends with Cabernet Sauvignon, Grenache and Syrah, usually labelled Pays d'Oc IGP. The other options are appellations from Bordeaux or the Northern Rhône, far from this region.":"Languedoc-Roussillon 很溫暖，梅洛在那裡廣泛種植。這裡有各個品質等級的單一品種酒，也有與卡本內蘇維濃、格那希和希哈的混調，通常標示為 Pays d'Oc IGP。其他選項都是遠離這個地區的波爾多或北隆河法定產區。","A medium-bodied red with soft, medium tannins, strawberry, red plum and a hint of green bell pepper. What is it most likely to be?":"一款酒體中等、單寧柔和中等、帶有草莓、紅李和一絲青椒的紅酒。它最可能是什麼？","Merlot from a moderate climate":"溫和氣候的梅洛","Napa Valley Cabernet Sauvignon":"Napa Valley 的卡本內蘇維濃","Barossa Valley Shiraz":"Barossa Valley 的希拉茲","Côte-Rôtie Syrah":"Côte-Rôtie 的希哈","Medium tannins and fresh red fruit with green pepper point to just-ripe Merlot.":"中等的單寧和帶青椒的新鮮紅色水果，指向剛成熟的梅洛。","Napa Valley Cabernet is full-bodied with ripe black fruit and high tannins. Barossa Shiraz is full-bodied with cooked black fruit and black pepper. Côte-Rôtie Syrah is spicy and peppery. Only Merlot from just-ripe grapes combines medium body, medium tannins, strawberry, red plum and herbaceous green bell pepper.":"Napa Valley 的卡本內酒體飽滿，帶有成熟的黑色水果和高單寧。Barossa 的希拉茲酒體飽滿，帶有煮過的黑色水果和黑胡椒。Côte-Rôtie 的希哈辛香帶胡椒味。只有用剛成熟葡萄釀的梅洛，結合了中等酒體、中等單寧、草莓、紅李和植物性的青椒。","Which oak flavours are often pronounced in Californian reds?":"加州紅酒中常有哪些明顯的橡木風味？","Leather, meat and earth":"皮革、肉和泥土","Liquorice, black pepper and herbs":"甘草、黑胡椒和香草植物","Vanilla, coconut and smoke are typical secondary flavours from oak, often new, in California.":"香草、椰子和煙燻是加州常見的、來自橡木桶（常是新桶）的典型二級風味。","In Californian reds, Merlot included, oak often leaves a clear mark. Very good or outstanding wines are frequently aged in new barrels, while high-volume producers get similar flavours from oak chips or staves. Leather, meat and earth are notes of bottle age; strawberry and bell pepper are primary flavours.":"在加州紅酒中，包括梅洛，橡木常留下清楚的印記。非常好或傑出的酒款常在新橡木桶中陳年，而大量生產的生產者則用橡木片或橡木條取得類似的風味。皮革、肉和泥土是瓶中陳年的氣息；草莓和甜椒是一級風味。","How do high-volume Californian producers often give their wines oak flavour?":"加州大量生產的生產者常如何為酒增添橡木風味？","With oak chips or staves":"用橡木片或橡木條","With years in new barrels":"在新橡木桶中放數年","With long bottle ageing":"長時間瓶中陳年","By co-fermenting white grapes":"與白葡萄共同發酵","Chips and staves give oak flavour far more cheaply than barrels.":"橡木片和橡木條帶來橡木風味的成本比橡木桶低得多。","New barrels are expensive and are mostly kept for very good or outstanding wines. For high-volume wines meant to be drunk young, producers use alternatives such as oak chips or staves, which add vanilla, coconut and smoke cheaply. Bottle ageing develops tertiary notes, not oak flavours.":"新橡木桶很昂貴，大多保留給非常好或傑出的酒款。對於要趁年輕喝的大量生產酒款，生產者使用橡木片或橡木條等替代品，以低成本增添香草、椰子和煙燻。瓶中陳年發展的是三級氣息，不是橡木風味。","Where do California's most concentrated, full-bodied Merlots come from?":"加州最濃縮、酒體最飽滿的梅洛來自哪裡？","Napa Valley and Sonoma":"Napa Valley 和 Sonoma","The statewide Central Valley":"全州性的 Central Valley","Hunter Valley and Barossa Valley":"Hunter Valley 和 Barossa Valley","Maipo Valley and Colchagua Valley":"Maipo Valley 和 Colchagua Valley","The neighbouring regions of Napa Valley and Sonoma give California's most concentrated Merlot.":"相鄰的 Napa Valley 和 Sonoma 產區出產加州最濃縮的梅洛。","In California, Merlot styles run from fruity, medium-bodied wines labelled California, often from the hot Central Valley, to full, concentrated wines from Napa Valley and Sonoma. Hunter Valley and Barossa are Australian regions linked to Shiraz, while Maipo and Colchagua are Chilean valleys known for Cabernet Sauvignon.":"在加州，梅洛的風格從常來自炎熱 Central Valley、標示 California 的果香豐富、酒體中等的酒，到來自 Napa Valley 和 Sonoma 的飽滿濃縮酒款都有。Hunter Valley 和 Barossa 是與希拉茲相關的澳洲產區，而 Maipo 和 Colchagua 是以卡本內蘇維濃著稱的智利山谷。","Why does Chile's Central Valley suit high-volume Merlot?":"為什麼智利的 Central Valley 適合大量生產的梅洛？","Its warm, dry climate ripens high yields every year":"溫暖乾燥的氣候讓高產量的葡萄每年都能成熟","Cloud cover and sea breezes slow ripening":"雲層和海風減緩成熟","Gravel soils hold heat into the evening":"礫石土壤把熱量保持到傍晚","Steep slopes force hand harvesting":"陡坡迫使人工採收","The warm, dry climate brings plenty of ripe fruit every year, ideal for soft branded wines.":"溫暖乾燥的氣候每年都帶來大量成熟的果實，非常適合柔和的品牌酒。","In the Central Valley, Merlot easily reaches full ripeness even at high yields, and does so reliably year after year. The result is soft, medium-bodied Merlot for high-volume brands to drink young. Where altitude tempers the heat, fresher styles are made too. The other options describe the Hunter Valley, Bordeaux and the Northern Rhône.":"在 Central Valley，梅洛即使在高產量下也很容易完全成熟，而且年年穩定。結果是柔和、酒體中等、適合大量生產品牌且要趁年輕喝的梅洛。在海拔緩和高溫的地方，也能釀出較清爽的風格。其他選項描述的是 Hunter Valley、波爾多和北隆河。","In Chile, what allows fresher styles of Merlot to be made?":"在智利，是什麼讓較清爽的梅洛風格成為可能？","The moderating effect of altitude":"海拔的調節作用","Irrigating valley-floor vineyards":"灌溉谷底的葡萄園","A later harvest":"較晚採收","The use of oak chips":"使用橡木片","Higher up, temperatures drop, so Merlot keeps more freshness.":"海拔越高，溫度越低，所以梅洛能保留更多清新感。","Chile's Central Valley is warm and dry, perfect for ripe, soft Merlot. Vineyards higher up, however, enjoy milder temperatures, which allows a fresher style. A later harvest would instead give riper grapes, and oak chips only add oak flavour, so neither helps to keep the wine fresh.":"智利的 Central Valley 溫暖乾燥，非常適合成熟柔和的梅洛。不過，海拔較高的葡萄園溫度較溫和，能釀出較清爽的風格。較晚採收反而會讓葡萄更成熟，而橡木片只會增添橡木風味，兩者都無助於保持酒的清新。","What makes Stellenbosch's climate range from moderate to warm?":"是什麼讓 Stellenbosch 的氣候從溫和到溫暖？","Vineyard altitude and sea breezes":"葡萄園的海拔和海風","Gravel soils and winter rain":"礫石土壤和冬季降雨","Cloud cover and cool southerly winds":"雲層和涼爽的南風","South-facing slopes and river nearby":"朝南的坡地和附近的河流","Stellenbosch is mountainous: altitude and sea breezes make sites cooler or warmer.":"Stellenbosch 多山：海拔和海風讓各園地較涼爽或較溫暖。","Stellenbosch is a mountainous South African region known for complex, age-worthy reds from Bordeaux varieties such as Merlot and Cabernet Sauvignon. Its climate ranges from moderate to warm depending on vineyard altitude and the influence of sea breezes. Cloud and southerly winds describe Coonawarra instead, and gravel is typical of the Left Bank.":"Stellenbosch 是南非多山的產區，以梅洛和卡本內蘇維濃等波爾多品種釀出的複雜、適合陳年的紅酒著稱。它的氣候依葡萄園海拔和海風影響，從溫和到溫暖。雲層和南風描述的則是 Coonawarra，而礫石是左岸的典型特徵。","Which region produces most of New Zealand's Merlot?":"哪個產區出產紐西蘭大部分的梅洛？","Hawke's Bay, on the North Island, is New Zealand's main source of Merlot.":"北島的 Hawke's Bay 是紐西蘭梅洛的主要來源。","Hawke's Bay has a moderate climate with plenty of rain. Merlot is grown more widely there than Cabernet Sauvignon and makes wines from light and fruity to full-bodied and long-lived, alone or blended with Cabernet. Marlborough, Central Otago and Martinborough are New Zealand regions linked more to other grapes.":"Hawke's Bay 屬於溫和氣候，雨量充沛。梅洛在那裡的種植比卡本內蘇維濃更廣，單獨或與卡本內混調，釀出從輕盈果香到飽滿長壽的各種酒。Marlborough、Central Otago 和 Martinborough 是與其他品種較相關的紐西蘭產區。","How has Merlot traditionally been used in Margaret River?":"在 Margaret River，梅洛傳統上如何使用？","Blended with Cabernet Sauvignon in quality wines":"在優質酒款中與卡本內蘇維濃混調","For sparkling reds labelled South Eastern Australia":"用於標示 South Eastern Australia 的氣泡紅酒","Co-fermented with Viognier for floral notes":"與維歐尼耶共同發酵以增添花香","Blended with Pinotage to make a Cape Blend":"與皮諾塔吉混調釀成 Cape Blend","In Australia Merlot traditionally partners Cabernet in high-quality wines, as in Margaret River.":"在澳洲，梅洛傳統上是優質酒款中卡本內的搭檔，例如在 Margaret River。","Margaret River in Western Australia is known for high-quality wines based on Cabernet Sauvignon, to which Merlot is often added. Co-fermenting with Viognier is a Côte-Rôtie tradition, the Cape Blend with Pinotage is South African, and the South Eastern Australia label is mainly used for high-volume Shiraz.":"西澳的 Margaret River 以卡本內蘇維濃為基礎的高品質酒款著稱，常會加入梅洛。與維歐尼耶共同發酵是 Côte-Rôtie 的傳統，與皮諾塔吉的 Cape Blend 是南非的，而 South Eastern Australia 標示主要用於大量生產的希拉茲。","Which statement about Merlot today is correct?":"關於今天的梅洛，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","On its own it can make complex, age-worthy wines":"它單獨就能釀出複雜、適合陳年的酒","It is only used for branded wines to drink young":"它只用於要趁年輕喝的品牌酒","It needs blending to have enough tannin":"它需要混調才有足夠的單寧","It cannot handle oak maturation":"它承受不了橡木桶熟成","Many producers now show that varietal Merlot can be complex and age-worthy.":"現在許多生產者證明，單一品種的梅洛可以複雜且適合陳年。","In the past Merlot was mostly seen as a grape for branded wines or blending. Today producers across the world make complex, long-lived varietal wines from it. With medium tannins and acidity it is very versatile: it suits fresh unoaked wines as well as powerful wines that improve with oak and bottle age.":"過去梅洛大多被視為品牌酒或混調用的品種。今天世界各地的生產者用它釀出複雜、長壽的單一品種酒。酸度和單寧都中等的它非常多才多藝：既適合清爽、不經橡木桶的酒，也適合經橡木桶和瓶中陳年而變好的強勁酒款。","Where is Merlot's homeland?":"梅洛的故鄉在哪裡？","Napa Valley, in California":"加州的 Napa Valley","Merlot comes from Bordeaux, from where it spread worldwide.":"梅洛（Merlot）來自波爾多，並從那裡傳遍世界。","Bordeaux, in south-west France, is its classic home, where it is now the most planted grape. Napa Valley makes excellent examples but is not its origin; the Northern Rhône and Burgundy are home to Syrah and Pinot Noir.":"法國西南部的波爾多是它的經典故鄉，現在也是那裡種植最多的品種。Napa Valley 出產優秀的酒款，但不是它的發源地；北隆河和布根地是希哈和黑皮諾的故鄉。","In which climates does Merlot grow?":"梅洛生長在哪些氣候中？","Moderate and warm":"溫和和溫暖","Only cool ones, near the limit of vine growing":"只在涼爽、接近葡萄種植極限的地方","Only very hot, irrigated ones":"只在非常炎熱、經灌溉的地方","Only cool, foggy ones":"只在涼爽多霧的地方","Merlot grows well in moderate and warm climates.":"梅洛在溫和和溫暖氣候中都長得很好。","In moderate climates such as Bordeaux it gives fresher styles; in warm ones it easily reaches full ripeness. It is not limited to cool or foggy places, nor only to very hot irrigated ones.":"在波爾多等溫和氣候中，它釀出較清爽的風格；在溫暖氣候中，它很容易完全成熟。它不限於涼爽或多霧的地方，也不只限於非常炎熱、經灌溉的地方。","Which rivers meet to form the Gironde Estuary?":"哪兩條河匯流形成吉倫特河口？","Garonne and Dordogne":"加隆河和多爾多涅河","Rhône and Saône, before reaching the sea":"隆河和索恩河，在入海之前","Loire and Seine":"羅亞爾河和塞納河","Mosel and Rhine":"Mosel 河和萊茵河","The Gironde forms where the Garonne and Dordogne meet.":"吉倫特河由加隆河和多爾多涅河匯流而成。","This estuary splits Bordeaux into Left and Right Banks. The Rhône and Saône lie further east, the Loire and Seine to the north, and the Mosel and Rhine mainly concern Germany.":"這個河口把波爾多分為左岸和右岸。隆河和索恩河在更東邊，羅亞爾河和塞納河在北邊，而 Mosel 河和萊茵河主要與德國有關。","Which Bordeaux districts lie on the Left Bank?":"波爾多哪些地區位於左岸？","Médoc, Graves and Sauternes":"Médoc、Graves 和 Sauternes","Hermitage, Crozes-Hermitage and Côte-Rôtie":"Hermitage、Crozes-Hermitage 和 Côte-Rôtie","Chablis, Côte de Nuits and Côte de Beaune":"Chablis、Côte de Nuits 和 Côte de Beaune","West and south of the Gironde and Garonne lie the Médoc, Graves and Sauternes.":"吉倫特河和加隆河以西和以南是 Médoc、Graves 和 Sauternes。","Cabernet Sauvignon generally leads here. Saint-Émilion and Pomerol form the Merlot-led Right Bank. The other two sets of names belong to the Northern Rhône and Burgundy.":"這裡一般以卡本內蘇維濃為主。Saint-Émilion 和 Pomerol 構成以梅洛為主的右岸。另外兩組名稱屬於北隆河和布根地。","A Merlot has medium to full body with cooked blackberry and black plum. What grapes was it most likely made from?":"一款梅洛酒體中等至飽滿，帶有煮過的黑莓和黑李。它最可能用什麼樣的葡萄釀造？","Riper grapes, from a warm climate or later harvest":"較成熟的葡萄，來自溫暖氣候或較晚採收","Just-ripe grapes, picked early":"剛成熟、提早採收的葡萄","Fuller body and cooked black fruit point to riper Merlot grapes.":"較飽滿的酒體和煮過的黑色水果，指向較成熟的梅洛葡萄。","The ripe style comes easily in warm climates, or by picking later in a moderate one. Just-ripe grapes give light to medium body, strawberry, red plum and green bell pepper. Frozen or botrytised grapes are for sweet wines.":"在溫暖氣候中，或在溫和氣候中較晚採收，都很容易得到成熟的風格。剛成熟的葡萄帶來輕盈至中等的酒體、草莓、紅李和青椒。冰凍或貴腐葡萄是用來釀甜酒的。","Which style of Merlot benefits most from oak maturation?":"哪一種風格的梅洛最受益於橡木桶熟成？","The fuller-bodied style":"酒體較飽滿的風格","The light, fruity style for drinking now":"適合現在喝的輕盈果香風格","High-volume sparkling Merlot":"大量生產的氣泡梅洛","Rosé Merlot from just-ripe, early-picked grapes":"用剛成熟、提早採收的葡萄釀的粉紅梅洛","A fuller Merlot gains softness and complexity from oak.":"較飽滿的梅洛能從橡木桶獲得柔和感和複雜度。","Merlot is made both oaked and unoaked: the light, fruity style has little need for long barrel ageing, which would mask its fresh fruit. The fuller style has the structure and concentration to carry oak.":"梅洛有經橡木桶和不經橡木桶的版本：輕盈果香的風格不太需要長時間的橡木桶陳年，那會掩蓋它新鮮的果味。較飽滿的風格則有足以承載橡木的結構和濃縮度。","Which flavour does Merlot bring to a blend with Cabernet Sauvignon?":"在與卡本內蘇維濃的混調中，梅洛帶來什麼風味？","Red fruit":"紅色水果","Black pepper and liquorice, typical of warm climates":"黑胡椒和甘草，溫暖氣候的典型特徵","Mint and cedar":"薄荷和雪松","Floral rose notes":"玫瑰花香","Merlot adds red-fruit flavours and lowers the blend's tannin.":"梅洛增添紅色水果風味，並降低混調的單寧。","This makes the wine ready sooner. Black pepper and liquorice are Syrah traits; mint belongs to Cabernet and cedar comes from oak; rose is typical of aromatic grapes such as Gewurztraminer.":"這讓酒更早適飲。黑胡椒和甘草是希哈的特徵；薄荷屬於卡本內，雪松來自橡木；玫瑰則是格烏茲塔明那等芳香型品種的典型特徵。","What is an outstanding young Saint-Émilion or Pomerol like?":"傑出的年輕 Saint-Émilion 或 Pomerol 是什麼樣子？","Full body, pronounced black fruit, oak notes":"酒體飽滿、濃郁的黑色水果、橡木氣息","Light, with fresh strawberry and no oak":"輕盈，帶新鮮草莓，沒有橡木味","Black pepper and Viognier flowers":"黑胡椒和維歐尼耶的花香","Sweet, with apricot and honey":"甜，帶有杏桃和蜂蜜","The best Saint-Émilion and Pomerol wines are full, with intense black fruit and oak.":"最好的 Saint-Émilion 和 Pomerol 酒款飽滿，帶有濃郁的黑色水果和橡木味。","These Merlot-led blends develop dried fruit and tobacco with time. The light, fresh style describes simpler Merlot; black pepper and Viognier point to Côte-Rôtie, apricot and honey to sweet wines.":"這些以梅洛為主的混調隨時間發展出果乾和菸草。輕盈清新的風格描述的是較簡單的梅洛；黑胡椒和維歐尼耶指向 Côte-Rôtie，杏桃和蜂蜜則指向甜酒。","A label reads Saint-Émilion Grand Cru AOC. What does it tell you?":"一張酒標上寫著 Saint-Émilion Grand Cru AOC。它告訴你什麼？","The more prestigious appellation within Saint-Émilion":"Saint-Émilion 之內較具聲望的法定產區","A single Burgundy grand cru vineyard with its own AOC":"擁有自己 AOC 的單一布根地 grand cru 葡萄園","A Cabernet-led wine from the Médoc":"來自 Médoc、以卡本內為主的酒","A sweet wine from botrytised grapes":"用貴腐葡萄釀的甜酒","Saint-Émilion Grand Cru AOC is the more prestigious appellation within Saint-Émilion AOC.":"Saint-Émilion Grand Cru AOC 是 Saint-Émilion AOC 之內較具聲望的法定產區。","This is the Right Bank, where Merlot is the key grape. Here Grand Cru does not mean a single vineyard as in Burgundy; the Médoc is on the Cabernet-led Left Bank, and this is not a sweet wine.":"這是右岸，梅洛是這裡的關鍵品種。在這裡，Grand Cru 並不像布根地那樣代表單一葡萄園；Médoc 位於以卡本內為主的左岸，而這也不是甜酒。","What role does Merlot usually play in Left Bank wines?":"梅洛在左岸酒款中通常扮演什麼角色？","It is part of the blend, but Cabernet leads":"它是混調的一部分，但以卡本內為主","It is always the leading grape, as in Pomerol":"它總是主導品種，就像在 Pomerol","It is banned by the rules":"法規禁止使用它","It is used only for the district's rosés, never for reds":"它只用於這個地區的粉紅酒，從不用於紅酒","On the Left Bank Merlot is usually present, but Cabernet is dominant.":"在左岸，梅洛通常會出現，但卡本內佔主導。","The Left Bank gravels favour Cabernet, and in difficult years the Merlot share can rise. Merlot leads on the Right Bank instead; it is neither banned nor limited to rosé.":"左岸的礫石有利於卡本內，在困難的年份梅洛的比例可能上升。梅洛則在右岸佔主導；它既沒有被禁止，也不只限於粉紅酒。","In Bordeaux, besides the intended style, what affects the blend's proportions?":"在波爾多，除了想要的風格，還有什麼影響混調的比例？","Soil types and each year's weather":"土壤類型和每年的天氣","A fixed share required by law every year across the region":"法律規定全區每年固定的比例","The age of the barrels used":"使用的橡木桶的年齡","The colour of the chosen bottle":"所選酒瓶的顏色","Soils and the year's weather weigh heavily on the proportions.":"土壤和當年的天氣對比例影響很大。","Gravel favours Cabernet, other soils Merlot; and in cool years, when Cabernet ripens poorly, the Merlot share rises. There is no fixed share for the whole region, and barrels or bottles do not decide the blend.":"礫石有利於卡本內，其他土壤有利於梅洛；而在卡本內成熟不佳的涼爽年份，梅洛的比例會上升。全區沒有固定的比例，橡木桶或酒瓶也不會決定混調。","In Languedoc-Roussillon, which grapes is Merlot often blended with?":"在 Languedoc-Roussillon，梅洛常與哪些品種混調？","Cabernet Sauvignon, Grenache and Syrah":"卡本內蘇維濃、格那希和希哈","Chardonnay and Viognier":"夏多內和維歐尼耶","Riesling, Pinot Gris and Gewurztraminer":"麗絲玲、灰皮諾和格烏茲塔明那","In France's warm south Merlot is blended with Cabernet, Grenache and Syrah.":"在法國溫暖的南部，梅洛與卡本內、格那希和希哈混調。","Single-varietal Merlot is also found here at every quality level, usually as Pays d'Oc IGP. Pinotage and Carmenère are South African and Chilean specialities; the others are white grapes.":"這裡也有各個品質等級的單一品種梅洛，通常標示為 Pays d'Oc IGP。皮諾塔吉和卡門內爾是南非和智利的特色品種；其他都是白葡萄。","What style can you expect from a Merlot labelled simply California?":"只標示 California 的梅洛，你可以預期什麼風格？","Fruity and medium-bodied":"果香豐富，酒體中等","Very concentrated, full-bodied and long-lived":"非常濃縮、酒體飽滿、長壽","Sweet, from grapes frozen on the vine":"甜，用在樹上結冰的葡萄釀造","Sparkling rosé":"粉紅氣泡酒","In California, Merlot labelled just California is usually fruity and medium-bodied.":"在加州，只標示 California 的梅洛通常果香豐富、酒體中等。","Concentrated, full-bodied examples come mainly from Napa Valley and Sonoma, which appear on the label. Wines from frozen grapes and sparkling rosé are not the typical style under this name.":"濃縮、酒體飽滿的酒款主要來自 Napa Valley 和 Sonoma，並會在酒標上標示。用冰凍葡萄釀的酒和粉紅氣泡酒不是這個名稱下的典型風格。","In California, how are very good or outstanding reds often matured?":"在加州，非常好或傑出的紅酒常如何熟成？","In new barrels":"在新橡木桶中","Only in steel tanks with no oak contact at all":"只在完全不接觸橡木的不鏽鋼槽中","With oak chips added to the tank":"在槽中加入橡木片","In buried clay amphorae":"在埋入地下的陶甕中","The best Californian reds often spend time in new barrels.":"最好的加州紅酒常在新橡木桶中度過一段時間。","Hence the pronounced vanilla, coconut and smoke of many Californian reds. Chips or staves are the cheaper option of high-volume producers; steel and amphorae do not explain these oak notes.":"因此許多加州紅酒帶有明顯的香草、椰子和煙燻。橡木片或橡木條是大量生產者較便宜的選擇；不鏽鋼槽和陶甕都無法解釋這些橡木氣息。","A buyer wants large volumes of soft, medium-bodied Merlot, ripe every year and ready to drink. Which source suits best?":"一位買家想要大量柔和、酒體中等、每年都成熟且已經適飲的梅洛。哪個來源最合適？","Pomerol AOC, from the Right Bank's most famous estates":"Pomerol AOC，來自右岸最著名的酒莊","High-altitude vineyards in the Andes":"安地斯山脈的高海拔葡萄園","The warm, dry Central Valley gives high yields of ripe Merlot every year for big brands.":"溫暖乾燥的 Central Valley 每年都為大品牌提供高產量的成熟梅洛。","It is the classic source of soft Merlot for drinking now. Pomerol and Saint-Émilion Grand Cru make expensive, age-worthy wines; high-altitude vineyards are used for fresher styles, not for steady, soft volume.":"這是適合現在喝的柔和梅洛的經典來源。Pomerol 和 Saint-Émilion Grand Cru 出產昂貴、適合陳年的酒；高海拔葡萄園用於較清爽的風格，而不是穩定、柔和的大量供應。","What has Stellenbosch built a strong reputation for?":"Stellenbosch 以什麼建立了良好的名聲？","Complex, age-worthy reds from Bordeaux grapes":"以波爾多品種釀出的複雜、適合陳年的紅酒","Sweet wines from grapes frozen on the vine":"用在樹上結冰的葡萄釀的甜酒","Light whites for drinking young, made from very cool-climate Riesling":"用極涼爽氣候的麗絲玲釀造、要趁年輕喝的輕盈白酒","Light Pinot Noir reds":"輕盈的黑皮諾紅酒","Stellenbosch is known for complex, age-worthy reds from the classic Bordeaux grapes.":"Stellenbosch 以經典波爾多品種釀出的複雜、適合陳年的紅酒著稱。","A mountainous region whose climate runs from moderate to warm with altitude and sea breezes, it does well with Merlot and Cabernet Sauvignon. The other styles are not what built its name.":"這是一個多山的產區，氣候依海拔和海風從溫和到溫暖，梅洛和卡本內蘇維濃在這裡表現很好。其他風格都不是讓它成名的原因。","Where is Hawke's Bay, New Zealand's main Merlot region?":"紐西蘭主要的梅洛產區 Hawke's Bay 在哪裡？","On the North Island":"在北島","In the far south of the South Island, among mountains":"在南島最南端的群山之間","On the South African coast":"在南非海岸","Hawke's Bay lies on New Zealand's North Island.":"Hawke's Bay 位於紐西蘭北島。","It has a moderate, rainy climate and gives Merlot from light and fruity to full and long-lived, alone or with Cabernet. The mountainous south of the South Island is Central Otago, Pinot Noir country; Western Australia is home to Margaret River.":"它屬於溫和多雨的氣候，出產從輕盈果香到飽滿長壽的梅洛，單獨或與卡本內一起。南島多山的南部是 Central Otago，黑皮諾的天下；西澳則是 Margaret River 的所在地。","Why is Merlot considered such a versatile grape?":"為什麼梅洛被視為如此多才多藝的品種？","Medium tannin and acidity suit both unoaked and oaked styles":"中等的單寧和酸度，同時適合不經橡木桶和經橡木桶的風格","It has very high acidity, mostly for sparkling wine":"它的酸度非常高，主要用於氣泡酒","It is a white grape that can also make very light reds":"它是也能釀出非常輕盈紅酒的白葡萄","It grows only in cold climates":"它只生長在寒冷氣候中","Thanks to medium tannin and acidity, Merlot makes both fresh unoaked reds and powerful oak-aged wines.":"由於單寧和酸度中等，梅洛既能釀出清爽、不經橡木桶的紅酒，也能釀出強勁、經橡木桶陳年的酒。","It ranges from light wines for drinking now to concentrated ones that improve in barrel and bottle, at all quality levels. It is neither a white nor a sparkling-wine grape, and it grows in moderate and warm climates.":"它的範圍從適合現在喝的輕盈酒款，到在橡木桶和瓶中變好的濃縮酒款，涵蓋所有品質等級。它既不是白葡萄，也不是氣泡酒品種，而且生長在溫和和溫暖的氣候中。","Which of these wines is most likely Cabernet-led rather than Merlot-led?":"下列哪一款酒最可能以卡本內而非梅洛為主？","Bordeaux Supérieur AOC, from grapes across the region":"Bordeaux Supérieur AOC，用來自全區的葡萄","Pauillac is in the Haut-Médoc on the Left Bank: Cabernet-led blends.":"Pauillac 位於左岸的 Haut-Médoc：以卡本內為主的混調。","Pomerol and Saint-Émilion Grand Cru are Merlot-led Right Bank wines. Bordeaux and Bordeaux Supérieur AOC are also usually Merlot-led, as it is the region's most planted grape.":"Pomerol 和 Saint-Émilion Grand Cru 是以梅洛為主的右岸酒款。Bordeaux 和 Bordeaux Supérieur AOC 通常也以梅洛為主，因為它是這個產區種植最多的品種。","A producer picks Merlot just ripe. What body will the wine probably have?":"一位生產者在梅洛剛成熟時採收。這款酒可能有什麼樣的酒體？","Light to medium":"輕盈至中等","Full and very alcoholic, with cooked black fruit and liquorice":"飽滿且酒精很高，帶有煮過的黑色水果和甘草","Full and sweet":"飽滿而甜","Heavy and tannic like a young Cabernet":"厚重且單寧多，就像年輕的卡本內","Just-ripe Merlot grapes give light- to medium-bodied wines.":"剛成熟的梅洛葡萄釀出酒體輕盈至中等的酒。","These wines show fresh red fruit and often a hint of green bell pepper. Full body, cooked fruit and high alcohol come from riper grapes; Merlot has medium tannins, not high ones like Cabernet, and is a dry wine.":"這些酒展現新鮮的紅色水果，常帶一絲青椒。飽滿的酒體、煮過的果味和高酒精來自較成熟的葡萄；梅洛的單寧中等，不像卡本內那麼高，而且它是不甜的酒。","What is the relationship between Syrah and Shiraz?":"Syrah 和 Shiraz 是什麼關係？","They are two names for the same grape":"它們是同一個品種的兩個名稱","They are two different but related grapes":"它們是兩個不同但相關的品種","Shiraz is a cross of Syrah and Grenache":"Shiraz 是 Syrah 和格那希的雜交種","Syrah is the white version of Shiraz":"Syrah 是 Shiraz 的白葡萄版本","Syrah is the French name, Shiraz the one mostly used in Australia: same grape.":"Syrah 是法文名稱，Shiraz 是澳洲最常用的名稱：同一個品種。","Syrah and Shiraz are the same black grape. France uses Syrah, while Australia usually says Shiraz. Outside these two countries, the name a producer chooses can hint at the style: Syrah suggests a fresher, peppery wine in the Northern Rhône mould, Shiraz a riper, fuller wine like those from warm Australia.":"Syrah（希哈）和 Shiraz（希拉茲）是同一個黑葡萄品種。法國使用 Syrah，而澳洲通常稱為 Shiraz。在這兩個國家以外，生產者選擇的名稱可以暗示風格：Syrah 暗示北隆河式較清爽、帶胡椒味的酒，Shiraz 暗示像溫暖澳洲那樣更成熟、更飽滿的酒。","Outside France and Australia, what does the choice of Syrah or Shiraz on a label usually suggest?":"在法國和澳洲以外，酒標上選擇 Syrah 或 Shiraz 通常暗示什麼？","The style of the wine":"酒的風格","The legal quality level":"法定的品質等級","Syrah points to a fresh, peppery style, Shiraz to a riper, richer one.":"Syrah 指向清爽、帶胡椒味的風格，Shiraz 指向更成熟、更豐潤的風格。","The classic Syrah style, in the Northern Rhône, is medium-bodied with fresh black fruit, herbal notes and black pepper. Shiraz from warm parts of Australia is full-bodied and high in alcohol, with cooked black fruit and liquorice. So when a producer elsewhere chooses one name or the other, it gives consumers a clue about the wine's style.":"經典的 Syrah 風格在北隆河，酒體中等，帶有新鮮的黑色水果、草本氣息和黑胡椒。來自澳洲溫暖地區的 Shiraz 酒體飽滿、酒精高，帶有煮過的黑色水果和甘草。所以當其他地方的生產者選擇其中一個名稱時，就給了消費者關於酒款風格的線索。","Which aroma is most characteristic of Syrah/Shiraz?":"哪一種香氣最能代表希哈／希拉茲？","Black pepper":"黑胡椒","Black pepper is Syrah/Shiraz's signature aroma, along with black fruit.":"黑胡椒是希哈／希拉茲的招牌香氣，再加上黑色水果。","Syrah/Shiraz is known for black fruit and a typical black pepper aroma, especially clear in moderate-climate styles such as the Northern Rhône. Green bell pepper is linked to less ripe Merlot and Cabernet, strawberry to just-ripe Merlot, and mint to Cabernet Sauvignon, for example from Coonawarra.":"希哈／希拉茲以黑色水果和典型的黑胡椒香氣著稱，在北隆河等溫和氣候的風格中尤其明顯。青椒與較不成熟的梅洛和卡本內有關，草莓與剛成熟的梅洛有關，而薄荷則與卡本內蘇維濃有關，例如來自 Coonawarra 的。","Which style is typical of moderate-climate Syrah?":"哪一種風格是溫和氣候希哈的典型特徵？","Medium body, fresh black fruit, herbs and black pepper":"酒體中等、新鮮的黑色水果、香草植物和黑胡椒","Full body, cooked black fruit, liquorice and high alcohol":"酒體飽滿、煮過的黑色水果、甘草和高酒精","Light body, strawberry, red plum and bell pepper":"酒體輕盈、草莓、紅李和甜椒","Full body, blackcurrant, mint and cedar":"酒體飽滿、黑醋栗、薄荷和雪松","In a moderate climate Syrah is medium-bodied, with fresh black fruit, herbal notes and black pepper.":"在溫和氣候中，希哈酒體中等，帶有新鮮的黑色水果、草本氣息和黑胡椒。","A cooler climate means slower ripening: the wine stays medium-bodied and shows fresh black fruit such as black cherry and blackberry, herbal notes and black pepper. This is the classic Northern Rhône style. In a warm climate, Shiraz becomes full-bodied and high in alcohol, with cooked fruit and liquorice, as in Australia's warmer areas.":"較涼爽的氣候代表成熟較慢：酒保持中等酒體，展現黑櫻桃和黑莓等新鮮的黑色水果、草本氣息和黑胡椒。這是經典的北隆河風格。在溫暖氣候中，希拉茲變得酒體飽滿、酒精高，帶有煮過的果味和甘草，就像澳洲較溫暖的地區。","Why is warm-climate Shiraz full-bodied, alcoholic and full of cooked black fruit?":"為什麼溫暖氣候的希拉茲酒體飽滿、酒精高、充滿煮過的黑色水果？","Heat brings the grapes to full ripeness, with more sugar":"高溫讓葡萄完全成熟，糖分更多","High yields concentrate sugars and flavours":"高產量濃縮了糖分和風味","Co-fermenting with Viognier raises alcohol":"與維歐尼耶共同發酵提高了酒精","New oak adds alcohol and body":"新橡木桶增添酒精和酒體","More heat means riper grapes: more sugar, so more alcohol and body, and cooked fruit.":"熱量越多葡萄越成熟：糖分更多，因此酒精和酒體更多，還有煮過的果味。","The chain is climate, ripeness, style. In a warm climate Syrah/Shiraz ripens fully: more sugar turns into more alcohol during fermentation and the wine gains body, while flavours shift from fresh to cooked black fruit and liquorice. Oak adds flavour and softens tannins, but it does not add alcohol.":"這條因果鏈是氣候、成熟度、風格。在溫暖氣候中，希哈／希拉茲完全成熟：更多的糖在發酵時轉化為更多的酒精，酒的酒體也更飽滿，同時風味從新鮮轉向煮過的黑色水果和甘草。橡木桶會增添風味並柔化單寧，但不會增加酒精。","What does Syrah bring when used in a blend?":"希哈用於混調時帶來什麼？","Colour, black fruit and tannin":"顏色、黑色水果和單寧","Freshness, red fruit and softness":"清新感、紅色水果和柔和感","Floral aromas and low acidity":"花香和低酸度","Sweetness and mint notes":"甜味和薄荷氣息","Thanks to its thick skins, Syrah gives a blend colour, black fruit and tannin.":"由於果皮厚，希哈為混調帶來顏色、黑色水果和單寧。","Syrah has small, thick-skinned berries, so it is rich in colour and tannin. In blends it brings exactly these, along with black fruit. Its most common partner is Grenache, with other Southern Rhône grapes, in what are called Rhône blends. The floral aromas in Côte-Rôtie come from Viognier instead.":"希哈的果粒小、果皮厚，所以富含顏色和單寧。在混調中，它帶來的正是這些，再加上黑色水果。它最常見的搭檔是格那希，以及其他南隆河品種，這類酒稱為隆河混調。Côte-Rôtie 的花香則來自維歐尼耶。","Which grape is Syrah most commonly blended with in Rhône blends?":"在隆河混調中，希哈最常與哪個品種混調？","Syrah is mostly blended with Grenache and other Southern Rhône grapes.":"希哈大多與格那希和其他南隆河品種混調。","Syrah's most typical blend is with local Southern Rhône grapes, above all Grenache; such wines are sometimes called Rhône blends. In Australia Shiraz is also blended with Cabernet Sauvignon, but that is not the Rhône blend. Pinotage goes into the South African Cape Blend with Cabernet and Merlot.":"希哈最典型的混調是與南隆河的在地品種，尤其是格那希；這類酒有時被稱為隆河混調。在澳洲，希拉茲也會與卡本內蘇維濃混調，但那不是隆河混調。皮諾塔吉則與卡本內和梅洛一起用於南非的 Cape Blend。","Why is oak often used in making Syrah/Shiraz?":"為什麼釀造希哈／希拉茲時常使用橡木桶？","To soften tannins and add smoke and spice":"柔化單寧，增添煙燻和香料","To raise acidity and add floral notes":"提高酸度，增添花香","To strip colour and lighten the body":"去除顏色，讓酒體更輕","To add black pepper and fresh black fruit":"增添黑胡椒和新鮮的黑色水果","Oak softens the tannins and adds smoke and spice.":"橡木桶柔化單寧，並增添煙燻和香料。","Syrah has medium to high tannins, and oak maturation makes them softer. Oak also adds secondary flavours of smoke and spice, and in Barossa Shiraz often vanilla and coconut. Black pepper and fresh black fruit come from the grape itself, while floral aromas can come from Viognier.":"希哈的單寧中等至高，橡木桶熟成能讓它們更柔和。橡木桶也會增添煙燻和香料的二級風味，在 Barossa 希拉茲中常還有香草和椰子。黑胡椒和新鮮的黑色水果來自葡萄本身，而花香可能來自維歐尼耶。","Which notes does a fine Syrah/Shiraz develop with age?":"優質的希哈／希拉茲隨陳年會發展出哪些氣息？","Dried fruit, leather, meat and earth":"果乾、皮革、肉和泥土","Smoke, vanilla and coconut":"煙燻、香草和椰子","Black cherry, blackberry and herbs":"黑櫻桃、黑莓和香草植物","With time, Syrah develops dried fruit and notes of leather, meat and earth.":"隨著時間，希哈會發展出果乾以及皮革、肉和泥土的氣息。","The best Syrahs, intense and tannic, can age for a decade or more. Over that time dried fruit and tertiary notes of leather, meat and earth appear. Dried fruit and tobacco describe aged Merlot, smoke, vanilla and coconut come from oak, and black cherry, blackberry and herbs are primary flavours of young wine.":"最好的希哈濃郁且單寧多，可以陳年十年以上。在這段時間裡，會出現果乾以及皮革、肉和泥土的三級氣息。果乾和菸草描述的是陳年梅洛，煙燻、香草和椰子來自橡木桶，而黑櫻桃、黑莓和香草植物是年輕酒款的一級風味。","Which black grape is the only one allowed in Northern Rhône AOC wines?":"哪一個黑葡萄是北隆河 AOC 酒款唯一允許的品種？","The Northern Rhône is Syrah's classic home and its only black grape for AOC wines.":"北隆河是希哈的經典故鄉，也是那裡 AOC 酒款唯一的黑葡萄。","In the Northern Rhône, red AOC wines are made only from Syrah, the sole black grape allowed; in Côte-Rôtie it may be co-fermented with a little Viognier, which is white. Grenache is the key grape of the Southern Rhône, where it is blended with Syrah. Merlot and Pinot Noir belong to other regions.":"在北隆河，AOC 紅酒只用希哈釀造，它是唯一允許的黑葡萄；在 Côte-Rôtie，它可以與少量白葡萄維歐尼耶共同發酵。格那希是南隆河的關鍵品種，在那裡與希哈混調。梅洛和黑皮諾則屬於其他產區。","Why are Northern Rhône wines expensive to produce?":"為什麼北隆河的酒生產成本很高？","Steep slopes force all work to be done by hand":"陡坡迫使所有工作都必須人工完成","The vines are irrigated all year":"葡萄樹全年灌溉","The rules require ten years in barrel":"法規要求在橡木桶中放十年","The grapes are bought from other regions":"葡萄是從其他產區買來的","Many vineyards are so steep that machines cannot be used.":"許多葡萄園陡峭到無法使用機器。","In the Northern Rhône the valley is narrow and the best vineyards are on very steep slopes. Machines cannot work there, so pruning, vineyard care and harvesting are done by hand, at high cost. Crozes-Hermitage, flatter and easier to mechanise, accordingly has lower prices.":"在北隆河，山谷狹窄，最好的葡萄園位於非常陡峭的坡地上。機器無法在那裡作業，所以修剪、葡萄園照料和採收都靠人工完成，成本很高。地勢較平坦、較容易機械化的 Crozes-Hermitage，價格也因此較低。","In the moderate Northern Rhône, what helps Syrah ripen?":"在溫和的北隆河，是什麼幫助希哈成熟？","The aspect of the slopes":"坡地的朝向","Vineyard irrigation":"葡萄園灌溉","Very high yields":"非常高的產量","Cool sea breezes":"涼爽的海風","Well-exposed slopes make up for a climate that is only moderate.":"日照良好的坡地彌補了只屬於溫和的氣候。","Syrah needs a moderate to warm climate. The Northern Rhône is moderate, but the best vineyards sit on steep slopes that face the sun, such as the south-facing hill of Hermitage. This aspect increases the warmth the vines receive and lets the grapes ripen. Cool breezes, by contrast, would slow ripening.":"希哈需要溫和至溫暖的氣候。北隆河屬於溫和氣候，但最好的葡萄園位於面向太陽的陡坡上，例如朝南的 Hermitage 山丘。這樣的坡向增加了葡萄樹接收的熱量，讓葡萄得以成熟。相反地，涼爽的微風會減緩成熟。","Which appellation marks Syrah's northern ripening limit and may include a little Viognier?":"哪一個法定產區是希哈成熟的北界，而且可能含有少量維歐尼耶？","Côte-Rôtie, in the far north, marks Syrah's limit; Viognier may traditionally be co-fermented.":"位於最北端的 Côte-Rôtie 是希哈的極限；傳統上可以與維歐尼耶共同發酵。","Côte-Rôtie lies in the far north of the Northern Rhône, at the limit of where Syrah can ripen. Its extremely steep, stony slopes give complex, peppery wines that age well. Some producers, not all, co-ferment a little Viognier, which can add floral aromas. Hermitage and Crozes-Hermitage are further south; Minervois is in the Languedoc.":"Côte-Rôtie 位於北隆河的最北端，處於希哈能夠成熟的極限。它極為陡峭多石的坡地，出產複雜、帶胡椒味、適合陳年的酒。有些生產者（並非全部）會共同發酵少量維歐尼耶，可能增添花香。Hermitage 和 Crozes-Hermitage 在更南邊；Minervois 則在 Languedoc。","What characterises the Hermitage AOC?":"Hermitage AOC 的特色是什麼？","A single steep, south-facing hill":"單一一座朝南的陡峭山丘","A broad plain that is easy to mechanise":"容易機械化的廣闊平原","Irrigated vineyards in an inland valley":"內陸山谷中經灌溉的葡萄園","Gravel soils on flat land":"平地上的礫石土壤","The whole Hermitage appellation is one steep, south-facing hill.":"整個 Hermitage 法定產區就是一座朝南的陡峭山丘。","Hermitage AOC, in the Northern Rhône south of Côte-Rôtie, is a high-quality appellation that consists of one steep, south-facing hill. That aspect helps Syrah ripen in a moderate climate. Around the hill lies Crozes-Hermitage AOC, larger and flatter, with less intense but cheaper wines.":"Hermitage AOC 位於北隆河 Côte-Rôtie 以南，是由一座朝南的陡峭山丘構成的高品質法定產區。這樣的坡向幫助希哈在溫和氣候中成熟。山丘周圍是 Crozes-Hermitage AOC，面積更大、地勢更平坦，酒款不那麼濃郁，但較便宜。","Why are Crozes-Hermitage wines usually cheaper than Hermitage?":"為什麼 Crozes-Hermitage 的酒通常比 Hermitage 便宜？","Higher yields and vineyards easier to mechanise":"產量較高，葡萄園較容易機械化","Using white grapes instead of Syrah":"使用白葡萄代替希哈","No bottle ageing is allowed":"不允許瓶中陳年","A warmer climate that cuts costs":"較溫暖的氣候降低了成本","Flatter land allows higher yields and machine work, so lower costs.":"較平坦的土地允許更高的產量和機械作業，因此成本較低。","Crozes-Hermitage surrounds the hill of Hermitage and is larger and flatter. Yields are higher and the vineyards can be worked by machine, whereas Hermitage's steep slopes need hand work. The result is wines that are generally less intense and complex, but more affordable.":"Crozes-Hermitage 環繞著 Hermitage 山丘，面積更大、地勢更平坦。產量較高，葡萄園可以用機器作業，而 Hermitage 的陡坡則需要人工。結果是酒款一般不那麼濃郁和複雜，但價格更親民。","In Languedoc-Roussillon, in which appellation is Syrah often blended with other grapes?":"在 Languedoc-Roussillon，希哈常在哪個法定產區與其他品種混調？","Minervois is a Languedoc appellation where Syrah is often blended.":"Minervois 是 Languedoc 的法定產區，希哈在那裡常被混調。","Languedoc-Roussillon's warm climate ripens Syrah reliably. It is often blended in appellation wines such as Minervois AOC, or bottled as a varietal under Pays d'Oc IGP. Crozes-Hermitage and Côte-Rôtie are in the Northern Rhône, where Syrah is the only black grape, and Pomerol is in Bordeaux.":"Languedoc-Roussillon 溫暖的氣候讓希哈穩定成熟。它常在 Minervois AOC 等法定產區酒款中被混調，或以 Pays d'Oc IGP 單一品種裝瓶。Crozes-Hermitage 和 Côte-Rôtie 位於北隆河，那裡希哈是唯一的黑葡萄，而 Pomerol 在波爾多。","Which grape is the most widely planted in Australia?":"澳洲種植最廣泛的品種是哪一個？","Shiraz is Australia's most planted grape; Australia has its largest plantings outside France.":"希拉茲是澳洲種植最多的品種；澳洲擁有法國以外最大的種植面積。","Outside France, Australia has by far the largest Syrah plantings; there it is called Shiraz and is the country's leading grape. Much is grown in warm inland areas for cheap, high-volume wine, but regions such as Barossa and Hunter Valley give Shiraz with real character. Cabernet matters, for example in Coonawarra, but it is not the most planted.":"在法國以外，澳洲的希哈種植面積遙遙領先；在那裡它稱為 Shiraz（希拉茲），是這個國家的首要品種。很多種在溫暖的內陸地區，用於便宜的大量生產酒款，但 Barossa 和 Hunter Valley 等產區出產真正有個性的希拉茲。卡本內也很重要，例如在 Coonawarra，但它不是種植最多的。","What does the label South Eastern Australia usually indicate on a Shiraz?":"希拉茲酒標上的 South Eastern Australia 通常代表什麼？","An inexpensive high-volume wine from warm inland areas":"來自溫暖內陸地區的平價大量生產酒款","A wine from old, low-yielding vines":"來自低產量老藤的酒","A wine from a single south-facing hill":"來自單一朝南山丘的酒","A wine from cool, cloud-cooled vineyards":"來自涼爽、受雲層降溫的葡萄園的酒","South Eastern Australia draws on large warm inland areas for cheap, high-volume brands.":"South Eastern Australia 取材自廣大的溫暖內陸地區，用於便宜的大量生產品牌。","Much of Australia's Shiraz is planted in warm inland regions. Its grapes go mainly into inexpensive, high-volume wines labelled with the broad South Eastern Australia name. Old, low-yielding vines describe the Barossa Valley instead, while cloud and breezes that slow ripening are typical of the Hunter Valley.":"澳洲大部分的希拉茲種在溫暖的內陸產區。它的葡萄主要用於標示廣泛的 South Eastern Australia 名稱的平價大量生產酒款。低產量的老藤描述的則是 Barossa Valley，而減緩成熟的雲層和微風是 Hunter Valley 的典型特徵。","A full-bodied Shiraz with high ripe tannins, cooked blackberry, black pepper, vanilla and coconut, from very old vines. Where is it most likely from?":"一款來自非常古老葡萄樹、酒體飽滿、單寧高而成熟、帶有煮過的黑莓、黑胡椒、香草和椰子的希拉茲。它最可能來自哪裡？","Warm Barossa has very old Shiraz vines giving full, ripe, often oaky wines.":"溫暖的 Barossa 擁有非常古老的希拉茲葡萄樹，出產飽滿、成熟、常帶橡木味的酒。","The Barossa Valley in South Australia is warm and home to some of the world's oldest Shiraz vines, with low yields of concentrated fruit. The wines are full-bodied with high, ripe tannins, cooked black fruit, black pepper and often vanilla and coconut from oak. Hunter Valley gives medium-bodied Shiraz; Côte-Rôtie and Crozes-Hermitage give fresher Syrah.":"南澳的 Barossa Valley 很溫暖，擁有一些世界上最古老的希拉茲葡萄樹，產量低、果實濃縮。這裡的酒酒體飽滿，單寧高而成熟，帶有煮過的黑色水果、黑胡椒，常還有來自橡木的香草和椰子。Hunter Valley 出產酒體中等的希拉茲；Côte-Rôtie 和 Crozes-Hermitage 出產較清爽的希哈。","Why is Hunter Valley Shiraz usually medium-bodied despite very hot summers?":"儘管夏天非常炎熱，為什麼 Hunter Valley 的希拉茲通常酒體中等？","Old vines give very low yields":"老藤的產量非常低","Grapes are harvested very late":"葡萄非常晚才採收","Gravel soils hold heat":"礫石土壤保留熱量","In summer, heavy cloud and sea breezes slow ripening, limiting body and alcohol.":"夏天濃厚的雲層和海風減緩成熟，限制了酒體和酒精。","The Hunter Valley in New South Wales lies at a relatively northerly latitude and so has very hot summers. But heavy summer cloud and sea breezes slow ripening. The resulting Shiraz is medium-bodied, with medium to high tannins and fresh black fruit, and with age it develops complex earthy and meaty notes.":"新南威爾斯的 Hunter Valley 位於相對偏北的緯度，所以夏天非常炎熱。但夏季濃厚的雲層和海風減緩了成熟。結果的希拉茲酒體中等，單寧中等至高，帶有新鮮的黑色水果，陳年後會發展出複雜的泥土和肉味。","Which statement about Australian Shiraz today is correct?":"關於今天的澳洲希拉茲，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","Styles are increasingly varied, even sparkling reds":"風格越來越多樣，甚至有氣泡紅酒","It is only made in a full, concentrated style":"它只釀成飽滿濃縮的風格","It is never blended with other grapes":"它從不與其他品種混調","It is never aged in oak":"它從不在橡木桶中陳年","Alongside full-bodied Shiraz, Australian producers make ever more varied styles, even sparkling.":"除了酒體飽滿的希拉茲，澳洲生產者也釀出越來越多樣的風格，甚至有氣泡酒。","Australia is best known for full-bodied, concentrated Shiraz, but its producers now offer an ever wider range of styles, even sparkling reds. Shiraz is usually a varietal but is also blended with Cabernet Sauvignon and Grenache, and oak is common, for example in Barossa with vanilla and coconut notes.":"澳洲最著名的是酒體飽滿、濃縮的希拉茲，但它的生產者現在提供越來越廣的風格範圍，甚至有氣泡紅酒。希拉茲通常是單一品種，但也會與卡本內蘇維濃和格那希混調，而橡木桶也很常見，例如 Barossa 帶有香草和椰子氣息的酒。","What are Syrah/Shiraz berries like?":"希哈／希拉茲的果粒是什麼樣子？","Small and thick-skinned":"小而果皮厚","Large and thin-skinned, very juicy":"大而果皮薄，非常多汁","Large and golden-white":"大而呈金白色","Small and thin-skinned":"小而果皮薄","Syrah is a black grape with small, thick-skinned berries.":"希哈是果粒小、果皮厚的黑葡萄。","Thick skins explain the deep colour and tannin, and why Syrah adds colour and structure to blends. It is not a white grape; large, thin-skinned berries would give paler, less tannic wines.":"厚果皮解釋了深色和單寧，以及為什麼希哈能為混調增添顏色和結構。它不是白葡萄；大而果皮薄的果粒會釀出顏色更淡、單寧更少的酒。","What climate does Syrah need to ripen fully?":"希哈需要什麼氣候才能完全成熟？","Moderate to warm":"溫和至溫暖","Cool, near the limit of cultivation, with frosts":"涼爽、接近種植極限、有霜凍","Only very hot and irrigated":"只在非常炎熱且經灌溉的地方","Cool and foggy":"涼爽多霧","Syrah ripens fully in moderate to warm climates.":"希哈在溫和至溫暖的氣候中能完全成熟。","In the moderate Northern Rhône it gives medium-bodied, peppery wines; in warm parts of Australia, full and alcoholic ones. Cool or foggy climates are not enough, and extreme irrigated heat is not required.":"在溫和的北隆河，它釀出酒體中等、帶胡椒味的酒；在澳洲溫暖的地區，則釀出飽滿、酒精高的酒。涼爽或多霧的氣候是不夠的，也不需要極端的灌溉高溫。","What levels of tannin and acidity does Syrah/Shiraz usually have?":"希哈／希拉茲通常有什麼程度的單寧和酸度？","Medium to high":"中等至高","Both low, for a very soft and round wine":"兩者都低，讓酒非常柔和圓潤","No tannin and very high acidity":"沒有單寧，酸度非常高","Very high tannin and no acidity":"單寧非常高，沒有酸度","Syrah gives wines with medium to high tannin and acidity.":"希哈釀出單寧和酸度中等至高的酒。","This structure, with intense flavours, lets the best examples age. A red is never without tannin or acidity, and a profile low in everything does not fit Syrah.":"這樣的結構加上濃郁的風味，讓最好的酒款能夠陳年。紅酒不會沒有單寧或酸度，而各方面都低的風味特徵也不符合希哈。","Where is medium-bodied Syrah with fresh black fruit and black pepper the signature style?":"在哪裡，酒體中等、帶新鮮黑色水果和黑胡椒的希哈是招牌風格？","Australia's warm inland, for high-volume wines":"澳洲溫暖的內陸，用於大量生產的酒款","Barossa Valley":"Barossa Valley","Pomerol":"Pomerol","The moderate, peppery style is the Northern Rhône's signature, where it is called Syrah.":"溫和、帶胡椒味的風格是北隆河的招牌，在那裡稱為 Syrah。","Australia's warm areas, Barossa included, give full, alcoholic Shiraz with cooked black fruit and liquorice instead. Pomerol is on Bordeaux's Right Bank and is Merlot-led.":"澳洲溫暖的地區，包括 Barossa，出產的則是飽滿、酒精高、帶有煮過的黑色水果和甘草的希拉茲。Pomerol 位於波爾多右岸，以梅洛為主。","What does the term 'Rhône blend' usually refer to?":"「隆河混調」這個術語通常指什麼？","Syrah with Southern Rhône grapes such as Grenache":"希哈與格那希等南隆河品種","Syrah with Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot":"希哈與卡本內蘇維濃和梅洛","A white wine from aromatic grapes only":"只用芳香型品種釀的白酒","A pure Syrah from a single vineyard":"來自單一葡萄園的純希哈","The name is used for Syrah blended with Southern Rhône grapes such as Grenache.":"這個名稱用於希哈與格那希等南隆河品種的混調。","In the blend Syrah adds colour, black fruit and tannin. Blending with Cabernet and Merlot is Bordeaux-style; a single-vineyard Syrah is not a blend, and the term does not mean a white wine.":"在混調中，希哈增添顏色、黑色水果和單寧。與卡本內和梅洛混調是波爾多式的；單一葡萄園的希哈不是混調，而這個術語也不是指白酒。","Why can the finest Syrahs age for a decade or more?":"為什麼最優質的希哈能陳年十年以上？","They have intense flavours and firm tannins":"它們有濃郁的風味和紮實的單寧","They have lots of residual sugar":"它們有大量殘糖","They are bottled with no oak maturation":"它們不經橡木桶熟成就裝瓶","They have little alcohol and acidity":"它們的酒精和酸度都很少","Intense flavours and tannins let the best Syrahs age long in bottle.":"濃郁的風味和單寧讓最好的希哈能在瓶中長期陳年。","With time, dried fruit, leather, meat and earth emerge. Syrahs are dry wines, oak maturation is in fact common, and low acidity and alcohol would not help ageing.":"隨著時間，果乾、皮革、肉和泥土會浮現。希哈是不甜的酒，橡木桶熟成其實很常見，而低酸度和低酒精無助於陳年。","Towards which sea does the Rhône Valley run?":"隆河谷地往哪個海延伸？","The Atlantic, through the Gironde Estuary":"大西洋，經由吉倫特河口","The North Sea":"北海","The Baltic Sea":"波羅的海","The Rhône Valley follows the river down to the Mediterranean; its northern part is the Northern Rhône.":"隆河谷地沿著河流向下延伸到地中海；它的北部是北隆河。","In the north the valley is very narrow and the best vineyards are on steep slopes; further south, towards the sea, lies the Grenache-based Southern Rhône. The Gironde and the Atlantic concern Bordeaux.":"在北部，山谷非常狹窄，最好的葡萄園位於陡坡上；更南邊、靠近海的地方，是以格那希為主的南隆河。吉倫特河和大西洋與波爾多有關。","What can a little Viognier co-fermented with Syrah add in Côte-Rôtie?":"在 Côte-Rôtie，與希哈共同發酵的少量維歐尼耶能增添什麼？","Floral aromas":"花香","More tannin and a much darker colour":"更多單寧和深得多的顏色","Mint and green bell pepper notes":"薄荷和青椒氣息","Viognier, an aromatic white grape, can add floral notes to Syrah.":"芳香型白葡萄維歐尼耶能為希哈增添花香氣息。","As a white grape it adds neither tannin nor colour. The wine stays dry; mint and green bell pepper are typical Cabernet Sauvignon notes.":"作為白葡萄，它既不增添單寧也不增添顏色。酒依然不甜；薄荷和青椒是卡本內蘇維濃的典型氣息。","Which statement about co-fermenting Viognier in Côte-Rôtie is correct?":"關於在 Côte-Rôtie 共同發酵維歐尼耶，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It is a tradition, but not every producer follows it":"這是一項傳統，但並非每位生產者都遵循","It is compulsory by law for every Côte-Rôtie made":"每款 Côte-Rôtie 依法都必須這樣做","Viognier must make up at least half the wine":"維歐尼耶必須至少佔酒的一半","It is done only in Hermitage":"只在 Hermitage 這樣做","Co-fermenting a little Viognier is traditional in Côte-Rôtie but not compulsory.":"共同發酵少量維歐尼耶是 Côte-Rôtie 的傳統，但不是強制的。","Only a small amount is used, and many producers make Syrah without Viognier. Syrah remains the only black grape allowed in Northern Rhône AOCs; the tradition belongs to Côte-Rôtie, not Hermitage.":"只使用少量，而且許多生產者釀的希哈不含維歐尼耶。希哈仍然是北隆河 AOC 唯一允許的黑葡萄；這項傳統屬於 Côte-Rôtie，不屬於 Hermitage。","A label shows Côte-Rôtie AOC. What wine can you expect?":"一張酒標上標示 Côte-Rôtie AOC。你可以預期什麼樣的酒？","A complex, peppery Syrah able to age":"複雜、帶胡椒味、能陳年的希哈","A soft Merlot-led blend ready at once":"柔和、以梅洛為主、立即適飲的混調","A high-volume Shiraz from flat, irrigated vineyards":"來自平坦、經灌溉葡萄園的大量生產希拉茲","A dry white made only from Viognier":"只用維歐尼耶釀的不甜白酒","Côte-Rôtie's steep, stony slopes give complex, peppery, long-lived Syrah.":"Côte-Rôtie 陡峭多石的坡地出產複雜、帶胡椒味、長壽的希哈。","It is Syrah's northern ripening limit, in the far north of the Northern Rhône. Viognier, if present, is only a small part of a red wine; Merlot and flat irrigated vineyards have nothing to do with it.":"它是希哈成熟的北界，位於北隆河的最北端。維歐尼耶即使存在，也只是紅酒的一小部分；梅洛和平坦的灌溉葡萄園都與它無關。","Where is Hermitage in relation to Côte-Rôtie?":"Hermitage 相對於 Côte-Rôtie 的位置在哪裡？","Further south, still in the Northern Rhône":"更南邊，仍在北隆河","Further north, beyond Syrah's ripening limit":"更北邊，超過希哈成熟的極限","In Languedoc-Roussillon":"在 Languedoc-Roussillon","On Bordeaux's Right Bank":"在波爾多右岸","Hermitage lies further south than Côte-Rôtie, in the Northern Rhône.":"Hermitage 位於 Côte-Rôtie 以南，在北隆河。","Côte-Rôtie is in the far north and marks Syrah's limit, so nothing of note lies further north. Hermitage is one steep, south-facing hill surrounded by Crozes-Hermitage; it is not in Languedoc or Bordeaux.":"Côte-Rôtie 位於最北端，是希哈的極限，所以更北邊沒有什麼值得一提的。Hermitage 是一座朝南的陡峭山丘，被 Crozes-Hermitage 環繞；它不在 Languedoc，也不在波爾多。","A customer wants an everyday Northern Rhône Syrah at a modest price. Which appellation should you suggest?":"一位顧客想要一款價格適中、適合日常飲用的北隆河希哈。你應該推薦哪個法定產區？","Côte-Rôtie AOC, from the steepest, stoniest slopes":"Côte-Rôtie AOC，來自最陡峭多石的坡地","Crozes-Hermitage, flatter and easier to mechanise, is usually cheaper.":"地勢較平坦、較容易機械化的 Crozes-Hermitage 通常較便宜。","Its wines are less intense and complex than Hermitage and Côte-Rôtie, which are costly because their steep slopes are worked by hand. Pomerol is a Merlot-led Bordeaux red, not a Syrah.":"它的酒不如 Hermitage 和 Côte-Rôtie 濃郁複雜，後兩者因為陡坡需要人工作業而昂貴。Pomerol 是以梅洛為主的波爾多紅酒，不是希哈。","In Languedoc-Roussillon, how is a single-varietal Syrah usually labelled?":"在 Languedoc-Roussillon，單一品種的希哈通常如何標示？","Single-varietal Languedoc-Roussillon Syrah is usually found as Pays d'Oc IGP.":"Languedoc-Roussillon 的單一品種希哈通常以 Pays d'Oc IGP 出現。","In the region's AOCs, such as Minervois, Syrah is instead often blended with other grapes. Hermitage is in the Northern Rhône; South Eastern Australia is an Australian label.":"在這個地區的 AOC，例如 Minervois，希哈則常與其他品種混調。Hermitage 在北隆河；South Eastern Australia 是澳洲的標示。","Where are the largest Syrah/Shiraz plantings outside France?":"法國以外最大的希哈／希拉茲種植面積在哪裡？","Australia":"澳洲","Chile, in the valleys between the Andes and the coast":"智利，在安地斯山脈與海岸之間的山谷","By far the largest plantings outside France are in Australia.":"法國以外遙遙領先的最大種植面積在澳洲。","In Australia it is called Shiraz and is the country's most planted grape, mostly in warm inland areas. Plantings have grown elsewhere but remain far smaller.":"在澳洲它稱為 Shiraz，是這個國家種植最多的品種，大多在溫暖的內陸地區。其他地方的種植面積雖有增加，但仍小得多。","In which Australian state is Barossa Valley?":"Barossa Valley 位於澳洲哪個州？","New South Wales, north of Sydney":"新南威爾斯，雪梨以北","The warm Barossa Valley is in South Australia.":"溫暖的 Barossa Valley 位於南澳。","It is home to some of the world's oldest Shiraz vines. Hunter Valley is in New South Wales, Margaret River in Western Australia; Tasmania is not a noted Shiraz area.":"這裡有一些世界上最古老的希拉茲葡萄樹。Hunter Valley 在新南威爾斯，Margaret River 在西澳；塔斯馬尼亞並不是知名的希拉茲產區。","Why does Hunter Valley have very hot summers?":"為什麼 Hunter Valley 的夏天非常炎熱？","Its relatively northerly latitude":"它相對偏北的緯度","Cold southern ocean currents":"寒冷的南方洋流","Gravel soils beside an estuary":"河口旁的礫石土壤","In the southern hemisphere, a more northerly latitude means closer to the equator, so hotter.":"在南半球，越偏北代表越接近赤道，因此越熱。","Summer cloud and sea breezes slow ripening, though, so the Shiraz stays medium-bodied. Altitude and cold currents would cool rather than heat; gravel beside an estuary describes Bordeaux.":"不過夏季的雲層和海風會減緩成熟，所以希拉茲保持中等酒體。海拔和寒冷洋流只會降溫而不是升溫；河口旁的礫石描述的是波爾多。","Which notes does Hunter Valley Shiraz develop with bottle age?":"Hunter Valley 的希拉茲經過瓶中陳年會發展出哪些氣息？","Fresh flowers and citrus, like a young aromatic white":"新鮮的花香和柑橘，就像年輕的芳香型白酒","Fresh strawberry and green bell pepper":"新鮮的草莓和青椒","With age, Hunter Valley Shiraz develops complex earth and meat notes.":"隨著陳年，Hunter Valley 的希拉茲會發展出複雜的泥土和肉味。","Young, it is medium-bodied with medium to high tannins and fresh black fruit. Vanilla and coconut come from new oak and are not ageing notes; flowers and citrus or strawberry and green pepper do not describe this wine.":"年輕時，它酒體中等，單寧中等至高，帶有新鮮的黑色水果。香草和椰子來自新橡木桶，不是陳年的氣息；花香和柑橘或草莓和青椒都不是在描述這款酒。","Which statement about Australian Shiraz and blending is correct?":"關於澳洲希拉茲和混調，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","Mostly single-varietal, but also blended with Cabernet and Grenache":"大多是單一品種，但也會與卡本內和格那希混調","By law it must always contain Viognier":"依法必須一律含有維歐尼耶","It is never made as a single varietal":"它從不以單一品種釀造","It is only blended with aromatic white grapes to soften it":"它只與芳香型白葡萄混調以柔化口感","Australian Shiraz is most often single-varietal, though blends with Cabernet and Grenache are common.":"澳洲希拉茲最常是單一品種，不過與卡本內和格那希的混調也很常見。","There is no Viognier requirement: co-fermentation is a Côte-Rôtie tradition. It is false that it is never single-varietal, and its usual partners are black grapes, not aromatic whites.":"沒有必須含維歐尼耶的規定：共同發酵是 Côte-Rôtie 的傳統。說它從不以單一品種釀造是錯的，而它常見的搭檔是黑葡萄，不是芳香型白葡萄。","Which dishes does Syrah/Shiraz pair well with, thanks to its peppery character?":"由於帶有胡椒味的特色，希哈／希拉茲適合搭配哪些菜餚？","Highly flavoured dishes":"風味濃郁的菜餚","Delicate fruit and cream desserts":"細緻的水果和鮮奶油甜點","Raw oysters":"生蠔","Light, undressed salads":"不加醬汁的清淡沙拉","Syrah's intense, peppery character makes it a good match for highly flavoured dishes.":"希哈濃郁、帶胡椒味的特色，讓它很適合搭配風味濃郁的菜餚。","A peppery, structured red would overwhelm delicate foods such as light salads or raw oysters. A dry wine with a sweet dessert would also taste more bitter and sour.":"帶胡椒味、結構紮實的紅酒會壓過清淡沙拉或生蠔等細緻的食物。不甜的酒配甜點，也會嚐起來更苦、更酸。","In a country other than France or Australia, a bottle says Shiraz rather than Syrah. What does this suggest?":"在法國或澳洲以外的國家，一瓶酒標示 Shiraz 而不是 Syrah。這暗示什麼？","A riper, fuller, warm-climate style":"更成熟、更飽滿的溫暖氣候風格","A fresher, medium-bodied, peppery style like the Northern Rhône":"類似北隆河、較清爽、酒體中等、帶胡椒味的風格","A different grape, related to Syrah":"與希哈相關的另一個品種","A sweet dessert wine":"甜型甜點酒","The name Shiraz points to the warm Australian style: full, ripe, with cooked black fruit.":"Shiraz 這個名稱指向溫暖的澳洲風格：飽滿、成熟，帶有煮過的黑色水果。","Syrah and Shiraz are the same grape; outside France and Australia the chosen name hints at the style. Syrah would suggest the fresh, peppery Northern Rhône style; it does not mean a sweet wine.":"Syrah 和 Shiraz 是同一個品種；在法國和澳洲以外，選用的名稱會暗示風格。Syrah 會暗示清爽、帶胡椒味的北隆河風格；它並不代表甜酒。","What distinguishes a Prädikatswein from a Qualitätswein?":"Prädikatswein 和 Qualitätswein 有什麼不同？","Higher minimum grape sugar and a single growing area":"葡萄最低糖分更高，且來自單一產區","Botrytis is compulsory for all the wines":"所有酒款都必須有貴腐菌","Compulsory maturation in oak barrels":"必須在橡木桶中熟成","The wine is always dry and full-bodied":"酒一定是不甜且酒體飽滿的","Prädikatswein needs sweeter grapes than Qualitätswein, all from one area.":"Prädikatswein 需要比 Qualitätswein 更甜的葡萄，而且全部來自同一個產區。","Qualitätswein must come from one of Germany's 13 wine-growing areas and reach a set ripeness. Prädikatswein raises the bar: it requires a higher minimum sugar level in the grapes, and the grapes must come from a single area. It is split into six categories, from Kabinett to Trockenbeerenauslese, which may be dry or sweet; neither botrytis nor oak is required.":"Qualitätswein 必須來自德國 13 個葡萄酒產區之一，並達到規定的成熟度。Prädikatswein 提高了門檻：它要求葡萄的最低糖分更高，而且葡萄必須來自單一產區。它分為六個類別，從 Kabinett 到 Trockenbeerenauslese，可以是不甜或甜的；貴腐菌和橡木桶都不是必要條件。","Why does a dry Auslese have more alcohol than a dry Kabinett?":"為什麼不甜的 Auslese 比不甜的 Kabinett 酒精更高？","The Auslese grapes contained more sugar":"Auslese 的葡萄含有更多糖分","Alcohol is added to Auslese after fermentation":"Auslese 在發酵後添加了酒精","Auslese is always made from frozen grapes":"Auslese 一定是用冰凍的葡萄釀造","Kabinett fermentation is stopped with Süssreserve":"Kabinett 的發酵以 Süssreserve 中止","More sugar in the grapes means more alcohol when the wine is fermented dry.":"葡萄中的糖越多，發酵至不甜時酒精就越高。","The Prädikat categories are ranked by minimum grape sugar. Auslese comes from selected extra-ripe bunches, Spätlese from late-picked grapes, and Kabinett from the least ripe grapes. If these wines are fermented to dryness, all the sugar becomes alcohol, so a dry Auslese is stronger than a dry Spätlese, which in turn is stronger than a dry Kabinett.":"Prädikat 類別依葡萄最低糖分排序。Auslese 來自精選的過熟果串，Spätlese 來自晚採的葡萄，Kabinett 則來自成熟度最低的葡萄。如果這些酒發酵至不甜，所有的糖都會變成酒精，所以不甜的 Auslese 比不甜的 Spätlese 酒精更高，而後者又比不甜的 Kabinett 更高。","How is Eiswein made?":"Eiswein 是怎麼釀造的？","From grapes frozen on the vine, without botrytis":"用在樹上結冰的葡萄，沒有貴腐菌","From selected berries dried out by botrytis":"用被貴腐菌風乾的精選果粒","From grapes frozen in the winery after harvest":"用採收後在酒廠冷凍的葡萄","From just-ripe grapes with added Süssreserve":"用剛成熟的葡萄加上 Süssreserve","Eiswein comes from grapes frozen on the vine; botrytis plays no part.":"Eiswein 來自在樹上結冰的葡萄；貴腐菌不參與其中。","Eiswein is made from grapes left on the vine until they freeze, which concentrates their sugars. Botrytis plays no part, so the wine has fresh, vibrant aromas of peach, apricot, mango and pineapple. The right conditions do not occur every year, the work is labour-intensive and yields are tiny, so this outstanding wine commands high prices.":"Eiswein 是用留在樹上直到結冰的葡萄釀造的，這會濃縮葡萄的糖分。貴腐菌不參與其中，所以這款酒帶有清新鮮明的桃子、杏桃、芒果和鳳梨香氣。合適的條件並非每年都會出現，工作耗費大量人力，產量又極少，所以這款傑出的酒價格高昂。","Which Prädikat category is made from individually selected berries dried by botrytis?":"哪一個 Prädikat 類別是用被貴腐菌風乾、逐粒精選的果粒釀造的？","TBA comes from individually picked, botrytis-dried berries: the rarest and most concentrated.":"TBA 來自逐粒採摘、被貴腐菌風乾的果粒：最稀有、最濃縮。","Trockenbeerenauslese is made from individually selected berries that have been dried out by botrytis. It is a rare, concentrated wine with flavours similar to, but even more intense than, a BA. Beerenauslese comes from selected bunches or berries concentrated by botrytis, Auslese from selected extra-ripe bunches, and Eiswein from grapes frozen on the vine, without botrytis.":"Trockenbeerenauslese 是用被貴腐菌風乾、逐粒精選的果粒釀造的。它是一款稀有、濃縮的酒，風味與 BA 相似，但更加濃郁。Beerenauslese 來自被貴腐菌濃縮的精選果串或果粒，Auslese 來自精選的過熟果串，而 Eiswein 來自在樹上結冰的葡萄，沒有貴腐菌。","What does Halbtrocken indicate on a German label?":"德國酒標上的 Halbtrocken 代表什麼？","A completely dry wine":"完全不甜的酒","A wine from frozen grapes":"用冰凍葡萄釀的酒","A light PGI wine":"輕盈的 PGI 酒款","Halbtrocken means some sweetness; Trocken means dry.":"Halbtrocken 代表帶有一些甜味；Trocken 代表不甜。","Many German wines have some sweetness. Sometimes the Prädikat category is enough to tell you, for example a Beerenauslese is always sweet. Where there could be doubt, producers can use terms that indicate sweetness: Trocken for a dry wine and Halbtrocken for a wine with some sweetness. The German PGI category, by contrast, is called Landwein.":"許多德國酒都帶有一些甜味。有時 Prädikat 類別就足以說明，例如 Beerenauslese 一定是甜的。在可能有疑問的地方，生產者可以使用表示甜度的術語：Trocken 代表不甜的酒，Halbtrocken 代表帶有一些甜味的酒。相反地，德國的 PGI 類別稱為 Landwein。","What do Premier Cru or Grand Cru indicate on a Chablis label?":"Chablis 酒標上的 Premier Cru 或 Grand Cru 代表什麼？","Grapes from the area's best vineyards":"葡萄來自這個地區最好的葡萄園","Wine matured in new oak":"在新橡木桶中熟成的酒","Wine from late-picked grapes":"用晚採葡萄釀的酒","Grapes from anywhere in Burgundy":"葡萄來自布根地任何地方","They mark the best vineyards, usually on well-exposed slopes.":"它們標示最好的葡萄園，通常位於日照良好的坡地。","In Chablis the best vineyards are labelled Premier Cru or Grand Cru. They usually lie on south/south-west facing hillsides that get more sun, so grapes ripen better and wines are more flavourful and complex. The terms do not mean oak, which is rare in Chablis; grapes from anywhere in Burgundy means Bourgogne AOC.":"在 Chablis，最好的葡萄園標示為 Premier Cru 或 Grand Cru。它們通常位於朝南／西南、接收更多日照的山坡上，所以葡萄成熟得更好，酒的風味更豐富、更複雜。這些術語不代表橡木桶，橡木桶在 Chablis 很少見；葡萄來自布根地任何地方代表的是 Bourgogne AOC。","Why are Alsace Grand Cru wines usually riper and fuller?":"為什麼 Alsace Grand Cru 的酒通常更成熟、更飽滿？","Sunnier east/south-east Vosges slopes":"孚日山脈朝東／東南、日照更多的坡地","High-yield vineyards on the plains":"平原上的高產量葡萄園","Compulsory fermentation in new oak":"必須在新橡木桶中發酵","Sugar added to the must":"在葡萄汁中加糖","Grand crus are on steep, well-exposed slopes sunnier than the plains.":"Grand cru 位於日照良好的陡坡上，比平原更晴朗。","Alsace Grand Cru wines must come from specific vineyards, mostly on steep Vosges foothills facing east and south-east. These positions receive more sunlight, so the grapes ripen further and the wines taste riper and are fuller-bodied than those from vineyards on the plains.":"Alsace Grand Cru 的酒必須來自特定的葡萄園，大多位於孚日山脈朝東和東南的陡峭山麓。這些位置接收更多日照，所以葡萄更成熟，酒嚐起來比平原葡萄園的更成熟、酒體更飽滿。","Which group of grapes is typically eligible for Alsace grands crus?":"哪一組品種典型地可以用於阿爾薩斯 grand cru？","Sauvignon Blanc, Semillon, Riesling":"白蘇維濃、榭密雍、麗絲玲","Riesling, Pinot Gris and Gewurztraminer are the typical Alsace grand cru grapes.":"麗絲玲、灰皮諾和格烏茲塔明那是阿爾薩斯 grand cru 的典型品種。","In Alsace grands crus the typical eligible grapes are Riesling, Pinot Gris and Gewurztraminer. Gewurztraminer makes some of the region's most prized wines alongside the other two. Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Viognier and Albariño are linked to other regions studied, such as Burgundy, the Loire, Condrieu and Rías Baixas.":"在阿爾薩斯 grand cru 中，典型的可用品種是麗絲玲、灰皮諾和格烏茲塔明那。格烏茲塔明那與另外兩個品種一起，釀出這個地區最受珍視的一些酒。夏多內、白蘇維濃、維歐尼耶和阿爾巴利諾則與課程中的其他產區有關，例如布根地、羅亞爾河、Condrieu 和 Rías Baixas。","What can white premier and grand crus from Meursault and Puligny-Montrachet develop in bottle?":"Meursault 和 Puligny-Montrachet 的 premier cru 和 grand cru 白酒在瓶中能發展出什麼？","Hazelnut and mushroom over decades":"數十年間發展出榛果和蘑菇","Vegetal notes within two years":"兩年內出現植物性氣息","These outstanding wines evolve for a long time, gaining hazelnut and mushroom.":"這些傑出的酒能長時間演變，增添榛果和蘑菇。","The premier cru and grand cru sites of Meursault and Puligny-Montrachet in the Côte de Beaune make outstanding Chardonnay, barrel fermented or matured and aged on lees. They can evolve for decades in bottle, developing tertiary hazelnut and mushroom, and many see them as the peak of Chardonnay.":"Côte de Beaune 的 Meursault 和 Puligny-Montrachet 的 premier cru 和 grand cru 園地，出產在橡木桶中發酵或熟成、並在酒渣上陳年的傑出夏多內。它們能在瓶中演變數十年，發展出榛果和蘑菇的三級香氣，許多人視之為夏多內的巔峰。","What is the difference between Alsace AOC and Alsace Grand Cru AOC?":"Alsace AOC 和 Alsace Grand Cru AOC 有什麼不同？","Whole region versus specific vineyards":"整個產區對比特定葡萄園","Dry wines versus always sweet wines":"不甜的酒對比一律是甜酒","Unoaked versus oaked wines":"不經橡木桶對比經橡木桶","Single varietals versus compulsory blends":"單一品種對比強制混調","Alsace AOC covers the whole region; Grand Cru requires specific selected vineyards.":"Alsace AOC 涵蓋整個產區；Grand Cru 則要求來自特定的精選葡萄園。","Alsace AOC is the regional appellation covering the whole area; wines usually show the grape and, from the 2021 vintage, sweetness on a standard scale. Alsace Grand Cru requires grapes from specific vineyards, mostly on the Vosges slopes. Sweetness can vary in both, and both can carry Vendanges tardives.":"Alsace AOC 是涵蓋整個地區的地區級法定產區；酒款通常標示品種，從 2021 年份起還要依標準刻度標示甜度。Alsace Grand Cru 要求葡萄來自特定的葡萄園，大多位於孚日山脈的坡地上。兩者的甜度都可能不同，也都可以標示 Vendanges tardives。","How does a Bordeaux Supérieur AOC differ from a Bordeaux AOC?":"Bordeaux Supérieur AOC 與 Bordeaux AOC 有什麼不同？","Slightly stricter rules on yields, ageing and alcohol":"在產量、陳年和酒精方面的規定稍嚴格一些","Grapes from the Left Bank only":"葡萄只來自左岸","It must be pure Cabernet Sauvignon":"必須是純卡本內蘇維濃","Grapes only from one classified Château":"葡萄只來自一座列級的 Château","Both cover all of Bordeaux; Supérieur simply has slightly stricter rules.":"兩者都涵蓋整個波爾多；Supérieur 只是規定稍嚴格一些。","Bordeaux AOC and Bordeaux Supérieur AOC are regional appellations: the grapes can come from anywhere in Bordeaux and the wines are usually Merlot-led blends. The difference is that Bordeaux Supérieur must meet slightly stricter rules on yields, ageing and minimum alcohol. It is not tied to one bank or to a classified Château.":"Bordeaux AOC 和 Bordeaux Supérieur AOC 是地區級法定產區：葡萄可以來自波爾多任何地方，酒款通常是以梅洛為主的混調。不同之處在於 Bordeaux Supérieur 必須符合產量、陳年和最低酒精方面稍嚴格的規定。它不限於某一岸，也不限於列級的 Château。","What does Grand Cru Classé indicate on a Bordeaux label?":"波爾多酒標上的 Grand Cru Classé 代表什麼？","A wine included in a classification of top Châteaux":"被列入頂級 Château 分級的酒","A wine made from grapes bought across the region":"用從全區買來的葡萄釀的酒","A Médoc wine left out of the classification":"未被列入分級的 Médoc 酒款","A wine with higher than normal yields":"產量高於正常水準的酒","Grand Cru Classé belongs to wines ranked in the classifications of some Bordeaux areas.":"Grand Cru Classé 屬於被列入某些波爾多地區分級的酒款。","Some Bordeaux areas drew up classifications to rank the best wines from the best Châteaux, and classified wines may use Grand Cru Classé or Cru Classé. Even though some classifications are old, they remain a strong sign of quality: these are expensive, sought-after wines that can age for decades. Unclassified Médoc wines may use Cru Bourgeois instead.":"波爾多有些地區制定了分級，為最好的 Château 中最好的酒排名，列級的酒款可以使用 Grand Cru Classé 或 Cru Classé。即使有些分級年代久遠，它們仍是強烈的品質指標：這些是昂貴、搶手、能陳年數十年的酒。未列級的 Médoc 酒款則可以使用 Cru Bourgeois。","Which wines can apply to use the term Cru Bourgeois?":"哪些酒可以申請使用 Cru Bourgeois 這個術語？","Médoc wines not classified as Grand Cru Classé":"未被列為 Grand Cru Classé 的 Médoc 酒款","Saint-Émilion and Pomerol wines":"Saint-Émilion 和 Pomerol 的酒款","Bordeaux AOC wines from the whole region":"來自全區的 Bordeaux AOC 酒款","Languedoc wines labelled Pays d'Oc IGP":"標示 Pays d'Oc IGP 的 Languedoc 酒款","Cru Bourgeois is for Médoc wines outside the Grand Cru Classé classification.":"Cru Bourgeois 適用於 Grand Cru Classé 分級之外的 Médoc 酒款。","The term Cru Bourgeois relates to the Médoc, on the Left Bank. Wines that have not been classified as Grand Cru Classé can apply to use it. With few exceptions they cost less than the classified Châteaux, but some are very good to outstanding and can age for a long time. Saint-Émilion and Pomerol are on the Right Bank instead.":"Cru Bourgeois 這個術語與左岸的 Médoc 有關。未被列為 Grand Cru Classé 的酒款可以申請使用。除了少數例外，它們比列級 Château 便宜，但有些非常好到傑出，能長期陳年。Saint-Émilion 和 Pomerol 則位於右岸。","Which statement about Cru Bourgeois wines is correct?":"關於 Cru Bourgeois 酒款，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","They usually cost less than classified wines, but some are outstanding":"它們通常比列級酒款便宜，但有些很傑出","They are always pricier than Grand Cru Classé":"它們總是比 Grand Cru Classé 更貴","They are simple wines to drink within a year":"它們是要在一年內喝掉的簡單酒款","They are made from grapes bought outside the Médoc":"它們是用 Médoc 以外買來的葡萄釀的","Apart from exceptions they do not reach classified prices, but some are very good to outstanding and age-worthy.":"除了例外，它們達不到列級酒款的價格，但有些非常好到傑出且適合陳年。","Cru Bourgeois wines are Médoc wines left out of the Grand Cru Classé classification. They generally lack the high prices of the classified Châteaux, but that does not make them simple: some reach very good to outstanding quality and can age for a long time in bottle. They are therefore often good value.":"Cru Bourgeois 酒款是被排除在 Grand Cru Classé 分級之外的 Médoc 酒款。它們一般沒有列級 Château 那樣的高價，但這不代表它們很簡單：有些達到非常好到傑出的品質，能在瓶中長期陳年。因此它們常常物超所值。","A label shows Château, Grand Cru Classé and Margaux AOC. What can you expect?":"一張酒標上標示 Château、Grand Cru Classé 和 Margaux AOC。你可以預期什麼？","A Cabernet-led blend, expensive and very long-lived":"以卡本內為主的混調，昂貴且非常長壽","A light Merlot from grapes across Bordeaux":"用全波爾多葡萄釀的輕盈梅洛","A wine from grapes bought from several growers":"用向數位種植者購買的葡萄釀的酒","An unclassified Médoc wine to drink now":"適合現在喝的未列級 Médoc 酒款","Margaux is on the Left Bank; Grand Cru Classé signals a classified, pricey, age-worthy wine.":"Margaux 位於左岸；Grand Cru Classé 表示列級、昂貴、適合陳年的酒。","Margaux AOC lies in the Haut-Médoc, on the Left Bank, where Cabernet Sauvignon usually dominates. Château means the wine is made from grapes grown on the estate's own land. Grand Cru Classé marks a classified wine: among Bordeaux's most expensive and sought-after, able to mature for many years or decades in bottle.":"Margaux AOC 位於左岸的 Haut-Médoc，那裡通常以卡本內蘇維濃為主。Château 表示這款酒是用酒莊自有土地上種植的葡萄釀的。Grand Cru Classé 標示列級酒款：屬於波爾多最昂貴、最搶手的酒，能在瓶中熟成多年甚至數十年。","What is the correct order of the Burgundy hierarchy, from lowest to highest?":"布根地分級由低到高的正確順序是什麼？","It rises from Bourgogne AOC to villages, then premiers crus and finally grands crus.":"從 Bourgogne AOC 往上到村莊級，接著是 premier cru，最後是 grand cru。","Bourgogne AOC covers the whole region; villages have their own appellations; premiers crus are selected vineyards within a village; grands crus are a handful of vineyards with their own AOC. The other orders mix up or reverse these levels.":"Bourgogne AOC 涵蓋整個地區；村莊有各自的法定產區；premier cru 是村莊內的精選葡萄園；grand cru 是少數幾座擁有自己 AOC 的葡萄園。其他順序都把這些等級搞混或顛倒了。","How does a Burgundy grand cru appear on the label?":"布根地的 grand cru 如何出現在酒標上？","The vineyard name with the words Grand Cru":"葡萄園名稱加上 Grand Cru 字樣","Only Bourgogne AOC, with nothing else":"只有 Bourgogne AOC，沒有其他資訊","The village name with Premier Cru":"村莊名稱加上 Premier Cru","The word Château and the estate name":"Château 字樣和酒莊名稱","Grands crus have their own AOC: the label shows the vineyard and Grand Cru.":"Grand cru 擁有自己的 AOC：酒標顯示葡萄園名稱和 Grand Cru。","They are a handful of small, well-sited vineyards, Burgundy's rarest and longest-lived wines. A village name with Premier Cru shows the level below; Château is a typical Bordeaux term.":"它們是少數幾座位置絕佳的小型葡萄園，出產布根地最稀有、最長壽的酒。村莊名稱加上 Premier Cru 表示的是下一級；Château 是典型的波爾多術語。","A label shows Gevrey-Chambertin Premier Cru plus a vineyard name. What does the vineyard name tell you?":"一張酒標上標示 Gevrey-Chambertin Premier Cru 加上一個葡萄園名稱。葡萄園名稱告訴你什麼？","The grapes come from a single premier cru vineyard":"葡萄來自單一 premier cru 葡萄園","The wine is a grand cru with its own appellation":"這款酒是擁有自己法定產區的 grand cru","The grapes were bought from several local growers":"葡萄是向數位當地種植者購買的","The wine blends several Côte d'Or villages":"這款酒混調了 Côte d'Or 的數個村莊","A wine from just one premier cru vineyard may show its name beside the village.":"只來自一座 premier cru 葡萄園的酒，可以在村莊名稱旁標示該葡萄園的名稱。","Wines made only from premier cru vineyards use Premier Cru with the village name; if there is just one vineyard, its name may appear too. A grand cru would have its own AOC instead, without the words Premier Cru.":"只用 premier cru 葡萄園葡萄釀的酒，使用 Premier Cru 加上村莊名稱；如果只有一座葡萄園，也可以標示它的名稱。Grand cru 則會擁有自己的 AOC，不使用 Premier Cru 字樣。","Why do Burgundy grands crus command such high prices?":"為什麼布根地的 grand cru 價格如此高昂？","Their quality and rarity":"它們的品質和稀有性","They come from large, high-yield vineyards that are easy to mechanise":"它們來自容易機械化的大型高產量葡萄園","The law requires ten years in barrel":"法律規定要在橡木桶中放十年","They are always sweet wines":"它們一定是甜酒","A few small vineyards give the most concentrated, long-lived wines: quality and rarity drive the price.":"少數幾座小型葡萄園出產最濃縮、最長壽的酒：品質和稀有性推高了價格。","Grands crus are small, well-sited plots that regularly give outstanding grapes. They are not large high-yield vineyards; no rule demands ten years in barrel, and Burgundy's reds and whites are dry.":"Grand cru 是位置絕佳的小地塊，經常產出傑出的葡萄。它們不是大型的高產量葡萄園；沒有規定要求在橡木桶中放十年，而布根地的紅酒和白酒都是不甜的。","What does the word Château indicate on a Bordeaux label?":"波爾多酒標上的 Château 這個字代表什麼？","Grapes grown on the producer's own land":"葡萄種植於生產者自有的土地上","That the wine was made in a historic castle over a century old":"這款酒是在有百年以上歷史的古堡中釀造的","That the wine is a Grand Cru Classé":"這款酒是 Grand Cru Classé","Grapes bought in from across the region":"葡萄是從全區買來的","Château means an estate: the wine comes from its own vineyards, not bought-in grapes.":"Château 代表一座酒莊：酒來自它自己的葡萄園，而不是買來的葡萄。","The term does not necessarily refer to a grand building. Nor does it mean the wine is classified: many Châteaux are not Grand Cru Classé.":"這個術語不一定指宏偉的建築。它也不代表這款酒已被列級：許多 Château 並不是 Grand Cru Classé。","Some Bordeaux classifications have not been updated for a long time. How should they be viewed?":"有些波爾多分級已經很久沒有更新了。應該如何看待它們？","Still a strong indication of quality":"仍然是強烈的品質指標","They no longer mean anything and have been abolished":"它們已經沒有意義，也被廢除了","They only mark simple wines for drinking young":"它們只標示要趁年輕喝的簡單酒款","They cover only the sweet wines of the Sauternes area":"它們只涵蓋 Sauternes 地區的甜酒","Even when old, these classifications are widely seen as a strong sign of quality.":"即使年代久遠，這些分級仍被廣泛視為強烈的品質指標。","Classified wines, which may state Grand Cru Classé or Cru Classé, are among Bordeaux's most expensive and sought-after and age for years or decades. They are neither simple wines nor only sweet ones.":"列級酒款可以標示 Grand Cru Classé 或 Cru Classé，屬於波爾多最昂貴、最搶手的酒，能陳年數年甚至數十年。它們既不是簡單的酒，也不只是甜酒。","Why does so much German label terminology relate to grape ripeness?":"為什麼這麼多德國酒標術語都與葡萄成熟度有關？","In Germany's cool climate ripeness is often hard to reach":"在德國涼爽的氣候中，成熟度常常很難達到","German grapes are always overripe":"德國葡萄總是過熟","Naming the grape is banned in Germany":"德國禁止標示品種","All German wines are sparkling":"所有德國酒都是氣泡酒","Reaching the desired ripeness is a struggle, so the categories are based on grape sugar.":"達到想要的成熟度很不容易，所以類別是以葡萄的糖分為基礎。","Ripeness is measured as sugar at harvest: from Landwein to Qualitätswein to the Prädikat levels, the minimum rises. The grapes are not overripe, the grape can be named (Riesling, for example) and not all wines are sparkling.":"成熟度以採收時的糖分衡量：從 Landwein 到 Qualitätswein 再到 Prädikat 等級，最低要求逐步提高。葡萄並沒有過熟，品種可以標示（例如 Riesling），也不是所有酒都是氣泡酒。","Which requirement applies to a wine labelled Qualitätswein?":"標示 Qualitätswein 的酒適用哪一項要求？","It must come from one of Germany's 13 winegrowing areas":"必須來自德國 13 個葡萄酒產區之一","It must be made from grapes frozen on the vine":"必須用在樹上結冰的葡萄釀造","It must always be sweet, with residual sugar":"必須一律是帶殘糖的甜酒","It must be a PGI wine from grapes anywhere in Germany":"必須是用德國各地葡萄釀的 PGI 酒款","Qualitätswein is a PDO wine from one of the 13 areas, with riper grapes than Landwein.":"Qualitätswein 是來自 13 個產區之一的 PDO 酒款，葡萄比 Landwein 更成熟。","Rheingau and Mosel are examples of these areas; the wines are usually more intense and fuller than Landwein, which is the PGI category. Frozen grapes are for Eiswein, and the wine need not be sweet.":"Rheingau 和 Mosel 是這些產區的例子；這些酒通常比 PGI 類別的 Landwein 更濃郁、更飽滿。冰凍葡萄用於 Eiswein，而這款酒不必是甜的。","Which two Prädikat categories require the same minimum sugar at harvest?":"哪兩個 Prädikat 類別要求相同的採收最低糖分？","Eiswein and Beerenauslese":"Eiswein 和 Beerenauslese","Auslese and Trockenbeerenauslese, the two selected harvests":"Auslese 和 Trockenbeerenauslese，兩種精選採收","Spätlese and Eiswein":"Spätlese 和 Eiswein","Eiswein and Beerenauslese are the one exception: the same sugar minimum.":"Eiswein 和 Beerenauslese 是唯一的例外：最低糖分相同。","The six categories rise in minimum sugar: Kabinett, Spätlese, Auslese, then Beerenauslese and Eiswein level, and finally Trockenbeerenauslese, the highest.":"六個類別的最低糖分逐級遞增：Kabinett、Spätlese、Auslese，接著是同一級的 Beerenauslese 和 Eiswein，最後是最高的 Trockenbeerenauslese。","Why are Beerenauslese, Trockenbeerenauslese and Eiswein naturally sweet and low in alcohol?":"為什麼 Beerenauslese、Trockenbeerenauslese 和 Eiswein 天然甜美且酒精低？","Yeast cannot ferment such high sugar levels":"酵母無法發酵這麼高的糖分","The grapes are picked unripe and early":"葡萄在未成熟時提早採收","The alcohol is removed by distillation":"酒精被蒸餾去除了","Sugar concentrated on the vine is so high that yeast cannot convert it all.":"在樹上濃縮的糖分高到酵母無法全部轉化。","Sugar is concentrated on the vine by botrytis or frost. Intense flavours and high acidity let these wines age for decades. No sugar is added, the grapes are not unripe and no alcohol is distilled off.":"糖分是透過貴腐菌或霜凍在樹上濃縮的。濃郁的風味和高酸度讓這些酒能陳年數十年。沒有添加糖，葡萄也沒有未成熟，更沒有蒸餾去除酒精。","Compared with a Kabinett from the same area, what does a Riesling Spätlese usually offer?":"與同一產區的 Kabinett 相比，麗絲玲 Spätlese 通常帶來什麼？","More concentrated flavours and fuller body":"風味更濃縮，酒體更飽滿","Lighter body and even more delicate green-apple aromas":"酒體更輕盈，青蘋果香氣更細緻","Botrytis notes of honey and dried fruit":"帶有蜂蜜和果乾的貴腐氣息","Bubbles from a second fermentation":"來自二次發酵的氣泡","Spätlese means late harvest: more concentration and body than Kabinett.":"Spätlese 是晚收的意思：比 Kabinett 更濃縮、酒體更飽滿。","It shows riper citrus (lemon, lime) and some stone fruit such as peach. Kabinett is the lightest, most delicate category; botrytis honey and dried fruit belong to BA and TBA; it is not sparkling.":"它展現更成熟的柑橘（檸檬、萊姆）和一些桃子等核果。Kabinett 是最輕盈、最細緻的類別；貴腐的蜂蜜和果乾屬於 BA 和 TBA；它也不是氣泡酒。","Which flavours would you expect from a Riesling Auslese?":"你會預期麗絲玲 Auslese 有哪些風味？","Apricot, mango and dried fruit":"杏桃、芒果和果乾","Green apple, lime and blossom, delicate and light":"青蘋果、萊姆和花香，細緻輕盈","Selected extra-ripe bunches give apricot, mango and dried fruit.":"精選的過熟果串帶來杏桃、芒果和果乾。","Auslese means selected harvest; it can be dry (trocken) but usually has some sweetness. Green apple, lime and blossom describe Kabinett; the other options are red-wine profiles.":"Auslese 是精選採收的意思；它可以是不甜的（trocken），但通常帶有一些甜味。青蘋果、萊姆和花香描述的是 Kabinett；其他選項則是紅酒的風味特徵。","Why does Eiswein command high prices?":"為什麼 Eiswein 價格高昂？","Suitable weather not every year, hard work, tiny yields":"並非每年都有合適的天氣，工作辛苦，產量極少","The grapes get noble rot in every vineyard, every year":"每座葡萄園每年都會出現貴腐","It must spend twenty years in barrel by law":"依法必須在橡木桶中放二十年","It is made from grapes frozen in a cold store":"它是用在冷藏庫中冷凍的葡萄釀的","The right frost does not come every year, the work is intense and yields are tiny.":"合適的霜凍並非每年都會出現，工作繁重，產量極少。","Eiswein comes from grapes frozen on the vine, not in the winery, and botrytis plays no part. There is no twenty-year barrel rule; the price comes from rarity and effort.":"Eiswein 來自在樹上而不是在酒廠中結冰的葡萄，貴腐菌不參與其中。沒有二十年橡木桶的規定；價格來自稀有性和付出的心力。","Which of these terms on its own guarantees a sweet German wine?":"下列哪一個術語單獨就能保證是甜的德國酒？","Auslese, from hand-selected extra-ripe bunches":"Auslese，來自人工精選的過熟果串","A Beerenauslese is always sweet.":"Beerenauslese 一定是甜的。","Kabinett, Spätlese and Auslese often have some sweetness but can be dry; where it is unclear, producers may add trocken or halbtrocken. In BA, sugar is too high to ferment fully.":"Kabinett、Spätlese 和 Auslese 常帶有一些甜味，但也可以是不甜的；在不清楚的情況下，生產者可以加上 trocken 或 halbtrocken。在 BA 中，糖分太高，無法完全發酵。","Since the 2021 vintage, what must an Alsace AOC label show?":"從 2021 年份起，Alsace AOC 的酒標必須標示什麼？","The sweetness level on a standard scale":"依標準刻度標示的甜度","A grand cru vineyard name, even for regional wines":"grand cru 葡萄園名稱，即使是地區級酒款","The word Château":"Château 字樣","The number of years spent in barrel":"在橡木桶中的年數","Besides the grape, the label must show sweetness on a standardised scale.":"除了品種，酒標還必須以標準化刻度標示甜度。","Alsace AOC is the regional appellation for the whole area, and wines usually name the grape. A vineyard name appears on Grand Cru wines, not regional ones; Château is a Bordeaux term.":"Alsace AOC 是涵蓋整個地區的地區級法定產區，酒款通常會標示品種。葡萄園名稱出現在 Grand Cru 酒款上，而不是地區級酒款；Château 是波爾多的術語。","Which statement about Vendanges tardives in Alsace is correct?":"關於阿爾薩斯的 Vendanges tardives，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It can appear on both Alsace and Alsace Grand Cru wines":"它可以出現在 Alsace 和 Alsace Grand Cru 酒款上","It is reserved for regional wines only":"它只保留給地區級酒款","It means a dry wine from early-picked grapes":"它代表用早採葡萄釀的不甜酒","It applies only to Gewurztraminer":"它只適用於格烏茲塔明那","Both Alsace and Alsace Grand Cru wines may be labelled Vendanges tardives.":"Alsace 和 Alsace Grand Cru 酒款都可以標示 Vendanges tardives。","The term means late harvest and usually marks a medium to sweet wine from extra-ripe grapes. It can apply to Pinot Gris, Riesling and Gewurztraminer, not just one; it does not mean a dry wine from early grapes.":"這個術語是晚收的意思，通常標示用過熟葡萄釀的半甜至甜型酒。它可以適用於灰皮諾、麗絲玲和格烏茲塔明那，不只一個品種；它不代表用早採葡萄釀的不甜酒。","Which region produces almost all Gamay wine?":"哪個產區出產幾乎所有的加美葡萄酒？","Gamay is known worldwide, yet its wines come almost exclusively from Beaujolais.":"加美聞名全球，但它的酒幾乎都來自 Beaujolais。","Gamay is a rare case: an internationally known grape whose wines come almost entirely from one region, Beaujolais, just south of Burgundy. There, a moderate climate and the winemaking techniques chosen give fresh, fruity reds. Burgundy is next door but is Pinot Noir country; the Rhône and Languedoc rely mainly on Grenache and Syrah.":"加美（Gamay）是一個罕見的例子：國際知名的品種，酒款卻幾乎全部來自單一產區 Beaujolais，就在布根地以南。在那裡，溫和的氣候和所選用的釀造技術，帶來清爽、果香豐富的紅酒。布根地就在隔壁，但那是黑皮諾的天下；隆河和 Languedoc 主要仰賴格那希和希哈。","Which structure is typical of a Gamay wine?":"哪一種結構是加美葡萄酒的典型特徵？","Low acidity, low to medium tannins":"低酸度，單寧低至中等","Gamay combines high acidity with modest tannins and prominent red fruit.":"加美結合了高酸度、適度的單寧和突出的紅色水果。","Gamay gives fresh reds thanks to high acidity, while its tannins stay low to medium; on top of that, Beaujolais techniques extract colour without much tannin. Aromas recall raspberry, red cherry and red plum. High tannin and low acidity describe very different grapes, more suited to warm climates or long-aged wines.":"加美因為高酸度而釀出清爽的紅酒，而它的單寧保持低至中等；此外，Beaujolais 的技術能萃取顏色而不帶出太多單寧。香氣讓人想到覆盆子、紅櫻桃和紅李。高單寧和低酸度描述的是截然不同的品種，更適合溫暖氣候或長期陳年的酒。","Why do some Beaujolais wines smell of banana and candy?":"為什麼有些 Beaujolais 聞起來有香蕉和糖果味？","Because of techniques that extract colour but little tannin":"因為萃取顏色但少萃取單寧的技術","Because of long maturation in new oak barrels":"因為在新橡木桶中長時間熟成","Because of extended ageing in bottle":"因為長時間瓶中陳年","Because of very low yields from old vines":"因為老藤的極低產量","Beaujolais techniques maximise colour, limit tannin and can create banana and candy aromas.":"Beaujolais 的技術最大化顏色、限制單寧，並可能產生香蕉和糖果香氣。","In Beaujolais, winemakers often use methods that extract plenty of colour and little tannin, to make soft, fruity reds. A side effect of these techniques is aromas of banana and candy. They do not come from oak, which Gamay rarely sees, nor from bottle ageing, which actually makes these wines lose their fresh fruit.":"在 Beaujolais，釀酒師常使用能萃取大量顏色、少量單寧的方法，釀出柔和、果香豐富的紅酒。這些技術的副作用就是香蕉和糖果的香氣。它們不是來自加美很少使用的橡木桶，也不是來自瓶中陳年，瓶中陳年其實會讓這些酒失去新鮮果味。","Where is Beaujolais located?":"Beaujolais 位於哪裡？","Directly south of Burgundy":"就在布根地以南","Directly north of Champagne":"就在 Champagne 以北","East of Provence":"普羅旺斯以東","West of Bordeaux":"波爾多以西","Beaujolais is a moderate-climate region lying immediately south of Burgundy.":"Beaujolais 是緊鄰布根地南邊的溫和氣候產區。","Beaujolais borders Burgundy to the north and has a moderate climate, well suited to a grape like Gamay that gives fresh, light- to medium-bodied wines. Its appellation system also resembles that of the Rhône further south: a regional base, a Villages level and, at the top, crus such as Fleurie.":"Beaujolais 北邊與布根地相鄰，屬於溫和氣候，非常適合加美這種釀出清爽、酒體輕盈至中等酒款的品種。它的法定產區體系也與更南邊的隆河相似：地區級的基礎、Villages 等級，以及最頂端的 Fleurie 等特級村莊（cru）。","Which appellation gives the lightest, simplest wines of Beaujolais?":"哪一個法定產區出產 Beaujolais 最輕盈、最簡單的酒？","Beaujolais AOC is the base level, mostly from flat, fertile, high-yielding southern vineyards.":"Beaujolais AOC 是基礎等級，大多來自南部平坦、肥沃、高產量的葡萄園。","Beaujolais AOC may use grapes from anywhere in the region, but most come from the flat, fertile south. High yields mean less concentration, which is why these are the lightest and simplest wines. Beaujolais Villages, from northern slopes, has more intensity and body; crus such as Fleurie are the most concentrated and structured.":"Beaujolais AOC 可以使用產區任何地方的葡萄，但大多來自平坦肥沃的南部。高產量代表濃縮度較低，這就是為什麼這些是最輕盈、最簡單的酒。來自北部坡地的 Beaujolais Villages 更濃郁、酒體更飽滿；Fleurie 等 cru 則最濃縮、結構最紮實。","Why do Beaujolais Villages wines have more intensity and body than basic Beaujolais?":"為什麼 Beaujolais Villages 的酒比基本的 Beaujolais 更濃郁、酒體更飽滿？","Sunny slopes and warm, free-draining soils help ripening":"陽光充足的坡地和溫暖、排水良好的土壤有助於成熟","Fertile plains and high yields increase concentration":"肥沃的平原和高產量提高了濃縮度","Long maturation in new oak adds body":"在新橡木桶中長時間熟成增添了酒體","A cooler, foggier climate slows ripening":"更涼爽、多霧的氣候減緩成熟","In the north, sloping vineyards get more sun and warm, free-draining soils aid ripening.":"在北部，坡地葡萄園接收更多陽光，溫暖、排水良好的土壤有助於成熟。","The northern villages entitled to Beaujolais Villages have sloping vineyards with more sun exposure and warm, well-drained soils. Riper grapes give wines with greater fruit intensity and more body. Fertile, high-yielding plains are instead typical of basic Beaujolais, and Gamay rarely sees oak.":"有權使用 Beaujolais Villages 的北部村莊，擁有日照更多的坡地葡萄園，以及溫暖、排水良好的土壤。更成熟的葡萄釀出果味更濃郁、酒體更飽滿的酒。肥沃、高產量的平原則是基本 Beaujolais 的典型特徵，而加美很少使用橡木桶。","What is Fleurie AOC?":"Fleurie AOC 是什麼？","One of the Beaujolais crus":"Beaujolais 的 cru 之一","One of the Southern Rhône crus":"南隆河的 cru 之一","A Provence rosé appellation":"普羅旺斯的粉紅酒法定產區","A Languedoc-Roussillon village":"Languedoc-Roussillon 的一個村莊","Fleurie is one of the ten Beaujolais crus, the top of the pyramid, made from Gamay.":"Fleurie 是 Beaujolais 十個 cru 之一，位於金字塔頂端，以加美釀造。","Within the Beaujolais Villages area, ten zones have been given their own appellation: the crus. Fleurie AOC is among the best known. These Gamay wines are the most concentrated and structured of the region, with intense red fruit and a medium to long finish; many are drunk young, but some can develop in bottle.":"在 Beaujolais Villages 區域內，有十個區域被賦予自己的法定產區：這些就是 cru。Fleurie AOC 是其中最知名的之一。這些加美酒款是這個地區最濃縮、結構最紮實的酒，帶有濃郁的紅色水果和中等至長的餘韻；許多是趁年輕喝，但有些能在瓶中發展。","Why is Beaujolais often served lightly chilled?":"為什麼 Beaujolais 常略微冰鎮後飲用？","To highlight the freshness of its delicate red fruit":"為了突顯它細緻紅色水果的清新感","To soften its very high tannins":"為了柔化它非常高的單寧","To hide the aromas of new oak":"為了掩蓋新橡木桶的香氣","To tone down its marked sweetness":"為了緩和它明顯的甜味","A slightly cool temperature brings out the freshness of Gamay's red fruit.":"略涼的溫度能帶出加美紅色水果的清新感。","Beaujolais is a dry red with low to medium tannins, high acidity and almost never any oak character. Its strength is fresh, delicate red fruit, which a slightly cool temperature shows off. The other answers do not fit: tannins are not high, oak is rare and the wine is not sweet.":"Beaujolais 是不甜的紅酒，單寧低至中等，酸度高，幾乎從不帶橡木特徵。它的強項是清新細緻的紅色水果，略涼的溫度正好能展現這一點。其他答案都不符合：單寧不高，橡木桶很少見，酒也不甜。","What does Grenache need to ripen successfully?":"格那希需要什麼才能順利成熟？","Plenty of summer rain":"充沛的夏季降雨","Grenache is a black grape that only ripens properly with warmth.":"格那希是只有在溫暖時才能好好成熟的黑葡萄。","Grenache needs a warm climate, which is why it thrives in the Southern Rhône, Languedoc-Roussillon, Priorat and the warm Barossa Valley and McLaren Vale. When ripe it is high in sugar and low in acidity. It also gives its best wines when yields are controlled, so very high yields work against quality.":"格那希（Grenache）需要溫暖的氣候，這就是為什麼它在南隆河、Languedoc-Roussillon、Priorat 以及溫暖的 Barossa Valley 和 McLaren Vale 生長茁壯。成熟時它糖分高、酸度低。它也在產量受控時釀出最好的酒，所以非常高的產量不利於品質。","What are ripe Grenache grapes typically like?":"成熟的格那希葡萄通常是什麼樣子？","High sugar and low acidity":"糖分高，酸度低","Low sugar and high acidity":"糖分低，酸度高","Thick skins and high tannin":"果皮厚，單寧高","High acidity and high tannin":"酸度高，單寧高","Ripe Grenache builds up sugar (hence alcohol) but keeps little acidity.":"成熟的格那希累積糖分（因此酒精高），但保留的酸度很少。","In the warmth where it grows, Grenache builds up a lot of sugar and loses acidity, so its wines are often high in alcohol and soft, like full-bodied Châteauneuf-du-Pape. Its skins are thin, however, so tannins are low to medium. That is why it is blended with Syrah or Tempranillo, which add colour, acidity and tannin.":"在它生長的溫暖環境中，格那希累積大量糖分並失去酸度，所以它的酒常常酒精高、口感柔和，就像酒體飽滿的 Châteauneuf-du-Pape。不過它的果皮薄，所以單寧低至中等。這就是為什麼它會與能增添顏色、酸度和單寧的希哈或田帕尼優混調。","Why do Grenache wines have low to medium tannins?":"為什麼格那希的酒單寧低至中等？","Because its skins are thin":"因為它的果皮薄","Because it ripens in cool climates":"因為它在涼爽氣候中成熟","Because it is always picked unripe":"因為它總是在未成熟時採收","Because it is always aged in new oak":"因為它總是在新橡木桶中陳年","Thin skins hold less tannin, so Grenache wines stay soft.":"薄果皮含有的單寧較少，所以格那希的酒保持柔和。","A red wine's tannins come mainly from the skins. Grenache has thin skins, so it gives wines with low to medium tannins and red fruit such as strawberry and cherry. It grows in warm, not cool, climates, and simple wines are often unoaked; when oak is used, some producers prefer old barrels.":"紅酒的單寧主要來自果皮。格那希果皮薄，所以釀出的酒單寧低至中等，帶有草莓和櫻桃等紅色水果。它生長在溫暖而非涼爽的氣候中，簡單的酒款常不經橡木桶；使用橡木桶時，有些生產者偏好舊桶。","Which combination of aromas is typical of Grenache?":"哪一組香氣是格那希的典型特徵？","Strawberry, red cherry, white pepper":"草莓、紅櫻桃、白胡椒","Blackberry, green pepper, tomato leaf":"黑莓、青椒、番茄葉","Blackberry, black plum, clove":"黑莓、黑李、丁香","Banana, candy, raspberry":"香蕉、糖果、覆盆子","Grenache gives red fruit (strawberry, red plum, red cherry) and sometimes white pepper and liquorice.":"格那希帶來紅色水果（草莓、紅李、紅櫻桃），有時還有白胡椒和甘草。","Grenache's profile is red fruit, led by strawberry, sometimes with spice such as white pepper and liquorice; simple Côtes du Rhône show exactly this red fruit and white pepper. Green pepper and tomato leaf point to underripe Carmenère, blackberry and clove to oaked Malbec, and banana and candy to some Beaujolais.":"格那希的風味特徵是以草莓為首的紅色水果，有時帶有白胡椒和甘草等香料；簡單的 Côtes du Rhône 展現的正是這種紅色水果和白胡椒。青椒和番茄葉指向未完全成熟的卡門內爾，黑莓和丁香指向經橡木桶的馬爾貝克，香蕉和糖果則指向某些 Beaujolais。","Why is Grenache often blended with Syrah or Tempranillo?":"為什麼格那希常與希哈或田帕尼優混調？","To add colour, acidity and tannin":"為了增添顏色、酸度和單寧","To add sugar and alcohol":"為了增添糖分和酒精","To reduce colour and tannin":"為了減少顏色和單寧","To add banana and candy notes":"為了增添香蕉和糖果氣息","Syrah and Tempranillo make up for what Grenache lacks: colour, acidity and tannin.":"希哈和田帕尼優彌補了格那希所缺乏的：顏色、酸度和單寧。","Grenache ripens with plenty of sugar and therefore alcohol, but has little acidity and, because of its thin skins, modest tannins. Blending it with Syrah in France or Tempranillo in Spain gives the wine more colour, freshness and structure. Sugar and alcohol, on the other hand, Grenache already supplies in abundance.":"格那希成熟時糖分充足、因此酒精也高，但酸度很少，而且由於果皮薄，單寧也不多。在法國與希哈、在西班牙與田帕尼優混調，能讓酒有更多顏色、清新感和結構。另一方面，糖分和酒精則是格那希本身就大量提供的。","Why do some Grenache producers prefer old oak to new oak?":"為什麼有些格那希生產者偏好舊橡木桶而不是新橡木桶？","So as not to mask its delicate red fruit":"以免掩蓋它細緻的紅色水果","To increase its already high tannins":"為了增加它已經很高的單寧","To add vanilla and coconut notes":"為了增添香草和椰子氣息","To raise its natural acidity":"為了提高它的天然酸度","Old oak gives fewer flavours than new oak and lets Grenache's delicate fruit show.":"舊橡木桶給的風味比新桶少，能讓格那希細緻的果味展現出來。","Very good or outstanding Grenache is often matured in barrel for extra complexity. New oak, however, adds a lot of flavour, such as vanilla, which can smother the grape's delicate red fruit. That is why some producers prefer old barrels. Grenache's tannins are not high, and oak does not raise acidity.":"非常好或傑出的格那希常在橡木桶中熟成以增添複雜度。不過，新橡木桶會增添大量香草等風味，可能掩蓋這個品種細緻的紅色水果。這就是為什麼有些生產者偏好舊桶。格那希的單寧並不高，而橡木桶也不會提高酸度。","What role do the large stones play in Châteauneuf-du-Pape vineyards?":"Châteauneuf-du-Pape 葡萄園中的大石頭扮演什麼角色？","They absorb heat by day and release it to the vines at night":"白天吸收熱量，夜間把熱量釋放給葡萄樹","They reflect light and cool the bunches":"反射光線，讓果串降溫","They hold water and increase yields":"保存水分，提高產量","They protect the vines from hail":"保護葡萄樹免受冰雹侵襲","The stones store daytime heat and release it at night, helping Grenache ripen fully.":"石頭儲存白天的熱量並在夜間釋放，幫助格那希完全成熟。","Many Châteauneuf-du-Pape vineyards are covered with large round stones. By day they heat up in the sun; at night they radiate that heat back to the vines. The extra warmth helps heat-loving Grenache reach full ripeness, giving full-bodied, high-alcohol wines that develop dried fruit, earth and meat with age.":"許多 Châteauneuf-du-Pape 的葡萄園覆蓋著大顆的圓石。白天它們在陽光下變熱；夜間則把熱量輻射回葡萄樹。這些額外的熱量幫助喜愛溫暖的格那希完全成熟，釀出酒體飽滿、酒精高、陳年後會發展出果乾、泥土和肉味的酒。","Which appellation is the broadest, simplest base level of the Rhône?":"哪一個法定產區是隆河範圍最廣、最簡單的基礎等級？","Côtes du Rhône AOC covers the whole valley and gives simple, medium-bodied reds for early drinking.":"Côtes du Rhône AOC 涵蓋整個河谷，出產簡單、酒體中等、適合早飲的紅酒。","The Rhône has a hierarchy similar to Beaujolais. At the base, Côtes du Rhône AOC covers the whole valley, but the grapes come almost entirely from the south: simple, medium-bodied wines with red fruit and white pepper. Above it is Côtes du Rhône Villages, more intense and complex; at the top are the crus, such as Châteauneuf-du-Pape in the south and Crozes-Hermitage in the north.":"隆河的分級與 Beaujolais 相似。在基礎等級，Côtes du Rhône AOC 涵蓋整個河谷，但葡萄幾乎全部來自南部：簡單、酒體中等、帶有紅色水果和白胡椒的酒。往上是 Côtes du Rhône Villages，更濃郁、更複雜；頂端是 cru，例如南部的 Châteauneuf-du-Pape 和北部的 Crozes-Hermitage。","Which wine style is Côtes de Provence AOC best known for?":"Côtes de Provence AOC 最著名的是哪一種酒款風格？","Dry, pale-coloured rosé":"不甜、顏色淺的粉紅酒","Powerful, long-lived reds":"強勁、長壽的紅酒","Sweet, deeply coloured rosé":"甜、顏色深的粉紅酒","Light reds served chilled":"冰鎮飲用的輕盈紅酒","Provence is famous for dry, pale rosé, mostly Côtes de Provence, often with Grenache in the blend.":"普羅旺斯以不甜、淺色的粉紅酒聞名，大多是 Côtes de Provence，混調中常有格那希。","Provence lies east of Languedoc-Roussillon and is best known for dry, pale rosé, most of it from the Côtes de Provence appellation. Grenache, with its red fruit, is often a key part of the blend alongside other local grapes. Light reds served chilled bring Beaujolais to mind instead.":"普羅旺斯位於 Languedoc-Roussillon 以東，最著名的是不甜、淺色的粉紅酒，大多來自 Côtes de Provence 法定產區。帶有紅色水果的格那希，常是混調中與其他在地品種並列的關鍵部分。冰鎮飲用的輕盈紅酒則讓人想到 Beaujolais。","In which region is Minervois AOC?":"Minervois AOC 位於哪個產區？","Minervois is one of the leading red wine appellations of Languedoc-Roussillon.":"Minervois 是 Languedoc-Roussillon 主要的紅酒法定產區之一。","In warm Languedoc-Roussillon, Grenache ripens well and gives red fruit and body to blends with other local grapes, Syrah included. Minervois AOC is one of the region's most important appellations for reds. The Southern Rhône's flagship is Châteauneuf-du-Pape, Provence is known for rosé and Beaujolais for Gamay.":"在溫暖的 Languedoc-Roussillon，格那希成熟良好，為與希哈等其他在地品種的混調帶來紅色水果和酒體。Minervois AOC 是這個地區最重要的紅酒法定產區之一。南隆河的旗艦是 Châteauneuf-du-Pape，普羅旺斯以粉紅酒著稱，Beaujolais 則以加美著稱。","Why is Priorat Garnacha so powerful and concentrated?":"為什麼 Priorat 的 Garnacha 如此強勁濃縮？","Very old vines in a warm, dry area give tiny yields":"溫暖乾燥地區的非常古老葡萄樹，產量極少","Young vines on fertile plains give high yields":"肥沃平原上的年輕葡萄樹，產量很高","A cool, rainy climate lengthens ripening":"涼爽多雨的氣候延長了成熟期","Blending with Gamay adds body and tannin":"與加美混調增添了酒體和單寧","Priorat's old vines, in a warm, dry climate, produce few, highly concentrated grapes.":"Priorat 的老藤在溫暖乾燥的氣候中，產出少量高度濃縮的葡萄。","Priorat DOCa, in Catalunya, is a warm, dry area with very old Garnacha vines. These vines give tiny yields of concentrated grapes, producing Spain's most powerful, full-bodied Garnacha wines. Usually blended with other black grapes, they can age for a long time and develop dried fruit and caramel in bottle.":"位於加泰隆尼亞的 Priorat DOCa 是溫暖乾燥的地區，擁有非常古老的 Garnacha 葡萄樹。這些葡萄樹產量極少，葡萄高度濃縮，釀出西班牙最強勁、酒體最飽滿的 Garnacha 酒款。它們通常與其他黑葡萄混調，能長期陳年，在瓶中發展出果乾和焦糖。","Besides reds, which Garnacha style is Navarra DO known for?":"除了紅酒，Navarra DO 還以哪一種 Garnacha 風格聞名？","Dry rosé":"不甜的粉紅酒","Sweet whites":"甜白酒","Sparkling reds":"氣泡紅酒","Fortified reds":"加烈紅酒","In Navarra, Garnacha adds body and red fruit to reds and is also known for dry rosé.":"在 Navarra，Garnacha 為紅酒增添酒體和紅色水果，也以不甜的粉紅酒聞名。","Navarra neighbours Rioja. In both, Garnacha gives body and fresh red fruit to the wines, but Navarra is also known for dry rosé. That is no accident: Garnacha's red fruit makes it ideal for short-maceration rosé, drunk chilled and young.":"Navarra 與 Rioja 相鄰。在兩地，Garnacha 都為酒帶來酒體和新鮮的紅色水果，但 Navarra 也以不甜的粉紅酒聞名。這並非偶然：Garnacha 的紅色水果讓它非常適合短時間浸皮的粉紅酒，冰鎮後趁年輕喝。","Which Australian regions are known for very old Grenache vines?":"澳洲哪些產區以非常古老的格那希葡萄樹聞名？","Barossa Valley and McLaren Vale":"Barossa Valley 和 McLaren Vale","Clare Valley and Eden Valley":"Clare Valley 和 Eden Valley","Margaret River and Coonawarra":"Margaret River 和 Coonawarra","The warm Barossa Valley and McLaren Vale in South Australia have many old Grenache vines.":"南澳溫暖的 Barossa Valley 和 McLaren Vale 有許多格那希老藤。","Grenache needs warmth, and the warm regions of Barossa Valley and McLaren Vale are home to many old vines. They give outstanding wines with concentrated red fruit, spice and long ageing potential, as well as Shiraz blends that can resemble Châteauneuf-du-Pape. The other pairs of regions are linked to other grapes.":"格那希需要熱量，而溫暖的 Barossa Valley 和 McLaren Vale 擁有許多老藤。它們出產帶有濃縮紅色水果、香料和長期陳年潛力的傑出酒款，以及可能類似 Châteauneuf-du-Pape 的希拉茲混調。其他產區組合則與其他品種有關。","Which method is commonly used to make Grenache rosé?":"釀造格那希粉紅酒常用哪一種方法？","Short maceration on the skins":"短時間浸皮","Long maceration and oak ageing":"長時間浸皮和橡木桶陳年","Fortification during fermentation":"在發酵期間加烈","Thanks to its red fruit, Grenache is widely used for short-maceration rosé.":"由於帶有紅色水果，格那希廣泛用於短時間浸皮的粉紅酒。","With short maceration, the juice stays in contact with the skins only briefly, picking up a pink colour and the grape's fruit. Grenache, with its strawberry and red cherry, is ideal for this style: dry to medium rosés for drinking chilled and young, like those of Navarra or Côtes de Provence.":"短時間浸皮時，果汁只與果皮短暫接觸，染上粉紅色和葡萄的果味。帶有草莓和紅櫻桃的格那希非常適合這種風格：不甜至半甜的粉紅酒，冰鎮後趁年輕喝，例如 Navarra 或 Côtes de Provence 的酒款。","Which conditions let Ribera del Duero Tempranillo be full-bodied yet fresh-fruited?":"哪些條件讓 Ribera del Duero 的田帕尼優酒體飽滿卻保有新鮮果味？","Altitude, warm days and cool nights":"海拔、溫暖的白天和涼爽的夜晚","Closeness to the sea and frequent fog":"靠近海洋和頻繁的霧氣","Fertile plains and high yields":"肥沃的平原和高產量","Stones that warm the vines at night":"在夜間為葡萄樹保溫的石頭","At altitude, warm days and cool nights give very full-bodied wines with fresh black fruit.":"在高海拔，溫暖的白天和涼爽的夜晚帶來酒體非常飽滿、帶新鮮黑色水果的酒。","Ribera del Duero DO lies inland in Spain, at high altitude. Warm days ripen Tempranillo well, giving very full body, while cool nights keep the black fruit fresh. The region makes very good to outstanding wines. Stones that warm vines at night are a feature of Châteauneuf-du-Pape instead.":"Ribera del Duero DO 位於西班牙內陸的高海拔地區。溫暖的白天讓田帕尼優好好成熟，帶來非常飽滿的酒體，而涼爽的夜晚則保留黑色水果的新鮮感。這個產區出產非常好到傑出的酒款。在夜間為葡萄樹保溫的石頭則是 Châteauneuf-du-Pape 的特色。","Which notes does new oak typically give a Tempranillo?":"新橡木桶通常為田帕尼優帶來哪些氣息？","Vanilla, smoke, cedar":"香草、煙燻、雪松","Mushroom, leather, dried fruit":"蘑菇、皮革、果乾","Green pepper, tomato leaf":"青椒、番茄葉","Small new oak barrels add secondary notes of vanilla, smoke and cedar and soften tannins.":"小型新橡木桶增添香草、煙燻和雪松的二級氣息，並柔化單寧。","Traditionally, in many parts of Spain Tempranillo is matured in small new oak barrels. The oak brings secondary aromas such as vanilla, smoke and cedar. Mushroom, leather and dried fruit are tertiary notes that appear after years in bottle; banana and candy belong to Beaujolais, and green pepper to underripe Carmenère.":"傳統上，在西班牙許多地方，田帕尼優（Tempranillo）在小型新橡木桶中熟成。橡木帶來香草、煙燻和雪松等二級香氣。蘑菇、皮革和果乾是瓶中多年後出現的三級氣息；香蕉和糖果屬於 Beaujolais，青椒則屬於未完全成熟的卡門內爾。","Which tertiary notes can a high-quality Tempranillo develop in bottle?":"高品質的田帕尼優在瓶中能發展出哪些三級氣息？","Strawberry, red cherry, blackberry":"草莓、紅櫻桃、黑莓","Coffee, chocolate, smoke":"咖啡、巧克力、煙燻","With bottle age the best Tempranillo develops mushroom, leather and dried fruit.":"經過瓶中陳年，最好的田帕尼優會發展出蘑菇、皮革和果乾。","Tertiary notes come from long ageing. Very good or outstanding Tempranillo, often also aged in bottle before release, develops mushroom, leather and dried fruit. Strawberry, red cherry and blackberry are primary grape aromas; vanilla, smoke and cedar are secondary, from oak; coffee and chocolate are oak-related notes in other grapes.":"三級氣息來自長期陳年。非常好或傑出的田帕尼優，上市前常也經過瓶中陳年，會發展出蘑菇、皮革和果乾。草莓、紅櫻桃和黑莓是葡萄的一級香氣；香草、煙燻和雪松是來自橡木的二級香氣；咖啡和巧克力則是其他品種中與橡木相關的氣息。","What characterises Catalunya DO for Tempranillo?":"就田帕尼優而言，Catalunya DO 的特色是什麼？","Large volumes in a wide range of styles":"產量大，風格範圍廣","Only Gran Reserva wines from old vines":"只有來自老藤的 Gran Reserva 酒款","Only dry rosés for drinking young":"只有要趁年輕喝的不甜粉紅酒","High altitude and tiny yields":"高海拔和極少的產量","The broad Catalunya DO makes lots of Tempranillo, from simple and fruity to powerful and oaked.":"範圍廣大的 Catalunya DO 出產大量田帕尼優，從簡單果香到強勁經橡木桶都有。","Catalunya DO is a broad appellation producing large volumes of Tempranillo and Tempranillo-based blends. Styles run from simple, fruity reds to powerful, oak-aged ones. Altitude and tiny yields describe Ribera del Duero or Priorat instead; Priorat is also in Catalunya but is known for Garnacha.":"Catalunya DO 是範圍廣大的法定產區，生產大量的田帕尼優及以田帕尼優為基礎的混調。風格從簡單、果香豐富的紅酒到強勁、經橡木桶陳年的都有。海拔和極少的產量描述的則是 Ribera del Duero 或 Priorat；Priorat 也在加泰隆尼亞，但以 Garnacha 著稱。","In a Rioja meant for long ageing, what is Tempranillo usually blended with?":"在要長期陳年的 Rioja 中，田帕尼優通常與什麼混調？","Local grapes that add tannin and acidity":"能增添單寧和酸度的在地品種","Garnacha for fruit and softness":"增添果味和柔和感的 Garnacha","Gamay for freshness and colour":"增添清新感和顏色的加美","White grapes to lighten the body":"讓酒體變輕的白葡萄","For long-ageing Rioja, local grapes are added to boost tannin and acidity.":"在要長期陳年的 Rioja 中，會加入在地品種以加強單寧和酸度。","Rioja is usually a blend in which Tempranillo dominates the best wines. For wines to be drunk young, Garnacha is often used, adding fruit and body. Wines intended for long ageing need more tannin and acidity, so other local grapes with these traits are added: structure helps the wine stand the test of time.":"Rioja 通常是混調，在最好的酒款中以田帕尼優為主。要趁年輕喝的酒常使用 Garnacha，增添果味和酒體。要長期陳年的酒需要更多單寧和酸度，所以會加入具備這些特性的其他在地品種：結構能幫助酒經得起時間的考驗。","Which Spanish label term has the longest minimum ageing requirements?":"哪一個西班牙酒標術語的最低陳年要求最長？","The order is Joven, Crianza, Reserva, Gran Reserva: the last has the longest minimums.":"順序是 Joven、Crianza、Reserva、Gran Reserva：最後一個的最低要求最長。","The four Spanish terms follow a clear ladder. Joven has no minimum; Crianza requires time in barrel; Reserva long ageing in barrel and bottle; Gran Reserva the longest minimums of all. As a result, Gran Reserva usually shows the most pronounced secondary and tertiary aromas.":"這四個西班牙術語遵循清楚的階梯。Joven 沒有最低要求；Crianza 要求在橡木桶中熟成一段時間；Reserva 要求在橡木桶和瓶中長時間陳年；Gran Reserva 的最低要求最長。因此，Gran Reserva 通常展現最明顯的二級和三級香氣。","What are Joven wines called in Rioja?":"在 Rioja，Joven 酒款叫什麼？","In Rioja, young fruity wines with no minimum ageing are called Genérico.":"在 Rioja，沒有最低陳年要求的年輕果香酒款稱為 Genérico。","Joven means young, fruity wines with no minimum ageing, usually sold the year after the harvest and dominated by primary fruit. In Rioja the same category is called Genérico. Crianza and Reserva are levels with compulsory ageing; Vino de la Tierra is a geographical indication category, not an ageing term.":"Joven 是指沒有最低陳年要求的年輕果香酒款，通常在採收後隔年出售，以一級果味為主。在 Rioja，同樣的類別稱為 Genérico。Crianza 和 Reserva 是有強制陳年要求的等級；Vino de la Tierra 是地理標示類別，不是陳年術語。","Which style would you expect from a Spanish Crianza?":"你會預期西班牙的 Crianza 是什麼風格？","Primary fruit plus oak notes such as vanilla and coconut":"一級果味加上香草和椰子等橡木氣息","Only fresh fruit, with no time in barrel":"只有新鮮果味，沒有在橡木桶中熟成","Dominant tertiary notes of mushroom and dried fruit":"以蘑菇和果乾等三級氣息為主","Banana and candy notes from winemaking":"來自釀造過程的香蕉和糖果氣息","Crianza spends time in barrel before release, adding secondary oak notes to its fruit.":"Crianza 在上市前會在橡木桶中熟成一段時間，為果味增添二級的橡木氣息。","A Crianza must be matured in oak barrels before it goes on sale. It keeps the grape's primary fruit but adds secondary notes such as vanilla, smoke and coconut. A wine with no oak would be a Joven; dominant tertiary notes are more typical of Reserva and Gran Reserva, which age longer, including in bottle.":"Crianza 必須在上市前於橡木桶中熟成。它保留葡萄的一級果味，但增添香草、煙燻和椰子等二級氣息。不經橡木桶的酒會是 Joven；以三級氣息為主更是 Reserva 和 Gran Reserva 的典型特徵，它們陳年更久，包括在瓶中。","Why might a producer decide not to make a Gran Reserva in a given vintage?":"為什麼生產者可能決定在某個年份不釀 Gran Reserva？","The grapes are not good enough for long ageing":"葡萄不夠好，無法長期陳年","The law bans Gran Reserva in hot years":"法律禁止在炎熱年份釀造 Gran Reserva","New oak is too expensive that year":"那一年新橡木桶太貴","The grapes have too much tannin and acidity":"葡萄的單寧和酸度太多","Only wines with enough fruit, acidity and tannin can take long ageing; others turn stale.":"只有果味、酸度和單寧都足夠的酒才經得起長期陳年；其他的會變得乏味。","Grape quality decides which style is possible. Long ageing needs fruit intensity, acidity and, in reds, enough tannin. A modest wine put through extended ageing ends up stale and short of fruit. So in weak vintages a producer may skip Gran Reserva. Plenty of tannin and acidity is actually an advantage.":"葡萄品質決定了哪種風格可行。長期陳年需要果味濃郁度、酸度，紅酒還需要足夠的單寧。一款普通的酒經過長時間陳年，最後會變得乏味、缺乏果味。所以在表現較弱的年份，生產者可能會略過 Gran Reserva。大量的單寧和酸度其實是優點。","What exactly are Crianza, Reserva and Gran Reserva?":"Crianza、Reserva 和 Gran Reserva 究竟是什麼？","National Spanish terms with minimum ageing rules":"有最低陳年規定的西班牙全國性術語","Terms reserved for Rioja wines only":"只保留給 Rioja 酒款的術語","Maximum yield levels per hectare":"每公頃的最高產量等級","Indications of sweetness level":"甜度標示","They are nationwide Spanish terms setting minimum ageing periods before release.":"它們是規定上市前最低陳年期的西班牙全國性術語。","Crianza, Reserva and Gran Reserva often appear on Rioja labels, but they are not unique to that region: they are national Spanish terms. They set legal minimum ageing periods before sale, from the shortest (Crianza) to the longest (Gran Reserva). Some regions are stricter and many producers exceed the minimums.":"Crianza、Reserva 和 Gran Reserva 常出現在 Rioja 的酒標上，但它們不是這個產區獨有的：它們是西班牙全國性的術語。它們規定上市前的法定最低陳年期，從最短（Crianza）到最長（Gran Reserva）。有些產區規定更嚴格，許多生產者也會超過最低要求。","Why is Gamay considered an unusual grape variety?":"為什麼加美被視為不尋常的葡萄品種？","It is famous worldwide yet comes almost only from one region":"它聞名全球，卻幾乎只來自一個產區","It is a black grape that always makes white wines":"它是總是釀成白酒的黑葡萄","It ripens only in Europe's hottest climates, close to the sea":"它只在歐洲最炎熱、靠近海洋的氣候中成熟","It must always be aged for a long time in new barrels":"它必須一律在新橡木桶中長時間陳年","Gamay enjoys global popularity even though its wines come almost entirely from Beaujolais.":"儘管加美的酒幾乎全部來自 Beaujolais，它卻享有全球人氣。","Most famous grapes are grown in many countries, but Gamay owes its fame almost entirely to Beaujolais. It suits a moderate rather than a very hot climate and is usually made in inert vessels, so long new-oak ageing is not the rule. It is a black grape that gives light, fruity reds.":"大多數知名品種都種植在許多國家，但加美的名氣幾乎完全來自 Beaujolais。它適合溫和而非非常炎熱的氣候，通常在惰性容器中釀造，所以長時間新橡木桶陳年並非常態。它是釀出輕盈果香紅酒的黑葡萄。","A red wine has high acidity, low tannin, raspberry and red cherry aromas and no oak notes. Which grape is most likely?":"一款紅酒酸度高、單寧低、帶有覆盆子和紅櫻桃香氣、沒有橡木氣息。最可能是哪個品種？","Tempranillo aged in new barrels":"在新橡木桶中陳年的田帕尼優","High acidity, low tannin, red fruit and no oak is the typical Gamay profile.":"高酸度、低單寧、紅色水果、沒有橡木味，是加美的典型風味特徵。","Gamay is almost always made in inert vessels and shows raspberry, red cherry and red plum. Malbec and Montepulciano give dark wines with high tannin and black fruit. A Tempranillo aged in new barrels would show vanilla, smoke and cedar.":"加美幾乎總是在惰性容器中釀造，展現覆盆子、紅櫻桃和紅李。馬爾貝克和蒙鐵布奇亞諾釀出單寧高、帶黑色水果的深色酒。在新橡木桶中陳年的田帕尼優則會展現香草、煙燻和雪松。","Why do Gamay wines rarely show oak aromas?":"為什麼加美葡萄酒很少展現橡木香氣？","They are usually made in inert vessels":"它們通常在惰性容器中釀造","Beaujolais law forbids any use of barrels":"Beaujolais 的法律禁止使用任何橡木桶","Their very high alcohol completely hides the oak notes":"它們非常高的酒精完全掩蓋了橡木氣息","They are bottled before fermentation ends":"它們在發酵結束前就裝瓶了","Gamay is generally made and stored in inert vessels, which add no flavour.":"加美一般在不會增添風味的惰性容器中釀造和儲存。","The aim is to keep the grape's fresh, delicate red fruit. No rule bans oak: it is a style choice. Beaujolais wines have moderate alcohol and are dry, fully fermented wines.":"目的是保留這個品種清新細緻的紅色水果。沒有規定禁止使用橡木桶：這是風格上的選擇。Beaujolais 的酒精適中，是不甜、完全發酵的酒。","Which Beaujolais wines are the most concentrated and structured?":"哪些 Beaujolais 酒款最濃縮、結構最紮實？","Those from the crus, such as Fleurie":"來自 cru 的酒款，例如 Fleurie","Those from the regional Beaujolais AOC":"來自地區級 Beaujolais AOC 的酒款","Those from the flat, fertile vineyards in the south of the region":"來自這個地區南部平坦肥沃葡萄園的酒款","Those sold as Côtes du Rhône":"以 Côtes du Rhône 出售的酒款","The crus are the top of the Beaujolais hierarchy and give its most concentrated, structured wines.":"Cru 位於 Beaujolais 分級的頂端，出產它最濃縮、結構最紮實的酒。","Good cru wines offer medium to pronounced red-fruit aromas and a medium to long finish. The flat, fertile, high-yielding southern vineyards instead supply the lightest Beaujolais AOC. Côtes du Rhône belongs to another region and another main grape.":"優質的 cru 酒款帶有中等至濃郁的紅色水果香氣，以及中等至長的餘韻。南部平坦肥沃、高產量的葡萄園則供應最輕盈的 Beaujolais AOC。Côtes du Rhône 屬於另一個產區和另一個主要品種。","How do most Beaujolais wines change over time in the bottle?":"大多數 Beaujolais 在瓶中隨時間如何變化？","They soon lose their fresh fruit: drink them young":"它們很快就失去新鮮果味：要趁年輕喝","They improve for decades, gaining mushroom and leather notes":"它們數十年間越來越好，增添蘑菇和皮革氣息","They become sweeter and deeper in colour":"它們變得更甜、顏色更深","They stay unchanged for many years":"它們多年保持不變","Most Beaujolais is made for immediate drinking and quickly loses its fresh fruit.":"大多數 Beaujolais 是為立即飲用而釀的，很快就會失去新鮮果味。","Beaujolais's charm is its fresh red fruit, which fades with time. Only some crus can develop in the bottle, and not for decades. A wine does not get sweeter or darker with age: red wines actually tend to lose colour.":"Beaujolais 的魅力在於新鮮的紅色水果，而這會隨時間消退。只有部分 cru 能在瓶中發展，而且不是數十年。酒不會隨陳年變甜或變深：紅酒其實往往會失去顏色。","Where are the ten Beaujolais crus located?":"Beaujolais 的十個 cru 位於哪裡？","Within the Beaujolais Villages area, in the north":"在北部的 Beaujolais Villages 區域內","On the fertile plains in the south of the region":"在這個地區南部肥沃的平原上","Spread across Beaujolais, Burgundy and the Northern Rhône":"分散在 Beaujolais、布根地和北隆河","Along the Mediterranean coast":"沿著地中海沿岸","The ten crus have their own appellations inside the northern Beaujolais Villages area.":"十個 cru 在北部 Beaujolais Villages 區域內擁有各自的法定產區。","Northern Beaujolais has sloped, sunny vineyards on warm, well-drained soils: this is where the villages and, among them, the crus lie. The flat, fertile south gives basic Beaujolais instead. All the crus stay inside Beaujolais, a single region south of Burgundy.":"Beaujolais 北部有位於溫暖、排水良好土壤上、陽光充足的坡地葡萄園：這裡是 Villages 村莊所在，cru 也在其中。平坦肥沃的南部則出產基本的 Beaujolais。所有的 cru 都在 Beaujolais 之內，那是布根地以南的單一產區。","Which statement about Beaujolais AOC is correct?":"關於 Beaujolais AOC，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It may use grapes from anywhere in the region, mostly the south":"它可以使用這個地區任何地方的葡萄，大多來自南部","It can only be made from grapes grown on the northern slopes":"它只能用種在北部坡地的葡萄釀造","It is the top level of the hierarchy, above the crus":"它是分級的最高等級，高於 cru","It must be aged at least two years in new oak barrels":"它必須在新橡木桶中陳年至少兩年","Beaujolais AOC can come from anywhere in the region but mostly comes from the flat southern vineyards.":"Beaujolais AOC 可以來自這個地區任何地方，但大多來自南部平坦的葡萄園。","It is the base of the pyramid: high-yielding vines on flat, fertile land give the lightest, simplest wines. The northern slopes are home to the Villages and the crus. Beaujolais Gamay has no oak-ageing requirement and usually sees no oak at all.":"它是金字塔的底層：平坦肥沃土地上的高產量葡萄樹，出產最輕盈、最簡單的酒。北部的坡地則是 Villages 和 cru 的所在。Beaujolais 的加美沒有橡木桶陳年的要求，通常完全不經橡木桶。","What is the correct order of the Beaujolais hierarchy, from the simplest level to the top?":"Beaujolais 分級從最簡單到最高等級的正確順序是什麼？","Beaujolais, Beaujolais Villages, cru (e.g. Fleurie)":"Beaujolais、Beaujolais Villages、cru（例如 Fleurie）","Beaujolais Villages, Beaujolais, cru (e.g. Fleurie)":"Beaujolais Villages、Beaujolais、cru（例如 Fleurie）","Cru (e.g. Fleurie), Beaujolais Villages, Beaujolais":"Cru（例如 Fleurie）、Beaujolais Villages、Beaujolais","Beaujolais, cru (e.g. Fleurie), Beaujolais Villages":"Beaujolais、cru（例如 Fleurie）、Beaujolais Villages","It starts with Beaujolais AOC, rises to Villages and ends with crus such as Fleurie.":"從 Beaujolais AOC 開始，往上到 Villages，最後是 Fleurie 等 cru。","Each step is a smaller area with more intense wines. A memory tip: a cru label often does not even say 'Beaujolais', only the village name. The Rhône uses a very similar scheme.":"每往上一級，區域越小，酒越濃郁。記憶小技巧：cru 的酒標上常常連「Beaujolais」都沒寫，只有村莊名稱。隆河使用非常相似的體系。","A label says only 'Fleurie, Appellation Fleurie Contrôlée', with no grape named. What does it tell you?":"一張酒標上只寫著「Fleurie, Appellation Fleurie Contrôlée」，沒有標示品種。它告訴你什麼？","It is a Gamay from a Beaujolais cru":"這是來自 Beaujolais cru 的加美","It is a Pinot Noir from a Burgundy village":"這是來自布根地村莊的黑皮諾","It is a Grenache rosé made in Provence":"這是普羅旺斯釀造的格那希粉紅酒","It is a basic wine from grapes grown all over France":"這是用法國各地種植的葡萄釀的基本酒款","Fleurie is one of the ten Beaujolais crus, and red Beaujolais is made from Gamay.":"Fleurie 是 Beaujolais 十個 cru 之一，而 Beaujolais 紅酒是用加美釀造的。","Many French labels show the place, not the grape: you need to know that Fleurie grows Gamay. As a cru it sits at the top of the hierarchy, so it is not a basic wine. Provence is known for rosé, not for Gamay crus.":"許多法國酒標標示的是地點，而不是品種：你需要知道 Fleurie 種的是加美。作為 cru，它位於分級的頂端，所以不是基本酒款。普羅旺斯以粉紅酒著稱，而不是加美 cru。","Which statement about the origin of Grenache/Garnacha is correct?":"關於格那希／Garnacha 的起源，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It evolved in Spain, then spread to southern France and the Rhône":"它在西班牙演化而來，之後傳到法國南部和隆河","It evolved in the Rhône and reached Spain only recently":"它在隆河演化而來，直到最近才傳到西班牙","It was bred in Australia by crossing Shiraz and Pinot Noir":"它是在澳洲以希拉茲和黑皮諾雜交育成的","It comes from Bordeaux, where it has almost vanished":"它來自波爾多，在那裡幾乎已經消失","The grape evolved in Spain as Garnacha and took the name Grenache in France.":"這個品種在西班牙以 Garnacha 之名演化而來，在法國則稱為 Grenache。","From Spain it moved into southern France and then the Rhône Valley; the French name, Grenache, is the one most used elsewhere. Australia has old Grenache vines but did not create it. The grape that has almost vanished from Bordeaux is Carmenère.":"它從西班牙傳入法國南部，然後到隆河谷地；法文名稱 Grenache 是其他地方最常用的名稱。澳洲有格那希老藤，但並非由澳洲創造。幾乎從波爾多消失的品種是卡門內爾。","When does Grenache produce its finest wines?":"格那希什麼時候能釀出最優質的酒？","When yields are carefully controlled":"當產量受到仔細控制時","When the vines produce as many grapes as possible":"當葡萄樹盡可能多結葡萄時","When grown in Europe's coolest, rainiest areas":"當種在歐洲最涼爽、最多雨的地區時","When picked before full ripeness":"當在完全成熟前採收時","With controlled yields Grenache concentrates fruit and structure and gives its finest wines.":"在控制產量的情況下，格那希的果味和結構更濃縮，能釀出最優質的酒。","Very high yields dilute flavour. Grenache needs warmth to ripen: in cool, rainy areas it does not get there, and picked unripe it would lose its red fruit. The low-yielding old vines of Priorat and the Barossa prove the point.":"非常高的產量會稀釋風味。格那希需要熱量才能成熟：在涼爽多雨的地區，它無法成熟，而未成熟就採收會失去紅色水果。Priorat 和 Barossa 的低產量老藤證明了這一點。","What style do Grenache rosés usually have?":"格那希粉紅酒通常是什麼風格？","Dry to medium-sweet, drunk chilled while young":"不甜至半甜，冰鎮後趁年輕喝","Always very sweet, to be cellared for years":"一律非常甜，要窖藏多年","Dry and tannic, aged for a long time in new barrels before sale":"不甜且有單寧，上市前在新橡木桶中長時間陳年","Sparkling, with a second fermentation in bottle":"在瓶中二次發酵的氣泡酒","Thanks to its red fruit, Grenache makes dry to medium-sweet rosés meant to be drunk chilled and young.":"由於帶有紅色水果，格那希釀出不甜至半甜、要冰鎮趁年輕喝的粉紅酒。","They are made with a short skin maceration, which gives colour but little tannin. Their strength is fresh fruit, so they are not aged or kept long in new oak. Bubbles are not part of this style.":"它們以短時間浸皮釀造，帶來顏色但單寧很少。它們的強項是新鮮的果味，所以不會陳年，也不會在新橡木桶中久放。氣泡不屬於這種風格。","Which flavours can a quality Grenache develop with bottle age?":"優質的格那希經過瓶中陳年能發展出哪些風味？","Earth, meat and dried fruit":"泥土、肉和果乾","Green bell pepper and tomato leaf":"青椒和番茄葉","Fresh raspberry, candy and banana":"新鮮覆盆子、糖果和香蕉","Green apple, lemon and white flowers":"青蘋果、檸檬和白花","Over time in bottle Grenache can develop complex notes of earth, meat and dried fruit.":"隨著在瓶中的時間，格那希能發展出泥土、肉和果乾的複雜氣息。","These are tertiary aromas, typical for instance of the best Châteauneuf-du-Pape. Green pepper and tomato leaf point to underripe Carmenère. Banana and candy come from Beaujolais techniques; apple and lemon are white-wine aromas.":"這些是三級香氣，例如最好的 Châteauneuf-du-Pape 的典型特徵。青椒和番茄葉指向未完全成熟的卡門內爾。香蕉和糖果來自 Beaujolais 的釀造技術；蘋果和檸檬是白酒的香氣。","How does the Southern Rhône differ from the Northern Rhône?":"南隆河與北隆河有什麼不同？","The valley flattens out and the climate is warm due to its southerly latitude":"河谷變得平坦，因緯度偏南而氣候溫暖","It is cooler, with very steep slopes above the river":"它更涼爽，河流上方有非常陡峭的坡地","It grows almost only Gamay":"它幾乎只種加美","It uses a completely different labelling system":"它使用完全不同的標示體系","In the south the Rhône Valley opens out and the climate is warm, letting Grenache ripen.":"在南部，隆河谷地變得開闊，氣候溫暖，讓格那希得以成熟。","The two halves differ in climate, aspect and grapes: steep slopes and single-varietal Syrah are typical of the north. The south mainly makes Grenache-based blends. The labelling hierarchy, however, is the same across the whole valley.":"兩半部在氣候、坡向和品種上都不同：陡坡和單一品種希哈是北部的典型特徵。南部主要釀造以格那希為基礎的混調。不過，標示分級在整個河谷都是一樣的。","Côtes du Rhône AOC covers the whole Rhône Valley. Where do almost all its grapes come from?":"Côtes du Rhône AOC 涵蓋整個隆河谷地。它的葡萄幾乎全部來自哪裡？","Equally from the northern slopes and the southern plain":"北部坡地和南部平原各佔一半","From crus such as Hermitage and Côte-Rôtie":"來自 Hermitage 和 Côte-Rôtie 等 cru","Although the appellation covers the whole valley, the grapes come almost exclusively from the south.":"雖然這個法定產區涵蓋整個河谷，葡萄幾乎全部來自南部。","That is why Côtes du Rhône is usually a simple, medium-bodied, Grenache-based blend. Northern vineyards are few and mostly go to the crus. Selling Hermitage grapes as Côtes du Rhône would be a waste.":"這就是為什麼 Côtes du Rhône 通常是簡單、酒體中等、以格那希為基礎的混調。北部的葡萄園很少，大多用於 cru。把 Hermitage 的葡萄當作 Côtes du Rhône 出售就太浪費了。","Which of these Rhône crus is in the Southern Rhône?":"下列哪一個隆河 cru 位於南隆河？","Châteauneuf-du-Pape is the best-known cru of the Southern Rhône.":"Châteauneuf-du-Pape 是南隆河最知名的 cru。","Rhône crus exist in both halves of the valley. Hermitage, Côte-Rôtie and Crozes-Hermitage are in the north, Syrah country (as is Condrieu, for white). Châteauneuf-du-Pape, in the south, makes full-bodied Grenache-based reds.":"隆河的 cru 在河谷的兩半部都有。Hermitage、Côte-Rôtie 和 Crozes-Hermitage 位於北部，是希哈的天下（白酒的 Condrieu 也是）。南部的 Châteauneuf-du-Pape 出產以格那希為基礎、酒體飽滿的紅酒。","What does Grenache bring to the red wines of Minervois AOC?":"格那希為 Minervois AOC 的紅酒帶來什麼？","Red fruit and body, blended with local grapes such as Syrah":"紅色水果和酒體，與希哈等在地品種混調","Very high tannin and near-black colour, as a single variety":"作為單一品種，帶來非常高的單寧和近乎黑色的顏色","Sharp acidity, because it ripens poorly in the cool climate":"尖銳的酸度，因為它在涼爽氣候中成熟不佳","Green bell pepper and tomato leaf notes":"青椒和番茄葉氣息","In warm Languedoc Grenache ripens well and gives red fruit and body to blends with Syrah and other grapes.":"在溫暖的 Languedoc，格那希成熟良好，為與希哈和其他品種的混調帶來紅色水果和酒體。","Minervois is one of the key red appellations of Languedoc-Roussillon. The climate is warm, not cool, and Grenache is thin-skinned: it gives neither near-black colour nor very high tannin. Green pepper notes are typical of underripe Carmenère.":"Minervois 是 Languedoc-Roussillon 重要的紅酒法定產區之一。氣候溫暖而非涼爽，而格那希果皮薄：它既不會帶來近乎黑色的顏色，也不會帶來非常高的單寧。青椒氣息是未完全成熟的卡門內爾的典型特徵。","Where is Provence in relation to Languedoc-Roussillon?":"普羅旺斯相對於 Languedoc-Roussillon 的位置在哪裡？","To the east":"東邊","To the west":"西邊","Directly north, near Burgundy":"正北方，靠近布根地","Much further south, near Spain":"更南邊得多，靠近西班牙","Provence lies east of Languedoc-Roussillon, along the Mediterranean coast.":"普羅旺斯位於 Languedoc-Roussillon 以東，沿著地中海沿岸。","Both regions are in warm southern France and use a lot of Grenache. Roussillon is the part closest to Spain, so Provence cannot lie further south-west. Provence is famous above all for the dry, pale rosés of Côtes de Provence AOC.":"兩個地區都位於溫暖的法國南部，都大量使用格那希。Roussillon 是最靠近西班牙的部分，所以普羅旺斯不可能位於更西南方。普羅旺斯最著名的是 Côtes de Provence AOC 不甜、淺色的粉紅酒。","What does Garnacha contribute to the wines of Rioja DOCa?":"Garnacha 為 Rioja DOCa 的酒帶來什麼？","Body and fresh red fruit":"酒體和新鮮的紅色水果","Acidity and tannin for long-ageing wines":"為長期陳年的酒帶來酸度和單寧","Very deep colour and black-fruit and oak aromas":"非常深的顏色以及黑色水果和橡木香氣","In Rioja and neighbouring Navarra, Garnacha adds body and fresh red fruit.":"在 Rioja 和鄰近的 Navarra，Garnacha 增添酒體和新鮮的紅色水果。","That is why in Rioja it is used mostly in wines for early drinking, alongside Tempranillo. Acidity and tannin for long-ageing wines come from other local grapes. Being thin-skinned, Garnacha gives no very deep colour, and Rioja reds are dry.":"這就是為什麼在 Rioja，它大多與田帕尼優一起用於適合早飲的酒。長期陳年酒款所需的酸度和單寧來自其他在地品種。由於果皮薄，Garnacha 不會帶來非常深的顏色，而 Rioja 紅酒是不甜的。","Which flavours do top Priorat Garnachas develop in the bottle?":"頂級的 Priorat Garnacha 在瓶中會發展出哪些風味？","Dried fruit and caramel":"果乾和焦糖","Banana and candy":"香蕉和糖果","Grapefruit and passion fruit":"葡萄柚和百香果","Green apple and fresh herbs":"青蘋果和新鮮香草植物","Priorat wines can age for a long time and develop dried-fruit and caramel notes in bottle.":"Priorat 的酒能長期陳年，在瓶中發展出果乾和焦糖氣息。","Old, low-yielding vines in a warm, dry corner of Catalunya give powerful wines, usually blended with other black grapes. Banana and candy belong to young Beaujolais. Grapefruit and green apple are white-wine aromas.":"在加泰隆尼亞溫暖乾燥的一角，低產量的老藤出產強勁的酒，通常與其他黑葡萄混調。香蕉和糖果屬於年輕的 Beaujolais。葡萄柚和青蘋果是白酒的香氣。","In Australia, Grenache-Shiraz blends can resemble which French wine in style and quality?":"在澳洲，格那希與希拉茲的混調在風格和品質上可能類似哪一款法國酒？","A dry, pale Côtes de Provence rosé":"不甜、淺色的 Côtes de Provence 粉紅酒","Australian blends of Grenache, Shiraz and other grapes can be similar to Châteauneuf-du-Pape.":"格那希、希拉茲和其他品種的澳洲混調可能類似 Châteauneuf-du-Pape。","Barossa Valley and McLaren Vale are warm areas with old Grenache vines, like the Southern Rhône. Shiraz is the same grape as Syrah, Grenache's classic partner in Châteauneuf. Beaujolais and Fleurie are light Gamays; Provence rosé is another style altogether.":"Barossa Valley 和 McLaren Vale 是擁有格那希老藤的溫暖地區，和南隆河一樣。希拉茲和希哈是同一個品種，是格那希在 Châteauneuf 的經典搭檔。Beaujolais 和 Fleurie 是輕盈的加美；普羅旺斯粉紅酒則完全是另一種風格。","Which of these aromas is NOT typical of young Tempranillo?":"下列哪一項香氣不是年輕田帕尼優的典型特徵？","Strawberry and red cherry":"草莓和紅櫻桃","Blackberry":"黑莓","Black plum":"黑李","Tempranillo combines red and black fruit; green pepper notes are not part of its profile.":"田帕尼優結合了紅色和黑色水果；青椒氣息不屬於它的風味特徵。","Strawberry, red cherry, blackberry and black plum are all typical primary aromas of Tempranillo. Green pepper and tomato leaf are the sign of Carmenère picked before full ripeness. With oak, Tempranillo gains vanilla, smoke and cedar, not green notes.":"草莓、紅櫻桃、黑莓和黑李都是田帕尼優典型的一級香氣。青椒和番茄葉是在完全成熟前採收的卡門內爾的特徵。經過橡木桶，田帕尼優會增添香草、煙燻和雪松，而不是青澀的氣息。","Besides adding flavour, what does maturation in small new barrels do to Tempranillo?":"除了增添風味，在小型新橡木桶中熟成對田帕尼優還有什麼作用？","It softens the tannins":"讓單寧變柔和","It greatly raises the acidity":"大幅提高酸度","It makes the wine sweet":"讓酒變甜","It turns the colour much darker, almost black with purple tints":"讓顏色深得多，近乎黑色帶紫色調","Small new barrels add vanilla, smoke and cedar and soften the tannins at the same time.":"小型新橡木桶增添香草、煙燻和雪松，同時柔化單寧。","In many parts of Spain it is traditional to age Tempranillo in small new oak barrels. Oak adds neither sugar nor acidity. Over time, the colour of red wines moves towards lighter, garnet tones, not darker ones.":"在西班牙許多地方，傳統上田帕尼優會在小型新橡木桶中陳年。橡木不會增添糖分或酸度。隨著時間，紅酒的顏色會轉向較淡的石榴紅色調，而不是更深。","Where is Rioja and what is its climate?":"Rioja 在哪裡？它的氣候如何？","North-east Spain, moderate climate":"西班牙東北部，溫和氣候","Southern Spain, very hot and dry climate":"西班牙南部，非常炎熱乾燥的氣候","On the north-west Atlantic coast, cool and rainy":"在西北部的大西洋沿岸，涼爽多雨","In Catalunya, near Barcelona, warm climate":"在加泰隆尼亞，靠近巴塞隆納，溫暖氣候","Rioja DOCa is a moderate-climate region in north-east Spain.":"Rioja DOCa 是西班牙東北部的溫和氣候產區。","It is the most famous area for Tempranillo-based wines. Catalunya is a different region, with a broad DO and the reds of Priorat. The cool north-west Atlantic coast is white-wine country, home to Albariño.":"它是以田帕尼優為基礎的酒款最著名的產區。加泰隆尼亞是另一個地區，有範圍廣大的 DO 和 Priorat 的紅酒。涼爽的西北大西洋沿岸是白酒的天下，阿爾巴利諾的故鄉。","In Rioja, in which wines is Tempranillo sometimes blended with Garnacha?":"在 Rioja，田帕尼優有時會在哪些酒款中與 Garnacha 混調？","Those intended for early drinking":"要早飲的酒款","Only in Gran Reservas meant for very long ageing":"只在要非常長期陳年的 Gran Reserva 中","In sweet dessert wines":"在甜型甜點酒中","In white wines for fish":"在搭配魚的白酒中","Garnacha, rich in red fruit and body, joins Tempranillo in Rioja wines for early drinking.":"富含紅色水果和酒體的 Garnacha，在 Rioja 適合早飲的酒款中與田帕尼優搭配。","For long-ageing wines producers prefer other local grapes that add tannin and acidity, which Garnacha does not provide. Red Riojas are dry, and Garnacha is a black grape, not used for whites.":"對於長期陳年的酒，生產者偏好能增添單寧和酸度的其他在地品種，而 Garnacha 無法提供這些。Rioja 紅酒是不甜的，而 Garnacha 是黑葡萄，不用於白酒。","Put these in order from the shortest to the longest minimum ageing:":"把這些依最低陳年要求由短到長排序：","Joven has no minimum, then come Crianza, Reserva and finally Gran Reserva, the longest.":"Joven 沒有最低要求，接著是 Crianza、Reserva，最後是最長的 Gran Reserva。","More than the numbers, remember the order and the style it signals. Joven is about primary fruit, Crianza adds oak notes, Reserva combines barrel and bottle, and Gran Reserva has the most pronounced secondary and tertiary aromas.":"比起數字，更要記住順序和它代表的風格。Joven 著重一級果味，Crianza 增添橡木氣息，Reserva 結合了橡木桶和瓶中陳年，而 Gran Reserva 有最明顯的二級和三級香氣。","What happens to a red Reserva during its long ageing in barrel and bottle?":"紅酒 Reserva 在橡木桶和瓶中長時間陳年期間會發生什麼？","Tannins soften and some fruit turns cooked or dried":"單寧變柔和，部分果味轉為煮過或乾燥的特徵","Tannins increase and the fruit becomes ever fresher and crunchier":"單寧增加，果味變得越來越新鮮爽脆","Sugar rises and the wine turns sweet":"糖分上升，酒變甜","Nothing changes; only the label matters":"什麼都不變；只有酒標才重要","Over time tannins soften and some of the fresh fruit takes on a cooked or dried character.":"隨著時間，單寧變柔和，部分新鮮果味帶上煮過或乾燥的特徵。","The result is a layered wine: primary fruit, secondary oak notes and tertiary notes such as dried fruit and mushroom. Ageing creates no sugar and does not make fruit fresher. Reserva legally requires ageing in both barrel and bottle.":"結果是一款層次豐富的酒：一級果味、二級橡木氣息，以及果乾和蘑菇等三級氣息。陳年不會產生糖分，也不會讓果味更新鮮。Reserva 依法必須同時在橡木桶和瓶中陳年。","Which statement about Spanish minimum ageing rules (Crianza, Reserva, Gran Reserva) is correct?":"關於西班牙的最低陳年規定（Crianza、Reserva、Gran Reserva），下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","Some regions have stricter rules and many producers exceed the minimums":"有些產區規定更嚴格，許多生產者也會超過最低要求","They apply only to Rioja wines":"它們只適用於 Rioja 酒款","No producer may age a wine beyond the minimum":"沒有生產者可以讓酒陳年超過最低要求","They are just marketing words with no legal meaning":"它們只是沒有法律意義的行銷用語","The terms set legal minimums across Spain; some regions demand more and many producers go further.":"這些術語在全西班牙規定法定最低要求；有些產區要求更多，許多生產者也會做得更多。","They are national terms, not reserved for Rioja, and they carry legal weight. A minimum is a starting point: anyone may age for longer. Rioja, for example, applies stricter rules than the national minimum.":"它們是全國性的術語，不是 Rioja 專屬的，而且具有法律效力。最低要求只是起點：任何人都可以陳年更久。例如 Rioja 就採用比全國最低要求更嚴格的規定。","A customer wants a young, fruity Spanish red with only fresh-fruit aromas and no oak. Which label term should you look for?":"一位顧客想要一款年輕、果香豐富、只有新鮮果香而沒有橡木味的西班牙紅酒。你應該找哪個酒標術語？","Gran Reserva, aged a long time before release":"Gran Reserva，上市前長時間陳年","Joven has no minimum ageing and is made to show the grape's primary fruit.":"Joven 沒有最低陳年要求，是為了展現葡萄的一級果味而釀的。","It is usually released the year after the harvest; in Rioja it is called Genérico. A Crianza must already spend time in barrel and picks up vanilla and coconut. Reserva and Gran Reserva also have tertiary aromas.":"它通常在採收後隔年出售；在 Rioja 稱為 Genérico。Crianza 已經必須在橡木桶中熟成一段時間，會帶上香草和椰子。Reserva 和 Gran Reserva 還有三級香氣。","A label reads 'Rioja Gran Reserva'. What style should you expect?":"一張酒標上寫著「Rioja Gran Reserva」。你應該預期什麼風格？","The most pronounced secondary and tertiary aromas, with soft tannins":"最明顯的二級和三級香氣，單寧柔和","A young wine with only fresh fruit and no oak":"只有新鮮果味、不經橡木桶的年輕酒款","A dry rosé to drink well chilled":"要冰得很涼喝的不甜粉紅酒","A light red with harsh tannins":"單寧粗糙的輕盈紅酒","Gran Reserva has the longest minimum ageing and usually the most pronounced secondary and tertiary aromas.":"Gran Reserva 的最低陳年要求最長，通常有最明顯的二級和三級香氣。","After years in barrel and bottle, tannins have softened and notes of dried fruit, mushroom and leather sit beside vanilla and cedar. Fresh fruit alone with no oak describes a Joven. Long ageing does not leave harsh tannins.":"在橡木桶和瓶中多年後，單寧已經變柔和，果乾、蘑菇和皮革的氣息與香草和雪松並存。只有新鮮果味且不經橡木桶描述的是 Joven。長期陳年不會留下粗糙的單寧。","Under what name is Zinfandel known in Puglia?":"金芬黛在普利亞以什麼名稱為人所知？","In Italy, and especially Puglia, Zinfandel is called Primitivo.":"在義大利，尤其是普利亞，金芬黛稱為 Primitivo（普里米蒂沃）。","Zinfandel and Primitivo are the same black grape, which has built its reputation in two different countries. In California it is called Zinfandel, while in Italy, especially warm Puglia, it goes by Primitivo. Montepulciano, Barbera and Sangiovese are other Italian red grapes, distinct from Primitivo.":"金芬黛（Zinfandel）和普里米蒂沃（Primitivo）是同一個黑葡萄品種，在兩個不同的國家建立了名聲。在加州它稱為 Zinfandel，而在義大利，尤其是溫暖的普利亞，它稱為 Primitivo。蒙鐵布奇亞諾、巴貝拉和山吉歐維榭是其他與普里米蒂沃不同的義大利紅葡萄。","Which wine style is typical of Puglian Primitivo for high-volume brands?":"哪一種酒款風格是普利亞大量生產品牌的普里米蒂沃的典型特徵？","Soft, fruity, dry red":"柔和、果香豐富、不甜的紅酒","Medium-sweet, low-alcohol rosé":"半甜、低酒精的粉紅酒","Light, acidic, very tannic red":"輕盈、酸、單寧非常多的紅酒","Sweet red made from dried grapes":"用風乾葡萄釀的甜紅酒","Puglia is an important source of soft, fruity, dry red Primitivo.":"普利亞是柔和、果香豐富、不甜的普里米蒂沃紅酒的重要來源。","Puglia's warm climate lets Primitivo ripen fully. Much of the production goes into high-volume brands, in a soft, fruity, dry red style that is easy to drink. The medium-sweet, low-alcohol rosé describes Californian White Zinfandel instead. With controlled yields, Puglia also makes higher-quality Primitivo.":"普利亞溫暖的氣候讓普里米蒂沃完全成熟。大部分的產量用於大量生產的品牌，風格是柔和、果香豐富、不甜、容易入口的紅酒。半甜、低酒精的粉紅酒描述的則是加州的 White Zinfandel。在控制產量的情況下，普利亞也出產品質更高的普里米蒂沃。","How are very good or outstanding Primitivos made in Puglia?":"在普利亞，非常好或傑出的普里米蒂沃是如何釀造的？","By controlling grape yields":"控制葡萄產量","By increasing vine yields":"提高葡萄樹產量","By fermenting without the skins":"不帶果皮發酵","By picking the grapes very unripe":"在葡萄非常不成熟時採收","Controlled yields give more concentrated grapes and higher-quality Primitivo.":"控制產量帶來更濃縮的葡萄和品質更高的普里米蒂沃。","Alongside simple wines for big brands, Puglia also makes very good and outstanding Primitivo. The key is controlling yields: less fruit per vine means more concentrated grapes and more intense, complex wines. These top Primitivos are also valued because they often offer excellent value for money.":"除了供應大品牌的簡單酒款，普利亞也出產非常好和傑出的普里米蒂沃。關鍵在於控制產量：每株葡萄樹的果實越少，葡萄就越濃縮，酒也越濃郁、越複雜。這些頂級普里米蒂沃也因為常常非常物超所值而受到重視。","Why is Puglia well suited to Primitivo?":"為什麼普利亞非常適合普里米蒂沃？","Its warm climate lets the grape ripen":"它溫暖的氣候讓這個品種得以成熟","Its cool climate preserves acidity":"它涼爽的氣候保留了酸度","Its fogs encourage noble rot":"它的霧氣助長貴腐菌","Its cold winters allow ice wine":"它寒冷的冬天適合釀冰酒","Primitivo needs warmth to ripen, and Puglia is a warm region.":"普里米蒂沃需要熱量才能成熟，而普利亞是溫暖的地區。","Primitivo, like Zinfandel, is a black grape that only ripens well with warmth. Puglia, in southern Italy, offers exactly that climate, bringing the grapes to full ripeness with black-fruit and sometimes dried-fruit flavours. The result is soft, fruity reds, from high-volume brand wines to the best examples from controlled yields.":"普里米蒂沃和金芬黛一樣，是只有在溫暖時才能好好成熟的黑葡萄。義大利南部的普利亞正好提供這樣的氣候，讓葡萄完全成熟，帶有黑色水果、有時還有果乾風味。結果是柔和、果香豐富的紅酒，從大量生產的品牌酒到控制產量的最佳酒款都有。","Which is the only grape permitted in Barolo DOCG?":"Barolo DOCG 唯一允許的品種是哪一個？","Barolo DOCG is made exclusively from Nebbiolo.":"Barolo DOCG 只用內比歐露釀造。","Barolo carries only the name of its area, so you need to know that the grape behind it is Nebbiolo, the only one allowed. Barbera is also from Piemonte, but its flagship wine is Barbera d'Asti. Sangiovese is Tuscan and Corvina is the grape of Valpolicella in the Veneto.":"Barolo 只標示它的地區名稱，所以你需要知道它背後的品種是內比歐露（Nebbiolo），也是唯一允許的品種。巴貝拉也來自皮埃蒙特，但它的旗艦酒款是 Barbera d'Asti。山吉歐維榭是托斯卡尼的，科維納則是威尼托 Valpolicella 的品種。","Where is Barbaresco DOCG located?":"Barbaresco DOCG 位於哪裡？","In Piemonte, north-east of Barolo":"在皮埃蒙特，Barolo 東北方","In the Veneto, near Valpolicella":"在威尼托，靠近 Valpolicella","In Tuscany, south of Chianti":"在托斯卡尼，Chianti 以南","In Abruzzo, on the east coast":"在阿布魯佐，東海岸","Barbaresco is a smaller Piemonte area, north-east of Barolo.":"Barbaresco 是皮埃蒙特一個較小的地區，位於 Barolo 東北方。","Barolo and Barbaresco are the two great Nebbiolo DOCGs of Piemonte. Barbaresco is smaller and lies north-east of Barolo, but it makes similarly powerful, long-lived wines. The Veneto, Tuscany and Abruzzo, the other options, are the home regions of Corvina, Sangiovese and Montepulciano respectively.":"Barolo 和 Barbaresco 是皮埃蒙特兩個偉大的內比歐露 DOCG。Barbaresco 較小，位於 Barolo 東北方，但出產同樣強勁、長壽的酒。其他選項中的威尼托、托斯卡尼和阿布魯佐，分別是科維納、山吉歐維榭和蒙鐵布奇亞諾的故鄉。","Which structure is typical of Nebbiolo?":"哪一種結構是內比歐露的典型特徵？","Medium acidity and high tannins":"中等酸度和高單寧","Low acidity and medium tannins":"低酸度和中等單寧","Nebbiolo combines high acidity and high tannins, the basis of its long life.":"內比歐露結合了高酸度和高單寧，這是它長壽的基礎。","High acidity with low or medium tannins describes Barbera and Corvina; medium acidity with high tannins describes Montepulciano. Nebbiolo has both high: that is why it is often matured long in oak, improves in bottle, and the best develop mushroom, tobacco and leather.":"高酸度加上低或中等單寧描述的是巴貝拉和科維納；中等酸度加上高單寧描述的是蒙鐵布奇亞諾。內比歐露兩者都高：這就是為什麼它常在橡木桶中長時間熟成、在瓶中變好，而最好的酒款會發展出蘑菇、菸草和皮革。","Why is Nebbiolo often matured for long periods in oak?":"為什麼內比歐露常在橡木桶中長時間熟成？","To soften its high tannins":"為了柔化它的高單寧","To lighten its colour":"為了讓它的顏色變淡","Long oak maturation helps soften Nebbiolo's very high tannins.":"長時間的橡木桶熟成有助於柔化內比歐露非常高的單寧。","Nebbiolo has very firm tannins that can feel harsh when young. A long spell in oak makes them softer. The type of barrel is a style choice: old barrels soften without adding much flavour, while new oak also adds its own typical aromas.":"內比歐露的單寧非常紮實，年輕時可能感覺粗糙。在橡木桶中待上很長一段時間能讓單寧變柔和。橡木桶的類型是風格上的選擇：舊桶能柔化單寧而不增添太多風味，新桶則還會增添它典型的香氣。","Which tertiary aromas do the best aged Nebbiolo wines develop?":"最好的陳年內比歐露會發展出哪些三級香氣？","Mushroom, tobacco and leather":"蘑菇、菸草和皮革","Honey, almond and nuts":"蜂蜜、杏仁和堅果","Cloves, cedar and vanilla":"丁香、雪松和香草","Prunes, raisins and figs":"黑李乾、葡萄乾和無花果","With age, the best Nebbiolo gains mushroom, tobacco and leather.":"隨著陳年，最好的內比歐露會增添蘑菇、菸草和皮革。","Tertiary aromas come from ageing. In Nebbiolo they are mushroom, tobacco and leather. Honey and almond are typical of aged whites such as Soave Classico; cloves, cedar and vanilla come from oak; prunes, raisins and figs are linked to the dried grapes of Amarone.":"三級香氣來自陳年。在內比歐露中，它們是蘑菇、菸草和皮革。蜂蜜和杏仁是 Soave Classico 等陳年白酒的典型特徵；丁香、雪松和香草來自橡木桶；黑李乾、葡萄乾和無花果則與 Amarone 的風乾葡萄有關。","What is the vineyard landscape of Barolo like?":"Barolo 的葡萄園地貌是什麼樣子？","Horseshoe-shaped valley with steep south-facing slopes":"馬蹄形的山谷，有朝南的陡坡","Flat river plain with fertile soils":"土壤肥沃的平坦河流平原","Windswept plateau facing north":"朝北、受風吹拂的高原","Coastal hills overlooking the sea":"俯瞰海洋的沿海丘陵","Barolo is a horseshoe-shaped valley with steep, south-facing vineyards.":"Barolo 是馬蹄形的山谷，葡萄園位於朝南的陡坡上。","Steep south-facing slopes are part of the character of the Barolo area, which makes full-bodied, intense wines with high tannin and acidity and long ageing potential. In northern Italy the finest sites benefit from mountain shelter and a variety of slopes and soils, not from the plains.":"朝南的陡坡是 Barolo 地區特色的一部分，這裡出產酒體飽滿、濃郁、單寧和酸度高、陳年潛力長的酒。在北義，最好的園地受益於山脈的屏障以及多樣的坡地和土壤，而不是平原。","Which structure is typical of Barbera?":"哪一種結構是巴貝拉的典型特徵？","High acidity and low to medium tannins":"高酸度，單寧低至中等","High acidity and very high tannins":"高酸度，單寧非常高","Barbera has high acidity but only low to medium tannins.":"巴貝拉酸度高，但單寧只有低至中等。","Barbera and Nebbiolo share high acidity, but Barbera has much softer tannins. The result is a fresh, juicy red with red cherry, red plum and sometimes black pepper. Very high tannins point to Nebbiolo or Brunello; medium acidity with high tannins points to Montepulciano.":"巴貝拉和內比歐露都有高酸度，但巴貝拉的單寧柔和得多。結果是一款清爽多汁的紅酒，帶有紅櫻桃、紅李，有時還有黑胡椒。非常高的單寧指向內比歐露或 Brunello；中等酸度加上高單寧則指向蒙鐵布奇亞諾。","Why can Barbera generally be enjoyed younger than Nebbiolo?":"為什麼巴貝拉一般可以比內比歐露更年輕時享用？","Because it has lower tannins":"因為它的單寧較低","Because it has lower acidity":"因為它的酸度較低","Because it comes from dried grapes":"因為它是用風乾的葡萄釀的","With lower tannins, Barbera is enjoyable sooner than Nebbiolo.":"單寧較低的巴貝拉比內比歐露更早好喝。","Nebbiolo's high tannins need time to soften, while Barbera's low to medium tannins make it pleasant when young. Barbera's acidity is high, so that is not the reason. The best wines can age, but generally for less time than Nebbiolo.":"內比歐露的高單寧需要時間柔化，而巴貝拉低至中等的單寧讓它年輕時就很宜人。巴貝拉的酸度很高，所以那不是原因。最好的酒款能夠陳年，但一般時間比內比歐露短。","Which wine is considered by many to give Barbera's highest-quality wines?":"許多人認為哪一款酒能展現巴貝拉最高的品質？","Many see Barbera d'Asti DOCG as giving the best Barbera.":"許多人認為 Barbera d'Asti DOCG 出產最好的巴貝拉。","The name Barbera d'Asti contains both grape and place and means 'Barbera from Asti'. Barbaresco, although from Piemonte, is Nebbiolo; Valpolicella Classico is based on Corvina in the Veneto; Montepulciano d'Abruzzo is a red made from the Montepulciano grape in east-central Italy.":"Barbera d'Asti 這個名稱同時包含品種和地點，意思是「來自 Asti 的巴貝拉」。Barbaresco 雖然來自皮埃蒙特，卻是內比歐露；Valpolicella Classico 以威尼托的科維納為基礎；Montepulciano d'Abruzzo 則是用義大利中東部的蒙鐵布奇亞諾葡萄釀的紅酒。","Which is the most important grape of Valpolicella?":"Valpolicella 最重要的品種是哪一個？","Corvina usually dominates the Valpolicella blend.":"科維納通常在 Valpolicella 的混調中佔主導。","Valpolicella is in the Veneto and its reds are usually based on Corvina, with other local grapes permitted. Garganega is also from the Veneto, but it is the white grape of Soave. Barbera and Sangiovese belong to Piemonte and Tuscany.":"Valpolicella 位於威尼托，它的紅酒通常以科維納（Corvina）為基礎，也允許使用其他在地品種。卡爾卡耐卡也來自威尼托，但它是 Soave 的白葡萄。巴貝拉和山吉歐維榭屬於皮埃蒙特和托斯卡尼。","What is the typical style of a basic Valpolicella DOC?":"基本的 Valpolicella DOC 是什麼典型風格？","Light, fruity, simple, for drinking young":"輕盈、果香豐富、簡單，要趁年輕喝","Full-bodied, high in alcohol, dried-fruit notes":"酒體飽滿、酒精高、帶果乾氣息","Sweet red from partially dried grapes":"用部分風乾葡萄釀的甜紅酒","Very tannic, long aged in new oak":"單寧非常多，在新橡木桶中長時間陳年","Basic Valpolicella DOC is light, fruity and made to be drunk young.":"基本的 Valpolicella DOC 輕盈、果香豐富，是要趁年輕喝的。","Basic Valpolicella is made from fresh grapes, rarely sees new oak and is simple. A full-bodied, high-alcohol style with dried fruit describes Amarone; a sweet red from dried grapes is Recioto della Valpolicella. Very high tannins and long oak ageing suggest Nebbiolo instead.":"基本的 Valpolicella 用新鮮葡萄釀造，很少使用新橡木桶，風格簡單。酒體飽滿、酒精高、帶果乾的風格描述的是 Amarone；用風乾葡萄釀的甜紅酒是 Recioto della Valpolicella。非常高的單寧和長時間的橡木桶陳年則指向內比歐露。","How does Valpolicella DOC Classico differ from Valpolicella DOC?":"Valpolicella DOC Classico 與 Valpolicella DOC 有什麼不同？","It comes from the hilly heartland and has more body and complexity":"它來自多丘陵的核心地帶，酒體更飽滿、更複雜","It is made from dried grapes and is always sweet":"它用風乾葡萄釀造，一定是甜的","It must age at least five years in oak":"它必須在橡木桶中陳年至少五年","It is made only from local white grapes":"它只用在地白葡萄釀造","Classico comes from the hillier heartland and has more body and complexity.":"Classico 來自丘陵更多的核心地帶，酒體更飽滿、更複雜。","Classico is about place: the historic centre of an area, often its hilliest part, which gives more concentrated wines. That is why Valpolicella Classico usually has more body and complexity than basic Valpolicella. Both are made from fresh grapes; dried grapes are used for Amarone and Recioto.":"Classico 說的是地點：一個地區的歷史核心，常常是丘陵最多的部分，能出產更濃縮的酒。這就是為什麼 Valpolicella Classico 通常比基本的 Valpolicella 酒體更飽滿、更複雜。兩者都用新鮮葡萄釀造；風乾葡萄用於 Amarone 和 Recioto。","What does appassimento involve?":"Appassimento 是指什麼？","Picking grapes and drying them indoors":"採收葡萄後在室內風乾","Leaving grapes to freeze on the vine":"讓葡萄在樹上結冰","Maturing the wine in new barrels":"在新橡木桶中熟成酒","Adding alcohol during fermentation":"在發酵期間添加酒精","In appassimento, picked grapes are dried indoors and become concentrated.":"在 appassimento 中，採收後的葡萄在室內風乾並變得濃縮。","Appassimento is widely used in the Veneto. After picking, the grapes are dried indoors: they lose water and concentrate their sugars, acids, tannins and flavours. It is the basis of Amarone, Recioto della Valpolicella and Recioto di Soave. It has nothing to do with frost, oak or adding alcohol.":"Appassimento 在威尼托廣泛使用。採收後，葡萄在室內風乾：它們失去水分，糖、酸、單寧和風味隨之濃縮。這是 Amarone、Recioto della Valpolicella 和 Recioto di Soave 的基礎。它與霜凍、橡木桶或添加酒精都無關。","Which description fits Amarone della Valpolicella DOCG?":"哪一項描述符合 Amarone della Valpolicella DOCG？","Dry to off-dry, full-bodied, about 15% abv, high tannins":"不甜至微甜、酒體飽滿、約 15% abv、高單寧","Sweet, light-bodied, low alcohol, low tannins":"甜、酒體輕盈、低酒精、低單寧","Dry, light-bodied, fruity, for drinking young":"不甜、酒體輕盈、果香豐富，要趁年輕喝","Dry, medium-bodied, medium acidity, black fruit":"不甜、酒體中等、中等酸度、黑色水果","Amarone, from partially dried grapes, is full-bodied, alcoholic and tannic.":"用部分風乾葡萄釀造的 Amarone，酒體飽滿、酒精高、單寧多。","Appassimento concentrates sugars, tannins and flavours: that is why Amarone reaches around 15% abv, with high tannins and pronounced cherry and dried-fruit flavours. A light, fruity style describes basic Valpolicella, made from fresh grapes; medium acidity and black fruit describe Montepulciano.":"Appassimento 濃縮了糖分、單寧和風味：這就是為什麼 Amarone 能達到約 15% abv，單寧高，帶有濃郁的櫻桃和果乾風味。輕盈、果香豐富的風格描述的是用新鮮葡萄釀的基本 Valpolicella；中等酸度和黑色水果描述的是蒙鐵布奇亞諾。","Why is Recioto della Valpolicella DOCG a sweet wine?":"為什麼 Recioto della Valpolicella DOCG 是甜酒？","Sugars are so concentrated the yeast cannot ferment them all":"糖分濃縮到酵母無法全部發酵","Fresh grape juice is added after fermentation":"在發酵後加入新鮮葡萄汁","The grapes are affected by noble rot in the vineyard":"葡萄在葡萄園中受到貴腐菌感染","The wine matures for a long time in new oak":"酒在新橡木桶中長時間熟成","Dried grapes hold so much sugar that the yeast cannot reach dryness.":"風乾的葡萄含糖量太高，酵母無法發酵至不甜。","Both Amarone and Recioto della Valpolicella are made from partially dried grapes. In Recioto, however, the sugars are so concentrated that the yeast stops before turning them all into alcohol, so sugar remains in the wine. Amarone instead ferments to a dry to off-dry style.":"Amarone 和 Recioto della Valpolicella 都是用部分風乾的葡萄釀造的。不過在 Recioto 中，糖分濃縮到酵母在把糖全部轉化為酒精之前就停止了，所以糖留在酒中。Amarone 則發酵成不甜至微甜的風格。","Which flavours are typical of Amarone?":"哪些風味是 Amarone 的典型特徵？","Fresh red cherry plus prunes, raisins and figs":"新鮮紅櫻桃加上黑李乾、葡萄乾和無花果","Apple, pear, lemon and fennel":"蘋果、梨、檸檬和茴香","Peach, melon, mango and smoke":"桃子、哈密瓜、芒果和煙燻","Red cherry, black pepper, no oak":"紅櫻桃、黑胡椒，沒有橡木味","Amarone combines fresh fruit with dried fruit from appassimento.":"Amarone 結合了新鮮果味和來自 appassimento 的果乾。","The dried grapes give Amarone, alongside fresh cherry, dried-fruit notes such as prunes, raisins and figs. Apple, lemon and fennel describe Verdicchio; peach, mango and smoke an oaked Fiano; cherry and black pepper with no oak suggest a simple Barbera.":"風乾的葡萄讓 Amarone 在新鮮櫻桃之外，帶有黑李乾、葡萄乾和無花果等果乾氣息。蘋果、檸檬和茴香描述的是維蒂奇諾；桃子、芒果和煙燻描述的是經橡木桶的菲亞諾；櫻桃和黑胡椒加上沒有橡木味則讓人想到簡單的巴貝拉。","Which of these wines is made from fresh rather than dried grapes?":"下列哪一款酒是用新鮮而非風乾的葡萄釀造的？","Valpolicella Classico uses fresh grapes; the other three use dried grapes.":"Valpolicella Classico 使用新鮮葡萄；其他三款使用風乾葡萄。","Amarone, Recioto della Valpolicella and Recioto di Soave all rely on appassimento. Valpolicella Classico, by contrast, is made from fresh grapes: it comes from the hilly heartland and has more body and complexity than basic Valpolicella, but not the concentration of dried grapes.":"Amarone、Recioto della Valpolicella 和 Recioto di Soave 都仰賴 appassimento。相反地，Valpolicella Classico 用新鮮葡萄釀造：它來自多丘陵的核心地帶，比基本的 Valpolicella 酒體更飽滿、更複雜，但沒有風乾葡萄的濃縮度。","Where is Sangiovese most famous for producing red wines?":"山吉歐維榭在哪裡以出產紅酒最為著名？","Chianti, in central Tuscany":"Chianti，在托斯卡尼中部","Valpolicella, in the Veneto":"Valpolicella，在威尼托","Asti, in Piemonte":"Asti，在皮埃蒙特","Abruzzo, on the east coast":"阿布魯佐，在東海岸","Sangiovese is most famous for the red wines of Chianti, in Tuscany.":"山吉歐維榭最著名的是托斯卡尼 Chianti 的紅酒。","Sangiovese is grown in many parts of Italy, but it owes its fame to Chianti, where it is the dominant grape, often with small amounts of other black grapes. Valpolicella is Corvina country, Asti is Barbera's, and Abruzzo, east of the Apennines, belongs to Montepulciano.":"山吉歐維榭（Sangiovese）種植於義大利許多地方，但它的名氣來自 Chianti，在那裡它是主導品種，常搭配少量其他黑葡萄。Valpolicella 是科維納的天下，Asti 是巴貝拉的，而亞平寧山脈以東的阿布魯佐屬於蒙鐵布奇亞諾。","Compared with the wider Chianti DOCG, Chianti Classico DOCG vineyards:":"與範圍更廣的 Chianti DOCG 相比，Chianti Classico DOCG 的葡萄園：","Sit higher and enjoy a long ripening season":"位置較高，享有漫長的成熟期","Lie on the plains and ripen very quickly":"位於平原，成熟得非常快","Lie on the coast and make sweet wines":"位於海岸，出產甜酒","Use only grapes dried indoors":"只使用在室內風乾的葡萄","Chianti Classico is at higher altitude, giving Sangiovese a long ripening season.":"Chianti Classico 海拔較高，讓山吉歐維榭有漫長的成熟期。","Chianti DOCG covers a wide area of varied quality, often simple, inexpensive wines. Chianti Classico DOCG, higher up, gives Sangiovese a long ripening season: the result is a medium-bodied wine with pronounced red fruit and dried herbs, often matured in oak.":"Chianti DOCG 涵蓋品質不一的廣大區域，常是簡單、平價的酒。位置較高的 Chianti Classico DOCG 讓山吉歐維榭有漫長的成熟期：結果是一款酒體中等、帶有濃郁紅色水果和乾燥香草植物、常經橡木桶熟成的酒。","Which notes does oak maturation often add to Chianti Classico?":"橡木桶熟成常為 Chianti Classico 增添哪些氣息？","Cloves and cedar":"丁香和雪松","Honey and almond":"蜂蜜和杏仁","Black pepper and black plum":"黑胡椒和黑李","Oak softens Chianti Classico's tannins and adds cloves and cedar.":"橡木桶柔化 Chianti Classico 的單寧，並增添丁香和雪松。","Sangiovese has high tannins, so Chianti Classico is often matured in oak: the tannins soften and complex aromas such as cloves and cedar appear. With bottle age the best develop meat and leather. Bread and biscuit, by contrast, come from lees.":"山吉歐維榭的單寧很高，所以 Chianti Classico 常在橡木桶中熟成：單寧變柔和，並出現丁香和雪松等複雜香氣。經過瓶中陳年，最好的酒款會發展出肉和皮革。相反地，麵包和餅乾來自酒渣。","What is Brunello?":"Brunello 是什麼？","The local name for Sangiovese in Montalcino":"山吉歐維榭在 Montalcino 的在地名稱","A white grape from southern Tuscany":"托斯卡尼南部的白葡萄","A synonym for Nebbiolo in Piemonte":"內比歐露在皮埃蒙特的同義名稱","A method of drying grapes":"一種風乾葡萄的方法","Brunello is the local name used for Sangiovese in Montalcino.":"Brunello 是 Montalcino 對山吉歐維榭的在地稱呼。","Brunello di Montalcino DOCG comes from the warm, sunny town of Montalcino in southern Tuscany. It is a powerful, full-bodied Sangiovese with very high tannin and acidity, which must mature in oak for an extended period before release and can age for a very long time in bottle.":"Brunello di Montalcino DOCG 來自托斯卡尼南部溫暖晴朗的 Montalcino 鎮。它是強勁、酒體飽滿的山吉歐維榭，單寧和酸度都非常高，上市前必須在橡木桶中長時間熟成，能在瓶中陳年非常久。","Which description fits Brunello di Montalcino DOCG?":"哪一項描述符合 Brunello di Montalcino DOCG？","Full-bodied, very high tannin and acidity, long oak, very long-lived":"酒體飽滿、單寧和酸度非常高、長時間橡木桶、非常長壽","Light, fruity, unoaked, for drinking young":"輕盈、果香豐富、不經橡木桶，要趁年輕喝","Deep colour, medium acidity, black fruit, inexpensive":"顏色深、中等酸度、黑色水果、價格平實","Brunello is a powerful, highly structured and very long-lived Sangiovese.":"Brunello 是強勁、結構非常紮實、非常長壽的山吉歐維榭。","Montalcino's warm, sunny climate gives a powerful, full-bodied Sangiovese with very high tannin and acidity. It must mature in oak for a long time before release and can age for many years. The light style describes Valpolicella, the sweet one Recioto, and deep colour with medium acidity Montepulciano d'Abruzzo.":"Montalcino 溫暖晴朗的氣候，帶來強勁、酒體飽滿、單寧和酸度非常高的山吉歐維榭。它上市前必須在橡木桶中長時間熟成，能陳年多年。輕盈的風格描述的是 Valpolicella，甜型描述的是 Recioto，而顏色深、中等酸度描述的是 Montepulciano d'Abruzzo。","Which profile best describes Montepulciano?":"哪一種風味特徵最能描述蒙鐵布奇亞諾？","Deep colour, medium acidity, high tannins, black fruit":"顏色深、中等酸度、高單寧、黑色水果","Pale colour, high acidity, low tannins, red fruit":"顏色淺、高酸度、低單寧、紅色水果","High acidity, high tannins, red fruit, dried herbs":"高酸度、高單寧、紅色水果、乾燥香草植物","High acidity, medium tannins, red fruit, black pepper":"高酸度、中等單寧、紅色水果、黑胡椒","Montepulciano is dark and tannic, with medium acidity and black fruit.":"蒙鐵布奇亞諾顏色深、單寧多，酸度中等，帶有黑色水果。","Montepulciano is the only red in the group with black fruit (black plum, black cherry) and medium acidity. High acidity and tannins with red fruit and dried herbs describe Sangiovese; high acidity, medium tannins, red fruit and black pepper suggest Barbera.":"蒙鐵布奇亞諾（Montepulciano）是這一組中唯一帶有黑色水果（黑李、黑櫻桃）且酸度中等的紅葡萄。高酸度和高單寧加上紅色水果和乾燥香草植物描述的是山吉歐維榭；高酸度、中等單寧、紅色水果和黑胡椒則讓人想到巴貝拉。","What is the style of most Montepulciano d'Abruzzo DOC?":"大多數 Montepulciano d'Abruzzo DOC 是什麼風格？","Simple, fruity, inexpensive, for early drinking":"簡單、果香豐富、價格平實，適合早飲","Powerful, long oak-aged, very long-lived":"強勁、長時間橡木桶陳年、非常長壽","Sweet, from partially dried grapes":"甜，用部分風乾的葡萄釀造","Light, pale, with very high acidity":"輕盈、顏色淺、酸度非常高","Abruzzo makes large volumes of simple, fruity, inexpensive Montepulciano.":"阿布魯佐生產大量簡單、果香豐富、價格平實的蒙鐵布奇亞諾。","Most Montepulciano d'Abruzzo is a simple, fruity red for drinking young, made in large volumes at low prices. Only the more concentrated wines may spend a short time in oak. Long oak ageing and great longevity describe Brunello or Barolo instead.":"大多數 Montepulciano d'Abruzzo 是要趁年輕喝的簡單果香紅酒，大量生產、價格低廉。只有較濃縮的酒款可能在橡木桶中待一小段時間。長時間的橡木桶陳年和極佳的陳年潛力描述的則是 Brunello 或 Barolo。","What does Riserva indicate on an Italian DOC or DOCG wine?":"義大利 DOC 或 DOCG 酒款上的 Riserva 代表什麼？","A minimum period of ageing before release":"上市前的最低陳年期","Grapes from the historic centre of the area":"葡萄來自這個地區的歷史核心","Grapes partially dried indoors":"葡萄在室內部分風乾","Vineyards at higher altitude":"海拔較高的葡萄園","Riserva means the wine was aged for at least a set number of months before release.":"Riserva 代表這款酒在上市前至少陳年了規定的月數。","Riserva is about time, Classico about place. A Chianti Classico DOCG Riserva, for example, must meet stricter ageing rules and may already show some tertiary notes on release. Appassimento is a winemaking technique, not a label term linked to age.":"Riserva 說的是時間，Classico 說的是地點。例如 Chianti Classico DOCG Riserva 必須符合更嚴格的陳年規定，上市時可能已經展現一些三級氣息。Appassimento 是一種釀造技術，不是與年齡相關的酒標術語。","Which of these wines is named after both its grape and its area?":"下列哪一款酒是同時以品種和地區命名的？","Barbera d'Asti means 'Barbera from Asti': grape plus area.":"Barbera d'Asti 的意思是「來自 Asti 的巴貝拉」：品種加上地區。","In Italy some wines are named only after their area, such as Barolo, Barbaresco and Valpolicella, so you need to know that Nebbiolo and Corvina lie behind them. Others combine grape and area, such as Barbera d'Asti or Montepulciano d'Abruzzo, and the name itself reveals the grape.":"在義大利，有些酒只以地區命名，例如 Barolo、Barbaresco 和 Valpolicella，所以你需要知道它們背後是內比歐露和科維納。其他的則結合品種和地區，例如 Barbera d'Asti 或 Montepulciano d'Abruzzo，名稱本身就透露了品種。","Where are northern Italy's vineyard regions located?":"北義的葡萄園產區位於哪裡？","In the Alpine foothills and on flat river plains":"在阿爾卑斯山麓和平坦的河流平原上","Only on the islands and along the coasts":"只在島嶼和沿海地區","High up on Alpine peaks, above the glaciers":"在阿爾卑斯山峰的高處，冰河之上","Along the Apennine spine, down to the south":"沿著亞平寧山脈一路往南","Northern Italy's wine regions lie in the Alpine foothills and on flat river plains.":"北義的葡萄酒產區位於阿爾卑斯山麓和平坦的河流平原上。","Many of the best areas are sheltered by the mountains to the north and offer a wide range of slopes and soils. The climate is generally moderate. The Apennines instead divide central Italy, home of Sangiovese and Montepulciano.":"許多最好的地區受到北方山脈的屏障，並提供多樣的坡地和土壤。氣候一般溫和。亞平寧山脈則把義大利中部一分為二，那裡是山吉歐維榭和蒙鐵布奇亞諾的故鄉。","Which aromas are typical of Nebbiolo?":"哪些香氣是內比歐露的典型特徵？","Red cherry, red plum, dried herbs, sometimes rose and violet":"紅櫻桃、紅李、乾燥香草植物，有時有玫瑰和紫羅蘭","Grapefruit, passion fruit and tomato leaf":"葡萄柚、百香果和番茄葉","Blackcurrant, mint and green bell pepper":"黑醋栗、薄荷和青椒","Nebbiolo smells of red fruit and dried herbs, often with floral rose and violet notes.":"內比歐露聞起來有紅色水果和乾燥香草植物，常帶有玫瑰和紫羅蘭的花香。","Its aromas are of red rather than black fruit. Blackcurrant, mint and green pepper suggest Cabernet Sauvignon; banana and candy suggest Beaujolais; grapefruit and passion fruit suggest Sauvignon Blanc.":"它的香氣是紅色而非黑色水果。黑醋栗、薄荷和青椒讓人想到卡本內蘇維濃；香蕉和糖果讓人想到 Beaujolais；葡萄柚和百香果讓人想到白蘇維濃。","At a tasting, a red shows rose, violet, red cherry, high acidity and very grippy tannins. Which grape is most likely?":"在一場品飲中，一款紅酒展現玫瑰、紫羅蘭、紅櫻桃、高酸度和非常緊澀的單寧。最可能是哪個品種？","Gamay made in inert vessels":"在惰性容器中釀造的加美","High acidity and high tannin with red fruit and floral notes is Nebbiolo's signature.":"高酸度和高單寧加上紅色水果和花香，是內比歐露的招牌特徵。","Barbera, Corvina and Gamay also have high acidity and red fruit, but low to medium tannin. The very firm tannin is the decisive clue: of these grapes only Nebbiolo has it.":"巴貝拉、科維納和加美也有高酸度和紅色水果，但單寧低至中等。非常紮實的單寧是決定性的線索：這些品種中只有內比歐露具備。","Why do Nebbiolo wines often improve with bottle age?":"為什麼內比歐露的酒常常隨瓶中陳年而變好？","Because of their high acidity and high tannins":"因為它們的高酸度和高單寧","Because they have a lot of residual sugar":"因為它們有大量殘糖","Because they are light and low in alcohol":"因為它們輕盈、酒精低","Because they are made from grapes dried indoors for months":"因為它們是用在室內風乾數月的葡萄釀的","High acidity and high tannin give Nebbiolo the structure to develop for a long time in bottle.":"高酸度和高單寧給了內比歐露在瓶中長期發展的結構。","Over time the best develop mushroom, tobacco and leather. Barolo and Barbaresco are dry wines from fresh grapes: appassimento belongs to the Veneto, for Amarone and Recioto. Lightness and low alcohol do not help a wine to last.":"隨著時間，最好的酒款會發展出蘑菇、菸草和皮革。Barolo 和 Barbaresco 是用新鮮葡萄釀的不甜酒：appassimento 屬於威尼托，用於 Amarone 和 Recioto。輕盈和低酒精無助於酒的保存。","Why do some Nebbiolo producers choose new barrels instead of old ones?":"為什麼有些內比歐露生產者選擇新橡木桶而不是舊橡木桶？","To add new-oak aromas to the wine":"為了為酒增添新橡木桶的香氣","Because Barolo law requires only new barrels":"因為 Barolo 的法律只允許使用新橡木桶","To raise the tannins, which are too low in Nebbiolo":"為了提高內比歐露太低的單寧","New oak gives aromas such as vanilla and toast, while old oak softens without adding them.":"新橡木桶帶來香草和烘烤等香氣，而舊桶能柔化單寧卻不增添這些香氣。","Nebbiolo is often aged for a long time in oak to soften its already high tannins. The choice between old and new oak is free and depends on the style wanted. Oak adds no sugar.":"內比歐露常在橡木桶中長時間陳年，以柔化它本來就很高的單寧。舊桶和新桶之間的選擇是自由的，取決於想要的風格。橡木桶不會增添糖分。","Which statement about Barolo and Barbaresco is correct?":"關於 Barolo 和 Barbaresco，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","Both are powerful, long-lived Nebbiolos; Barbaresco is the smaller area":"兩者都是強勁、長壽的內比歐露；Barbaresco 的區域較小","Barolo is Nebbiolo, Barbaresco is Barbera":"Barolo 是內比歐露，Barbaresco 是巴貝拉","Barbaresco is a light wine to drink within a year":"Barbaresco 是要在一年內喝掉的輕盈酒款","They are in Tuscany, on either side of the Apennines":"它們位於托斯卡尼，在亞平寧山脈兩側","Barbaresco, smaller and north-east of Barolo, makes equally powerful, long-lived Nebbiolo.":"較小、位於 Barolo 東北方的 Barbaresco，出產同樣強勁、長壽的內比歐露。","Both DOCGs are in Piemonte, in the north-west, not in Tuscany. Barbera's flagship DOCG is in Asti. With such high tannin and acidity, Barbaresco is not a wine for immediate drinking.":"這兩個 DOCG 都位於西北部的皮埃蒙特，不在托斯卡尼。巴貝拉的旗艦 DOCG 在 Asti。單寧和酸度這麼高的 Barbaresco，不是適合立即飲用的酒。","Which aromas are typical of Barbera?":"哪些香氣是巴貝拉的典型特徵？","Red cherry and red plum, sometimes black pepper":"紅櫻桃和紅李，有時有黑胡椒","Green apple, lemon and fennel":"青蘋果、檸檬和茴香","Prunes, raisins and figs from dried grapes":"來自風乾葡萄的黑李乾、葡萄乾和無花果","Blackberry and chocolate":"黑莓和巧克力","Barbera smells of red fruit (cherry, red plum) and sometimes black pepper.":"巴貝拉（Barbera）聞起來有紅色水果（櫻桃、紅李），有時還有黑胡椒。","Apple, lemon and fennel describe a white such as Verdicchio. Prunes and figs come from Amarone's appassimento. Blackberry and chocolate suggest an oaked Carmenère or Pinotage.":"蘋果、檸檬和茴香描述的是維蒂奇諾這樣的白酒。黑李乾和無花果來自 Amarone 的 appassimento。黑莓和巧克力則讓人想到經橡木桶的卡門內爾或皮諾塔吉。","Which statement about oak use in Barbera is correct?":"關於巴貝拉使用橡木桶，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","Many are unoaked and fruity; some are oak-aged for complexity":"許多不經橡木桶、果香豐富；有些經橡木桶陳年以增添複雜度","It must always age at least five years in new barrels":"它必須一律在新橡木桶中陳年至少五年","Oak is banned by law throughout Piemonte for any red wine":"整個皮埃蒙特依法禁止任何紅酒使用橡木桶","It is used only to make it sweet":"它只用來讓酒變甜","Many Barberas are unoaked and fruity, but some producers age them in oak for extra complexity.":"許多巴貝拉不經橡木桶、果香豐富，但有些生產者會讓它在橡木桶中陳年以增添複雜度。","Oak is a style choice, neither required nor banned. With its low tannins Barbera does not need long ageing to soften, unlike Nebbiolo. Oak does not create sweetness.":"橡木桶是風格上的選擇，既非必要也未被禁止。單寧低的巴貝拉不像內比歐露那樣需要長時間陳年來柔化。橡木桶不會帶來甜味。","How does Barbera's ageing potential compare with Nebbiolo's?":"巴貝拉的陳年潛力與內比歐露相比如何？","It is generally shorter":"一般較短","It is always much longer, thanks to higher tannins":"由於單寧更高，總是長得多","It is identical":"完全相同","Barbera cannot age at all":"巴貝拉完全無法陳年","Barbera wines generally have shorter ageing potential than Nebbiolo wines.":"巴貝拉的陳年潛力一般比內比歐露短。","Barbera has low to medium tannin while Nebbiolo's is high. Very good Barberas can still age, so it is not true that they cannot; they simply last less long.":"巴貝拉的單寧低至中等，而內比歐露的單寧很高。非常好的巴貝拉仍然能陳年，所以說它們無法陳年是錯的；只是時間較短。","A customer wants a Piemonte red to drink young, with lively acidity and soft tannins. What do you suggest?":"一位顧客想要一款要趁年輕喝、酸度活潑、單寧柔和的皮埃蒙特紅酒。你會推薦什麼？","A Barbera d'Asti":"Barbera d'Asti","A young Barolo, just released":"剛上市的年輕 Barolo","A Barbaresco":"Barbaresco","An Amarone della Valpolicella":"Amarone della Valpolicella","Barbera combines high acidity with low tannin, so it is enjoyable sooner than Nebbiolo.":"巴貝拉結合了高酸度和低單寧，所以比內比歐露更早好喝。","Barolo and Barbaresco are high-tannin Nebbiolos that usually need years to soften. Amarone comes from the Veneto, not Piemonte, and has high tannin and about 15% alcohol.":"Barolo 和 Barbaresco 是高單寧的內比歐露，通常需要多年才能柔化。Amarone 來自威尼托而不是皮埃蒙特，單寧高、酒精約 15%。","A Barolo DOCG from a producer using only old barrels":"只使用舊橡木桶的生產者釀的 Barolo DOCG","Barbera d'Asti is made from Barbera, as its name says; Barolo and Barbaresco are Nebbiolo.":"Barbera d'Asti 顧名思義是用巴貝拉釀的；Barolo 和 Barbaresco 是內比歐露。","All three are Piemonte DOCGs, which can confuse. Nebbiolo is the only grape allowed in Barolo, whatever barrels are used. Barbaresco uses the same grape in a smaller area.":"三者都是皮埃蒙特的 DOCG，可能讓人混淆。無論使用什麼橡木桶，內比歐露都是 Barolo 唯一允許的品種。Barbaresco 在較小的區域使用同一個品種。","What structure does Corvina typically have?":"科維納通常有什麼樣的結構？","High acidity, low to medium tannin":"高酸度，單寧低至中等","Low acidity, very high tannin":"低酸度，單寧非常高","Medium acidity, high tannin, black fruit and deep colour":"中等酸度、高單寧、黑色水果和深色","Low acidity, low tannin":"低酸度，低單寧","Corvina gives wines with high acidity, low to medium tannin and red fruit.":"科維納釀出高酸度、單寧低至中等、帶紅色水果的酒。","Its aromas are red cherry and red plum. Deep colour, high tannin and black fruit describe Montepulciano. Amarone's high tannin comes not from the grape itself but from appassimento, which also concentrates tannin.":"它的香氣是紅櫻桃和紅李。深色、高單寧和黑色水果描述的是蒙鐵布奇亞諾。Amarone 的高單寧不是來自葡萄本身，而是來自同樣會濃縮單寧的 appassimento。","What role does Corvina play in the Valpolicella blend?":"科維納在 Valpolicella 的混調中扮演什麼角色？","It usually dominates, with other local grapes allowed":"它通常佔主導，也允許其他在地品種","It is the only grape allowed, like Nebbiolo in Barolo":"它是唯一允許的品種，就像 Barolo 的內比歐露","It is a small addition to a Sangiovese blend":"它是山吉歐維榭混調中的少量添加","It is used only for the area's rosés, never for reds":"它只用於這個地區的粉紅酒，從不用於紅酒","Corvina is Valpolicella's main grape and usually dominates the blend.":"科維納是 Valpolicella 的主要品種，通常在混調中佔主導。","Unlike Barolo, Valpolicella also allows other local grapes. Sangiovese belongs to Tuscany. Corvina makes reds, from simple Valpolicella to Amarone and Recioto.":"與 Barolo 不同，Valpolicella 也允許其他在地品種。山吉歐維榭屬於托斯卡尼。科維納用來釀紅酒，從簡單的 Valpolicella 到 Amarone 和 Recioto 都有。","In which region is Valpolicella?":"Valpolicella 位於哪個地區？","Veneto, in the north-east":"威尼托，在東北部","Piemonte, in the north-west":"皮埃蒙特，在西北部","Tuscany, in the centre":"托斯卡尼，在中部","Abruzzo, on the east-central Adriatic coast":"阿布魯佐，在中東部的亞得里亞海沿岸","Valpolicella is in the Veneto, in north-east Italy.":"Valpolicella 位於義大利東北部的威尼托。","The Veneto makes wide use of appassimento, the basis of Amarone, Recioto della Valpolicella and Recioto di Soave. Piemonte is home to Nebbiolo and Barbera, Tuscany to Sangiovese, Abruzzo to Montepulciano.":"威尼托廣泛使用 appassimento，這是 Amarone、Recioto della Valpolicella 和 Recioto di Soave 的基礎。皮埃蒙特是內比歐露和巴貝拉的故鄉，托斯卡尼是山吉歐維榭的，阿布魯佐是蒙鐵布奇亞諾的。","What do Recioto della Valpolicella and Recioto di Soave share, and how do they differ?":"Recioto della Valpolicella 和 Recioto di Soave 有什麼共同點和不同點？","Both are sweet, from dried grapes; the first is red, the second white":"兩者都是用風乾葡萄釀的甜酒；前者是紅酒，後者是白酒","Both are dry and sparkling; the first is rosé, the second red":"兩者都是不甜的氣泡酒；前者是粉紅酒，後者是紅酒","Both are red; the first is sweet, the second dry and made from fresh grapes":"兩者都是紅酒；前者是甜的，後者是用新鮮葡萄釀的不甜酒","Both are Nebbiolo, from two Piemonte areas":"兩者都是內比歐露，來自皮埃蒙特的兩個地區","Both are sweet Veneto wines made by appassimento: Valpolicella gives a red, Soave a white.":"兩者都是以 appassimento 釀造的威尼托甜酒：Valpolicella 出產紅酒，Soave 出產白酒。","Dried grapes have such concentrated sugars that the yeast cannot ferment them all. Recioto della Valpolicella is mainly Corvina; Recioto di Soave is Garganega, a white grape. Neither is sparkling or from Piemonte.":"風乾葡萄的糖分非常濃縮，酵母無法全部發酵。Recioto della Valpolicella 以科維納為主；Recioto di Soave 則是白葡萄卡爾卡耐卡。兩者都不是氣泡酒，也不來自皮埃蒙特。","Amarone and Recioto della Valpolicella both use dried grapes. What is the main difference in style?":"Amarone 和 Recioto della Valpolicella 都使用風乾葡萄。風格上的主要差異是什麼？","Amarone is dry to off-dry; Recioto is sweet":"Amarone 不甜至微甜；Recioto 是甜的","Amarone is sweet; Recioto is dry":"Amarone 是甜的；Recioto 不甜","Amarone is white; Recioto is red":"Amarone 是白酒；Recioto 是紅酒","Amarone is light and low in alcohol; Recioto is powerful and long-aged":"Amarone 輕盈、酒精低；Recioto 強勁、長時間陳年","In Amarone almost all the sugar ferments (dry to off-dry wine); in Recioto much remains (sweet wine).":"在 Amarone 中，幾乎所有的糖都發酵掉了（不甜至微甜）；在 Recioto 中，大量的糖留了下來（甜酒）。","Because sugar turns into alcohol, Amarone reaches about 15% and is full-bodied: it is far from light. Both are Corvina-based reds; a white Recioto exists, but in Soave.":"由於糖轉化為酒精，Amarone 達到約 15%，酒體飽滿：它絕不輕盈。兩者都是以科維納為基礎的紅酒；白色的 Recioto 是存在的，但在 Soave。","A dry red at about 15% abv has high tannin, fresh cherry plus prunes, raisins and figs. What is it most likely to be?":"一款約 15% abv 的不甜紅酒，單寧高，帶有新鮮櫻桃加上黑李乾、葡萄乾和無花果。它最可能是什麼？","A basic Valpolicella DOC":"基本的 Valpolicella DOC","An unoaked Barbera d'Asti DOCG for drinking young":"要趁年輕喝、不經橡木桶的 Barbera d'Asti DOCG","Fresh and dried fruit, about 15% alcohol and high tannin in a dry wine: that is Amarone.":"不甜的酒中有新鮮和乾燥的果味、約 15% 的酒精和高單寧：那就是 Amarone。","The dried-fruit notes come from appassimento. Recioto would have similar aromas but be sweet. A basic Valpolicella and a young Barbera are light or fruity, with no raisin notes and lower alcohol.":"果乾氣息來自 appassimento。Recioto 會有類似的香氣，但是甜的。基本的 Valpolicella 和年輕的巴貝拉輕盈或果香豐富，沒有葡萄乾氣息，酒精也較低。","How do very good Amarones behave in the bottle?":"非常好的 Amarone 在瓶中表現如何？","They can age positively":"它們能正向陳年","They must be drunk within a few months":"它們必須在幾個月內喝掉","They start fermenting again and turn sparkling":"它們會重新開始發酵並產生氣泡","They quickly lose all their alcohol, body and much of their colour":"它們很快就失去所有酒精、酒體和大部分的顏色","Very good and outstanding Amarones can develop well in the bottle.":"非常好和傑出的 Amarone 能在瓶中好好發展。","Concentration, high alcohol and high tannin are a fine basis for ageing. It is basic Valpolicella that should be drunk young. Alcohol does not vanish in the bottle, and a second fermentation is not part of this style.":"濃縮度、高酒精和高單寧是陳年的良好基礎。要趁年輕喝的是基本的 Valpolicella。酒精不會在瓶中消失，二次發酵也不屬於這種風格。","Which description fits Sangiovese?":"哪一項描述符合山吉歐維榭？","Dry, high tannin and acidity, red cherry, red plum, dried herbs":"不甜、單寧和酸度高、紅櫻桃、紅李、乾燥香草植物","Low tannin, low acidity, banana and candy":"低單寧、低酸度、香蕉和糖果","Deep colour, medium acidity, black plum and black cherry":"顏色深、中等酸度、黑李和黑櫻桃","Sweet, low alcohol, strawberry and raspberry":"甜、低酒精、草莓和覆盆子","Sangiovese gives dry wines with high tannin and acidity, red fruit and dried herbs.":"山吉歐維榭釀出單寧和酸度高、帶紅色水果和乾燥香草植物的不甜酒。","Deep colour, medium acidity and black fruit describe Montepulciano, the other great red of central Italy. Banana and candy belong to Beaujolais; sweet, light and strawberry-scented is White Zinfandel.":"顏色深、中等酸度和黑色水果描述的是義大利中部的另一個偉大紅葡萄——蒙鐵布奇亞諾。香蕉和糖果屬於 Beaujolais；甜、輕盈、帶草莓香的是 White Zinfandel。","Which statement about Chianti DOCG is correct?":"關於 Chianti DOCG，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It covers a wide area of varied quality; many wines are simple":"它涵蓋品質不一的廣大區域；許多酒款很簡單","It makes only very long-ageing wines":"它只出產非常適合長期陳年的酒","It lies in the Alps, in Piemonte":"它位於阿爾卑斯山區的皮埃蒙特","It is smaller and higher than Chianti Classico DOCG, which lies on the plain":"它比位於平原的 Chianti Classico DOCG 更小、更高","Chianti DOCG covers a wide area in the Apennine foothills, with wines of varied quality, often simple and inexpensive.":"Chianti DOCG 涵蓋亞平寧山麓的廣大區域，酒款品質不一，常是簡單、平價的酒。","Many Chianti DOCGs are not made for ageing. It is Chianti Classico that sits higher, with a long ripening season. Chianti is in Tuscany, not Piemonte.":"許多 Chianti DOCG 不是為陳年而釀的。位置較高、成熟期漫長的是 Chianti Classico。Chianti 位於托斯卡尼，不在皮埃蒙特。","What is a Chianti usually made from?":"Chianti 通常用什麼釀造？","Mostly Sangiovese, often with small amounts of other black grapes":"大部分是山吉歐維榭，常搭配少量其他黑葡萄","Mostly Montepulciano with a little Corvina":"大部分是蒙鐵布奇亞諾加上少許科維納","Equal parts white and black grapes, picked and dried together":"白葡萄和黑葡萄各半，一起採收並風乾","Sangiovese dominates Chianti, often with small additions of other black grapes.":"山吉歐維榭在 Chianti 中佔主導，常加入少量其他黑葡萄。","Chianti, in central Tuscany, is Sangiovese's most famous wine. Nebbiolo and Corvina are northern grapes; Montepulciano is mainly planted in Abruzzo, across the Apennines. Chianti is made from fresh, not dried, grapes.":"位於托斯卡尼中部的 Chianti 是山吉歐維榭最著名的酒款。內比歐露和科維納是北部的品種；蒙鐵布奇亞諾主要種在亞平寧山脈另一側的阿布魯佐。Chianti 是用新鮮而非風乾的葡萄釀造的。","What style does a typical Chianti Classico DOCG have?":"典型的 Chianti Classico DOCG 是什麼風格？","Medium body, pronounced red fruit and dried herbs":"酒體中等、濃郁的紅色水果和乾燥香草植物","Light body, banana and candy, served chilled":"酒體輕盈、香蕉和糖果，冰鎮飲用","Full body, about 15% abv, dried fruit":"酒體飽滿、約 15% abv、果乾","Sweet, black colour, black fruit and chocolate from new oak":"甜、黑色、帶黑色水果和來自新橡木桶的巧克力","A typical Chianti Classico is medium-bodied with pronounced red fruit and dried-herb notes.":"典型的 Chianti Classico 酒體中等，帶有濃郁的紅色水果和乾燥香草植物氣息。","It is often oak-aged, which softens tannins and adds clove and cedar. Full body, 15% and dried fruit describe Amarone. Chianti Classico is dry, and banana and candy are typical of Beaujolais.":"它常經橡木桶陳年，能柔化單寧並增添丁香和雪松。酒體飽滿、15% 和果乾描述的是 Amarone。Chianti Classico 是不甜的，而香蕉和糖果是 Beaujolais 的典型特徵。","Which flavours do the best Chianti Classicos develop in the bottle?":"最好的 Chianti Classico 在瓶中會發展出哪些風味？","Meat and leather":"肉和皮革","Grapefruit and gooseberry":"葡萄柚和醋栗","White flowers, fresh peach and apricot":"白花、新鮮桃子和杏桃","With bottle age the best Chianti Classicos develop meat and leather notes.":"經過瓶中陳年，最好的 Chianti Classico 會發展出肉和皮革氣息。","These are tertiary aromas that only come with time. Banana and candy come from Beaujolais winemaking techniques. Grapefruit, gooseberry, peach and white flowers are primary aromas of white wines.":"這些是只有隨時間才會出現的三級香氣。香蕉和糖果來自 Beaujolais 的釀造技術。葡萄柚、醋栗、桃子和白花是白酒的一級香氣。","Compared with a Chianti Classico DOCG, what can you expect from a Chianti Classico DOCG Riserva?":"與 Chianti Classico DOCG 相比，Chianti Classico DOCG Riserva 可以預期有什麼不同？","Longer ageing and perhaps some tertiary notes already":"陳年更久，可能已經帶有一些三級氣息","A younger, fruitier wine":"更年輕、果香更豐富的酒","Grapes from a different area, outside Chianti Classico and away from the historic hills":"葡萄來自不同的地區，在 Chianti Classico 之外、遠離歷史丘陵","Riserva has stricter ageing rules and may already show tertiary notes on release.":"Riserva 有更嚴格的陳年規定，上市時可能已經展現三級氣息。","Riserva is about ageing time, not area: the grapes are still from Chianti Classico. More time before release means less youthful fruit, not more. The term says nothing about sweetness.":"Riserva 說的是陳年時間，不是地區：葡萄仍然來自 Chianti Classico。上市前的時間越長，年輕的果味越少，而不是越多。這個術語與甜度無關。","Where is Montalcino, home of Brunello?":"Brunello 的故鄉 Montalcino 在哪裡？","In southern Tuscany, in a warm, sunny area":"在托斯卡尼南部，溫暖晴朗的地區","In northern Piemonte, at the foot of the Alps":"在皮埃蒙特北部，阿爾卑斯山腳下","In the Veneto, near Soave":"在威尼托，靠近 Soave","In Abruzzo, on the Adriatic coast, in its coolest, rainiest part":"在阿布魯佐的亞得里亞海沿岸，最涼爽多雨的地方","Montalcino is a warm, sunny town in southern Tuscany.":"Montalcino 是托斯卡尼南部一個溫暖晴朗的小鎮。","Heat and sun let Sangiovese, called Brunello here, make powerful, full-bodied wines. Piemonte and the Veneto are in the north; Abruzzo, across the Apennines, is Montepulciano country.":"高溫和陽光讓山吉歐維榭（在這裡稱為 Brunello）釀出強勁、酒體飽滿的酒。皮埃蒙特和威尼托位於北部；亞平寧山脈另一側的阿布魯佐是蒙鐵布奇亞諾的天下。","What do the Apennine Mountains separate in central Italy?":"在義大利中部，亞平寧山脈把什麼分隔開來？","Tuscany in the west (Sangiovese) from Abruzzo in the east (Montepulciano)":"西邊的托斯卡尼（山吉歐維榭）和東邊的阿布魯佐（蒙鐵布奇亞諾）","Piemonte (Nebbiolo) from the Veneto (Corvina)":"皮埃蒙特（內比歐露）和威尼托（科維納）","Tuscany in the east (Montepulciano) from Abruzzo in the west (Sangiovese)":"東邊的托斯卡尼（蒙鐵布奇亞諾）和西邊的阿布魯佐（山吉歐維榭）","Puglia from Sicily":"普利亞和西西里","The Apennines run down Italy's spine, dividing Tuscany in the west from Abruzzo in the east.":"亞平寧山脈沿著義大利的脊梁延伸，把西邊的托斯卡尼和東邊的阿布魯佐分隔開來。","Sangiovese dominates Tuscany and Montepulciano is widely planted in Abruzzo: central Italy's two key reds, both helped by the warm climate. Take care not to swap the directions. Piemonte and the Veneto are in the north, at the foot of the Alps.":"山吉歐維榭在托斯卡尼佔主導，蒙鐵布奇亞諾則廣泛種植於阿布魯佐：這是義大利中部的兩個關鍵紅葡萄，都受益於溫暖的氣候。小心不要把方向搞反了。皮埃蒙特和威尼托位於北部，阿爾卑斯山腳下。","What does the term 'Classico' indicate on an Italian label?":"義大利酒標上的「Classico」代表什麼？","Grapes from the historic heart of the region, often its hilliest part":"葡萄來自這個地區的歷史核心，常是丘陵最多的部分","A legal minimum ageing period before release":"上市前的法定最低陳年期","A wine made from dried grapes":"用風乾葡萄釀的酒","A wine made in an old-fashioned style, unoaked":"以傳統方式釀造、不經橡木桶的酒","Classico means the historic heart of a region; these often hilly sites give more concentrated wines.":"Classico 代表一個地區的歷史核心；這些常位於丘陵的園地能出產更濃縮的酒。","Minimum ageing is the meaning of 'Riserva', often confused with Classico. Examples: Chianti Classico and Valpolicella Classico. The term says nothing about appassimento or oak use.":"最低陳年是「Riserva」的意思，常與 Classico 混淆。例如：Chianti Classico 和 Valpolicella Classico。這個術語與 appassimento 或使用橡木桶無關。","A label shows 'Barolo DOCG' but no grape variety. Why?":"一張酒標上標示「Barolo DOCG」，但沒有標示品種。為什麼？","The wine is named after its area; the grape, Nebbiolo, is implied":"這款酒以地區命名；品種內比歐露是不言而喻的","The producer blended many different grapes and cannot declare them":"生產者混調了許多不同的品種，無法一一申報","It is a table wine with no appellation":"這是沒有法定產區的餐酒","Barolo is the name of a grape":"Barolo 是一個品種的名稱","Barolo is named after its region, and Nebbiolo is the only grape allowed.":"Barolo 以它的產區命名，而內比歐露是唯一允許的品種。","In Italy some wines carry only the area name (Barolo, Barbaresco, Valpolicella), others the grape and the area (Barbera d'Asti). DOCG is the top PDO category, not a table wine. Barolo is not a blend.":"在義大利，有些酒只標示地區名稱（Barolo、Barbaresco、Valpolicella），有些則標示品種和地區（Barbera d'Asti）。DOCG 是最高的 PDO 類別，不是餐酒。Barolo 也不是混調。","Which fruit flavours are typical of Montepulciano?":"哪些果味是蒙鐵布奇亞諾的典型特徵？","Black plum and black cherry":"黑李和黑櫻桃","Green apple and pear":"青蘋果和梨","Prunes, raisins and figs from grapes dried indoors":"來自室內風乾葡萄的黑李乾、葡萄乾和無花果","Montepulciano gives dark wines with black fruit: black plum and black cherry.":"蒙鐵布奇亞諾釀出帶有黑色水果的深色酒：黑李和黑櫻桃。","It is one of the few Italian grapes in this chapter with black rather than red fruit. Strawberry and raspberry suggest Grenache or Pinotage; apple and pear are white-wine aromas. Dried-fruit notes come from appassimento, used for Amarone, not Montepulciano d'Abruzzo.":"它是本章少數帶有黑色而非紅色水果的義大利品種之一。草莓和覆盆子讓人想到格那希或皮諾塔吉；蘋果和梨是白酒的香氣。果乾氣息來自用於 Amarone 而不是 Montepulciano d'Abruzzo 的 appassimento。","What is often done with the more concentrated Montepulciano d'Abruzzo wines?":"較濃縮的 Montepulciano d'Abruzzo 酒款常會怎麼處理？","They are aged for a short time in oak":"在橡木桶中短時間陳年","The grapes are dried to make sweet wines":"把葡萄風乾以釀造甜酒","They are turned into bottle-fermented sparkling wines":"釀成瓶中發酵的氣泡酒","They are made as white wine, removing the dark skins at once":"釀成白酒，立刻去除深色果皮","The more concentrated Montepulcianos may be matured for a short time in oak.":"較濃縮的蒙鐵布奇亞諾可能在橡木桶中短時間熟成。","Abruzzo makes large volumes of inexpensive wine, mostly simple, fruity and for early drinking. Only the more concentrated wines see a little oak. Appassimento and sparkling methods are not part of this style.":"阿布魯佐生產大量平價的酒，大多簡單、果香豐富、適合早飲。只有較濃縮的酒款會經過少許橡木桶。Appassimento 和氣泡酒的方法都不屬於這種風格。","What sets Montepulciano apart from Sangiovese in the glass?":"在杯中，蒙鐵布奇亞諾與山吉歐維榭有什麼不同？","Deeper colour, medium acidity and black fruit":"顏色更深、中等酸度、黑色水果","Paler colour, higher acidity and red fruit":"顏色更淺、酸度更高、紅色水果","Much lower tannin and floral rose and violet notes":"單寧低得多，帶有玫瑰和紫羅蘭花香","No difference: they are the same grape":"沒有不同：它們是同一個品種","Montepulciano is darker, with medium acidity and black fruit; Sangiovese has high acidity and red fruit.":"蒙鐵布奇亞諾顏色更深，酸度中等，帶黑色水果；山吉歐維榭酸度高，帶紅色水果。","Both have high tannin, so that is not what sets them apart. Rose and violet are typical of Nebbiolo. Montepulciano is grown mainly in Abruzzo, Sangiovese in Tuscany.":"兩者的單寧都很高，所以那不是區別所在。玫瑰和紫羅蘭是內比歐露的典型特徵。蒙鐵布奇亞諾主要種在阿布魯佐，山吉歐維榭則在托斯卡尼。","In which part of Italy is Puglia, home of Primitivo?":"普里米蒂沃的故鄉普利亞位於義大利哪個部分？","In the south":"南部","In the north-west, next to Piemonte":"西北部，緊鄰皮埃蒙特","In the north-east, in the Alpine foothills, near Valpolicella":"東北部的阿爾卑斯山麓，靠近 Valpolicella","In the centre, between Tuscany and Abruzzo":"中部，在托斯卡尼和阿布魯佐之間","Puglia is a warm region in southern Italy.":"普利亞是義大利南部的溫暖地區。","The southern heat lets Primitivo, a grape that needs a warm climate, ripen fully. The north (Piemonte, Veneto) is more moderate; the centre is home to Sangiovese and Montepulciano.":"南部的高溫讓需要溫暖氣候的普里米蒂沃完全成熟。北部（皮埃蒙特、威尼托）較溫和；中部則是山吉歐維榭和蒙鐵布奇亞諾的故鄉。","How is the medium sweetness of White Zinfandel achieved?":"White Zinfandel 的半甜是怎麼達成的？","By removing the yeasts before fermentation finishes":"在發酵結束前去除酵母","By drying the grapes after harvest":"在採收後風乾葡萄","By adding alcohol during fermentation":"在發酵期間添加酒精","By using grapes affected by noble rot":"使用受貴腐菌感染的葡萄","Stopping fermentation by removing yeasts leaves residual sugar and low alcohol.":"去除酵母以中止發酵，會留下殘糖和低酒精。","White Zinfandel is a medium-sweet Californian rosé, usually made with brief skin contact. To keep some of the sugar, the yeasts are removed before they have turned it all into alcohol. The result is a simple, fruity pink wine with low alcohol, typically 8 to 10%, and aromas of strawberry and raspberry.":"White Zinfandel 是加州的半甜粉紅酒，通常以短暫的果皮接觸釀造。為了保留部分糖分，會在酵母把糖全部轉化為酒精之前把它們去除。結果是一款簡單、果香豐富的粉紅酒，酒精低，通常為 8 到 10%，帶有草莓和覆盆子香氣。","Which description fits a typical Californian red Zinfandel?":"哪一項描述符合典型的加州金芬黛紅酒？","Dry, high alcohol, full body, black and dried fruit":"不甜、酒精高、酒體飽滿、黑色水果和果乾","Medium-sweet, low alcohol, simple red fruit":"半甜、酒精低、簡單的紅色水果","Light, low tannin, fresh strawberry":"輕盈、低單寧、新鮮草莓","Dry, low alcohol, grassy green notes":"不甜、酒精低、青草般的青澀氣息","Red Zinfandel is dry, powerful and high in alcohol, with red, black and dried fruit.":"金芬黛紅酒不甜、強勁、酒精高，帶有紅色水果、黑色水果和果乾。","Red Zinfandel ferments fully on its skins and is often matured in oak. It shows pronounced raspberry, blueberry and blackberry, dried fruit such as raisin and prune, and vanilla and coffee from oak. It is dry, with medium to high acidity and tannin, high alcohol and full body. The sweet, light profile describes White Zinfandel instead.":"金芬黛紅酒帶皮完全發酵，常經橡木桶熟成。它展現濃郁的覆盆子、藍莓和黑莓，葡萄乾和黑李乾等果乾，以及來自橡木的香草和咖啡。它不甜，酸度和單寧中等至高，酒精高，酒體飽滿。甜而輕盈的風味特徵描述的則是 White Zinfandel。","Why can Zinfandel show raisin and prune flavours?":"為什麼金芬黛可能展現葡萄乾和黑李乾的風味？","Some berries raisin before the others have ripened":"有些果粒在其他果粒成熟之前就乾縮了","The grapes are picked very early":"葡萄非常早就採收","The wine ferments in stainless steel":"酒在不鏽鋼槽中發酵","The grapes are affected by noble rot":"葡萄受到貴腐菌感染","Uneven ripening shrivels some berries, giving high sugar and dried-fruit notes.":"成熟不均讓部分果粒乾縮，帶來高糖分和果乾氣息。","Zinfandel ripens unevenly: within one bunch, some berries can start to shrivel while others are not yet ripe. The shrivelled berries concentrate sugar and bring dried-fruit aromas such as prune and raisin. This also helps explain the high alcohol of the reds. Noble rot plays no part; it is linked to sweet wines such as those of Tokaj or Sauternes.":"金芬黛成熟不均：在同一串果串中，有些果粒可能開始乾縮，而其他的還沒成熟。乾縮的果粒濃縮了糖分，帶來黑李乾和葡萄乾等果乾香氣。這也有助於解釋紅酒的高酒精。貴腐菌不參與其中；它與 Tokaj 或 Sauternes 等甜酒有關。","What climate does Zinfandel need to ripen successfully?":"金芬黛需要什麼氣候才能順利成熟？","Cold and foggy":"寒冷多霧","Zinfandel is a black grape that needs a warm climate to ripen.":"金芬黛是需要溫暖氣候才能成熟的黑葡萄。","Unlike Pinot Noir, which prefers cool or moderate climates, Zinfandel needs warmth to ripen. With heat its flavours shift from red to black fruit, and some berries may shrivel, raising sugar levels. That is why its reds, in California as in Puglia, are often rich, soft and high in alcohol.":"黑皮諾偏好涼爽或溫和的氣候，金芬黛則不同，它需要熱量才能成熟。在高溫下，它的風味從紅色水果轉向黑色水果，有些果粒可能乾縮，提高糖分。這就是為什麼它的紅酒，無論在加州或普利亞，常常豐潤、柔和、酒精高。","Which tertiary aromas can an old-vine Zinfandel develop?":"老藤金芬黛能發展出哪些三級香氣？","Lime and blossom":"萊姆和花香","Old-vine Zinfandels can evolve in bottle towards earth and meat notes.":"老藤金芬黛能在瓶中朝泥土和肉味演變。","California has some very old Zinfandel vines with low yields and highly concentrated fruit. Their wines have the structure to evolve in bottle and develop tertiary aromas of earth and meat. Honey and petrol are typical of aged Riesling, lime and blossom are primary aromas of white wines, and vanilla comes from oak.":"加州有一些非常古老的金芬黛葡萄樹，產量低、果實高度濃縮。它們的酒有在瓶中演變的結構，能發展出泥土和肉的三級香氣。蜂蜜和汽油是陳年麗絲玲的典型特徵，萊姆和花香是白酒的一級香氣，香草則來自橡木桶。","Which French region does Carmenère originally come from?":"卡門內爾原本來自法國哪個產區？","Carmenère comes from Bordeaux, where it is now rare, and is widely grown in Chile.":"卡門內爾來自波爾多，現在在那裡很少見，而在智利廣泛種植。","Carmenère originated in Bordeaux but is rarely found there today. It found a home in Chile, where it became a national speciality. Its origin also explains why it is often blended with Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot, two Bordeaux grapes. Burgundy, the Rhône and Alsace are linked to other grapes.":"卡門內爾（Carmenère）起源於波爾多，但今天在那裡已經很少見。它在智利找到了歸宿，成為全國性的特色品種。它的起源也解釋了為什麼它常與卡本內蘇維濃和梅洛這兩個波爾多品種混調。布根地、隆河和阿爾薩斯則與其他品種有關。","Which aromas show a Carmenère picked before full ripeness?":"哪些香氣表示卡門內爾是在完全成熟前採收的？","Blackberry and black plum":"黑莓和黑李","Coffee and chocolate":"咖啡和巧克力","Leather and earth":"皮革和泥土","Underripe Carmenère has pungent herbaceous notes such as green bell pepper and tomato leaf.":"未完全成熟的卡門內爾帶有青椒和番茄葉等刺鼻的草本氣息。","Carmenère ripens with difficulty. If picked too early, the wine shows pungent herbaceous characters: green bell pepper and tomato leaf. Fully ripe, it gives fresh black fruit such as blackberry instead. Coffee and chocolate come from oak; leather and earth are tertiary notes of the best aged wines.":"卡門內爾很難成熟。如果太早採收，酒會展現刺鼻的草本特徵：青椒和番茄葉。完全成熟時，它則帶來黑莓等新鮮的黑色水果。咖啡和巧克力來自橡木桶；皮革和泥土是最好的陳年酒款的三級氣息。","Why does Carmenère ripen well only in the warmest, sunniest Central Valley sites?":"為什麼卡門內爾只在 Central Valley 最溫暖、陽光最充足的園地才能好好成熟？","It needs a long, sunny growing season":"它需要漫長而晴朗的生長季","It needs a cool, foggy climate":"它需要涼爽多霧的氣候","It has thin skins and fears the sun":"它果皮薄，怕太陽","It buds late and ripens very early":"它發芽晚、成熟非常早","Carmenère needs a long, sunny season, which in Chile only the warmest sites provide.":"卡門內爾需要漫長晴朗的生長季，在智利只有最溫暖的園地能提供。","To ripen fully, Carmenère needs a long, sunny growing season. Even in Chile it struggles, except in the warmest, sunniest sites of the Central Valley. If it does not ripen, the wine smells of green pepper; when ripe, it shows fresh black fruit. A cool, foggy climate would make the problem worse.":"要完全成熟，卡門內爾需要漫長而晴朗的生長季。即使在智利它也很難成熟，除非是在 Central Valley 最溫暖、陽光最充足的園地。如果沒有成熟，酒聞起來會有青椒味；成熟時則展現新鮮的黑色水果。涼爽多霧的氣候只會讓問題更嚴重。","Which profile describes a typical ripe Carmenère?":"哪一種風味特徵描述典型的成熟卡門內爾？","Deep colour, high tannin, full body, blackberry":"顏色深、高單寧、酒體飽滿、黑莓","Pale colour, low tannin, light body, raspberry":"顏色淺、低單寧、酒體輕盈、覆盆子","Medium colour, low tannin, medium body, strawberry":"顏色中等、低單寧、酒體中等、草莓","Pale colour, low acidity, full body, banana":"顏色淺、低酸度、酒體飽滿、香蕉","Ripe Carmenère is dark, tannic and full, with medium to high acidity and fresh black fruit.":"成熟的卡門內爾顏色深、單寧多、酒體飽滿，酸度中等至高，帶有新鮮的黑色水果。","A typical Carmenère has deep colour, medium to high acidity, high tannins and full body; when ripe it smells of fresh black fruit such as blackberry. It is often oak-matured to soften the tannins. Pale, light, red-fruited profiles suggest Gamay or Grenache instead; banana and low acidity do not fit.":"典型的卡門內爾顏色深，酸度中等至高，單寧高，酒體飽滿；成熟時聞起來有黑莓等新鮮的黑色水果。它常經橡木桶熟成以柔化單寧。淺色、輕盈、帶紅色水果的風味特徵則讓人想到加美或格那希；香蕉和低酸度都不符合。","What does oak maturation bring to Carmenère?":"橡木桶熟成為卡門內爾帶來什麼？","Softer tannins and coffee and chocolate notes":"更柔和的單寧以及咖啡和巧克力氣息","More acidity and green pepper notes":"更多酸度和青椒氣息","Paler colour and banana notes":"更淺的顏色和香蕉氣息","Harder tannins and strawberry notes":"更硬的單寧和草莓氣息","Oak softens Carmenère's high tannins and adds coffee and chocolate.":"橡木桶柔化卡門內爾的高單寧，並增添咖啡和巧克力。","Carmenère has high tannins, so it is often matured in oak barrels: the wood softens them and adds flavours such as coffee and chocolate. Very good or outstanding examples then develop tertiary notes of leather and earth. Green pepper comes from underripe grapes, not from oak.":"卡門內爾的單寧很高，所以常在橡木桶中熟成：木頭讓單寧變柔和，並增添咖啡和巧克力等風味。非常好或傑出的酒款接著會發展出皮革和泥土的三級氣息。青椒來自未成熟的葡萄，不是來自橡木桶。","Which grapes is Carmenère most often blended with?":"卡門內爾最常與哪些品種混調？","Grenache and Syrah":"格那希和希哈","Tempranillo and Garnacha":"田帕尼優和 Garnacha","Pinot Noir and Gamay":"黑皮諾和加美","Carmenère can be single-varietal but is more often blended with Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot.":"卡門內爾可以是單一品種，但更常與卡本內蘇維濃和梅洛混調。","In Chile, Carmenère exists as a single-varietal wine, but it is more commonly blended with Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot, grapes that, like it, have Bordeaux connections. Grenache and Syrah are the classic southern French pairing, and Tempranillo and Garnacha the Rioja one.":"在智利，卡門內爾有單一品種的酒款，但更常與卡本內蘇維濃和梅洛混調，這些品種和它一樣與波爾多有淵源。格那希和希哈是法國南部的經典組合，田帕尼優和 Garnacha 則是 Rioja 的組合。","Malbec is the most important black grape of which country?":"馬爾貝克是哪個國家最重要的黑葡萄？","Malbec is Argentina's flagship black grape, grown mostly in Mendoza.":"馬爾貝克是阿根廷的旗艦黑葡萄，大多種在 Mendoza。","Each of the three regional specialities is tied to one country: Carmenère to Chile, Malbec to Argentina, Pinotage to South Africa. Malbec came from south-west France and adapted well to the warmer South American climate; most plantings are in the high-altitude region of Mendoza.":"三個地區特色品種各自與一個國家相連：卡門內爾與智利，馬爾貝克與阿根廷，皮諾塔吉與南非。馬爾貝克（Malbec）來自法國西南部，很能適應南美洲較溫暖的氣候；大部分的種植位於高海拔的 Mendoza 產區。","Where are most of Argentina's Malbec plantings?":"阿根廷大部分的馬爾貝克種在哪裡？","Mendoza, a high-altitude region":"Mendoza，高海拔產區","Central Valley, a coastal region":"Central Valley，沿海產區","Western Cape, a warm, dry region":"西開普，溫暖乾燥的產區","Barossa Valley, a lowland region":"Barossa Valley，低地產區","Malbec is grown across Argentina, but mostly in the high-altitude region of Mendoza.":"馬爾貝克種植於阿根廷各地，但大多在高海拔的 Mendoza 產區。","Mendoza is the key region for Malbec: most of the country's plantings are there, at high altitude. Labels often show Mendoza alongside Malbec and Wine of Argentina. The Central Valley is Carmenère's area in Chile, the Western Cape is Pinotage's, and Barossa Valley is in Australia.":"Mendoza 是馬爾貝克的關鍵產區：全國大部分的種植都在那裡，位於高海拔。酒標上常在 Malbec 和 Wine of Argentina 旁邊標示 Mendoza。Central Valley 是卡門內爾在智利的產區，西開普是皮諾塔吉的，而 Barossa Valley 在澳洲。","Which notes does new oak give a Malbec?":"新橡木桶為馬爾貝克帶來哪些氣息？","Clove and vanilla":"丁香和香草","Green pepper and tomato leaf":"青椒和番茄葉","Strawberry and white pepper":"草莓和白胡椒","New oak maturation softens Malbec and adds spice such as clove and vanilla.":"新橡木桶熟成讓馬爾貝克變柔和，並增添丁香和香草等香料。","Malbec gives dark, full-bodied, tannic wines with black fruit. New oak softens them and adds spicy notes of clove and vanilla; with bottle age, the best develop dried fruit and meat. Banana and candy are typical of some Beaujolais, and strawberry and white pepper of Grenache.":"馬爾貝克釀出顏色深、酒體飽滿、單寧多、帶黑色水果的酒。新橡木桶讓它們變柔和，並增添丁香和香草的香料氣息；經過瓶中陳年，最好的酒款會發展出果乾和肉味。香蕉和糖果是某些 Beaujolais 的典型特徵，草莓和白胡椒則是格那希的。","Which description matches a typical Malbec?":"哪一項描述符合典型的馬爾貝克？","Deep colour, full body, high tannin, black fruit":"顏色深、酒體飽滿、高單寧、黑色水果","Pale colour, light body, low tannin, red fruit":"顏色淺、酒體輕盈、低單寧、紅色水果","Medium colour, medium body, medium tannin, citrus":"顏色中等、酒體中等、中等單寧、柑橘","Pale colour, full body, low tannin, strawberry":"顏色淺、酒體飽滿、低單寧、草莓","Malbec gives dark, full-bodied wines with high tannins, blackberry and black plum.":"馬爾貝克釀出顏色深、酒體飽滿、單寧高、帶有黑莓和黑李的酒。","Argentine Malbec is typically deeply coloured, full-bodied and high in tannin, with black fruit such as blackberry and black plum. It is often single-varietal but also blended with Cabernet Sauvignon and/or Merlot. Pale, light profiles with red fruit describe Gamay instead; strawberry is typical of Grenache and Pinotage.":"阿根廷馬爾貝克通常顏色很深、酒體飽滿、單寧高，帶有黑莓和黑李等黑色水果。它常是單一品種，但也會與卡本內蘇維濃和／或梅洛混調。顏色淺、輕盈、帶紅色水果的風味特徵描述的則是加美；草莓是格那希和皮諾塔吉的典型特徵。","Where does Malbec originally come from?":"馬爾貝克原本來自哪裡？","North-east Spain":"西班牙東北部","Like Carmenère, Malbec comes from south-west France and has adapted well to South America.":"和卡門內爾一樣，馬爾貝克來自法國西南部，並很好地適應了南美洲。","Malbec, like Carmenère, is a French grape from the south-west of the country. In Argentina it found a warmer climate that suits it and became the country's most important black grape. Pinotage, by contrast, does not come from France: it was bred in South Africa for the local climate.":"馬爾貝克和卡門內爾一樣，是來自法國西南部的法國品種。在阿根廷，它找到了適合它的較溫暖氣候，成為這個國家最重要的黑葡萄。相反地，皮諾塔吉不是來自法國：它是在南非為了當地氣候而育成的。","Which grape is Pinotage closely related to?":"皮諾塔吉與哪個品種關係密切？","Pinotage is closely related to Pinot Noir and shares its red fruit.":"皮諾塔吉與黑皮諾關係密切，也有相同的紅色水果。","Pinotage was bred specially for South Africa and is closely related to Pinot Noir. That is why its wines show similar red fruit: strawberry, raspberry and red cherry. Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot are grapes it is often blended with, not close relatives.":"皮諾塔吉（Pinotage）是專門為南非育成的，與黑皮諾關係密切。這就是為什麼它的酒展現相似的紅色水果：草莓、覆盆子和紅櫻桃。卡本內蘇維濃和梅洛是常與它混調的品種，而不是近親。","Which structure is typical of Pinotage?":"哪一種結構是皮諾塔吉的典型特徵？","Medium tannins and high acidity":"中等單寧和高酸度","High tannins and low acidity":"高單寧和低酸度","Low tannins and low acidity":"低單寧和低酸度","High tannins and medium acidity":"高單寧和中等酸度","Pinotage wines usually have medium tannins and high acidity.":"皮諾塔吉的酒通常單寧中等、酸度高。","Pinotage gives wines with medium tannins and high acidity. Styles range from fruity, medium-bodied reds with strawberry and red cherry to powerful, full-bodied wines with concentrated red and black fruit. High tannins are more typical of Malbec and Carmenère, while low acidity is a Grenache trait.":"皮諾塔吉釀出單寧中等、酸度高的酒。風格從帶有草莓和紅櫻桃、果香豐富、酒體中等的紅酒，到帶有濃縮紅色和黑色水果、強勁飽滿的酒都有。高單寧更是馬爾貝克和卡門內爾的典型特徵，而低酸度是格那希的特性。","Which aromas can Pinotage take on from contact with oak?":"皮諾塔吉與橡木接觸可能帶上哪些香氣？","Coffee, chocolate and smoke":"咖啡、巧克力和煙燻","Banana, candy and raspberry":"香蕉、糖果和覆盆子","White pepper and liquorice":"白胡椒和甘草","With oak, Pinotage can show pronounced coffee, chocolate and smoke aromas.":"經過橡木桶，皮諾塔吉可能展現濃郁的咖啡、巧克力和煙燻香氣。","When matured in contact with oak, Pinotage can develop intense coffee, chocolate and smoke aromas on top of its red fruit and, in more powerful styles, black fruit. Green pepper signals underripe Carmenère; white pepper and liquorice are typical Grenache spices; banana and candy belong to some Beaujolais.":"與橡木接觸熟成時，皮諾塔吉在紅色水果（較強勁的風格還有黑色水果）之上，可能發展出濃烈的咖啡、巧克力和煙燻香氣。青椒表示未完全成熟的卡門內爾；白胡椒和甘草是格那希典型的香料；香蕉和糖果屬於某些 Beaujolais。","Which climate was Pinotage bred for?":"皮諾塔吉是為哪一種氣候育成的？","South Africa's warm, dry climate":"南非溫暖乾燥的氣候","Chile's cool, damp climate":"智利涼爽潮濕的氣候","Burgundy's moderate climate":"布根地溫和的氣候","Mendoza's high-altitude climate":"Mendoza 的高海拔氣候","Unlike Carmenère and Malbec, Pinotage was developed specially for South Africa's warm, dry climate.":"與卡門內爾和馬爾貝克不同，皮諾塔吉是專門為南非溫暖乾燥的氣候開發的。","Carmenère and Malbec are French grapes that found a new home in South America. Pinotage, however, was born in South Africa, bred specially for the country's warm, dry climate, and is grown throughout the Western Cape. Although related to Pinot Noir, it was not designed for Burgundy's moderate climate.":"卡門內爾和馬爾貝克是在南美洲找到新家的法國品種。皮諾塔吉則誕生於南非，專門為這個國家溫暖乾燥的氣候育成，種植於整個西開普。雖然它與黑皮諾有親緣關係，卻不是為布根地的溫和氣候而設計的。","Why are grapes like Carmenère, Malbec and Pinotage valuable to their countries?":"為什麼卡門內爾、馬爾貝克和皮諾塔吉這類品種對它們的國家很有價值？","They give a point of difference and an identity in a crowded market":"它們在競爭激烈的市場中提供差異點和獨特身分","They are the only grapes that grow in those countries":"它們是那些國家唯一能生長的品種","They always give the world's cheapest wines, fit only for big brands":"它們總是釀出世界上最便宜的酒，只適合大品牌","They need no sun to ripen":"它們不需要陽光就能成熟","These regional specialities set Chile, Argentina and South Africa apart and shape their wine identity.":"這些地區特色品種讓智利、阿根廷和南非與眾不同，塑造了它們的葡萄酒身分。","These countries also succeed with better-known grapes such as Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot, so these are not the only ones grown. Their specialities range from simple to outstanding wines. Carmenère in fact needs a long, sunny season.":"這些國家也成功種植卡本內蘇維濃和梅洛等較知名的品種，所以它們不是唯一種植的品種。它們的特色品種從簡單到傑出的酒款都有。卡門內爾其實需要漫長晴朗的生長季。","Which grape–country pairing is correct?":"下列哪一組品種與國家的配對是正確的？","Carmenère–Chile, Malbec–Argentina, Pinotage–South Africa":"卡門內爾–智利、馬爾貝克–阿根廷、皮諾塔吉–南非","Carmenère–Argentina, Malbec–South Africa, Pinotage–Chile":"卡門內爾–阿根廷、馬爾貝克–南非、皮諾塔吉–智利","Carmenère–South Africa, Malbec–Chile, Pinotage–Argentina":"卡門內爾–南非、馬爾貝克–智利、皮諾塔吉–阿根廷","Carmenère–Chile, Malbec–South Africa, Pinotage–Argentina":"卡門內爾–智利、馬爾貝克–南非、皮諾塔吉–阿根廷","Carmenère is Chile's speciality, Malbec Argentina's and Pinotage South Africa's.":"卡門內爾是智利的特色品種，馬爾貝克是阿根廷的，皮諾塔吉是南非的。","A memory aid: 'Pinotage' echoes Pinot Noir, its relative, and was born in South Africa; Malbec grows mostly in Mendoza; Carmenère ripens in the warmest sites of Chile's Central Valley.":"記憶小技巧：「皮諾塔吉」讓人想到它的親戚黑皮諾，誕生於南非；馬爾貝克大多種在 Mendoza；卡門內爾在智利 Central Valley 最溫暖的園地成熟。","Which statement about Carmenère in Bordeaux today is correct?":"關於今天波爾多的卡門內爾，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It is native there but rarely found there now":"它原生於那裡，但現在很少見","It is the region's most planted grape":"它是這個地區種植最多的品種","It recently arrived there from Chile, where it was born":"它最近才從它的發源地智利傳到那裡","It is banned by law in every appellation":"所有法定產區都依法禁止使用它","Carmenère is native to Bordeaux but is rare there now: its modern home is Chile.":"卡門內爾原生於波爾多，但現在在那裡很少見：它現代的家是智利。","It needs a long, sunny season to ripen, which it finds in the warmest Central Valley sites. Its origin is French, not Chilean. In Bordeaux the main grapes are others, such as Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot.":"它需要漫長晴朗的生長季才能成熟，而它在 Central Valley 最溫暖的園地找到了這樣的條件。它的起源是法國，不是智利。在波爾多，主要的品種是其他的，例如卡本內蘇維濃和梅洛。","How is Carmenère most commonly found in the bottle?":"卡門內爾在瓶中最常以什麼形式出現？","As part of a blend with other grapes":"作為與其他品種混調的一部分","Always single-varietal, as blends are banned":"一律是單一品種，因為混調被禁止","As a base for sparkling wines":"作為氣泡酒的基酒","As a sweet wine from grapes sun-dried after harvest":"作為用採收後曬乾的葡萄釀的甜酒","Carmenère exists as a single-varietal wine but is more often part of a blend.":"卡門內爾有單一品種的酒款，但更常是混調的一部分。","Its usual partners are Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot; in Chile Cabernet is also blended with this local speciality. Carmenère makes dry, full-bodied, tannic reds, not sparkling or sweet wines.":"它常見的搭檔是卡本內蘇維濃和梅洛；在智利，卡本內也會與這個在地特色品種混調。卡門內爾釀出不甜、酒體飽滿、單寧多的紅酒，而不是氣泡酒或甜酒。","Which tertiary flavours can the best Carmenères develop?":"最好的卡門內爾能發展出哪些三級風味？","Green pepper and tomato leaf, from grapes picked too early":"青椒和番茄葉，來自太早採收的葡萄","Very good or outstanding Carmenère can develop leather and earth notes in bottle.":"非常好或傑出的卡門內爾在瓶中能發展出皮革和泥土氣息。","Green pepper is a primary aroma linked to underripe grapes, not an effect of ageing. Strawberry and raspberry are primary red-fruit aromas; banana and candy come from Beaujolais winemaking techniques.":"青椒是與未成熟葡萄相關的一級香氣，不是陳年的效果。草莓和覆盆子是一級的紅色水果香氣；香蕉和糖果來自 Beaujolais 的釀造技術。","Which flavours can the best Malbecs develop in the bottle?":"最好的馬爾貝克在瓶中能發展出哪些風味？","Dried fruit and meat":"果乾和肉","Fresh strawberry and candy":"新鮮草莓和糖果","Grapefruit, gooseberry and white flowers":"葡萄柚、醋栗和白花","With age, very good or outstanding Malbecs develop dried-fruit and meat notes.":"隨著陳年，非常好或傑出的馬爾貝克會發展出果乾和肉味。","When young, Malbec shows blackberry and black plum, plus clove and vanilla from new oak. The other options are primary aromas of whites or light, fruity reds, not tertiary notes.":"年輕時，馬爾貝克展現黑莓和黑李，加上來自新橡木桶的丁香和香草。其他選項是白酒或輕盈果香紅酒的一級香氣，不是三級氣息。","What do Carmenère and Malbec have in common?":"卡門內爾和馬爾貝克有什麼共同點？","Both are French in origin and now shine in South America":"兩者都起源於法國，現在在南美洲大放異彩","Both were bred in South Africa for its warm, dry climate":"兩者都是在南非為了溫暖乾燥的氣候育成的","Both give light, low-tannin wines":"兩者都釀出輕盈、低單寧的酒","Both are aromatic white grapes, grown mainly in northern Italy":"兩者都是主要種在北義的芳香型白葡萄","Both come from south-west France and found success in Chile and Argentina.":"兩者都來自法國西南部，並在智利和阿根廷獲得成功。","Carmenère comes from Bordeaux, Malbec from France's south-west, and both have adapted well to South America's warmer climate. The grape bred in South Africa is Pinotage. Both give dark, full-bodied, tannic reds.":"卡門內爾來自波爾多，馬爾貝克來自法國西南部，兩者都很好地適應了南美洲較溫暖的氣候。在南非育成的品種是皮諾塔吉。兩者都釀出顏色深、酒體飽滿、單寧多的紅酒。","Which statement about how Malbec is found in the bottle is correct?":"關於馬爾貝克在瓶中的形式，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It is often single-varietal, but also blended with Cabernet Sauvignon and/or Merlot":"它常是單一品種，但也會與卡本內蘇維濃和／或梅洛混調","It is always blended; Argentine law bans single-varietal Malbec":"它一律是混調；阿根廷法律禁止單一品種的馬爾貝克","It is mostly blended with white grapes":"它大多與白葡萄混調","Malbec is often seen on its own but is also commonly blended with Cabernet Sauvignon and/or Merlot.":"馬爾貝克常單獨出現，但也常與卡本內蘇維濃和／或梅洛混調。","No law requires or bans blending: it is the producer's choice. Malbec wines are dark, full-bodied, tannic reds, not rosés, and its usual partners are black grapes.":"沒有法律要求或禁止混調：這是生產者的選擇。馬爾貝克是顏色深、酒體飽滿、單寧多的紅酒，不是粉紅酒，它常見的搭檔是黑葡萄。","Which of these grapes is NOT French in origin?":"下列哪一個品種不是起源於法國？","Gamay, the grape of Beaujolais":"加美，Beaujolais 的品種","Pinotage was developed in South Africa, while the others come from France.":"皮諾塔吉是在南非開發的，其他品種則來自法國。","Pinotage was created specially for South Africa's warm, dry climate and is a close relative of Pinot Noir. Carmenère (Bordeaux), Malbec (south-west) and Gamay (Beaujolais) are all French.":"皮諾塔吉是專門為南非溫暖乾燥的氣候創造的，是黑皮諾的近親。卡門內爾（波爾多）、馬爾貝克（西南部）和加美（Beaujolais）都是法國品種。","Which red fruits does Pinotage share with Pinot Noir?":"皮諾塔吉與黑皮諾共有哪些紅色水果？","Lemon, grapefruit, lime":"檸檬、葡萄柚、萊姆","Like Pinot Noir, Pinotage shows red fruit such as strawberry, raspberry and red cherry.":"和黑皮諾一樣，皮諾塔吉展現草莓、覆盆子和紅櫻桃等紅色水果。","The most powerful Pinotages also add red plum and blackberry, but red fruit is the trait shared with Pinot Noir. Citrus is a white-wine aroma, and dried fruit is typical of Amarone.":"最強勁的皮諾塔吉還會增添紅李和黑莓，但紅色水果才是與黑皮諾共有的特徵。柑橘是白酒的香氣，而果乾是 Amarone 的典型特徵。","What range of styles does Pinotage produce?":"皮諾塔吉能釀出什麼樣的風格範圍？","From fruity, medium-bodied reds to powerful, full-bodied reds":"從果香豐富、酒體中等的紅酒，到強勁、酒體飽滿的紅酒","Only sweet dessert wines":"只有甜型甜點酒","Only very light reds to drink chilled":"只有要冰鎮飲用的非常輕盈紅酒","Only traditional-method sparkling wines with long lees ageing":"只有長時間酒渣陳年的傳統法氣泡酒","Pinotage ranges from fruity, medium-bodied wines to powerful, full-bodied examples with concentrated red and black fruit.":"皮諾塔吉的範圍從果香豐富、酒體中等的酒，到帶有濃縮紅色和黑色水果的強勁飽滿酒款。","The lighter ones show strawberry and red cherry; the most powerful red plum and blackberry. With oak it can take on coffee, chocolate and smoke. It is not a dessert-wine or sparkling grape in this context.":"較輕盈的酒款展現草莓和紅櫻桃；最強勁的則有紅李和黑莓。經過橡木桶，它可能帶上咖啡、巧克力和煙燻。在這裡，它不是甜點酒或氣泡酒的品種。","Where is Pinotage grown in South Africa?":"皮諾塔吉在南非種在哪裡？","Throughout the Western Cape":"整個西開普","Only in one small vineyard near Johannesburg":"只在約翰尼斯堡附近的一座小葡萄園","Only in the coolest coastal areas, next to Pinot Noir":"只在最涼爽的沿海地區，與黑皮諾相鄰","In Mendoza":"在 Mendoza","Pinotage is grown throughout the Western Cape.":"皮諾塔吉種植於整個西開普。","South African labels often show 'Western Cape' or one of its areas, such as Stellenbosch. It is Pinot Noir that is focused on the coolest coastal areas; Pinotage was bred for warmth. Mendoza is in Argentina, Malbec's home.":"南非酒標上常標示「Western Cape」或它的某個地區，例如 Stellenbosch。集中在最涼爽沿海地區的是黑皮諾；皮諾塔吉是為溫暖而育成的。Mendoza 在阿根廷，是馬爾貝克的故鄉。","How do Zinfandel's flavours change as it ripens on the vine?":"金芬黛在樹上成熟時，風味如何變化？","From strawberry and raspberry to black plum, blackberry and blueberry":"從草莓和覆盆子到黑李、黑莓和藍莓","From blackberry and blueberry to strawberry and raspberry":"從黑莓和藍莓到草莓和覆盆子","From lemon and green apple to peach and apricot, then tropical fruit":"從檸檬和青蘋果到桃子和杏桃，再到熱帶水果","From green pepper to tomato leaf":"從青椒到番茄葉","As it ripens, Zinfandel moves from red fruit to black fruit.":"隨著成熟，金芬黛從紅色水果轉向黑色水果。","First strawberry and raspberry, then black plum, blackberry and blueberry. Some berries may also raisin before the others ripen, adding prune and raisin. Green pepper notes belong to underripe Carmenère.":"先是草莓和覆盆子，接著是黑李、黑莓和藍莓。有些果粒也可能在其他果粒成熟前乾縮，增添黑李乾和葡萄乾。青椒氣息屬於未完全成熟的卡門內爾。","Which technique is usually used to make White Zinfandel?":"釀造 White Zinfandel 通常使用哪一種技術？","A short skin maceration, as for rosé":"短時間浸皮，就像釀粉紅酒","White winemaking of white grapes with no skin contact at all":"用白葡萄以白酒方式釀造，完全不接觸果皮","Drying the grapes indoors":"在室內風乾葡萄","Long maceration and long ageing in new barrels":"長時間浸皮並在新橡木桶中長時間陳年","White Zinfandel is a rosé, usually made with a short skin maceration.":"White Zinfandel 是粉紅酒，通常以短時間浸皮釀造。","Despite its name, it is not a white wine: it is pink, from a black grape. Brief skin contact gives colour without much tannin. The yeasts are then removed before fermentation ends to keep sweetness. Long macerations and oak belong to red Zinfandel.":"儘管名字如此，它不是白酒：它是用黑葡萄釀的粉紅酒。短暫的果皮接觸帶來顏色，卻沒有太多單寧。接著在發酵結束前去除酵母以保留甜味。長時間浸皮和橡木桶屬於金芬黛紅酒。","A Sonoma label reads 'Old Vine Zinfandel, 15.5% vol'. What should you expect?":"一張 Sonoma 的酒標上寫著「Old Vine Zinfandel, 15.5% vol」。你應該預期什麼？","A dry, full-bodied red from low-yielding old vines":"來自低產量老藤、不甜且酒體飽滿的紅酒","A light, sweet rosé of about 9%":"約 9% 的輕盈甜型粉紅酒","A light, dry, unoaked white to drink very young":"要非常年輕時喝的輕盈、不甜、不經橡木桶的白酒","A sweet fortified wine":"甜型加烈酒","High alcohol points to a dry, full-bodied red Zinfandel; 'Old Vine' suggests old vines and concentrated fruit.":"高酒精指向不甜、酒體飽滿的金芬黛紅酒；「Old Vine」暗示老藤和濃縮的果實。","Zinfandel rosés usually have low alcohol (8–10%), reds high. Old vines give few, very concentrated grapes, and such wines can develop earth and meat notes. Note: 'Old Vine' is not a legally defined term.":"金芬黛粉紅酒的酒精通常很低（8–10%），紅酒則很高。老藤產出少量非常濃縮的葡萄，這樣的酒能發展出泥土和肉味。注意：「Old Vine」不是法律定義的術語。","How is red Zinfandel made in California?":"加州的金芬黛紅酒是怎麼釀造的？","Full fermentation with the juice kept on the skins throughout":"完全發酵，果汁全程與果皮接觸","Fermentation stopped halfway by removing the yeasts":"在發酵中途去除酵母以中止發酵","A few hours' maceration, then fermentation without skins":"浸皮幾個小時，然後不帶果皮發酵","With grapes dried indoors for some months":"使用在室內風乾數個月的葡萄","Red Zinfandel follows red winemaking: a complete fermentation with the juice on the skins.":"金芬黛紅酒遵循紅酒的釀法：果汁帶皮完全發酵。","Long skin contact extracts colour and tannin, and full fermentation gives a dry, high-alcohol wine. The other techniques (stopped fermentation, short maceration) are for White Zinfandel; appassimento is typical of the Veneto.":"長時間的果皮接觸萃取顏色和單寧，完全發酵則帶來不甜、酒精高的酒。其他技術（中止發酵、短時間浸皮）用於 White Zinfandel；appassimento 是威尼托的典型做法。","Why is red Zinfandel often matured in oak?":"為什麼金芬黛紅酒常在橡木桶中熟成？","To soften the tannins and add complexity":"柔化單寧並增添複雜度","To lower its alcohol":"降低酒精","To make it sweet and pinker, like a White Zinfandel":"讓它變甜、更粉紅，像 White Zinfandel 一樣","To raise the acidity":"提高酸度","Oak softens red Zinfandel's tannins and adds flavours such as vanilla and coffee.":"橡木桶柔化金芬黛紅酒的單寧，並增添香草和咖啡等風味。","Red Zinfandel has medium to high acidity and tannin, high alcohol and full body. Oak does not change alcohol, add sugar or raise acidity. White Zinfandel is a different wine made a different way.":"金芬黛紅酒的酸度和單寧中等至高，酒精高，酒體飽滿。橡木桶不會改變酒精、增加糖分或提高酸度。White Zinfandel 是用不同方式釀造的另一種酒。","What do California's very old Zinfandel vines produce?":"加州非常古老的金芬黛葡萄樹產出什麼？","Small quantities of very concentrated fruit":"少量非常濃縮的果實","Large amounts of dilute fruit for bulk wine":"大量被稀釋、用於散裝酒的果實","Only grapes for White Zinfandel":"只有用於 White Zinfandel 的葡萄","Very acidic, low-sugar grapes that never fully ripen":"非常酸、糖分低、永遠無法完全成熟的葡萄","Old vines give small crops of very concentrated fruit.":"老藤產出小量但非常濃縮的果實。","This fruit makes wines that can develop tertiary earth and meat notes in bottle. Low yields are the opposite of large bulk volumes. Zinfandel needs warmth and ripens well in California.":"這樣的果實釀出的酒能在瓶中發展出泥土和肉的三級氣息。低產量與大量的散裝產量正好相反。金芬黛需要熱量，在加州成熟良好。","A customer wants a pink, medium-sweet, light, low-alcohol wine that smells of strawberry. What do you suggest?":"一位顧客想要一款粉紅色、半甜、輕盈、低酒精、聞起來有草莓香的酒。你會推薦什麼？","A Californian White Zinfandel":"加州的 White Zinfandel","A Côtes de Provence AOC":"Côtes de Provence AOC","A full-bodied, heavily oaked, high-alcohol Old Vine Zinfandel":"酒體飽滿、橡木味重、酒精高的 Old Vine Zinfandel","A Western Cape Pinotage":"西開普的皮諾塔吉","White Zinfandel is pink, medium-sweet, 8–10% alcohol, with simple strawberry and raspberry aromas.":"White Zinfandel 是粉紅色、半甜、酒精 8–10%，帶有簡單的草莓和覆盆子香氣。","Côtes de Provence is also rosé, but dry and pale. Old Vine Zinfandel is a dry, powerful red. Pinotage is a dry red with high acidity.":"Côtes de Provence 也是粉紅酒，但不甜且顏色淺。Old Vine Zinfandel 是不甜、強勁的紅酒。皮諾塔吉是高酸度的不甜紅酒。","Which of these grapes usually has the lowest tannin?":"下列哪一個品種的單寧通常最低？","Fully ripe Carmenère":"完全成熟的卡門內爾","Montepulciano from Abruzzo, with its very deep colour":"來自阿布魯佐、顏色非常深的蒙鐵布奇亞諾","Pinotage has medium tannin; Malbec, Carmenère and Montepulciano are high in tannin.":"皮諾塔吉的單寧中等；馬爾貝克、卡門內爾和蒙鐵布奇亞諾的單寧都很高。","Pinotage, a relative of Pinot Noir, combines medium tannin with high acidity. Malbec and Carmenère make dark, full-bodied, very tannic wines, often softened in oak. Montepulciano also has high tannin and deep colour.":"黑皮諾的親戚皮諾塔吉結合了中等的單寧和高酸度。馬爾貝克和卡門內爾釀出顏色深、酒體飽滿、單寧非常多的酒，常經橡木桶柔化。蒙鐵布奇亞諾也有高單寧和深色。","Why can Chenin Blanc make wines from dry to sweet?":"為什麼白梢楠能釀出從不甜到甜的酒？","High acidity and susceptibility to botrytis":"高酸度且容易感染貴腐菌","Low acidity and fast ripening":"低酸度且成熟快速","Neutral aromas and light body":"香氣中性且酒體輕盈","High acidity allows late harvesting, and botrytis concentrates sugars for sweet styles.":"高酸度讓晚收成為可能，而貴腐菌為甜型風格濃縮糖分。","Chenin Blanc has high natural acidity, which suits late harvesting, and it is susceptible to noble rot. These two traits allow a very wide range of styles: dry, off-dry, medium, sweet and even sparkling, as in Vouvray. The acidity also helps the best wines age for many years.":"白梢楠（Chenin Blanc）有高天然酸度，適合晚收，而且容易感染貴腐菌。這兩個特性造就了非常廣泛的風格：不甜、微甜、半甜、甜，甚至氣泡酒，例如 Vouvray。酸度也幫助最好的酒款陳年多年。","Which grape is the only one permitted in Vouvray AOC?":"哪一個品種是 Vouvray AOC 唯一允許的品種？","Vouvray, in the Loire, is a classic region where only Chenin Blanc is allowed.":"羅亞爾河的 Vouvray 是只允許白梢楠的經典產區。","Vouvray AOC, in the Loire Valley, is one of the classic homes of Chenin Blanc, the only grape permitted. Even with a single grape, very different styles are made: dry, Demi-Sec, sweet and sparkling. Sauvignon Blanc and Sémillon are the typical grapes of white Bordeaux, while Chardonnay is Burgundy's great white grape.":"羅亞爾河谷的 Vouvray AOC 是白梢楠的經典產區之一，也是唯一允許的品種。即使只有一個品種，也釀出非常不同的風格：不甜、Demi-Sec、甜和氣泡酒。白蘇維濃和榭密雍是波爾多白酒的典型品種，而夏多內是布根地偉大的白葡萄。","What does Demi-Sec indicate on a Vouvray label?":"Vouvray 酒標上的 Demi-Sec 代表什麼？","An off-dry or medium style":"微甜或半甜的風格","A very sweet botrytised wine":"非常甜的貴腐酒","A wine aged in new oak":"在新橡木桶中陳年的酒","Demi-Sec marks off-dry or medium Vouvray.":"Demi-Sec 標示微甜或半甜的 Vouvray。","In Vouvray, Chenin Blanc gives many styles. Dry wines often taste of fresh apple; off-dry and medium styles are labelled Demi-Sec; the sweetest come from extra-ripe or botrytised grapes and show stone or tropical fruit. Generally none of these wines is oaked, to keep the fruit fresh.":"在 Vouvray，白梢楠釀出許多風格。不甜的酒常帶有新鮮蘋果的味道；微甜和半甜的風格標示為 Demi-Sec；最甜的來自過熟或貴腐的葡萄，展現核果或熱帶水果。一般來說，這些酒都不經橡木桶，以保持果味新鮮。","Why is Vouvray usually unoaked?":"為什麼 Vouvray 通常不經橡木桶？","To keep its fresh fruit character":"為了保持新鮮的果味特徵","Because oak is banned across the Loire":"因為整個羅亞爾河都禁止使用橡木桶","To encourage botrytis in the winery":"為了在酒廠中促進貴腐菌","Without oak, Vouvray keeps Chenin Blanc's typical fresh fruit.":"不經橡木桶，Vouvray 保留了白梢楠典型的新鮮果味。","Whatever the style, dry, Demi-Sec or sweet, Vouvray is usually made without oak. The aim is to preserve Chenin Blanc's fresh fruit, from the apple of dry wines to the stone and tropical fruit of sweet styles. With bottle age, the best still gain complexity, with notes of honey and dried fruit.":"無論是不甜、Demi-Sec 或甜的風格，Vouvray 通常都不使用橡木桶釀造。目的是保留白梢楠的新鮮果味，從不甜酒款的蘋果到甜型風格的核果和熱帶水果。經過瓶中陳年，最好的酒款仍會增添複雜度，帶有蜂蜜和果乾氣息。","Why is Chenin Blanc so valued in South Africa?":"為什麼白梢楠在南非如此受到重視？","It keeps high acidity even in a warm climate":"即使在溫暖氣候中也能保持高酸度","It only ripens in the coldest areas":"它只在最寒冷的地區成熟","It is naturally low in acidity":"它天生酸度低","It always gives botrytised sweet wines":"它總是釀出貴腐甜酒","Chenin Blanc holds its acidity in the heat, a valuable trait in South Africa.":"白梢楠在高溫中也能保持酸度，這在南非是很寶貴的特性。","Chenin Blanc is South Africa's most planted white grape. It is valued above all because it keeps high acidity even in a warm climate, giving fresh wines. Quality ranges from inexpensive high-volume brands, often Western Cape, to very good and outstanding old-vine wines with pronounced tropical fruit and oak notes.":"白梢楠是南非種植最多的白葡萄。它受重視主要是因為即使在溫暖氣候中也能保持高酸度，釀出清爽的酒。品質從常標示 Western Cape 的平價大量生產品牌，到帶有濃郁熱帶水果和橡木氣息、非常好和傑出的老藤酒款都有。","Which description fits an inexpensive Chenin Blanc labelled Western Cape?":"哪一項描述符合標示 Western Cape 的平價白梢楠？","Dry, medium body, peach, pineapple, sometimes vanilla":"不甜、酒體中等、桃子、鳳梨，有時帶香草","Sweet, amber, caramel and nuts":"甜、琥珀色、焦糖和堅果","Light, neutral, low alcohol, for ageing":"輕盈、中性、低酒精，適合陳年","Sparkling, dry, yeasty notes":"氣泡、不甜、帶酵母氣息","These warm-inland wines are dry and medium-bodied with peach, pineapple and sometimes vanilla.":"這些來自溫暖內陸的酒不甜、酒體中等，帶有桃子、鳳梨，有時還有香草。","Inexpensive high-volume Chenin Blanc, often labelled Western Cape, uses grapes from South Africa's warmer inland areas and is often blended with other grapes such as Chardonnay. It is dry and medium-bodied, with peach and pineapple and sometimes vanilla from oak chips or staves. The light, neutral style built for ageing is typical of Hunter Valley.":"平價的大量生產白梢楠常標示 Western Cape，使用來自南非較溫暖內陸地區的葡萄，常與夏多內等其他品種混調。它不甜、酒體中等，帶有桃子和鳳梨，有時還有來自橡木片或橡木條的香草。輕盈、中性、適合陳年的風格則是 Hunter Valley 的典型特徵。","What does Sémillon bring to Bordeaux blends with Sauvignon Blanc?":"在與白蘇維濃的波爾多混調中，榭密雍帶來什麼？","Body and ageing potential":"酒體和陳年潛力","Grassy notes and low alcohol":"青草氣息和低酒精","In Bordeaux blends, Sémillon adds body and helps the wines age.":"在波爾多混調中，榭密雍增添酒體並幫助酒陳年。","Bordeaux is the most important region for Sémillon in France. There it is often blended with Sauvignon Blanc for both dry and sweet wines. Sémillon contributes body and ageing potential; the best wines are often oak-matured and can develop for many years in bottle. As a white grape, it adds no tannin or colour.":"波爾多是法國最重要的榭密雍產區。在那裡它常與白蘇維濃混調，釀造不甜和甜型的酒。榭密雍（Sémillon）帶來酒體和陳年潛力；最好的酒款常經橡木桶熟成，能在瓶中發展多年。作為白葡萄，它不會增添單寧或顏色。","Why is Sémillon the most important grape in Sauternes?":"為什麼榭密雍是 Sauternes 最重要的品種？","It is particularly susceptible to botrytis":"它特別容易感染貴腐菌","It is fully resistant to rot":"它完全不會腐爛","It ripens very early with little sugar":"它很早成熟，糖分很少","It has black, tannic skins":"它的果皮是黑色的，帶有單寧","Sauternes is made from botrytised grapes, and Sémillon is highly prone to botrytis.":"Sauternes 是用貴腐葡萄釀造的，而榭密雍非常容易感染貴腐菌。","Sauternes is a sweet white wine from Bordeaux made from grapes concentrated by noble rot. Sémillon is particularly susceptible to botrytis, which makes it ideal for this style and the area's main grape. The wine is sweet and full-bodied, with high acidity, apricot aromas and oak notes, and it develops dried fruit, honey and caramel with age.":"Sauternes 是用貴腐濃縮的葡萄釀造的波爾多甜白酒。榭密雍特別容易感染貴腐菌，非常適合這種風格，也是這個地區的主要品種。這款酒甜而酒體飽滿，酸度高，帶有杏桃香氣和橡木氣息，陳年後會發展出果乾、蜂蜜和焦糖。","Why is Hunter Valley Semillon light and low in alcohol despite the warm climate?":"儘管氣候溫暖，為什麼 Hunter Valley 的榭密雍輕盈且酒精低？","Grapes are picked early, low in sugar and high in acid":"葡萄提早採收，糖分低、酸度高","Fermentation is stopped with Süssreserve":"以 Süssreserve 中止發酵","The wine is diluted with water":"酒被加水稀釋","The grapes are frozen on the vine":"葡萄在樹上結冰","Early picking gives low-sugar, acidic grapes: a light, dry, low-alcohol wine.":"提早採收帶來低糖、高酸的葡萄：輕盈、不甜、低酒精的酒。","In the warm Hunter Valley, Semillon is picked early, while sugar is still low and acidity high. Fermented dry in inert vessels and bottled young, it gives a light, low-alcohol wine that is fairly neutral at first. After several years in bottle, however, it develops pronounced, complex aromas of honey and nuts.":"在溫暖的 Hunter Valley，榭密雍在糖分仍低、酸度仍高時提早採收。在惰性容器中發酵至不甜並趁年輕裝瓶，它釀出輕盈、低酒精、起初相當中性的酒。不過，在瓶中多年後，它會發展出濃郁、複雜的蜂蜜和堅果香氣。","Which characteristics make Furmint ideal for sweet wines?":"哪些特性讓弗明非常適合釀造甜酒？","High acidity and strong susceptibility to botrytis":"高酸度且非常容易感染貴腐菌","Low acidity and very thick skins":"低酸度且果皮非常厚","Neutral aromas and early ripening":"香氣中性且早熟","Rot resistance and high tannins":"抗腐爛且單寧高","Furmint combines high acidity with strong botrytis susceptibility, perfect for sweet wines.":"弗明結合了高酸度和極易感染貴腐菌的特性，非常適合甜酒。","Furmint is a white grape grown mainly in Hungary. Its high natural acidity balances sweetness, while its strong susceptibility to botrytis lets sugars concentrate in the grapes. It is the most planted grape in Tokaj and the backbone of Tokaji Aszú, one of the world's most famous and complex sweet wines.":"弗明（Furmint）是主要種植於匈牙利的白葡萄。它的高天然酸度能平衡甜度，而極易感染貴腐菌的特性讓糖分在葡萄中濃縮。它是 Tokaj 種植最多的品種，也是 Tokaji Aszú 的骨幹，Tokaji Aszú 是世界上最著名、最複雜的甜酒之一。","What does the number of Puttonyos on a Tokaji Aszú label indicate?":"Tokaji Aszú 酒標上的 Puttonyos 數字代表什麼？","The sweetness level: 6 is sweeter than 5":"甜度：6 比 5 更甜","The years spent ageing in oak":"在橡木桶中陳年的年數","The percentage of Furmint in the wine":"酒中弗明的比例","The alcohol level of the wine":"酒的酒精濃度","Puttonyos show sweetness: a 6 Puttonyos is sweeter than a 5 Puttonyos.":"Puttonyos 顯示甜度：6 Puttonyos 比 5 Puttonyos 更甜。","Tokaji Aszú is always sweet, but how sweet can vary. A good guide is the number of Puttonyos on the label. Most wines are labelled 5 Puttonyos or 6 Puttonyos, and the higher the number, the sweeter the wine, so 6 Puttonyos has more sweetness than 5.":"Tokaji Aszú 一定是甜的，但甜的程度可能不同。酒標上的 Puttonyos 數字是很好的指引。大多數酒款標示 5 Puttonyos 或 6 Puttonyos，數字越高酒越甜，所以 6 Puttonyos 比 5 更甜。","Why is Tokaji Aszú amber in colour?":"為什麼 Tokaji Aszú 是琥珀色的？","Because it ages for a long time in oak":"因為它在橡木桶中長時間陳年","Because it is made from black grapes":"因為它是用黑葡萄釀的","Because the grapes freeze on the vine":"因為葡萄在樹上結冰","Because unfermented juice is added":"因為加入了未發酵的葡萄汁","Long traditional oak ageing gives Tokaji Aszú its amber colour.":"傳統上在橡木桶中長時間陳年，讓 Tokaji Aszú 呈現琥珀色。","Tokaji Aszú traditionally spends a long time in oak, and this ageing gives it an amber colour. On the nose it combines primary, secondary and tertiary aromas: fresh and dried apricot, citrus, vanilla and smoke from oak, plus dried fruit, caramel and nuts. Its sweetness and full body are balanced by high acidity.":"Tokaji Aszú 傳統上在橡木桶中待很長時間，這樣的陳年讓它呈現琥珀色。香氣上它結合了一級、二級和三級香氣：新鮮和乾燥的杏桃、柑橘，來自橡木的香草和煙燻，以及果乾、焦糖和堅果。它的甜度和飽滿的酒體由高酸度平衡。","Why does a dry Gewurztraminer often have high alcohol?":"為什麼不甜的格烏茲塔明那常常酒精很高？","The grapes build up high sugar levels":"葡萄累積了很高的糖分","It is fortified with spirit":"它以烈酒加烈","It is aged long in new oak":"它在新橡木桶中長時間陳年","It grows only in very hot climates":"它只生長在非常炎熱的氣候中","Lots of sugar fermented to dryness becomes lots of alcohol.":"大量的糖發酵至不甜，就變成大量的酒精。","Gewurztraminer builds up high sugar levels during ripening. When the juice is fermented to dryness, all that sugar becomes alcohol, so the wine is high in alcohol and full-bodied. The grape prefers cool to moderate climates and is usually unoaked.":"格烏茲塔明那（Gewurztraminer）在成熟過程中累積很高的糖分。當果汁發酵至不甜時，所有的糖都變成酒精，所以酒精高、酒體飽滿。這個品種偏好涼爽至溫和的氣候，通常不經橡木桶。","Which aroma combination typically points to Gewurztraminer?":"哪一組香氣通常指向格烏茲塔明那？","Rose, lychee, peach and apricot":"玫瑰、荔枝、桃子和杏桃","Grass, asparagus and grapefruit":"青草、蘆筍和葡萄柚","Butter, vanilla and pineapple":"奶油、香草和鳳梨","Rose and lychee, with peach and apricot, are Gewurztraminer's signature.":"玫瑰和荔枝，加上桃子和杏桃，是格烏茲塔明那的招牌特徵。","Gewurztraminer shows pronounced floral rose, stone fruit such as peach and apricot, and tropical lychee. Grass, asparagus and grapefruit indicate Sauvignon Blanc; apple, lemon and wet stones a cool-climate Chardonnay; butter, vanilla and pineapple an oaked warm-climate Chardonnay. These are very intense, easy-to-recognise aromas.":"格烏茲塔明那展現濃郁的玫瑰花香、桃子和杏桃等核果，以及熱帶水果荔枝。青草、蘆筍和葡萄柚表示白蘇維濃；蘋果、檸檬和濕石頭表示涼爽氣候的夏多內；奶油、香草和鳳梨表示經橡木桶的溫暖氣候夏多內。這些是非常濃烈、容易辨識的香氣。","What acidity level does Gewurztraminer usually have?":"格烏茲塔明那通常有什麼程度的酸度？","Low to medium":"低至中等","High":"高","Very high":"非常高","It is a full, alcoholic white with low to medium acidity.":"它是酒體飽滿、酒精高、酸度低至中等的白酒。","Typical Gewurztraminer is full-bodied with high alcohol and low to medium acidity. That sets it apart from crisp whites such as Albariño or Sauvignon Blanc, which have high acidity. Its aromatic richness and body make up for the more modest freshness.":"典型的格烏茲塔明那酒體飽滿、酒精高、酸度低至中等。這讓它與阿爾巴利諾或白蘇維濃等高酸度的爽脆白酒區隔開來。它豐富的香氣和酒體彌補了較不突出的清新感。","What is the most famous region for Gewurztraminer?":"格烏茲塔明那最著名的產區是哪裡？","Alsace (Alsace AOC)":"阿爾薩斯（Alsace AOC）","In Alsace it makes some of the top grand crus, with Riesling and Pinot Gris.":"在阿爾薩斯，它與麗絲玲和灰皮諾一起釀出一些頂級的 grand cru。","The most famous region for Gewurztraminer is Alsace in France. There it makes some of the highest-quality grand cru wines alongside Riesling and Pinot Gris, and can also be labelled Vendanges tardives. Condrieu is dedicated to Viognier, Rías Baixas to Albariño, and the Loire is known for Sauvignon Blanc.":"格烏茲塔明那最著名的產區是法國的阿爾薩斯。在那裡它與麗絲玲和灰皮諾一起釀出一些品質最高的 grand cru 酒款，也可以標示 Vendanges tardives。Condrieu 專門釀造維歐尼耶，Rías Baixas 專門釀造阿爾巴利諾，而羅亞爾河以白蘇維濃著稱。","Which flavours do very good or outstanding Gewurztraminers develop in bottle?":"非常好或傑出的格烏茲塔明那在瓶中會發展出哪些風味？","With ageing they evolve towards honey and dried fruit.":"隨著陳年，它們會朝蜂蜜和果乾演變。","The best Gewurztraminers can age in bottle, developing honey and dried fruit. Grass and green pepper are primary aromas of Sauvignon Blanc; butter and cream come from malolactic conversion; smoke and coconut from oak, which is avoided for Gewurztraminer to protect its floral aromas.":"最好的格烏茲塔明那能在瓶中陳年，發展出蜂蜜和果乾。青草和青椒是白蘇維濃的一級香氣；奶油和鮮奶油來自乳酸轉化；煙燻和椰子來自橡木桶，而釀造格烏茲塔明那時會避免使用橡木桶，以保護它的花香。","Which profile best describes a typical Viognier?":"哪一種風味特徵最能描述典型的維歐尼耶？","Dry, high alcohol, blossom, peach, apricot":"不甜、酒精高、花香、桃子、杏桃","Dry, high acidity, lemon, grapefruit":"不甜、高酸度、檸檬、葡萄柚","Light, high acidity, pear, lemon":"輕盈、高酸度、梨、檸檬","Light, grass, green pepper, asparagus":"輕盈、青草、青椒、蘆筍","Viognier is dry, alcoholic, medium-full, floral and stone-fruited.":"維歐尼耶不甜、酒精高、酒體中等至飽滿，帶花香和核果。","Typical Viognier is dry with low to medium acidity, high alcohol and medium to full body, with pronounced blossom and stone fruit such as peach and apricot. Lemon and grapefruit with high acidity point to Albariño; light pear and lemon to Pinot Grigio; grass and asparagus to Sauvignon Blanc.":"典型的維歐尼耶（Viognier）不甜，酸度低至中等，酒精高，酒體中等至飽滿，帶有濃郁的花香和桃子、杏桃等核果。檸檬和葡萄柚加上高酸度指向阿爾巴利諾；輕盈的梨和檸檬指向 Pinot Grigio；青草和蘆筍指向白蘇維濃。","What is unusual about how some Viogniers are made?":"有些維歐尼耶的釀造方式有什麼不尋常之處？","They are oak-aged, rare for an aromatic grape":"它們經過橡木桶陳年，這對芳香型品種來說很少見","They are fortified with spirit":"它們以烈酒加烈","They ferment on skins like reds":"它們像紅酒一樣帶皮發酵","They are always made sparkling":"它們一律釀成氣泡酒","Aromatic grapes usually avoid oak, yet some Viogniers are oak-aged.":"芳香型品種通常避免橡木桶，但有些維歐尼耶會經橡木桶陳年。","Most Viognier ferments in inert vessels, as with nearly all aromatic grapes whose perfume oak could mask. Unusually, though, some oak-aged Viogniers are made. In Condrieu a light vanilla touch is common, judged so as not to overpower the floral aromas.":"大多數維歐尼耶在惰性容器中發酵，就像幾乎所有芳香型品種一樣，因為橡木可能掩蓋它們的香氣。不過不尋常的是，也有一些經橡木桶陳年的維歐尼耶。在 Condrieu，常見一絲輕微的香草味，拿捏得當，不會壓過花香。","Which Northern Rhône appellation is dedicated to single-varietal Viognier?":"哪一個北隆河法定產區專門釀造單一品種的維歐尼耶？","Condrieu AOC makes some of the finest Viognier, from that grape alone.":"Condrieu AOC 只用這個品種，釀出一些最優質的維歐尼耶。","Condrieu AOC in the Northern Rhône is an appellation dedicated to single-varietal Viognier and gives some of its finest examples. The wines often have a light vanilla touch from oak. Hermitage, Côte-Rôtie and Crozes-Hermitage are appellations in the same area known mainly for Syrah reds.":"北隆河的 Condrieu AOC 是專門釀造單一品種維歐尼耶的法定產區，出產一些最優質的酒款。這些酒常帶有來自橡木的一絲輕微香草味。Hermitage、Côte-Rôtie 和 Crozes-Hermitage 是同一地區主要以希哈紅酒著稱的法定產區。","Why is Viognier also used as a blending partner?":"為什麼維歐尼耶也被用作混調的搭檔？","It adds floral notes and body":"它增添花香和酒體","It adds high acidity and freshness":"它增添高酸度和清新感","It adds tannin and colour":"它增添單寧和顏色","It lowers the blend's alcohol":"它降低混調的酒精","Its perfume and body make it useful for enriching other wines.":"它的香氣和酒體讓它很適合用來豐富其他酒款。","Viognier's aromatic character and body suit it to both single-varietal wines and blends, where it brings floral notes and extra body. It is not a high-acid grape (its acidity is low to medium) and, with its high alcohol, it does nothing to lower strength.":"維歐尼耶的芳香特色和酒體讓它既適合單一品種酒款，也適合混調，在混調中它帶來花香和額外的酒體。它不是高酸度的品種（酸度低至中等），而且酒精高，對降低酒精濃度毫無幫助。","Why is Rías Baixas suited to refreshing white wines?":"為什麼 Rías Baixas 適合釀造令人清爽的白酒？","Cooler, wetter, cloudier Atlantic climate":"較涼爽、潮濕、多雲的大西洋氣候","Hot, dry inland climate":"炎熱乾燥的內陸氣候","Very high-altitude vineyards":"海拔非常高的葡萄園","Being near the Atlantic makes the climate moderate, cooler and cloudier.":"靠近大西洋讓氣候溫和、較涼爽且多雲。","Rías Baixas DO lies in the north-west corner of Spain, close to the Atlantic Ocean. The climate is moderate and noticeably cooler, wetter and cloudier than in many other Spanish wine regions. These conditions preserve acidity and favour refreshing whites such as Albariño.":"Rías Baixas DO 位於西班牙西北角，靠近大西洋。氣候溫和，明顯比西班牙許多其他葡萄酒產區更涼爽、更潮濕、更多雲。這些條件能保留酸度，有利於阿爾巴利諾這類令人清爽的白酒。","Which profile best describes a typical Albariño?":"哪一種風味特徵最能描述典型的阿爾巴利諾？","Dry, high acidity, lemon, grapefruit, peach":"不甜、高酸度、檸檬、葡萄柚、桃子","Full, new oak, vanilla and coconut":"飽滿、新橡木桶、香草和椰子","Sweet, honey and dried fruit":"甜、蜂蜜和果乾","Albariño is dry, crisp, medium-bodied with citrus and stone fruit.":"阿爾巴利諾不甜、爽脆、酒體中等，帶有柑橘和核果。","Typical Albariño is dry with high acidity and medium body, with citrus (lemon, grapefruit) and stone fruit (peach, apricot). It is usually unoaked and drunk young. Rose and lychee with low acidity describe Gewurztraminer; vanilla and coconut signal new oak.":"典型的阿爾巴利諾（Albariño）不甜，酸度高，酒體中等，帶有柑橘（檸檬、葡萄柚）和核果（桃子、杏桃）。它通常不經橡木桶，趁年輕喝。玫瑰和荔枝加上低酸度描述的是格烏茲塔明那；香草和椰子則表示新橡木桶。","Which technique is sometimes used to add body and complexity to Albariño?":"有時會用哪一種技術為阿爾巴利諾增添酒體和複雜度？","A little lees contact":"少許酒渣接觸","Long ageing in new oak":"在新橡木桶中長時間陳年","Harvesting raisined grapes":"採收風乾的葡萄","A little lees contact adds body and complexity without masking the fruit.":"少許酒渣接觸能增添酒體和複雜度，而不掩蓋果味。","Albariño is usually an unoaked wine meant to be drunk young and fresh. Sometimes producers leave the wine briefly in contact with its lees, which adds body and complexity while keeping the citrus fruit and freshness intact. New oak and fortification are not part of the style.":"阿爾巴利諾通常是不經橡木桶、要趁年輕清爽時喝的酒。有時生產者會讓酒與酒渣短暫接觸，增添酒體和複雜度，同時完整保留柑橘果味和清新感。新橡木桶和加烈都不屬於這種風格。","Which grape is Gavi DOCG made from?":"Gavi DOCG 是用哪個品種釀造的？","Gavi DOCG, in Piemonte, is the best-known wine made from Cortese.":"皮埃蒙特的 Gavi DOCG 是以柯蒂斯釀造的最著名酒款。","Gavi shows the place name, not the grape, on the label, so the link has to be memorised: Gavi = Cortese. Garganega is the grape of Soave in the Veneto, Verdicchio is linked to the Marche and Fiano to Campania. All are Italian whites, which is why they are easy to mix up.":"Gavi 的酒標上顯示的是地名而不是品種，所以這個關聯必須記住：Gavi = 柯蒂斯（Cortese）。卡爾卡耐卡是威尼托 Soave 的品種，維蒂奇諾與馬凱有關，菲亞諾與坎帕尼亞有關。它們都是義大利白葡萄，所以很容易搞混。","In which region is Gavi DOCG found?":"Gavi DOCG 位於哪個地區？","Gavi DOCG is in Piemonte, in north-west Italy.":"Gavi DOCG 位於義大利西北部的皮埃蒙特。","Each white in this chapter has its own region: Gavi (Cortese) in Piemonte, Soave (Garganega) in the Veneto, Verdicchio dei Castelli di Jesi in the Marche and Fiano di Avellino in Campania. Linking wine, grape and region lets you answer many different questions with one mental map.":"本章的每一款白酒都有自己的地區：Gavi（柯蒂斯）在皮埃蒙特，Soave（卡爾卡耐卡）在威尼托，Verdicchio dei Castelli di Jesi 在馬凱，Fiano di Avellino 在坎帕尼亞。把酒款、品種和地區連起來，就能用一張心智地圖回答許多不同的問題。","Which description best fits a typical Cortese wine?":"哪一項描述最符合典型的柯蒂斯酒款？","Dry, light body, high acidity, blossom, apple and lemon":"不甜、酒體輕盈、高酸度、花香、蘋果和檸檬","Dry, full body, medium acidity, peach, mango and smoke":"不甜、酒體飽滿、中等酸度、桃子、芒果和煙燻","Sweet, full body, high acidity, honey and dried fruit":"甜、酒體飽滿、高酸度、蜂蜜和果乾","Dry, medium body, high acidity, apple and fennel":"不甜、酒體中等、高酸度、蘋果和茴香","Cortese gives dry, light, high-acid whites with blossom, green fruit and lemon.":"柯蒂斯釀出不甜、輕盈、高酸度、帶花香、綠色水果和檸檬的白酒。","The other options describe neighbouring grapes: full body, tropical fruit and oak smoke point to Fiano; fennel with medium body is typical of Verdicchio; a sweet white with dried fruit suggests Recioto di Soave. Cortese is the lightest and most delicate of the group.":"其他選項描述的是相近的品種：飽滿的酒體、熱帶水果和橡木煙燻指向菲亞諾；帶茴香、酒體中等是維蒂奇諾的典型特徵；帶果乾的甜白酒則讓人想到 Recioto di Soave。柯蒂斯是這一組中最輕盈、最細緻的。","Which is the most important grape in Soave DOC?":"Soave DOC 最重要的品種是哪一個？","Garganega, widely planted in the Veneto, is the key grape of Soave.":"廣泛種植於威尼托的卡爾卡耐卡是 Soave 的關鍵品種。","Soave and Valpolicella are both in the Veneto, but Soave is a white based on Garganega, while Valpolicella is a red based on Corvina. Cortese belongs to Gavi in Piemonte and Fiano to Campania. The name Soave on the label refers to the area, not the grape.":"Soave 和 Valpolicella 都位於威尼托，但 Soave 是以卡爾卡耐卡（Garganega）為基礎的白酒，而 Valpolicella 是以科維納為基礎的紅酒。柯蒂斯屬於皮埃蒙特的 Gavi，菲亞諾屬於坎帕尼亞。酒標上的 Soave 指的是地區，不是品種。","How is Recioto di Soave DOCG made?":"Recioto di Soave DOCG 是怎麼釀造的？","From grapes picked and then dried (appassimento)":"用採收後風乾的葡萄（appassimento）","From grapes left to freeze on the vine":"用留在樹上結冰的葡萄","By blending dry wine with grape juice":"把不甜的酒與葡萄汁混合","Recioto di Soave is a sweet white made from grapes dried after harvest.":"Recioto di Soave 是用採收後風乾的葡萄釀造的甜白酒。","In appassimento the grapes are picked and dried indoors: they lose water and concentrate their sugars, acids and flavours. The result is a rich, sweet white. The other options are real ways of making sweet wines, but they are not the method used for Recioto di Soave.":"在 appassimento 中，葡萄採收後在室內風乾：它們失去水分，糖、酸和風味隨之濃縮。結果是一款豐潤的甜白酒。其他選項都是釀造甜酒的真實方法，但不是 Recioto di Soave 使用的方法。","What does the term Classico indicate on an Italian label?":"義大利酒標上的 Classico 這個術語代表什麼？","Grapes from the historic centre of the region":"葡萄來自這個地區的歷史核心","A minimum ageing period before release":"上市前的最低陳年期","Compulsory maturation in new oak":"必須在新橡木桶中熟成","Grapes from a single named vineyard":"葡萄來自單一具名葡萄園","Classico marks the historic heart of a region, often its hilliest part.":"Classico 標示一個地區的歷史核心，常是丘陵最多的部分。","Classico is about place: the grapes come from the historic centre of the area, often hillier, and the wines are usually more concentrated. Do not confuse it with Riserva, which refers to a minimum ageing period before release. In Soave, the best Classico wines can evolve towards honey and almond.":"Classico 說的是地點：葡萄來自這個地區的歷史核心，常常丘陵更多，酒通常更濃縮。不要把它與 Riserva 混淆，Riserva 指的是上市前的最低陳年期。在 Soave，最好的 Classico 酒款能朝蜂蜜和杏仁演變。","Compared with wines from the wider region, Classico wines are typically:":"與來自更廣大地區的酒相比，Classico 酒款通常：","More concentrated in flavour":"風味更濃縮","Lighter and lower in acidity":"更輕盈、酸度更低","Sweeter and higher in alcohol":"更甜、酒精更高","Simpler and for immediate drinking":"更簡單，適合立即飲用","Classico sites, often on hills, usually give more concentrated wines.":"常位於丘陵上的 Classico 園地通常能出產更濃縮的酒。","Classico zones often cover the hilliest part of the area and produce wines with more concentrated flavours. That is why the best Soave Classico can develop honey and almond notes in bottle, while basic Soave DOC is best drunk young and fresh. Classico has nothing to do with sweetness.":"Classico 區域常涵蓋地區中丘陵最多的部分，出產風味更濃縮的酒。這就是為什麼最好的 Soave Classico 能在瓶中發展出蜂蜜和杏仁氣息，而基本的 Soave DOC 最好趁年輕清爽時喝。Classico 與甜度無關。","In which region is Verdicchio mainly grown?":"維蒂奇諾主要種植在哪個地區？","Verdicchio is widely planted in central Italy, especially the Marche on the east coast.":"維蒂奇諾廣泛種植於義大利中部，尤其是東海岸的馬凱。","The Marche lies on the east coast of central Italy and is home to Verdicchio dei Castelli di Jesi DOC. Piemonte (Gavi, Cortese) and the Veneto (Soave, Garganega) are in the north, while Campania (Fiano di Avellino) is in the south. Knowing the geography helps you rule out the distractors.":"馬凱位於義大利中部的東海岸，是 Verdicchio dei Castelli di Jesi DOC 的所在地。皮埃蒙特（Gavi、柯蒂斯）和威尼托（Soave、卡爾卡耐卡）位於北部，坎帕尼亞（Fiano di Avellino）則在南部。了解地理有助於排除干擾選項。","Which herbal note is typical of Verdicchio?":"哪一種草本氣息是維蒂奇諾的典型特徵？","Fennel":"茴香","Eucalyptus":"尤加利","Besides apple, pear and lemon, Verdicchio shows a herbal note of fennel.":"除了蘋果、梨和檸檬，維蒂奇諾還展現茴香的草本氣息。","Fennel is the clue that sets Verdicchio apart from the other dry, high-acid Italian whites in this group. Cortese and Garganega share green fruit and lemon, but not this herbal note. Linking fennel to Verdicchio is useful in style-recognition questions.":"茴香是讓維蒂奇諾（Verdicchio）與這一組其他不甜、高酸度義大利白酒區隔開來的線索。柯蒂斯和卡爾卡耐卡也有綠色水果和檸檬，但沒有這種草本氣息。把茴香和維蒂奇諾連在一起，在風格辨識題中很有用。","What is the most famous wine made from Verdicchio?":"以維蒂奇諾釀造的最著名酒款是什麼？","Verdicchio dei Castelli di Jesi DOC, in the Marche, is the grape's flagship wine.":"馬凱的 Verdicchio dei Castelli di Jesi DOC 是這個品種的旗艦酒款。","The name already contains the answer: it joins the grape, Verdicchio, and the place, Castelli di Jesi. Soave Classico is Garganega from the Veneto, Gavi is Cortese from Piemonte and Fiano di Avellino is Fiano from Campania. Each wine has its own grape-place pair to remember.":"名稱本身就包含答案：它結合了品種 Verdicchio 和地點 Castelli di Jesi。Soave Classico 是威尼托的卡爾卡耐卡，Gavi 是皮埃蒙特的柯蒂斯，Fiano di Avellino 是坎帕尼亞的菲亞諾。每款酒都有自己要記住的品種與地點組合。","Which region does Fiano di Avellino DOCG come from?":"Fiano di Avellino DOCG 來自哪個地區？","Fiano di Avellino DOCG comes from Campania, a mountainous region of southern Italy.":"Fiano di Avellino DOCG 來自義大利南部多山的坎帕尼亞。","Fiano is an important white grape of southern Italy, and its best-known wine is Fiano di Avellino DOCG, in Campania. It is the only one of the four whites in this chapter linked to the south: Cortese and Garganega are northern grapes, and Verdicchio belongs to central Italy.":"菲亞諾（Fiano）是義大利南部重要的白葡萄，它最知名的酒款是坎帕尼亞的 Fiano di Avellino DOCG。它是本章四款白酒中唯一與南部相關的：柯蒂斯和卡爾卡耐卡是北部的品種，維蒂奇諾屬於義大利中部。","Which Italian white grape has medium acidity, medium to full body and notes of peach, melon and mango?":"哪一個義大利白葡萄酸度中等、酒體中等至飽滿，帶有桃子、哈密瓜和芒果氣息？","Fiano is the richest of the group: medium acidity and tropical fruit.":"菲亞諾是這一組中最豐潤的：中等酸度和熱帶水果。","Cortese, Garganega and Verdicchio all have high acidity with green and citrus fruit. Fiano instead has medium acidity, a fuller body and riper fruit, both stone and tropical. The key word for spotting it is tropical fruit, which the other three lack.":"柯蒂斯、卡爾卡耐卡和維蒂奇諾都有高酸度，帶綠色水果和柑橘。菲亞諾則酸度中等，酒體更飽滿，果味更成熟，有核果也有熱帶水果。辨認它的關鍵詞是熱帶水果，這是其他三者所沒有的。","A Fiano shows bread and biscuit notes. Which winery choice explains them?":"一款菲亞諾展現麵包和餅乾氣息。哪一個酒廠選擇能解釋這一點？","Fermenting in steel":"在不鏽鋼槽中發酵","Very early harvest":"非常早採收","Lees contact adds secondary aromas of bread and biscuit to Fiano.":"酒渣接觸為菲亞諾增添麵包和餅乾的二級香氣。","Many producers ferment Fiano in inert vessels to preserve the fruit, but some look for secondary aromas. Lees bring bread and biscuit, while oak gives a smoky touch. Fermenting in steel on its own keeps the wine fruity without adding these notes.":"許多生產者在惰性容器中發酵菲亞諾以保留果味，但有些人追求二級香氣。酒渣帶來麵包和餅乾，橡木桶則帶來一絲煙燻。單純在不鏽鋼槽中發酵能讓酒保持果香，但不會增添這些氣息。","Which statement best describes how Gavi is typically made?":"哪一項敘述最能描述 Gavi 的典型釀造方式？","Inert vessels, no oak, drink on release":"惰性容器、不經橡木桶、上市即飲","Long new-oak ageing, made to cellar":"在新橡木桶中長時間陳年，適合窖藏","Dried grapes, sweet and long-lived":"風乾葡萄，甜且長壽","Long lees ageing, biscuit notes":"長時間酒渣陳年，帶餅乾氣息","Gavi is fermented in inert vessels, not oaked, and usually drunk young.":"Gavi 在惰性容器中發酵，不經橡木桶，通常趁年輕喝。","The aim is to protect Cortese's delicate aromas: blossom, apple, pear and lemon. Without oak or long ageing, the wine stays light, fresh and high in acid. Most Gavi is ready on release and not meant for ageing, so the options about long life are wrong.":"目的是保護柯蒂斯細緻的香氣：花香、蘋果、梨和檸檬。不經橡木桶也不長時間陳年，酒保持輕盈、清爽、高酸度。大多數 Gavi 上市時就已適飲，不是為陳年而釀的，所以關於長壽的選項都是錯的。","Which flavours can outstanding Verdicchio develop in bottle?":"傑出的維蒂奇諾在瓶中能發展出哪些風味？","Mushroom and leather":"蘑菇和皮革","Prunes and figs":"黑李乾和無花果","With age, the best Verdicchio gain notes of honey and nuts.":"隨著陳年，最好的維蒂奇諾會增添蜂蜜和堅果氣息。","Most Verdicchio is simple and drunk young, but outstanding wines evolve towards honey and nuts. Mushroom and leather are typical of mature reds such as Nebbiolo, cloves and cedar come from oak, and prunes and figs from dried grapes. They are distractors from other styles.":"大多數維蒂奇諾簡單且趁年輕喝，但傑出的酒款會朝蜂蜜和堅果演變。蘑菇和皮革是內比歐露等成熟紅酒的典型特徵，丁香和雪松來自橡木桶，黑李乾和無花果來自風乾的葡萄。這些都是來自其他風格的干擾選項。","Which of these wines is a sweet white?":"下列哪一款酒是甜白酒？","Recioto di Soave is sweet because it is made from dried grapes.":"Recioto di Soave 是甜的，因為它是用風乾的葡萄釀造的。","Soave Classico, Gavi and Verdicchio dei Castelli di Jesi are dry whites. Recioto di Soave, by contrast, is made by appassimento: the grapes dry after harvest and concentrate their sugars, giving a sweet wine. Take care not to confuse it with Soave Classico from the same area.":"Soave Classico、Gavi 和 Verdicchio dei Castelli di Jesi 都是不甜的白酒。相反地，Recioto di Soave 是以 appassimento 釀造的：葡萄在採收後風乾並濃縮糖分，釀出甜酒。小心不要把它與同一地區的 Soave Classico 混淆。","In which climates does Chenin Blanc grow well?":"白梢楠在哪些氣候中生長良好？","Cool, moderate and warm":"涼爽、溫和和溫暖","Only in cool climates with rainy autumns":"只在秋天多雨的涼爽氣候","Only in hot, dry climates":"只在炎熱乾燥的氣候","Only in moderate maritime climates":"只在溫和的海洋性氣候","Chenin Blanc adapts to cool, moderate and warm climates.":"白梢楠能適應涼爽、溫和和溫暖的氣候。","It is one of the most versatile white grapes: it thrives in the cool Loire as well as in warm parts of South Africa. Climate mainly changes ripeness and therefore flavour, from apple and lemon to peach and tropical fruit. Options that restrict it to a single climate are wrong.":"它是最多才多藝的白葡萄之一：在涼爽的羅亞爾河和南非溫暖的地區都生長茁壯。氣候主要改變成熟度，因此改變風味，從蘋果和檸檬到桃子和熱帶水果。把它限制在單一氣候的選項都是錯的。","A Chenin Blanc from very ripe grapes: which flavours are most likely?":"一款用非常成熟的葡萄釀的白梢楠：最可能有哪些風味？","Pineapple and mango":"鳳梨和芒果","Blackcurrant and green bell pepper":"黑醋栗和青椒","Bread dough, almond and dried nuts":"麵團、杏仁和乾堅果","With more ripeness Chenin moves from apple and lemon to peach and tropical fruit.":"成熟度越高，白梢楠就從蘋果和檸檬轉向桃子和熱帶水果。","Chenin's flavours track ripeness: green fruit and citrus when just ripe, stone and tropical fruit when very ripe. Green apple and lemon point to less ripe grapes. Bread dough and almond suggest a Fino Sherry, and blackcurrant a red wine.":"白梢楠的風味隨成熟度變化：剛成熟時是綠色水果和柑橘，非常成熟時是核果和熱帶水果。青蘋果和檸檬指向較不成熟的葡萄。麵團和杏仁讓人想到 Fino Sherry，黑醋栗則是紅酒。","Why can the best Chenin Blancs age for many years in bottle?":"為什麼最好的白梢楠能在瓶中陳年多年？","Thanks to their high acidity":"多虧了它們的高酸度","Thanks to tannins extracted from the skins":"多虧了從果皮萃取的單寧","Because they are always fortified with spirit":"因為它們總是以烈酒加烈","Because they always spend a long time in new barrels":"因為它們總是在新橡木桶中待很久","Its naturally high acidity gives Chenin the structure to age.":"天然的高酸度給了白梢楠陳年的結構。","Acidity is the key: it keeps the wine fresh while it develops honey and dried-fruit notes. White wines have little tannin, and Chenin is not fortified. Some oaked versions exist, but many unoaked wines age well too, including almost all Vouvray.":"酸度是關鍵：它讓酒在發展出蜂蜜和果乾氣息的同時保持清爽。白酒的單寧很少，而白梢楠也不加烈。確實有經橡木桶的版本，但許多不經橡木桶的酒也能好好陳年，包括幾乎所有的 Vouvray。","Which flavour is typical of a dry Vouvray?":"哪一種風味是不甜 Vouvray 的典型特徵？","Fresh apple, with no oak character":"新鮮蘋果，沒有橡木特徵","Lychee and rose petals":"荔枝和玫瑰花瓣","Vanilla and coconut from new oak":"來自新橡木桶的香草和椰子","Fig, prune and liquorice":"無花果、黑李乾和甘草","Dry Vouvray often shows fresh apple flavours.":"不甜的 Vouvray 常展現新鮮蘋果的風味。","In Vouvray, Chenin is almost always unoaked to keep its fresh fruit, and in dry wines apple dominates. Lychee and rose belong to Gewurztraminer. Fig, prune and liquorice describe a PX Sherry, not a dry Loire white.":"在 Vouvray，白梢楠幾乎總是不經橡木桶，以保持新鮮的果味，而在不甜的酒中以蘋果為主。荔枝和玫瑰屬於格烏茲塔明那。無花果、黑李乾和甘草描述的是 PX Sherry，不是不甜的羅亞爾河白酒。","How are the sweeter styles of Vouvray usually made?":"較甜風格的 Vouvray 通常是怎麼釀造的？","From extra-ripe or botrytis-affected grapes":"用過熟或受貴腐菌感染的葡萄","By adding grape spirit during fermentation":"在發酵期間加入葡萄烈酒","By drying the grapes indoors for a few months after harvest":"在採收後把葡萄放在室內風乾幾個月","By blending them with a sweet Moscato":"與甜的 Moscato 混調","Extra-ripe or botrytised grapes give sweet Vouvray.":"過熟或貴腐的葡萄釀出甜型 Vouvray。","High acidity and susceptibility to botrytis make Chenin ideal for late harvest and noble rot; these wines show stone or tropical fruit. Fortification belongs to Port and Sherry, and indoor drying is an Italian technique (e.g. Recioto). Only Chenin Blanc is allowed in Vouvray, so no Moscato blending.":"高酸度和容易感染貴腐菌，讓白梢楠非常適合晚收和貴腐；這些酒展現核果或熱帶水果。加烈屬於 Port 和 Sherry，室內風乾是義大利的技術（例如 Recioto）。Vouvray 只允許白梢楠，所以不會與 Moscato 混調。","Which of these styles is NOT produced in Vouvray?":"下列哪一種風格不是 Vouvray 出產的？","A red from Cabernet Franc":"以卡本內弗朗釀的紅酒","An off-dry wine labelled Demi-Sec":"標示 Demi-Sec 的微甜酒","Vouvray is a Chenin Blanc-only appellation, so it is white.":"Vouvray 是只允許白梢楠的法定產區，所以是白酒。","Vouvray covers the whole range with one grape: dry, off-dry, medium, sweet and sparkling. Because Chenin Blanc is the only permitted variety, a red cannot carry this name. The other three options are all typical styles of the appellation.":"Vouvray 用一個品種涵蓋全部範圍：不甜、微甜、半甜、甜和氣泡酒。由於白梢楠是唯一允許的品種，紅酒不能使用這個名稱。其他三個選項都是這個法定產區的典型風格。","Which notes do the best Vouvrays, dry or sweet, develop in bottle?":"最好的 Vouvray，無論不甜或甜，在瓶中會發展出哪些氣息？","Butter and cream from malolactic":"來自乳酸轉化的奶油和鮮奶油","Bread dough and toasted crust from yeast":"來自酵母的麵團和烤麵包皮","With age, great Vouvray gains honey and dried-fruit notes.":"隨著陳年，偉大的 Vouvray 會增添蜂蜜和果乾氣息。","These are tertiary notes typical of high-acid whites that age well. Leather and forest floor describe mature reds such as Vintage Port. Butter and yeasty notes come from winery choices (malolactic, lees contact), not from bottle ageing.":"這些是能好好陳年的高酸度白酒典型的三級氣息。皮革和森林地表描述的是 Vintage Port 等成熟紅酒。奶油和酵母氣息來自酒廠的選擇（乳酸轉化、酒渣接觸），不是來自瓶中陳年。","Where do the grapes for inexpensive South African Chenin labelled Western Cape usually come from?":"標示 Western Cape 的平價南非白梢楠，葡萄通常來自哪裡？","Wind-cooled coastal vineyards in Walker Bay":"Walker Bay 受風降溫的沿海葡萄園","Low-yielding old vines":"低產量的老藤","High-altitude vineyards":"高海拔葡萄園","High-volume wines use grapes from the hot inland areas.":"大量生產的酒使用來自炎熱內陸地區的葡萄。","Hot inland areas give high yields and ripe fruit, ideal for inexpensive wines often blended with Chardonnay. Low-yielding old vines instead give the top-quality Chenins. Walker Bay is one of the country's coolest areas, known for good-quality wines.":"炎熱的內陸地區帶來高產量和成熟的果實，非常適合常與夏多內混調的平價酒款。低產量的老藤則出產頂級品質的白梢楠。Walker Bay 是這個國家最涼爽的地區之一，以優質酒款著稱。","An inexpensive South African Chenin smells of vanilla. Where does this note probably come from?":"一款平價的南非白梢楠聞起來有香草味。這個氣息可能來自哪裡？","Oak chips or staves":"橡木片或橡木條","Noble rot on the grapes":"葡萄上的貴腐菌","Long ageing on the lees in bottle":"在瓶中與酒渣長時間陳年","Adding Viognier juice":"加入維歐尼耶的果汁","Chips and staves add oak flavour cheaply.":"橡木片和橡木條以低成本增添橡木風味。","In high-volume wines, chips or staves replace expensive new barrels to add vanilla. Botrytis brings concentrated sweetness, not vanilla. Lees give bread and biscuit notes, and Viognier adds blossom and peach.":"在大量生產的酒中，橡木片或橡木條取代昂貴的新橡木桶來增添香草味。貴腐菌帶來濃縮的甜味，不是香草。酒渣帶來麵包和餅乾氣息，而維歐尼耶增添花香和桃子。","Which South African vineyard is most likely to give an outstanding, intense, oak-matured Chenin Blanc?":"哪一種南非葡萄園最可能出產傑出、濃郁、經橡木桶熟成的白梢楠？","Old vines with low yields":"低產量的老藤","Young irrigated vines in the hot interior with high yields":"炎熱內陸中經灌溉、高產量的年輕葡萄樹","Newly planted vines":"新種植的葡萄樹","Machine-harvested vines":"機器採收的葡萄樹","Old vines give small quantities of concentrated fruit.":"老藤產出少量濃縮的果實。","The best Chenins come from old vines: intense pineapple and mango, often with smoke and vanilla from oak. High yields in the hot interior give simple, inexpensive wines instead. Vine age and yield matter far more than the harvesting method.":"最好的白梢楠來自老藤：濃郁的鳳梨和芒果，常帶有來自橡木的煙燻和香草。炎熱內陸的高產量則帶來簡單、平價的酒。樹齡和產量遠比採收方式重要。","Some South African producers blend Chenin Blanc with Viognier. Which style are they after?":"有些南非生產者把白梢楠與維歐尼耶混調。他們追求的是什麼風格？","A refreshing, floral white":"令人清爽、帶花香的白酒","A traditional-method sparkling wine":"傳統法氣泡酒","A sweet fortified wine from sun-dried grapes":"用曬乾葡萄釀的甜型加烈酒","A tannic white for long ageing":"適合長期陳年、有單寧的白酒","Aromatic Viognier brings blossom, Chenin brings freshness.":"芳香的維歐尼耶帶來花香，白梢楠帶來清新感。","It is a recent experiment: Chenin's acidity plus Viognier's floral scent give a refreshing white. The style is neither sparkling nor fortified. White wines are not defined by tannin either.":"這是近期的嘗試：白梢楠的酸度加上維歐尼耶的花香，造就令人清爽的白酒。這種風格既不是氣泡酒也不是加烈酒。白酒也不是以單寧來定義的。","A label says 'Semillon' with no accent. What does this suggest?":"一張酒標上寫著沒有重音符號的「Semillon」。這暗示什麼？","The wine comes from an English-speaking country":"這款酒來自英語系國家","The wine is definitely sweet":"這款酒肯定是甜的","It is a different, more aromatic grape from French Sémillon":"它是與法國 Sémillon 不同、更芳香的品種","The wine has been oak-aged":"這款酒經過橡木桶陳年","Sémillon with an accent in France, Semillon in English-speaking countries.":"在法國寫作帶重音的 Sémillon，在英語系國家寫作 Semillon。","It is the same grape: only the spelling changes with the origin, e.g. Australia for Semillon. The spelling says nothing about sweetness or oak. Semillon is not an aromatic grape: when young it has simple apple, lemon and grass flavours.":"這是同一個品種：只是拼法隨產地而變，例如澳洲寫 Semillon。拼法與甜度或橡木桶無關。榭密雍不是芳香型品種：年輕時它帶有簡單的蘋果、檸檬和青草風味。","Which primary flavours does a young Semillon usually show?":"年輕的榭密雍通常展現哪些一級風味？","Apple, lemon and grass":"蘋果、檸檬和青草","Honey, nuts and dried fruit":"蜂蜜、堅果和果乾","Ripe peach, melon and mango with white-flower notes":"成熟的桃子、哈密瓜和芒果，帶白花氣息","Young Semillon has simple apple, lemon and grass flavours.":"年輕的榭密雍帶有簡單的蘋果、檸檬和青草風味。","Honey, nuts and dried fruit are tertiary notes that appear only after years in bottle. Rose and lychee point to Gewurztraminer. Peach, melon and mango suggest Fiano rather than a young Semillon.":"蜂蜜、堅果和果乾是瓶中多年後才出現的三級氣息。玫瑰和荔枝指向格烏茲塔明那。桃子、哈密瓜和芒果讓人想到菲亞諾，而不是年輕的榭密雍。","Where is Sauternes AOC?":"Sauternes AOC 在哪裡？","A small sub-region of Bordeaux":"波爾多的一個小子產區","In the Loire Valley, next to Vouvray":"在羅亞爾河谷，Vouvray 旁邊","In Alsace, in the Vosges foothills":"在阿爾薩斯，孚日山脈山麓","In the Northern Rhône, near Condrieu":"在北隆河，靠近 Condrieu","Sauternes is a small sub-region within Bordeaux.":"Sauternes 是波爾多之內的一個小子產區。","Sauternes lies on Bordeaux's 'Left Bank', where autumn mists favour noble rot. Vouvray is in the Loire and Condrieu in the Northern Rhône. Alsace makes late-harvest sweet wines, but Sauternes is not part of it.":"Sauternes 位於波爾多「左岸」，那裡秋天的霧氣有利於貴腐菌。Vouvray 在羅亞爾河，Condrieu 在北隆河。阿爾薩斯出產晚收甜酒，但 Sauternes 不屬於阿爾薩斯。","Which weather lets botrytis become noble rot rather than destroy the grapes?":"什麼樣的天氣讓貴腐菌成為貴腐，而不是毀掉葡萄？","Damp, misty mornings and warm, dry afternoons":"潮濕多霧的早晨和溫暖乾燥的午後","Constant rain throughout harvest":"整個採收期持續下雨","Night frosts that freeze the grapes on the vine":"讓葡萄在樹上結冰的夜間霜凍","Constant dry heat day and night":"日夜持續的乾熱","Mist lets the fungus grow, dry afternoons hold it back.":"霧氣讓真菌生長，乾燥的午後則抑制它。","Botrytis must attack ripe grapes; morning humidity spreads it and afternoon sun limits it. Constant rain would let the fungus destroy the crop, while constant dry heat would stop it developing. Grapes frozen on the vine give Icewine, a different technique.":"貴腐菌必須侵襲成熟的葡萄；早晨的濕氣讓它蔓延，午後的陽光限制它。持續下雨會讓真菌毀掉收成，而持續乾熱會阻止它發展。在樹上結冰的葡萄釀出冰酒，那是另一種技術。","Which description fits a typical young Sauternes?":"哪一項描述符合典型的年輕 Sauternes？","Sweet, full-bodied, high acidity, apricot and vanilla":"甜、酒體飽滿、高酸度、杏桃和香草","Sweet, light, low alcohol, fizzy, grapey and floral":"甜、輕盈、低酒精、有氣泡、葡萄味和花香","Dry, light, neutral, low alcohol":"不甜、輕盈、中性、低酒精","Sweet, brown, fortified, with fig, liquorice and molasses":"甜、褐色、加烈，帶有無花果、甘草和糖蜜","Sauternes is sweet and full, balanced by high acidity, with apricot and oak notes.":"Sauternes 甜而飽滿，以高酸度平衡，帶有杏桃和橡木氣息。","It also has medium to high alcohol and, with age, gains dried fruit, honey and caramel. The sweet, light, fizzy wine is Asti. The dry, light, neutral wine sounds like a young Hunter Valley Semillon, and the brown fortified wine is a PX Sherry.":"它的酒精也中等至高，陳年後會增添果乾、蜂蜜和焦糖。甜、輕盈、有氣泡的酒是 Asti。不甜、輕盈、中性的酒聽起來像年輕的 Hunter Valley 榭密雍，而褐色的加烈酒是 PX Sherry。","A customer orders a Sauternes with dessert. At what temperature should it be served?":"一位顧客點了一杯 Sauternes 搭配甜點。應該在什麼溫度下侍酒？","Well chilled, 6-8 °C":"充分冰鎮，6–8 °C","Lightly chilled, 10-13 °C":"略微冰鎮，10–13 °C","Room temperature, 15-18 °C, like a full-bodied red":"室溫 15–18 °C，就像酒體飽滿的紅酒","Slightly warmed to lift the aromas":"稍微加溫以提升香氣","Sweet wines such as Sauternes are served well chilled.":"Sauternes 等甜酒要充分冰鎮後侍酒。","Cold keeps the sweetness feeling fresh. 10-13 °C suits full-bodied whites such as oaked Chardonnay. A wine should never be heated, for example near a radiator, as this damages its flavours.":"低溫讓甜味感覺清爽。10–13 °C 適合經橡木桶的夏多內等酒體飽滿的白酒。酒絕不應該加熱，例如放在暖氣旁，因為這會損害風味。","How is a Hunter Valley Semillon usually made and bottled?":"Hunter Valley 的榭密雍通常如何釀造和裝瓶？","In inert vessels, bottled young":"在惰性容器中，趁年輕裝瓶","In new oak barrels, bottled after two years":"在新橡木桶中，兩年後裝瓶","In a solera of old casks, then fortified":"在舊桶的 solera 中，然後加烈","With a second fermentation in bottle and long lees contact":"在瓶中二次發酵並長時間與酒渣接觸","Inert vessels and early bottling keep the light style.":"惰性容器和提早裝瓶保持了輕盈的風格。","The complex honey and nut flavours come only after several years in bottle, not from oak. Long barrel ageing applies to some Barossa Semillons. Solera, fortification and second fermentation belong to Sherry and sparkling wine.":"複雜的蜂蜜和堅果風味要在瓶中多年後才會出現，不是來自橡木桶。長時間的橡木桶陳年適用於部分 Barossa 榭密雍。Solera、加烈和二次發酵屬於 Sherry 和氣泡酒。","What sets Barossa Valley Semillon apart from Hunter Valley Semillon?":"Barossa Valley 的榭密雍與 Hunter Valley 的榭密雍有什麼不同？","Barossa makes a range of styles, including full-bodied oaked ones":"Barossa 出產多種風格，包括酒體飽滿、經橡木桶的風格","Barossa makes only sweet botrytised wines":"Barossa 只出產貴腐甜酒","Barossa makes only sparkling wines":"Barossa 只出產氣泡酒","None: Australian law imposes the same light style everywhere":"沒有不同：澳洲法律規定各地都是同樣的輕盈風格","Barossa ranges from Hunter-like wines to full-bodied, oaked ones.":"Barossa 的範圍從類似 Hunter 的酒到酒體飽滿、經橡木桶的酒都有。","Hunter Valley has one clear style: dry, light, low-alcohol and unoaked. Barossa is more varied and can also make Hunter-like wines. No rule imposes a single style, and the region is not limited to sweet or sparkling wines.":"Hunter Valley 有一種清楚的風格：不甜、輕盈、低酒精、不經橡木桶。Barossa 更多樣，也能釀出類似 Hunter 的酒。沒有規定強制單一風格，這個產區也不只限於甜酒或氣泡酒。","Which of these uses of Semillon is NOT typical in Australia?":"下列哪一種榭密雍的用途在澳洲並不典型？","Base for a fortified wine aged in a solera":"作為在 solera 中陳年的加烈酒的基酒","Blending with Sauvignon Blanc":"與白蘇維濃混調","Sweet wines from botrytised grapes":"用貴腐葡萄釀的甜酒","Dry single-varietal wines in various styles":"各種風格的不甜單一品種酒","In Australia Semillon makes blends, botrytised sweet wines and dry wines, not solera wines.":"在澳洲，榭密雍用於混調、貴腐甜酒和不甜的酒，而不是 solera 酒款。","Australia has large Semillon plantings and uses it in blends with Sauvignon Blanc, for botrytised sweet wines and for dry wines such as those of Hunter and Barossa. The solera system belongs to Sherry, made almost entirely from Palomino.":"澳洲的榭密雍種植面積很大，用於與白蘇維濃的混調、貴腐甜酒，以及 Hunter 和 Barossa 那樣的不甜酒款。Solera 系統屬於幾乎全用帕洛米諾釀造的 Sherry。","How are very good or outstanding Sémillon-based white Bordeaux often matured?":"非常好或傑出、以榭密雍為主的波爾多白酒常如何熟成？","In oak, then they develop for years in bottle":"在橡木桶中，之後在瓶中發展多年","In steel tanks, to drink within a year":"在不鏽鋼槽中，要在一年內喝掉","Under a yeast layer, like Sherry":"在一層酵母之下，就像 Sherry","In amphora, with no contact with oxygen or wood":"在陶甕中，不接觸氧氣或木頭","The best Sémillon-based white Bordeaux are often oak-matured and age well.":"最好的以榭密雍為主的波爾多白酒常經橡木桶熟成，陳年潛力佳。","Sémillon brings body and ageing potential to blends with Sauvignon Blanc, and oak adds complexity. The flor layer belongs to Fino Sherry. A wine to drink within a year describes simple whites, not Bordeaux's best.":"榭密雍為與白蘇維濃的混調帶來酒體和陳年潛力，而橡木桶增添複雜度。酒花層屬於 Fino Sherry。要在一年內喝掉的酒描述的是簡單的白酒，不是波爾多最好的酒款。","In which country is Furmint most widely grown?":"弗明在哪個國家種植最廣？","Germany, along the Mosel":"德國，沿著 Mosel 河","Furmint is above all a Hungarian grape.":"弗明首先是匈牙利的品種。","It is the most planted grape of the Tokaj region, famous for the sweet Tokaji Aszú. Portugal is home to Port, made from local black grapes. The Mosel is Riesling country, not Furmint.":"它是 Tokaj 產區種植最多的品種，這個產區以甜型的 Tokaji Aszú 聞名。葡萄牙是 Port 的故鄉，Port 用在地黑葡萄釀造。Mosel 是麗絲玲的天下，不是弗明。","Which statement about the Tokaj region is correct?":"關於 Tokaj 產區，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It lies in north-east Hungary and also makes dry and medium wines":"它位於匈牙利東北部，也出產不甜和半甜的酒","It lies in southern Hungary and makes only sweet wines":"它位於匈牙利南部，只出產甜酒","It is mainly famous for tannic reds":"它主要以單寧多的紅酒聞名","Its main grape is Muscat":"它的主要品種是蜜思嘉","Tokaj, in north-east Hungary, makes dry and medium wines as well as Aszú.":"位於匈牙利東北部的 Tokaj，除了 Aszú 也出產不甜和半甜的酒。","Its fame comes from sweet Tokaji Aszú, but the region does not make only sweet wines. It is a white-wine area and its most planted grape is Furmint, not Muscat.":"它的名聲來自甜型的 Tokaji Aszú，但這個產區並不只出產甜酒。它是白酒產區，種植最多的品種是弗明，不是蜜思嘉。","Why is Furmint in Tokaji Aszú often blended with other local grapes?":"為什麼 Tokaji Aszú 中的弗明常與其他在地品種混調？","For greater aroma complexity":"為了增添香氣的複雜度","To raise the acidity, which is low in Furmint":"為了提高弗明偏低的酸度","To give the wine its amber colour":"為了讓酒呈現琥珀色","Because Furmint alone is never affected by botrytis in Hungary":"因為在匈牙利，弗明單獨從不會感染貴腐菌","Other local grapes add aroma complexity.":"其他在地品種增添香氣的複雜度。","Furmint already has high acidity and is very prone to botrytis: that is exactly why it is the main grape. The amber colour comes from long oak ageing, not from blending.":"弗明本身酸度就很高，又非常容易感染貴腐菌：這正是它成為主要品種的原因。琥珀色來自長時間的橡木桶陳年，不是來自混調。","How is most Tokaji Aszú labelled?":"大多數 Tokaji Aszú 如何標示？","5 Puttonyos or 6 Puttonyos":"5 Puttonyos 或 6 Puttonyos","Brut or Demi-Sec":"Brut 或 Demi-Sec","Classico or Riserva":"Classico 或 Riserva","With an age indication of 10, 20, 30 or 40 years":"標示 10、20、30 或 40 年的年齡","Most Tokaji Aszú is labelled 5 or 6 Puttonyos.":"大多數 Tokaji Aszú 標示 5 或 6 Puttonyos。","The number of Puttonyos shows sweetness: 6 is sweeter than 5. Brut and Demi-Sec are sparkling-wine terms, Classico and Riserva are Italian. Age indications of 10-40 years are typical of Tawny Port.":"Puttonyos 的數字表示甜度：6 比 5 更甜。Brut 和 Demi-Sec 是氣泡酒術語，Classico 和 Riserva 是義大利術語。10–40 年的年齡標示是 Tawny Port 的典型特徵。","Which combination of aromas is typical of Tokaji Aszú?":"哪一組香氣是 Tokaji Aszú 的典型特徵？","Apricot, citrus, vanilla, caramel and nuts":"杏桃、柑橘、香草、焦糖和堅果","Black cherry, blackberry and pepper":"黑櫻桃、黑莓和胡椒","Apple, lemon and bread dough":"蘋果、檸檬和麵團","Cut grass, gooseberry and green bell pepper":"青草、醋栗和青椒","Tokaji Aszú mixes primary, oak and tertiary aromas.":"Tokaji Aszú 混合了一級、橡木和三級香氣。","Fresh and dried apricot and citrus come from the grape, vanilla and smoke from oak, caramel and nuts from age. Black fruit and pepper describe a red. Apple, lemon and bread dough suggest Fino Sherry.":"新鮮和乾燥的杏桃以及柑橘來自葡萄，香草和煙燻來自橡木桶，焦糖和堅果來自陳年。黑色水果和胡椒描述的是紅酒。蘋果、檸檬和麵團讓人想到 Fino Sherry。","In Tokaji Aszú, why does fermentation stop with lots of sugar left?":"在 Tokaji Aszú 中，為什麼發酵會在留下大量糖分時停止？","The botrytised juice holds more sugar than the yeast can eat":"貴腐果汁的糖分多到酵母吃不完","Grape spirit is added mid-fermentation":"在發酵中途加入葡萄烈酒","The yeast is removed with very fine filters":"用非常細的過濾器去除酵母","Sweet, unfermented grape juice is added after fermentation ends":"在發酵結束後加入甜的未發酵葡萄汁","With such concentrated sugars, the yeast cannot consume them all.":"糖分如此濃縮，酵母無法全部消耗。","Noble-rotted grapes have highly concentrated sugar and acid, so fermentation stops by itself. Adding spirit is the Port technique, and filtering out yeast is used for wines such as White Zinfandel. Adding sweet juice is another way to sweeten, but not the Aszú way.":"貴腐葡萄的糖和酸高度濃縮，所以發酵會自行停止。加入烈酒是 Port 的技術，過濾去除酵母用於 White Zinfandel 等酒款。加入甜葡萄汁是另一種增甜方法，但不是 Aszú 的做法。","In which climates does Gewurztraminer grow best?":"格烏茲塔明那在哪些氣候中生長得最好？","Warm and sunny":"溫暖晴朗","Very hot, with early harvests":"非常炎熱，提早採收","Only in humid, high-altitude tropical climates":"只在潮濕的高海拔熱帶氣候","Gewurztraminer prefers cool to moderate climates.":"格烏茲塔明那偏好涼爽至溫和的氣候。","Even in cool climates the grape builds up a lot of sugar, so a dry wine ends up full and high in alcohol. In hot climates it would lose even more of its already low-to-medium acidity. The classic case is Alsace, cool but dry and sunny.":"即使在涼爽氣候中，這個品種也會累積大量糖分，所以不甜的酒最後酒體飽滿、酒精很高。在炎熱的氣候中，它本來就低至中等的酸度會流失更多。經典的例子是阿爾薩斯，涼爽但乾燥晴朗。","Which of these grapes is NOT one of the typical varieties of Alsace's grands crus?":"下列哪一個品種不是阿爾薩斯 grand cru 的典型品種之一？","Riesling, Pinot Gris and Gewurztraminer are the typical grand cru grapes in Alsace.":"麗絲玲、灰皮諾和格烏茲塔明那是阿爾薩斯典型的 grand cru 品種。","Gewurztraminer gives some of Alsace's finest grand cru wines, alongside Riesling and Pinot Gris. Chardonnay is mainly linked to Burgundy and Champagne, not to Alsace's grands crus.":"格烏茲塔明那與麗絲玲和灰皮諾一起，釀出阿爾薩斯一些最優質的 grand cru 酒款。夏多內主要與布根地和 Champagne 相關，不屬於阿爾薩斯的 grand cru。","Why are Alsace Grand Cru wines usually riper and fuller than those from the plains?":"為什麼 Alsace Grand Cru 的酒通常比平原的酒更成熟、更飽滿？","Vineyards on steep east/south-east slopes get more sunlight":"位於朝東／東南陡坡的葡萄園獲得更多日照","They are irrigated more often":"它們更常灌溉","They are near the sea, which warms them at night":"它們靠近海洋，夜間受海洋保溫","The grapes are picked earlier to keep acidity":"葡萄較早採收以保留酸度","The east/south-east facing Vosges foothills catch more sunlight.":"朝東／東南的孚日山麓接收更多日照。","Grands crus come from specific vineyards, mostly on the steep Vosges foothills that catch the morning sun. More light means riper grapes and fuller wines. Alsace is far from the sea, and an early harvest would give lighter wines, not fuller ones.":"Grand cru 來自特定的葡萄園，大多位於能接收早晨陽光的孚日山脈陡峭山麓。更多的光照代表更成熟的葡萄和更飽滿的酒。阿爾薩斯遠離海洋，而提早採收會讓酒更輕盈，而不是更飽滿。","An Alsace Gewurztraminer says 'Vendanges tardives'. What should you expect?":"一款阿爾薩斯格烏茲塔明那標示「Vendanges tardives」。你應該預期什麼？","A wine fortified with grape spirit after fermentation":"在發酵後以葡萄烈酒加烈的酒","'Vendanges tardives' means late harvest: medium or sweet wines.":"「Vendanges tardives」是晚收的意思：半甜或甜型的酒。","Leaving the grapes longer on the vine raises the sugar, so the wine stays sweet. In Alsace the term is used for Gewurztraminer, Riesling and Pinot Gris, for both Alsace and Alsace Grand Cru. It indicates neither bubbles nor fortification.":"讓葡萄在樹上留得更久會提高糖分，所以酒保持甜味。在阿爾薩斯，這個術語用於格烏茲塔明那、麗絲玲和灰皮諾，Alsace 和 Alsace Grand Cru 皆可。它既不代表氣泡，也不代表加烈。","Why is Alsace one of the driest, sunniest wine regions in France?":"為什麼阿爾薩斯是法國最乾燥、陽光最充足的葡萄酒產區之一？","The Vosges shelter it from rain-bearing westerly winds":"孚日山脈為它擋住帶雨的西風","It is close to the Mediterranean":"它靠近地中海","It lies at a low latitude":"它位於低緯度","It gets river mists every autumn morning that quickly dry the bunches":"每個秋天早晨都有河霧，能迅速吹乾果串","The Vosges act as a barrier to rain from the west.":"孚日山脈是阻擋西方雨水的屏障。","Alsace lies east of the Vosges, in their rain shadow: dry autumns extend ripening. It is in north-east France, far from the Mediterranean and not at a low latitude. Morning mists favour botrytis rather than drying the grapes.":"阿爾薩斯位於孚日山脈以東的雨影區：乾燥的秋天延長了成熟期。它在法國東北部，遠離地中海，也不在低緯度。晨霧有利於貴腐菌，而不是吹乾葡萄。","In which kind of climate is Viognier mainly grown?":"維歐尼耶主要種植在哪一種氣候中？","Cold, like the Mosel":"寒冷，像 Mosel","Cool and rainy, like Atlantic Galicia":"涼爽多雨，像大西洋岸的加利西亞","Cool and misty, ideal for noble rot":"涼爽多霧，非常適合貴腐","Viognier is an aromatic grape mostly grown in moderate climates.":"維歐尼耶是主要種植於溫和氣候的芳香型品種。","It needs warmth to reach full ripeness, hence high alcohol and medium to full body. The cool, rainy Atlantic climate is the home of Albariño. Noble rot is not linked to Viognier, which is usually dry.":"它需要熱量才能完全成熟，因此酒精高、酒體中等至飽滿。涼爽多雨的大西洋氣候是阿爾巴利諾的故鄉。貴腐與通常不甜的維歐尼耶無關。","When a Condrieu producer uses oak, what must they avoid?":"Condrieu 的生產者使用橡木桶時，必須避免什麼？","Overpowering the delicate floral aromas":"壓過細緻的花香","Reducing the wine's red colour":"減少酒的紅色","Stopping the second fermentation":"中止二次發酵","Letting a layer of yeast form on the surface":"讓酒液表面形成一層酵母","In Condrieu oak adds only light vanilla, without masking the blossom.":"在 Condrieu，橡木桶只增添輕微的香草味，不會掩蓋花香。","Viognier lives on its blossom, peach and apricot scents: too much oak would hide them. Condrieu is a still white, so red colour and second fermentation are irrelevant. A yeast layer (flor) is typical of Fino Sherry.":"維歐尼耶的魅力在於它的花香、桃子和杏桃香氣：太多橡木會把它們掩蓋。Condrieu 是靜態白酒，所以紅色和二次發酵都無關。一層酵母（酒花）是 Fino Sherry 的典型特徵。","Of Gewurztraminer, Viognier and Albariño, which usually gives high-acid wines?":"在格烏茲塔明那、維歐尼耶和阿爾巴利諾中，哪一個通常釀出高酸度的酒？","All three equally":"三者都一樣","Albariño is dry and high in acidity; the other two have low to medium acidity.":"阿爾巴利諾不甜且酸度高；另外兩者酸度低至中等。","Gewurztraminer and Viognier are full, high-alcohol, perfumed whites with low to medium acidity. Albariño from cool north-west Spain makes lively, refreshing wines instead. So the three are not alike.":"格烏茲塔明那和維歐尼耶是酒體飽滿、酒精高、香氣濃郁、酸度低至中等的白酒。來自涼爽西班牙西北部的阿爾巴利諾則釀出活潑清爽的酒。所以三者並不相同。","In which part of Spain is Rías Baixas DO?":"Rías Baixas DO 位於西班牙哪個部分？","The north-west corner, near the Atlantic":"西北角，靠近大西洋"});(window.TWG_I18N_F=window.TWG_I18N_F||{})["zh-hant/l2"]=1;
